__d(function(a,e,i,s,o,t,n){o.exports=[{id:"vism-1.1",pali:"S\u012ble pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya naro sapa\xf1\xf1o, citta\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1a\xf1ca bh\u0101vaya\u1e43; \u0100t\u0101p\u012b nipako bhikkhu, so ima\u1e43 vija\u1e6daye ja\u1e6danti.",translations:{en:"A wise man, established in virtue, developing mind and wisdom, an ardent and discerning bhikkhu\u2014he can disentangle this tangle.",pt:"\u201cEstabelecendo-se na virtude, o homem s\xe1bio, desenvolvendo a mente e a sabedoria, sendo ardente e prudente, esse bhikkhu desembara\xe7a este emaranhado.\u201d",es:"Habi\xe9ndose establecido en la virtud, el hombre sabio que desarrolla la mente y la sabidur\xeda, el monje ardiente y prudente, \xe9l puede desenredar este enredo."}},{id:"vism-1.2",pali:"Iti hida\u1e43 vutta\u1e43, kasm\u0101 paneta\u1e43 vutta\u1e43, bhagavanta\u1e43 kira s\u0101vatthiya\u1e43 viharanta\u1e43 rattibh\u0101ge a\xf1\xf1ataro devaputto upasa\u1e45kamitv\u0101 attano sa\u1e43sayasamuggh\u0101\u1e6dattha\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"Thus was this said. Why was this said? It is said that while the Blessed One was dwelling at S\u0101vatth\u012b, a certain devaputta approached him during the night to dispel his own doubt, asking:",pt:"Assim isto foi dito. Mas porque isso foi dito? Diz-se que, enquanto o Aben\xe7oado residia em S\u0101vatth\u012b, durante a noite, um certo jovem deva aproximou-se dele para erradicar suas pr\xf3prias d\xfavidas:",es:"As\xed fue dicho esto. Pero, \xbfpor qu\xe9 fue dicho? Se dice que, mientras el Bienaventurado resid\xeda en S\u0101vatth\u012b, durante la noche, cierto joven de los dioses se le acerc\xf3 para eliminar su propia duda."}},{id:"vism-1.3",pali:"Tattha visuddh\u012bti sabbamalavirahita\u1e43 accantaparisuddha\u1e43 nibb\u0101na\u1e43 veditabba\u1e43. Tass\u0101 visuddhiy\u0101 maggoti visuddhimaggo. Maggoti adhigam\u016bp\u0101yo vuccati. Ta\u1e43 visuddhimagga\u1e43 bh\u0101siss\u0101m\u012bti attho.",translations:{en:"Herein, 'purification' should be understood as Nibb\u0101na, which is completely free from all stains and utterly pure. The path to that purification is the 'Path of Purification' (Visuddhimagga). 'Path' is said to be the means of attainment. The meaning is: \"I shall expound that Path of Purification.\"",pt:"Aqui, por 'purifica\xe7\xe3o' (visuddhi) deve-se entender o Nibb\u0101na, que \xe9 livre de todas as impurezas e absolutamente puro. O caminho para essa purifica\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o 'Caminho da Purifica\xe7\xe3o' (visuddhimagga). Por 'caminho' (magga) entende-se o meio de realiza\xe7\xe3o. 'Eu exporei esse Caminho da Purifica\xe7\xe3o' \u2014 este \xe9 o significado.",es:"3. En ese contexto, por \xabpurificaci\xf3n\xbb debe entenderse el Nibb\u0101na, que es absolutamente puro y est\xe1 libre de toda mancha. El camino hacia esa purificaci\xf3n es el \xabCamino de la Purificaci\xf3n\xbb (Visuddhimagga). Por \xabcamino\xbb se entiende el medio para la obtenci\xf3n. \xabExpondr\xe9 ese camino de la purificaci\xf3n\xbb es el sentido."}},{id:"vism-1.4",pali:"Eva\u1e43 anekagu\u1e47asa\u1e45g\u0101hakena s\u012blasam\u0101dhipa\xf1\xf1\u0101mukhena desitopi panesa visuddhimaggo atisa\u1e45khepadesitoyeva hoti. Tasm\u0101 n\u0101la\u1e43 sabbesa\u1e43 upak\u0101r\u0101y\u0101ti vitth\u0101ramassa dassetu\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43 t\u0101va \u0101rabbha ida\u1e43 pa\xf1h\u0101kamma\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"Though this Path of Purification has thus been taught by way of the gate of virtue, concentration, and wisdom, which encompasses many qualities, it has nevertheless been taught only in a very condensed way; thus it is not adequate for the benefit of all. Therefore, to set forth its elaboration, this inquiry begins first with virtue.",pt:"No entanto, embora este Caminho da Purifica\xe7\xe3o tenha sido ensinado por meio da virtude, da concentra\xe7\xe3o e da sabedoria, que abrangem in\xfameras qualidades, ele foi ensinado de forma extremamente resumida. Portanto, como n\xe3o \xe9 suficiente para beneficiar a todos, apresenta-se a seguinte s\xe9rie de perguntas, come\xe7ando primeiramente com a virtude, a fim de mostrar sua explica\xe7\xe3o detalhada:",es:"Aunque este Camino de la Purificaci\xf3n (Visuddhimagga) ha sido ense\xf1ado a trav\xe9s de la virtud, la concentraci\xf3n y la sabidur\xeda, que comprenden numerosas cualidades, se ha expuesto de forma muy resumida. Por lo tanto, dado que no es suficiente para el beneficio de todos, se presentan las siguientes preguntas comenzando por la virtud, con el fin de mostrar su explicaci\xf3n detallada:"}},{id:"vism-1.5",pali:"Ki\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43, kena\u1e6d\u1e6dhena s\u012bla\u1e43, k\u0101nassa lakkha\u1e47arasapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni, kim\u0101nisa\u1e43sa\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43, katividha\u1e43 ceta\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43, ko cassa sa\u1e43kileso, ki\u1e43 vod\u0101nanti.",translations:{en:"What is virtue? In what sense is it virtue? What are its characteristic, function, manifestation, and proximate cause? What is the benefit of virtue? How many kinds of virtue are there? What is its defilement, and what is its cleansing?",pt:"O que \xe9 a virtude? Em que sentido \xe9 virtude? Quais s\xe3o as suas caracter\xedsticas, fun\xe7\xe3o, manifesta\xe7\xe3o e causa pr\xf3xima? Quais s\xe3o os seus benef\xedcios? Quantos tipos de virtude existem? O que \xe9 a sua corrup\xe7\xe3o? O que \xe9 a sua purifica\xe7\xe3o?",es:"\xbfQu\xe9 es la virtud? \xbfEn qu\xe9 sentido es virtud? \xbfCu\xe1les son sus caracter\xedsticas, su funci\xf3n, su manifestaci\xf3n y su causa pr\xf3xima? \xbfCu\xe1les son los beneficios de la virtud? \xbfDe cu\xe1ntas clases es la virtud? \xbfQu\xe9 es su contaminaci\xf3n y qu\xe9 es su purificaci\xf3n?"}},{id:"vism-1.6",pali:"Tatrida\u1e43 vissajjana\u1e43. Ki\u1e43 s\u012blanti p\u0101\u1e47\u0101tip\u0101t\u0101d\u012bhi v\u0101 viramantassa vattapa\u1e6dipatti\u1e43 v\u0101 p\u016brentassa cetan\u0101dayo dhamm\u0101. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101ya\u1e43 \"ki\u1e43 s\u012blanti cetan\u0101 s\u012bla\u1e43, cetasika\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43, sa\u1e43varo s\u012bla\u1e43, av\u012btikkamo s\u012bla\"nti. Tattha cetan\u0101 s\u012bla\u1e43 n\u0101ma p\u0101\u1e47\u0101tip\u0101t\u0101d\u012bhi v\u0101 viramantassa vattapa\u1e6dipatti\u1e43 v\u0101 p\u016brentassa cetan\u0101. Cetasika\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43 n\u0101ma p\u0101\u1e47\u0101tip\u0101t\u0101d\u012bhi viramantassa virati. Apica cetan\u0101 s\u012bla\u1e43 n\u0101ma p\u0101\u1e47\u0101tip\u0101t\u0101d\u012bni pajahantassa satta kammapathacetan\u0101. Cetasika\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43 n\u0101ma \"abhijjha\u1e43 pah\u0101ya vigat\u0101bhijjhena cetas\u0101 viharat\u012b\"ti \u0101din\u0101 nayena vutt\u0101 anabhijjh\u0101by\u0101p\u0101dasamm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhidhamm\u0101. Sa\u1e43varo s\u012blanti ettha pa\xf1cavidhena sa\u1e43varo veditabbo p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varo, satisa\u1e43varo, \xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e43varo, khantisa\u1e43varo, v\u012briyasa\u1e43varoti. Tattha imin\u0101 p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varena upeto hoti samupetoti aya\u1e43 p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varo. Rakkhati cakkhundriya\u1e43, cakkhundriye sa\u1e43vara\u1e43 \u0101pajjat\u012bti aya\u1e43 satisa\u1e43varo.",translations:{en:"Herein is the explanation. What is virtue? It is the states, such as volition, of one who abstains from killing living beings and so forth, or of one who fulfills the practice of duties. For it is said in the Pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101magga: \u201cWhat is virtue? Volition is virtue, a mental factor is virtue, restraint is virtue, non-transgression is virtue\u201d (Pa\u1e6di. Ma. 1.39). Therein, \u2018volition as virtue\u2019 is the volition of one who abstains from killing living beings and so forth, or of one who fulfills the practice of duties. \u2018A mental factor as virtue\u2019 is the abstinence of one who abstains from killing living beings and so forth. Furthermore, \u2018volition as virtue\u2019 refers to the seven volitions of the courses of action of one who abandons killing living beings and so forth. \u2018A mental factor as virtue\u2019 refers to the states of non-covetousness, non-ill will, and right view, spoken of in the manner beginning: \u201cHaving abandoned covetousness, he dwells with a mind free from covetousness\u201d (D\u012b. Ni. 1.217). As for \u2018restraint as virtue,\u2019 herein restraint is to be understood as fivefold: restraint by the P\u0101timokkha, restraint by mindfulness, restraint by knowledge, restraint by patience, and restraint by energy. Therein, \u201cHe is endowed, possessed of this restraint of the P\u0101timokkha\u201d (Vibh. 511)\u2014this is restraint by the P\u0101timokkha. \u201cHe guards the eye faculty, he undertakes restraint in the eye faculty\u201d (D\u012b. Ni. 1.213)\u2014this is restraint by mindfulness.",pt:"Aqui est\xe1 a resposta. 'O que \xe9 a virtude (s\u012bla)?': Para quem se abst\xe9m de matar seres vivos, etc., ou para quem cumpre os deveres e pr\xe1ticas (como os deveres para com o preceptor), os estados mentais como a voli\xe7\xe3o (cetan\u0101), etc., s\xe3o a virtude. Pois foi dito no Pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101magga: 'O que \xe9 a virtude? A voli\xe7\xe3o \xe9 virtude, o fator mental (cetasika) \xe9 virtude, o refreamento (sa\u1e43vara) \xe9 virtude, a n\xe3o transgress\xe3o (av\u012btikkamo) \xe9 virtude'. Aqui, a 'virtude como voli\xe7\xe3o' (cetan\u0101s\u012bla) \xe9 a voli\xe7\xe3o de quem se abst\xe9m de matar, etc., ou de quem cumpre os deveres. A 'virtude como fator mental' (cetasikas\u012bla) \xe9 a abstin\xeancia (virati) de quem se abst\xe9m de matar, etc. Al\xe9m disso, a 'virtude como voli\xe7\xe3o' refere-se \xe0s sete voli\xe7\xf5es dos caminhos de a\xe7\xe3o (kammapatha) de quem abandona o matar, etc. A 'virtude como fator mental' refere-se aos dhammas de n\xe3o cobi\xe7a, n\xe3o malevol\xeancia e vis\xe3o correta, descritos na passagem: 'Abandonando a cobi\xe7a, ele habita com a mente livre de cobi\xe7a', e assim por diante. Na frase 'o refreamento \xe9 virtude' (sa\u1e43varo s\u012bla\u1e43), o refreamento deve ser compreendido em cinco aspectos: refreamento pelo P\u0101timokkha, refreamento pela aten\xe7\xe3o plena (sati), refreamento pelo conhecimento (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), refreamento pela paci\xeancia (khanti) e refreamento pela energia (v\u012briya). Aqui, 'ele \xe9 dotado, plenamente dotado deste refreamento do P\u0101timokkha' \xe9 o refreamento pelo P\u0101timokkha. 'Ele protege a faculdade do olho, ele realiza o refreamento da faculdade do olho' \xe9 o refreamento pela aten\xe7\xe3o plena.",es:"Esta es la respuesta a esa pregunta: \xbfQu\xe9 es la virtud (s\u012bla)? Son los estados como la voluntad (cetan\u0101), etc., de quien se abstiene de matar seres vivos, etc., o de quien cumple con los deberes y las pr\xe1cticas (vatta-pa\u1e6dipatti). As\xed se ha dicho en el Pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101magga: '\xbfQu\xe9 es la virtud? La voluntad es virtud, el factor mental es virtud, el autocontrol es virtud, la no transgresi\xf3n es virtud'. All\xed, la virtud de la voluntad es la intenci\xf3n de quien se abstiene de matar seres, etc., o de quien cumple con sus deberes. La virtud como factor mental es la abstenci\xf3n (virati) de quien se aparta de matar seres, etc. O bien, la virtud de la voluntad son las siete voluntades de los caminos de la acci\xf3n (kammapatha) de quien abandona el matar seres, etc. La virtud como factor mental son los estados de no codicia (anabhijjh\u0101), no malevolencia (aby\u0101p\u0101da) y visi\xf3n correcta (samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi), descritos de esta manera: 'Habiendo abandonado la codicia, mora con la mente libre de codicia', etc. En cuanto a 'el autocontrol es virtud', aqu\xed el autocontrol (sa\u1e43vara) debe entenderse de cinco tipos: autocontrol del P\u0101timokkha, autocontrol de la atenci\xf3n (sati), autocontrol del conocimiento (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), autocontrol de la paciencia (khanti) y autocontrol de la energ\xeda (v\u012briya). De ellos, 'estar dotado y bien provisto de este autocontrol del P\u0101timokkha' es el autocontrol del P\u0101timokkha. 'Protege el sentido del ojo, logra el autocontrol en el sentido del ojo' es el autocontrol de la atenci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-1.7",pali:"Aya\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e43varo. Paccayapa\u1e6disevanampi ettheva samodh\u0101na\u1e43 gacchati. Yo pan\u0101ya\u1e43 khamo hoti s\u012btassa u\u1e47hass\u0101ti\u0101din\u0101 nayena \u0101gato, aya\u1e43 khantisa\u1e43varo n\u0101ma. Yo c\u0101ya\u1e43 uppanna\u1e43 k\u0101mavitakka\u1e43 n\u0101dhiv\u0101set\u012bti\u0101din\u0101 nayena \u0101gato, aya\u1e43 v\u012briyasa\u1e43varo n\u0101ma. \u0100j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhipi ettheva samodh\u0101na\u1e43 gacchati. Iti aya\u1e43 pa\xf1cavidhopi sa\u1e43varo, y\u0101 ca p\u0101pabh\u012bruk\u0101na\u1e43 kulaputt\u0101na\u1e43 sampattavatthuto virati, sabbampeta\u1e43 sa\u1e43varas\u012blanti veditabba\u1e43. Av\u012btikkamo s\u012blanti sam\u0101dinnas\u012blassa k\u0101yikav\u0101casiko anatikkamo. Ida\u1e43 t\u0101va ki\u1e43 s\u012blanti pa\xf1hassa vissajjana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"This is restraint by wisdom. Reflection on the use of requisites is also included right here. And that which comes by way of enduring cold and heat, and so forth (MN 1.24; AN 6.58), this is called restraint by patience. And that which comes by way of not tolerating an arisen sensual thought, and so forth (MN 1.26; AN 6.58), this is called restraint by energy. Purification of livelihood is also included right here. Thus, this fivefold restraint, and the abstinence concerning things encountered on the part of clansmen who are fearful of evil\u2014all this should be understood as the virtue of restraint. Non-transgression as virtue is the bodily and verbal non-transgression of one who has undertaken virtue. This, then, is the answer to the question, 'What is virtue?'",pt:"Este \xe9 o refreamento pelo conhecimento (\xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e43vara). O uso reflexivo dos requisitos tamb\xe9m est\xe1 inclu\xeddo neste refreamento pelo conhecimento. Aquele que \xe9 descrito na passagem: 'Ele \xe9 tolerante ao frio e ao calor', etc., \xe9 chamado de refreamento pela paci\xeancia (khantisa\u1e43vara). Aquele que \xe9 descrito na passagem: 'Ele n\xe3o tolera pensamentos sensuais que surgiram', etc., \xe9 chamado de refreamento pela energia (v\u012briyasa\u1e43vara). A purifica\xe7\xe3o dos meios de subsist\xeancia (\u0101j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhi) tamb\xe9m est\xe1 inclu\xedda neste refreamento pela energia. Assim, este refreamento de cinco tipos, juntamente com a abstin\xeancia (virati) dos filhos de boa fam\xedlia que temem o mal diante de objetos encontrados, tudo isso deve ser compreendido como 'virtude como refreamento' (sa\u1e43varas\u012bla). 'A n\xe3o transgress\xe3o \xe9 virtude' (av\u012btikkamo s\u012bla\u1e43) refere-se \xe0 n\xe3o transgress\xe3o f\xedsica e verbal de quem assumiu os preceitos. Esta \xe9, primeiramente, a resposta \xe0 pergunta 'O que \xe9 a virtude?'.",es:"Este es el autocontrol del conocimiento (\xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e43varo). El uso reflexivo de los requisitos (paccaya) tambi\xe9n se incluye en este. Aquel que es paciente ante el fr\xedo y el calor, etc., se llama autocontrol de la paciencia (khantisa\u1e43varo). Aquel que no tolera los pensamientos sensuales surgidos, etc., se llama autocontrol de la energ\xeda (v\u012briyasa\u1e43varo). La pureza del medio de vida (\u0101j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhi) tambi\xe9n se incluye aqu\xed. As\xed, estos cinco tipos de autocontrol, junto con la abstenci\xf3n (virati) de los hijos de buena familia temerosos del mal ante las situaciones que se presentan, todo ello debe entenderse como virtud de autocontrol. La no transgresi\xf3n como virtud es la no violaci\xf3n corporal y verbal de quien ha emprendido los preceptos. Esta es la respuesta a la pregunta: '\xbfQu\xe9 es la virtud?'."}},{id:"vism-1.8",pali:"Avasesesu kena\u1e6d\u1e6dhena s\u012blanti s\u012blana\u1e6d\u1e6dhena s\u012bla\u1e43. Kimida\u1e43 s\u012blana\u1e43 n\u0101ma. Sam\u0101dh\u0101na\u1e43 v\u0101, k\u0101yakamm\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 sus\u012blyavasena avippaki\u1e47\u1e47at\u0101ti attho. Upadh\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101, kusal\u0101na\u1e43 dhamm\u0101na\u1e43 pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101navasena \u0101dh\u0101rabh\u0101voti attho. Etadeva hettha atthadvaya\u1e43 saddalakkha\u1e47avid\u016b anuj\u0101nanti. A\xf1\xf1e pana sira\u1e6d\u1e6dho s\u012blattho, s\u012btala\u1e6d\u1e6dho s\u012blatthoti evam\u0101din\u0101pi nayenettha attha\u1e43 va\u1e47\u1e47ayanti.",translations:{en:"As for the remaining questions, in what sense is it virtue? It is virtue in the sense of composing (s\u012blana). What is this composing? It is either composure (sam\u0101dh\u0101na), meaning the non-dispersion of bodily actions and so forth by way of good conduct; or it is upholding (upadh\u0101ra\u1e47a), meaning the state of being a support by way of being a foundation for wholesome qualities. This indeed is the twofold meaning here that those skilled in the characteristics of words acknowledge. Others, however, explain the meaning here in such ways as: 'virtue has the meaning of head (chief),' 'virtue has the meaning of coolness,' and so on.",pt:"Dentre as perguntas restantes, 'Em que sentido \xe9 virtude (kena\u1e6d\u1e6dhena s\u012bla)?': \xc9 virtude no sentido de harmonizar (s\u012blana). O que \xe9 este harmonizar? \xc9 a coordena\xe7\xe3o (sam\u0101dh\u0101na), que significa a n\xe3o dispers\xe3o das a\xe7\xf5es corporais, etc., em raz\xe3o de uma boa conduta; ou \xe9 a sustenta\xe7\xe3o (upadh\u0101ra\u1e47a), que significa o estado de ser um fundamento para os dhammas ben\xe9ficos (kusala), servindo como suporte para eles. Apenas estes dois significados s\xe3o aceitos aqui pelos conhecedores da gram\xe1tica. Outros, por\xe9m, explicam o significado neste contexto de maneiras como: 'o sentido de cabe\xe7a (siras) \xe9 o significado de virtude', ou 'o sentido de frescor (s\u012btala) \xe9 o significado de virtude'.",es:"Respecto a las dem\xe1s preguntas: (b) '\xbfEn qu\xe9 sentido es virtud (s\u012bla)?', es virtud en el sentido de armonizar o fundamentar (s\u012blana). \xbfQu\xe9 es este armonizar? Es la composici\xf3n (sam\u0101dh\u0101na), es decir, el estado de no estar disperso en las acciones corporales y verbales debido a la buena conducta. O bien es el sost\xe9n (upadh\u0101ra\u1e47a), es decir, el estado de ser el fundamento donde se establecen los estados saludables. Solo estos dos sentidos son aceptados aqu\xed por los expertos en gram\xe1tica. Otros, sin embargo, explican el significado de virtud en el sentido de 'cabeza' (sira), o en el sentido de 'frescura' (s\u012btala), y as\xed sucesivamente."}},{id:"vism-1.9",pali:"S\u012blana\u1e43 lakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 tassa, bhinnass\u0101pi anekadh\u0101; Sanidassanatta\u1e43 r\u016bpassa, yath\u0101 bhinnassanekadh\u0101.",translations:{en:"Its characteristic is composing (s\u012blana), even when it is differentiated in many ways; just as being visible is for form, even when it is differentiated in many ways.",pt:"O harmonizar \xe9 a sua caracter\xedstica, embora ela seja de muitos tipos, assim como a visibilidade \xe9 a caracter\xedstica da forma (r\u016bpa), embora esta seja de muitos tipos.",es:"La armonizaci\xf3n es su caracter\xedstica, aunque la virtud sea de muchos tipos, as\xed como la visibilidad es la caracter\xedstica de la forma, aunque esta sea de muchos tipos."}},{id:"vism-1.10",pali:"Tasm\u0101 ida\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43 n\u0101ma kicca\u1e6d\u1e6dhena rasena duss\u012blyaviddha\u1e43sanarasa\u1e43, sampattiatthena rasena anavajjarasanti veditabba\u1e43. Lakkha\u1e47\u0101d\u012bsu hi kiccameva sampatti v\u0101 rasoti vuccati.",translations:{en:"Therefore, this virtue should be understood as having the function of destroying moral depravity in the sense of a task, and as having the function of being blameless in the sense of an accomplishment. For among characteristics and so forth, it is the task itself or the accomplishment that is called the function.",pt:"Portanto, esta virtude deve ser compreendida como tendo a destrui\xe7\xe3o da imoralidade como sua fun\xe7\xe3o no sentido de tarefa, e o ser irrepreens\xedvel como sua fun\xe7\xe3o no sentido de realiza\xe7\xe3o. Pois, nas explica\xe7\xf5es de caracter\xedsticas, etc., ou uma tarefa ou uma realiza\xe7\xe3o \xe9 chamada de 'fun\xe7\xe3o' (rasa).",es:"Por lo tanto, debe entenderse que esta virtud tiene la funci\xf3n de destruir la mala conducta en el sentido de tarea (kicca), y la funci\xf3n de ser irreprochable en el sentido de logro (sampatti). En las explicaciones de caracter\xedsticas, etc., tanto la tarea como el logro se denominan 'funci\xf3n' (rasa)."}},{id:"vism-1.11",pali:"Tayida\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43 k\u0101yasoceyya\u1e43 vac\u012bsoceyya\u1e43 manosoceyyanti eva\u1e43 vuttasoceyyapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, soceyyabh\u0101vena paccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti gaha\u1e47abh\u0101va\u1e43 gacchati. Hirottappa\xf1ca panassa vi\xf1\xf1\u016bhi pada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanti va\u1e47\u1e47ita\u1e43, \u0101sannak\u0101ra\u1e47anti attho. Hirottappe hi sati s\u012bla\u1e43 uppajjati ceva ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhati ca. Asati neva uppajjati, na ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhat\u012bti. Eva\u1e43 s\u012blassa lakkha\u1e47arasapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni veditabb\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"This virtue, as declared in terms of 'purity of body, purity of speech, and purity of mind' (AN 3.121), has purity as its manifestation; it manifests as a state of purity and thus becomes comprehensible. Furthermore, moral shame and moral dread are described by the wise as its proximate cause, meaning its immediate cause. For when moral shame and moral dread are present, virtue arises and endures. When they are absent, it neither arises nor endures. Thus, the characteristic, function, manifestation, and proximate cause of virtue should be understood.",pt:"Esta virtude tem a pureza como sua manifesta\xe7\xe3o, descrita como pureza do corpo, pureza da fala e pureza da mente; ela se manifesta como pureza e \xe9 percebida como tal. Al\xe9m disso, a vergonha moral e o temor moral (hir\u012b-ottappa) foram descritos pelos s\xe1bios como sua causa pr\xf3xima (pada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na), o que significa a causa imediata. Pois, quando a vergonha moral e o temor moral est\xe3o presentes, a virtude surge e persiste; quando est\xe3o ausentes, ela n\xe3o surge nem persiste. Assim devem ser compreendidos a caracter\xedstica, a fun\xe7\xe3o, a manifesta\xe7\xe3o e a causa pr\xf3xima da virtude.",es:"Esta virtud tiene como manifestaci\xf3n la pureza, descrita como 'pureza corporal, pureza verbal y pureza mental'; aparece bajo el aspecto de pureza en el conocimiento de quienes la observan. Adem\xe1s, los sabios han descrito la verg\xfcenza y el temor moral como su causa pr\xf3xima; 'causa pr\xf3xima' significa la causa inmediata. Pues cuando hay verg\xfcenza y temor moral, la virtud surge y permanece; cuando no los hay, ni surge ni permanece. As\xed deben entenderse la caracter\xedstica, la funci\xf3n, la manifestaci\xf3n y la causa pr\xf3xima de la virtud."}},{id:"vism-1.12",pali:"Kim\u0101nisa\u1e43sa\u1e43 s\u012blanti avippa\u1e6dis\u0101r\u0101dianekagu\u1e47apa\u1e6dil\u0101bh\u0101nisa\u1e43sa\u1e43. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 \u2013 \"avippa\u1e6dis\u0101ratth\u0101ni kho, \u0101nanda, kusal\u0101ni s\u012bl\u0101ni avippa\u1e6dis\u0101r\u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101n\u012b\"ti.",translations:{en:"What is the benefit of virtue? Its benefit is the acquisition of many qualities, beginning with freedom from remorse. For it was said: \u201c\u0100nanda, wholesome virtues have freedom from remorse as their aim and as their benefit\u201d (AN 11.1).",pt:"Quanto \xe0 pergunta 'Quais s\xe3o os benef\xedcios da virtude (kim\u0101nisa\u1e43sa\u1e43 s\u012bla)?': Seu benef\xedcio \xe9 a aquisi\xe7\xe3o de muitas qualidades, tais como a aus\xeancia de remorso (avippa\u1e6dis\u0101ra), etc. Pois foi dito: 'Ananda, as virtudes ben\xe9ficas t\xeam a aus\xeancia de remorso como seu prop\xf3sito, a aus\xeancia de remorso como seu benef\xedcio'.",es:"\xbfQu\xe9 beneficio tiene la virtud? Tiene como beneficio la obtenci\xf3n de muchas cualidades, como la ausencia de remordimiento, etc. Pues as\xed se ha dicho: '\u0100nanda, las virtudes saludables tienen como prop\xf3sito la ausencia de remordimiento y como beneficio la ausencia de remordimiento'."}},{id:"vism-1.13",pali:"Id\u0101ni ya\u1e43 vutta\u1e43 katividha\u1e43 ceta\u1e43 s\u012blanti, tatrida\u1e43 vissajjana\u1e43. Sabbameva t\u0101va ida\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43 attano s\u012blanalakkha\u1e47ena ekavidha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now, as to the question that was asked, 'Of how many kinds is this virtue?', this is the answer. In the first place, all this virtue is of one kind in that it has the characteristic of composing.",pt:"Agora, quanto \xe0 pergunta 'De quantos tipos \xe9 esta virtude (katividha\u1e43 ceta\u1e43 s\u012bla)?': Aqui est\xe1 a resposta. Primeiramente, toda virtude \xe9 de um \xfanico tipo em raz\xe3o de sua caracter\xedstica de harmonizar (s\u012blana).",es:"Ahora, en cuanto a lo que se dijo: '\xbfDe cu\xe1ntas clases es la virtud?', he aqu\xed la respuesta. En primer lugar, toda esta virtud es de una sola clase por su caracter\xedstica de conducta \xe9tica (s\u012blana)."}},{id:"vism-1.14",pali:"C\u0101rittav\u0101rittavasena duvidha\u1e43. Tath\u0101 \u0101bhisam\u0101c\u0101rika\u0101dibrahmacariyakavasena, viratiavirativasena, nissit\u0101nissitavasena, k\u0101lapariyanta\u0101p\u0101\u1e47ako\u1e6dikavasena, sapariyant\u0101pariyantavasena, lokiyalokuttaravasena ca.",translations:{en:"It is twofold by way of observance and avoidance. Likewise, it is twofold by way of good conduct and the fundamentals of the holy life; by way of abstinence and non-abstinence; by way of being dependent and independent; by way of being limited by time and for life; by way of having a limit and being limitless; and by way of being mundane and supramundane.",pt:"Ela \xe9 de dois tipos como: conduta de a\xe7\xe3o (c\u0101ritta) e conduta de absten\xe7\xe3o (v\u0101ritta). Da mesma forma, como: de bom comportamento (\u0101bhisam\u0101c\u0101rika) e do in\xedcio da vida santa (\u0101dibrahmacariyaka); como abstin\xeancia (virati) e n\xe3o abstin\xeancia (avirati); como dependente (nissita) e independente (anissita); como tempor\xe1ria (k\u0101lapariyanta) e vital\xedcia (\u0101p\u0101\u1e47ako\u1e6dika); como limitada (sapariyanta) e ilimitada (apariyanta); e como mundana (lokiya) e supramundana (lokuttara).",es:"Es de dos clases seg\xfan el cumplimiento (c\u0101ritta) y la evitaci\xf3n (v\u0101ritta). Asimismo, seg\xfan la conducta menor (\u0101bhisam\u0101c\u0101rika) y la conducta esencial para la vida santa (\u0101dibrahmacariyaka), seg\xfan la abstenci\xf3n y la no abstenci\xf3n, seg\xfan lo dependiente y lo independiente, seg\xfan lo limitado en el tiempo y lo que dura hasta el fin de la vida, seg\xfan lo finito y lo infinito, y seg\xfan lo mundano y lo supramundano."}},{id:"vism-1.15",pali:"Tividha\u1e43 h\u012bnamajjhimapa\u1e47\u012btavasena. Tath\u0101 att\u0101dhipateyyalok\u0101dhipateyyadhamm\u0101dhipateyyavasena, par\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101par\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dhapa\u1e6dippassaddhivasena, visuddh\u0101visuddhavematikavasena, sekkh\u0101sekkhanevasekkhan\u0101sekkhavasena ca.",translations:{en:"It is threefold by way of being inferior, middling, and excellent. Likewise, it is threefold by way of self-sovereignty, world-sovereignty, and Dhamma-sovereignty; by way of being clung to, not clung to, and tranquillized; by way of being pure, impure, and doubtful; and by way of being that of a trainee, an adept, and one who is neither a trainee nor an adept.",pt:"Ela \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos como: inferior, m\xe9dia e superior. Da mesma forma, como: governada por si mesmo (att\u0101dhipateyya), governada pelo mundo (lok\u0101dhipateyya) e governada pelo Dhamma (dhamm\u0101dhipateyya); como apegada (par\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dha), n\xe3o apegada (apar\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dha) e pacificada (pa\u1e6dippassaddhi); como pura, impura e duvidosa; e como do aprendiz (sekkha), do mestre (asekha) e de quem n\xe3o \xe9 aprendiz nem mestre.",es:"Es de tres clases seg\xfan lo inferior, lo medio y lo superior. Asimismo, seg\xfan la predominancia de uno mismo, la predominancia del mundo y la predominancia del Dhamma; seg\xfan lo que es mal interpretado, lo no mal interpretado y lo apaciguado; seg\xfan lo puro, lo impuro y lo dudoso; y seg\xfan la virtud del que est\xe1 en formaci\xf3n (sekkha), la del que ya no est\xe1 en formaci\xf3n (asekkha) y la del que no es ninguno de los dos."}},{id:"vism-1.16",pali:"Catubbidha\u1e43 h\u0101nabh\u0101giya\u1e6dhitibh\u0101giyavisesabh\u0101giyanibbedhabh\u0101giyavasena. Tath\u0101 bhikkhubhikkhun\u012banupasampannagaha\u1e6d\u1e6dhas\u012blavasena, pakati\u0101c\u0101radhammat\u0101pubbahetukas\u012blavasena, p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varaindriyasa\u1e43vara\u0101j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhipaccayasannissitas\u012blavasena ca.",translations:{en:"It is fourfold by way of partaking in decline, in stagnation, in distinction, and in penetration. Likewise, it is fourfold by way of the virtue of monks, of nuns, of those not yet fully ordained, and of householders; by way of natural virtue, customary virtue, virtue as a natural law, and virtue rooted in a past cause; and by way of the restraint of the P\u0101timokkha, the restraint of the sense faculties, the purification of livelihood, and the virtue concerning the requisites.",pt:"Ela \xe9 de quatro tipos como: aquela que leva ao decl\xednio, aquela que leva \xe0 estagna\xe7\xe3o, aquela que leva \xe0 distin\xe7\xe3o e aquela que leva \xe0 penetra\xe7\xe3o. Da mesma forma, como: virtude de um monge, de uma monja, de um n\xe3o ordenado e de um chefe de fam\xedlia; como virtude natural, virtude costumeira, virtude necess\xe1ria e virtude decorrente de causas passadas; e como refreamento do P\u0101timokkha, refreamento das faculdades sensoriais, purifica\xe7\xe3o dos meios de subsist\xeancia e virtude relativa aos requisitos.",es:"Es de cuatro clases seg\xfan lo que conduce al declive, a la estabilidad, a la distinci\xf3n y a la penetraci\xf3n. Asimismo, seg\xfan la virtud de los monjes, de las monjas, de los no ordenados y de los laicos; seg\xfan la virtud natural, la de las costumbres, la de la naturaleza de las cosas y la debida a causas previas; y seg\xfan la virtud del autocontrol del P\u0101timokkha, del control de los sentidos, de la pureza del medio de vida y la relacionada con el uso de los requisitos."}},{id:"vism-1.17",pali:"Catutthacatukke ya\u1e43 bhagavat\u0101 \"idha bhikkhu p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varasa\u1e43vuto viharati \u0101c\u0101ragocarasampanno a\u1e47umattesu vajjesu bhayadass\u0101v\u012b sam\u0101d\u0101ya sikkhati sikkh\u0101pades\u016b\"ti va\u1e43 vutta\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43, ida\u1e43 p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varas\u012bla\u1e43 n\u0101ma. Ya\u1e43 pana \"so cakkhun\u0101 r\u016bpa\u1e43 disv\u0101 na nimittagg\u0101h\u012b hoti n\u0101nubya\xf1janagg\u0101h\u012b, yatv\u0101dhikara\u1e47amena\u1e43 cakkhundriya\u1e43 asa\u1e43vuta\u1e43 viharanta\u1e43 abhijjh\u0101domanass\u0101 p\u0101pak\u0101 akusal\u0101 dhamm\u0101 anv\u0101ssaveyyu\u1e43, tassa sa\u1e43var\u0101ya pa\u1e6dipajjati, rakkhati cakkhundriya\u1e43, cakkhundriye sa\u1e43vara\u1e43 \u0101pajjati. Sotena sadda\u1e43 sutv\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 gh\u0101nena gandha\u1e43 gh\u0101yitv\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 jivh\u0101ya rasa\u1e43 s\u0101yitv\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 k\u0101yena pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43 phusitv\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 manas\u0101 dhamma\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101ya na nimittagg\u0101h\u012b\u2026pe\u2026 manindriye sa\u1e43vara\u1e43 \u0101pajjat\u012b\"ti vutta\u1e43, ida\u1e43 indriyasa\u1e43varas\u012bla\u1e43. Y\u0101 pana \u0101j\u012bvahetupa\xf1\xf1att\u0101na\u1e43 channa\u1e43 sikkh\u0101pad\u0101na\u1e43 v\u012btikkamassa, \"kuhan\u0101 lapan\u0101 nemittikat\u0101 nippesikat\u0101 l\u0101bhena l\u0101bha\u1e43 nijig\u012bsanat\u0101\"ti evam\u0101d\u012bna\xf1ca p\u0101padhamm\u0101na\u1e43 vasena pavatt\u0101 micch\u0101j\u012bv\u0101 virati, ida\u1e43 \u0101j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhis\u012bla\u1e43. \"Pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101 yoniso c\u012bvara\u1e43 pa\u1e6disevati, y\u0101vadeva s\u012btassa pa\u1e6digh\u0101t\u0101y\u0101\"ti \u0101din\u0101 nayena vutto pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101naparisuddho catupaccayaparibhogo paccayasannissitas\u012bla\u1e43 n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"In the fourth tetrad, the virtue spoken of by the Blessed One thus: \"Here, a bhikkhu dwells restrained by the restraint of the P\u0101timokkha, accomplished in conduct and resort, seeing danger in the slightest faults, and undertaking to train in the training rules\"\u2014this is called the virtue of P\u0101timokkha restraint. That which is spoken of thus: \"Having seen a form with the eye, he does not grasp at its signs or features. Since, if he were to dwell with the eye faculty unrestrained, evil unwholesome states of covetousness and grief might assail him, he practices for its restraint, guards the eye faculty, and undertakes restraint of the eye faculty. Having heard a sound with the ear\u2026 Having smelled an odor with the nose\u2026 Having tasted a flavor with the tongue\u2026 Having felt a tactile sensation with the body\u2026 Having cognized a mental object with the mind, he does not grasp at its signs or features\u2026 he undertakes restraint of the mind faculty\"\u2014this is called the virtue of sense-faculty restraint. Furthermore, the abstinence from wrong livelihood, which proceeds by way of the transgression of the six training rules laid down concerning livelihood, and by way of evil states such as hypocrisy, babbling, hinting, belittling, and pursuing gain with gain\u2014this is called the virtue of purity of livelihood. The use of the four requisites, purified by reflection, as stated in the manner: \"Reflecting wisely, he uses robes only for the purpose of warding off cold\"\u2014this is called the virtue dependent on the requisites.",pt:"Na quarta t\xe9trade, a moralidade descrita pelo Aben\xe7oado como: 'Aqui, um monge vive contido pela conten\xe7\xe3o do P\u0101timokkha, dotado de conduta e local de busca adequados, vendo perigo mesmo nas menores falhas, assumindo e treinando-se nas regras de treinamento', \xe9 chamada de moralidade de conten\xe7\xe3o do P\u0101timokkha (p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43vara-s\u012bla). Aquela descrita como: 'Tendo visto uma forma com os olhos, ele n\xe3o se apega aos seus sinais gerais nem aos seus detalhes secund\xe1rios. Visto que, se ele vivesse deixando a faculdade do olho desprotegida, dhammas prejudiciais e ruins de cobi\xe7a e descontentamento poderiam invadi-lo, ele se aplica \xe0 sua conten\xe7\xe3o, protege a faculdade do olho e alcan\xe7a a conten\xe7\xe3o na faculdade do olho. Tendo ouvido um som com o ouvido... tendo cheirado um odor com o nariz... tendo provado um sabor com a l\xedngua... tendo tocado um objeto tang\xedvel com o corpo... tendo conhecido um dhamma mental com a mente, ele n\xe3o se apega aos seus sinais gerais... ele alcan\xe7a a conten\xe7\xe3o na faculdade da mente', \xe9 chamada de moralidade de conten\xe7\xe3o das faculdades sensoriais (indriyasa\u1e43vara-s\u012bla). A absten\xe7\xe3o do meio de vida incorreto que ocorre atrav\xe9s da transgress\xe3o das seis regras de treinamento promulgadas por causa do meio de vida, e atrav\xe9s de dhammas prejudiciais como 'hipocrisia, bajula\xe7\xe3o, insinua\xe7\xe3o, deprecia\xe7\xe3o e busca de ganho com ganho', \xe9 chamada de moralidade de pureza do meio de vida (\u0101j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhi-s\u012bla). O uso dos quatro requisitos purificado pela reflex\xe3o s\xe1bia, descrito pelo m\xe9todo que come\xe7a com: 'Refletindo sabiamente, ele usa o manto apenas para se proteger do frio...', \xe9 chamado de moralidade baseada nos requisitos (paccayasannissita-s\u012bla).",es:"En el cuarto cuarteto, la virtud descrita por el Bendito de esta manera: \xabAqu\xed, un monje vive restringido por la restricci\xf3n del P\u0101timokkha, dotado de buena conducta y lugar de recurso, viendo peligro incluso en las faltas m\xe1s peque\xf1as, se entrena asumiendo los preceptos de entrenamiento\xbb, se llama virtud de restricci\xf3n del P\u0101timokkha. Aquella descrita como: \xab\xc9l, habiendo visto una forma con el ojo, no se aferra a sus signos generales ni a sus detalles secundarios; puesto que, si viviera con la facultad del ojo sin restricci\xf3n, podr\xedan invadirlo estados malvados y perjudiciales como la codicia y el pesar, se aplica a su restricci\xf3n, protege la facultad del ojo y alcanza la restricci\xf3n en la facultad del ojo. Habiendo escuchado un sonido con el o\xeddo... habiendo olido un aroma con la nariz... habiendo saboreado un sabor con la lengua... habiendo tocado un objeto tangible con el cuerpo... habiendo conocido un fealidade con la mente, no se aferra a sus signos generales... alcanza la restricci\xf3n en la facultad de la mente\xbb, es la virtud de restricci\xf3n de los sentidos (indriyasa\u1e43varas\u012bla). La abstenci\xf3n del medio de vida incorrecto que ocurre mediante la transgresi\xf3n de los seis preceptos prescritos por causa del sustento, y de estados malvados como \xabel enga\xf1o, la lisonja, la insinuaci\xf3n, la extorsi\xf3n y la b\xfasqueda de ganancias mediante ganancias\xbb, es la virtud de la pureza del medio de vida (\u0101j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhis\u012bla). El uso de los cuatro requisitos purificado por la reflexi\xf3n, descrito mediante el m\xe9todo: \xabReflexionando sabiamente, utiliza el manto, solo para protegerse del fr\xedo...\xbb, se llama virtud relacionada con los requisitos (paccayasannissitas\u012bla)."}},{id:"vism-1.18",pali:"Tatr\u0101ya\u1e43 \u0101dito pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya anupubbapadava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101ya saddhi\u1e43 vinicchayakath\u0101. Idh\u0101ti imasmi\u1e43 s\u0101sane. Bhikkh\u016bti sa\u1e43s\u0101re bhaya\u1e43 ikkha\u1e47at\u0101ya v\u0101 bhinnapa\u1e6dadhar\u0101dit\u0101ya v\u0101 eva\u1e43 laddhavoh\u0101ro saddh\u0101pabbajito kulaputto. P\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varasa\u1e43vutoti ettha p\u0101timokkhanti sikkh\u0101padas\u012bla\u1e43. Ta\xf1hi yo na\u1e43 p\u0101ti rakkhati, ta\u1e43 mokkheti mocayati \u0101p\u0101yik\u0101d\u012bhi dukkhehi, tasm\u0101 p\u0101timokkhanti vuccati. Sa\u1e43vara\u1e47a\u1e43 sa\u1e43varo, k\u0101yikav\u0101casikassa av\u012btikkamasseta\u1e43 n\u0101ma\u1e43. P\u0101timokkhameva sa\u1e43varo p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varo. Tena p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varena sa\u1e43vuto p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varasa\u1e43vuto, upagato samann\u0101gatoti attho. Viharat\u012bti iriyati. \u0100c\u0101ragocarasampannoti\u0101d\u012bnamattho p\u0101\u1e37iya\u1e43 \u0101gatanayeneva veditabbo. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"Herein, starting from the beginning, is the discourse of analysis together with the word-by-word explanation. Idha: In this Dispensation. Bhikkhu: A son of a good family who has gone forth out of faith, thus designated because he perceives fear in the round of existence or because he wears torn cloths and so on. P\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varasa\u1e43vuto: Here, P\u0101timokkha refers to the virtue of the training rules. For it protects (p\u0101ti) one who observes it, and it liberates (mokkheti) and frees them from sufferings such as those of the lower realms; therefore, it is called P\u0101timokkha. Sa\u1e43vara\u1e47a\u1e43 sa\u1e43varo: Restraint is the name for non-transgression in bodily and verbal actions. The P\u0101timokkha itself is restraint; this is P\u0101timokkha restraint. Tena p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varena sa\u1e43vuto p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varasa\u1e43vuto: One who is restrained by this P\u0101timokkha restraint, meaning he has approached and is endowed with it. Viharat\u012bti: He dwells, he conducts himself. \u0100c\u0101ragocarasampannoti\u0101d\u012bnamattho: The meaning of terms beginning with 'accomplished in conduct and resort' should be understood according to the method given in the P\u0101li text itself. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43: For this has been said:",pt:"Aqui, a partir do in\xedcio, segue-se a discuss\xe3o anal\xedtica junto com a explica\xe7\xe3o sucessiva das palavras. 'Aqui' (idha) significa nesta Dispensa\xe7\xe3o. 'Monge' (bhikkhu) \xe9 o filho de boa fam\xedlia que se ordenou por f\xe9, que obteve essa designa\xe7\xe3o por ver o perigo no ciclo de exist\xeancias (sa\u1e43s\u0101re bhaya\u1e43 ikkha\u1e47at\u0101ya) ou por usar mantos remendados, etc. Na express\xe3o 'contido pela conten\xe7\xe3o do P\u0101timokkha' (p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varasa\u1e43vuto), 'P\u0101timokkha' refere-se \xe0 moralidade das regras de treinamento. Pois ela liberta (mokkheti) aquele que a protege (p\u0101ti) dos sofrimentos dos dhammas de priva\xe7\xe3o, etc.; por isso, \xe9 chamada de P\u0101timokkha. 'Conten\xe7\xe3o' (sa\u1e43vara) significa o ato de conter; este \xe9 o nome para a n\xe3o transgress\xe3o corporal e verbal. O pr\xf3prio P\u0101timokkha \xe9 a conten\xe7\xe3o; da\xed 'conten\xe7\xe3o do P\u0101timokkha'. 'Contido pela conten\xe7\xe3o do P\u0101timokkha' significa aquele que alcan\xe7ou ou est\xe1 dotado de tal conten\xe7\xe3o do P\u0101timokkha. 'Vive' (viharati) significa que ele conduz sua exist\xeancia. O significado de 'dotado de conduta e local de busca adequados' (\u0101c\u0101ragocarasampanno), etc., deve ser compreendido exatamente pelo m\xe9todo que consta no texto can\xf4nico. Pois foi dito:",es:"En este contexto, empezando desde el principio, esta es la exposici\xf3n de la determinaci\xf3n junto con la explicaci\xf3n palabra por palabra en orden. \xabAqu\xed\xbb (idha) significa en esta Dispensaci\xf3n. \xabMonje\xbb (bhikkhu) es el hijo de familia que se ha ordenado por fe y ha recibido este nombre, ya sea por ver el peligro en el ciclo de nacimientos (sa\u1e43s\u0101ra) o por vestir mantos de trapos remendados, etc. En la expresi\xf3n \xabp\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varasa\u1e43vuto\xbb, \xabP\u0101timokkha\xbb es la virtud de los preceptos de entrenamiento. Pues a aquel que lo protege (p\u0101ti), a ese lo libera (mokkheti) de los sufrimientos de los estados de privaci\xf3n y otros; por eso se llama P\u0101timokkha. \xabRestricci\xf3n\xbb (sa\u1e43vara) significa cerramiento; es el nombre para la no transgresi\xf3n f\xedsica y verbal. El P\u0101timokkha mismo es la restricci\xf3n, por tanto, \xabrestricci\xf3n del P\u0101timokkha\xbb. Estar \xabrestringido por la restricci\xf3n del P\u0101timokkha\xbb significa que ha accedido a ella o que est\xe1 dotado de ella. \xabVive\xbb (viharati) significa que mantiene su existencia. El significado de \xabdotado de buena conducta y lugar de recurso\xbb y dem\xe1s debe entenderse seg\xfan el m\xe9todo que aparece en el texto can\xf3nico. Pues se ha dicho:"}},{id:"vism-1.19",pali:"Ya\u1e43 paneta\u1e43 tadanantara\u1e43 \"so cakkhun\u0101 r\u016bpa\u1e43 disv\u0101\"ti\u0101din\u0101 nayena dassita\u1e43 indriyasa\u1e43varas\u012bla\u1e43, tattha soti p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varas\u012ble \u1e6dhito bhikkhu. Cakkhun\u0101 r\u016bpa\u1e43 disv\u0101ti k\u0101ra\u1e47avasena cakkh\u016bti laddhavoh\u0101rena r\u016bpadassanasamatthena cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena r\u016bpa\u1e43 disv\u0101. Por\u0101\u1e47\u0101 pan\u0101hu \"cakkhu r\u016bpa\u1e43 na passati, acittakatt\u0101, citta\u1e43 na passati, acakkhukatt\u0101, dv\u0101r\u0101ramma\u1e47asa\u1e45gha\u1e6d\u1e6de pana cakkhupas\u0101davatthukena cittena passati. \u012adis\u012b panes\u0101 \u2018dhanun\u0101 vijjhat\u012b\u2019ti\u0101d\u012bsu viya sasambh\u0101rakath\u0101 n\u0101ma hoti, tasm\u0101 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena r\u016bpa\u1e43 disv\u0101ti ayamevettha attho\"ti. Na nimittagg\u0101h\u012bti itthipurisanimitta\u1e43 v\u0101 subhanimitt\u0101dika\u1e43 v\u0101 kilesavatthubh\u016bta\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 na ga\u1e47h\u0101ti, di\u1e6d\u1e6dhamatteyeva sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101ti. N\u0101nubya\xf1janagg\u0101h\u012bti kiles\u0101na\u1e43 anuanubya\xf1janato p\u0101ka\u1e6dabh\u0101vakara\u1e47ato anubya\xf1jananti laddhavoh\u0101ra\u1e43 hatthap\u0101dasitahasitakathitavilokit\u0101dibheda\u1e43 \u0101k\u0101ra\u1e43 na ga\u1e47h\u0101ti, ya\u1e43 tattha bh\u016bta\u1e43, tadeva ga\u1e47h\u0101ti, cetiyapabbatav\u0101s\u012b mah\u0101tissatthero viya.",translations:{en:"Now, as for the virtue of sense-restraint shown immediately thereafter by the method beginning with \u2018he, having seen a form with the eye,\u2019 therein, \u2018he\u2019 is the monk established in the virtue of P\u0101timokkha-restraint. \u2018Having seen a form with the eye\u2019 means having seen a form with eye-consciousness, which is capable of seeing a form and is conventionally called \u2018the eye\u2019 because it is the instrument. The ancients, however, said: \u2018The eye does not see a form, for it is without a mind; the mind does not see, for it is without an eye. Rather, upon the collision of the sense-door and the object, the mind, based on the eye-sensitivity, sees. This is what is called a statement including the apparatus, like the expression \u2018he shoots with a bow.\u2019 Therefore, the meaning here is precisely \u2018one sees a form with eye-consciousness.\u2019 \u2018He is not a grasper of the sign\u2019 means he does not grasp a sign that is a basis for defilements\u2014such as the sign of a woman or a man, or a beautiful sign\u2014but stands fast at the mere sight. \u2018He is not a grasper of the features\u2019 means he does not grasp the particular features\u2014such as the hand, foot, smiling, laughing, speaking, or glancing\u2014which are conventionally called \u2018features\u2019 because they make defilements manifest again and again. He grasps only what is actually there, like the Elder Mah\u0101tissa, the dweller of Cetiyapabbata.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 virtude da restri\xe7\xe3o das faculdades dos sentidos, que \xe9 mostrada imediatamente a seguir pelo m\xe9todo que come\xe7a com 'ele, tendo visto uma forma com o olho', ali, 'ele' (so) refere-se ao monge estabelecido na virtude da restri\xe7\xe3o do P\u0101timokkha. 'Tendo visto uma forma com o olho' significa ter visto uma forma com a consci\xeancia visual (cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), que \xe9 capaz de ver formas e recebe o nome de 'olho' (cakkhu) em virtude de ser a causa instrumental. Os antigos, por\xe9m, disseram: 'O olho n\xe3o v\xea a forma, por ser desprovido de mente; a mente n\xe3o v\xea, por ser desprovida de olho; mas quando h\xe1 o impacto entre a porta e o objeto, v\xea-se com a mente que tem a sensibilidade ocular (cakkhupas\u0101da) como base f\xedsica. Tal express\xe3o \xe9 uma figura de linguagem que inclui os fatores instrumentais (sasambh\u0101rakath\u0101), como na frase 'ele atira com o arco'; portanto, o significado aqui \xe9 simplesmente 'tendo visto uma forma com a consci\xeancia visual'. 'Ele n\xe3o se apega aos sinais gerais' (na nimittagg\u0101h\u012b) significa que ele n\xe3o apreende o sinal de mulher ou de homem, ou o sinal de beleza (subhanimitta), etc., que servem de base para as defilezas (kilesa), mas permanece apenas no que \xe9 visto. 'Ele n\xe3o se apega aos detalhes secund\xe1rios' (n\u0101nubya\xf1janagg\u0101h\u012b) significa que ele n\xe3o apreende os detalhes que recebem o nome de 'detalhes secund\xe1rios' (anubya\xf1jana) por fazerem com que as defilezas se manifestem repetidamente, tais como as m\xe3os, os p\xe9s, o sorriso, o riso, a fala, o olhar para frente, o olhar para os lados, etc.; ele apreende apenas o que realmente est\xe1 ali, assim como o Anci\xe3o Mah\u0101tissa, que vivia na Montanha do Santu\xe1rio (Cetiyapabbata).",es:"Adem\xe1s, respecto a esta virtud del refrenamiento de los sentidos (indriyasa\u1e43varas\u012bla) que se muestra a continuaci\xf3n mediante el m\xe9todo que comienza con '\xe9l, viendo una forma con el ojo', en este contexto, '\xe9l' (so) se refiere al monje que est\xe1 establecido en la virtud del refrenamiento del Patimokkha. 'Viendo una forma con el ojo' significa ver una forma con la conciencia visual que es capaz de ver formas y que recibe el nombre de 'ojo' debido a su causa. Los antiguos maestros dec\xedan: 'El ojo no ve las formas porque carece de mente; la mente no ve porque carece de ojo. Pero cuando ocurre el impacto entre la puerta y el objeto, uno ve a trav\xe9s de la mente que tiene como base la sensibilidad ocular (cakkhupas\u0101da)'. Esta es una expresi\xf3n basada en sus componentes (sasambh\u0101rakath\u0101), similar a decir 'dispara con el arco'; por lo tanto, el significado aqu\xed es simplemente 'viendo una forma con la conciencia visual'. 'No captar las se\xf1ales' (na nimittagg\u0101h\u012b) significa que no toma la se\xf1al de mujer o de hombre, ni la se\xf1al de lo bello ni ninguna otra se\xf1al que sea base para las impurezas (kilesas), sino que se detiene \xfanicamente en lo que es visto. 'No captar los detalles' (n\u0101nubya\xf1janagg\u0101h\u012b) significa que no toma los rasgos secundarios que, al manifestarse repetidamente, provocan el surgimiento de las impurezas, tales como las manos, los pies, la sonrisa, el habla, la mirada directa o la mirada de soslayo; solo toma aquello que es real en ese objeto (como los elementos o la impureza del cuerpo), tal como el anciano Mah\u0101tissa, que resid\xeda en Cetiyapabbata."}},{id:"vism-1.20",pali:"Id\u0101ni indriyasa\u1e43varas\u012bl\u0101nantara\u1e43 vutte \u0101j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhis\u012ble \u0101j\u012bvahetu pa\xf1\xf1att\u0101na\u1e43 channa\u1e43 sikkh\u0101pad\u0101nanti y\u0101ni t\u0101ni \"\u0101j\u012bvahetu \u0101j\u012bvak\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 p\u0101piccho icch\u0101pakato asanta\u1e43 abh\u016bta\u1e43 uttarimanussadhamma\u1e43 ullapati, \u0101patti p\u0101r\u0101jikassa. \u0100j\u012bvahetu \u0101j\u012bvak\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 sa\xf1caritta\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjati, \u0101patti sa\u1e45gh\u0101disesassa. \u0100j\u012bvahetu \u0101j\u012bvak\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 \u2018yo te vih\u0101re vasati so bhikkhu arah\u0101\u2019ti bha\u1e47ati, pa\u1e6divij\u0101nantassa \u0101patti thullaccayassa. \u0100j\u012bvahetu \u0101j\u012bvak\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 bhikkhu pa\u1e47\u012btabhojan\u0101ni agil\u0101no attano atth\u0101ya vi\xf1\xf1\u0101petv\u0101 bhu\xf1jati, \u0101patti p\u0101cittiyassa. \u0100j\u012bvahetu \u0101j\u012bvak\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 bhikkhun\u012b pa\u1e47\u012btabhojan\u0101ni agil\u0101n\u0101 attano atth\u0101ya vi\xf1\xf1\u0101petv\u0101 bhu\xf1jati, \u0101patti p\u0101\u1e6didesan\u012byassa. \u0100j\u012bvahetu \u0101j\u012bvak\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 s\u016bpa\u1e43 v\u0101 odana\u1e43 v\u0101 agil\u0101no attano atth\u0101ya vi\xf1\xf1\u0101petv\u0101 bhu\xf1jati, \u0101patti dukka\u1e6dass\u0101\"ti eva\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1att\u0101ni cha sikkh\u0101pad\u0101ni, imesa\u1e43 channa\u1e43 sikkh\u0101pad\u0101na\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now, in the virtue of purity of livelihood, which was stated after the virtue of restraint of the sense faculties, [this is the explanation] of the six training rules laid down for the sake of livelihood. The six training rules laid down are as follows: (1) 'For the sake of livelihood, for the reason of livelihood, being of evil desires and overcome by desire, if one boasts of a non-existent, unreal superhuman quality, it is an offense of defeat. (2) For the sake of livelihood, for the reason of livelihood, if one engages in matchmaking, it is an offense entailing an initial and subsequent meeting of the Sangha. (3) For the sake of livelihood, for the reason of livelihood, if one says, \u201cThe monk living in your monastery is an arahant,\u201d and the other person understands, it is a grave offense. (4) For the sake of livelihood, for the reason of livelihood, if a monk who is not ill, having requested choice foods for his own sake, consumes them, it is an offense requiring expiation. (5) For the sake of livelihood, for the reason of livelihood, if a nun who is not ill, having requested choice foods for her own sake, consumes them, it is an offense requiring confession. (6) For the sake of livelihood, for the reason of livelihood, if one who is not ill, having requested curry or boiled rice for one's own sake, consumes it, it is an offense of wrong-doing.' These are the six training rules thus laid down.",pt:"Agora, em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 virtude da purifica\xe7\xe3o dos meios de vida, mencionada imediatamente ap\xf3s a virtude da conten\xe7\xe3o das faculdades, a express\xe3o 'seis regras de treinamento estabelecidas por causa dos meios de vida' refere-se \xe0quelas seis regras de treinamento estabelecidas da seguinte forma: 'Por causa dos meios de vida, por motivo de subsist\xeancia, algu\xe9m de maus desejos, dominado pela cobi\xe7a, alega falsamente um estado sobre-humano (uttarimanussadhamma) inexistente e falso \u2014 h\xe1 uma ofensa de derrota (p\u0101r\u0101jika). Por causa dos meios de vida, por motivo de subsist\xeancia, algu\xe9m atua como intermedi\xe1rio (sa\xf1caritta) \u2014 h\xe1 uma ofensa que requer uma assembleia da Comunidade (sa\u1e45gh\u0101disesa). Por causa dos meios de vida, por motivo de subsist\xeancia, algu\xe9m diz: \"O bhikkhu que vive em seu mosteiro \xe9 um arahant\" \u2014 se o ouvinte compreender, h\xe1 uma ofensa grave (thullaccaya). Por causa dos meios de vida, por motivo de subsist\xeancia, um bhikkhu que n\xe3o est\xe1 doente solicita alimentos finos para seu pr\xf3prio benef\xedcio e os consome \u2014 h\xe1 uma ofensa de expia\xe7\xe3o (p\u0101cittiya). Por causa dos meios de vida, por motivo de subsist\xeancia, uma bhikkhun\u012b que n\xe3o est\xe1 doente solicita alimentos finos para seu pr\xf3prio benef\xedcio e os consome \u2014 h\xe1 uma ofensa que requer confiss\xe3o (p\u0101\u1e6didesan\u012bya). Por causa dos meios de vida, por motivo de subsist\xeancia, um bhikkhu que n\xe3o est\xe1 doente solicita sopa ou arroz para seu pr\xf3prio benef\xedcio e os consome \u2014 h\xe1 uma ofensa de conduta impr\xf3pria (dukka\u1e6da)'. Essas s\xe3o as seis regras de treinamento estabelecidas.",es:"Ahora, a continuaci\xf3n de la conducta \xe9tica de la restricci\xf3n de las facultades (indriyasa\u1e43varas\u012bla), con respecto a la conducta \xe9tica de la pureza de los medios de vida (\u0101j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhis\u012bla), se presentan los seis preceptos establecidos por causa de los medios de vida: (1) \u2018Si por causa de los medios de vida, por motivo de la subsistencia, un monje de deseos malvados y abrumado por la codicia, proclama falsamente un estado humano superior (jh\u0101na, magga o phala) que no posee, incurre en una ofensa de derrota (p\u0101r\u0101jika). (2) Si por motivo de la subsistencia act\xfaa como intermediario (en asuntos de hombres y mujeres), incurre en una ofensa de suspensi\xf3n formal (sa\u1e45gh\u0101disesa). (3) Si por motivo de la subsistencia dice: \u201cAquel que vive en tu monasterio es un arahant\u201d (refiri\xe9ndose a s\xed mismo), si el interlocutor lo comprende, incurre en una ofensa grave (thullaccaya). (4) Si por motivo de la subsistencia, un monje que no est\xe1 enfermo solicita y come alimentos exquisitos para su propio beneficio, incurre en una ofensa que requiere confesi\xf3n (p\u0101cittiya). (5) Si por motivo de la subsistencia, una monja que no est\xe1 enferma solicita y come alimentos exquisitos para su propio beneficio, incurre en una ofensa que debe ser reconocida (p\u0101\u1e6didesan\u012bya). (6) Si por motivo de la subsistencia, un monje que no est\xe1 enfermo solicita y come curry o arroz para su propio beneficio, incurre en una ofensa de mala conducta (dukka\u1e6da)\u2019. Estos son los seis preceptos as\xed establecidos."}},{id:"vism-1.21",pali:"Ya\u1e43 paneta\u1e43 tadanantara\u1e43 paccayasannissitas\u012bla\u1e43 vutta\u1e43, tattha pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101 yonisoti up\u0101yena pathena pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101ya \xf1atv\u0101, paccavekkhitv\u0101ti attho. Ettha ca s\u012btassa pa\u1e6digh\u0101t\u0101y\u0101ti\u0101din\u0101 nayena vuttapaccavekkha\u1e47ameva \"yoniso pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101\"ti veditabba\u1e43. Tattha c\u012bvaranti antarav\u0101sak\u0101d\u012bsu ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci. Pa\u1e6disevat\u012bti paribhu\xf1jati, niv\u0101seti v\u0101 p\u0101rupati v\u0101. Y\u0101vadev\u0101ti payojan\u0101vadhiparicchedaniyamavacana\u1e43, ettakameva hi yogino c\u012bvarapa\u1e6disevane payojana\u1e43 yadida\u1e43 s\u012btassa pa\u1e6digh\u0101t\u0101y\u0101ti\u0101di, na ito bhiyyo. S\u012btass\u0101ti ajjhattadh\u0101tukkhobhavasena v\u0101 bahiddh\u0101utupari\u1e47\u0101manavasena v\u0101 uppannassa yassa kassaci s\u012btassa. Pa\u1e6digh\u0101t\u0101y\u0101ti pa\u1e6dihananattha\u1e43. Yath\u0101 sar\u012bre \u0101b\u0101dha\u1e43 na upp\u0101deti, eva\u1e43 tassa vinodanattha\u1e43. S\u012btabbh\u0101hate hi sar\u012bre vikkhittacitto yoniso padahitu\u1e43 na sakkoti, tasm\u0101 s\u012btassa pa\u1e6digh\u0101t\u0101ya c\u012bvara\u1e43 pa\u1e6disevitabbanti bhagav\u0101 anu\xf1\xf1\u0101si. Esa nayo sabbattha. Kevala\xf1hettha u\u1e47hass\u0101ti aggisant\u0101passa. Tassa vanad\u0101h\u0101d\u012bsu sambhavo veditabbo. \u1e0ca\u1e43samakasav\u0101t\u0101tapasar\u012bsapasamphass\u0101nanti ettha pana \u1e0da\u1e43s\u0101ti \u1e0da\u1e43sanamakkhik\u0101, andhamakkhik\u0101tipi vuccanti. Makas\u0101 makas\u0101 eva. V\u0101t\u0101ti sarajaaraj\u0101dibhed\u0101. \u0100tapoti s\u016briy\u0101tapo. Sar\u012bsap\u0101ti ye keci sarant\u0101 gacchanti d\u012bghaj\u0101tik\u0101 sapp\u0101dayo, tesa\u1e43 da\u1e6d\u1e6dhasamphasso ca phu\u1e6d\u1e6dhasamphasso c\u0101ti duvidho samphasso, sopi c\u012bvara\u1e43 p\u0101rupitv\u0101 nisinna\u1e43 na b\u0101dhati, tasm\u0101 t\u0101disesu \u1e6dh\u0101nesu tesa\u1e43 pa\u1e6digh\u0101tatth\u0101ya pa\u1e6disevati. Y\u0101vadev\u0101ti puna etassa vacana\u1e43 niyatapayojan\u0101vadhiparicchedadassanattha\u1e43, hirikop\u012bnapa\u1e6dicch\u0101dana\xf1hi niyatapayojana\u1e43, itar\u0101ni kad\u0101ci kad\u0101ci honti. Tattha hirikop\u012bnanti ta\u1e43 ta\u1e43 samb\u0101dha\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43. Yasmi\u1e43 yasmi\xf1hi a\u1e45ge vivariyam\u0101ne hir\u012b kuppati vinassati, ta\u1e43 ta\u1e43 hiri\u1e43 kopanato hirikop\u012bnanti vuccati. Tassa ca hirikop\u012bnassa pa\u1e6dicch\u0101danatthanti hirikop\u012bnapa\u1e6dicch\u0101danattha\u1e43. Hirikop\u012bna\u1e43 pa\u1e6dicch\u0101danatthantipi p\u0101\u1e6dho.",translations:{en:"Now, as for what was said next about the virtue dependent on requisites, therein 'wisely reflecting' means having known and considered by means of a proper method and path; this is the meaning. Here, the reflection mentioned in the manner of 'for the warding off of cold' and so forth should be understood as 'wisely reflecting.' In this context, 'a robe' refers to any garment such as the inner robe and so on. 'One uses' means one makes use of, wears, or puts on. 'Only for' is a term defining the limit and boundary of the purpose, for this much alone is the purpose for a yog\u012b in using a robe\u2014namely, beginning with 'for the warding off of cold'\u2014and no more. 'Of cold' refers to any cold that arises either due to the disturbance of internal elements or due to changes in external weather. 'For the warding off' means for the purpose of striking it down. It is for the purpose of dispelling it so that it does not cause affliction to the body. For when the body is afflicted by cold, the mind becomes distracted and one cannot strive with proper attention; therefore, the Blessed One allowed the use of a robe for the warding off of cold. This same method applies everywhere. Here, however, 'of heat' refers to the heat of a fire. Its occurrence should be understood in contexts like forest fires and so on. Regarding 'contact with gadflies, mosquitoes, wind, sun, and creeping things'\u2014here, 'gadflies' are biting flies, also called blind flies. 'Mosquitoes' are simply mosquitoes. 'Wind' includes various types such as those with and without dust. 'Sun' means the heat of the sun. 'Creeping things' refers to any long-bodied creatures like snakes and so on that move by slithering. Their contact is of two kinds: the contact of a bite and the contact of a touch. Such contact does not harm one who is seated wearing a robe; therefore, in such places, one uses it for the purpose of warding them off. The repetition of 'only for' is to show the definition of the limit of a fixed purpose, for the covering of the private parts is a fixed purpose, while the others occur only occasionally. Herein, 'that which provokes shame' refers to this or that private place. For when any such limb is exposed, shame is provoked and destroyed; thus, because it provokes shame, it is called 'that which provokes shame.' And 'for the covering of that which provokes shame' is 'hirikop\u012bnapa\u1e6dicch\u0101danattha\u1e43.' There is also the reading 'hirikop\u012bna\u1e43 pa\u1e6dicch\u0101danattha\u1e43.'",pt:"Quanto \xe0 moralidade baseada no uso dos requisitos (paccayasannissitas\u012bla) mencionada logo ap\xf3s aquela [a moralidade da purifica\xe7\xe3o dos meios de vida], nela, \"refletindo sabiamente\" (pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101 yoniso) significa tendo conhecido por meio de m\xe9todos adequados e caminhos corretos, tendo refletido. E aqui, deve-se entender que apenas a reflex\xe3o expressa na forma \"para afastar o frio\", etc., \xe9 \"refletindo sabiamente\". Ali, \"manto\" (c\u012bvara) refere-se a qualquer um entre o manto interno, etc. \"Usa\" (pa\u1e6disevati) significa desfruta, veste ou cobre-se. \"Apenas para\" (y\u0101vadeva) \xe9 uma express\xe3o que define e limita o prop\xf3sito; pois este \xe9 o \xfanico prop\xf3sito para o praticante (yog\u012b) ao usar o manto, a saber, \"para afastar o frio\", etc., e nada al\xe9m disso. \"Do frio\" (s\u012btassa) refere-se a qualquer tipo de frio que surja, seja devido \xe0 perturba\xe7\xe3o dos elementos internos ou devido \xe0 mudan\xe7a clim\xe1tica externa. \"Para afastar\" (pa\u1e6digh\u0101t\u0101ya) significa com o prop\xf3sito de eliminar. De modo que n\xe3o cause afli\xe7\xe3o ao corpo, assim \xe9 para a sua remo\xe7\xe3o. Pois quando o corpo \xe9 afligido pelo frio, a mente se dispersa e n\xe3o se \xe9 capaz de se esfor\xe7ar sabiamente; por isso, o Aben\xe7oado permitiu o uso do manto para afastar o frio. Este m\xe9todo se aplica a todos os casos. No entanto, a \xfanica diferen\xe7a aqui \xe9 que \"do calor\" (u\u1e47hassa) refere-se ao calor do fogo. Sua ocorr\xeancia deve ser entendida em casos como inc\xeandios florestais, etc. Na express\xe3o \"do contato com mutucas, mosquitos, vento, sol e r\xe9pteis\", \"mutucas\" (\u1e0da\u1e43sa) s\xe3o moscas picadoras, tamb\xe9m chamadas de moscas-cegas. \"Mosquitos\" (makas\u0101) s\xe3o os pr\xf3prios mosquitos. \"Vento\" (v\u0101t\u0101) refere-se aos ventos com poeira, sem poeira, etc. \"Sol\" (\u0101tapo) \xe9 o calor do sol. \"R\xe9pteis\" (sar\u012bsapa) s\xe3o quaisquer criaturas de corpo longo que se movem rastejando, como cobras, etc. O contato com eles \xe9 de dois tipos: o contato por picada e o contato por toque f\xedsico. Mesmo esse duplo contato n\xe3o aflige o monge que est\xe1 sentado coberto com o manto; portanto, em tais lugares, ele usa o manto para afastar o contato deles. A repeti\xe7\xe3o da palavra \"apenas para\" (y\u0101vadeva) serve para mostrar o limite do prop\xf3sito constante; pois a cobertura das partes pudendas (hirikop\u012bna) \xe9 um prop\xf3sito constante, enquanto os outros ocorrem apenas de tempos em tempos. Ali, \"partes pudendas\" (hirikop\u012bna) refere-se \xe0quelas respectivas partes \xedntimas. Pois qualquer membro que, se exposto, cause a perturba\xe7\xe3o ou destrui\xe7\xe3o da vergonha (hir\u012b), \xe9 chamado de \"hirikop\u012bna\" porque arru\xedna a vergonha. E \"para cobrir essas partes pudendas\" \xe9 o significado de \"hirikop\u012bnapa\u1e6dicch\u0101danattha\u1e43\". H\xe1 tamb\xe9m a leitura \"hirikop\u012bna\u1e43 pa\u1e6dicch\u0101danattha\u1e43\".",es:"En cuanto a lo que se llama 'moralidad relacionada con el uso de los requisitos' que sigue a continuaci\xf3n, 'reflexionando sabiamente' (pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101 yoniso) significa conocer tras haber reflexionado por el m\xe9todo y camino correctos. Aqu\xed, la reflexi\xf3n mencionada como 'para protegerse del fr\xedo', etc., debe entenderse como 'reflexionar sabiamente'. En ese contexto, 'el manto' (c\u012bvara\u1e43) se refiere a cualquiera de ellos, como el manto interior, etc. 'Utiliza' (pa\u1e6disevati) significa que lo usa, ya sea visti\xe9ndolo o cubri\xe9ndose con \xe9l. 'Solo para' (y\u0101vadeva) es una expresi\xf3n que define el l\xedmite del prop\xf3sito; pues este es el \xfanico prop\xf3sito para el cual el practicante utiliza el manto, a saber, 'para protegerse del fr\xedo', etc., y nada m\xe1s. 'Del fr\xedo' (s\u012btassa) se refiere a cualquier tipo de fr\xedo que surja, ya sea por el trastorno de los elementos internos o por el cambio de estaci\xf3n externo. 'Para protegerse' (pa\u1e6digh\u0101t\u0101y\u0101) significa con el fin de eliminarlo; esto es, para eliminarlo de tal modo que no cause enfermedad en el cuerpo. Pues si el cuerpo es afligido por el fr\xedo, la mente se distrae y uno no puede esforzarse sabiamente; por ello, el Bienaventurado permiti\xf3: 'se debe utilizar el manto para protegerse del fr\xedo'. Este m\xe9todo se aplica en todo. La \xfanica diferencia aqu\xed es 'del calor' (u\u1e47hassa), que se refiere al calor del fuego; su posibilidad debe entenderse en incendios forestales y casos similares. En la frase 'el contacto de t\xe1banos, mosquitos, viento, sol y reptiles', 't\xe1banos' (\u1e0da\u1e43s\u0101) son las moscas que pican, tambi\xe9n llamadas moscas ciegas. 'Mosquitos' (makas\u0101) son simplemente mosquitos. 'Viento' (v\u0101t\u0101) se refiere a los diversos tipos de viento, con polvo o sin polvo. 'Sol' (\u0101tapo) es el calor del sol. 'Reptiles' (sar\u012bsap\u0101) son todos los seres de cuerpo largo que se desplazan arrastr\xe1ndose, como las serpientes; el contacto con ellos es de dos tipos: el contacto por mordedura y el contacto por roce. Ni siquiera estos molestan al monje que est\xe1 sentado cubierto con su manto; por lo tanto, en tales lugares, lo utiliza para protegerse de ellos. El uso repetido de la palabra 'solo para' (y\u0101vadeva) es para mostrar la definici\xf3n del l\xedmite del prop\xf3sito constante; pues cubrir las partes que causan verg\xfcenza es un prop\xf3sito constante, mientras que los otros ocurren ocasionalmente. All\xed, 'partes que causan verg\xfcenza' (hirikop\u012bna\u1e43) se refiere a las diversas partes pudendas. Pues en cualquier parte del cuerpo que, al quedar descubierta, la verg\xfcenza (hir\u012b) se pierde, esa parte se llama hirikop\u012bna por alterar la verg\xfcenza. Debido a que sirve para cubrir esas partes, se llama 'con el fin de cubrir las partes que causan verg\xfcenza' (hirikop\u012bnapa\u1e6dicch\u0101danattha\u1e43). Tambi\xe9n existe la variante hirikop\u012bna\u1e43 pa\u1e6dicch\u0101danattha\u1e43."}},{id:"vism-1.22",pali:"Evametasmi\u1e43 catubbidhe s\u012ble saddh\u0101ya p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varo samp\u0101detabbo. Saddh\u0101s\u0101dhano hi so, s\u0101vakavisay\u0101t\u012btatt\u0101 sikkh\u0101padapa\xf1\xf1attiy\u0101. Sikkh\u0101padapa\xf1\xf1attiy\u0101canapa\u1e6dikkhepo cettha nidassana\u1e43. Tasm\u0101 yath\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1atta\u1e43 sikkh\u0101pada\u1e43 anavasesa\u1e43 saddh\u0101ya sam\u0101diyitv\u0101 j\u012bvitepi apekkha\u1e43 akarontena s\u0101dhuka\u1e43 samp\u0101detabba\u1e43. Vuttampi heta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"In this fourfold virtue, the restraint of the P\u0101timokkha should be accomplished with faith. For it is accomplished through faith, since the establishment of the training precepts transcends the sphere of disciples. The rejection of a request for the establishment of a training precept is an example here. Therefore, having completely undertaken the training precept as prescribed with faith, one should accomplish it well, without any concern even for one's life. For this has been said:",pt:"Assim, dentre estes quatro tipos de moralidade, a conten\xe7\xe3o do P\u0101timokkha deve ser realizada por meio da f\xe9. Pois ela \xe9 realizada pela f\xe9, visto que a promulga\xe7\xe3o das regras de treinamento (sikkh\u0101pada) transcende o dom\xednio dos disc\xedpulos. A rejei\xe7\xe3o ao pedido para promulgar as regras de treinamento \xe9 uma ilustra\xe7\xe3o disso aqui. Portanto, tendo assumido plenamente com f\xe9 as regras de treinamento exatamente como foram prescritas, deve-se cumpri-las perfeitamente, sem demonstrar qualquer apego sequer \xe0 pr\xf3pria vida. Pois isto tamb\xe9m foi dito:",es:"De esta manera, en esta moralidad de cuatro clases, la restricci\xf3n del P\u0101timokkha debe completarse mediante la fe (saddh\u0101). Pues tal restricci\xf3n se logra a trav\xe9s de la fe, ya que el establecimiento de las reglas de entrenamiento (sikkh\u0101pada) est\xe1 m\xe1s all\xe1 del alcance del conocimiento de los disc\xedpulos. El rechazo del Buda a la petici\xf3n de Sariputta para establecer las reglas es una prueba de esto. Por lo tanto, habiendo asumido por fe cada regla de entrenamiento tal como fue prescrita, sin omitir ninguna, debe completarse perfectamente, incluso sin tener apego por la propia vida. Pues as\xed se ha dicho:"}}]},419,[]);
__d(function(a,e,s,o,i,t,n){i.exports=[{id:"vism-2.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni yehi appicchat\u0101santu\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101d\u012bhi gu\u1e47ehi vuttappak\u0101rassa s\u012blassa vod\u0101na\u1e43 hoti, te gu\u1e47e samp\u0101detu\u1e43 yasm\u0101 sam\u0101dinnas\u012blena yogin\u0101 dhuta\u1e45gasam\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Eva\xf1hissa appicchat\u0101santu\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101sallekhapavivek\u0101pacayav\u012briy\u0101rambhasubharat\u0101digu\u1e47asalilavikkh\u0101litamala\u1e43 s\u012bla\xf1ceva suparisuddha\u1e43 bhavissati, vat\u0101ni ca sampajjissanti. Iti anavajjas\u012blabbatagu\u1e47aparisuddhasabbasam\u0101c\u0101ro por\u0101\u1e47e ariyava\u1e43sattaye pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya catutthassa bh\u0101van\u0101r\u0101mat\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101tassa ariyava\u1e43sassa adhigam\u0101raho bhavissati. Tasm\u0101 dhuta\u1e45gakatha\u1e43 \u0101rabhiss\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"Now, since the purification of virtue of the kind described comes about by means of such qualities as fewness of wishes, contentment, and so forth, a yogin who has undertaken virtue should undertake the ascetic practices in order to bring about those qualities. For in this way, his virtue\u2014its defilement washed away by the water of such qualities as fewness of wishes, contentment, effacement, seclusion, non-accumulation, arousal of energy, and ease of maintenance\u2014will become thoroughly purified, and his observances will be fulfilled. Thus, with all his conduct purified by the quality of blameless virtue and observances, established in the three ancient noble lineages, he will become worthy of attaining the fourth noble lineage, known as delight in meditative cultivation. Therefore, we shall begin the discourse on the ascetic practices.",pt:"Agora, visto que a purifica\xe7\xe3o da virtude do tipo descrito ocorre por meio de qualidades como o desejo limitado, o contentamento e outras semelhantes, para realizar essas qualidades, o praticante que estabeleceu a sua virtude deve assumir os fatores de purifica\xe7\xe3o. Pois, agindo assim, a sua virtude \u2014 com as suas impurezas lavadas pela \xe1gua de qualidades como o desejo limitado, o contentamento, a austeridade, o isolamento, a diminui\xe7\xe3o dos la\xe7os, o in\xedcio do esfor\xe7o vigoroso e a facilidade de manuten\xe7\xe3o \u2014 tornar-se\xe1 extremamente pura, e os seus votos ser\xe3o cumpridos. Assim, com toda a sua conduta purificada pelas qualidades da virtude irrepreens\xedvel e dos votos asc\xe9ticos, estabelecendo-se na antiga e tr\xedplice linhagem dos nobres, ele se tornar\xe1 digno de alcan\xe7ar a quarta linhagem dos nobres, que consiste no deleite na medita\xe7\xe3o. Portanto, iniciaremos a explica\xe7\xe3o sobre os fatores de purifica\xe7\xe3o.",es:"Ahora bien, dado que la purificaci\xf3n de la virtud del tipo ya mencionado se logra mediante cualidades como el poco deseo, el contentamiento, etc., el yogui que ha asumido la virtud debe emprender la asunci\xf3n de las pr\xe1cticas asc\xe9ticas (dhuta\u1e45ga) para perfeccionar dichas cualidades. Pues as\xed, su virtud tendr\xe1 sus impurezas lavadas por el agua de cualidades tales como el poco deseo, el contentamiento, la austeridad, el aislamiento, la disminuci\xf3n de las impurezas, el inicio de la energ\xeda y la facilidad de ser sustentado; por lo cual ser\xe1 plenamente pura y sus votos se cumplir\xe1n. As\xed, aquel cuya conducta completa es pura por la virtud irreprochable y las cualidades de los votos, habi\xe9ndose establecido en el triple linaje de los nobles (ariyava\u1e43sa) tradicional, ser\xe1 digno de alcanzar el cuarto linaje de los nobles, conocido como el deleite en el desarrollo de la meditaci\xf3n. Por lo tanto, comenzaremos la explicaci\xf3n de las pr\xe1cticas asc\xe9ticas."}},{id:"vism-2.2",pali:"Bhagavat\u0101 hi pariccattalok\u0101mis\u0101na\u1e43 k\u0101ye ca j\u012bvite ca anapekkh\u0101na\u1e43 anulomapa\u1e6dipada\u1e43yeva \u0101r\u0101dhetuk\u0101m\u0101na\u1e43 kulaputt\u0101na\u1e43 terasadhuta\u1e45g\u0101ni anu\xf1\xf1\u0101t\u0101ni. Seyyathida\u1e43 \u2013 pa\u1e43suk\u016blika\u1e45ga\u1e43, tec\u012bvarika\u1e45ga\u1e43, pi\u1e47\u1e0dap\u0101tika\u1e45ga\u1e43, sapad\u0101nac\u0101rika\u1e45ga\u1e43, ek\u0101sanika\u1e45ga\u1e43, pattapi\u1e47\u1e0dika\u1e45ga\u1e43, khalupacch\u0101bhattika\u1e45ga\u1e43, \u0101ra\xf1\xf1ika\u1e45ga\u1e43, rukkham\u016blika\u1e45ga\u1e43, abbhok\u0101sika\u1e45ga\u1e43, sos\u0101nika\u1e45ga\u1e43, yath\u0101santhatika\u1e45ga\u1e43, nesajjika\u1e45ganti. Tattha \u2013",translations:{en:"Indeed, the Blessed One has permitted thirteen ascetic practices for sons of good families who have abandoned worldly allurements, are indifferent to body and life, and wish to accomplish the conforming practice. They are as follows: the rag-robe-wearer's practice, the triple-robe-wearer's practice, the alms-food-eater's practice, the house-to-house-wanderer's practice, the one-sessioner's practice, the bowl-food-eater's practice, the later-food-refuser's practice, the forest-dweller's practice, the tree-root-dweller's practice, the open-air-dweller's practice, the charnel-ground-dweller's practice, the any-lodging-user's practice, and the sitter's practice. Therein\u2014",pt:"Pois o Aben\xe7oado permitiu treze fatores de purifica\xe7\xe3o para os filhos de boa fam\xedlia que renunciaram aos ganhos mundanos, que n\xe3o t\xeam apego ao corpo nem \xe0 vida, e que desejam realizar a pr\xe1tica que est\xe1 em conformidade com o Nibb\u0101na. A saber: o fator de usar mantos feitos de trapos descartados, o fator de usar apenas os tr\xeas mantos, o fator de viver apenas de esmolas de comida, o fator de esmolar de casa em casa sem interrup\xe7\xe3o, o fator de comer em uma \xfanica sess\xe3o, o fator de comer apenas da tigela de esmolas, o fator de recusar comida adicional ap\xf3s ter terminado de comer, o fator de viver na floresta, o fator de viver ao p\xe9 de uma \xe1rvore, o fator de viver ao ar livre, o fator de viver em um cemit\xe9rio, o fator de aceitar qualquer assento que lhe for designado e o fator de permanecer na postura sentada sem nunca se deitar. Entre estes:",es:"En efecto, el Bendito autoriz\xf3 trece pr\xe1cticas asc\xe9ticas para los hijos de buena familia que han renunciado a los cebos mundanos y, sin consideraci\xf3n por su cuerpo ni por su vida, desean perfeccionar la pr\xe1ctica que est\xe1 en conformidad con el camino. Estas son: la pr\xe1ctica del que viste harapos (pa\u1e43suk\u016blika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de los tres mantos (tec\u012bvarika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de la comida recolectada (pi\u1e47\u1e0dap\u0101tika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de ir por orden de casa en casa (sapad\u0101nac\u0101rika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de una sola sesi\xf3n para comer (ek\u0101sanika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de comer solo del cuenco (pattapi\u1e47\u1e0dika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de no comer despu\xe9s de haber terminado (khalupacch\u0101bhattika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de vivir en el bosque (\u0101ra\xf1\xf1ika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de vivir al pie de un \xe1rbol (rukkham\u016blika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de vivir al aire libre (abbhok\u0101sika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de vivir en un cementerio (sos\u0101nika\u1e45ga), la pr\xe1ctica de aceptar cualquier asiento que se asigne (yath\u0101santhatika\u1e45ga) y la pr\xe1ctica de permanecer sentado sin acostarse (nesajjika\u1e45ga). En este contexto:"}},{id:"vism-2.3",pali:"Sabb\u0101neva panet\u0101ni tena tena sam\u0101d\u0101nena dhutakilesatt\u0101 dhutassa bhikkhuno a\u1e45g\u0101ni, kilesadhunanato v\u0101 dhutanti laddhavoh\u0101ra\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 a\u1e45ga\u1e43 etesanti dhuta\u1e45g\u0101ni. Atha v\u0101 dhut\u0101ni ca t\u0101ni pa\u1e6dipakkhaniddhunanato a\u1e45g\u0101ni ca pa\u1e6dipattiy\u0101tipi dhuta\u1e45g\u0101ni. Eva\u1e43 t\u0101vettha atthato vi\xf1\xf1\u0101tabbo vinicchayo.",translations:{en:"Moreover, all these are factors of a monk who is 'one who has shaken off' ('dhuta') because he has shaken off defilements by means of this or that undertaking. Or, they are 'dhuta\u1e45gas' because knowledge\u2014which has received the designation 'dhuta' from its shaking off of defilements\u2014is a factor ('a\u1e45ga') of them. Alternatively, they are also 'dhuta\u1e45gas' because they are both 'dhuta' (things that shake off), due to their shaking off of opposing states, and they are 'a\u1e45gas' (factors) of the practice. Thus, the analysis here is to be understood in terms of its meaning.",pt:"Todos estes, por terem as impurezas eliminadas por meio de suas respectivas determina\xe7\xf5es, s\xe3o fatores do monge que eliminou as impurezas (dhuta). Ou, porque elimina as impurezas, o conhecimento que obteve a designa\xe7\xe3o de 'dhuta' \xe9 o fator dessas pr\xe1ticas, da\xed 'dhuta\u1e45g\u0101ni' (fatores de purifica\xe7\xe3o). Ou ainda, elas s\xe3o 'dhuta' porque eliminam os estados opostos e s\xe3o 'a\u1e45ga' (fatores) da pr\xe1tica espiritual; por isso tamb\xe9m s\xe3o chamadas de 'dhuta\u1e45g\u0101ni'. Assim, primeiramente, deve-se compreender a decis\xe3o a respeito disso quanto ao significado literal.",es:"Todas estas son 'factores' (a\u1e45ga) del monje que es 'sacudido' (dhuta), porque mediante cada una de esas asunciones ha sacudido sus impurezas. O bien, el conocimiento que ha recibido el nombre de 'dhuta' por sacudir las impurezas es el 'factor' (a\u1e45ga) de estas pr\xe1cticas; de ah\xed 'dhuta\u1e45ga'. O bien, se llaman 'dhuta\u1e45ga' porque son tanto 'dhuta' (sacudidos), por sacudir lo que es opuesto a ellos, como 'a\u1e45ga' (factores) de la pr\xe1ctica. As\xed debe entenderse la determinaci\xf3n por medio del significado."}},{id:"vism-2.4",pali:"Sabb\u0101neva panet\u0101ni sam\u0101d\u0101nacetan\u0101lakkha\u1e47\u0101ni. Vuttampi ceta\u1e43 \"yo sam\u0101diyati, so puggalo. Yena sam\u0101diyati, cittacetasik\u0101 ete dhamm\u0101. Y\u0101 sam\u0101d\u0101nacetan\u0101, ta\u1e43 dhuta\u1e45ga\u1e43. Ya\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhipati, ta\u1e43 vatth\u016b\"ti. Sabb\u0101neva ca loluppaviddha\u1e43sanaras\u0101ni, nilloluppabh\u0101vapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni appicchat\u0101diariyadhammapada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni. Evamettha lakkha\u1e47\u0101d\u012bhi veditabbo vinicchayo.",translations:{en:"Moreover, all these have the characteristic of the volition of undertaking. It has also been said: 'The person who undertakes is the individual. The mental states and their concomitants by which one undertakes are these phenomena. The volition of undertaking is the ascetic practice. That which one rejects is the object.' Moreover, all these have the function of dispelling craving, the manifestation of non-craving, and are the proximate cause for noble qualities such as having few wishes. Thus, the determination here should be understood by means of these characteristics and so on.",pt:"Todos estes t\xeam como caracter\xedstica a voli\xe7\xe3o de determina\xe7\xe3o. Pois tamb\xe9m foi dito: 'Aquele que determina \xe9 a pessoa. Aquilo com que se determina s\xe3o os estados mentais de mente e fatores mentais. A voli\xe7\xe3o de determina\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o fator asc\xe9tico (dhuta\u1e45ga). O que se rejeita \xe9 o objeto'. E todos eles t\xeam como fun\xe7\xe3o a destrui\xe7\xe3o da gan\xe2ncia, manifestam-se como a aus\xeancia de gan\xe2ncia, e t\xeam como causa pr\xf3xima os nobres estados como a pouca cobi\xe7a e afins. Assim, deve-se compreender a decis\xe3o a respeito disso por meio das caracter\xedsticas e outros aspectos.",es:"Todas ellas tienen como caracter\xedstica la voluntad de asunci\xf3n. Al respecto se ha dicho: 'Aquel que asume es la persona. Aquello por lo cual se asume son estos estados de la mente y los factores mentales. Aquello que es la voluntad de asunci\xf3n es la pr\xe1ctica asc\xe9tica. Aquello que se rechaza es el objeto'. Todas tienen como funci\xf3n la destrucci\xf3n de la avidez, se manifiestan como el estado de ausencia de avidez y tienen como causa pr\xf3xima los nobles estados como el poco deseo. As\xed debe entenderse aqu\xed la determinaci\xf3n por medio de las caracter\xedsticas y dem\xe1s t\xe9rminos."}},{id:"vism-2.5",pali:"Sam\u0101d\u0101navidh\u0101natoti\u0101d\u012bsu pana pa\xf1casu sabb\u0101neva dhuta\u1e45g\u0101ni dharam\u0101ne bhagavati bhagavatova santike sam\u0101d\u0101tabb\u0101ni. Parinibbute mah\u0101s\u0101vakassa santike. Tasmi\u1e43 asati kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101savassa, an\u0101g\u0101missa, sakad\u0101g\u0101missa, sot\u0101pannassa, tipi\u1e6dakassa, dvipi\u1e6dakassa, ekapi\u1e6dakassa, ekasa\u1e45g\u012btikassa, a\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101cariyassa. Tasmi\u1e43 asati dhuta\u1e45gadharassa, tasmimpi asati cetiya\u1e45ga\u1e47a\u1e43 sammajjitv\u0101 ukku\u1e6dika\u1e43 nis\u012bditv\u0101 samm\u0101sambuddhassa santike vadantena viya sam\u0101d\u0101tabb\u0101ni, apica sayampi sam\u0101d\u0101tu\u1e43 va\u1e6d\u1e6dati eva. Ettha ca cetiyapabbate dve bh\u0101tikatther\u0101na\u1e43 je\u1e6d\u1e6dhakabh\u0101tu dhuta\u1e45gappicchat\u0101ya vatthu kathetabba\u1e43. Aya\u1e43 t\u0101va s\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47akath\u0101.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, concerning the five points beginning with the method of undertaking, all the ascetic practices should be undertaken in the presence of the Blessed One himself while he is living. After his final passing, they should be undertaken in the presence of a great disciple. In his absence, in the presence of one who has destroyed the corruptions, a non-returner, a once-returner, a stream-enterer, a master of the Three Pi\u1e6dakas, of the Two Pi\u1e6dakas, of one Pi\u1e6daka, of one Collection, or a teacher of the commentaries. In the absence of such a one, in the presence of an observer of the ascetic practices. In the absence of even that one, after sweeping the courtyard of a shrine and sitting on one's heels, they should be undertaken as if speaking in the presence of the Perfectly Enlightened One. Moreover, it is also permissible to undertake them by oneself. Here, the story of the elder brother of the two sibling elders on Cetiyapabbata, on account of his having few wishes with regard to the ascetic practices, should be told. This, for now, is the general discussion.",pt:"Quanto aos cinco t\xf3picos, come\xe7ando com o procedimento de ado\xe7\xe3o: enquanto o Aben\xe7oado estava vivo, todos os fatores asc\xe9ticos deviam ser adotados na presen\xe7a do pr\xf3prio Aben\xe7oado. Ap\xf3s o seu parinibbana, na presen\xe7a de um grande disc\xedpulo. Na aus\xeancia deste, na presen\xe7a de um arahant, de um n\xe3o-retornante, de um que retorna uma vez, de um que entrou na corrente, de um conhecedor do Tipitaka, de um conhecedor de dois Pitakas, de um conhecedor de um Pitaka, de um conhecedor de uma \xfanica cole\xe7\xe3o (Nikaya), ou de um mestre dos Coment\xe1rios. Na aus\xeancia deste, na presen\xe7a de um portador dos fatores asc\xe9ticos. Na aus\xeancia deste tamb\xe9m, ap\xf3s varrer o p\xe1tio de uma estupa e sentar-se de c\xf3coras, deve-se adot\xe1-los como se estivesse falando na presen\xe7a do Buda perfeitamente iluminado. Al\xe9m disso, \xe9 perfeitamente adequado adot\xe1-los por si mesmo. E aqui deve-se contar a hist\xf3ria da pouca cobi\xe7a em rela\xe7\xe3o aos fatores asc\xe9ticos do irm\xe3o mais velho entre os dois irm\xe3os anci\xe3os na montanha Cetiyapabbata. Esta \xe9, primeiramente, a explica\xe7\xe3o geral.",es:"En cuanto a los cinco puntos, comenzando con el procedimiento de compromiso (sam\u0101d\u0101navidh\u0101na), todas las pr\xe1cticas asc\xe9ticas (dhuta\u1e45gas) deben emprenderse en presencia del Bienaventurado mientras \xc9l vive. Tras su Parinibb\u0101na, deben emprenderse ante un Gran Disc\xedpulo. Si no hay ninguno presente, ante un Arahant (kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sava), un No-Retornante (an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), un Retornante-Una-Vez (sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), un Entrado-en-la-Corriente (sot\u0101panna), uno que conozca los tres Pi\u1e6dakas, uno que conozca dos Pi\u1e6dakas, uno que conozca un Pi\u1e6daka, uno que conozca una de las colecciones (sa\u1e45g\u012btikassa), o ante un maestro de los Comentarios (a\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101cariya). Si no hay ninguno presente, ante un practicante de los dhuta\u1e45gas. Si tampoco hay ninguno presente, uno debe limpiar el patio de una estupa (cetiya), sentarse en cuclillas y emprenderlas como si hablara ante el Buda Completamente Iluminado; adem\xe1s, tambi\xe9n es v\xe1lido emprenderlas por uno mismo. En este punto, se debe relatar la historia de dos hermanos ancianos en la monta\xf1a Cetiyapabbata con respecto a la modestia (appicchat\u0101) de los dhuta\u1e45gas del hermano mayor. Esta es la explicaci\xf3n general inicial."}},{id:"vism-2.6",pali:"Id\u0101ni ekekassa sam\u0101d\u0101navidh\u0101nappabhedabhed\u0101nisa\u1e43se va\u1e47\u1e47ayiss\u0101ma. Pa\u1e43suk\u016blika\u1e45ga\u1e43 t\u0101va \"gahapatid\u0101nac\u012bvara\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, pa\u1e43suk\u016blika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesu dv\u012bsu vacanesu a\xf1\xf1atarena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti. Ida\u1e43 t\u0101vettha sam\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now we shall explain for each practice its method of undertaking, procedure, grades, breaking, and benefits. The refuse-rag wearer's practice, to begin with, is undertaken with one of these two phrases: 'I refuse a robe given by a householder,' or 'I undertake the refuse-rag wearer's practice.' This, then, is the undertaking.",pt:"Agora descreveremos o procedimento de ado\xe7\xe3o, a classifica\xe7\xe3o, a ruptura e os benef\xedcios de cada um deles. O fator do usu\xe1rio de manto de trapos, primeiramente, \xe9 adotado por meio de uma destas duas f\xf3rmulas: 'Rejeito o manto oferecido por um chefe de fam\xedlia; adoto o fator do usu\xe1rio de manto de trapos'. Este \xe9, primeiramente, o procedimento de ado\xe7\xe3o a esse respeito.",es:"A continuaci\xf3n, describiremos el procedimiento de compromiso, las clasificaciones, la ruptura y los beneficios de cada pr\xe1ctica. Primero, la pr\xe1ctica de los mantos de desecho (pa\u1e43suk\u016blika\u1e45ga) se considera emprendida a trav\xe9s de una de estas dos f\xf3rmulas: \u201cRechazo el manto ofrecido por un jefe de hogar (gahapatid\u0101na)\u201d o \u201cEmprendo la pr\xe1ctica del uso de mantos de desecho\u201d. Esto constituye el compromiso inicial para esta pr\xe1ctica."}},{id:"vism-2.7",pali:"Tadanantara\u1e43 pana tec\u012bvarika\u1e45ga\u1e43 \"catutthakac\u012bvara\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, tec\u012bvarika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"Next, the triple-robe-wearer's practice is undertaken with one of these statements: 'I refuse a fourth robe; I undertake the triple-robe-wearer's practice.'",pt:"Imediatamente depois disso, o fator do usu\xe1rio de tr\xeas mantos \xe9 adotado por meio de uma destas f\xf3rmulas: 'Rejeito um quarto manto; adoto o fator do usu\xe1rio de tr\xeas mantos'.",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s, el factor del que posee los tres mantos se asume mediante una de estas dos declaraciones: \"Rechazo un cuarto manto\" o \"Asumo el factor del que posee los tres mantos\"."}},{id:"vism-2.8",pali:"Pi\u1e47\u1e0dap\u0101tika\u1e45gampi \"atirekal\u0101bha\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, pi\u1e47\u1e0dap\u0101tika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The alms-food-eater's practice is also undertaken with one of these statements: \u201cI refuse extra gains; I undertake the alms-food-eater's practice.\u201d",pt:"A pr\xe1tica de comer apenas alimentos de esmola tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumida por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito ganhos extras (como refei\xe7\xf5es oferecidas ao Sangha)' ou 'Assumo a pr\xe1tica de comer apenas alimentos de esmola'.",es:"El factor del que se alimenta solo de limosnas se asume mediante una de estas dos declaraciones: \"Rechazo las ganancias adicionales\" o \"Asumo el factor del que se alimenta solo de limosnas\"."}},{id:"vism-2.9",pali:"Sapad\u0101nac\u0101rika\u1e45gampi \"loluppac\u0101ra\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, sapad\u0101nac\u0101rika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The ascetic practice of going for alms in unbroken sequence is undertaken with one of the following statements: \u201cI reject selective wandering for alms. I undertake the ascetic practice of going for alms in unbroken sequence.\u201d",pt:"A pr\xe1tica de ir de casa em casa sem interrup\xe7\xe3o tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumida por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito a conduta gananciosa (de pular casas)' ou 'Assumo a pr\xe1tica de ir de casa em casa sem interrup\xe7\xe3o'.",es:"La pr\xe1ctica del buscador de limosnas casa por casa (sapad\u0101nac\u0101rika\u1e45ga) tambi\xe9n se emprende mediante una de estas dos declaraciones: 'Rechazo el deambular codicioso' o 'Asumo la pr\xe1ctica del buscador de limosnas casa por casa'."}},{id:"vism-2.10",pali:"Ek\u0101sanika\u1e45gampi \"n\u0101n\u0101sanabhojana\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, ek\u0101sanika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The ascetic practice of eating in one session is undertaken with one of the following statements: \u201cI reject eating in various sessions. I undertake the ascetic practice of eating in one session.\u201d",pt:"A pr\xe1tica de comer em uma \xfanica sess\xe3o tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumida por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito comer em m\xfaltiplos assentos' ou 'Assumo a pr\xe1tica de comer em uma \xfanica sess\xe3o'.",es:"La pr\xe1ctica de comer en una sola sesi\xf3n tambi\xe9n se emprende mediante una de estas dos declaraciones: 'Rechazo comer en varios asientos' o 'Asumo la pr\xe1ctica de comer en una sola sesi\xf3n'."}},{id:"vism-2.11",pali:"Pattapi\u1e47\u1e0dika\u1e45gampi \"dutiyakabh\u0101jana\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, pattapi\u1e47\u1e0dika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The bowl-food-eater's practice is also undertaken with one of these statements: 'I reject a second vessel,' or 'I undertake the bowl-food-eater's practice.'",pt:"A pr\xe1tica de comer apenas de uma \xfanica tigela tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumida por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito um segundo recipiente' ou 'Assumo a pr\xe1tica de comer apenas de uma \xfanica tigela'.",es:"La pr\xe1ctica de comer de un solo cuenco tambi\xe9n se emprende mediante una de estas dos declaraciones: 'Rechazo un segundo recipiente' o 'Asumo la pr\xe1ctica de comer de un solo cuenco'."}},{id:"vism-2.12",pali:"Khalupacch\u0101bhattika\u1e45gampi \"atirittabhojana\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, khalupacch\u0101bhattika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The practice of refusing subsequent food is also undertaken by one of these statements: 'I reject leftover food; I undertake the practice of refusing subsequent food.'",pt:"O fator do n\xe3o-comedor de comida posterior tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumido por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito o alimento excedente' ou 'Assumo o fator do n\xe3o-comedor de comida posterior'.",es:"El factor del practicante que no acepta comida posterior se asume mediante una de estas dos f\xf3rmulas: \u201cRechazo la comida adicional\u201d o \u201cAsumo el factor del practicante que no acepta comida despu\xe9s de haber rehusado\u201d."}},{id:"vism-2.13",pali:"\u0100ra\xf1\xf1ika\u1e45gampi \"g\u0101mantasen\u0101sana\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, \u0101ra\xf1\xf1ika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The forest-dweller's practice is also undertaken by one of these statements: \"I reject a dwelling near a village; I undertake the forest-dweller's practice.\"",pt:"O fator do habitante da floresta tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumido por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito uma morada nos limites da aldeia' ou 'Assumo o fator do habitante da floresta'.",es:"El factor del practicante que vive en el bosque se asume mediante una de estas dos f\xf3rmulas: \u201cRechazo las moradas situadas en los l\xedmites de una aldea\u201d o \u201cAsumo el factor del practicante que vive en el bosque\u201d."}},{id:"vism-2.14",pali:"Rukkham\u016blika\u1e45gampi \"channa\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, rukkham\u016blika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The tree-root-dweller's practice is also undertaken with one of these statements: 'I reject a roofed dwelling,' or 'I undertake the tree-root-dweller's practice.'",pt:"O fator do habitante ao p\xe9 de uma \xe1rvore tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumido por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito um teto' ou 'Assumo o fator do habitante ao p\xe9 de uma \xe1rvore'.",es:"La pr\xe1ctica del morador al pie de un \xe1rbol tambi\xe9n se adopta mediante una de estas dos frases: 'Rechazo un refugio cubierto' o 'Adopto la pr\xe1ctica del morador al pie de un \xe1rbol'."}},{id:"vism-2.15",pali:"Abbhok\u0101sika\u1e45gampi \"channa\xf1ca rukkham\u016bla\xf1ca pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, abbhok\u0101sika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The open-air-dweller's practice is also undertaken with one of these statements: 'I reject a roofed dwelling and the root of a tree,' or 'I undertake the open-air-dweller's practice.'",pt:"O fator do morador ao ar livre tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumido por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito um lugar coberto e a base de uma \xe1rvore; assumo o fator do morador ao ar livre'.",es:"La pr\xe1ctica del morador a la intemperie tambi\xe9n se adopta mediante una de estas dos frases: 'Rechazo un refugio cubierto y la base de un \xe1rbol' o 'Adopto la pr\xe1ctica del morador a la intemperie'."}},{id:"vism-2.16",pali:"Sos\u0101nika\u1e45gampi \"na sus\u0101na\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, sos\u0101nika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The charnel-ground-dweller's practice is also undertaken with one of these statements: 'I reject a non-charnel ground,' or 'I undertake the charnel-ground-dweller's practice.'",pt:"O fator do morador em um cemit\xe9rio tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumido por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito um lugar que n\xe3o seja um cemit\xe9rio; assumo o fator do morador em um cemit\xe9rio'.",es:"La pr\xe1ctica del morador del cementerio tambi\xe9n se asume mediante una de estas dos declaraciones: 'Rechazo lo que no es un cementerio' o 'Asumo el factor del morador del cementerio'."}},{id:"vism-2.17",pali:"Yath\u0101santhatika\u1e45gampi \"sen\u0101sanaloluppa\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, yath\u0101santhatika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The any-lodging-as-allotted practice is also undertaken by means of one of these statements: \"I reject greed for lodgings,\" or \"I undertake the any-lodging-as-allotted practice.\"",pt:"O fator do morador em qualquer assento que lhe for designado tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumido por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito a gan\xe2ncia por moradias; assumo o fator do morador em qualquer assento que lhe for designado'.",es:"La pr\xe1ctica del morador en el asiento asignado tambi\xe9n se asume mediante una de estas dos declaraciones: 'Rechazo la codicia por los alojamientos' o 'Asumo el factor del morador en el asiento asignado'."}},{id:"vism-2.18",pali:"Nesajjika\u1e45gampi \"seyya\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhip\u0101mi, nesajjika\u1e45ga\u1e43 sam\u0101diy\u0101m\u012b\"ti imesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravacanena sam\u0101dinna\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"The sitter's practice, too, is undertaken by one of these statements: \"I reject lying down; I undertake the sitter's practice.\"",pt:"O fator do praticante que permanece sentado tamb\xe9m \xe9 assumido por meio de uma destas declara\xe7\xf5es: 'Rejeito a posi\xe7\xe3o deitada; assumo o fator do praticante que permanece sentado'.",es:"La pr\xe1ctica de permanecer sentado tambi\xe9n se asume mediante una de estas dos declaraciones: 'Rechazo el acostarme' o 'Asumo el factor de quien permanece sentado'."}},{id:"vism-2.19",pali:"Puna dve c\u012bvarapa\u1e6disa\u1e43yutt\u0101ni, pa\xf1ca pi\u1e47\u1e0dap\u0101tapa\u1e6disa\u1e43yutt\u0101ni, pa\xf1ca sen\u0101sanapa\u1e6disa\u1e43yutt\u0101ni, eka\u1e43 v\u012briyapa\u1e6disa\u1e43yuttanti eva\u1e43 catt\u0101rova honti. Tattha nesajjika\u1e45ga\u1e43 v\u012briyapa\u1e6disa\u1e43yutta\u1e43. Itar\u0101ni p\u0101ka\u1e6d\u0101neva.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, there are two connected with robes, five connected with almsfood, five connected with lodgings, and one connected with energy\u2014thus there are just four groups. Therein, the sitter's practice is connected with energy. The others are evident.",pt:"De outra forma, eles s\xe3o apenas quatro: dois relacionados aos mantos, cinco relacionados \xe0 comida de esmola, cinco relacionados ao alojamento e um relacionado \xe0 energia. Dentre estes, o fator de permanecer sentado (nesajjika\u1e45ga) \xe9 o relacionado \xe0 energia. Os outros s\xe3o evidentes.",es:"Nuevamente, hay cuatro categor\xedas: dos relacionadas con el manto, cinco relacionadas con la comida de limosna, cinco relacionadas con el alojamiento y una relacionada con el esfuerzo. De ellas, la pr\xe1ctica del que siempre est\xe1 sentado est\xe1 relacionada con el esfuerzo. Las otras son ya conocidas."}},{id:"vism-2.20",pali:"Ett\u0101vat\u0101 ca \"s\u012ble pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya naro sapa\xf1\xf1o\"ti imiss\u0101 g\u0101th\u0101ya s\u012blasam\u0101dhipa\xf1\xf1\u0101mukhena desite visuddhimagge yehi appicchat\u0101santu\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101d\u012bhi gu\u1e47ehi vuttappak\u0101rassa s\u012blassa vod\u0101na\u1e43 hoti, tesa\u1e43 samp\u0101danattha\u1e43 sam\u0101d\u0101tabbadhuta\u1e45gakath\u0101 bh\u0101sit\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"And thus far, in the Path of Purification, which is taught by way of virtue, concentration, and wisdom in accordance with the verse, 'A wise person, established in virtue...,' the discourse on the ascetic practices to be undertaken has been delivered for the accomplishment of those qualities\u2014such as fewness of wishes and contentment\u2014by which the purification of virtue of the kind described takes place.",pt:"E com isso, neste Visuddhimagga ensinado por meio da virtude, da concentra\xe7\xe3o e da sabedoria no verso 'O homem s\xe1bio, estabelecido na virtude...', o discurso sobre os fatores asc\xe9ticos a serem empreendidos foi proferido com o prop\xf3sito de realizar aquelas qualidades, tais como o desejo de ter pouco e o contentamento, pelas quais se realiza a purifica\xe7\xe3o da virtude do tipo descrito.",es:"Con esto, en este Visuddhimagga expuesto mediante la virtud, la concentraci\xf3n y la sabidur\xeda a partir del verso 'El hombre sabio, establecido en la virtud...', se ha expuesto el discurso sobre las dhuta\u1e45gas que deben ser emprendidas para perfeccionar las cualidades de pocos deseos, satisfacci\xf3n, etc., mediante las cuales se produce la purificaci\xf3n de la virtud de la clase ya descrita."}}]},420,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,s,t,i,n){t.exports=[{id:"vism-3.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni yasm\u0101 eva\u1e43 dhuta\u1e45gaparihara\u1e47asamp\u0101ditehi appicchat\u0101d\u012bhi gu\u1e47ehi pariyod\u0101te imasmi\u1e43 s\u012ble pati\u1e6d\u1e6dhitena \"s\u012ble pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya naro sapa\xf1\xf1o, citta\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1a\xf1ca bh\u0101vaya\"nti vacanato cittas\u012bsena niddi\u1e6d\u1e6dho sam\u0101dhi bh\u0101vetabbo. So ca atisa\u1e45khepadesitatt\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101tumpi t\u0101va na sukaro, pageva bh\u0101vetu\u1e43, tasm\u0101 tassa vitth\u0101ra\xf1ca bh\u0101van\u0101naya\xf1ca dassetu\u1e43 ida\u1e43 pa\xf1h\u0101kamma\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"Now, since one established in this virtue\u2014purified by qualities such as fewness of wishes, accomplished through the observance of the ascetic practices\u2014should develop the concentration indicated by the heading 'mind,' in accordance with the saying, 'A wise person, established in virtue, should develop mind and wisdom'; and since this concentration, because it has been taught too briefly, is not easy even to understand, let alone to develop; therefore, to show its details and the method of development, this questioning is undertaken.",pt:"Agora, visto que a concentra\xe7\xe3o, indicada sob o t\xedtulo de 'mente' (citta) na passagem 'O homem s\xe1bio, estabelecido na virtude, deve desenvolver a mente e a sabedoria', deve ser desenvolvida por aquele que est\xe1 estabelecido nesta virtude purificada pelas qualidades de desejo de ter pouco e outras, alcan\xe7adas pela pr\xe1tica dos fatores asc\xe9ticos; e visto que essa concentra\xe7\xe3o, tendo sido ensinada de forma extremamente breve, n\xe3o \xe9 f\xe1cil sequer de compreender, quanto mais de desenvolver; portanto, a fim de mostrar os seus detalhes e o m\xe9todo de seu desenvolvimento, apresenta-se este conjunto de perguntas.",es:"Ahora bien, puesto que el monje establecido en esta virtud, purificada por las cualidades de pocos deseos y otras virtudes perfeccionadas mediante la observancia de las dhuta\u1e45gas, debe desarrollar la concentraci\xf3n \u2014la cual ha sido se\xf1alada bajo el encabezado de 'mente' (citta) en el verso 'El hombre sabio, establecido en la virtud, que desarrolla la mente y la sabidur\xeda'\u2014, y puesto que dicha concentraci\xf3n ha sido expuesta de forma extremadamente breve, no es f\xe1cil ni siquiera de comprender, y mucho menos de desarrollar. Por lo tanto, para mostrar su detalle y el m\xe9todo de desarrollo, se presenta la siguiente serie de preguntas."}},{id:"vism-3.2",pali:"Ko sam\u0101dhi? Kena\u1e6d\u1e6dhena sam\u0101dhi? K\u0101nassa lakkha\u1e47arasapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni? Katividho sam\u0101dhi? Ko cassa sa\u1e43kileso? Ki\u1e43 vod\u0101na\u1e43? Katha\u1e43 bh\u0101vetabbo? Sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101ya ko \u0101nisa\u1e43soti?",translations:{en:"What is concentration? In what sense is it concentration? What are its characteristic, function, manifestation, and proximate cause? How many kinds of concentration are there? What is its defilement? What is its purification? How should it be developed? What is the benefit of developing concentration?",pt:"O que \xe9 a concentra\xe7\xe3o? Em que sentido \xe9 concentra\xe7\xe3o? Quais s\xe3o as suas caracter\xedsticas, fun\xe7\xe3o, manifesta\xe7\xe3o e causa pr\xf3xima? Quantos tipos de concentra\xe7\xe3o existem? O que \xe9 a sua impureza? O que \xe9 a sua purifica\xe7\xe3o? Como deve ser desenvolvida? Quais s\xe3o os benef\xedcios do desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o?",es:"\xbfQu\xe9 es la concentraci\xf3n? \xbfEn qu\xe9 sentido es concentraci\xf3n? \xbfCu\xe1les son sus caracter\xedsticas, funciones, manifestaciones y causas pr\xf3ximas? \xbfDe cu\xe1ntos tipos es la concentraci\xf3n? \xbfCu\xe1l es su corrupci\xf3n? \xbfCu\xe1l es su purificaci\xf3n? \xbfC\xf3mo debe desarrollarse? \xbfCu\xe1l es el beneficio del desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n?"}},{id:"vism-3.3",pali:"Yo pan\u0101ya\u1e43 lokiyo, so vuttanayena s\u012bl\u0101ni visodhetv\u0101 suparisuddhe s\u012ble pati\u1e6d\u1e6dhitena yv\u0101ssa dasasu palibodhesu palibodho atthi, ta\u1e43 upacchinditv\u0101 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nad\u0101yaka\u1e43 kaly\u0101\u1e47amitta\u1e43 upasa\u1e45kamitv\u0101 attano cariy\u0101nuk\u016bla\u1e43 catt\u0101l\u012bs\u0101ya kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu a\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 gahetv\u0101 sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101ya ananur\u016bpa\u1e43 vih\u0101ra\u1e43 pah\u0101ya anur\u016bpe vih\u0101re viharantena khuddakapalibodhupaccheda\u1e43 katv\u0101 sabba\u1e43 bh\u0101van\u0101vidh\u0101na\u1e43 aparih\u0101pentena bh\u0101vetabboti ayamettha sa\u1e45khepo.",translations:{en:"As for this mundane concentration, it is to be developed by one who, having purified the moral precepts in the manner described and being established in perfectly pure morality, has cut off whatever impediment he has among the ten impediments; has approached a good friend who gives a meditation subject; has taken up a meditation subject from among the forty suitable to his own temperament; has abandoned a dwelling unsuitable for the development of concentration and dwells in a suitable one; has cut off the minor impediments; and does not neglect any part of the procedure of development. This is the summary here.",pt:"Mas quanto \xe0 concentra\xe7\xe3o mundana, ela deve ser desenvolvida por aquele que, tendo purificado suas virtudes pelo m\xe9todo mencionado e estando estabelecido em uma virtude perfeitamente pura, corta qualquer impedimento que tenha entre os dez impedimentos, aproxima-se de um bom amigo que d\xe1 um objeto de medita\xe7\xe3o, aprende um dos quarenta objetos de medita\xe7\xe3o que seja adequado ao seu pr\xf3prio temperamento, abandona uma morada inadequada para o desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o, reside em uma morada adequada, corta os pequenos impedimentos e realiza todo o procedimento de medita\xe7\xe3o sem negligenciar nada. Este \xe9 o resumo sobre este assunto.",es:"En cuanto a esta concentraci\xf3n mundana, habiendo purificado la virtud seg\xfan el m\xe9todo mencionado y establecido en una virtud bien pura, aquel que tenga cualquiera de los diez obst\xe1culos debe cortarlo, acercarse a un buen amigo que otorgue un tema de meditaci\xf3n, recibir uno de los cuarenta temas de meditaci\xf3n adecuado a su propio temperamento, abandonar un monasterio inapropiado para el desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n y, viviendo en un monasterio adecuado, habiendo cortado los peque\xf1os obst\xe1culos, debe desarrollarla sin descuidar ning\xfan procedimiento de meditaci\xf3n; este es el resumen sobre este punto."}},{id:"vism-3.4",pali:"Aya\u1e43 pana vitth\u0101ro, ya\u1e43 t\u0101va vutta\u1e43 \"yv\u0101ssa dasasu palibodhesu palibodho atthi, ta\u1e43 upacchinditv\u0101\"ti, ettha \u2013",translations:{en:"This, however, is the detailed explanation. Regarding what was first said, \u201cFor whom there is an impediment among the ten impediments, having cut it off,\u201d here\u2014",pt:"Esta, por\xe9m, \xe9 a explica\xe7\xe3o detalhada. Quanto ao que foi dito primeiro: 'corta qualquer impedimento que tenha entre os dez impedimentos', aqui:",es:"Esta es la explicaci\xf3n detallada. En lo que respecta a lo dicho anteriormente: \xabaquel que tenga cualquiera de los diez obst\xe1culos debe cortarlo\xbb, aqu\xed [se explica]:"}},{id:"vism-3.5",pali:"Kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nad\u0101yaka\u1e43 kaly\u0101\u1e47amitta\u1e43 upasa\u1e45kamitv\u0101ti ettha pana duvidha\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 sabbatthakakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 p\u0101rih\u0101riyakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\xf1ca. Tattha sabbatthakakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101ma bhikkhusa\u1e45gh\u0101d\u012bsu mett\u0101 mara\u1e47assati ca. Asubhasa\xf1\xf1\u0101tipi eke.",translations:{en:"Now, here in the text beginning 'having approached a good friend, a giver of a meditation subject,' the meditation subject is of two kinds: the meditation subject suitable for all situations and the meditation subject to be constantly maintained. Among these, loving-kindness towards the community of monks and others, and mindfulness of death, are called the meditation subject suitable for all situations. Some also say that the perception of unattractiveness is a meditation subject suitable for all situations.",pt:"Na frase 'tendo se aproximado de um belo amigo que d\xe1 um tema de medita\xe7\xe3o', existem dois tipos de temas de medita\xe7\xe3o: o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o universalmente \xfatil (sabbatthakakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na) e o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o a ser constantemente mantido (p\u0101rih\u0101riyakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na). Entre eles, o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o universalmente \xfatil refere-se \xe0 amor-bondade (mett\u0101) em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 comunidade de monges e outros, e \xe0 medita\xe7\xe3o sobre a morte (mara\u1e47assati). Alguns dizem que a percep\xe7\xe3o da impureza do corpo (asubhasa\xf1\xf1\u0101) tamb\xe9m \xe9 um deles.",es:"Respecto a la frase \"Habi\xe9ndose acercado a un buen amigo (kaly\u0101\u1e47amitta) que otorga el tema de meditaci\xf3n\", existen dos tipos de temas de meditaci\xf3n: el tema universal (sabbatthaka-kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na) y el tema de pr\xe1ctica constante (p\u0101rih\u0101riya-kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na). Entre ellos, el tema universal consiste en la amorosa bondad (mett\u0101) hacia la comunidad de monjes y otros, y el recuerdo de la muerte (mara\u1e47assati). Algunos tambi\xe9n incluyen la percepci\xf3n de lo impuro (asubhasa\xf1\xf1\u0101)."}},{id:"vism-3.6",pali:"Kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nikena hi bhikkhun\u0101 pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 t\u0101va paricchinditv\u0101 s\u012bma\u1e6d\u1e6dhakabhikkhusa\u1e45ghe sukhit\u0101 hontu aby\u0101pajj\u0101ti mett\u0101 bh\u0101vetabb\u0101. Tato s\u012bma\u1e6d\u1e6dhakadevat\u0101su. Tato gocarag\u0101mamhi issarajane. Tato tattha manusse up\u0101d\u0101ya sabbasattesu. So hi bhikkhusa\u1e45ghe mett\u0101ya sahav\u0101s\u012bna\u1e43 muducittata\u1e43 janeti. Athassa te sukhasa\u1e43v\u0101s\u0101 honti. S\u012bma\u1e6d\u1e6dhakadevat\u0101su mett\u0101ya mudukatacitt\u0101hi devat\u0101hi dhammik\u0101ya rakkh\u0101ya susa\u1e43vihitarakkho hoti. Gocarag\u0101mamhi issarajane mett\u0101ya mudukatacittasant\u0101nehi issarehi dhammik\u0101ya rakkh\u0101ya surakkhitaparikkh\u0101ro hoti. Tattha manussesu mett\u0101ya pas\u0101ditacittehi tehi aparibh\u016bto hutv\u0101 vicarati. Sabbasattesu mett\u0101ya sabbattha appa\u1e6dihatac\u0101ro hoti. Mara\u1e47assatiy\u0101 pana avassa\u1e43 may\u0101 maritabbanti cintento anesana\u1e43 pah\u0101ya upar\u016bpari va\u1e0d\u1e0dham\u0101nasa\u1e43vego anol\u012bnavuttiko hoti. Asubhasa\xf1\xf1\u0101paricitacittassa panassa dibb\u0101nipi \u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni lobhavasena citta\u1e43 na pariy\u0101diyanti.",translations:{en:"For a monk devoted to meditation should, first of all, having delimited the scope, develop loving-kindness towards the community of monks within the boundary, thinking: 'May they be happy, may they be free from distress.' Then, towards the deities within the boundary. Then, towards the ruling people in the alms-village. Then, towards all beings, beginning with the humans there. Indeed, by means of loving-kindness towards the community of monks, he generates a gentleness of heart in his fellow residents. Then they become pleasant to live with for him. By means of loving-kindness towards the deities of the boundary, he becomes one who is well-protected with righteous protection by those deities whose minds have been made gentle. By means of loving-kindness towards the ruling people in the alms-village, he becomes one whose requisites are well-protected with righteous protection by those rulers whose mental continuums have been made gentle. By means of loving-kindness towards the people there, he moves about without being despised by those people whose minds have been made confident. By means of loving-kindness towards all beings, he becomes one whose movement is unobstructed everywhere. Furthermore, with mindfulness of death, reflecting, 'I must surely die,' having abandoned improper seeking, he has a sense of urgency that grows ever stronger and becomes one whose conduct is unshrinking. And for one whose mind is familiar with the perception of unattractiveness, even divine objects do not overwhelm his mind through the power of greed.",pt:"Pois, pelo monge que pratica a medita\xe7\xe3o, primeiramente, tendo delimitado o espa\xe7o, deve-se desenvolver a amor-bondade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 comunidade de monges dentro desse limite, pensando: 'Que eles sejam felizes, livres de m\xe1 vontade'. Depois, em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s divindades dentro desse limite. Em seguida, em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s pessoas influentes na aldeia onde esmola comida. Depois, come\xe7ando pelas pessoas dali, em rela\xe7\xe3o a todos os seres sencientes. Pois, atrav\xe9s da amor-bondade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 comunidade de monges, ele gera suavidade mental em seus co-residentes. Assim, torna-se agrad\xe1vel viver com eles. Atrav\xe9s da amor-bondade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s divindades dentro do limite, ele \xe9 bem protegido pelas divindades cujas mentes se tornaram suaves, com uma prote\xe7\xe3o justa. Atrav\xe9s da amor-bondade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s pessoas influentes na aldeia onde esmola comida, seus utens\xedlios s\xe3o bem guardados pelos governantes cujas mentes se tornaram suaves, com uma prote\xe7\xe3o justa. Atrav\xe9s da amor-bondade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s pessoas dali, ele caminha sem ser molestado por aqueles cujas mentes se tornaram confiantes. Atrav\xe9s da amor-bondade em rela\xe7\xe3o a todos os seres sencientes, ele viaja por toda parte sem obstru\xe7\xf5es. Pela medita\xe7\xe3o sobre a morte, pensando 'certamente devo morrer', ele abandona os meios de vida incorretos e, com um senso de urg\xeancia cada vez maior, torna-se diligente em sua conduta. Para aquele cuja mente est\xe1 familiarizada com a percep\xe7\xe3o da impureza do corpo, mesmo os objetos celestiais n\xe3o dominam sua mente com cobi\xe7a.",es:"Ciertamente, el monje que practica la meditaci\xf3n primero debe desarrollar la amorosa bondad delimitando el \xe1rea, deseando que \"los monjes que residen dentro de los l\xedmites del monasterio sean felices y est\xe9n libres de aflicci\xf3n\". Luego, hacia las deidades de los l\xedmites; despu\xe9s, hacia las personas prominentes en la aldea de limosna; y finalmente, comenzando por las personas de all\xed, hacia todos los seres. Pues, mediante la amorosa bondad hacia la comunidad de monjes, genera docilidad en el coraz\xf3n de sus compa\xf1eros de vida; entonces, su convivencia se vuelve placentera. Mediante la amorosa bondad hacia las deidades locales, estas, con corazones suavizados, le brindan una protecci\xf3n justa y bien dispuesta. Mediante la amorosa bondad hacia los l\xedderes de la aldea, estos, con mentes d\xf3ciles, protegen debidamente sus requisitos mon\xe1sticos. A trav\xe9s de la amorosa bondad hacia los habitantes de la aldea, camina libre de hostilidad por parte de ellos, quienes tienen corazones purificados. Con la amorosa bondad hacia todos los seres, su andar no tiene obst\xe1culos en ninguna parte. Adem\xe1s, al reflexionar mediante el recuerdo de la muerte que \"ciertamente debo morir\", abandona la b\xfasqueda inapropiada de recursos, incrementando su urgencia espiritual (sa\u1e43vega) y manteniendo una conducta diligente. Para aquel cuyo coraz\xf3n est\xe1 familiarizado con la percepci\xf3n de lo impuro, ni siquiera los objetos celestiales subyugan su mente mediante la codicia."}},{id:"vism-3.7",pali:"Piyo garu bh\u0101van\u012byo, vatt\u0101 ca vacanakkhamo; Gambh\u012bra\xf1ca katha\u1e43 katt\u0101, no ca\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne niyojakoti.",translations:{en:"He is dear, venerable, and worthy of esteem, an admonisher and patient of speech, a speaker of profound discourse, and one who does not engage you in a wrong place.",pt:"\"Ele \xe9 am\xe1vel, respeit\xe1vel e vener\xe1vel; um conselheiro que aceita conselhos; capaz de proferir discursos profundos e que nunca induz ao que \xe9 inadequado.\"",es:"Es amable, respetable y digno de estima; es un consejero y es paciente ante las cr\xedticas; habla sobre temas profundos y nunca incita a lo que no es provechoso."}},{id:"vism-3.8",pali:"Evam\u0101digu\u1e47asamann\u0101gata\u1e43 ekantena hitesi\u1e43 vuddhipakkhe \u1e6dhita\u1e43 kaly\u0101\u1e47amitta\u1e43.",translations:{en:"...a good friend who is endowed with such virtues, solely intent on one's welfare, and established in the faction of growth.",pt:"Um belo amigo \xe9 aquele dotado de qualidades como estas, que deseja absolutamente o bem-estar alheio e se posiciona do lado do crescimento espiritual.",es:"Se refiere al buen amigo que est\xe1 dotado de tales cualidades, que busca exclusivamente el bienestar de los dem\xe1s y se mantiene firme en el bando del progreso espiritual (virtud, concentraci\xf3n y sabidur\xeda)."}},{id:"vism-3.9",pali:"\"Mama\u1e43 hi, \u0101nanda, kaly\u0101\u1e47amitta\u1e43 \u0101gamma j\u0101tidhamm\u0101 satt\u0101 j\u0101tiy\u0101 parimuccant\u012b\"ti \u0101divacanato pana samm\u0101sambuddhoyeva sabb\u0101k\u0101rasampanno kaly\u0101\u1e47amitto. Tasm\u0101 tasmi\u1e43 sati tasseva bhagavato santike gahitakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 sugahita\u1e43 hoti. Parinibbute pana tasmi\u1e43 as\u012btiy\u0101 mah\u0101s\u0101vakesu yo dharati, tassa santike gahetu\u1e43 va\u1e6d\u1e6dati. Tasmi\u1e43 asati ya\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 gahetuk\u0101mo hoti, tasseva vasena catukkapa\xf1cakajjh\u0101n\u0101ni nibbattetv\u0101 jh\u0101napada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 vipassana\u1e43 va\u1e0d\u1e0dhetv\u0101 \u0101savakkhayappattassa kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101savassa santike gahetabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"From the saying beginning, 'Indeed, \u0100nanda, by relying on me as a good friend, beings subject to birth are freed from birth,' it follows that the Perfectly Self-Enlightened One is the good friend complete in all aspects. Therefore, while he is present, a meditation subject taken in the presence of that very Blessed One is well-taken. But when he has attained Parinibb\u0101na, it is proper to take it from whichever of the eighty great disciples is still living. If such a one is not present, one who wishes to take a meditation subject should, by means of that very subject, produce the fourfold and fivefold jh\u0101nas, develop insight that has jh\u0101na as its proximate cause, and then take it in the presence of one who has destroyed the taints, who has reached the destruction of the cankers.",pt:"Mas, devido a ensinamentos como: 'De fato, \u0100nanda, ao se apoiarem em mim como um belo amigo, os seres sujeitos ao nascimento libertam-se do nascimento', somente o Buda Perfeitamente Desperto \xe9 o belo amigo dotado de todas as qualidades. Portanto, enquanto ele estiver vivo, um tema de medita\xe7\xe3o recebido na presen\xe7a do pr\xf3prio Aben\xe7oado \xe9 perfeitamente recebido. Mas, ap\xf3s o seu parinibb\u0101na, \xe9 apropriado receb\xea-lo na presen\xe7a de qualquer um dos oitenta grandes disc\xedpulos que ainda esteja vivo. Quando nenhum deles estiver vivo, deve-se receb\xea-lo na presen\xe7a de um Arahant (kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sava) que destruiu as impurezas mentais, o qual, por meio daquele mesmo tema de medita\xe7\xe3o que se deseja praticar, tenha produzido os quatro ou cinco jh\u0101nas e, tendo feito do jh\u0101na a causa pr\xf3xima, tenha desenvolvido a vis\xe3o libertadora e alcan\xe7ado a destrui\xe7\xe3o das impurezas.",es:"\xabAnanda, es gracias a m\xed como buen amigo que los seres sujetos al nacimiento se liberan del nacimiento\xbb, por tales palabras, solo el Buda Perfectamente Iluminado es el buen amigo dotado de todas las cualidades. Por lo tanto, mientras \xe9l est\xe1 presente, el tema de meditaci\xf3n recibido directamente del Bendito es el mejor recibido. Una vez que el Bendito ha alcanzado el Parinibbana, conviene recibirlo de uno de los ochenta grandes disc\xedpulos que a\xfan viva. Si no los hay, debe recibirse de un Arahant (kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sava) que haya alcanzado los cuatro o cinco Jhanas, haya desarrollado la visi\xf3n cabal basada en el Jhana y haya llegado a la destrucci\xf3n de las impurezas."}},{id:"vism-3.10",pali:"Tasm\u0101 sace kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sava\u1e43 labhati, icceta\u1e43 kusala\u1e43, no ce labhati, an\u0101g\u0101misakad\u0101g\u0101misot\u0101pannajh\u0101nal\u0101bh\u012bputhujjanatipi\u1e6dakadharadvipi\u1e6dakadharaekapi\u1e6dakadharesu purimassa purimassa santike. Ekapi\u1e6dakadharepi asati yassa ekasa\u1e45g\u012btipi a\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101ya saddhi\u1e43 pagu\u1e47\u0101, aya\xf1ca lajj\u012b hoti, tassa santike gahetabba\u1e43. Evar\u016bpo hi tantidharo va\u1e43s\u0101nurakkhako pave\u1e47\u012bp\u0101lako \u0101cariyo \u0101cariyamatikova hoti, na attanomatiko hoti. Teneva por\u0101\u1e47akatther\u0101 \"lajj\u012b rakkhissati lajj\u012b rakkhissat\u012b\"ti tikkhattu\u1e43 \u0101ha\u1e43su.",translations:{en:"Therefore, if one finds one who has destroyed the taints, that is excellent. If one does not, then one should learn from a Non-returner, a Once-returner, a Stream-enterer, a worldling who has attained jh\u0101na, one who knows the three Pi\u1e6dakas, one who knows two Pi\u1e6dakas, or one who knows one Pi\u1e6daka\u2014in the presence of each preceding one in turn. If even one who knows one Pi\u1e6daka is not available, one should learn in the presence of a person who is proficient in even a single Nik\u0101ya together with its commentary, and who is also conscientious. For such a person\u2014a bearer of the scriptures, a preserver of the lineage, a guardian of the teaching-tradition\u2014is a teacher who adheres to the teachers' view and is not one who follows his own opinion. For that very reason, the ancient elders said three times: 'The conscientious one will protect! The conscientious one will protect!'",pt:"Portanto, se se encontrar um Arahant, isso \xe9 excelente. Se n\xe3o, deve-se buscar na presen\xe7a do anterior na ordem de preced\xeancia entre: o N\xe3o-retornante (An\u0101g\u0101mi), o que Retorna uma vez (Sakad\u0101g\u0101mi), o que Entrou na corrente (Sot\u0101panna), o cidad\xe3o comum que obteve os jh\u0101nas, o mestre dos Tr\xeas Pi\u1e6dakas, o mestre de Dois Pi\u1e6dakas e o mestre de Um Pi\u1e6daka. Se nem mesmo um mestre de Um Pi\u1e6daka estiver dispon\xedvel, deve-se receb\xea-lo na presen\xe7a de algu\xe9m para quem ao menos uma \xfanica cole\xe7\xe3o (Nik\u0101ya), junto com seu coment\xe1rio, seja familiar, e que seja consciencioso (lajj\u012b). Pois um mestre desse tipo, que preserva os textos sagrados, protege a linhagem e guarda a tradi\xe7\xe3o, fala apenas de acordo com o entendimento dos mestres, e n\xe3o segundo sua pr\xf3pria opini\xe3o. Por essa raz\xe3o, os antigos anci\xe3os disseram tr\xeas vezes: 'O consciencioso proteger\xe1 a Dispensa\xe7\xe3o, o consciencioso a proteger\xe1'.",es:"Por lo tanto, si se encuentra a un Arahant, es excelente. Si no se encuentra, se debe recurrir a uno de los siguientes, en orden de preferencia: un No-Retornante, un Una-Vez-Retornante, un Entrado-en-la-Corriente, un mundano que posee Jhana, un conocedor de los tres Pitakas, de dos, o de uno. Si no hay ni siquiera un conocedor de un Pitaka, debe recibirse de alguien que sea experto al menos en una colecci\xf3n (Nikaya) junto con su comentario, y que adem\xe1s sea una persona \xedntegra y escrupulosa (lajj\u012b). Pues tal maestro, portador de las escrituras, protector del linaje y guardi\xe1n de la tradici\xf3n, ense\xf1a solo de acuerdo con la doctrina de los maestros y no seg\xfan su propia opini\xf3n. Por esta misma raz\xf3n, los antiguos maestros dijeron tres veces: \xabEl escrupuloso proteger\xe1 la religi\xf3n\xbb."}},{id:"vism-3.11",pali:"Pubbe vuttakh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sav\u0101dayo cettha attan\u0101 adhigatamaggameva \u0101cikkhanti. Bahussuto pana ta\u1e43 ta\u1e43 \u0101cariya\u1e43 upasa\u1e45kamitv\u0101 uggahaparipucch\u0101na\u1e43 visodhitatt\u0101 ito cito ca sutta\xf1ca k\u0101ra\u1e47a\xf1ca sallakkhetv\u0101 sapp\u0101y\u0101sapp\u0101ya\u1e43 yojetv\u0101 gahana\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne gacchanto mah\u0101hatth\u012b viya mah\u0101magga\u1e43 dassento kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 kathessati. Tasm\u0101 evar\u016bpa\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nad\u0101yaka\u1e43 kaly\u0101\u1e47amitta\u1e43 upasa\u1e45kamitv\u0101 tassa vattapa\u1e6dipatti\u1e43 katv\u0101 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 gahetabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Among these, the aforementioned destroyers of the taints and so on declare only the path they themselves have attained. A very learned person, however, having approached various teachers and having clarified his learning and questioning, having marked well the Sutta passages and the reasoning from here and there, and having applied what is suitable and unsuitable, will teach the meditation subject like a great elephant that, when going into a dense place, shows a great path. Therefore, having approached such a good friend who is a giver of a meditation subject, and having performed the duties towards him, one should receive the meditation subject.",pt:"Dentre estes, os j\xe1 mencionados que destru\xedram as m\xe1culas (kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101savas) e outros ensinam apenas o caminho que eles pr\xf3prios alcan\xe7aram. No entanto, um mestre de grande conhecimento (bahussuta), por ter se aproximado de v\xe1rios professores e esclarecido as li\xe7\xf5es e perguntas, e por ter examinado os discursos (suttas) e as raz\xf5es de uma parte e de outra, discernindo o que \xe9 adequado e inadequado, ensinar\xe1 o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o (kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na) mostrando o caminho como um grande elefante que avan\xe7a por uma floresta densa. Portanto, deve-se aproximar de um amigo admir\xe1vel (kaly\u0101\u1e47amitta) que conceda o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o, cumprir os deveres para com ele e receber o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o.",es:"En este contexto, los ya mencionados Arahants y dem\xe1s disc\xedpulos superiores ense\xf1an el camino que ellos mismos han alcanzado. Sin embargo, un monje de gran conocimiento (bahussuto), por haber acudido a diversos maestros y aclarado sus dudas mediante el estudio y la indagaci\xf3n, podr\xe1 explicar el tema de meditaci\xf3n se\xf1alando el gran camino \u2014como un gran elefante que avanza por un lugar intrincado\u2014 tras haber discernido las escrituras y sus razones, y haber determinado lo que es adecuado o inadecuado. Por lo tanto, habi\xe9ndose acercado a tal buen amigo que otorga el tema de meditaci\xf3n y habiendo cumplido con los deberes hacia \xe9l, se debe recibir el tema de meditaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-3.12",pali:"Id\u0101ni attano cariy\u0101nuk\u016blanti ettha cariy\u0101ti cha cariy\u0101 r\u0101gacariy\u0101, dosacariy\u0101, mohacariy\u0101, saddh\u0101cariy\u0101, buddhicariy\u0101, vitakkacariy\u0101ti. Keci pana r\u0101g\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 sa\u1e43saggasannip\u0101tavasena apar\u0101pi catasso, tath\u0101 saddh\u0101d\u012bnanti im\u0101hi a\u1e6d\u1e6dhahi saddhi\u1e43 cuddasa icchanti. Eva\u1e43 pana bhede vuccam\u0101ne r\u0101g\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 saddh\u0101d\u012bhipi sa\u1e43sagga\u1e43 katv\u0101 anek\u0101 cariy\u0101 honti, tasm\u0101 sa\u1e45khepena cha\u1e37eva cariy\u0101 veditabb\u0101. Cariy\u0101, pakati, ussannat\u0101ti atthato eka\u1e43. T\u0101sa\u1e43 vasena cha\u1e37eva puggal\u0101 honti r\u0101gacarito, dosacarito, mohacarito, saddh\u0101carito, buddhicarito, vitakkacaritoti.",translations:{en:"Now, regarding the phrase 'suitable for one's own temperament': here, 'temperament' refers to six temperaments: lustful temperament, hateful temperament, deluded temperament, faithful temperament, intelligent temperament, and discursive temperament. Some, however, desire fourteen temperaments, positing four others by way of the combination and conjunction of lust, etc., and similarly four more from faith, etc., thus making eight additional temperaments. However, if the division is spoken of in this way, by making a combination of lust, etc., with faith, etc., there would be many temperaments. Therefore, in brief, only six temperaments should be understood. 'Temperament' (cariy\u0101), 'nature' (pakati), and 'predominance' (ussannat\u0101) are one in meaning. According to these, there are six types of individuals: one of lustful temperament, one of hateful temperament, one of deluded temperament, one of faithful temperament, one of intelligent temperament, and one of discursive temperament.",pt:"Agora, quanto \xe0 express\xe3o 'adequado ao seu pr\xf3prio temperamento' (cariy\u0101nuk\u016bla), existem seis tipos de temperamento (cariy\u0101): o temperamento ganancioso (r\u0101gacariy\u0101), o temperamento col\xe9rico (dosacariy\u0101), o temperamento iludido (mohacariy\u0101), o temperamento fiel (saddh\u0101cariy\u0101), o temperamento intelectual (buddhicariy\u0101) e o temperamento especulativo (vitakkacariy\u0101). Alguns mestres, no entanto, admitem quatorze tipos, combinando estes com mais quatro temperamentos decorrentes da mistura e associa\xe7\xe3o da gan\xe2ncia e outros, e da mesma forma quatro temperamentos para a f\xe9 e outros. Mas se tal divis\xe3o for feita, ao misturar a gan\xe2ncia e outros com a f\xe9 e outros, haver\xe1 in\xfameros temperamentos; portanto, em resumo, deve-se conhecer apenas seis temperamentos. Temperamento (cariy\u0101), natureza intr\xednseca (pakati) e predomin\xe2ncia (ussannat\u0101) t\xeam o mesmo significado. De acordo com eles, existem apenas seis tipos de pessoas: a pessoa de temperamento ganancioso, de temperamento col\xe9rico, de temperamento iludido, de temperamento fiel, de temperamento intelectual e de temperamento especulativo.",es:"Ahora, respecto a 'acorde a su propio temperamento', aqu\xed hay seis temperamentos: temperamento de deseo (r\u0101gacariy\u0101), temperamento de odio (dosacariy\u0101), temperamento de enga\xf1o (mohacariy\u0101), temperamento de fe (saddh\u0101cariy\u0101), temperamento de inteligencia (buddhicariy\u0101) y temperamento de pensamiento especulativo (vitakkacariy\u0101). Algunos, debido a la mezcla y combinaci\xf3n de deseo y dem\xe1s, aceptan otros cuatro; y de la misma manera para la fe y dem\xe1s, sumando catorce junto con estos ocho. Si se hiciera tal distinci\xf3n, resultar\xeda en innumerables temperamentos al combinar el deseo, etc., con la fe, etc. Por lo tanto, en resumen, deben conocerse solo seis temperamentos. 'Temperamento' (cariy\u0101), 'naturaleza' (pakati) y 'predominancia' (ussannat\u0101) tienen el mismo significado. Seg\xfan estos, hay solo seis tipos de personas: la persona de temperamento de deseo, de odio, de enga\xf1o, de fe, de inteligencia y de pensamiento especulativo."}},{id:"vism-3.13",pali:"Sesa\u1e43 r\u0101gacaritassa vuttasadisamev\u0101ti ida\u1e43 vitakkacaritassa sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. Aya\u1e43 attano cariy\u0101nuk\u016blanti ettha \u0101gatacariy\u0101na\u1e43 pabhedanid\u0101navibh\u0101vanasapp\u0101yaparicchedato vitth\u0101ro. Na ca t\u0101va cariy\u0101nuk\u016bla\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 sabb\u0101k\u0101rena \u0101vikata\u1e43. Ta\xf1hi anantarassa m\u0101tik\u0101padassa vitth\u0101re sayameva \u0101vibhavissati.",translations:{en:"The rest is just as was said for one of a lustful temperament. This is what is suitable for one of a speculative temperament. This is the detailed explanation\u2014by way of the sections on classification, cause, analysis, and suitability\u2014of the temperaments that have been discussed in the context of the phrase 'in accordance with one's own temperament.' And yet, the meditation subject suitable for one's temperament has not yet been revealed in all its aspects. For it will become clear by itself in the detailed explanation of the immediately following matrix heading.",pt:"O restante \xe9 semelhante ao que foi dito para o temperamento cobi\xe7oso (r\u0101gacarita). Isso \xe9 o que \xe9 adequado para algu\xe9m de temperamento discursivo. Esta \xe9 a explica\xe7\xe3o detalhada sobre os temperamentos mencionados na frase 'adequado ao pr\xf3prio temperamento' (attano cariy\u0101nuk\u016bla\u1e43), por meio da defini\xe7\xe3o de suas divis\xf5es, origens, manifesta\xe7\xf5es e adequa\xe7\xf5es. Contudo, o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o adequado ao temperamento ainda n\xe3o foi revelado em todos os seus aspectos. Pois ele se manifestar\xe1 por si mesmo na explica\xe7\xe3o detalhada do termo seguinte da matriz (m\u0101tik\u0101pada).",es:"El resto es similar a lo dicho para el temperamento codicioso. Esto es lo adecuado para el temperamento especulativo. Esta es la explicaci\xf3n detallada seg\xfan la clasificaci\xf3n, el origen, la aclaraci\xf3n y la adecuaci\xf3n de los temperamentos que aparecen en la frase \"conforme a su propio temperamento\". Sin embargo, el tema de meditaci\xf3n adecuado al temperamento a\xfan no se ha manifestado en todos sus aspectos. Esto se har\xe1 evidente por s\xed mismo en la explicaci\xf3n detallada del siguiente enunciado de la matriz."}},{id:"vism-3.14",pali:"Tasm\u0101 ya\u1e43 vutta\u1e43 catt\u0101l\u012bs\u0101ya kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu a\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 gahetv\u0101ti ettha sa\u1e45kh\u0101taniddesato, upac\u0101rappan\u0101vahato, jh\u0101nappabhedato, samatikkamato, va\u1e0d\u1e0dhan\u0101va\u1e0d\u1e0dhanato, \u0101ramma\u1e47ato, bh\u016bmito, gaha\u1e47ato, paccayato, cariy\u0101nuk\u016blatoti imehi t\u0101va dasah\u0101k\u0101rehi kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101navinicchayo veditabbo.",translations:{en:"Therefore, regarding what was said\u2014'having taken one of the forty meditation subjects'\u2014herein the discernment of meditation subjects should be known for now by these ten aspects: by way of enumeration and explanation, by way of leading to access and absorption, by way of the classification of jh\u0101nas, by way of transcending, by way of development and non-development, by way of the object, by way of the plane, by way of grasping, by way of conditions, and by way of suitability to one's temperament.",pt:"Portanto, quanto ao que foi dito: 'tendo tomado um dos quarenta temas de medita\xe7\xe3o', aqui, a determina\xe7\xe3o dos temas de medita\xe7\xe3o deve ser compreendida por meio destes dez aspectos: (1) pela enumera\xe7\xe3o num\xe9rica, (2) por conduzir ao acesso ou \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o, (3) pela classifica\xe7\xe3o dos jhanas, (4) pela transcend\xeancia, (5) pela expans\xe3o ou n\xe3o expans\xe3o, (6) pelo objeto, (7) pelo plano de exist\xeancia, (8) pela apreens\xe3o, (9) pela condi\xe7\xe3o, e (10) pela adequa\xe7\xe3o ao temperamento.",es:"Por tanto, con respecto a lo que se ha dicho: \"habiendo tomado uno de los cuarenta temas de meditaci\xf3n\", el an\xe1lisis de los temas de meditaci\xf3n debe entenderse primeramente mediante estos diez modos: por la enumeraci\xf3n y explicaci\xf3n, por la capacidad de conducir al acceso o a la absorci\xf3n, por la clasificaci\xf3n de los jh\u0101nas, por la trascendencia, por el desarrollo o falta de desarrollo, por el objeto, por el plano, por la forma de aprehenderlos, por la condici\xf3n y por la adecuaci\xf3n al temperamento."}},{id:"vism-3.15",pali:"Tattha sa\u1e45kh\u0101taniddesatoti catt\u0101l\u012bs\u0101ya kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nes\u016bti hi vutta\u1e43, tatrim\u0101ni catt\u0101l\u012bsa kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni dasa kasi\u1e47\u0101, dasa asubh\u0101, dasa anussatiyo, catt\u0101ro brahmavih\u0101r\u0101, catt\u0101ro \u0101rupp\u0101, ek\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101, eka\u1e43 vavatth\u0101nanti.",translations:{en:"Therein, as to 'by way of enumeration and explanation': for it was said, 'among forty meditation subjects.' Therein, these are the forty meditation subjects: ten kasi\u1e47as, ten foulnesses, ten recollections, four divine abidings, four formless states, one perception, and one defining.",pt:"Entre estes, quanto \xe0 'enumera\xe7\xe3o num\xe9rica': foi dito 'entre os quarenta temas de medita\xe7\xe3o'. Neles, estes s\xe3o os quarenta temas de medita\xe7\xe3o: dez kasi\u1e47as, dez impurezas (asubha), dez recorda\xe7\xf5es (anussati), quatro moradas divinas (brahmavih\u0101ra), quatro dhammas imateriais (\u0101ruppa), uma percep\xe7\xe3o (sa\xf1\xf1\u0101) e uma defini\xe7\xe3o (vavatth\u0101na).",es:"En cuanto a \"por la enumeraci\xf3n y explicaci\xf3n\", se ha dicho: \"en los cuarenta temas de meditaci\xf3n\". Estos cuarenta temas de meditaci\xf3n son: los diez kasi\u1e47as, las diez impurezas, las diez recordaciones, las cuatro moradas divinas, las cuatro esferas inmateriales, la \xfanica percepci\xf3n y el \xfanico an\xe1lisis."}},{id:"vism-3.16",pali:"Tattha pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47a\u1e43, \u0101pokasi\u1e47a\u1e43, tejokasi\u1e47a\u1e43, v\u0101yokasi\u1e47a\u1e43, n\u012blakasi\u1e47a\u1e43, p\u012btakasi\u1e47a\u1e43, lohitakasi\u1e47a\u1e43, od\u0101takasi\u1e47a\u1e43, \u0101lokakasi\u1e47a\u1e43, paricchinn\u0101k\u0101sakasi\u1e47anti ime dasa kasi\u1e47\u0101.",translations:{en:"Therein, the earth kasi\u1e47a, water kasi\u1e47a, fire kasi\u1e47a, air kasi\u1e47a, blue kasi\u1e47a, yellow kasi\u1e47a, red kasi\u1e47a, white kasi\u1e47a, light kasi\u1e47a, and the delimited-space kasi\u1e47a\u2014these are the ten kasi\u1e47as.",pt:"Entre estes, o kasi\u1e47a da terra, o kasi\u1e47a da \xe1gua, o kasi\u1e47a do fogo, o kasi\u1e47a do ar, o kasi\u1e47a do azul, o kasi\u1e47a do amarelo, o kasi\u1e47a do vermelho, o kasi\u1e47a do branco, o kasi\u1e47a da luz e o kasi\u1e47a do espa\xe7o limitado \u2014 estes s\xe3o os dez kasi\u1e47as.",es:"Entre ellos, el kasi\u1e47a de tierra, el kasi\u1e47a de agua, el kasi\u1e47a de fuego, el kasi\u1e47a de aire, el kasi\u1e47a azul, el kasi\u1e47a amarillo, el kasi\u1e47a rojo, el kasi\u1e47a blanco, el kasi\u1e47a de luz y el kasi\u1e47a de espacio limitado; estos son los diez kasi\u1e47as."}},{id:"vism-3.17",pali:"Uddhum\u0101taka\u1e43, vin\u012blaka\u1e43, vipubbaka\u1e43, vicchiddaka\u1e43, vikkh\u0101yitaka\u1e43, vikkhittaka\u1e43, hatavikkhittaka\u1e43, lohitaka\u1e43, pu\u1e37avaka\u1e43, a\u1e6d\u1e6dhikanti ime dasa asubh\u0101.",translations:{en:"The bloated, the livid, the festering, the cut-up, the gnawed, the scattered, the hacked-and-scattered, the bloody, the worm-infested, and the skeleton\u2014these are the ten foulnesses.",pt:"O cad\xe1ver inchado, o cad\xe1ver l\xedvido, o cad\xe1ver purulento, o cad\xe1ver cortado ao meio, o cad\xe1ver dilacerado, o cad\xe1ver disperso, o cad\xe1ver retalhado e disperso, o cad\xe1ver sangrento, o cad\xe1ver infestado de vermes e o esqueleto \u2014 estas s\xe3o as dez impurezas (asubha).",es:"El cad\xe1ver hinchado, el amoratado, el purulento, el fracturado, el devorado, el disperso, el mutilado y disperso, el sangriento, el infestado de gusanos y el esqueleto; estas son las diez impurezas."}},{id:"vism-3.18",pali:"Buddh\u0101nussati, dhamm\u0101nussati, sa\u1e45gh\u0101nussati, s\u012bl\u0101nussati, c\u0101g\u0101nussati, devat\u0101nussati, mara\u1e47\u0101nussati, k\u0101yagat\u0101sati, \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassati, upasam\u0101nussat\u012bti im\u0101 dasa anussatiyo.",translations:{en:"Recollection of the Buddha, recollection of the Dhamma, recollection of the Sa\u1e45gha, recollection of virtue, recollection of generosity, recollection of deities, recollection of death, mindfulness directed to the body, mindfulness of breathing, and recollection of peace\u2014these are the ten recollections.",pt:"A recorda\xe7\xe3o do Buda, a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Dhamma, a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Sangha, a recorda\xe7\xe3o da virtude, a recorda\xe7\xe3o da generosidade, a recorda\xe7\xe3o dos devas, a recorda\xe7\xe3o da morte, a aten\xe7\xe3o plena voltada ao corpo, a aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o e a recorda\xe7\xe3o da paz \u2014 estas s\xe3o as dez recorda\xe7\xf5es (anussati).",es:"La recordaci\xf3n del Buddha, la recordaci\xf3n del Dhamma, la recordaci\xf3n de la Sa\u1e45gha, la recordaci\xf3n de la virtud, la recordaci\xf3n de la generosidad, la recordaci\xf3n de los devas, la recordaci\xf3n de la muerte, la atenci\xf3n al cuerpo, la atenci\xf3n a la respiraci\xf3n y la recordaci\xf3n de la paz; estas son las diez recordaciones."}},{id:"vism-3.19",pali:"Mett\u0101, karu\u1e47\u0101, mudit\u0101, upekkh\u0101ti ime catt\u0101ro brahmavih\u0101r\u0101.",translations:{en:"Loving-kindness, compassion, sympathetic joy, and equanimity\u2014these are the four divine abidings.",pt:"O amor-bondade (mett\u0101), a compaix\xe3o (karu\u1e47\u0101), a alegria altru\xedsta (mudit\u0101) e a equanimidade (upekkh\u0101) \u2014 estas s\xe3o as quatro moradas divinas (brahmavih\u0101ra).",es:"El amor benevolente, la compasi\xf3n, la alegr\xeda altruista y la ecuanimidad; estas son las cuatro moradas divinas."}},{id:"vism-3.20",pali:"\u0100k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatana\u1e43, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatana\u1e43, \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana\u1e43, nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatananti ime catt\u0101ro \u0101rupp\u0101. \u0100h\u0101re pa\u1e6dik\u016blasa\xf1\xf1\u0101 ek\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101. Catudh\u0101tuvavatth\u0101na\u1e43 eka\u1e43 vavatth\u0101nanti eva\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101taniddesato vinicchayo veditabbo.",translations:{en:"The base of infinite space, the base of infinite consciousness, the base of nothingness, and the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception\u2014these are the four formless states. The perception of loathsomeness in food is the one perception. The defining of the four elements is the one defining. Thus the discernment should be known by way of enumeration and explanation.",pt:"A esfera do espa\xe7o infinito, a esfera da consci\xeancia infinita, a esfera do nada e a esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o percep\xe7\xe3o \u2014 estes s\xe3o os quatro dhammas imateriais (\u0101ruppa). A percep\xe7\xe3o da repulsividade do alimento \xe9 a \xfanica percep\xe7\xe3o (sa\xf1\xf1\u0101). A defini\xe7\xe3o dos quatro elementos \xe9 a \xfanica defini\xe7\xe3o (vavatth\u0101na). Assim deve ser compreendida a determina\xe7\xe3o por meio da enumera\xe7\xe3o num\xe9rica.",es:"La base del espacio infinito, la base de la conciencia infinita, la base de la nada y la base de la ni percepci\xf3n ni no percepci\xf3n; estas son las cuatro esferas inmateriales. La percepci\xf3n de lo repulsivo en la comida es la \xfanica percepci\xf3n. El an\xe1lisis de los cuatro elementos es el \xfanico an\xe1lisis. De esta manera, debe entenderse el an\xe1lisis por la enumeraci\xf3n y explicaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-3.21",pali:"Upac\u0101rappan\u0101vahatoti \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 k\u0101yagat\u0101sati\xf1ca \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassati\xf1ca avases\u0101 a\u1e6d\u1e6dha anussatiyo, \u0101h\u0101re pa\u1e6dik\u016blasa\xf1\xf1\u0101, catudh\u0101tuvavatth\u0101nanti im\u0101neva hettha dasakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni upac\u0101ravah\u0101ni. Ses\u0101ni appan\u0101vah\u0101ni. Eva\u1e43 upac\u0101rappan\u0101vahato.",translations:{en:"As to 'by way of leading to access and absorption': setting aside mindfulness directed to the body and mindfulness of breathing, the remaining eight recollections, the perception of loathsomeness in food, and the defining of the four elements\u2014herein, these ten meditation subjects alone lead to access. The remaining ones lead to absorption. Thus it is by way of leading to access and absorption.",pt:"Quanto a 'conduzir ao acesso ou \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o': excluindo a aten\xe7\xe3o plena voltada ao corpo e a aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o, as oito recorda\xe7\xf5es restantes, a percep\xe7\xe3o da repulsividade do alimento e a defini\xe7\xe3o dos quatro elementos \u2014 apenas estes dez temas de medita\xe7\xe3o aqui conduzem somente ao acesso (upac\u0101ra). Os restantes conduzem \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101). Assim \xe9 a determina\xe7\xe3o por meio de conduzir ao acesso ou \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o.",es:"En cuanto a \"por la capacidad de conducir al acceso o a la absorci\xf3n\": exceptuando la atenci\xf3n al cuerpo y la atenci\xf3n a la respiraci\xf3n, las ocho recordaciones restantes, la percepci\xf3n de lo repulsivo en la comida y el an\xe1lisis de los cuatro elementos; estos diez temas de meditaci\xf3n solo conducen al acceso. Los restantes conducen a la absorci\xf3n. As\xed es por la capacidad de conducir al acceso o a la absorci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-3.22",pali:"Jh\u0101nappabhedatoti appan\u0101vahesu cettha \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassatiy\u0101 saddhi\u1e43 dasa kasi\u1e47\u0101 catukkajjh\u0101nik\u0101 honti. K\u0101yagat\u0101satiy\u0101 saddhi\u1e43 dasa asubh\u0101 pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nik\u0101. Purim\u0101 tayo brahmavih\u0101r\u0101 tikajjh\u0101nik\u0101. Catutthabrahmavih\u0101ro catt\u0101ro ca \u0101rupp\u0101 catutthajjh\u0101nik\u0101ti eva\u1e43 jh\u0101nappabhedato.",translations:{en:"By way of the classification of jh\u0101nas: Herein, among those meditation subjects leading to absorption, the ten kasi\u1e47as together with mindfulness of breathing are associated with four jh\u0101nas. The ten kinds of foulness together with mindfulness of the body are associated with the first jh\u0101na. The first three divine abidings are associated with three jh\u0101nas. The fourth divine abiding and the four formless attainments are associated with the fourth jh\u0101na. Thus, by way of the classification of jh\u0101nas.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 'classifica\xe7\xe3o dos jhanas': entre os que conduzem \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o, os dez kasi\u1e47as junto com a aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o possuem os quatro jhanas. As dez impurezas junto com a aten\xe7\xe3o plena voltada ao corpo possuem apenas o primeiro jh\u0101na. As tr\xeas primeiras moradas divinas possuem os tr\xeas primeiros jhanas. A quarta morada divina e os quatro dhammas imateriais possuem o quarto jh\u0101na. Assim \xe9 a determina\xe7\xe3o por meio da classifica\xe7\xe3o dos jhanas.",es:"En cuanto a \"por la clasificaci\xf3n de los jh\u0101nas\": entre aquellos que conducen a la absorci\xf3n, los diez kasi\u1e47as junto con la atenci\xf3n a la respiraci\xf3n pueden alcanzar los cuatro jh\u0101nas. Las diez impurezas junto con la atenci\xf3n al cuerpo alcanzan el primer jh\u0101na. Las tres primeras moradas divinas alcanzan tres jh\u0101nas. La cuarta morada divina y las cuatro esferas inmateriales alcanzan el cuarto jh\u0101na. As\xed es por la clasificaci\xf3n de los jh\u0101nas."}}]},421,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,i,t,n,s){t.exports=[{id:"vism-4.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni ya\u1e43 vutta\u1e43 \"sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101ya ananur\u016bpa\u1e43 vih\u0101ra\u1e43 pah\u0101ya anur\u016bpe vih\u0101re viharanten\u0101\"ti ettha yassa t\u0101v\u0101cariyena saddhi\u1e43 ekavih\u0101re vasato ph\u0101su hoti, tena tattheva kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 parisodhentena vasitabba\u1e43. Sace tattha ph\u0101su na hoti, yo a\xf1\xf1o g\u0101vute v\u0101 a\u1e0d\u1e0dhayojane v\u0101 yojanamattepi v\u0101 sapp\u0101yo vih\u0101ro hoti, tattha vasitabba\u1e43. Eva\xf1hi sati kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nassa kismi\xf1cideva \u1e6dh\u0101ne sandehe v\u0101 satisammose v\u0101 j\u0101te k\u0101lasseva vih\u0101re vatta\u1e43 katv\u0101 antar\u0101magge pi\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101ya caritv\u0101 bhattakiccapariyos\u0101neyeva \u0101cariyassa vasana\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 gantv\u0101 ta\u1e43divasam\u0101cariyassa santike kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 sodhetv\u0101 dutiyadivase \u0101cariya\u1e43 vanditv\u0101 nikkhamitv\u0101 antar\u0101magge pi\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101ya caritv\u0101 akilamantoyeva attano vasana\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101gantu\u1e43 sakkhissati. Yo pana yojanappam\u0101\u1e47epi ph\u0101suka\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 na labhati, tena kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne sabba\u1e43 ga\u1e47\u1e6dhi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 chinditv\u0101 suvisuddha\u1e43 \u0101vajjanapa\u1e6dibaddha\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 katv\u0101 d\u016brampi gantv\u0101 sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101ya ananur\u016bpa\u1e43 vih\u0101ra\u1e43 pah\u0101ya anur\u016bpe vih\u0101re vih\u0101tabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now, regarding what was said, 'Having abandoned a monastery unsuitable for the development of concentration, one should dwell in a suitable monastery': Herein, for whichever meditator it is comfortable to live in the same monastery with his teacher, he should dwell right there, purifying the meditation subject. If it is not comfortable there, he should dwell in whatever other suitable monastery there is, a g\u0101vuta, half a yojana, or even a yojana away. For, this being so, if doubt or forgetfulness should arise in any place regarding the meditation subject, he can perform his duties in the monastery early, wander for alms on the way, and only after the meal is finished, go to the teacher's dwelling place. Having purified the meditation subject in the teacher's presence on that day, and on the second day, having paid respects to the teacher and departed, he can wander for alms on the way and will be able to return to his own dwelling place without fatigue. But whoever does not find a comfortable place even within the measure of a yojana, he, having cut off all knotty points in the meditation subject and having made the meditation subject thoroughly purified and connected with attention, should go even far, and having abandoned a monastery unsuitable for the development of concentration, should dwell in a suitable monastery.",pt:"Agora, quanto ao que foi dito: 'abandonando um mosteiro inadequado para o desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o e habitando em um mosteiro adequado' \u2014 primeiramente, se for confort\xe1vel para quem vive no mesmo mosteiro com o seu professor, ele deve habitar ali mesmo, purificando o seu tema de medita\xe7\xe3o. Se n\xe3o for confort\xe1vel ali, ele deve habitar em outro mosteiro adequado que fique a uma dist\xe2ncia de um g\u0101vuta, de meia yojana ou de at\xe9 uma yojana. Pois, sendo assim, se surgir alguma d\xfavida ou esquecimento em rela\xe7\xe3o a qualquer ponto do tema de medita\xe7\xe3o, ele poder\xe1, logo cedo, cumprir os seus deveres no mosteiro, sair para esmolar comida no caminho e, logo ap\xf3s terminar a refei\xe7\xe3o, ir \xe0 resid\xeancia do professor. Tendo purificado o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o junto ao professor durante todo aquele dia, no segundo dia ele poder\xe1 saudar o professor, partir, esmolar comida no caminho e retornar ao seu pr\xf3prio local de resid\xeancia sem se cansar. Mas se ele n\xe3o encontrar um local confort\xe1vel mesmo a uma dist\xe2ncia de uma yojana, ele deve cortar todos os pontos dif\xedceis no tema de medita\xe7\xe3o, tornando-o extremamente claro e dependente da aten\xe7\xe3o reflexiva, e ent\xe3o ir mesmo para longe, abandonando o mosteiro inadequado para o desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o e habitando em um mosteiro adequado.",es:"Ahora, respecto a lo que se dijo: \"abandonando un monasterio inadecuado para el desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n y viviendo en uno adecuado\", en este punto, si para aquel que vive en el mismo monasterio con el maestro es c\xf3modo, debe permanecer all\xed mismo purificando su tema de meditaci\xf3n. Si all\xed no es c\xf3modo, debe vivir en otro monasterio adecuado que est\xe9 a una distancia de un g& caron;vuta, media yojana o incluso a una yojana. Pues siendo as\xed, si surge duda o confusi\xf3n en alg\xfan punto del tema de meditaci\xf3n, habiendo cumplido temprano con los deberes en el monasterio, habiendo caminado por limosna en el camino y justo al finalizar la comida, podr\xe1 ir al lugar donde reside el maestro, purificar el tema de meditaci\xf3n ante el maestro ese mismo d\xeda y, al d\xeda siguiente, tras saludar al maestro, salir, pedir limosna en el camino y regresar a su propio lugar de residencia sin cansarse. Pero aquel que no encuentra un lugar c\xf3modo ni siquiera a una yojana de distancia, habiendo resuelto todas las dificultades del tema de meditaci\xf3n, habi\xe9ndolo dejado bien purificado y vinculado a la atenci\xf3n, debe ir incluso lejos, abandonar el monasterio inadecuado para el desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n y vivir en un monasterio adecuado."}},{id:"vism-4.2",pali:"Yo pana gocarag\u0101mato n\u0101tid\u016bran\u0101cc\u0101sannat\u0101d\u012bhi pa\xf1caha\u1e45gehi samann\u0101gato, aya\u1e43 anur\u016bpo n\u0101ma. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 bhagavat\u0101 \u2013 \"katha\xf1ca, bhikkhave, sen\u0101sana\u1e43 pa\xf1ca\u1e45gasamann\u0101gata\u1e43 hoti? Idha, bhikkhave, sen\u0101sana\u1e43 n\u0101tid\u016bra\u1e43 hoti n\u0101cc\u0101sanna\u1e43 gaman\u0101gamanasampanna\u1e43, div\u0101 app\u0101ki\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 ratti\u1e43 appasadda\u1e43 appanigghosa\u1e43, appa\u1e0da\u1e43samakasav\u0101t\u0101tapasar\u012bsapasamphassa\u1e43, tasmi\u1e43 kho pana sen\u0101sane viharantassa appakasireneva uppajjanti c\u012bvarapi\u1e47\u1e0dap\u0101tasen\u0101sanagil\u0101napaccayabhesajjaparikkh\u0101r\u0101. Tasmi\u1e43 kho pana sen\u0101sane ther\u0101 bhikkh\u016b viharanti bahussut\u0101 \u0101gat\u0101gam\u0101 dhammadhar\u0101 vinayadhar\u0101 m\u0101tik\u0101dhar\u0101, te k\u0101lena k\u0101la\u1e43 upasa\u1e45kamitv\u0101 paripucchati paripa\xf1hati \u2018ida\u1e43, bhante, katha\u1e43 imassa ko attho\u2019ti, tassa te \u0101yasmanto aviva\u1e6da\xf1ceva vivaranti, anutt\u0101n\u012bkata\xf1ca utt\u0101n\u012bkaronti, anekavihitesu ca ka\u1e45kha\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101niyesu dhammesu ka\u1e45kha\u1e43 pa\u1e6divinodenti. Eva\u1e43 kho, bhikkhave, sen\u0101sana\u1e43 pa\xf1ca\u1e45gasamann\u0101gata\u1e43 hot\u012b\"ti.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, that monastery which is endowed with five factors, such as being neither too far from nor too near to the alms-resort village, is called a suitable one. For this was said by the Blessed One: 'And how, bhikkhus, is a lodging endowed with five factors? Here, bhikkhus, a lodging is neither too far nor too near, and is convenient for coming and going; by day it is not crowded, and at night it is quiet and free from noise; it is free from contact with gadflies, mosquitoes, wind, sun, and creeping things. Moreover, for one dwelling in that lodging, the requisites of robes, almsfood, lodging, and medicines as a support for the sick arise with little difficulty. Furthermore, in that lodging dwell elder bhikkhus who are learned, who have mastered the traditions, who are bearers of the Dhamma, bearers of the Vinaya, and bearers of the M\u0101tik\u0101s. From time to time, one approaches them to question and inquire: \u2018Venerable sirs, how is this? What is the meaning of this?\u2019 Those venerable ones then reveal what has not been revealed, make plain what has not been made plain, and they dispel doubt concerning various matters that are grounds for doubt. In this way, bhikkhus, a lodging is endowed with five factors.' (A. Ni. 10.11)",pt:"Mas aquele que possui os cinco fatores, tais como n\xe3o ser nem muito longe nem muito perto da aldeia de esmolas, \xe9 chamado de adequado. Pois isso foi dito pelo Aben\xe7oado: 'E como, monges, um alojamento possui os cinco fatores? Aqui, monges, o alojamento n\xe3o \xe9 muito longe nem muito perto, e possui uma rota de ida e volta adequada; de dia n\xe3o \xe9 lotado, e \xe0 noite \xe9 silencioso e livre de ru\xeddos; \xe9 pouco exposto ao toque de mutucas, mosquitos, vento, sol e r\xe9pteis; al\xe9m disso, para quem habita em tal alojamento, os requisitos de mantos, esmolas de comida, alojamento e medicamentos para os enfermos surgem facilmente e sem dificuldade; e em tal alojamento habitam monges anci\xe3os que s\xe3o muito instru\xeddos, herdeiros da tradi\xe7\xe3o, conhecedores do Dhamma, conhecedores do Vinaya, conhecedores dos resumos, aos quais o monge se aproxima de tempos em tempos para perguntar e indagar: \"Como \xe9 isso, vener\xe1vel? Qual \xe9 o significado disso?\"; e esses vener\xe1veis lhe revelam o que n\xe3o estava revelado, tornam claro o que n\xe3o estava claro e removem as suas d\xfavidas sobre v\xe1rios pontos que geram hesita\xe7\xe3o. Assim, monges, um alojamento possui os cinco fatores.' (AN 10.11)",es:"Aquel que posee los cinco factores, como no estar ni muy lejos ni muy cerca del pueblo de limosna, se llama adecuado. Pues el Bienaventurado dijo: '\xbfY c\xf3mo, monjes, una residencia posee cinco factores? Aqu\xed, monjes, la residencia no est\xe1 ni muy lejos ni muy cerca, tiene buen acceso; de d\xeda no est\xe1 concurrida, de noche es silenciosa y sin ruidos, libre del contacto con t\xe1banos, mosquitos, viento, sol y reptiles. En tal residencia, quien mora obtiene sin dificultad mantos, comida de limosna, alojamiento y medicinas. En tal residencia moran monjes ancianos eruditos, conocedores de la tradici\xf3n, que mantienen el Dhamma, el Vinaya y los Matikas; acerc\xe1ndose a ellos de vez en cuando, el monje pregunta e inquiere: 'Venerable, \xbfc\xf3mo es esto? \xbfCu\xe1l es el significado de esto?'. Aquellos venerables le revelan lo que no estaba claro, le aclaran lo que no estaba iluminado y disipan sus dudas sobre los diversos puntos del Dhamma. As\xed, monjes, una residencia posee cinco factores'."}},{id:"vism-4.3",pali:"Khuddakapalibodhupaccheda\u1e43 katv\u0101ti eva\u1e43 patir\u016bpe vih\u0101re viharantena yepissa te honti khuddakapalibodh\u0101, tepi upacchinditabb\u0101. Seyyathida\u1e43, d\u012bgh\u0101ni kesanakhalom\u0101ni chinditabb\u0101ni. Ji\u1e47\u1e47ac\u012bvaresu da\u1e37h\u012bkamma\u1e43 v\u0101 tunnakamma\u1e43 v\u0101 k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Kili\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ni v\u0101 rajitabb\u0101ni. Sace patte mala\u1e43 hoti, patto pacitabbo. Ma\xf1cap\u012b\u1e6dh\u0101d\u012bni sodhetabb\u0101n\u012bti. \"Aya\u1e43 khuddakapalibodhupaccheda\u1e43 katv\u0101\"ti ettha vitth\u0101ro.",translations:{en:"Regarding the phrase 'having cut off the minor impediments': by one dwelling thus in a suitable monastery, whatever minor impediments there may be for him, those too should be cut off. That is to say: long hair of the head, nails, and body hair should be cut. On worn-out robes, the work of reinforcement or darning should be done. Or, soiled robes should be dyed. If there is dirt in the bowl, the bowl should be fired. Beds, chairs, and so forth should be cleaned. This is the detailed explanation here of 'having cut off the minor impediments.'",pt:"Quanto a 'tendo cortado os pequenos impedimentos' \u2014 quem habita em um mosteiro adequado dessa maneira deve cortar tamb\xe9m os pequenos impedimentos que porventura tenha. A saber: cabelos, unhas e pelos longos devem ser cortados. Nos mantos velhos, deve-se fazer remendos ou costuras. Mantos sujos devem ser tingidos. Se houver manchas na tigela, ela deve ser cozida no fogo. Camas, cadeiras, etc., devem ser limpas. Esta \xe9 a explica\xe7\xe3o detalhada sobre 'tendo cortado os pequenos impedimentos'.",es:"En cuanto a la frase \"habiendo cortado los impedimentos menores\", esto significa lo siguiente: el yogui que reside en un monasterio adecuado debe eliminar los obst\xe1culos menores que pueda tener. Espec\xedficamente, se deben cortar el cabello, las u\xf1as y la barba si est\xe1n largos. En cuanto a las t\xfanicas viejas, se debe realizar el trabajo de refuerzo o de remiendo. Si las t\xfanicas est\xe1n sucias, deben ser te\xf1idas. Si el cuenco tiene manchas, el cuenco debe ser cocido. Los lechos, asientos y otros utensilios deben ser limpiados. Esta es la explicaci\xf3n detallada de \"habiendo cortado los impedimentos menores\" en este contexto."}},{id:"vism-4.4",pali:"Id\u0101ni sabba\u1e43 bh\u0101van\u0101vidh\u0101na\u1e43 aparih\u0101pentena bh\u0101vetabboti ettha aya\u1e43 pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101di\u1e43 katv\u0101 sabbakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101navasena vitth\u0101rakath\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"Now, in the context of the statement, 'One should develop, not neglecting any part of the entire method of development,' this will be a detailed exposition by means of all meditation subjects, beginning with the earth kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"Agora, com rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 afirma\xe7\xe3o: 'Todo o m\xe9todo de desenvolvimento mental deve ser cultivado sem neglig\xeancia', segue-se a explica\xe7\xe3o detalhada, come\xe7ando com o kasi\u1e47a de terra e abrangendo todos os objetos de medita\xe7\xe3o.",es:"Ahora, respecto a la frase \"debe desarrollarse sin omitir ninguna parte del procedimiento de meditaci\xf3n\", esta es una exposici\xf3n detallada que comienza con el kasi\u1e47a de tierra y abarca todos los temas de meditaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-4.5",pali:"Eva\u1e43 upacchinnakhuddakapalibodhena hi bhikkhun\u0101 pacch\u0101bhatta\u1e43 pi\u1e47\u1e0dap\u0101tapa\u1e6dikkantena bhattasammada\u1e43 pa\u1e6divinodetv\u0101 pavivitte ok\u0101se sukhanisinnena kat\u0101ya v\u0101 akat\u0101ya v\u0101 pathaviy\u0101 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitabba\u1e43. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"Indeed, a bhikkhu who has thus cut off the minor impediments, having returned from the alms-round after the meal, having dispelled the drowsiness from the meal, and sitting comfortably in a secluded place, should apprehend the sign on the earth, whether it is prepared or unprepared. For this has been said:",pt:"Assim, o bhikkhu que cortou os pequenos impedimentos, tendo retornado de sua ronda de esmolas ap\xf3s a refei\xe7\xe3o, tendo dissipado a sonol\xeancia causada pela comida e sentando-se confortavelmente em um local isolado, deve apreender o sinal (nimitta) na terra, seja ela preparada ou n\xe3o preparada. Pois isto foi dito:",es:"En efecto, el monje que ha cortado los impedimentos menores de esta manera, despu\xe9s de la comida, tras regresar de la ronda de limosnas y habiendo disipado el letargo de la comida, debe captar el signo en la tierra, ya sea preparada o no preparada, sentado c\xf3modamente en un lugar solitario. Pues se ha dicho lo siguiente:"}},{id:"vism-4.6",pali:"\"Pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47a\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hanto pathaviya\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47h\u0101ti kate v\u0101 akate v\u0101 s\u0101ntake, no anantake, sako\u1e6diye, no ako\u1e6diye, sava\u1e6d\u1e6dume, no ava\u1e6d\u1e6dume, sapariyante, no apariyante, suppamatte v\u0101 sar\u0101vamatte v\u0101. So ta\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 suggahita\u1e43 karoti, s\u016bpadh\u0101rita\u1e43 upadh\u0101reti, suvavatthita\u1e43 vavatthapeti. So ta\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 suggahita\u1e43 katv\u0101 s\u016bpadh\u0101rita\u1e43 upadh\u0101retv\u0101 suvavatthita\u1e43 vavatthapetv\u0101 \u0101nisa\u1e43sadass\u0101v\u012b ratanasa\xf1\xf1\u012b hutv\u0101 citt\u012bk\u0101ra\u1e43 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhapetv\u0101 sampiy\u0101yam\u0101no tasmi\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47e citta\u1e43 upanibandhati \u2018addh\u0101 im\u0101ya pa\u1e6dipad\u0101ya jar\u0101mara\u1e47amh\u0101 mucciss\u0101m\u012b\u2019ti. So vivicceva k\u0101mehi\u2026pe\u2026 pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 jh\u0101na\u1e43 upasampajja viharat\u012b\"ti.",translations:{en:"\u201cOne who apprehends the earth kasi\u1e47a apprehends the sign on the earth\u2014whether prepared or unprepared; with a limit, not without a limit; with a boundary, not without a boundary; circular, not non-circular; with a perimeter, not without a perimeter; about the size of a small winnowing basket or a dish. He makes that sign well-grasped; he retains it well; he establishes it well. Having made that sign well-grasped, having retained it well, and having established it well, seeing its benefit, perceiving it as a treasure, establishing regard, and delighting in it, he binds his mind to that object, thinking: \u2018Surely, by this practice, I shall be freed from aging and death.\u2019 He, quite secluded from sensual pleasures\u2026 enters and dwells in the first jh\u0101na.\u201d",pt:"\u201cAquele que aprende o kasi\u1e47a de terra apreende o sinal na terra, seja ela preparada ou n\xe3o preparada, limitada e n\xe3o ilimitada, com bordas e n\xe3o sem bordas, com circunfer\xeancia e n\xe3o sem circunfer\xeancia, com limites e n\xe3o sem limites, do tamanho de uma peneira ou de uma tampa de pote de argila. Ele torna esse sinal bem apreendido, fixa-o firmemente na mem\xf3ria e o define claramente. Tendo tornado esse sinal bem apreendido, fixado firmemente na mem\xf3ria e definido claramente, vendo os seus benef\xedcios, considerando-o como uma joia preciosa, gerando profundo respeito e estimando-o, ele vincula a sua mente a esse objeto, pensando: \u2018Certamente, por meio desta pr\xe1tica, me libertarei do envelhecimento e da morte\u2019. Afastado dos prazeres sensoriais... ele alcan\xe7a e permanece no primeiro jh\u0101na.\u201d",es:"\"Aquel que aprende el kasi\u1e47a de tierra capta el signo en la tierra, ya sea preparada o no preparada, limitada y no ilimitada, con bordes y no sin bordes, circular y no irregular, con periferia y no sin periferia, del tama\xf1o de un cedazo o de la tapa de una vasija. \xc9l hace que ese signo sea bien captado, bien retenido y bien definido. Habi\xe9ndolo captado, retenido y definido bien, viendo sus beneficios, consider\xe1ndolo como un tesoro, estableciendo respeto por \xe9l y apreci\xe1ndolo, vincula su mente a ese objeto pensando: 'Ciertamente, mediante esta pr\xe1ctica me liberar\xe9 de la vejez y de la muerte'. Apartado de los deseos sensoriales... entra y permanece en el primer jhana\"."}},{id:"vism-4.7",pali:"Tasm\u0101 eva\u1e43 vuttappam\u0101\u1e47apariccheda\u1e43 katv\u0101 rukkhap\u0101\u1e47ik\u0101 visabh\u0101gava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 samu\u1e6d\u1e6dhapeti. Tasm\u0101 ta\u1e43 aggahetv\u0101 p\u0101s\u0101\u1e47ap\u0101\u1e47ik\u0101ya gha\u1e43setv\u0101 sama\u1e43 bher\u012btalasadisa\u1e43 katv\u0101 ta\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 sammajjitv\u0101 nhatv\u0101 \u0101gantv\u0101 kasi\u1e47ama\u1e47\u1e0dalato a\u1e0d\u1e0dhateyyahatthantare padese pa\xf1\xf1atte vidatthicatura\u1e45gulap\u0101dake suatthate p\u012b\u1e6dhe nis\u012bditabba\u1e43. Tato d\u016bratare nisinnassa hi kasi\u1e47a\u1e43 na upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti, \u0101sannatare kasi\u1e47ados\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101yanti. Uccatare nisinnena g\u012bva\u1e43 onamitv\u0101 oloketabba\u1e43 hoti, n\u012bcatare ja\u1e47\u1e47uk\u0101ni rujanti. Tasm\u0101 vuttanayeneva nis\u012bditv\u0101 \"appass\u0101d\u0101 k\u0101m\u0101\"ti\u0101din\u0101 nayena k\u0101mesu \u0101d\u012bnava\u1e43 paccavekkhitv\u0101 k\u0101manissara\u1e47e sabbadukkhasamatikkamup\u0101yabh\u016bte nekkhamme j\u0101t\u0101bhil\u0101sena buddhadhammasa\u1e45ghagu\u1e47\u0101nussara\u1e47ena p\u012btip\u0101mojja\u1e43 janayitv\u0101 \"aya\u1e43 d\u0101ni s\u0101 sabbabuddha paccekabuddha ariyas\u0101vakehi pa\u1e6dipann\u0101 nekkhammapa\u1e6dipad\u0101\"ti pa\u1e6dipattiy\u0101 sa\xf1j\u0101tag\u0101ravena \"addh\u0101 im\u0101ya pa\u1e6dipad\u0101ya pavivekasukharasassa bh\u0101g\u012b bhaviss\u0101m\u012b\"ti uss\u0101ha\u1e43 janayitv\u0101 samena \u0101k\u0101rena cakkh\u016bni umm\u012bletv\u0101 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hantena bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Therefore, having made the boundary of the prescribed measure, a wooden trowel produces a dissimilar color. Therefore, not taking that, one should smooth it with a stone trowel, make it even like the surface of a great drum, sweep that place, bathe, and come to sit on a well-spread seat with legs a span and four finger-breadths high, placed in a spot within two and a half cubits from the kasi\u1e47a-circle. Indeed, for one sitting too far away, the kasi\u1e47a does not appear; for one sitting too close, the kasi\u1e47a's faults become apparent. For one sitting on a seat that is too high, one must bend the neck to look; for one sitting on a seat that is too low, the knees ache. Therefore, having sat down in the prescribed manner, one should reflect on the danger in sensual pleasures by the method beginning with, \u201cSensual pleasures are of little delight.\u201d With desire arisen for renunciation\u2014which is the escape from sensual pleasures and the means for overcoming all suffering\u2014and having generated rapture and gladness by recollecting the virtues of the Buddha, Dhamma, and Sangha; with respect arisen for the practice, thinking, \u201cThis is now that path of renunciation practiced by all Buddhas, Paccekabuddhas, and noble disciples,\u201d and having generated enthusiasm by thinking, \u201cSurely, by this practice I shall become a partaker of the taste of the bliss of seclusion,\u201d one should develop it by opening the eyes in a balanced manner while apprehending the sign.",pt:"Portanto, tendo estabelecido a delimita\xe7\xe3o do tamanho conforme mencionado, uma esp\xe1tula de madeira produz uma cor discordante. Por isso, sem utiliz\xe1-la, deve-se polir a superf\xedcie com uma esp\xe1tula de pedra, tornando-a plana como a pele de um tambor. Em seguida, deve-se varrer o local, tomar um banho, retornar e sentar-se em um banco bem nivelado, com pernas de um palmo e quatro dedos de altura, posicionado a uma dist\xe2ncia de dois c\xf4vados e meio do c\xedrculo do kasi\u1e47a. Pois, para quem se senta mais longe do que isso, o kasi\u1e47a n\xe3o aparece claramente; para quem se senta mais perto, os defeitos do kasi\u1e47a tornam-se vis\xedveis. Se sentar em um banco muito alto, ter\xe1 de olhar curvando o pesco\xe7o; se for muito baixo, os joelhos doer\xe3o. Portanto, tendo se sentado exatamente da maneira descrita, contemplando o perigo nos prazeres sensoriais atrav\xe9s do m\xe9todo que come\xe7a com 'os prazeres sensoriais oferecem pouca satisfa\xe7\xe3o', gerando o desejo pela ren\xfancia (nekkhamma) \u2014 que \xe9 a sa\xedda dos prazeres sensoriais e o meio para superar todo o sofrimento \u2014, despertando a alegria e o contentamento pela recorda\xe7\xe3o das qualidades do Buda, do Dhamma e do Sangha, gerando respeito pela pr\xe1tica ao pensar: 'Esta \xe9 a senda da ren\xfancia trilhada por todos os Budas, Paccekabuddhas e nobres disc\xedpulos', e despertando o entusiasmo ao pensar: 'Certamente, por esta pr\xe1tica, serei um participante do sabor da felicidade do isolamento', ele deve abrir os olhos de maneira equilibrada, apreender o sinal e cultiv\xe1-lo.",es:"Por lo tanto, habiendo establecido la delimitaci\xf3n de la medida mencionada, dado que una esp\xe1tula de madera produce un color desigual, se debe evitar su uso y, en su lugar, frotar con una esp\xe1tula de piedra para dejar la superficie lisa como la de un tambor. Tras limpiar ese lugar, ba\xf1arse y regresar, se debe sentar en un taburete de un palmo y cuatro dedos de altura, bien nivelado, colocado a una distancia de dos codos y medio del c\xedrculo del kasi\u1e47a. Pues para quien se sienta m\xe1s lejos, el kasi\u1e47a no aparece claramente; para quien se sienta m\xe1s cerca, se perciben los defectos del kasi\u1e47a. Si se sienta en un taburete muy alto, debe mirar inclinando el cuello; si es muy bajo, le duelen las rodillas. Por lo tanto, sentado de la manera descrita, habiendo reflexionado sobre las desventajas de los placeres sensoriales mediante el m\xe9todo de \"los deseos sensoriales brindan poco placer\", etc., y habiendo generado el deseo por la renuncia (nekkhamme), que es el medio para superar todo sufrimiento; habiendo generado gozo y alegr\xeda mediante el recuerdo de las virtudes del Buda, el Dhamma y el Sangha; pensando: \"Esta es la pr\xe1ctica de renuncia seguida por todos los Budas, Budas Pacceka y nobles disc\xedpulos\"; con el respeto nacido por la pr\xe1ctica y generando el esfuerzo de pensar: \"ciertamente, mediante esta pr\xe1ctica participar\xe9 del sabor de la felicidad de la reclusi\xf3n\", debe desarrollarla abriendo los ojos de manera equilibrada y captando el signo."}},{id:"vism-4.8",pali:"Atiumm\u012blayato hi cakkhu kilamati, ma\u1e47\u1e0dala\xf1ca ativibh\u016bta\u1e43 hoti, tenassa nimitta\u1e43 nuppajjati. Atimanda\u1e43 umm\u012blayato ma\u1e47\u1e0dalamavibh\u016bta\u1e43 hoti, citta\xf1ca l\u012bna\u1e43 hoti, evampi nimitta\u1e43 nuppajjati. Tasm\u0101 \u0101d\u0101satale mukhanimittadassin\u0101 viya samen\u0101k\u0101rena cakkh\u016bni umm\u012bletv\u0101 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hantena bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43, na va\u1e47\u1e47o paccavekkhitabbo, na lakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 manasik\u0101tabba\u1e43. Apica va\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 amu\xf1citv\u0101 nissayasava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 ussadavasena pa\u1e47\u1e47attidhamme citta\u1e43 pa\u1e6d\u1e6dhapetv\u0101 manasi k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Pathav\u012b mah\u012b, medin\u012b, bh\u016bmi, vasudh\u0101, vasundhar\u0101ti\u0101d\u012bsu pathav\u012bn\u0101mesu yamicchati, yadassa sa\xf1\xf1\u0101nuk\u016bla\u1e43 hoti, ta\u1e43 vattabba\u1e43. Apica pathav\u012bti etadeva n\u0101ma\u1e43 p\u0101ka\u1e6da\u1e43, tasm\u0101 p\u0101ka\u1e6davaseneva pathav\u012b pathav\u012bti bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43. K\u0101lena umm\u012bletv\u0101 k\u0101lena nim\u012bletv\u0101 \u0101vajjitabba\u1e43. Y\u0101va uggahanimitta\u1e43 nuppajjati, t\u0101va k\u0101lasatampi k\u0101lasahassampi tato bhiyyopi eteneva nayena bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Indeed, for one opening the eyes too widely, the eye becomes fatigued, and the circle becomes too distinct; thereby the sign does not arise for him. For one opening the eyes too faintly, the circle is indistinct, and the mind is sluggish; even so the sign does not arise. Therefore, like one seeing the reflection of one\u2019s face in a mirror, it should be developed by opening the eyes in a balanced manner and apprehending the sign; the color should not be reviewed, nor should the characteristic be attended to. Moreover, without abandoning the color, taking the support together with its color, one should establish the mind on the conceptual object by way of its prominence and attend to it. Among the names for earth\u2014such as pathav\u012b, mah\u012b, medin\u012b, bh\u016bmi, vasudh\u0101, vasundhar\u0101, and so forth\u2014one should utter whichever one wishes, whichever is agreeable to one\u2019s perception. However, this very name \u2018pathav\u012b\u2019 is well-known; therefore, by the power of the well-known name, it should be developed as \u2018pathav\u012b, pathav\u012b\u2019. One should attend, at times opening the eyes and at times closing them. For as long as the learning sign does not arise, for that long it should be developed by this very method, even for a hundred periods of time, a thousand periods of time, or even more than that.",pt:"Pois, se ele abrir demais os olhos, estes se cansar\xe3o e o c\xedrculo se tornar\xe1 excessivamente n\xedtido, de modo que o sinal n\xe3o surgir\xe1 nele. Se os abrir muito pouco, o c\xedrculo n\xe3o ficar\xe1 claro e a mente se tornar\xe1 pregui\xe7osa; dessa forma tamb\xe9m o sinal n\xe3o surgir\xe1. Portanto, como algu\xe9m que observa o reflexo do pr\xf3prio rosto na superf\xedcie de um espelho, ele deve abrir os olhos de maneira equilibrada, apreender o sinal e cultiv\xe1-lo. A cor n\xe3o deve ser analisada, nem a caracter\xedstica (dureza) deve ser trazida \xe0 mente. Em vez disso, sem abandonar a cor, tomando-a junto com o seu suporte f\xedsico e fixando a mente no conceito (pa\u1e47\u1e47atti) por meio da predomin\xe2ncia do elemento terra, ele deve mentaliz\xe1-lo. Entre os nomes da terra, tais como pathav\u012b, mah\u012b, medin\u012b, bh\u016bmi, vasudh\u0101, vasundhar\u0101, ele deve pronunciar aquele que desejar, o que for mais compat\xedvel com a sua percep\xe7\xe3o. Contudo, o nome 'pathav\u012b' (terra) \xe9 o mais conhecido; portanto, ele deve cultiv\xe1-lo por meio desse nome popular, repetindo mentalmente: 'pathav\u012b, pathav\u012b' (terra, terra). Ele deve contempl\xe1-lo, ora abrindo os olhos, ora fechando-os. Enquanto o sinal de aprendizagem (uggahanimitta) n\xe3o surgir, ele deve cultiv\xe1-lo exatamente dessa maneira por cem vezes, mil vezes ou at\xe9 mais.",es:"Pues, al abrir excesivamente los ojos, estos se fatigan y el disco resulta demasiado n\xedtido; por ello, el signo no surge en tal yogui. Al abrirlos demasiado poco, el disco no es n\xedtido y la mente se vuelve perezosa; de este modo, tampoco surge el signo. Por lo tanto, como quien mira el reflejo de su rostro en la superficie de un espejo, uno debe desarrollar el signo abriendo los ojos de manera equilibrada, sin considerar el color ni prestar atenci\xf3n a la caracter\xedstica de dureza. Por el contrario, sin abandonar el color, pero tom\xe1ndolo como base junto con el color, debe prestarse atenci\xf3n fijando la mente en la realidad conceptual mediante la predominancia del elemento tierra. De entre los nombres de la tierra, como pathav\u012b, mah\u012b, medin\u012b, bh\u016bmi, vasudh\u0101, vasundhar\u0101, se debe recitar el que se desee y que sea acorde con la percepci\xf3n previa de cada uno. Sin embargo, el nombre \"pathav\u012b\" (tierra) es el m\xe1s conocido; por lo tanto, bas\xe1ndose en su notoriedad, debe desarrollarse repitiendo \"tierra, tierra\". Debe reflexionarse abriendo los ojos a veces y cerr\xe1ndolos otras. Mientras no surja el signo de aprendizaje (uggahanimitta), debe desarrollarse de esta misma manera durante cien veces, mil veces o incluso m\xe1s."}},{id:"vism-4.9",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 bh\u0101vayato yad\u0101 nim\u012bletv\u0101 \u0101vajjantassa umm\u012blitak\u0101le viya \u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gacchati, tad\u0101 uggahanimitta\u1e43 j\u0101ta\u1e43 n\u0101ma hoti. Tassa j\u0101tak\u0101lato pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya na tasmi\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101ne nis\u012bditabba\u1e43. Attano vasana\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 pavisitv\u0101 tattha nisinnena bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43. P\u0101dadhovanapapa\xf1caparih\u0101rattha\u1e43 panassa ekapa\u1e6dalikup\u0101han\u0101 ca kattarada\u1e47\u1e0do ca icchitabbo. Ath\u0101nena sace taru\u1e47o sam\u0101dhi kenacideva asapp\u0101yak\u0101ra\u1e47ena nassati, up\u0101han\u0101 \u0101ruyha kattarada\u1e47\u1e0da\u1e43 gahetv\u0101 ta\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 gantv\u0101 nimitta\u1e43 \u0101d\u0101ya \u0101gantv\u0101 sukhanisinnena bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43, punappuna\u1e43 samann\u0101haritabba\u1e43, takk\u0101hata\u1e43 vitakk\u0101hata\u1e43 k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Tasseva\u1e43 karontassa anukkamena n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101ni vikkhambhanti, kiles\u0101 sannis\u012bdanti, upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhin\u0101 citta\u1e43 sam\u0101dhiyati, pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 uppajjati.",translations:{en:"When, as he thus develops, the sign comes into range for him when he attends with eyes closed, just as it does when his eyes are open, then the learning sign is said to have arisen. From the time of its arising, one should not sit in that place. Having entered one\u2019s dwelling place, one should develop it while seated there. But for the sake of avoiding the trouble of washing the feet, single-soled slippers and a walking stick should be desired by him. Then, if the tender concentration is lost due to some unsuitable cause, he should put on the slippers, take the walking stick, go to that place, apprehend the sign, return, and develop it while comfortably seated. It should be repeatedly attended to; it should be struck by thought and struck by applied thought. As he does so, the hindrances are gradually suppressed, the defilements subside, the mind becomes concentrated with access concentration, and the counterpart sign arises.",pt:"Quando ele o cultiva dessa maneira, e quando, ao fechar os olhos e refletir sobre ele, o sinal entra em seu campo de foco exatamente como quando seus olhos estavam abertos, ent\xe3o se diz que o sinal de aprendizagem (uggahanimitta) surgiu. A partir do momento de seu surgimento, ele n\xe3o deve mais permanecer sentado naquele local. Deve entrar em seus pr\xf3prios aposentos e cultiv\xe1-lo ali sentado. Para evitar a perda de tempo com a lavagem dos p\xe9s, ele deve dispor de sand\xe1lias de sola \xfanica e de um cajado. Ent\xe3o, se a sua fr\xe1gil concentra\xe7\xe3o se perder devido a alguma causa inadequada, ele deve cal\xe7ar as sand\xe1lias, pegar o cajado, ir at\xe9 aquele local, apreender o sinal, retornar e cultiv\xe1-lo sentando-se confortavelmente. Ele deve direcionar a mente a ele repetidas vezes, aplicando o pensamento inicial (takka) e o pensamento sustentado (vitakka). Enquanto ele age assim, gradualmente os obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101) s\xe3o suprimidos, as impurezas mentais (kiles\u0101) se acalmam, a mente se concentra com a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso (upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi) e o sinal de contrapartida (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta) surge.",es:"Para quien lo desarrolla de este modo, cuando al cerrar los ojos y reflexionar, el signo aparece en su mente tal como cuando los ten\xeda abiertos, se dice que ha surgido el signo de aprendizaje (uggahanimitta). A partir del momento en que este surge, ya no debe permanecer sentado en ese lugar. Debe entrar en su lugar de residencia y desarrollarlo sentado all\xed. Para evitar la demora de lavarse los pies, el yogui debe procurarse sandalias de una sola suela y un bast\xf3n. Entonces, si su incipiente concentraci\xf3n se pierde debido a alguna circunstancia inadecuada, debe calzarse las sandalias, tomar el bast\xf3n, regresar a aquel lugar, captar el signo, volver y desarrollarlo sentado c\xf3modamente. Debe aplicarse a \xe9l una y otra vez, golpe\xe1ndolo con el pensamiento inicial y golpe\xe1ndolo con el pensamiento sostenido. Al actuar as\xed, gradualmente los obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101ni) se disipan, las impurezas se asientan, la mente se unifica mediante la concentraci\xf3n de acceso (upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi) y surge el signo de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta)."}},{id:"vism-4.10",pali:"Tatr\u0101ya\u1e43 purimassa ca uggahanimittassa imassa ca viseso, uggahanimitte kasi\u1e47adoso pa\xf1\xf1\u0101yati, pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 thavikato nihat\u0101d\u0101sama\u1e47\u1e0dala\u1e43 viya sudhotasa\u1e45khath\u0101la\u1e43 viya val\u0101hakantar\u0101 nikkhantacandama\u1e47\u1e0dala\u1e43 viya meghamukhe bal\u0101k\u0101 viya uggahanimitta\u1e43 pad\u0101letv\u0101 nikkhantamiva tato satagu\u1e47a\u1e43 sahassagu\u1e47a\u1e43 suparisuddha\u1e43 hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Ta\xf1ca kho neva va\u1e47\u1e47avanta\u1e43, na sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101navanta\u1e43. Yadi hi ta\u1e43 \u012bdisa\u1e43 bhaveyya, cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1eyya\u1e43 siy\u0101 o\u1e37\u0101rika\u1e43 sammasanupaga\u1e43 tilakkha\u1e47abbh\u0101hata\u1e43, na paneta\u1e43 t\u0101disa\u1e43. Kevala\xf1hi sam\u0101dhil\u0101bhino upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101k\u0101ramatta\u1e43 sa\xf1\xf1ajametanti.",translations:{en:"Herein, this is the difference between the former learning sign and this one: in the learning sign, the kasi\u1e47a faults are apparent; but the counterpart sign appears\u2014as if having broken through the learning sign and emerged\u2014having become a hundred times, a thousand times, more purified than that, like a mirror-disc taken out of its case, like a well-polished conch-bowl, like the moon-disc emerged from among the clouds, or like a heron in the mouth of a cloud. And indeed, it is neither possessed of color nor possessed of shape. For if it were such, it would be cognizable by eye-consciousness, gross, subject to comprehension, and struck by the three characteristics; but it is not like that. For it is merely a mode of appearance for one who has gained concentration, something born of perception.",pt:"Aqui reside a diferen\xe7a entre o sinal de aprendizagem anterior e este sinal de contrapartida: no sinal de aprendizagem, os defeitos do kasi\u1e47a s\xe3o vis\xedveis. O sinal de contrapartida, por\xe9m, aparece como um disco de espelho retirado de uma bolsa, como um vaso de concha bem lavado, como o disco da lua surgindo de tr\xe1s de uma nuvem ou como uma gar\xe7a contra uma nuvem escura. Ele surge como se estivesse rompendo o sinal de aprendizagem e saindo dele, cem ou mil vezes mais purificado do que este. No entanto, ele n\xe3o possui cor nem forma. Pois, se as tivesse, seria cognosc\xedvel pela consci\xeancia visual, grosseiro, sujeito \xe0 investiga\xe7\xe3o (por vipassana) e marcado pelas tr\xeas caracter\xedsticas da exist\xeancia. Mas ele n\xe3o \xe9 assim. Trata-se apenas de um modo de manifesta\xe7\xe3o para quem obteve a concentra\xe7\xe3o, nascido puramente da percep\xe7\xe3o meditativa (sa\xf1\xf1\u0101-ja).",es:"En esto, esta es la distinci\xf3n entre el anterior signo de aprendizaje y este signo de contraparte: en el signo de aprendizaje se perciben los defectos del kasina, pero el signo de contraparte aparece como un disco de espejo sacado de su funda, como un cuenco de n\xe1car bien pulido, como el disco de la luna saliendo de entre las nubes o como garzas frente a un nubarr\xf3n; aparece rompiendo el signo de aprendizaje, surgiendo de \xe9l cientos y miles de veces m\xe1s puro. Y este, ciertamente, no posee color ni forma f\xedsica. Pues si fuera as\xed, ser\xeda perceptible por la conciencia visual, ser\xeda burdo, objeto de examen y afectado por las tres caracter\xedsticas; pero no es de tal naturaleza. Es meramente un modo de apariencia para quien ha obtenido la concentraci\xf3n, nacido \xfanicamente de la percepci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-4.11",pali:"Uppannak\u0101lato ca panassa pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101ni vikkhambhit\u0101neva honti, kiles\u0101 sannisinn\u0101va, upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhin\u0101 citta\u1e43 sam\u0101hitamev\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, from the time of its arising, the hindrances are indeed suppressed, the defilements are indeed settled, and the mind is indeed concentrated with access concentration.",pt:"E a partir do momento do seu surgimento, os obst\xe1culos mentais (n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101) s\xe3o suprimidos, as impurezas (kiles\u0101) se acalmam e a mente se estabelece firmemente na concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso (upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi).",es:"A partir del momento en que este signo de contraparte surge, los obst\xe1culos quedan verdaderamente disipados, las impurezas se asientan y la mente queda ciertamente unificada mediante la concentraci\xf3n de acceso."}},{id:"vism-4.12",pali:"Duvidho hi sam\u0101dhi upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi ca appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi ca. Dv\u012bh\u0101k\u0101rehi citta\u1e43 sam\u0101dhiyati upac\u0101rabh\u016bmiya\u1e43 v\u0101 pa\u1e6dil\u0101bhabh\u016bmiya\u1e43 v\u0101. Tattha upac\u0101rabh\u016bmiya\u1e43 n\u012bvara\u1e47appah\u0101nena citta\u1e43 sam\u0101hita\u1e43 hoti. Pa\u1e6dil\u0101bhabh\u016bmiya\u1e43 a\u1e45gap\u0101tubh\u0101vena.",translations:{en:"Indeed, concentration is of two kinds: access concentration and absorption concentration. The mind is concentrated in two ways: either in the access stage or in the attainment stage. Therein, in the access stage, the mind is concentrated through the abandonment of the hindrances. In the attainment stage, it is through the manifestation of the factors.",pt:"Pois a concentra\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de dois tipos: a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso (upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi) e a concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi). A mente se concentra de duas maneiras: no n\xedvel de acesso ou no n\xedvel de obten\xe7\xe3o. No n\xedvel de acesso, a mente se concentra por meio do abandono dos obst\xe1culos. No n\xedvel de obten\xe7\xe3o, ela se concentra por meio do manifesto surgimento dos fatores do jh\u0101na.",es:"Pues la concentraci\xf3n es de dos tipos: concentraci\xf3n de acceso y concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n. La mente se concentra de dos maneras: ya sea en el nivel de acceso o en el nivel de obtenci\xf3n de la absorci\xf3n. En el nivel de acceso, la mente est\xe1 concentrada mediante el abandono de los obst\xe1culos; en el nivel de obtenci\xf3n, mediante la manifestaci\xf3n de los factores del jh\u0101na."}},{id:"vism-4.13",pali:"Tatra yadeta\u1e43 upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhin\u0101 saddhi\u1e43 pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 uppanna\u1e43, tassa upp\u0101dana\u1e43 n\u0101ma atidukkara\u1e43. Tasm\u0101 sace teneva palla\u1e45kena ta\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 va\u1e0d\u1e0dhetv\u0101 appana\u1e43 adhigantu\u1e43 sakkoti, sundara\u1e43. No ce sakkoti, ath\u0101nena ta\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 appamattena cakkavattigabbho viya rakkhitabba\u1e43. Eva\xf1hi \u2013",translations:{en:"Therein, the causing of this counterpart sign to arise together with access concentration is extremely difficult to accomplish. Therefore, if one is able, with that very same cross-legged posture, to develop that sign and attain absorption, it is excellent. If one is not able, then that sign should be guarded by this yogi with diligence, like the embryo of a wheel-turning monarch. For thus\u2014",pt:"Dentre esses sinais, o surgimento do sinal de contrapartida junto com a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso \xe9 extremamente dif\xedcil. Portanto, se ele puder, naquela mesma sess\xe3o de medita\xe7\xe3o, expandir esse sinal e alcan\xe7ar a absor\xe7\xe3o, isso ser\xe1 excelente. Se n\xe3o puder, ele deve proteger esse sinal com dilig\xeancia, assim como se protegeria a gesta\xe7\xe3o de um monarca universal (cakkavatti). Pois:",es:"De ellos, el surgimiento de ese signo de contraparte junto con la concentraci\xf3n de acceso es sumamente dif\xedcil. Por lo tanto, si en esa misma postura de meditaci\xf3n uno puede desarrollar dicho signo y alcanzar la absorci\xf3n, es excelente. Si no puede, entonces debe proteger ese signo con diligencia, como si se tratara de la gestaci\xf3n de un monarca universal. Pues as\xed se dice:"}},{id:"vism-4.14",pali:"Yassa pana evampi pa\u1e6dipajjato na hoti, tena dasavidha\u1e43 appan\u0101kosalla\u1e43 samp\u0101detabba\u1e43. Tatr\u0101ya\u1e43 nayo, das\u0101h\u0101k\u0101rehi appan\u0101kosalla\u1e43 icchitabba\u1e43, vatthuvisadakiriyato, indriyasamattapa\u1e6dip\u0101danato, nimittakusalato, yasmi\u1e43 samaye citta\u1e43 paggahetabba\u1e43 tasmi\u1e43 samaye citta\u1e43 pagga\u1e47h\u0101ti, yasmi\u1e43 samaye citta\u1e43 niggahetabba\u1e43 tasmi\u1e43 samaye citta\u1e43 nigga\u1e47h\u0101ti, yasmi\u1e43 samaye citta\u1e43 sampaha\u1e43sitabba\u1e43 tasmi\u1e43 samaye citta\u1e43 sampaha\u1e43seti, yasmi\u1e43 samaye citta\u1e43 ajjhupekkhitabba\u1e43 tasmi\u1e43 samaye citta\u1e43 ajjhupekkhati, asam\u0101hitapuggalaparivajjanato, sam\u0101hitapuggalasevanato, tadadhimuttatoti.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, for one for whom absorption does not arise even when practicing thus, the tenfold skill in absorption should be accomplished. Herein is the method: skill in absorption should be sought in ten ways: by purification of the basis, by balancing the spiritual faculties, by skill in the sign, by uplifting the mind at the time it should be uplifted, by restraining the mind at the time it should be restrained, by gladdening the mind at the time it should be gladdened, by regarding the mind with equanimity at the time it should be so regarded, by avoiding unconcentrated persons, by associating with concentrated persons, and by being inclined towards that.",pt:"Mas para aquele iogue para quem, mesmo praticando dessa maneira, a absor\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o ocorre, as dez formas de habilidade na absor\xe7\xe3o devem ser aperfei\xe7oadas. Aqui est\xe1 o m\xe9todo: a habilidade na absor\xe7\xe3o deve ser buscada de dez maneiras: purificando as bases f\xedsicas e materiais; equilibrando as faculdades espirituais; sendo habilidoso em rela\xe7\xe3o ao sinal; estimulando a mente no momento em que ela deve ser estimulada; refreando a mente no momento em que ela deve ser refreada; alegrando a mente no momento em que ela deve ser alegrada; observando a mente com equanimidade no momento em que ela deve ser observada com equanimidade; evitando pessoas n\xe3o concentradas; associando-se a pessoas concentradas; e sendo inclinado a essa mesma absor\xe7\xe3o.",es:"Sin embargo, para aquel que, aun practicando de esta manera, no alcanza la absorci\xf3n, debe perfeccionar las diez habilidades en la absorci\xf3n. El m\xe9todo es el siguiente: se debe buscar la habilidad en la absorci\xf3n mediante diez formas: 1) mediante la limpieza de las bases, 2) mediante el equilibrio de las facultades, 3) mediante la destreza en el signo, 4) elevando la mente cuando debe ser elevada, 5) refrenando la mente cuando debe ser refrenada, 6) alegrando la mente cuando debe ser alegrada, 7) observando la mente con ecuanimidad cuando debe ser observada con ecuanimidad, 8) evitando a las personas no concentradas, 9) asoci\xe1ndose con personas concentradas y 10) mediante la inclinaci\xf3n hacia ese sam\u0101dhi de absorci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-4.15",pali:"Tatr\u0101yamatthad\u012bpan\u0101 \u2013 yath\u0101 hi acheko madhukaro asukasmi\u1e43 rukkhe puppha\u1e43 pupphitanti \xf1atv\u0101 tikkhena vegena pakkhando ta\u1e43 atikkamitv\u0101 pa\u1e6dinivattento kh\u012b\u1e47e re\u1e47umhi samp\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101ti. Aparo acheko mandena javena pakkhando kh\u012b\u1e47eyeva samp\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101ti. Cheko pana samena javena pakkhando sukhena pupphar\u0101si\u1e43 sampatv\u0101 y\u0101vadicchaka\u1e43 re\u1e47u\u1e43 \u0101d\u0101ya madhu\u1e43 samp\u0101detv\u0101 madhurasamanubhavati.",translations:{en:"Here is the explanation of the meaning: Just as an unskilled bee, knowing that flowers have bloomed on a certain tree, flies forth with sharp speed, overshoots it, and turning back, arrives when the pollen is exhausted. Another unskilled one, flying forth with sluggish speed, arrives only when it is exhausted. But a skilled one, flying forth with even speed, easily reaches the mass of flowers, takes as much pollen as it desires, prepares honey, and experiences the taste of honey.",pt:"Aqui est\xe1 a explica\xe7\xe3o do significado: assim como uma abelha inexperiente, sabendo que uma flor desabrochou em determinada \xe1rvore, voa com velocidade excessiva, passa al\xe9m dela e, ao retornar, chega quando o p\xf3len j\xe1 acabou. Outra abelha inexperiente, voando com velocidade muito lenta, chega somente quando o p\xf3len j\xe1 acabou. Mas a abelha experiente, voando com velocidade equilibrada, chega facilmente ao monte de flores, recolhe o p\xf3len conforme deseja, produz o mel e desfruta do sabor doce.",es:"Esta es la explicaci\xf3n del significado: Una abeja inexperta, sabiendo que las flores han brotado en cierto \xe1rbol, vuela con una velocidad excesiva, pasa de largo el \xe1rbol y, al regresar, llega cuando el polen ya se ha agotado. Otra abeja inexperta vuela con una velocidad muy lenta y llega tambi\xe9n cuando el polen ya se ha agotado. Pero la abeja experta vuela con una velocidad moderada y equilibrada, llega f\xe1cilmente al c\xfamulo de flores, toma el polen seg\xfan su deseo, produce miel y disfruta de su dulce sabor."}},{id:"vism-4.16",pali:"Iti eva\u1e43 nimitt\u0101bhimukha\u1e43 m\u0101nasa\u1e43 pa\u1e6dip\u0101dayato panassa id\u0101ni appan\u0101 ijjhissat\u012bti bhava\u1e45ga\u1e43 upacchinditv\u0101 pathav\u012b pathav\u012bti anuyogavasena upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43 tadeva pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjanamuppajjati. Tato tasmi\u1e43yev\u0101ramma\u1e47e catt\u0101ri pa\xf1ca v\u0101 javan\u0101ni javanti. Tesu avas\u0101ne eka\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101vacara\u1e43, ses\u0101ni k\u0101m\u0101vacar\u0101ni. Pakaticittehi balavataravitakkavic\u0101rap\u012btisukhacittekaggat\u0101ni y\u0101ni appan\u0101ya parikammatt\u0101 parikamm\u0101n\u012btipi, yath\u0101 g\u0101m\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 \u0101sannapadeso g\u0101m\u016bpac\u0101ro nagar\u016bpac\u0101roti vuccati, eva\u1e43 appan\u0101ya \u0101sannatt\u0101 sam\u012bpac\u0101ratt\u0101 v\u0101 upac\u0101r\u0101n\u012btipi, ito pubbe parikamm\u0101na\u1e43, upari appan\u0101ya ca anulomato anulom\u0101n\u012btipi vuccanti. Ya\xf1cettha sabbantima\u1e43, ta\u1e43 parittagott\u0101bhibhavanato, mahaggatagottabh\u0101vanato ca gotrabh\u016btipi vuccati. Agahitaggaha\u1e47ena panettha pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 parikamma\u1e43, dutiya\u1e43 upac\u0101ra\u1e43, tatiya\u1e43 anuloma\u1e43, catuttha\u1e43 gotrabhu. Pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 v\u0101 upac\u0101ra\u1e43, dutiya\u1e43 anuloma\u1e43, tatiya\u1e43 gotrabhu, catuttha\u1e43 pa\xf1cama\u1e43 v\u0101 appan\u0101citta\u1e43. Catutthameva hi pa\xf1cama\u1e43 v\u0101 appeti, ta\xf1ca kho khipp\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1adandh\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1avasena. Tato para\u1e43 javana\u1e43 patati. Bhava\u1e45gassa v\u0101ro hoti.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, for this yogi who directs his meditation mind towards the counterpart sign, when the thought arises, 'Now absorption will be accomplished,' the mind-door adverting consciousness arises. It does so after cutting off the life-continuum and taking as its object that very earth-kasi\u1e47a which has appeared through the application, 'earth, earth.' After that, on that very object, four or five impulsions run. Among these, the one at the end is a fine-material sphere consciousness, while the remaining are sense-sphere consciousnesses. These sense-sphere impulsions, possessing stronger initial application, sustained application, rapture, happiness, and one-pointedness than ordinary consciousnesses, are also called 'preparatory' (parikamma) because they are a preparation for absorption. And just as the area near a village is called the 'village-approach' (g\u0101m\u016bpac\u0101ra) or 'town-approach' (nagar\u016bpac\u0101ra), so too, because of their nearness to absorption or because they move in its vicinity, they are also called 'access' (upac\u0101ra). And because they conform to the preceding preparatory states and the subsequent absorption, they are also called 'conformity' (anuloma). And that which is the very last among these is also called 'change-of-lineage' (gotrabh\u016b) because it overcomes the lineage of the limited and develops the lineage of the exalted. Herein, by grasping what has not been grasped, the first is preparatory, the second is access, the third is conformity, and the fourth is change-of-lineage. Alternatively, the first is access, the second is conformity, the third is change-of-lineage, and the fourth or fifth is the absorption consciousness. For indeed, it is the fourth or the fifth that attains absorption, and that is in accordance with whether one has quick or slow direct knowledge. After that, the impulsion lapses, and it becomes the turn of the life-continuum.",pt:"Assim, para aquele que direciona a mente para o sinal, pensando 'agora a absor\xe7\xe3o se realizar\xe1', o fluxo do shava\u1e45ga (bhava\u1e45ga) \xe9 interrompido, e surge a advert\xeancia pelo portal da mente (manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana), tomando como objeto aquele mesmo kasina de terra que apareceu por meio da pr\xe1tica repetida de 'terra, terra'. Depois disso, naquele mesmo objeto, ocorrem quatro ou cinco momentos de impuls\xe3o (javana). Entre estes, o \xfaltimo \xe9 de esfera sutil (r\u016bp\u0101vacara), e os anteriores s\xe3o de esfera sensorial (k\u0101m\u0101vacar\u0101ni). Estes \xfaltimos, que possuem aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial, aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, \xeaxtase, felicidade e unifocaliza\xe7\xe3o mental mais fortes do que as mentes comuns, s\xe3o chamados de 'preparat\xf3rios' (parikamma) por prepararem para a absor\xe7\xe3o; e assim como a \xe1rea pr\xf3xima a uma aldeia ou cidade \xe9 chamada de 'arredores da aldeia' (g\u0101m\u016bpac\u0101ra) ou 'arredores da cidade' (nagar\u016bpac\u0101ra), eles tamb\xe9m s\xe3o chamados de 'acesso' (upac\u0101ra) por estarem pr\xf3ximos ou vizinhos \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o; e tamb\xe9m s\xe3o chamados de 'conformidade' (anuloma) por estarem em conformidade com os momentos preparat\xf3rios anteriores e com a absor\xe7\xe3o subsequente. E aquele que \xe9 o \xfaltimo de todos entre estes \xe9 tamb\xe9m chamado de 'mudan\xe7a de linhagem' (gotrabhu), por superar a linhagem limitada e desenvolver a linhagem grandiosa. De acordo com o m\xe9todo de contagem que inclui o preparat\xf3rio, o primeiro \xe9 o preparat\xf3rio (parikamma), o segundo \xe9 o acesso (upac\u0101ra), o terceiro \xe9 a conformidade (anuloma) e o quarto \xe9 a mudan\xe7a de linhagem (gotrabhu). Ou, de outra forma, o primeiro \xe9 o acesso, o segundo \xe9 a conformidade, o terceiro \xe9 a mudan\xe7a de linhagem, e o quarto ou quinto \xe9 a mente de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101citta). Pois a absor\xe7\xe3o ocorre de fato no quarto ou no quinto momento, e isso deve ser compreendido de acordo com a cogni\xe7\xe3o r\xe1pida ou lenta. Depois disso, a impuls\xe3o cessa e ocorre o momento do shava\u1e45ga (bhava\u1e45ga).",es:"69. As\xed pues, para aquel que dirige su mente hacia el signo de esta manera, pensando: \xabAhora la absorci\xf3n se cumplir\xe1\xbb, se interrumpe el continuo vital (bhava\u1e45ga) y surge la advertencia por la puerta de la mente (manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana), tomando como objeto ese mismo signo de contraparte de la totalidad de tierra (pathav\u012b-kasi\u1e47a) que ha aparecido mediante la pr\xe1ctica de meditaci\xf3n repetida: \xabtierra, tierra\xbb. Despu\xe9s de esto, surgen cuatro o cinco impulsos (javan\u0101ni) sobre ese mismo objeto. De estos, el \xfaltimo es un momento de conciencia de la esfera de la forma (r\u016bp\u0101vacara), mientras que los anteriores pertenecen a la esfera del sentido (k\u0101m\u0101vacara). Estos \xfaltimos poseen una fuerza mayor de vitakka, vic\u0101ra, p\u012bti, sukha y ekaggat\u0101 que los estados mentales ordinarios; se denominan \xabpreparatorios\xbb (parikamma) porque preparan para la absorci\xf3n; \xabde acceso\xbb (upac\u0101ra) porque est\xe1n cerca de la absorci\xf3n o se mueven en su proximidad, al igual que los alrededores de una aldea se llaman acceso a la aldea; y \xabde conformidad\xbb (anuloma) porque son conformes tanto a los preparatorios anteriores como a la absorci\xf3n posterior. De estos, el que es absolutamente el \xfaltimo se llama tambi\xe9n \xabcambio de linaje\xbb (gotrabh\u016b), porque trasciende el linaje limitado (del sentido) y cultiva el linaje de lo sublime (mahaggata). Seg\xfan el m\xe9todo de no contar lo ya contado, el primero es el preparatorio, el segundo es el de acceso, el tercero es el de conformidad y el cuarto es el cambio de linaje. O bien, el primero es el de acceso, el segundo es el de conformidad, el tercero es el cambio de linaje y el cuarto o el quinto es el momento de absorci\xf3n. Pues la absorci\xf3n ocurre en el cuarto o en el quinto momento, dependiendo de si se trata de alguien de comprensi\xf3n r\xe1pida o lenta. Despu\xe9s de eso, el proceso de impulsos cesa y llega el turno del continuo vital (bhava\u1e45ga)."}},{id:"vism-4.17",pali:"Ett\u0101vat\u0101 ca panesa vivicceva k\u0101mehi vivicca akusalehi dhammehi savitakka\u1e43 savic\u0101ra\u1e43 vivekaja\u1e43 p\u012btisukha\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 jh\u0101na\u1e43 upasampajja viharati. Evamanena pa\xf1ca\u1e45gavippah\u012bna\u1e43 pa\xf1ca\u1e45gasamann\u0101gata\u1e43 tividhakaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 dasalakkha\u1e47asampanna\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 jh\u0101na\u1e43 adhigata\u1e43 hoti pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, by this much, this meditator, being secluded indeed from sensual pleasures and secluded from unwholesome states, enters and abides in the first jh\u0101na, which is accompanied by initial and sustained application, with rapture and happiness born of seclusion. Thus, this meditator has attained the first jh\u0101na with the earth kasi\u1e47a as its object, which has five factors abandoned, is endowed with five factors, possesses threefold goodness, and is complete with ten characteristics.",pt:"E, com este procedimento de medita\xe7\xe3o, o meditador, afastado dos prazeres sensoriais, afastado dos dhammas prejudiciais, entra e permanece no primeiro jh\u0101na, que \xe9 acompanhado de aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial e aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, com o \xeaxtase e a felicidade nascidos do afastamento. Assim, ele alcan\xe7a o primeiro jh\u0101na baseado no kasina de terra, que \xe9 livre de os cinco fatores, dotado de cinco fatores, possuidor de uma tr\xedplice bondade e de dez caracter\xedsticas.",es:"Hasta este punto, mediante este proceso de desarrollo, este meditador, \xabalejado ciertamente de los placeres sensoriales, alejado de los estados perjudiciales, entra y permanece en el primer jh\u0101na, que est\xe1 acompa\xf1ado por el pensamiento aplicado y el pensamiento sostenido, con el gozo y la felicidad nacidos del retiro\xbb. De esta manera, ha alcanzado el primer jh\u0101na basado en la totalidad de tierra, el cual ha abandonado cinco factores, posee cinco factores, tiene una triple excelencia y est\xe1 dotado de diez caracter\xedsticas."}},{id:"vism-4.18",pali:"Ett\u0101vat\u0101 ca pa\u1e6dhamassa jh\u0101nassa pah\u0101na\u1e45ga\u1e43 dassetv\u0101 id\u0101ni sampayoga\u1e45ga\u1e43 dassetu\u1e43 savitakka\u1e43 savic\u0101ranti\u0101di vutta\u1e43. Tattha vitakkana\u1e43 vitakko, \u016bhananti vutta\u1e43 hoti. Sv\u0101ya\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47e cittassa abhiniropanalakkha\u1e47o, \u0101hananapariy\u0101hananaraso. Tath\u0101 hi tena yog\u0101vacaro \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 vitakk\u0101hata\u1e43 vitakkapariy\u0101hata\u1e43 karot\u012bti vuccati. \u0100ramma\u1e47e cittassa \u0101nayanapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101no.",translations:{en:"And thus, having shown the factor of abandonment of the first jh\u0101na, now, to show its associated factor, the phrase 'with applied thought, with sustained thought,' etc., is stated. Therein, applying the mind is applied thought (vitakka); it is said to be directing. This has the characteristic of directing the mind onto an object. Its function is striking and striking all around. For so it is said that by means of it, the yog\u012b makes the object struck and struck all around by applied thought. Its manifestation is the leading of the mind to the object.",pt:"Tendo assim mostrado o fator de abandono do primeiro jh\u0101na, agora, para mostrar o fator de associa\xe7\xe3o, diz-se \"com aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial (vitakka) e aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada (vic\u0101ra)\", etc. Ali, o ato de aplicar a mente \xe9 a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial (vitakka); \"ponderar\" \xe9 o que se quer dizer. Esta [aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial] tem a caracter\xedstica de direcionar a mente ao objeto, e a fun\xe7\xe3o de tocar e retocar [o objeto]. Pois, de fato, por meio dela, diz-se que o praticante (yog\u0101vacaro) faz com que o objeto seja tocado e retocado pela aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial. Manifesta-se como o ato de conduzir a mente ao objeto.",es:"Habiendo mostrado hasta aqu\0 el factor de abandono del primer jhana, ahora para mostrar el factor de asociaci\0n se dice: \u2018con pensamiento aplicado (vitakka) y pensamiento sostenido (vic\u0101ra)\u2019, etc. All\0, 'pensar' es vitakka; se dice que es el acto de aplicar la mente. Este tiene la caracter\0stica de dirigir la mente hacia el objeto; su funci\0n es el impacto inicial y continuo. As\0, se dice que a trav\0s de este, el practicante del yoga hace que el objeto sea impactado y golpeado por el pensamiento aplicado. Su manifestaci\0n es el acto de conducir la mente hacia el objeto."}},{id:"vism-4.19",pali:"Santepi ca nesa\u1e43 katthaci avippayoge o\u1e37\u0101rika\u1e6d\u1e6dhena pubba\u1e45gama\u1e6d\u1e6dhena ca gha\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101bhigh\u0101to viya cetaso pa\u1e6dham\u0101bhinip\u0101to vitakko. Sukhuma\u1e6d\u1e6dhena anumajjanasabh\u0101vena ca gha\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101nuravo viya anuppabandho vic\u0101ro. Vipph\u0101rav\u0101 cettha vitakko pa\u1e6dhamuppattik\u0101le paripphandanabh\u016bto cittassa \u0101k\u0101se uppatituk\u0101massa pakkhino pakkhavikkhepo viya padum\u0101bhimukhap\u0101to viya ca gandh\u0101nubandhacetaso bhamarassa. Santavutti vic\u0101ro n\u0101tiparipphandanabh\u0101vo cittassa \u0101k\u0101se uppatitassa pakkhino pakkhappas\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e43 viya, paribbhamana\u1e43 viya ca padum\u0101bhimukhapatitassa bhamarassa padumassa uparibh\u0101ge. Dukanip\u0101ta\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101ya\u1e43 pana \"\u0101k\u0101se gacchato mah\u0101saku\u1e47assa ubhohi pakkhehi v\u0101ta\u1e43 gahetv\u0101 pakkhe sannis\u012bd\u0101petv\u0101 gamana\u1e43 viya \u0101ramma\u1e47e cetaso abhiniropanabh\u0101vena pavatto vitakko. V\u0101taggaha\u1e47attha\u1e43 pakkhe phand\u0101payam\u0101nassa gamana\u1e43 viya anumajjanabh\u0101vena pavatto vic\u0101ro\"ti vutta\u1e43, ta\u1e43 anuppabandhena pavattiya\u1e43 yujjati. So pana nesa\u1e43 viseso pa\u1e6dhamadutiyajjh\u0101nesu p\u0101ka\u1e6do hoti.",translations:{en:"And although in some cases they are not dissociated, applied thought (vitakka) is the initial impact of the mind, due to its grossness and its being a forerunner, like the initial striking of a bell. Sustained thought (vic\u0101ra), which is the continuous binding, is due to its subtlety and its nature of repeatedly examining, like the reverberation of a bell. Herein, applied thought is agitated, being the mind's trembling at the time of its first arising, like the flapping of the wings of a bird that wishes to fly up into the sky, and like the descent towards a lotus of a bee whose mind follows the scent. Sustained thought has a calm activity, being the state of the mind's non-excessive agitation, like the spreading of the wings of a bird that has flown up into the sky, and like the circling above the upper part of the lotus by a bee that has descended towards the lotus. But in the commentary to the Dukanip\u0101ta, it is said: 'Applied thought, which occurs by way of directing the mind onto an object, is like the flight of a great bird going in the sky, which, having caught the wind with both wings, flies with its wings settled. Sustained thought, which occurs by way of examining, is like the flight of one who makes the wings tremble in order to catch the wind.' That statement is suitable for its continuous occurrence. But that distinction between them becomes manifest in the first and second jh\u0101nas.",pt:"Embora n\xe3o haja dissocia\xe7\xe3o entre eles em certos estados mentais, a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial (vitakka) \xe9 o primeiro impacto da mente [no objeto], como o golpe em um sino, devido \xe0 sua natureza grosseira e por ser precursora. A aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada (vic\u0101ra) \xe9 a vincula\xe7\xe3o cont\xednua, como a reverbera\xe7\xe3o do sino, devido \xe0 sua sutileza e \xe0 sua natureza de examinar. Al\xe9m disso, a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial \xe9 vibrante, constituindo a agita\xe7\xe3o da mente no momento de seu primeiro surgimento, como o bater de asas de um grande p\xe1ssaro que deseja al\xe7ar voo no c\xe9u, ou como o mergulho de uma abelha em dire\xe7\xe3o a um l\xf3tus, atra\xedda pelo aroma. A aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada tem uma atividade pac\xedfica, sendo o estado em que a mente n\xe3o vibra excessivamente, como o planar de um p\xe1ssaro que j\xe1 al\xe7ou voo no c\xe9u, ou como o pairar de uma abelha acima do l\xf3tus ap\xf3s ter mergulhado em sua dire\xe7\xe3o. No entanto, no Coment\xe1rio do Dukanip\u0101ta diz-se: \"A aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial \xe9 como o voo de um grande p\xe1ssaro no c\xe9u que, tendo capturado o vento com ambas as asas, voa mantendo-as im\xf3veis, ocorrendo como o direcionamento da mente ao objeto. A aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada \xe9 como o voo daquele que bate as asas para capturar o vento, ocorrendo como o ato de examinar.\" Essa afirma\xe7\xe3o \xe9 apropriada para a ocorr\xeancia cont\xednua [no acesso ou na absor\xe7\xe3o]. E essa distin\xe7\xe3o entre eles torna-se clara no primeiro e no segundo jhanas.",es:"Aunque en algunos estados mentales (como el primer jh\u0101na y la conciencia de la esfera de los sentidos) el pensamiento aplicado y el pensamiento sostenido coexisten sin separarse, el pensamiento aplicado (vitakka) es el impacto inicial de la mente sobre el objeto, similar al golpe de una campana, debido a su naturaleza m\xe1s tosca y a que act\xfaa como precursor del pensamiento sostenido. El pensamiento sostenido (vic\u0101ra) es la conexi\xf3n continua de la mente con el objeto, similar a la resonancia de la campana, debido a su naturaleza sutil y a su funci\xf3n de examinar repetidamente el objeto. En este contexto, vitakka es vibrante, representando la agitaci\xf3n de la mente en el momento de su surgimiento inicial, como el aleteo de las alas de un ave que desea emprender el vuelo en el aire, o como el descenso de una abeja hacia un loto atra\xedda por su aroma. El pensamiento sostenido (vic\u0101ra) tiene una actividad tranquila, siendo un estado de menor agitaci\xf3n de la mente, similar a la extensi\xf3n de las alas de un ave que ya vuela en el aire, o como el revoloteo de una abeja sobre el loto despu\xe9s de haber descendido sobre \xe9l. En el comentario al Dukanip\u0101ta, sin embargo, se dice: \xabComo el vuelo de un gran p\xe1jaro en el cielo que atrapa el aire con ambas alas y luego las aquieta para elevarse, el pensamiento aplicado se manifiesta como el acto de dirigir la mente hacia el objeto. Como el movimiento de las alas para captar el aire, el pensamiento sostenido se manifiesta como la naturaleza de examinar el objeto\xbb. Esta declaraci\xf3n es adecuada con respecto a la continuidad del proceso. Esta distinci\xf3n entre ellos se hace evidente en el primer y segundo jh\u0101nas."}},{id:"vism-4.20",pali:"Vivekajanti ettha vivitti viveko, n\u012bvara\u1e47avigamoti attho. Vivittoti v\u0101 viveko, n\u012bvara\u1e47avivitto jh\u0101nasampayuttadhammar\u0101s\u012bti attho. Tasm\u0101 vivek\u0101, tasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 viveke j\u0101tanti vivekaja\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Herein, regarding 'born of seclusion' (vivekaja\u1e43): seclusion (vivitti) is viveka; the meaning is the removal of the hindrances. Or, viveka is that which is secluded (vivitto); the meaning is the aggregate of states associated with jh\u0101na which is secluded from the hindrances. Therefore, it is 'born of seclusion' (vivekaja\u1e43) because it is born from that seclusion (vivek\u0101), or born in that seclusion (viveke).",pt:"Em \"nascido do isolamento\" (vivekaja), \"isolamento\" (viveka) significa afastamento, isto \xe9, a remo\xe7\xe3o dos obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47as). Ou \"isolamento\" significa o que \xe9 isolado, referindo-se ao grupo de estados mentais associados ao jh\u0101na que est\xe1 isolado dos obst\xe1culos. Nascido daquele isolamento, ou nascido naquele isolamento, \xe9 \"nascido do isolamento\" (vivekaja).",es:"En cuanto a la expresi\xf3n \xabnacido de la reclusi\xf3n\xbb (vivekaja), aqu\xed \xabreclusi\xf3n\xbb (viveko) significa alejamiento, es decir, la eliminaci\xf3n de los obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47a). O tambi\xe9n, viveko es lo que est\xe1 recluido; es decir, el conjunto de estados asociados con el jh\u0101na que est\xe1n alejados de los obst\xe1culos. Se llama \xabnacido de la reclusi\xf3n\xbb porque nace de esa reclusi\xf3n o en esa reclusi\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-4.21",pali:"S\u0101 panes\u0101 pa\xf1cavidh\u0101 p\u012bti gabbha\u1e43 ga\u1e47hant\u012b parip\u0101ka\u1e43 gacchant\u012b duvidha\u1e43 passaddhi\u1e43 parip\u016breti k\u0101yapassaddhi\xf1ca cittapassaddhi\xf1ca. Passaddhi gabbha\u1e43 ga\u1e47hant\u012b parip\u0101ka\u1e43 gacchant\u012b duvidhampi sukha\u1e43 parip\u016breti k\u0101yika\xf1ca cetasika\xf1ca. Sukha\u1e43 gabbha\u1e43 ga\u1e47hanta\u1e43 parip\u0101ka\u1e43 gacchanta\u1e43 tividha\u1e43 sam\u0101dhi\u1e43 parip\u016breti kha\u1e47ikasam\u0101dhi\u1e43 upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi\u1e43 appan\u0101 sam\u0101dhinti. T\u0101su y\u0101 appan\u0101sam\u0101dhissa m\u016bla\u1e43 hutv\u0101 va\u1e0d\u1e0dham\u0101n\u0101 sam\u0101dhisampayoga\u1e43 gat\u0101 phara\u1e47\u0101p\u012bti, aya\u1e43 imasmi\u1e43 atthe adhippet\u0101 p\u012bt\u012bti.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, this fivefold rapture, by conceiving and maturing, fulfills the twofold tranquility: tranquility of body and tranquility of mind. Tranquility, by conceiving and maturing, fulfills the twofold happiness: bodily and mental. Happiness, by conceiving and maturing, fulfills the threefold concentration: momentary concentration, access concentration, and absorption concentration. Among these, that pervasive rapture which, having become the root of absorption concentration, develops and attains association with concentration\u2014this is intended as 'rapture' in this context.",pt:"Este \xeaxtase de cinco tipos, ao conceber [a tranquilidade] e atingir a maturidade, preenche a dupla tranquilidade: a tranquilidade do corpo (k\u0101yapassaddhi) e a tranquilidade do mente (cittapassaddhi). A tranquilidade, ao conceber [a felicidade] e atingir a maturidade, preenche a dupla felicidade: a felicidade f\xedsica (k\u0101yika) e a felicidade mental (cetasika). A felicidade, ao conceber [a concentra\xe7\xe3o] e atingir a maturidade, preenche a tr\xedplice concentra\xe7\xe3o: a concentra\xe7\xe3o moment\xe2nea (kha\u1e47ikasam\u0101dhi), a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso (upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi) e a concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi). Entre estes, o \xeaxtase pervasivo que, tendo se tornado a raiz da concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o, cresce e alcan\xe7a a associa\xe7\xe3o com a concentra\xe7\xe3o, \xe9 o que se entende aqui por '\xeaxtase' (p\u012bti).",es:"Adem\xe1s, este gozo (p\u012bti) de cinco clases, al concebir la tranquilidad y alcanzar la madurez, completa la doble tranquilidad: la tranquilidad corporal (k\u0101yapassaddhi) y la tranquilidad mental (cittapassaddhi). La tranquilidad, al concebir la felicidad y alcanzar la madurez, completa la doble felicidad (sukha): la f\xedsica y la mental. La felicidad, al concebir la concentraci\xf3n y alcanzar la madurez, completa la triple concentraci\xf3n (sam\u0101dhi): la concentraci\xf3n moment\xe1nea (kha\u1e47ikasam\u0101dhi), la concentraci\xf3n de acceso (upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi) y la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n (appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi). De estas cinco clases de gozo, aquel gozo difusivo (phara\u1e47\u0101p\u012bti) que, actuando como la ra\xedz de la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n y habi\xe9ndose desarrollado previamente en asociaci\xf3n con la concentraci\xf3n de acceso, alcanza la asociaci\xf3n con la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n, es el que se entiende aqu\xed como 'p\u012bti' en este contexto."}},{id:"vism-4.22",pali:"Itara\u1e43 pana sukhana\u1e43 sukha\u1e43, su\u1e6d\u1e6dhu v\u0101 kh\u0101dati, khanati ca k\u0101yacitt\u0101b\u0101dhanti sukha\u1e43, ta\u1e43 s\u0101talakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, sampayutt\u0101na\u1e43 upabr\u016bhanarasa\u1e43, anuggahapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43. Satipi ca nesa\u1e43 katthaci avippayoge i\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ramma\u1e47apa\u1e6dil\u0101bhatu\u1e6d\u1e6dhi p\u012bti. Pa\u1e6diladdharas\u0101nubhavana\u1e43 sukha\u1e43. Yattha p\u012bti, tattha sukha\u1e43. Yattha sukha\u1e43, tattha na niyamato p\u012bti. Sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandhasa\u1e45gahit\u0101 p\u012bti. Vedan\u0101kkhandhasa\u1e45gahita\u1e43 sukha\u1e43. Kant\u0101rakhinnassa vanantudakadassanasavanesu viya p\u012bti. Vanacch\u0101y\u0101pavesanaudakaparibhogesu viya sukha\u1e43. Tasmi\u1e43 tasmi\u1e43 samaye p\u0101ka\u1e6dabh\u0101vato ceta\u1e43 vuttanti veditabba\u1e43. Iti aya\xf1ca p\u012bti ida\xf1ca sukha\u1e43 assa jh\u0101nassa, asmi\u1e43 v\u0101 jh\u0101ne atth\u012bti ida\u1e43 jh\u0101na\u1e43 p\u012btisukhanti vuccati.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, as for the other term, happiness (sukha) is a state of well-being; or, because it thoroughly consumes (su\u1e6d\u1e6dhu kh\u0101dati) and destroys (khanati) bodily and mental affliction, it is called 'happiness' (sukha). It has the characteristic of gratification, the function of enhancing associated states, and its manifestation is support. And although they are inseparable in certain cases, rapture is the delight in obtaining a desirable object, while happiness is the experience of the flavor of what has been obtained. Where there is rapture, there is happiness. Where there is happiness, there is not necessarily rapture. Rapture is included in the aggregate of formations. Happiness is included in the aggregate of feeling. Rapture is like the delight of a person exhausted in the wilderness upon seeing or hearing of a forest grove and water. Happiness is like entering the forest shade and making use of the water. And it should be understood that this is said because of their prominence at their respective times. Thus, because this rapture and this happiness belong to this jh\u0101na, or exist in this jh\u0101na, this jh\u0101na is called 'possessing rapture and happiness' (p\u012btisukha).",pt:"Por outro lado, o termo 'felicidade' (sukha) \xe9 aquilo que agrada (sukhana). Ou \xe9 'felicidade' porque consome completamente (kh\u0101dati) ou escava (khanati) a afli\xe7\xe3o f\xedsica e mental. Tem a caracter\xedstica de ser agrad\xe1vel, a fun\xe7\xe3o de intensificar os dhammas associados e manifesta-se como aux\xedlio. E embora n\xe3o haja dissocia\xe7\xe3o entre eles em certos estados, o \xeaxtase (p\u012bti) \xe9 o contentamento ao obter um objeto desejado. A felicidade (sukha) \xe9 a experi\xeancia do sabor daquilo que foi obtido. Onde h\xe1 \xeaxtase, h\xe1 felicidade. Onde h\xe1 felicidade, n\xe3o h\xe1 necessariamente \xeaxtase. O \xeaxtase est\xe1 inclu\xeddo no agregado das forma\xe7\xf5es mentais (sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandha). A felicidade est\xe1 inclu\xedda no agregado da sensa\xe7\xe3o (vedan\u0101kkhandha). O \xeaxtase \xe9 como o estado de uma pessoa exausta no deserto ao ver ou ouvir falar de uma floresta e de \xe1gua. A felicidade \xe9 como o estado de entrar na sombra da floresta e usufruir da \xe1gua. Deve-se entender que isso foi dito devido \xe0 clareza de ambos em seus respectivos momentos. Assim, este \xeaxtase e esta felicidade pertencem a este jh\u0101na, ou existem neste jh\u0101na; por isso, este jh\u0101na \xe9 chamado 'com \xeaxtase e felicidade' (p\u012btisukha).",es:"En cuanto al otro t\xe9rmino, la felicidad (sukha) se define como aquello que procura bienestar; se llama 'sukha' porque 'devora' (kh\u0101dati) o 'excava' (khanati) completamente las aflicciones del cuerpo y de la mente. Posee la caracter\xedstica de ser placentero (s\u0101ta), la funci\xf3n de intensificar los estados asociados y la manifestaci\xf3n de ser un apoyo. Aunque estos dos (gozo y felicidad) no se separan en ciertos niveles de absorci\xf3n, el gozo (p\u012bti) es el deleite por obtener el objeto deseado, mientras que la felicidad (sukha) es la experiencia de disfrutar el sabor de lo ya obtenido. Donde hay gozo, hay felicidad; pero donde hay felicidad, no hay necesariamente gozo. El gozo se incluye en el agregado de las formaciones (sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandha), mientras que la felicidad se incluye en el agregado de las sensaciones (vedan\u0101kkhandha). El gozo es como la alegr\xeda de un viajero agotado en un desierto al ver o escuchar sobre un bosque y agua; la felicidad es como el placer al entrar en la sombra del bosque y consumir el agua. Debe entenderse que esta distinci\xf3n se hace por su claridad manifiesta en esos respectivos momentos. As\xed, dado que este gozo y esta felicidad pertenecen a este jh\u0101na, o est\xe1n presentes en \xe9l, este jh\u0101na se denomina 'con gozo y felicidad'."}},{id:"vism-4.23",pali:"Et\u0101ni ca pa\xf1ca\u1e45g\u0101ni ki\xf1c\u0101pi upac\u0101rakkha\u1e47epi atthi, atha kho upac\u0101re pakaticittato balavatar\u0101ni. Idha pana upac\u0101ratopi balavatar\u0101ni r\u016bp\u0101vacaralakkha\u1e47appatt\u0101ni. Ettha hi vitakko suvisadena \u0101k\u0101rena \u0101ramma\u1e47e citta\u1e43 abhiniropayam\u0101no uppajjati. Vic\u0101ro ativiya \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 anumajjam\u0101no. P\u012btisukha\u1e43 sabb\u0101vantampi k\u0101ya\u1e43 pharam\u0101na\u1e43. Tenev\u0101ha \u2013 \"n\u0101ssa ki\xf1ci sabb\u0101vato k\u0101yassa vivekajena p\u012btisukhena apphu\u1e6da\u1e43 hot\u012b\"ti. Cittekaggat\u0101pi he\u1e6d\u1e6dhimamhi samuggapa\u1e6dale uparima\u1e43 samuggapa\u1e6dala\u1e43 viya \u0101ramma\u1e47esu phusit\u0101 hutv\u0101 uppajjati, ayametesa\u1e43 itarehi viseso. Tattha cittekaggat\u0101 ki\xf1c\u0101pi savitakka\u1e43 savic\u0101ranti imasmi\u1e43 p\u0101\u1e6dhe na niddi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101, tath\u0101pi vibha\u1e45ge \"jh\u0101nanti vitakko vic\u0101ro p\u012bti sukha\u1e43 cittassekaggat\u0101\"ti eva\u1e43 vuttatt\u0101 a\u1e45gameva. Yena hi adhipp\u0101yena bhagavat\u0101 uddeso kato, soyeva tena vibha\u1e45ge pak\u0101sitoti.",translations:{en:"And although these five factors exist even at the moment of access concentration, in access they are stronger than in an ordinary mind. Here, however, they are even stronger than in access, having attained the characteristic of the fine-material sphere. For here, applied thought arises, directing the mind onto the object with a very clear aspect. Sustained thought arises, exceedingly examining the object. Joy and happiness arise, pervading the entire body. For that reason, He said: 'There is nothing whatsoever of his entire body that is not pervaded by the joy and happiness born of seclusion.' One-pointedness of mind also arises, having made firm contact with the objects like an upper lid on a lower casket; this is their distinction from the others. Therein, although one-pointedness of mind is not specified in this text\u2014'with applied thought, with sustained thought'\u2014nevertheless, because it is stated thus in the Vibha\u1e45ga: 'Jh\u0101na is applied thought, sustained thought, joy, happiness, and one-pointedness of mind,' it is indeed a factor. For with whatever intention the summary was made by the Blessed One, that very intention was declared by Him in the Vibha\u1e45ga.",pt:"E embora estes cinco fatores tamb\xe9m existam no momento do acesso (upac\u0101ra), no acesso eles s\xe3o mais fortes do que na mente comum. Aqui (no jh\u0101na), por\xe9m, eles s\xe3o ainda mais fortes do que no acesso, tendo alcan\xe7ado as caracter\xedsticas da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil (r\u016bp\u0101vacara). Pois aqui o pensamento aplicado surge direcionando a mente ao objeto de uma maneira extremamente clara. O pensamento sustentado surge examinando o objeto intensamente. O \xeaxtase e a felicidade surgem permeando todo o corpo. Por isso foi dito: 'N\xe3o h\xe1 nenhuma parte de todo o seu corpo que n\xe3o esteja permeada pelo \xeaxtase e pela felicidade nascidos do isolamento' (DN 1.228). A unifica\xe7\xe3o mental tamb\xe9m surge tocando firmemente o objeto, assim como a tampa superior de uma caixa se encaixa perfeitamente na sua base inferior; esta \xe9 a diferen\xe7a deles em rela\xe7\xe3o aos outros (no momento do acesso). Embora a unifica\xe7\xe3o mental n\xe3o seja explicitamente mencionada nesta passagem 'com pensamento aplicado e pensamento sustentado', ainda assim, no Vibha\u1e45ga, por ter sido dito: 'Jh\u0101na \xe9 o pensamento aplicado, o pensamento sustentado, o \xeaxtase, a felicidade e a unifica\xe7\xe3o da mente' (Vibh. 569), ela \xe9 de fato um fator. Pois a mesma inten\xe7\xe3o com a qual o Aben\xe7oado fez a exposi\xe7\xe3o resumida foi por Ele esclarecida no Vibha\u1e45ga.",es:"Y estos cinco factores, aunque existen tambi\xe9n en el momento del acceso (upac\u0101ra), en el acceso son m\xe1s fuertes que en el estado mental ordinario. No obstante, aqu\xed [en el jh\u0101na] son a\xfan m\xe1s fuertes que en el acceso y alcanzan las caracter\xedsticas propias del plano de la forma (r\u016bp\u0101vacara). Pues aqu\xed, el vitakka surge elevando la mente hacia el objeto de manera muy clara. El vic\u0101ra surge examinando minuciosamente el objeto. El p\u012bti y el sukha surgen impregnando todo el cuerpo. Por eso se dijo: \xabNo hay ninguna parte de todo su cuerpo que no est\xe9 impregnada por el p\u012bti y el sukha nacidos del aislamiento\xbb (D.N. 1.228). Tambi\xe9n la unidireccionalidad de la mente (cittekaggat\u0101) surge habiendo contactado plenamente el objeto, tal como la tapa superior de un cofre encaja perfectamente con la parte inferior; esta es la distinci\xf3n de estos factores respecto a los otros [del acceso]. All\xed, aunque la unidireccionalidad de la mente no se menciona expl\xedcitamente en el pasaje \xabcon vitakka y vic\u0101ra\xbb, sin embargo, por haberse dicho en el Vibha\u1e45ga: \xabJh\u0101na es vitakka, vic\u0101ra, p\u012bti, sukha y la unidireccionalidad de la mente\xbb (Vibh. 569), es ciertamente un factor. Pues la intenci\xf3n con la que el Bienaventurado realiz\xf3 la exposici\xf3n resumida es la misma intenci\xf3n que \xc9l mismo aclar\xf3 en el Vibha\u1e45ga."}}]},422,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,i,t,s,n){t.exports=[{id:"vism-5.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47\u0101nantare \u0101pokasi\u1e47e vitth\u0101rakath\u0101 hoti. Yatheva hi pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47a\u1e43, eva\u1e43 \u0101pokasi\u1e47ampi bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena sukhanisinnena \u0101pasmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitabba\u1e43, kate v\u0101 akate v\u0101ti sabba\u1e43 vitth\u0101retabba\u1e43. Yath\u0101 ca idha, eva\u1e43 sabbattha. Ito para\xf1hi ettakampi avatv\u0101 visesamattameva vakkh\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"Now, following the earth kasi\u1e47a, there is the detailed discourse on the water kasi\u1e47a. For just as with the earth kasi\u1e47a, so too should one who wishes to develop the water kasi\u1e47a sit comfortably and apprehend the sign in water. The entire method, beginning with 'whether prepared or unprepared,' should be elaborated. And as it is here, so it is in all cases. From this point on, without stating even this much, we shall speak only of the specific details.",pt:"Agora segue-se a explica\xe7\xe3o detalhada sobre o kasina de \xe1gua, logo ap\xf3s o kasina de terra. Pois, assim como no kasina de terra, aquele que deseja desenvolver o kasina de \xe1gua deve, sentado confortavelmente, tomar o sinal na \xe1gua; seja ela preparada ou n\xe3o preparada, tudo deve ser detalhado da mesma maneira. E como \xe9 aqui, assim \xe9 em todos os outros. Doravante, sem repetir tudo isso, explicaremos apenas as particularidades.",es:"Ahora, tras el kasina de tierra, sigue la explicaci\xf3n detallada sobre el kasina de agua. Aquel que desea desarrollar el kasina de agua debe, sentado c\xf3modamente, captar el signo en el agua. Todo debe detallarse de la misma manera que en el kasina de tierra, ya sea en un soporte preparado o no preparado. Y as\xed como se explica aqu\xed, debe entenderse en todos los dem\xe1s casos. A partir de ahora, sin repetir lo que ya se ha dicho, explicaremos solamente los puntos distintivos."}},{id:"vism-5.2",pali:"Idh\u0101pi pubbekat\u0101dhik\u0101rassa pu\xf1\xf1avato akate \u0101pasmi\u1e43 pokkhara\u1e47iy\u0101 v\u0101 ta\u1e37\u0101ke v\u0101 lo\u1e47iya\u1e43 v\u0101 samudde v\u0101 nimitta\u1e43 uppajjati c\u016b\u1e37asivattherassa viya. Tassa kir\u0101yasmato l\u0101bhasakk\u0101ra\u1e43 pah\u0101ya vivittav\u0101sa\u1e43 vasiss\u0101m\u012bti mah\u0101titthe n\u0101vam\u0101r\u016bhitv\u0101 jambud\u012bpa\u1e43 gacchato antar\u0101 mah\u0101samudda\u1e43 olokayato tappa\u1e6dibh\u0101ga\u1e43 kasi\u1e47animitta\u1e43 udap\u0101di.",translations:{en:"Here also, for a person of merit who has made a foundation in the past, the sign arises in unprepared water\u2014in a lotus pond, a lake, a salt-pan, or the ocean\u2014just as it did for the Elder C\u016b\u1e37as\u012bva. It is said that for this venerable one, as he was abandoning gain and honor with the thought, 'I will live in seclusion,' and had boarded a ship at Mah\u0101tittha to go to Jambud\u012bpa, a counterpart kasi\u1e47a sign arose while he was looking upon the great ocean along the way.",pt:"Tamb\xe9m aqui, para aquele que possui m\xe9rito e realizou pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via no passado, o sinal surge na \xe1gua n\xe3o preparada, seja em um lago de l\xf3tus, em um tanque, em uma salina ou no oceano, como no caso do Vener\xe1vel C\u016b\u1e37asiva. Diz-se que para aquele vener\xe1vel, que havia abandonado os ganhos e as honras para viver em reclus\xe3o, ao embarcar em um navio em Mah\u0101tittha para ir \xe0 Terra de Jambu (Jambud\u012bpa), ao olhar para o grande oceano no caminho, surgiu o sinal correspondente do kasina.",es:"Incluso en este caso, para una persona de m\xe9rito que ha realizado pr\xe1cticas previas, el signo surge en agua no preparada, ya sea en un estanque de lotos, un lago, un dep\xf3sito de sal o en el oc\xe9ano, tal como le sucedi\xf3 al Venerable C\u016b\u1e37asiva. Se dice que este venerable, tras abandonar las ganancias y el honor con la intenci\xf3n de vivir en soledad, al subir a un barco en Mah\u0101tittha para ir a Jambud\u012bpa y observar el gran oc\xe9ano durante la traves\xeda, se le manifest\xf3 el signo del kasina correspondiente a lo que estaba contemplando."}},{id:"vism-5.3",pali:"Akat\u0101dhik\u0101rena catt\u0101ro kasi\u1e47adose pariharantena n\u012blap\u012btalohitod\u0101tava\u1e47\u1e47\u0101nama\xf1\xf1atarava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101pa\u1e43 agahetv\u0101 ya\u1e43 pana bh\u016bmi\u1e43 asampattameva \u0101k\u0101se suddhavatthena gahita\u1e43 udaka\u1e43, a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 v\u0101 tath\u0101r\u016bpa\u1e43 vippasanna\u1e43 an\u0101vila\u1e43, tena patta\u1e43 v\u0101 ku\u1e47\u1e0dika\u1e43 v\u0101 samatittika\u1e43 p\u016bretv\u0101 vih\u0101rapaccante vuttappak\u0101re pa\u1e6dicchanne ok\u0101se \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 sukhanisinnena na va\u1e47\u1e47o paccavekkhitabbo. Na lakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 manasi k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Nissayasava\u1e47\u1e47ameva katv\u0101 ussadavasena pa\u1e47\u1e47attidhamme citta\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 ambu, udaka\u1e43, v\u0101ri, salilanti\u0101d\u012bsu \u0101pon\u0101mesu p\u0101ka\u1e6dan\u0101mavaseneva \"\u0101po \u0101po\"ti bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"One who has not made a foundation in the past should, while avoiding the four kasi\u1e47a faults, not take water that has any of the colors blue, yellow, red, or white. Rather, one should take rainwater that has been caught with a clean cloth in the sky before it has reached the ground, or other such water that is clear and limpid. With that water, having filled a bowl or a water pot to the brim and placed it in a secluded location at the edge of the monastery as previously described, one should sit comfortably. The color should not be reflected upon, nor should the characteristic be attended to. Taking the support itself along with its color, and by way of its predominance, having established the mind on the concept, one should develop it by way of a common name from among the names for water\u2014such as ambu, udaka, v\u0101ri, salila\u2014repeating '\u0101po, \u0101po'.",pt:"Aquele que n\xe3o tem pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via deve evitar os quatro defeitos do kasina e n\xe3o deve pegar \xe1gua que tenha uma das cores azul, amarelo, vermelho ou branco. Em vez disso, deve usar \xe1gua que tenha sido recolhida no ar com um pano limpo antes de tocar o solo, ou outra \xe1gua semelhante que seja extremamente l\xedmpida e n\xe3o turva. Com essa \xe1gua, ele deve encher uma tigela ou um jarro at\xe9 a borda e coloc\xe1-lo em um local coberto na periferia do mosteiro, conforme descrito anteriormente. Sentado confortavelmente, ele n\xe3o deve examinar a cor, nem deve trazer \xe0 mente a caracter\xedstica da \xe1gua, como a fluidez. Mantendo o foco no suporte f\xedsico junto com a sua cor, e fixando a mente no conceito de designa\xe7\xe3o (pa\u1e47\u1e47atti) por meio do elemento predominante, ele deve meditar usando o nome mais familiar entre os nomes da \xe1gua, tais como 'ambu', 'udaka', 'v\u0101ri', 'salila', repetindo: '\xe1gua, \xe1gua'.",es:"Quien no tiene pr\xe1cticas previas, evitando los cuatro defectos del kasina, no debe tomar agua que tenga uno de los colores azul, amarillo, rojo o blanco. En su lugar, debe tomar agua que se haya recogido en el aire con un pa\xf1o limpio antes de que llegue a la tierra, u otra agua similar que sea muy clara y no est\xe9 turbia. Con ella debe llenar un cuenco o una vasija hasta el borde y colocarla en un lugar resguardado en los l\xedmites del monasterio, tal como se describi\xf3 anteriormente. Sentado c\xf3modamente, no debe considerar el color ni reflexionar sobre la caracter\xedstica (del elemento agua). Tomando el color como base, debe fijar la mente en el concepto convencional de \xabagua\xbb debido a su predominancia, y desarrollarlo usando uno de los nombres comunes para el agua como \xabambu\xbb, \xabudaka\xbb, \xabv\u0101ri\xbb, \xabsalila\xbb, pero especialmente bajo el nombre m\xe1s conocido: \xab\u0101po, \u0101po\xbb (agua, agua)."}},{id:"vism-5.4",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 bh\u0101vayato anukkamena vuttanayeneva nimittadvaya\u1e43 uppajjati. Idha pana uggahanimitta\u1e43 calam\u0101na\u1e43 viya upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti, sace phe\u1e47apupphu\u1e37akamissa\u1e43 udaka\u1e43 hoti, t\u0101disameva upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti, kasi\u1e47adoso pa\xf1\xf1\u0101yati. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 pana nipparipphanda\u1e43 \u0101k\u0101se \u1e6dhapitama\u1e47it\u0101lava\u1e47\u1e6da\u1e43 viya ma\u1e47imay\u0101d\u0101sama\u1e47\u1e0dalamiva ca hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. So tassa saha upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101neneva upac\u0101rajjh\u0101na\u1e43, vuttanayeneva catukkapa\xf1cakajjh\u0101n\u0101ni ca p\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101t\u012bti. \u0100pokasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"For one thus developing, the two signs gradually arise by the very method already described. Here, however, the learning sign appears as if moving. If the water is mixed with foam and bubbles, it appears just so, and the defect of the kasi\u1e47a is discerned. The counterpart sign, however, being motionless, appears like a jeweled fan-disc placed in the sky and like a jeweled mirror-disc. Together with its very appearance, one attains access concentration and, by the very method already described, the fourfold and fivefold jh\u0101nas. The Water Kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"Para quem medita dessa forma, os dois sinais surgem gradualmente, conforme o m\xe9todo descrito. Aqui, no entanto, o sinal aprendido (uggaha-nimitta) aparece como se estivesse em movimento; se a \xe1gua estiver misturada com espuma e bolhas, ela aparece exatamente assim, e o defeito do kasina torna-se vis\xedvel. O sinal de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ga-nimitta), contudo, aparece completamente im\xf3vel, como um leque de joias suspenso no ar ou como o disco de um espelho feito de pedras preciosas. Com o surgimento desse sinal, ele alcan\xe7a simultaneamente a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso (upac\u0101ra-jh\u0101na) e, pelo m\xe9todo j\xe1 descrito, os jhanas de quatro e de cinco fatores. Assim termina o kasina de \xe1gua.",es:"Para aquel que lo desarrolla de este modo, sucesivamente surgen los dos signos seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ya descrito. Sin embargo, aqu\xed el signo de aprendizaje (uggahanimitta) aparece como si se moviera; si el agua est\xe1 mezclada con espuma o burbujas, el signo aparece de esa misma manera y el defecto del kasina es visible. Pero el signo de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta) aparece inm\xf3vil, como un abanico de joyas de cristal puesto en el cielo o como el c\xedrculo de un espejo de cristal. Junto con la aparici\xf3n de ese signo, el meditador alcanza el jhana de acceso y, mediante el m\xe9todo ya descrito, los jhanas de las clasificaciones de cuatro y cinco. (As\xed concluye el) kasina de agua."}},{id:"vism-5.5",pali:"Tejokasi\u1e47a\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101men\u0101pi tejasmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitabba\u1e43. Tattha kat\u0101dhik\u0101rassa pu\xf1\xf1avato akate nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hantassa d\u012bpasikh\u0101ya v\u0101 uddhane v\u0101 pattapacana\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne v\u0101 davad\u0101he v\u0101 yattha katthaci aggij\u0101la\u1e43 olokentassa nimitta\u1e43 uppajjati cittaguttattherassa viya. Tassa h\u0101yasmato dhammassavanadivase uposath\u0101g\u0101ra\u1e43 pavi\u1e6d\u1e6dhassa d\u012bpasikha\u1e43 olokentasseva nimitta\u1e43 uppajji.",translations:{en:"By one who wishes to develop the fire kasi\u1e47a, the sign should be apprehended in fire. Therein, for a meritorious person who has made the necessary foundation, while apprehending the sign in an unprepared object, the sign arises when looking at a flame anywhere whatsoever\u2014in a lamp flame, in a stove, in a place for baking bowls, or in a forest fire\u2014as it did for the Elder Cittagutta. Indeed, for that venerable one, the sign arose just from looking at a lamp flame upon entering the Uposatha hall on the day of hearing the Dhamma.",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver o kasina de fogo tamb\xe9m deve tomar o sinal no fogo. Para quem possui m\xe9rito e realizou pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via no passado, ao tomar o sinal no fogo n\xe3o preparado, o sinal surge ao olhar para a chama de uma l\xe2mpada, em um forno, no local onde se cozinham tigelas, em um inc\xeandio florestal ou em qualquer chama de fogo, como no caso do Vener\xe1vel Cittagutta. Diz-se que para esse vener\xe1vel, ao entrar na casa de Uposatha no dia de ouvir o Dhamma, o sinal surgiu enquanto ele apenas olhava para a chama de uma l\xe2mpada.",es:"Aquel que desea desarrollar el kasina de fuego tambi\xe9n debe captar el signo en el fuego. En este caso, para quien tiene m\xe9rito por pr\xe1cticas previas, al captar el signo en un fuego no preparado, este surge mientras observa la llama de una l\xe1mpara, el fuego en un horno, en un lugar donde se cuecen cuencos o en un incendio forestal, o en cualquier llama de fuego, tal como le sucedi\xf3 al Venerable Cittagutta. Se dice que a ese venerable, al entrar en la casa del Uposatha el d\xeda de la escucha del Dhamma, se le manifest\xf3 el signo mientras simplemente observaba la llama de una l\xe1mpara."}},{id:"vism-5.6",pali:"Itarena pana k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Tatrida\u1e43 kara\u1e47avidh\u0101na\u1e43, siniddh\u0101ni s\u0101rad\u0101r\u016bni ph\u0101letv\u0101 sukkh\u0101petv\u0101 gha\u1e6dika\u1e43 gha\u1e6dika\u1e43 katv\u0101 patir\u016bpa\u1e43 rukkham\u016bla\u1e43 v\u0101 ma\u1e47\u1e0dapa\u1e43 v\u0101 gantv\u0101 pattapacan\u0101k\u0101rena r\u0101si\u1e43 katv\u0101 \u0101limpetv\u0101 ka\u1e6das\u0101rake v\u0101 camme v\u0101 pa\u1e6de v\u0101 vidatthicatura\u1e45gulappam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 chidda\u1e43 k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Ta\u1e43 purato \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 vuttanayeneva nis\u012bditv\u0101 he\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101 ti\u1e47aka\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43 v\u0101 upari dh\u016bmasikha\u1e43 v\u0101 amanasikaritv\u0101 vemajjhe ghanaj\u0101l\u0101ya nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitabba\u1e43, n\u012blanti v\u0101 p\u012btanti v\u0101ti\u0101divasena va\u1e47\u1e47o na paccavekkhitabbo, u\u1e47hattavasena lakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 na manasi k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Nissayasava\u1e47\u1e47ameva katv\u0101 ussadavasena pa\u1e47\u1e47attidhamme citta\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 p\u0101vako, ka\u1e47havattan\u012b, j\u0101tavedo, hut\u0101sanoti\u0101d\u012bsu aggin\u0101mesu p\u0101ka\u1e6dan\u0101mavaseneva \"tejo tejo\"ti bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"For the other, however, it must be prepared. Herein, this is the method of preparation: split resinous heartwood, dry it, and cut it into pieces. Then, go to a suitable tree root or a pavilion, arrange the wood in a pile in the manner of firing an alms-bowl, and set it alight. Make a hole of a span and four fingers in measure in a straw mat, a hide, or a cloth. Place this in front, sit as previously described, and without attending to the grass or wood below or the plume of smoke above, apprehend the sign in the dense flame in the middle. The color should not be reflected upon as 'blue' or 'yellow,' etc., nor should the characteristic be attended to by way of its hotness. Taking the support itself along with its color, and establishing the mind on the concept by way of predominance, one should develop it by way of a well-known name among the names for fire\u2014such as P\u0101vaka, Ka\u1e47havattan\u012b, J\u0101tavedo, and Hut\u0101sana\u2014as 'tejo, tejo'.",pt:"Por outro lado, aquele que n\xe3o tem pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via deve preparar o kasina. Eis o procedimento para isso: deve-se rachar lenha resinosa e de cerne, sec\xe1-la, cort\xe1-la em peda\xe7os pequenos e, indo para um local apropriado, como o p\xe9 de uma \xe1rvore ou um pavilh\xe3o, fazer uma pilha semelhante \xe0 usada para queimar tigelas e acend\xea-la. Em seguida, deve-se fazer uma abertura de um palmo e quatro dedos de largura em uma esteira de palha, em um peda\xe7o de couro ou em um pano. Colocando isso \xe0 sua frente e sentando-se conforme o m\xe9todo descrito, sem prestar aten\xe7\xe3o \xe0 grama ou \xe0 lenha abaixo, nem \xe0 coluna de fuma\xe7a acima, deve-se tomar o sinal no meio da chama densa. N\xe3o se deve examinar a cor como 'azul' ou 'amarelo', etc., nem se deve trazer \xe0 mente a caracter\xedstica do calor. Mantendo o foco no suporte f\xedsico junto com a sua cor, e fixando a mente no conceito de designa\xe7\xe3o (pa\u1e47\u1e47atti) por meio do elemento predominante, deve-se meditar usando o nome mais familiar entre os nomes do fogo, tais como 'p\u0101vaka', 'ka\u1e47havattan\u012b', 'j\u0101tavedo', 'hut\u0101sana', repetindo: 'fogo, fogo'.",es:"Por el contrario, el practicante que no tiene m\xe9rito previo debe prepararlo. Este es el procedimiento para ello: despu\xe9s de cortar y secar maderas duras y resinosas, y de dividirlas en trozos, debe dirigirse a la base de un \xe1rbol adecuado o a un pabell\xf3n. All\xed, tras amontonarlas al modo de un horno para cocer cuencos e incendiarlas, debe hacer un agujero de un palmo y cuatro dedos de ancho en una estera, una pieza de cuero o una tela. Habiendo colocado eso frente a s\xed y sent\xe1ndose seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ya descrito, debe captar el signo en la densa llama central, sin prestar atenci\xf3n a la hierba y le\xf1a de abajo ni a la punta del humo de arriba. No se debe observar el color seg\xfan sea azul o amarillo, ni se debe reflexionar sobre la caracter\xedstica en t\xe9rminos de calor. Manteniendo el objeto asociado al color de su base, y fijando la mente en la realidad conceptual en t\xe9rminos de su predominancia, debe cultivarlo como 'fuego, fuego', usando nombres comunes para el fuego como p\u0101vaka, ka\u1e47havattan\u012b, j\u0101tavedo o hut\u0101sana."}},{id:"vism-5.7",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 bh\u0101vayato anukkamena vuttanayeneva nimittadvaya\u1e43 uppajjati. Tattha uggahanimitta\u1e43 j\u0101la\u1e43 chijjitv\u0101 chijjitv\u0101 patanasadisa\u1e43 hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Akate ga\u1e47hantassa pana kasi\u1e47adoso pa\xf1\xf1\u0101yati, al\u0101takha\u1e47\u1e0da\u1e43 v\u0101 a\u1e45g\u0101rapi\u1e47\u1e0do v\u0101 ch\u0101rik\u0101 v\u0101 dh\u016bmo v\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 niccala\u1e43 \u0101k\u0101se \u1e6dhapitarattakambalakkha\u1e47\u1e0da\u1e43 viya suva\u1e47\u1e47at\u0101lava\u1e47\u1e6da\u1e43 viya ka\xf1canatthambho viya ca upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. So tassa saha upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101neneva upac\u0101rajjh\u0101na\u1e43, vuttanayeneva catukkapa\xf1cakajjh\u0101n\u0101ni ca p\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101t\u012bti. Tejokasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"As he develops it in this way, the pair of signs arises in due course in the way already described. Therein, the learning sign appears like a flame breaking up repeatedly and falling. But for one who apprehends it in an unprepared object, a fault of the kasi\u1e47a appears: a piece of firebrand, or a mass of embers, or ash, or smoke appears. The counterpart sign appears motionless, like a piece of red blanket placed in the sky, like a golden fan, or like a golden pillar. Simultaneously with its appearance, he attains access concentration and, in the way already described, the fourfold and fivefold jh\u0101nas. The Fire Kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"Para quem medita dessa forma, os dois sinais surgem gradualmente, conforme o m\xe9todo descrito. Entre eles, o sinal aprendido (uggaha-nimitta) aparece como uma chama que se fragmenta e parece cair. No entanto, para quem toma o sinal no fogo n\xe3o preparado, o defeito do kasina torna-se vis\xedvel: aparece um peda\xe7o de ti\xe7\xe3o, uma brasa, cinzas ou fuma\xe7a. O sinal de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ga-nimitta) aparece im\xf3vel, como um peda\xe7o de manta vermelha suspenso no ar, como um leque de ouro ou como uma coluna de ouro. Com o surgimento desse sinal, ele alcan\xe7a simultaneamente a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso (upac\u0101ra-jh\u0101na) e, pelo m\xe9todo j\xe1 descrito, os jhanas de quatro e de cinco fatores. Assim termina o kasina de fogo.",es:"Para quien cultiva de este modo, gradualmente y seg\xfan el m\xe9todo descrito, surgen los dos signos. Entre ellos, el signo aprendido aparece como una llama que se fragmenta y cae repetidamente. Sin embargo, para quien lo capta de un fuego no preparado, se manifiestan los defectos del kasi\u1e47a: aparecen trozos de le\xf1a encendida, brasas, cenizas o humo. El signo de contraparte aparece inm\xf3vil en el espacio, como un trozo de tela de lana roja, como un abanico de oro o como una columna de oro. Con la sola aparici\xf3n de dicho signo, el practicante alcanza el jh\u0101na de acceso y, por el m\xe9todo ya descrito, los cuatro y cinco jh\u0101nas. Con esto concluye la explicaci\xf3n del kasi\u1e47a de fuego."}},{id:"vism-5.8",pali:"V\u0101yokasi\u1e47a\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101men\u0101pi v\u0101yusmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitabba\u1e43. Ta\xf1ca kho di\u1e6d\u1e6dhavasena v\u0101 phu\u1e6d\u1e6dhavasena v\u0101. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 a\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101su \"v\u0101yokasi\u1e47a\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hanto v\u0101yusmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47h\u0101ti, ucchagga\u1e43 v\u0101 erita\u1e43 samerita\u1e43 upalakkheti, ve\u1e37agga\u1e43 v\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 rukkhagga\u1e43 v\u0101 kesagga\u1e43 v\u0101 erita\u1e43 samerita\u1e43 upalakkheti, k\u0101yasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 phu\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43 upalakkhet\u012b\"ti. Tasm\u0101 samas\u012bsa\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43 ghanapatta\u1e43 ucchu\u1e43 v\u0101 ve\u1e37u\u1e43 v\u0101 rukkha\u1e43 v\u0101 catura\u1e45gulappam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 ghanakesassa purisassa s\u012bsa\u1e43 v\u0101 v\u0101tena pahariyam\u0101na\u1e43 disv\u0101 \"aya\u1e43 v\u0101to etasmi\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101ne paharat\u012b\"ti sati\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetv\u0101, ya\u1e43 v\u0101 panassa v\u0101tap\u0101nantarik\u0101ya v\u0101 bhittichiddena v\u0101 pavisitv\u0101 v\u0101to k\u0101yappadesa\u1e43 paharati, tattha sati\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 v\u0101tam\u0101lutaanil\u0101d\u012bsu v\u0101yun\u0101mesu p\u0101ka\u1e6dan\u0101mavaseneva \"v\u0101to v\u0101to\"ti bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43. Idha uggahanimittava\u1e0d\u1e0dhanato ot\u0101ritamattassa p\u0101y\u0101sassa usumava\u1e6d\u1e6disadisa\u1e43 cala\u1e43 hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 sannisinna\u1e43 hoti niccala\u1e43. Sesa\u1e43 vuttanayeneva veditabbanti. V\u0101yokasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"One who wishes to develop the wind kasi\u1e47a should grasp the sign in the wind, either by sight or by touch. For it is stated in the commentaries: 'When learning the wind kasi\u1e47a, one grasps the sign in the wind. One observes the tip of a sugarcane swaying back and forth, the tip of a bamboo... the top of a tree, or the tip of hair swaying back and forth; or one observes the touch of wind on the body.' Therefore, having seen a dense-leaved sugarcane, bamboo, or tree standing with a level top, or the head of a man with thick hair about four finger-breadths long being struck by the wind, one should establish mindfulness, thinking, 'This wind strikes in this place.' Or else, when wind enters through a window opening or a crack in the wall and strikes a part of one's body, one should establish mindfulness there and, by means of a common name for wind\u2014such as v\u0101ta, m\u0101luta, and anila\u2014develop the meditation by repeating, 'wind, wind.' Here, the learning sign appears as something moving, like a wisp of steam from rice porridge just taken off the fire. The counterpart sign becomes settled and motionless. The rest should be understood in the way already explained. The Wind Kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver o kasina de ar tamb\xe9m deve tomar o sinal no ar. E isso pode ser feito por meio da vis\xe3o ou do tato. Pois foi dito nos Coment\xe1rios: 'Aquele que aprende o kasina de ar toma o sinal no ar; ele observa a ponta de uma cana-de-a\xe7\xfacar que \xe9 movida ou agitada pelo vento, ou a ponta de um bambu... pe... ou a copa de uma \xe1rvore, ou a ponta dos cabelos sendo movidos ou agitados pelo vento, ou observa o vento que toca o seu corpo'. Portanto, ao ver a copa de uma cana-de-a\xe7\xfacar, de um bambu ou de uma \xe1rvore com folhagem densa e de altura uniforme, ou a cabe\xe7a de um homem com cabelos densos de quatro dedos de comprimento sendo a\xe7oitados pelo vento, ele deve estabelecer a aten\xe7\xe3o pensando: 'Este vento sopra neste lugar'. Ou ent\xe3o, quando o vento entra por uma fresta de janela ou por uma abertura na parede e toca uma parte do seu corpo, ele deve estabelecer a aten\xe7\xe3o ali e, usando o nome mais familiar entre os nomes do ar, tais como 'v\u0101ta', 'm\u0101luta', 'anila', meditar repetindo: 'ar, ar'. Aqui, o sinal aprendido (uggaha-nimitta) aparece em movimento, como a coluna de vapor que sobe do arroz doce com leite rec\xe9m-retirado do fog\xe3o. O sinal de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ga-nimitta) \xe9 calmo e im\xf3vel. O restante deve ser compreendido da mesma maneira descrita anteriormente. Assim termina o kasina de ar.",es:"Quien desee cultivar el kasi\u1e47a de aire debe captar el signo en el aire. Y esto puede ser mediante la vista o mediante el tacto. Pues as\xed se ha dicho en los Comentarios: 'Quien aprende el kasi\u1e47a de aire capta el signo en el aire; observa la punta de la ca\xf1a de az\xfacar cuando es movida o agitada, o la punta del bamb\xfa... la punta del \xe1rbol o la punta del cabello movido o agitado; o bien observa el contacto en el cuerpo'. Por lo tanto, al ver una planta de ca\xf1a de az\xfacar, un bamb\xfa o un \xe1rbol de follaje denso que est\xe9 a la altura de la cabeza, o la cabeza de un hombre con cabello denso de cuatro dedos de largo siendo golpeados por el viento, debe establecer la atenci\xf3n pensando: 'Este viento golpea en este lugar'. O bien, dondequiera que el viento golpee una parte de su cuerpo tras entrar por el marco de una ventana o por una grieta en la pared, all\xed debe establecer la atenci\xf3n y cultivar como 'aire, aire', usando nombres comunes para el viento como v\u0101ta, m\u0101luta o anila. Aqu\xed, el signo aprendido aparece movi\xe9ndose como el rastro de vapor de un arroz con leche reci\xe9n bajado del fuego. El signo de contraparte es sosegado e inm\xf3vil. Lo restante debe entenderse seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ya descrito. Con esto concluye la explicaci\xf3n del kasi\u1e47a de aire."}},{id:"vism-5.9",pali:"Tadanantara\u1e43 pana n\u012blakasi\u1e47a\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hanto n\u012blakasmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47h\u0101ti pupphasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 vatthasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 va\u1e47\u1e47adh\u0101tuy\u0101 v\u0101ti vacanato kat\u0101dhik\u0101rassa pu\xf1\xf1avato t\u0101va tath\u0101r\u016bpa\u1e43 m\u0101l\u0101gaccha\u1e43 v\u0101 p\u016bj\u0101\u1e6dh\u0101nesu pupphasanthara\u1e43 v\u0101 n\u012blavatthama\u1e47\u012bna\u1e43 v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 disv\u0101va nimitta\u1e43 uppajjati. Itarena n\u012bluppalagirika\u1e47\u1e47ik\u0101d\u012bni pupph\u0101ni gahetv\u0101 yath\u0101 kesara\u1e43 v\u0101 va\u1e47\u1e6da\u1e43 v\u0101 na pa\xf1\xf1\u0101yati, eva\u1e43 ca\u1e45go\u1e6daka\u1e43 v\u0101 kara\u1e47\u1e0dapa\u1e6dala\u1e43 v\u0101 pattehiyeva samatittika\u1e43 p\u016bretv\u0101 santharitabba\u1e43. N\u012blava\u1e47\u1e47ena v\u0101 vatthena bha\u1e47\u1e0dika\u1e43 bandhitv\u0101 p\u016bretabba\u1e43. Mukhava\u1e6d\u1e6diya\u1e43 v\u0101 assa bheritalamiva bandhitabba\u1e43. Ka\u1e43san\u012blapal\u0101san\u012blaa\xf1janan\u012bl\u0101na\u1e43 v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atarena dh\u0101tun\u0101 pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47e vuttanayena sa\u1e43h\u0101rima\u1e43 v\u0101 bhittiya\u1e43yeva v\u0101 kasi\u1e47ama\u1e47\u1e0dala\u1e43 katv\u0101 visabh\u0101gava\u1e47\u1e47ena paricchinditabba\u1e43. Tato pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47e vuttanayena \"n\u012bla\u1e43 n\u012bla\"nti manasik\u0101ro pavattetabbo. Idh\u0101pi uggahanimitte kasi\u1e47adoso pa\xf1\xf1\u0101yati, kesarada\u1e47\u1e0dakapattantarik\u0101d\u012bni upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhahanti. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 kasi\u1e47ama\u1e47\u1e0dalato mu\xf1citv\u0101 \u0101k\u0101se ma\u1e47it\u0101lava\u1e47\u1e6dasadisa\u1e43 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Sesa\u1e43 vuttanayeneva veditabbanti. N\u012blakasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Next, one who undertakes the blue kasi\u1e47a grasps the sign in what is blue\u2014whether in a flower, in a cloth, or in a color-element. Because it is said thus, for a meritorious person who has done the preparatory work, the sign arises just by seeing such a thing as a bush of blue flowers, a carpet of flowers in a place of worship, or one among blue cloths and gems. For another person, having taken flowers such as blue water lilies or Girika\u1e47\u1e47ik\u0101, a basket or the lid of a casket should be filled level to the brim with only the petals and arranged well, in such a way that no stamen or stalk is visible. Alternatively, having tied a bundle with a blue cloth, it should be filled. Or, on its rim, it should be tied taut like a drum-skin. Or, with one of the elements\u2014bronze-blue, leaf-blue, or collyrium-blue\u2014a portable kasi\u1e47a-disk or one right on a wall should be made by the method stated in the earth kasi\u1e47a, and it should be demarcated with a dissimilar color. Thereafter, by the method stated in the earth kasi\u1e47a, attention should be applied thus: \u201cBlue, blue.\u201d Here also, in the learning sign, a kasi\u1e47a-fault appears: stamens, stalks, gaps between petals, and so on, appear. The counterpart sign, having been released from the kasi\u1e47a-disk, appears in space like a fan made of jewels. The rest should be understood by the method already stated. The Blue Kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"Logo em seguida, de acordo com a instru\xe7\xe3o: 'Aquele que aprende o kasina azul toma o sinal em algo azul, seja em uma flor, em um pano ou em um pigmento colorido', para quem possui m\xe9rito e realizou pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via no passado, o sinal surge ao apenas ver um arbusto de flores azuis, uma oferenda de flores azuis em locais de adora\xe7\xe3o, ou um pano azul ou uma gema azul. Por outro lado, aquele que n\xe3o tem pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via deve colher flores como l\xf3tus azuis ou flores de feij\xe3o-borboleta azul (girika\u1e47\u1e47ik\u0101) e, de modo que o p\xf3len ou o talo n\xe3o fiquem vis\xedveis, deve encher uma cesta de flores ou a tampa de um estojo at\xe9 a borda apenas com as p\xe9talas, organizando-as bem. Ou ent\xe3o, deve-se encher um pacote feito com um pano azul. Ou a borda desse recipiente deve ser amarrada como a pele de um tambor. Ou, usando um dos pigmentos como o azul de bronze, o azul de folha ou o azul de col\xedrio, deve-se fazer um disco de kasina port\xe1til ou pintado diretamente na parede, conforme o m\xe9todo descrito no kasina de terra, e delimit\xe1-lo com uma cor contrastante. Depois disso, deve-se direcionar a aten\xe7\xe3o repetindo 'azul, azul', conforme o m\xe9todo descrito no kasina de terra. Tamb\xe9m aqui, no sinal aprendido, o defeito do kasina torna-se vis\xedvel: aparecem o p\xf3len, os talos e os espa\xe7os entre as p\xe9talas. O sinal de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ga-nimitta) aparece desprendido do disco do kasina, como um leque de safira suspenso no ar. O restante deve ser compreendido da mesma maneira descrita anteriormente. Assim termina o kasina azul.",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s, quien aprende el kasi\u1e47a azul capta el signo en el color azul, ya sea en una flor, en una tela o en un elemento coloreado. Seg\xfan estas palabras, para aquel que posee m\xe9rito y ha realizado la preparaci\xf3n necesaria, el signo surge al ver un arbusto de flores, una ofrenda de flores en lugares de adoraci\xf3n, o una tela o gema azul. Por el contrario, el que no tiene m\xe9rito previo debe tomar flores como el loto azul o la clitoria azul y, de tal manera que no se distingan ni el polen ni el tallo, debe llenar un cesto o una caja hasta el borde con p\xe9talos extendidos. O bien, debe llenar un fardo at\xe1ndolo con una tela de color azul. O se debe tensar una tela sobre la abertura como la piel de un tambor. O bien, usando uno de los pigmentos como el bronce azulado, el verde hoja o el colirio negro, se debe fabricar un c\xedrculo de kasi\u1e47a port\xe1til o uno en la pared, tal como se describi\xf3 en el kasi\u1e47a de tierra, delimit\xe1ndolo con un color discordante. Despu\xe9s de eso, se debe dirigir la atenci\xf3n como 'azul, azul', seg\xfan el m\xe9todo descrito en el kasi\u1e47a de tierra. Tambi\xe9n aqu\xed, en el signo aprendido se manifiestan los defectos del kasi\u1e47a: aparecen los espacios entre el polen, los tallos y los p\xe9talos. El signo de contraparte aparece liberado del c\xedrculo del kasi\u1e47a en el espacio, como un abanico enjoyado. Lo restante debe entenderse seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ya descrito. Con esto concluye la explicaci\xf3n del kasi\u1e47a azul."}},{id:"vism-5.10",pali:"P\u012btakasi\u1e47epi eseva nayo. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 p\u012btakasi\u1e47a\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hanto p\u012btakasmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47h\u0101ti pupphasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 vatthasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 va\u1e47\u1e47adh\u0101tuy\u0101 v\u0101ti. Tasm\u0101 idh\u0101pi kat\u0101dhik\u0101rassa pu\xf1\xf1avato tath\u0101r\u016bpa\u1e43 m\u0101l\u0101gaccha\u1e43 v\u0101 pupphasanthara\u1e43 v\u0101 p\u012btavatthadh\u0101t\u016bna\u1e43 v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 disv\u0101va nimitta\u1e43 uppajjati cittaguttattherassa viya. Tassa kir\u0101yasmato cittalapabbate patta\u1e45gapupphehi kata\u1e43 \u0101sanap\u016bja\u1e43 passato saha dassaneneva \u0101sanappam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 udap\u0101di. Itarena ka\u1e47ik\u0101rapupph\u0101din\u0101 v\u0101 p\u012btavatthena v\u0101 dh\u0101tun\u0101 v\u0101 n\u012blakasi\u1e47e vuttanayeneva kasi\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 \"p\u012btaka\u1e43 p\u012btaka\"nti manasik\u0101ro pavattetabbo. Sesa\u1e43 t\u0101disamev\u0101ti. P\u012btakasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"This same method should be understood for the yellow kasi\u1e47a as well. For it is said: \u201cOne learning the yellow kasi\u1e47a apprehends the sign in something yellow\u2014whether in a flower, a cloth, or a color-element.\u201d Therefore, here too, for a meritorious person who has done the preparatory work, upon seeing such a flower bush, a spread of flowers, or any one among yellow cloths and color-elements, the sign arises\u2014just as it did for the Elder Cittagutta. It is said that for that venerable one, while looking at a seat-offering made with patta\u1e45ga flowers on Mount Cittalapabbata, a sign the size of the seat arose simultaneously with the seeing of it. For another person, having prepared the kasi\u1e47a with ka\u1e47ik\u0101ra flowers and so on, or with a yellow cloth, or with a color-element, by the same method stated in the blue kasi\u1e47a section, attention should be directed to it as \u201cyellow, yellow.\u201d The rest is just the same. The Yellow Kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"No kasina amarelo, o m\xe9todo \xe9 exatamente o mesmo. Pois foi dito: 'Aquele que aprende o kasina amarelo toma o sinal em algo amarelo, seja em uma flor, em um pano ou em um pigmento colorido'. Portanto, tamb\xe9m aqui, para quem possui m\xe9rito e realizou pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via no passado, o sinal surge ao apenas ver um arbusto de flores amarelas, uma oferenda de flores amarelas, ou um pano amarelo ou um pigmento amarelo, como no caso do Vener\xe1vel Cittagutta. Diz-se que para esse vener\xe1vel, ao olhar para uma oferenda de flores amarelas de patta\u1e45ga feita no altar do mosteiro de Cittalapabbata, o sinal do tamanho da oferenda surgiu imediatamente ao v\xea-la. Por outro lado, aquele que n\xe3o tem pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via deve fazer um kasina com flores de ka\u1e47ik\u0101ra, etc., ou com um pano amarelo ou com um pigmento amarelo, conforme o m\xe9todo descrito no kasina azul, e direcionar a aten\xe7\xe3o repetindo 'amarelo, amarelo'. O restante \xe9 exatamente igual. Assim termina o kasina amarelo.",es:"En el kasi\u1e47a amarillo se sigue el mismo m\xe9todo. Pues se ha dicho: 'Quien aprende el kasi\u1e47a amarillo capta el signo en lo amarillo, ya sea en una flor, en una tela o en un elemento coloreado'. Por lo tanto, tambi\xe9n aqu\xed, para quien posee m\xe9rito y ha realizado la preparaci\xf3n necesaria, el signo surge al ver un arbusto de flores de ese tipo, una ofrenda de flores, o una tela o elemento amarillo, tal como le ocurri\xf3 al venerable anciano Cittagutta. Se dice que a ese venerable le surgi\xf3 un signo del tama\xf1o de un asiento mientras observaba una ofrenda de flores hecha con flores de patta\u1e45ga en la monta\xf1a Cittala, en el momento mismo de verla. El otro practicante, habiendo preparado el kasi\u1e47a con flores de ka\u1e47ik\u0101ra y similares, o con una tela amarilla o pigmento, seg\xfan el m\xe9todo descrito en el kasi\u1e47a azul, debe dirigir la atenci\xf3n como 'amarillo, amarillo'. Lo dem\xe1s es igual. Con esto concluye la explicaci\xf3n del kasi\u1e47a amarillo."}},{id:"vism-5.11",pali:"Lohitakasi\u1e47epi eseva nayo. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 lohitakasi\u1e47a\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hanto lohitakasmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47h\u0101ti pupphasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 vatthasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 va\u1e47\u1e47adh\u0101tuy\u0101 v\u0101ti. Tasm\u0101 idh\u0101pi kat\u0101dhik\u0101rassa pu\xf1\xf1avato tath\u0101r\u016bpa\u1e43 bandhuj\u012bvak\u0101dim\u0101l\u0101gaccha\u1e43 v\u0101 pupphasanthara\u1e43 v\u0101 lohitakavatthama\u1e47idh\u0101t\u016bna\u1e43 v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 disv\u0101va nimitta\u1e43 uppajjati. Itarena jayasumanabandhuj\u012bvakarattakora\u1e47\u1e0dak\u0101dipupphehi v\u0101 rattavatthena v\u0101 dh\u0101tun\u0101 v\u0101 n\u012blakasi\u1e47e vuttanayeneva kasi\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 \"lohitaka\u1e43 lohitaka\"nti manasik\u0101ro pavattetabbo. Sesa\u1e43 t\u0101disamev\u0101ti. Lohitakasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"This same method should be understood for the red kasi\u1e47a as well. For it is said: \u201cOne learning the red kasi\u1e47a apprehends the sign in something red\u2014whether in a flower, a cloth, or a color-element.\u201d Therefore, here too, for a meritorious person who has done the preparatory work, upon seeing such a flower bush of bandhuj\u012bvaka and so on, a spread of flowers, or any one among red cloths, gems, and color-elements, the sign arises. For another person, having prepared the kasi\u1e47a with flowers such as jayasumana, bandhuj\u012bvaka, rattakora\u1e47\u1e0daka, and so on, or with a red cloth, or with a color-element, by the same method stated in the blue kasi\u1e47a section, attention should be directed to it as \u201cred, red.\u201d The rest is just the same. The Red Kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"No kasina vermelho, o m\xe9todo \xe9 exatamente o mesmo. Pois foi dito: 'Aquele que aprende o kasina vermelho toma o sinal em algo vermelho, seja em uma flor, em um pano ou em um pigmento colorido'. Portanto, tamb\xe9m aqui, para quem possui m\xe9rito e realizou pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via no passado, o sinal surge ao apenas ver um arbusto de flores vermelhas como bandhuj\u012bvaka, uma oferenda de flores vermelhas, ou um pano vermelho, uma gema vermelha ou um pigmento vermelho. Por outro lado, aquele que n\xe3o tem pr\xe1tica pr\xe9via deve fazer um kasina com flores de jayasumana, bandhuj\u012bvaka, kora\u1e47\u1e0daka vermelho, etc., ou com um pano vermelho ou com um pigmento vermelho, conforme o m\xe9todo descrito no kasina azul, e direcionar a aten\xe7\xe3o repetindo 'vermelho, vermelho'. O restante \xe9 exatamente igual. Assim termina o kasina vermelho.",es:"En el kasi\u1e47a rojo se sigue el mismo m\xe9todo. Pues se ha dicho: 'Quien aprende el kasi\u1e47a rojo capta el signo en lo rojo, ya sea en una flor, en una tela o en un elemento coloreado'. Por lo tanto, tambi\xe9n aqu\xed, para quien posee m\xe9rito y ha realizado la preparaci\xf3n necesaria, el signo surge al ver un arbusto de flores de bandhuj\u012bvaka y similares, una ofrenda de flores, o una tela, gema o elemento rojo. El otro practicante, habiendo preparado el kasi\u1e47a con flores de jayasumana, bandhuj\u012bvaka, kora\u1e47\u1e0daka rojo y similares, o con una tela roja o pigmento, seg\xfan el m\xe9todo descrito en el kasi\u1e47a azul, debe dirigir la atenci\xf3n como 'rojo, rojo'. Lo dem\xe1s es igual. Con esto concluye la explicaci\xf3n del kasi\u1e47a rojo."}},{id:"vism-5.12",pali:"Od\u0101takasi\u1e47epi od\u0101takasi\u1e47a\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hanto od\u0101tasmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47h\u0101ti pupphasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 vatthasmi\u1e43 v\u0101 va\u1e47\u1e47adh\u0101tuy\u0101 v\u0101ti vacanato kat\u0101dhik\u0101rassa t\u0101va pu\xf1\xf1avato tath\u0101r\u016bpa\u1e43 m\u0101l\u0101gaccha\u1e43 v\u0101 vassikasuman\u0101dipupphasanthara\u1e43 v\u0101 kumudapadumar\u0101si\u1e43 v\u0101 od\u0101tavatthadh\u0101t\u016bna\u1e43 v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 disv\u0101va nimitta\u1e43 uppajjati, tipuma\u1e47\u1e0dalarajatama\u1e47\u1e0dalacandama\u1e47\u1e0dalesupi uppajjatiyeva. Itarena vuttappak\u0101rehi od\u0101tapupphehi v\u0101 od\u0101tavatthena v\u0101 dh\u0101tun\u0101 v\u0101 n\u012blakasi\u1e47e vuttanayeneva kasi\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 \"od\u0101ta\u1e43 od\u0101ta\"nti manasik\u0101ro pavattetabbo. Sesa\u1e43 t\u0101disamev\u0101ti. Od\u0101takasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"In the white kasi\u1e47a also, one learning the white kasi\u1e47a takes the sign in something white\u2014whether in a flower, a cloth, or a color element. Thus, for a meritorious person who has done the preparatory work, the sign arises just upon seeing such a garland-bush, a spread of vassika jasmine or other flowers, a heap of kumuda water lilies or paduma lotuses, or any one among white cloths or elements. It also arises in a disc of lead, a disc of silver, and the moon-disc. For another person, using the aforementioned white flowers, white cloth, or element, the kasi\u1e47a should be prepared by the very method described for the blue kasi\u1e47a, and attention should be directed with the thought, \u201cwhite, white.\u201d The rest is just the same. The White Kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"No kasina branco (od\u0101takasi\u1e47a), conforme a passagem: 'Aquele que aprende o kasina branco capta o sinal no branco, seja em uma flor, em um tecido ou em um elemento de cor', para quem possui m\xe9rito acumulado e realizou a prepara\xe7\xe3o necess\xe1ria no passado, o sinal surge assim que v\xea um arbusto de flores brancas, ou um leito de flores como jasmim-\xe1rabe ou jasmim-da-espanha, ou um monte de l\xf3tus brancos ou l\xf3tus vermelhos, ou qualquer tecido branco ou elemento mineral branco. O sinal tamb\xe9m surge em um disco de estanho, em um disco de prata ou no disco da lua. Para outra pessoa (sem m\xe9rito acumulado), ela deve preparar o kasina usando flores brancas, tecido branco ou elemento mineral branco, conforme o m\xe9todo descrito para o kasina azul, e aplicar a aten\xe7\xe3o mental dizendo: 'Branco, branco'. O restante \xe9 exatamente igual. Assim termina o kasina branco.",es:"En el kasi\u1e47a blanco (od\u0101takasi\u1e47a), aquel que aprende el kasi\u1e47a blanco toma el signo en lo blanco, ya sea en una flor, en una tela o en un elemento de color [mineral], seg\xfan se dice. Por lo tanto, para una persona meritoria que ha realizado m\xe9ritos previos en esta pr\xe1ctica, el signo surge con solo ver un arbusto de flores de tal naturaleza, o un lecho de flores como el jazm\xedn vassika o sumana, etc., o un mont\xf3n de lotos kumuda o paduma, o cualquiera de las telas o elementos blancos; tambi\xe9n surge en un disco de plomo, un disco de plata o en el disco de la luna. Para otros [que no poseen m\xe9ritos previos], se debe preparar el dispositivo del kasi\u1e47a de la misma manera descrita para el kasi\u1e47a azul, utilizando flores blancas, tela blanca o elementos minerales blancos mencionados, y dirigir la atenci\xf3n diciendo: 'blanco, blanco'. El resto es igual a lo anterior. (Kasi\u1e47a blanco)."}},{id:"vism-5.13",pali:"\u0100lokakasi\u1e47e pana \u0101lokakasi\u1e47a\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hanto \u0101lokasmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47h\u0101ti bhittichidde v\u0101 t\u0101\u1e37acchidde v\u0101 v\u0101tap\u0101nantarik\u0101ya v\u0101ti vacanato kat\u0101dhik\u0101rassa t\u0101va pu\xf1\xf1avato ya\u1e43 bhittichidd\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1atarena s\u016briy\u0101loko v\u0101 cand\u0101loko v\u0101 pavisitv\u0101 bhittiya\u1e43 v\u0101 bh\u016bmiya\u1e43 v\u0101 ma\u1e47\u1e0dala\u1e43 samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101peti, ghanapa\u1e47\u1e47arukkhas\u0101khantarena v\u0101 ghanas\u0101kh\u0101ma\u1e47\u1e0dapantarena v\u0101 nikkhamitv\u0101 bh\u016bmiyameva ma\u1e47\u1e0dala\u1e43 samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101peti, ta\u1e43 disv\u0101va nimitta\u1e43 uppajjati. Itaren\u0101pi tadeva vuttappak\u0101ramobh\u0101sama\u1e47\u1e0dala\u1e43 \"obh\u0101so obh\u0101so\"ti v\u0101 \"\u0101loko \u0101loko\"ti v\u0101 bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43. Tath\u0101 asakkontena gha\u1e6de d\u012bpa\u1e43 j\u0101letv\u0101 gha\u1e6damukha\u1e43 pidahitv\u0101 gha\u1e6de chidda\u1e43 katv\u0101 bhittimukha\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetabba\u1e43. Tena chiddena d\u012bp\u0101loko nikkhamitv\u0101 bhittiya\u1e43 ma\u1e47\u1e0dala\u1e43 karoti, ta\u1e43 \u0101loko \u0101lokoti bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43. Idamitarehi cira\u1e6d\u1e6dhitika\u1e43 hoti. Idha uggahanimitta\u1e43 bhittiya\u1e43 v\u0101 bh\u016bmiya\u1e43 v\u0101 u\u1e6d\u1e6dhitama\u1e47\u1e0dalasadisameva hoti. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 ghanavippasanna\u0101lokapu\xf1jasadisa\u1e43. Sesa\u1e43 t\u0101disamev\u0101ti. \u0100lokakasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now, regarding the light kasi\u1e47a, one learning the light kasi\u1e47a takes the sign in the light entering through a hole in a wall, a keyhole, or an interstice of a window. Thus, for a meritorious person who has done the preparatory work, when sunlight or moonlight enters through one of these and forms a circle on a wall or the ground; or when it emerges through the dense foliage of a tree or a thick canopy of branches and forms a circle on the ground, upon seeing that, the sign arises. For another person, that same kind of luminous circle should be developed with the thought, \u201cradiance, radiance\u201d or \u201clight, light.\u201d If unable to do so, one should light a lamp inside a pot, cover the mouth of the pot, make a hole in the pot, and place it facing a wall. The light from the lamp passes through the hole and forms a circle on the wall, which should then be developed as \u201clight, light.\u201d This is more long-lasting than the others. Here, the learning sign is just like the circle that appears on the wall or ground. The counterpart sign resembles a mass of dense and very clear light. The rest is just the same. The Light Kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"No kasina da luz (\u0101lokakasi\u1e47a), conforme a passagem: 'Aquele que aprende o kasina da luz capta o sinal na luz, seja atrav\xe9s de uma fresta na parede, de um buraco de fechadura ou de uma abertura na janela', para quem possui m\xe9rito acumulado e realizou a prepara\xe7\xe3o necess\xe1ria no passado, o sinal surge assim que v\xea o c\xedrculo de luz que se projeta na parede ou no ch\xe3o quando a luz do sol ou da lua entra por uma fresta na parede ou similar, ou o c\xedrculo de luz que se projeta no ch\xe3o ao passar por entre os galhos de uma \xe1rvore de folhagem densa ou por entre a ramagem de um pavilh\xe3o de folhagem espessa. Para outra pessoa (sem m\xe9rito acumulado), esse mesmo c\xedrculo de luz descrito deve ser desenvolvido mentalmente como 'brilho, brilho' ou 'luz, luz'. Se ela n\xe3o for capaz de fazer isso, deve acender uma l\xe2mpada dentro de um pote de barro, cobrir a boca do pote, fazer um furo no pote e coloc\xe1-lo de frente para a parede. A luz da l\xe2mpada que sai por esse furo formar\xe1 um c\xedrculo na parede, e ela deve desenvolv\xea-lo mentalmente como 'luz, luz'. Este c\xedrculo de luz \xe9 mais duradouro do que os outros (do sol ou da lua). Aqui, o sinal de apreens\xe3o (uggahanimitta) \xe9 exatamente igual ao c\xedrculo de luz projetado na parede ou no ch\xe3o. O sinal de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta) \xe9 semelhante a um feixe de luz denso e extremamente l\xedmpido. O restante \xe9 exatamente igual. Assim termina o kasina da luz.",es:"En el kasi\u1e47a de luz (\u0101lokakasi\u1e47a), aquel que aprende el kasi\u1e47a de luz toma el signo en la luz, ya sea en un agujero en la pared, el ojo de una cerradura o el espacio entre las contraventanas de una ventana, seg\xfan se dice. Por lo tanto, para una persona meritoria que ha realizado m\xe9ritos previos, el signo surge con solo ver el c\xedrculo de luz que se produce cuando la luz del sol o de la luna entra a trav\xe9s de alguno de estos agujeros en la pared, etc., y se proyecta en la pared o en el suelo; o cuando pasa a trav\xe9s del follaje espeso de las ramas de un \xe1rbol o de un pabell\xf3n de ramas densas y se proyecta en el suelo. Para otros, se debe meditar en ese mismo c\xedrculo de resplandor descrito como 'resplandor, resplandor' o 'luz, luz'. Si no se puede generar el signo de esa manera, se debe encender una l\xe1mpara dentro de una vasija, cubrir la boca de la vasija, hacerle un agujero y colocarla frente a una pared. La luz de la l\xe1mpara saldr\xe1 por ese agujero y formar\xe1 un c\xedrculo en la pared; ese c\xedrculo debe ser meditado como 'luz, luz'. Este c\xedrculo de luz de l\xe1mpara es de mayor duraci\xf3n que los otros [producidos por el sol o la luna]. Aqu\xed, el signo aprendido (uggahanimitta) es igual al c\xedrculo que aparece en la pared o en el suelo. El signo de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta) es similar a una masa de luz densa y muy clara. El resto es igual a lo anterior. (Kasi\u1e47a de luz)."}},{id:"vism-5.14",pali:"Paricchinn\u0101k\u0101sakasi\u1e47epi \u0101k\u0101sakasi\u1e47a\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hanto \u0101k\u0101sasmi\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47h\u0101ti bhittichidde v\u0101 t\u0101\u1e37acchidde v\u0101 v\u0101tap\u0101nantarik\u0101ya v\u0101ti vacanato kat\u0101dhik\u0101rassa t\u0101va pu\xf1\xf1avato bhittichidd\u0101d\u012bsu a\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 disv\u0101va nimitta\u1e43 uppajjati. Itarena succhannama\u1e47\u1e0dape v\u0101 cammaka\u1e6das\u0101rak\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atarasmi\u1e43 vidatthicatura\u1e45gulappam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 chidda\u1e43 katv\u0101 tadeva v\u0101 bhittichidd\u0101dibheda\u1e43 chidda\u1e43 \"\u0101k\u0101so \u0101k\u0101so\"ti bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43. Idha uggahanimitta\u1e43 saddhi\u1e43 bhittipariyant\u0101d\u012bhi chiddasadisameva hoti, va\u1e0d\u1e0dhiyam\u0101nampi na va\u1e0d\u1e0dhati. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimittam\u0101k\u0101sama\u1e47\u1e0dalameva hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti, va\u1e0d\u1e0dhiyam\u0101na\xf1ca va\u1e0d\u1e0dhati. Sesa\u1e43 pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47e vuttanayeneva veditabbanti. Paricchinn\u0101k\u0101sakasi\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"In the bounded space kasi\u1e47a also, it is said: 'One who is apprehending the space kasi\u1e47a takes the sign in space, such as in a hole in a wall, a keyhole, or the gap of a window.' Therefore, for a fortunate person who has made the requisite preparations, the sign arises simply upon seeing one among such things as a hole in a wall. For another, in a well-covered pavilion or on one among such things as a leather mat, a hole measuring a span and four fingers should be made, or that very hole, being one of the various kinds such as a hole in a wall, should be developed as \u201cspace, space.\u201d Here, the learning sign is just like the hole itself, together with the edges of the wall and so on; even when one tries to expand it, it does not expand. The counterpart sign appears, having become a mere circle of space; and when one tries to expand it, it expands. The rest should be understood in the very way spoken of in the earth kasi\u1e47a. The Bounded Space Kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"No kasina do espa\xe7o limitado (paricchinn\u0101k\u0101sakasi\u1e47a), conforme a passagem: 'Aquele que aprende o kasina do espa\xe7o capta o sinal no espa\xe7o, seja atrav\xe9s de uma fresta na parede, de um buraco de fechadura ou de uma abertura na janela', para quem possui m\xe9rito acumulado e realizou a prepara\xe7\xe3o necess\xe1ria no passado, o sinal surge assim que v\xea qualquer uma dessas aberturas, como uma fresta na parede. Para outra pessoa (sem m\xe9rito acumulado), ela deve fazer um furo com a medida de um palmo e quatro dedos em um pavilh\xe3o bem coberto, ou em uma esteira de couro ou similar, e desenvolver mentalmente esse mesmo furo, ou uma fresta na parede ou similar, como 'espa\xe7o, espa\xe7o'. Aqui, o sinal de apreens\xe3o (uggahanimitta) \xe9 exatamente igual ao furo, juntamente com as bordas da parede ou do material, e mesmo quando se tenta expandi-lo, ele n\xe3o se expande. O sinal de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta) aparece apenas como um c\xedrculo de espa\xe7o e, quando expandido, ele se expande. O restante deve ser compreendido conforme o m\xe9todo descrito para o kasina da terra. Assim termina o kasina do espa\xe7o limitado.",es:"En el kasi\u1e47a de espacio limitado (paricchinn\u0101k\u0101sakasi\u1e47a), aquel que aprende el kasi\u1e47a de espacio toma el signo en el espacio, ya sea en un agujero en la pared, el ojo de una cerradura o el espacio entre las contraventanas, seg\xfan se dice. Por lo tanto, para una persona meritoria que ha realizado m\xe9ritos previos, el signo surge con solo ver uno de esos agujeros en la pared, etc. Para otros, se debe hacer un agujero de un palmo y cuatro dedos de ancho en un pabell\xf3n bien cubierto o en algo como una estera de cuero, etc., y meditar en ese agujero o en uno similar en una pared diciendo: 'espacio, espacio'. Aqu\xed, el signo aprendido es igual al agujero junto con los bordes de la pared, etc.; aunque se intente ampliar, no se expande. El signo de contraparte aparece solo como un c\xedrculo de espacio y, al ser ampliado, se expande. El resto debe entenderse de la misma manera que se describi\xf3 en el kasi\u1e47a de tierra. (Kasi\u1e47a de espacio limitado)."}},{id:"vism-5.15",pali:"Iti kasi\u1e47\u0101ni dasabalo, Dasa y\u0101ni avoca sabbadhammadaso; R\u016bp\u0101vacaramhi catukkapa\xf1cakajjh\u0101nahet\u016bni.",translations:{en:"Thus, the Ten-Powered One, the Seer of all things, taught the ten kasi\u1e47as which are the causes of the fourfold and fivefold jh\u0101nas in the form sphere.",pt:"Assim, o Possuidor das Dez For\xe7as (Dasabalo), Aquele que v\xea todas as coisas, ensinou estes dez kasinas, que s\xe3o as causas para os quatro e cinco jhanas na esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil (r\u016bp\u0101vacara).",es:"As\xed, el Poseedor de los Diez Poderes (Dasabalo), quien ve todos los fealidades (sabbadhammadaso), declar\xf3 estos diez kasi\u1e47as como las causas para los cuatro y cinco jhanas del reino de la forma (r\u016bp\u0101vacara)."}},{id:"vism-5.16",pali:"Imesu hi pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47avasena ekopi hutv\u0101 bahudh\u0101 hot\u012bti\u0101dibh\u0101vo, \u0101k\u0101se v\u0101 udake v\u0101 pathavi\u1e43 nimminitv\u0101 padas\u0101 gamana\u1e43, \u1e6dh\u0101nanisajj\u0101dikappana\u1e43 v\u0101, parittaappam\u0101\u1e47anayena abhibh\u0101yatanapa\u1e6dil\u0101bhoti evam\u0101d\u012bni ijjhanti.",translations:{en:"Indeed, among these kasi\u1e47as, by means of the earth kasi\u1e47a, such things as the state of 'having been one, he becomes many'; creating earth in the sky or on water and walking on foot; or the arranging of postures such as standing and sitting; and the attainment of the spheres of mastery by the method of the limited and the unlimited\u2014these and other such things are accomplished.",pt:"Pois, por meio do kasina da terra, realizam-se poderes como: tornar-se muitos sendo um s\xf3, caminhar a p\xe9 no ar ou na \xe1gua ap\xf3s criar terra firme, permanecer de p\xe9 ou sentar-se neles, e a obten\xe7\xe3o das bases de transcend\xeancia (abhibh\u0101yatana) por meio do m\xe9todo limitado ou imensur\xe1vel.",es:"Ciertamente, a trav\xe9s del kasi\u1e47a de tierra, se logran beneficios tales como: ser uno y convertirse en muchos, caminar sobre el agua o en el aire tras crear tierra, realizar posturas como estar de pie o sentado en ellos, y la obtenci\xf3n de las bases de maestr\xeda (abhibh\u0101yatana) mediante los m\xe9todos de lo limitado y lo imnensurable."}},{id:"vism-5.17",pali:"\u0100pokasi\u1e47avasena pathaviya\u1e43 ummujjananimmujjana\u1e43, udakavu\u1e6d\u1e6dhisamupp\u0101dana\u1e43, nad\u012bsamudd\u0101dinimm\u0101na\u1e43, pathav\u012bpabbatap\u0101s\u0101d\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 kampananti evam\u0101d\u012bni ijjhanti.",translations:{en:"By means of the water kasi\u1e47a, emerging from and diving into the earth, causing a shower of water to arise, creating rivers and oceans, and causing the earth, mountains, palaces, and so forth to shake\u2014these and other such things are accomplished.",pt:"Por meio do kasina da \xe1gua, realizam-se poderes como: mergulhar e emergir na terra, fazer chover, criar rios e oceanos, e fazer tremer a terra, montanhas e pal\xe1cios.",es:"A trav\xe9s del kasi\u1e47a de agua, se logran: emerger y sumergirse en la tierra, producir lluvia, crear r\xedos y oc\xe9anos, y hacer temblar la tierra, las monta\xf1as y los palacios."}},{id:"vism-5.18",pali:"Tejokasi\u1e47avasena dh\u016bm\u0101yan\u0101, pajjalan\u0101, a\u1e45g\u0101ravu\u1e6d\u1e6dhisamupp\u0101dana\u1e43, tejas\u0101 tejopariy\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43, yadeva so icchati tassa \u1e0dahanasamatthat\u0101, dibbena cakkhun\u0101 r\u016bpadassanatth\u0101ya \u0101lokakara\u1e47a\u1e43, parinibb\u0101nasamaye tejodh\u0101tuy\u0101 sar\u012brajjh\u0101pananti evam\u0101d\u012bni ijjhanti.",translations:{en:"By means of the fire kasi\u1e47a, emitting smoke, emitting flames, causing a shower of embers to arise, overpowering another's heat with one's own heat, the ability to burn whatsoever one wishes, creating light for the purpose of seeing forms with the divine eye, and the burning of the body by means of the fire element at the time of final Nibb\u0101na\u2014these and other such things are accomplished.",pt:"Por meio do kasina do fogo, realizam-se poderes como: produzir fuma\xe7a, chamas e chuva de brasas, subjugar o poder alheio com o pr\xf3prio poder, queimar apenas o que se deseja queimar, criar luz para ver formas com o olho divino (dibbacakkhu) e queimar o pr\xf3prio corpo com o elemento fogo no momento do parinibbana.",es:"A trav\xe9s del kasi\u1e47a de fuego, se logran: la emisi\xf3n de humo y llamas, la producci\xf3n de una lluvia de carbones ardientes, consumir el calor ajeno con el propio calor, la capacidad de quemar solo lo que se desea, la creaci\xf3n de luz para ver formas con el ojo divino (dibba-cakkhu), y la incineraci\xf3n del cuerpo con el elemento fuego en el momento del parinibb\u0101na."}},{id:"vism-5.19",pali:"V\u0101yokasi\u1e47avasena v\u0101yugatigamana\u1e43, v\u0101tavu\u1e6d\u1e6dhisamupp\u0101dananti evam\u0101d\u012bni ijjhanti.",translations:{en:"By means of the air kasi\u1e47a, traveling with the speed of wind and producing a great wind\u2014these and other such things are accomplished.",pt:"Por meio do kasina do ar, realizam-se poderes como: mover-se com a velocidade do vento e provocar vendavais e tempestades.",es:"A trav\xe9s del kasi\u1e47a de aire, se logran: desplazarse con la velocidad del aire y la producci\xf3n de r\xe1fagas de viento y tormentas."}},{id:"vism-5.20",pali:"N\u012blakasi\u1e47avasena n\u012blar\u016bpanimm\u0101na\u1e43, andhak\u0101rakara\u1e47a\u1e43, suva\u1e47\u1e47adubba\u1e47\u1e47anayena abhibh\u0101yatanapa\u1e6dil\u0101bho, subhavimokkh\u0101dhigamoti evam\u0101d\u012bni ijjhanti.",translations:{en:"By means of the blue kasi\u1e47a, creating blue forms, producing darkness, the attainment of the spheres of mastery by the method of pure and impure colors, and the attainment of the beautiful liberation\u2014these and other such things are accomplished.",pt:"Por meio do kasina azul, realizam-se poderes como: criar formas azuis, produzir escurid\xe3o, obter as bases de transcend\xeancia (abhibh\u0101yatana) pelo m\xe9todo da beleza e da feiura, e alcan\xe7ar a liberta\xe7\xe3o bela (subhavimokkha).",es:"A trav\xe9s del kasi\u1e47a azul, se logran: la creaci\xf3n de formas azules, la producci\xf3n de oscuridad, la obtenci\xf3n de las bases de maestr\xeda mediante el m\xe9todo de lo bello y lo no bello, y el logro de la liberaci\xf3n de lo bello (subhavimokkha)."}},{id:"vism-5.21",pali:"\u0100lokakasi\u1e47avasena sappabh\u0101r\u016bpanimm\u0101na\u1e43, thinamiddhassa d\u016brabh\u0101vakara\u1e47a\u1e43, andhak\u0101ravidhamana\u1e43, dibbena cakkhun\u0101 r\u016bpadassanattha\u1e43 \u0101lokakara\u1e47anti evam\u0101d\u012bni ijjhanti.",translations:{en:"By means of the light kasi\u1e47a, creating radiant forms, making sloth and torpor far away, dispelling darkness, and producing light for the purpose of seeing forms with the divine eye\u2014these and other such things are accomplished.",pt:"Por meio do kasina da luz, realizam-se poderes como: criar formas luminosas, afastar a pregui\xe7a e o torpor, dissipar a escurid\xe3o e criar luz para ver formas com o olho divino.",es:"A trav\xe9s del kasi\u1e47a de luz, se logran: la creaci\xf3n de formas radiantes, el alejamiento de la pereza y el letargo, la disipaci\xf3n de la oscuridad y la creaci\xf3n de luz para ver formas con el ojo divino."}},{id:"vism-5.22",pali:"Sabb\u0101neva uddha\u1e43 adho tiriya\u1e43 advaya\u1e43 appam\u0101\u1e47anti ima\u1e43 pabheda\u1e43 labhanti. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 \"pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47ameko sa\xf1j\u0101n\u0101ti. Uddhamadhotiriya\u1e43 advayamappam\u0101\u1e47a\"nti\u0101di.",translations:{en:"All ten kasi\u1e47as indeed attain this distinction: 'above, below, across, non-dual, immeasurable.' For it was said: 'One perceives the earth kasi\u1e47a: above, below, across, non-dual, immeasurable,' and so forth.",pt:"Todos os dez kasinas admitem esta classifica\xe7\xe3o: para cima, para baixo, horizontalmente, sem dualidade (indivis\xedvel) e imensur\xe1vel. Pois foi dito: 'Algu\xe9m percebe o kasina da terra para cima, para baixo, horizontalmente, sem dualidade, imensur\xe1vel', e assim por diante.",es:"Todos los diez kasi\u1e47as adquieren estas distinciones: hacia arriba, hacia abajo, a los lados, no dual e imnensurable. Pues se ha dicho: 'Uno percibe el kasi\u1e47a de tierra: hacia arriba, hacia abajo, a los lados, no dual e imnensurable', etc."}}]},423,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,i,s,t,n){s.exports=[{id:"vism-6.1",pali:"Kasi\u1e47\u0101nantaramuddi\u1e6d\u1e6dhesu pana uddhum\u0101taka\u1e43, vin\u012blaka\u1e43, vipubbaka\u1e43, vicchiddaka\u1e43, vikkh\u0101yitaka\u1e43, vikkhittaka\u1e43, hatavikkhittaka\u1e43, lohitaka\u1e43, pu\u1e37avaka\u1e43, a\u1e6d\u1e6dhikanti dasasu avi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47ak\u0101subhesu bhast\u0101 viya v\u0101yun\u0101 uddha\u1e43 j\u012bvitapariy\u0101d\u0101n\u0101 yath\u0101nukkama\u1e43 samuggatena s\u016bnabh\u0101vena uddhum\u0101tatt\u0101 uddhum\u0101ta\u1e43, uddhum\u0101tameva uddhum\u0101taka\u1e43. Pa\u1e6dikk\u016blatt\u0101 v\u0101 kucchita\u1e43 uddhum\u0101tanti uddhum\u0101taka\u1e43. Tath\u0101r\u016bpassa chavasar\u012brasseta\u1e43 adhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now, as for the section on the ten inanimate foul objects enumerated after the kasi\u1e47as\u2014the bloated (uddhum\u0101taka), the livid (vin\u012blaka), the festering (vipubbaka), the cut-up (vicchiddaka), the gnawed (vikkh\u0101yitaka), the scattered (vikkhittaka), the hacked and scattered (hatavikkhittaka), the bloody (lohitaka), the worm-infested (pu\u1e37avaka), and the skeletal (a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika)\u2014it is called 'bloated' (uddhum\u0101ta) because, like a leather bag inflated with air, it is bloated due to the swollen state that arises in due course after the cessation of life. 'Uddhum\u0101ta' itself is 'uddhum\u0101taka'. Or, because it is repulsive, it is a contemptible bloated thing (kucchita\u1e43 uddhum\u0101ta\u1e43); therefore, it is 'uddhum\u0101taka'. This is a designation for a corpse of such a nature.",pt:"Imediatamente ap\xf3s os kasinas, entre as dez impurezas sem consci\xeancia (avi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47ak\u0101subha) que foram enumeradas, a saber: o inchado (uddhum\u0101taka), o l\xedvido (vin\u012blaka), o purulento (vipubbaka), o cortado ao meio (vicchiddaka), o ro\xeddo (vikkh\u0101yitaka), o disperso (vikkhittaka), o retalhado e disperso (hatavikkhittaka), o sangrento (lohitaka), o infestado de vermes (pu\u1e37avaka) e o esqueleto (a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika); o cad\xe1ver que, ap\xf3s o fim da vida, gradualmente se infla e incha devido ao ac\xfamulo de gases, como um fole de couro cheio de ar, \xe9 chamado de 'inchado' (uddhum\u0101ta), e o pr\xf3prio inchado \xe9 chamado de 'uddhum\u0101taka'. Ou, por ser repulsivo, \xe9 um 'inchado desprez\xedvel', da\xed 'uddhum\u0101taka'. Este \xe9 o termo para um cad\xe1ver com tal apar\xeancia.",es:"Respecto a los diez tipos de impureza inanimada mencionados inmediatamente despu\xe9s de los kasi\u1e47as, a saber: el hinchado, el l\xedvido, el purulento, el seccionado, el devorado, el disperso, el mutilado y disperso, el sangriento, el infestado de gusanos y el esquel\xe9tico; se llama 'hinchado' porque, tras el cese de la vida, se infla gradualmente por el estado de hinchaz\xf3n ascendente como un saco de cuero lleno de aire. 'Hinchado' es lo mismo que 'hinchado-ka'. O bien, se llama 'hinchado-ka' porque es un cad\xe1ver hinchado despreciable debido a su car\xe1cter repulsivo. Este es el nombre para un cuerpo muerto de tal naturaleza."}},{id:"vism-6.2",pali:"Vin\u012bla\u1e43 vuccati viparibhinnan\u012blava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43, vin\u012blameva vin\u012blaka\u1e43. Pa\u1e6dikk\u016blatt\u0101 v\u0101 kucchita\u1e43 vin\u012blanti vin\u012blaka\u1e43. Ma\u1e43sussada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu rattava\u1e47\u1e47assa pubbasannicaya\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu setava\u1e47\u1e47assa yebhuyyena ca n\u012blava\u1e47\u1e47assa n\u012bla\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne n\u012blas\u0101\u1e6dakap\u0101rutasseva chavasar\u012brassetamadhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"A corpse that is of a discolored dark blue color is called 'livid' (vin\u012bla). 'Vin\u012bla' itself is 'vin\u012blaka'. Or, because it is repulsive, it is a contemptible livid thing; therefore, it is 'vin\u012blaka'. This is a designation for a corpse that is of a red color in places with much flesh, of a white color in places where pus has collected, and is predominantly of a dark blue color, appearing as if wrapped in a blue cloth in the dark blue areas.",pt:"O cad\xe1ver que apresenta uma colora\xe7\xe3o azulada ou escura devido \xe0 altera\xe7\xe3o de sua cor natural \xe9 chamado de 'l\xedvido' (vin\u012bla), e o pr\xf3prio l\xedvido \xe9 chamado de 'vin\u012blaka'. Ou, por ser repulsivo, \xe9 um 'l\xedvido desprez\xedvel', da\xed 'vin\u012blaka'. Este \xe9 o termo para um cad\xe1ver que apresenta uma cor avermelhada nas partes com mais carne, esbranqui\xe7ada onde o pus se acumula e, em sua maior parte, uma colora\xe7\xe3o azul-escura, como se estivesse envolto em um manto azul-escuro.",es:"Se llama 'l\xedvido' a aquello que tiene un color negruzco y azulado alterado; 'l\xedvido' es lo mismo que 'l\xedvido-ka'. O bien, se llama 'l\xedvido-ka' porque es un cad\xe1ver l\xedvido despreciable por su car\xe1cter repulsivo. Este es el nombre para un cuerpo muerto que tiene color rojo en las partes carnosas, color blanco en las partes donde se acumula el pus, y generalmente es de color negruzco y azulado, como si estuviera envuelto en una tela azul en las partes oscuras."}},{id:"vism-6.3",pali:"Paribhinna\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu vissandam\u0101na\u1e43 pubba\u1e43 vipubba\u1e43, vipubbameva vipubbaka\u1e43. Pa\u1e6dikk\u016blatt\u0101 v\u0101 kucchita\u1e43 vipubbanti vipubbaka\u1e43. Tath\u0101r\u016bpassa chavasar\u012brassetamadhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"A corpse with pus oozing in places torn apart is called 'festering' (vipubba). 'Vipubba' itself is 'vipubbaka'. Or, because it is repulsive, it is a contemptible festering thing; therefore, it is 'vipubbaka'. This is a designation for a corpse of such a nature.",pt:"O cad\xe1ver que verte pus pelas partes rompidas \xe9 chamado de 'purulento' (vipubba), e o pr\xf3prio purulento \xe9 chamado de 'vipubbaka'. Ou, por ser repulsivo, \xe9 um 'purulento desprez\xedvel', da\xed 'vipubbaka'. Este \xe9 o termo para um cad\xe1ver com tal apar\xeancia.",es:"Lo que supura pus en las partes desgarradas se llama 'purulento'; 'purulento' es lo mismo que 'purulento-ka'. O bien, se llama 'purulento-ka' porque es un cad\xe1ver purulento despreciable por su car\xe1cter repulsivo. Este es el nombre para un cuerpo muerto de tal naturaleza."}},{id:"vism-6.4",pali:"Vicchidda\u1e43 vuccati dvidh\u0101 chindanena apadh\u0101rita\u1e43, vicchiddameva vicchiddaka\u1e43. Pa\u1e6dikk\u016blatt\u0101 v\u0101 kucchita\u1e43 vicchiddanti vicchiddaka\u1e43. Vemajjhe chinnassa chavasar\u012brassetamadhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"A corpse that has been split by being cut in two is called 'cut-up' (vicchidda). 'Vicchidda' itself is 'vicchiddaka'. Or, because it is repulsive, it is a contemptible cut-up thing; therefore, it is 'vicchiddaka'. This is a designation for a corpse cut in the middle.",pt:"O cad\xe1ver que foi cortado em dois peda\xe7os e aberto \xe9 chamado de 'cortado ao meio' (vicchidda), e o pr\xf3prio cortado ao meio \xe9 chamado de 'vicchiddaka'. Ou, por ser repulsivo, \xe9 um 'cortado ao meio desprez\xedvel', da\xed 'vicchiddaka'. Este \xe9 o termo para um cad\xe1ver cortado ao meio.",es:"Se llama 'seccionado' a lo que ha sido abierto y separado al ser cortado en dos partes; 'seccionado' es lo mismo que 'seccionado-ka'. O bien, se llama 'seccionado-ka' porque es un cad\xe1ver seccionado despreciable por su car\xe1cter repulsivo. Este es el nombre para un cuerpo muerto cortado por la mitad."}},{id:"vism-6.5",pali:"Ito ca etto ca vividh\u0101k\u0101rena so\u1e47asi\u1e45g\u0101l\u0101d\u012bhi kh\u0101ditanti vikkh\u0101yita\u1e43, vikkh\u0101yitameva vikkh\u0101yitaka\u1e43. Pa\u1e6dikk\u016blatt\u0101 v\u0101 kucchita\u1e43 vikkh\u0101yitanti vikkh\u0101yitaka\u1e43. Tath\u0101r\u016bpassa chavasar\u012brassetamadhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"It is called 'gnawed' (vikkh\u0101yita) because it is a corpse eaten from here and there in various ways by dogs, jackals, and so on. 'Vikkh\u0101yita' itself is 'vikkh\u0101yitaka'. Or, because it is repulsive, it is a contemptible gnawed thing; therefore, it is 'vikkh\u0101yitaka'. This is a designation for a corpse of such a nature.",pt:"O cad\xe1ver que foi mordido e comido aqui e ali, de v\xe1rias maneiras, por c\xe3es, chacais e outros animais, \xe9 chamado de 'ro\xeddo' (vikkh\u0101yita), e o pr\xf3prio ro\xeddo \xe9 chamado de 'vikkh\u0101yitaka'. Ou, por ser repulsivo, \xe9 um 'ro\xeddo desprez\xedvel', da\xed 'vikkh\u0101yitaka'. Este \xe9 o termo para um cad\xe1ver com tal apar\xeancia.",es:"Lo que ha sido mordido de diversas formas por perros, chacales, etc., aqu\xed y all\xe1, se llama 'devorado'; 'devorado' es lo mismo que 'devorado-ka'. O bien, se llama 'devorado-ka' porque es un cad\xe1ver devorado despreciable por su car\xe1cter repulsivo. Este es el nombre para un cuerpo muerto de tal naturaleza."}},{id:"vism-6.6",pali:"Vividha\u1e43 khitta\u1e43 vikkhitta\u1e43, vikkhittameva vikkhittaka\u1e43. Pa\u1e6dikk\u016blatt\u0101 v\u0101 kucchita\u1e43 vikkhittanti vikkhittaka\u1e43. A\xf1\xf1ena hattha\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ena p\u0101da\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ena s\u012bsanti eva\u1e43 tato tato khittassa chavasar\u012brassetamadhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Scattered in various ways, it is 'scattered' (vikkhitta). 'Vikkhitta' itself is 'vikkhittaka'. Or, because it is repulsive, it is a contemptible scattered thing; therefore, it is 'vikkhittaka'. This is a designation for a corpse scattered about, with a hand in one place, a foot in another, and the head in yet another.",pt:"O cad\xe1ver cujas partes foram jogadas em dire\xe7\xf5es diversas \xe9 chamado de 'disperso' (vikkhitta), e o pr\xf3prio disperso \xe9 chamado de 'vikkhittaka'. Ou, por ser repulsivo, \xe9 um 'disperso desprez\xedvel', da\xed 'vikkhittaka'. Este \xe9 o termo para um cad\xe1ver cujas partes foram desmembradas e jogadas aqui e ali, como a m\xe3o em um lugar, o p\xe9 em outro e a cabe\xe7a em outro.",es:"Lo que ha sido arrojado de diversas maneras se llama 'disperso'; 'disperso' es lo mismo que 'disperso-ka'. O bien, se llama 'disperso-ka' porque es un cad\xe1ver disperso despreciable por su car\xe1cter repulsivo. Este es el nombre para un cuerpo muerto que ha sido arrojado aqu\xed y all\xe1, con una mano en un lugar, un pie en otro y la cabeza en otro."}},{id:"vism-6.7",pali:"Hata\xf1ca ta\u1e43 purimanayeneva vikkhittaka\xf1c\u0101ti hatavikkhittaka\u1e43. K\u0101kapad\u0101k\u0101rena a\u1e45gapacca\u1e45gesu satthena hanitv\u0101 vuttanayena vikkhittassa chavasar\u012brassetamadhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"It is both hacked and scattered in the aforementioned manner; therefore, it is called 'hacked and scattered' (hatavikkhittaka). This is a designation for a corpse whose major and minor limbs have been hacked with a weapon in the shape of a crow's foot and scattered in the manner previously stated.",pt:"O cad\xe1ver que foi golpeado e cujas partes foram dispersas conforme o m\xe9todo anterior \xe9 chamado de 'retalhado e disperso' (hatavikkhittaka). Este \xe9 o termo para um cad\xe1ver que foi golpeado nos membros com uma arma, deixando marcas em forma de p\xe9 de corvo, e depois disperso da maneira j\xe1 descrita.",es:"Aquel que ha sido mutilado y adem\xe1s disperso seg\xfan el m\xe9todo anterior es el 'mutilado y disperso'. Este es el nombre para un cuerpo muerto que ha sido herido en sus miembros y partes con un arma al estilo de una pata de cuervo, y luego dispersado seg\xfan el m\xe9todo mencionado."}},{id:"vism-6.8",pali:"Lohita\u1e43 kirati vikkhipati ito cito ca paggharat\u012bti lohitaka\u1e43. Paggharitalohitamakkhitassa chavasar\u012brassetamadhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"It is 'lohitaka' because it sheds and scatters blood, and it oozes from here and there. This is a designation for a corpse smeared with blood that has oozed from it.",pt:"O cad\xe1ver que espalha, jorra e verte sangue aqui e ali \xe9 chamado de 'sangrento' (lohitaka). Este \xe9 o termo para um cad\xe1ver coberto pelo sangue que dele escorre.",es:"Se llama 'sangriento' porque esparce, arroja y derrama sangre por todas partes. Este es el nombre para un cuerpo muerto que est\xe1 untado y manchado por la sangre que de \xe9l fluye."}},{id:"vism-6.9",pali:"Pu\u1e37av\u0101 vuccanti kimayo, pu\u1e37ave kirat\u012bti pu\u1e37avaka\u1e43. Kimiparipu\u1e47\u1e47assa chavasar\u012brassetamadhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Worms are called 'pu\u1e37av\u0101'; it is 'pu\u1e37avaka' because it discharges worms. This is a designation for a corpse full of worms.",pt:"Os vermes s\xe3o chamados de 'pu\u1e37av\u0101'; o cad\xe1ver que espalha vermes \xe9 chamado de 'pu\u1e37avaka'. Este \xe9 o termo para um cad\xe1ver repleto de vermes.",es:"A los gusanos se les llama 'pu\u1e37ava'; aquel que esparce gusanos es 'infestado de gusanos'. Este es el nombre para un cuerpo muerto que est\xe1 lleno de gusanos."}},{id:"vism-6.10",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dhiyeva a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika\u1e43. Pa\u1e6dikk\u016blatt\u0101 v\u0101 kucchita\u1e43 a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u012bti a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika\u1e43. A\u1e6d\u1e6dhisa\u1e45khalik\u0101yapi eka\u1e6d\u1e6dhikassapetamadhivacana\u1e43. Im\u0101ni ca pana uddhum\u0101tak\u0101d\u012bni niss\u0101ya uppannanimitt\u0101nampi nimittesu pa\u1e6diladdhajjh\u0101n\u0101nampet\u0101neva n\u0101m\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"The bone itself is 'a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika'. Or, because of its repulsiveness, it is a loathsome bone; therefore, it is called 'a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika'. This is a designation for both a chain of bones (a skeleton) and for a single bone. Furthermore, these very names, 'bloated corpse' and so on, are also the names for the learning signs that have arisen depending on these foul objects, and for the jh\u0101nas that have been attained in the counterpart signs.",pt:"O pr\xf3prio osso \xe9 chamado de 'a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika'. Ou, por ser repulsivo, \xe9 um 'osso desprez\xedvel', da\xed 'a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika'. Este \xe9 o termo tanto para um esqueleto completo quanto para um \xfanico osso. Al\xe9m disso, estes mesmos nomes, como 'inchado' e outros, aplicam-se tamb\xe9m aos sinais (uggaha e pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ga) que surgem com base nessas impurezas, bem como aos jhanas obtidos atrav\xe9s desses sinais.",es:"El hueso mismo es 'esquel\xe9tico'. O bien, se llama 'esquel\xe9tico' porque es un hueso despreciable debido a su car\xe1cter repulsivo. Este es el nombre tanto para una cadena de huesos como para un solo hueso. Adem\xe1s, estos nombres como 'hinchado' y los dem\xe1s se aplican tanto a los signos [nimitta] que surgen basados en estos cuerpos, como a los jh\u0101nas obtenidos en dichos signos."}},{id:"vism-6.11",pali:"Tattha uddhum\u0101takasar\u012bre uddhum\u0101takanimitta\u1e43 upp\u0101detv\u0101 uddhum\u0101takasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 jh\u0101na\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena yogin\u0101 pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47e vuttanayeneva vuttappak\u0101ra\u1e43 \u0101cariya\u1e43 upasa\u1e45kamitv\u0101 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 uggahetabba\u1e43. Tenassa kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 kathentena asubhanimittatth\u0101ya gamanavidh\u0101na\u1e43, samant\u0101 nimittupalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, ek\u0101dasavidhena nimittagg\u0101ho, gat\u0101gatamaggapaccavekkha\u1e47anti eva\u1e43 appan\u0101vidh\u0101napariyos\u0101na\u1e43 sabba\u1e43 kathetabba\u1e43. Ten\u0101pi sabba\u1e43 s\u0101dhuka\u1e43 uggahetv\u0101 pubbe vuttappak\u0101ra\u1e43 sen\u0101sana\u1e43 upagantv\u0101 uddhum\u0101takanimitta\u1e43 pariyesantena vih\u0101tabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Herein, a yog\u012b who wishes to develop the jh\u0101na known as 'bloated' by producing the sign of the bloated corpse on a bloated body should, in the very manner described in the case of the earth kasi\u1e47a, approach a teacher of the kind described and properly learn the meditation subject. That teacher, when explaining this meditation subject to the yog\u012b, should explain the entire procedure, ending with the procedure for absorption: namely, the procedure for going for the purpose of taking the foul sign, the marking of the learning sign all around, the grasping of the sign in eleven ways, and the reviewing of the path gone and returned. That yog\u012b, too, having properly learned everything, should go to a dwelling of the kind previously described and should dwell while searching for the sign of a bloated corpse.",pt:"Dentre estes, o iogue que deseja desenvolver o jh\u0101na chamado de 'o inchado', gerando o sinal do cad\xe1ver inchado no corpo inchado, deve se aproximar de um mestre com as qualidades descritas anteriormente e aprender o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o exatamente de acordo com o m\xe9todo explicado no kasina de terra. Ao explicar o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o a esse iogue, o mestre deve expor todo o procedimento que culmina na absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101), a saber: o m\xe9todo de ir para obter o sinal de impureza, a marca\xe7\xe3o dos sinais ao redor, a apreens\xe3o do sinal de onze maneiras e a revis\xe3o do caminho de ida e volta. O iogue, por sua vez, tendo aprendido tudo perfeitamente, deve se dirigir a uma habita\xe7\xe3o do tipo descrito anteriormente e viver buscando o sinal do cad\xe1ver inchado.",es:"En relaci\xf3n con esto, el yogui que desea desarrollar el jhana conocido como 'lo hinchado', habiendo producido el signo de lo hinchado en un cad\xe1ver hinchado, debe acercarse a un maestro con las cualidades descritas anteriormente, siguiendo el mismo m\xe9todo explicado en el kasina de tierra, para aprender el tema de meditaci\xf3n. Al ense\xf1arle el tema de meditaci\xf3n, dicho maestro debe explicarle todo el procedimiento hasta la conclusi\xf3n con la absorci\xf3n (appan\u0101), a saber: el modo de ir para captar el signo de la impureza, la observaci\xf3n de las marcas en los alrededores, la captaci\xf3n del signo de once maneras y la reflexi\xf3n sobre el camino de ida y vuelta. El yogui, por su parte, habiendo aprendido todo correctamente, debe retirarse a una morada con las caracter\xedsticas mencionadas anteriormente y permanecer all\xed buscando el signo de lo hinchado."}},{id:"vism-6.12",pali:"Eva\u1e43 viharantena ca asukasmi\u1e43 n\u0101ma g\u0101madv\u0101re v\u0101 a\u1e6davimukhe v\u0101 panthe v\u0101 pabbatap\u0101de v\u0101 rukkham\u016ble v\u0101 sus\u0101ne v\u0101 uddhum\u0101takasar\u012bra\u1e43 nikkhittanti kathent\u0101na\u1e43 vacana\u1e43 sutv\u0101pi na t\u0101vadeva atitthena pakkhandantena viya gantabba\u1e43. Kasm\u0101? Asubha\u1e43 hi n\u0101meta\u1e43 v\u0101\u1e37amig\u0101dhi\u1e6d\u1e6dhitampi amanuss\u0101dhi\u1e6d\u1e6dhitampi hoti. Tatrassa j\u012bvitantar\u0101yopi siy\u0101. Gamanamaggo v\u0101 panettha g\u0101madv\u0101rena v\u0101 nah\u0101natitthena v\u0101 ked\u0101rako\u1e6diy\u0101 v\u0101 hoti. Tattha visabh\u0101gar\u016bpa\u1e43 \u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gacchati, tadeva v\u0101 sar\u012bra\u1e43 visabh\u0101ga\u1e43 hoti. Purisassa hi itthisar\u012bra\u1e43 itthiy\u0101 ca purisasar\u012bra\u1e43 visabh\u0101ga\u1e43, tadeta\u1e43 adhun\u0101mata\u1e43 subhatopi upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti, tenassa brahmacariyantar\u0101yopi siy\u0101. Sace pana \"nayida\u1e43 m\u0101disassa bh\u0101riya\"nti att\u0101na\u1e43 takkayati, eva\u1e43 takkayam\u0101nena gantabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"And for one dwelling thus, even having heard the words of those who say, 'A bloated corpse has been discarded at such-and-such a village gate, or at the entrance of a forest, or on a path, or at the foot of a mountain, or at the root of a tree, or in a charnel ground,' one should not go at that very moment, like one descending hastily by an improper landing-place. Why? For this foul object may be guarded by wild beasts or guarded by non-human beings. There, a danger to one's life might also arise. Or else, the path to it may be through a village gate, or by a bathing ford, or by the edge of a paddy field. There, an incompatible form comes into the range of vision, or that very corpse itself is incompatible. Indeed, for a man, a woman's body is incompatible, and for a woman, a man's body is incompatible. That incompatible body, being recently dead, can also appear as beautiful. Thereby, a danger to one's holy life might also arise. But if one considers oneself, thinking, 'This is not a heavy matter for one like me,' then one who considers thus should go.",pt:"E enquanto vive assim, mesmo ouvindo as palavras de pessoas que dizem: 'Um corpo inchado foi deixado em tal entrada de vila, ou na entrada da floresta, ou no caminho, ou no sop\xe9 da montanha, ou na base de uma \xe1rvore, ou no cemit\xe9rio', ele n\xe3o deve ir imediatamente de forma precipitada, como quem se lan\xe7a em \xe1guas profundas onde n\xe3o h\xe1 porto. Por qu\xea? Pois esse cad\xe1ver impuro pode estar sob a guarda de feras ou de seres n\xe3o humanos. L\xe1, poderia haver perigo para a sua vida. Al\xe9m disso, o caminho para chegar l\xe1 pode passar pela entrada de uma vila, por um local de banho ou pela borda de campos de cultivo. Nesses locais, uma forma do sexo oposto pode entrar no seu campo de vis\xe3o, ou o pr\xf3prio cad\xe1ver pode ser do sexo oposto. Pois, para um homem, o corpo de uma mulher \xe9 do sexo oposto, e para uma mulher, o corpo de um homem; se o cad\xe1ver for de algu\xe9m rec\xe9m-falecido, pode at\xe9 parecer atraente, e com isso haveria perigo para a sua vida santa. Se, contudo, ele refletir sobre si mesmo: 'Isso n\xe3o \xe9 um fardo pesado para algu\xe9m como eu', pensando dessa forma, ele pode ir.",es:"Para el yogui que vive de esta manera, aun si escucha decir a otros: 'En tal puerta de aldea, o en tal entrada del bosque, o en tal camino, o al pie de tal monta\xf1a, o bajo tal \xe1rbol, o en tal cementerio ha sido arrojado un cad\xe1ver hinchado', no debe dirigirse all\xed de inmediato, como quien se lanza apresuradamente a un r\xedo por un lugar que no es un muelle. \xbfPor qu\xe9? Porque tal objeto impuro (asubha) puede estar ocupado por animales salvajes o por seres no humanos (esp\xedritus); all\xed podr\xeda haber peligro para la vida de dicho yogui. Adem\xe1s, el camino hacia donde est\xe1 el cad\xe1ver puede pasar por una puerta de aldea, un lugar de ba\xf1o o el borde de un campo de cultivo; en tales lugares, una forma de g\xe9nero opuesto (visabh\u0101gar\u016bpa) podr\xeda entrar en su campo visual, o el cad\xe1ver mismo podr\xeda ser de g\xe9nero opuesto. Para un hombre, el cuerpo de una mujer es un objeto discordante (visabh\u0101ga), y para una mujer lo es el cuerpo de un hombre; si este objeto discordante ha muerto recientemente y a\xfan no ha alcanzado el estado de hinchaz\xf3n, puede parecer incluso hermoso (subha). Debido a esa percepci\xf3n de belleza, podr\xeda haber peligro para la vida de celibato (brahmacariya) del yogui. Sin embargo, si reflexiona sobre s\xed mismo diciendo: 'Esto no es una carga dif\xedcil para alguien como yo', entonces, reflexionando de tal modo sobre su capacidad de autocontrol, debe ir."}},{id:"vism-6.13",pali:"Gacchantena ca sa\u1e45ghattherassa v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atarassa v\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101tassa bhikkhuno kathetv\u0101 gantabba\u1e43. Kasm\u0101? Sace hissa sus\u0101ne amanussas\u012bhabyaggh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 r\u016bpasadd\u0101diani\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101bhibh\u016btassa a\u1e45gapacca\u1e45g\u0101ni v\u0101 pavedhenti, bhutta\u1e43 v\u0101 na parisa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101ti, a\xf1\xf1o v\u0101 \u0101b\u0101dho hoti. Athassa so vih\u0101re pattac\u012bvara\u1e43 surakkhita\u1e43 karissati. Dahare v\u0101 s\u0101ma\u1e47ere v\u0101 pahi\u1e47itv\u0101 ta\u1e43 bhikkhu\u1e43 pa\u1e6dijaggissati. Apica sus\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101ma nir\u0101sa\u1e45ka\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanti ma\xf1\xf1am\u0101n\u0101 katakamm\u0101pi akatakamm\u0101pi cor\u0101 samosaranti. Te manussehi anubaddh\u0101 bhikkhussa sam\u012bpe bha\u1e47\u1e0daka\u1e43 cha\u1e0d\u1e0detv\u0101pi pal\u0101yanti. Manuss\u0101 \"saho\u1e0d\u1e0dha\u1e43 cora\u1e43 addas\u0101m\u0101\"ti bhikkhu\u1e43 gahetv\u0101 vihe\u1e6dhenti. Athassa so \"m\u0101 ima\u1e43 vihe\u1e6dhayittha, mam\u0101ya\u1e43 kathetv\u0101 imin\u0101 n\u0101ma kammena gato\"ti te manusse sa\xf1\xf1\u0101petv\u0101 sotthibh\u0101va\u1e43 karissati. Aya\u1e43 \u0101nisa\u1e43so kathetv\u0101 gamane. Tasm\u0101 vuttappak\u0101rassa bhikkhuno kathetv\u0101 asubhanimittadassane sa\xf1j\u0101t\u0101bhil\u0101sena yath\u0101n\u0101ma khattiyo abhiseka\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, yajam\u0101no ya\xf1\xf1as\u0101la\u1e43, adhano v\u0101 pana nidhi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 p\u012btisomanassaj\u0101to gacchati, eva\u1e43 p\u012btisomanassa\u1e43 upp\u0101detv\u0101 a\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101su vuttena vidhin\u0101 gantabba\u1e43. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"When going, one should inform the Sangha elder or any other well-known bhikkhu before going. Why? Because if, while in the charnel ground, one is overwhelmed by unpleasant objects such as the sights and sounds of non-human beings, lions, tigers, and so on, causing one's limbs to tremble, or if the food one has eaten does not settle, or if some other illness arises, then that bhikkhu will ensure the bowl and robe are well-protected in the monastery. Or he may send young bhikkhus or novices to attend to that bhikkhu. Moreover, thieves\u2014both those who have committed theft and those who wish to do so\u2014may gather there, considering the charnel ground to be a place free from suspicion. Pursued by people, they might drop stolen goods near the bhikkhu and flee. People, thinking, 'We saw the thief together with the stolen goods,' may seize and harass the bhikkhu. Then, that bhikkhu who was informed can explain, 'Do not harass him; he informed me before he went to perform such-and-such an action,' and thus make the people understand, ensuring his safety. This is the benefit of informing someone before going. Therefore, having informed a bhikkhu of the kind described, one should go with the desire to see the sign of foulness, filled with joy and happiness\u2014just as a khattiya goes to the place of consecration, a sacrificer to the sacrificial hall, or a poor person to a place of hidden treasure\u2014generating such joy and happiness, following the method explained in the commentaries. For it is said:",pt:"Ao ir, ele deve partir ap\xf3s informar o anci\xe3o da comunidade ou outro monge conhecido. Por qu\xea? Pois se, no cemit\xe9rio, ele for dominado por vis\xf5es e sons desagrad\xe1veis de seres n\xe3o humanos, le\xf5es, tigres, etc., e seus membros tremerem, ou a comida ingerida n\xe3o parar no est\xf4mago, ou se surgir alguma outra enfermidade, aquele monge no mosteiro proteger\xe1 bem a sua tigela e os seus mantos. Ou enviar\xe1 monges jovens ou novi\xe7os para cuidar dele. Al\xe9m disso, ladr\xf5es que j\xe1 cometeram crimes ou que planejam comet\xea-los costumam se reunir no cemit\xe9rio, considerando-o um local livre de suspeitas. Se forem perseguidos pelas pessoas, eles podem fugir ap\xf3s lan\xe7ar os bens roubados perto do monge. As pessoas, pensando: 'Encontramos o ladr\xe3o com o produto do roubo', podem capturar e agredir o monge. Nesse momento, aquele monge informado esclarecer\xe1 as pessoas, dizendo: 'N\xe3o agridam este monge; ele me informou e foi para l\xe1 com tal prop\xf3sito', garantindo assim a sua seguran\xe7a. Esse \xe9 o benef\xedcio de ir ap\xf3s informar. Portanto, tendo informado um monge do tipo descrito, e com um forte desejo de ver o sinal do cad\xe1ver impuro \u2014 assim como um nobre se dirige ao local de sua consagra\xe7\xe3o, ou um sacrificador ao pavilh\xe3o de sacrif\xedcios, ou um homem pobre ao local de um tesouro escondido, cheios de alegria e contentamento \u2014, ele deve ir gerando alegria e contentamento, seguindo o m\xe9todo descrito nos Coment\xe1rios. Pois foi dito o seguinte:",es:"Al ir, el yogui debe informar al Sa\u1e45ghatthera (monje anciano de la comunidad) o a otro monje reconocido antes de partir. \xbfPor qu\xe9? Porque si en el cementerio sus extremidades tiemblan al ser abrumado por objetos desagradables como seres no humanos, leones o tigres, o si la comida ingerida no se asienta bien y vomita, o si surge cualquier otra enfermedad, aquel monje informado cuidar\xe1 bien de su cuenco y mantos en el monasterio, o enviar\xe1 a monjes j\xf3venes o novicios para asistir a ese monje enfermo. Adem\xe1s, los ladrones, pensando que el cementerio es un lugar libre de sospechas, se re\xfanen all\xed, tanto los que ya han cometido cr\xedmenes como los que planean hacerlo. Si estos ladrones son perseguidos por los due\xf1os de lo robado o por la autoridad, pueden huir arrojando el bot\xedn cerca del monje; entonces las personas, pensando: 'Hemos encontrado al ladr\xf3n junto con el bot\xedn', podr\xedan arrestar y maltratar al monje. En tal caso, aquel monje anciano aclarar\xe1 la situaci\xf3n a la gente diciendo: 'No maltraten a este monje; \xe9l me inform\xf3 y fue con tal prop\xf3sito de meditaci\xf3n', asegurando as\xed su bienestar. Este es el beneficio de informar antes de partir. Por lo tanto, informando a un monje de las caracter\xedsticas mencionadas, con un deseo ferviente de ver el signo de lo impuro (asubhanimitta), debe ir con alegr\xeda y regocijo, tal como un rey va al lugar de su consagraci\xf3n, un celebrante a la sala de sacrificio, o un hombre pobre al lugar donde hay un tesoro oculto; generando tal alegr\xeda, debe ir siguiendo el m\xe9todo descrito en los Comentarios. Pues as\xed se ha dicho:"}},{id:"vism-6.14",pali:"\"Uddhum\u0101taka\u1e43 asubhanimitta\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hanto eko adutiyo gacchati upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101ya satiy\u0101 asammu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya antogatehi indriyehi abahigatena m\u0101nasena gat\u0101gatamagga\u1e43 paccavekkham\u0101no. Yasmi\u1e43 padese uddhum\u0101taka\u1e43 asubhanimitta\u1e43 nikkhitta\u1e43 hoti, tasmi\u1e43 padese p\u0101s\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 vammika\u1e43 v\u0101 rukkha\u1e43 v\u0101 gaccha\u1e43 v\u0101 lata\u1e43 v\u0101 sanimitta\u1e43 karoti, s\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 karoti. Sanimitta\u1e43 katv\u0101 s\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 uddhum\u0101taka\u1e43 asubhanimitta\u1e43 sabh\u0101vabh\u0101vato upalakkheti, va\u1e47\u1e47atopi li\u1e45gatopi sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101natopi disatopi ok\u0101satopi paricchedatopi sandhito vivarato ninnato thalato samantato. So ta\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 suggahita\u1e43 karoti, s\u016bpadh\u0101rita\u1e43 upadh\u0101reti, suvavatthita\u1e43 vavatthapeti. So ta\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 suggahita\u1e43 katv\u0101 s\u016bpadh\u0101rita\u1e43 upadh\u0101retv\u0101 suvavatthita\u1e43 vavatthapetv\u0101 eko adutiyo gacchati upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101ya satiy\u0101 asammu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya antogatehi indriyehi abahigatena m\u0101nasena gat\u0101gatamagga\u1e43 paccavekkham\u0101no. So ca\u1e45kamantopi tabbh\u0101giya\xf1\xf1eva ca\u1e45kama\u1e43 adhi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Nis\u012bdantopi tabbh\u0101giya\xf1\xf1eva \u0101sana\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1apeti.",translations:{en:"One who is grasping the foul sign of a bloated corpse goes alone, without a companion, with established and unconfused mindfulness, with inwardly directed faculties, with a mind not gone abroad, reflecting on the path gone and returned. In whatever place the foul sign of a bloated corpse is laid down, in that place he makes a mark of a stone, or an anthill, or a tree, or a bush, or a creeper; he makes it an object. Having made a mark, having made it an object, he discerns the foul sign of a bloated corpse by its own nature: by color, by characteristic, by shape, by direction, by location, by delimitation, by joint, by opening, by depression, by elevation, and from all around. He makes that sign well-grasped, bears it well in mind, and establishes it well. Having made that sign well-grasped, having borne it well in mind, and having established it well, he goes alone, without a companion, with established and unconfused mindfulness, with inwardly directed faculties, with a mind not gone abroad, reflecting on the path gone and returned. When walking, he resolves upon only a walking path related to that. When sitting, he prepares only a seat related to that.",pt:"\u2018Aquele que aprende o sinal do cad\xe1ver inchado vai sozinho, sem companheiro, com a aten\xe7\xe3o plena estabelecida e sem esquecimento, com as faculdades voltadas para dentro e a mente n\xe3o dispersa para o exterior, revisando o caminho de ida e volta. No local onde o sinal do cad\xe1ver inchado foi deixado, ele associa o sinal e o objeto a uma rocha, a um formigueiro, a uma \xe1rvore, a um arbusto ou a uma trepadeira que esteja naquele local. Tendo associado o sinal e o objeto, ele marca o sinal do cad\xe1ver inchado de acordo com a sua natureza intr\xednseca: pela cor, pelas caracter\xedsticas distintivas, pela configura\xe7\xe3o, pela dire\xe7\xe3o, pela localiza\xe7\xe3o, pela delimita\xe7\xe3o, pelas articula\xe7\xf5es, pelas aberturas, pelas depress\xf5es, pelas eleva\xe7\xf5es e por todo o seu redor. Ele apreende bem esse sinal, grava-o bem na mente e define-o bem. Tendo apreendido bem esse sinal, gravado-o bem na mente e definido-o bem, ele retorna sozinho, sem companheiro, com a aten\xe7\xe3o plena estabelecida e sem esquecimento, com as faculdades voltadas para dentro e a mente n\xe3o dispersa para o exterior, revisando o caminho de ida e volta. Ao caminhar em medita\xe7\xe3o, ele determina apenas uma caminhada que seja favor\xe1vel a isso. Ao sentar-se, ele prepara apenas um assento que seja favor\xe1vel a isso.\u2019",es:"\u201cAquel que aprehende el signo de lo impuro de un cad\xe1ver hinchado, va solo y sin compa\xf1\xeda, con la atenci\xf3n establecida y sin confusi\xf3n, con los sentidos dirigidos hacia adentro y la mente no distra\xedda hacia el exterior, observando atentamente el camino de ida y vuelta. En el lugar donde se encuentra el cad\xe1ver hinchado, toma como referencia una piedra, un hormiguero, un \xe1rbol, un arbusto o una enredadera, vincul\xe1ndolos con el signo y convirti\xe9ndolos en soporte del objeto. Tras haberlos vinculado y convertido en soporte, distingue el signo de lo impuro del cad\xe1ver hinchado seg\xfan su naturaleza esencial: por color, por sexo, por forma, por direcci\xf3n, por ubicaci\xf3n, por delimitaci\xf3n, por sus coyunturas, sus aberturas, sus partes bajas, sus partes altas y por todo su alrededor. \xc9l aprehende bien ese signo, lo reflexiona correctamente y lo define con precisi\xf3n. Tras haberlo aprehendido, reflexionado y definido bien, regresa solo y sin compa\xf1\xeda, con la atenci\xf3n establecida y sin confusi\xf3n, con los sentidos hacia adentro y la mente no distra\xedda, observando el camino de ida y vuelta. Al caminar en meditaci\xf3n, se determina a realizar solo una caminata acorde a ese objeto; al sentarse, prepara su asiento de manera acorde al mismo.\u201d"}},{id:"vism-6.15",pali:"Eva\u1e43 gatena pana na t\u0101va asubhanimitta\u1e43 oloketabba\u1e43. Dis\u0101 vavatthapetabb\u0101. Ekasmi\u1e43 hi dis\u0101bh\u0101ge \u1e6dhitassa \u0101ramma\u1e47a\xf1ca na vibh\u016bta\u1e43 hutv\u0101 kh\u0101yati, citta\xf1ca na kammaniya\u1e43 hoti. Tasm\u0101 ta\u1e43 vajjetv\u0101 yattha \u1e6dhitassa \u0101ramma\u1e47a\xf1ca vibh\u016bta\u1e43 hutv\u0101 kh\u0101yati, citta\xf1ca kammaniya\u1e43 hoti, tattha \u1e6dh\u0101tabba\u1e43. Pa\u1e6div\u0101t\u0101nuv\u0101ta\xf1ca pah\u0101tabba\u1e43. Pa\u1e6div\u0101te \u1e6dhitassa hi ku\u1e47apagandhena ubb\u0101\u1e37hassa citta\u1e43 vidh\u0101vati. Anuv\u0101te \u1e6dhitassa sace tattha adhivatth\u0101 amanuss\u0101 honti, te kujjhitv\u0101 anattha\u1e43 karonti. Tasm\u0101 \u012bsaka\u1e43 ukkamma n\u0101tianuv\u0101te \u1e6dh\u0101tabba\u1e43. Eva\u1e43 ti\u1e6d\u1e6dham\u0101nen\u0101pi n\u0101tid\u016bre n\u0101cc\u0101sanne n\u0101nup\u0101da\u1e43 n\u0101nus\u012bsa\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101tabba\u1e43. Atid\u016bre \u1e6dhitassa hi \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 avibh\u016bta\u1e43 hoti. Acc\u0101sanne bhayamuppajjati. Anup\u0101da\u1e43 v\u0101 anus\u012bsa\u1e43 v\u0101 \u1e6dhitassa sabba\u1e43 asubha\u1e43 sama\u1e43 na pa\xf1\xf1\u0101yati. Tasm\u0101 n\u0101tid\u016bre n\u0101cc\u0101sanne olokentassa ph\u0101suka\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne sar\u012bravemajjhabh\u0101ge \u1e6dh\u0101tabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Having gone thus, one should not yet look at the sign of foulness. The directions should be determined. For, when standing in one direction, the object may not appear distinctly, and the mind may not be workable. Therefore, avoiding that place, one should stand where the object does appear distinctly and the mind is workable. Both upwind and downwind positions should be abandoned. For when standing upwind, the mind of one oppressed by the stench of the corpse is scattered. When standing downwind, if there are non-human beings dwelling there, they may become angry and cause harm. Therefore, having moved slightly aside, one should stand in a place that is not excessively downwind. Even when standing thus, one should stand neither too far nor too near, not at the foot-end nor at the head-end. For if one stands too far, the object is indistinct. If one stands too near, fear arises. If one stands at the foot-end or the head-end, the entire foul object is not perceived equally. Therefore, one should stand neither too far nor too near, at a comfortable place for viewing, in line with the middle part of the body.",pt:"Tendo chegado l\xe1, ele n\xe3o deve olhar imediatamente para o sinal do cad\xe1ver impuro. As dire\xe7\xf5es devem ser definidas. Pois, para quem est\xe1 posicionado em uma determinada dire\xe7\xe3o, o objeto n\xe3o aparece claramente e a mente n\xe3o se torna male\xe1vel para a medita\xe7\xe3o. Portanto, evitando essa dire\xe7\xe3o, ele deve se posicionar onde o objeto apare\xe7a claramente e a mente se torne male\xe1vel. E as posi\xe7\xf5es diretamente contra o vento ou diretamente a favor do vento devem ser evitadas. Pois, para quem est\xe1 diretamente contra o vento, a mente se dispersa por ser perturbada pelo cheiro de cad\xe1ver. Para quem est\xe1 diretamente a favor do vento, se houver seres n\xe3o humanos habitando ali, eles podem se irar e causar danos. Portanto, afastando-se um pouco, ele deve se posicionar em um local que n\xe3o seja diretamente a favor do vento. Mesmo ao se posicionar assim, ele n\xe3o deve ficar nem muito longe, nem muito perto, nem alinhado diretamente com os p\xe9s, nem com a cabe\xe7a. Pois, para quem est\xe1 muito longe, o objeto n\xe3o fica claro. Para quem est\xe1 muito perto, surge o medo. Para quem est\xe1 alinhado diretamente com os p\xe9s ou com a cabe\xe7a, o cad\xe1ver impuro n\xe3o aparece de forma uniforme em sua totalidade. Portanto, ele deve se posicionar nem muito longe, nem muito perto, em um local confort\xe1vel para observar, alinhado com a parte central do corpo.",es:"Una vez llegado, sin embargo, todav\xeda no se debe observar el signo de lo impuro. Se deben delimitar las direcciones donde situarse. Pues, para quien se ubica en una direcci\xf3n determinada, el objeto no se manifiesta claramente y la mente no se vuelve apta para la meditaci\xf3n. Por tanto, evitando tal lugar, uno debe situarse donde el objeto se manifieste claramente y la mente sea apta para el trabajo mental. Tambi\xe9n se debe evitar estar directamente a favor o en contra del viento. Para quien est\xe1 contra el viento, la mente se dispersa perturbada por el olor del cad\xe1ver. Para quien est\xe1 a favor del viento, si hay seres no humanos habitando all\xed, podr\xedan enojarse y causar da\xf1o. Por tanto, apart\xe1ndose un poco, uno debe situarse en un lugar que no est\xe9 excesivamente a favor del viento. Al situarse de este modo, no debe estar ni muy lejos ni muy cerca, ni hacia los pies ni hacia la cabeza. Para quien est\xe1 muy lejos, el objeto resulta poco claro. Para quien est\xe1 muy cerca, surge el temor. Para quien est\xe1 hacia los pies o hacia la cabeza, la totalidad de lo impuro no se percibe de manera uniforme. Por tanto, uno debe situarse ni muy lejos ni muy cerca, en un lugar c\xf3modo para la observaci\xf3n, frente a la parte media del cuerpo."}},{id:"vism-6.16",pali:"Eva\u1e43 vavatthapetv\u0101 va\u1e47\u1e47atopi li\u1e45gatopi sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101natopi disatopi ok\u0101satopi paricchedatop\u012bti chabbidhena nimitta\u1e43 gahetabba\u1e43. Katha\u1e43? Tena hi yogin\u0101 ida\u1e43 sar\u012bra\u1e43 k\u0101\u1e37assa v\u0101 od\u0101tassa v\u0101 ma\u1e45guracchavino v\u0101ti va\u1e47\u1e47ato vavatthapetabba\u1e43. Li\u1e45gato pana itthili\u1e45ga\u1e43 v\u0101 purisali\u1e45ga\u1e43 v\u0101ti avavatthapetv\u0101 pa\u1e6dhamavaye v\u0101 majjhimavaye v\u0101 pacchimavaye v\u0101 \u1e6dhitassa ida\u1e43 sar\u012branti vavatthapetabba\u1e43. Sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101nato uddhum\u0101takassa sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101navaseneva idamassa s\u012bsasa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, ida\u1e43 g\u012bv\u0101sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, ida\u1e43 hatthasa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, ida\u1e43 udarasa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, ida\u1e43 n\u0101bhisa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, ida\u1e43 ka\u1e6disa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, ida\u1e43 \u016brusa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, ida\u1e43 ja\u1e45gh\u0101sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, ida\u1e43 p\u0101dasa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101nanti vavatthapetabba\u1e43. Disato pana imasmi\u1e43 sar\u012bre dve dis\u0101 n\u0101bhiy\u0101 adho he\u1e6d\u1e6dhimadis\u0101 uddha\u1e43 uparimadis\u0101ti vavatthapetabba\u1e43. Atha v\u0101 aha\u1e43 imiss\u0101 dis\u0101ya \u1e6dhito asubhanimitta\u1e43 imiss\u0101ti vavatthapetabba\u1e43. Ok\u0101sato pana imasmi\u1e43 n\u0101ma ok\u0101se hatth\u0101, imasmi\u1e43 p\u0101d\u0101, imasmi\u1e43 s\u012bsa\u1e43, imasmi\u1e43 majjhimak\u0101yo \u1e6dhitoti vavatthapetabba\u1e43. Atha v\u0101 aha\u1e43 imasmi\u1e43 ok\u0101se \u1e6dhito asubhanimitta\u1e43 imasminti vavatthapetabba\u1e43. Paricchedato ida\u1e43 sar\u012bra\u1e43 adho p\u0101datalena upari kesamatthakena tiriya\u1e43 tacena paricchinna\u1e43, yath\u0101paricchinne ca \u1e6dh\u0101ne dvatti\u1e43saku\u1e47apabharitamev\u0101ti vavatthapetabba\u1e43. Atha v\u0101 ayamassa hatthaparicchedo, aya\u1e43 p\u0101daparicchedo, aya\u1e43 s\u012bsaparicchedo, aya\u1e43 majjhimak\u0101yaparicchedoti vavatthapetabba\u1e43. Yattaka\u1e43 v\u0101 pana \u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 ga\u1e47hati, tattakameva ida\u1e43 \u012bdisa\u1e43 uddhum\u0101takanti paricchinditabba\u1e43. Purisassa pana itthisar\u012bra\u1e43 itthiy\u0101 v\u0101 purisasar\u012bra\u1e43 na va\u1e6d\u1e6dati. Visabh\u0101ge sar\u012bre \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 na upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti, vipphandanasseva paccayo hoti. \"Uggh\u0101\u1e6dit\u0101pi hi itth\u012b purisassa citta\u1e43 pariy\u0101d\u0101ya ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhat\u012b\"ti majjhima\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101ya\u1e43 vutta\u1e43. Tasm\u0101 sabh\u0101gasar\u012breyeva eva\u1e43 chabbidhena nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Having thus determined, the sign should be grasped in six ways: by color, by characteristic, by shape, by direction, by location, and by delimitation. How? That yogi should determine this body by color, as: 'It is the body of a dark person,' or 'of a fair person,' or 'of one with a dusky complexion.' By characteristic: without determining it as 'a female characteristic' or 'a male characteristic,' it should be determined by age: 'This is the body of one who was in the first stage of life,' or 'in the middle stage of life,' or 'in the final stage of life.' By shape, in accordance with the shape of the bloated corpse itself, one should determine: 'This is the shape of its head, this is the shape of its neck, this is the shape of its hands, this is the shape of its belly, this is the shape of its navel, this is the shape of its waist, this is the shape of its thighs, this is the shape of its calves, this is the shape of its feet.' By direction, one should determine: 'In this body, there are two directions\u2014below the navel is the lower direction, and above is the upper direction.' Alternatively, one should determine: 'I am standing in this direction, and the sign of foulness is situated in this direction.' By location, one should determine: 'In this particular location are the hands, in this the feet, in this the head, in this the middle part of the body.' Alternatively, one should determine: 'I am standing in this location, and the sign of foulness is situated in this location.' By delimitation, one should determine: 'This body is delimited below by the soles of the feet, above by the tips of the hair, and across by the skin; and in the place thus delimited, it is simply filled with thirty-two kinds of impurities.' Alternatively, one should determine: 'This is the delimitation of its hand, this is the delimitation of its foot, this is the delimitation of its head, this is the delimitation of the middle part of its body.' Or, whatever part one apprehends, just that much should be delimited thus: 'This bloated corpse is of such a nature.' However, a woman's body is not suitable for a man, nor is a man's body for a woman. In a dissimilar body, the meditation object does not become manifest; it is only a condition for the agitation of defilements. For it is said in the Majjhima\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101: 'Indeed, a woman, even when bloated, seizes and overcomes a man\u2019s mind.' Therefore, the sign should be grasped in these six ways only in a body of the same sex.",pt:"Tendo assim determinado, o sinal deve ser apreendido de seis maneiras: pela cor, pela caracter\xedstica, pela forma, pela dire\xe7\xe3o, pela localiza\xe7\xe3o e pela delimita\xe7\xe3o. Como? Por aquele iogue, este corpo deve ser determinado pela cor: 'Este \xe9 o corpo de algu\xe9m de pele escura', ou 'de pele clara', ou 'de pele bronzeada'. Pela caracter\xedstica, no entanto, sem determinar como 'caracter\xedstica feminina' ou 'caracter\xedstica masculina', deve-se determinar: 'Este \xe9 o corpo de algu\xe9m que estava na primeira fase da vida', ou 'na meia-idade', ou 'na \xfaltima fase da vida'. Pela forma, apenas por meio da forma do corpo inchado, deve-se determinar: 'Esta \xe9 a forma da sua cabe\xe7a, esta \xe9 a forma do pesco\xe7o, esta \xe9 a forma das m\xe3os, esta \xe9 a forma do abd\xf4men, esta \xe9 a forma do umbigo, esta \xe9 a forma dos quadris, esta \xe9 a forma das coxas, esta \xe9 a forma das panturrilhas, esta \xe9 a forma dos p\xe9s'. Pela dire\xe7\xe3o, no entanto, neste corpo h\xe1 duas dire\xe7\xf5es: abaixo do umbigo \xe9 a dire\xe7\xe3o inferior, acima \xe9 a dire\xe7\xe3o superior; assim deve ser determinado. Ou ent\xe3o: 'Eu estou situado nesta dire\xe7\xe3o, e o sinal de impureza est\xe1 naquela dire\xe7\xe3o'; assim deve ser determinado. Pela localiza\xe7\xe3o, no entanto, deve-se determinar: 'Neste local est\xe3o as m\xe3os, neste os p\xe9s, neste a cabe\xe7a, neste a parte central do corpo'. Ou ent\xe3o: 'Eu estou situado neste local, e o sinal de impureza est\xe1 naquele local'; assim deve ser determinado. Pela delimita\xe7\xe3o, deve-se determinar: 'Este corpo \xe9 delimitado abaixo pelas solas dos p\xe9s, acima pelo topo do cabelo e ao redor pela pele; e neste espa\xe7o assim delimitado, ele est\xe1 repleto apenas de trinta e duas partes impuras'. Ou ent\xe3o: 'Esta \xe9 a delimita\xe7\xe3o das suas m\xe3os, esta \xe9 a delimita\xe7\xe3o dos p\xe9s, esta \xe9 a delimita\xe7\xe3o da cabe\xe7a, esta \xe9 a delimita\xe7\xe3o da parte central do corpo'; assim deve ser determinado. Ou ainda, qualquer que seja a extens\xe3o da \xe1rea que se apreenda, apenas essa extens\xe3o deve ser delimitada: 'Esta parte \xe9 assim, um corpo inchado'. Para um homem, no entanto, o corpo de uma mulher n\xe3o \xe9 adequado; e para uma mulher, o corpo de um homem n\xe3o \xe9 adequado. Num corpo de g\xeanero oposto, o objeto n\xe3o se manifesta claramente; em vez disso, torna-se apenas uma causa para a agita\xe7\xe3o das impurezas. Pois foi dito no Coment\xe1rio M\xe9dio: 'Mesmo que esteja desfigurada, a mulher permanece cativando completamente a mente do homem'. Portanto, o sinal deve ser apreendido apenas em um corpo do mesmo g\xeanero, destas seis maneiras mencionadas.",es:"Habiendo definido as\xed [el objeto], el signo debe ser tomado de seis maneras: por el color, por la marca, por la forma, por la direcci\xf3n, por la ubicaci\xf3n y por la delimitaci\xf3n. \xbfC\xf3mo? Por ese yogui, este cuerpo debe ser definido por el color de la siguiente manera: 'Este es el cuerpo de una persona de piel oscura', o 'de piel clara', o 'de piel cobriza'. Respecto a la marca, sin definir si es 'marca femenina' o 'marca masculina', debe definirse como: 'Este cuerpo pertenece a alguien que estaba en la primera etapa de la vida', o 'en la etapa media', o 'en la \xfaltima etapa'. Por la forma, de acuerdo con la hinchaz\xf3n del cad\xe1ver hinchado: 'Esta es la forma de su cabeza', 'esta es la forma del cuello', 'esta es la forma de los brazos', 'esta es la forma del vientre', 'esta es la forma del ombligo', 'esta es la forma de la cadera', 'esta es la forma de los muslos', 'esta es la forma de las pantorrillas', 'esta es la forma de los pies'; as\xed debe ser definido. Por la direcci\xf3n, en este cuerpo hay dos direcciones: desde el ombligo hacia abajo es la direcci\xf3n inferior, y hacia arriba es la direcci\xf3n superior; as\xed debe ser definido. O bien: 'Yo estoy en esta direcci\xf3n, el signo de lo impuro est\xe1 en aquella direcci\xf3n'. Por la ubicaci\xf3n: 'En este lugar est\xe1n las manos', 'en este las piernas', 'en este la cabeza', 'en este el tronco'; as\xed debe ser definido. O bien: 'Yo estoy en este lugar, el signo de lo impuro est\xe1 en aquel lugar'. Por la delimitaci\xf3n: 'Este cuerpo est\xe1 limitado por abajo por las plantas de los pies, por arriba por las puntas de los cabellos, y lateralmente por la piel; y dentro de ese espacio delimitado est\xe1 lleno de los treinta y dos componentes impuros'; as\xed debe ser definido. O bien: 'Esta es la delimitaci\xf3n de las manos', 'esta es la de las piernas', 'esta es la de la cabeza', 'esta es la del tronco'; as\xed debe ser definido. O bien, debe delimitarse simplemente la parte que se percibe: 'Esta parte es as\xed de hinchada'. Sin embargo, para un hombre no es adecuado meditar sobre un cuerpo femenino, ni para una mujer sobre un cuerpo masculino. En un cuerpo de sexo opuesto, el objeto [de asco] no se manifiesta con claridad, sino que se convierte en causa de agitaci\xf3n [sensual]. Pues se dice en el Comentario Medio: 'Incluso una mujer diseccionada permanece cautivando la mente del hombre'. Por lo tanto, el signo debe ser tomado de estas seis maneras solo en un cuerpo del mismo sexo."}},{id:"vism-6.17",pali:"Tena yogin\u0101 tasmi\u1e43 sar\u012bre yath\u0101vuttanimittagg\u0101havasena su\u1e6d\u1e6dhu nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitabba\u1e43. Sati\u1e43 s\u016bpa\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43 katv\u0101 \u0101vajjitabba\u1e43. Eva\u1e43 punappuna\u1e43 karontena s\u0101dhuka\u1e43 upadh\u0101retabba\xf1ceva vavatthapetabba\xf1ca. Sar\u012brato n\u0101tid\u016bre n\u0101cc\u0101sanne padese \u1e6dhitena v\u0101 nisinnena v\u0101 cakkhu\u1e43 umm\u012bletv\u0101 oloketv\u0101 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitabba\u1e43. \"Uddhum\u0101takapa\u1e6dikk\u016bla\u1e43 uddhum\u0101takapa\u1e6dikk\u016bla\"nti satakkhattu\u1e43 sahassakkhattu\u1e43 umm\u012bletv\u0101 oloketabba\u1e43, nimm\u012bletv\u0101 \u0101vajjitabba\u1e43. Eva\u1e43 punappuna\u1e43 karontassa uggahanimitta\u1e43 suggahita\u1e43 hoti. Kad\u0101 suggahita\u1e43 hoti? Yad\u0101 umm\u012bletv\u0101 olokentassa nimm\u012bletv\u0101 \u0101vajjentassa ca ekasadisa\u1e43 hutv\u0101 \u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gacchati, tad\u0101 suggahita\u1e43 n\u0101ma hoti.",translations:{en:"By that yogi, the sign in that body should be thoroughly grasped by means of apprehending the sign in the way described. Having well-established mindfulness, he should advert to it. By doing so again and again, it should be well noted and well determined. Standing or sitting in a place not too far from nor too close to the body, having opened the eyes and looked, the sign should be grasped. As \u201cBloated and repulsive, bloated and repulsive,\u201d having opened the eyes, he should look a hundred times, a thousand times; having closed them, he should advert to it. For one doing so again and again, the learning sign becomes well-grasped. When does it become well-grasped? When, for one looking with eyes open and for one adverting with eyes closed, it appears as one and the same, then it is called well-grasped.",pt:"Por aquele iogue, o sinal naquele corpo deve ser muito bem apreendido por meio do m\xe9todo de apreens\xe3o do sinal conforme descrito. Tendo estabelecido firmemente a aten\xe7\xe3o, ele deve refletir sobre ele. Fazendo isso repetidamente, ele deve memoriz\xe1-lo bem com aten\xe7\xe3o e determin\xe1-lo com sabedoria. Estando de p\xe9 ou sentado em um local nem muito longe nem muito perto do corpo, ele deve abrir os olhos, olhar e apreender o sinal. Pensando 'corpo inchado e repulsivo, corpo inchado e repulsivo', ele deve olhar com os olhos abertos cem vezes, mil vezes, e depois fechar os olhos e refletir sobre ele. Para quem faz isso repetidamente, o sinal de apreens\xe3o torna-se bem apreendido. Quando ele se torna bem apreendido? Quando ele aparece no campo mental exatamente da mesma forma, tanto para quem olha com os olhos abertos quanto para quem reflete com os olhos fechados; ent\xe3o ele \xe9 chamado de 'bem apreendido'.",es:"Ese yogui debe tomar el signo adecuadamente en ese cuerpo mediante la forma de captar el signo mencionada anteriormente. Debe reflexionar habiendo establecido firmemente la atenci\xf3n. Al hacerlo as\xed repetidamente, debe tanto observarlo bien como definirlo. Estando de pie o sentado en un lugar ni muy lejos ni muy cerca del cuerpo, debe tomar el signo abriendo los ojos y mirando. Debe mirar abriendo los ojos y reflexionar cerr\xe1ndolos cien o mil veces, pensando: 'Lo impuro hinchado, lo impuro hinchado'. Para quien lo hace as\xed repetidamente, el signo de aprendizaje queda bien captado. \xbfCu\xe1ndo queda bien captado? Cuando el objeto aparece de la misma manera tanto para quien mira con los ojos abiertos como para quien reflexiona con los ojos cerrados, entonces se dice que ha sido bien captado."}},{id:"vism-6.18",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 karoto pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 uppajjati. Tatrida\u1e43 nimittadvayassa n\u0101n\u0101kara\u1e47a\u1e43, uggahanimitta\u1e43 vir\u016bpa\u1e43 b\u012bbhaccha\u1e43 bheravadassana\u1e43 hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 pana y\u0101vadattha\u1e43 bhu\xf1jitv\u0101 nipanno th\u016bla\u1e45gapacca\u1e45gapuriso viya. Tassa pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimittapa\u1e6dil\u0101bhasamak\u0101lameva bahiddh\u0101 k\u0101m\u0101na\u1e43 amanasik\u0101r\u0101 vikkhambhanavasena k\u0101macchando pah\u012byati. Anunayappah\u0101neneva cassa lohitappah\u0101nena pubbo viya by\u0101p\u0101dopi pah\u012byati. Tath\u0101 \u0101raddhav\u012briyat\u0101ya thinamiddha\u1e43, avippa\u1e6dis\u0101rakarasantadhamm\u0101nuyogavasena uddhaccakukkucca\u1e43, adhigatavisesassa paccakkhat\u0101ya pa\u1e6dipattidesake satthari pa\u1e6dipattiya\u1e43 pa\u1e6dipattiphale ca vicikicch\u0101 pah\u012byat\u012bti pa\xf1ca n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101ni pah\u012byanti. Tasmi\xf1\xf1eva ca nimitte cetaso abhiniropanalakkha\u1e47o vitakko, nimitt\u0101numajjanakicca\u1e43 s\u0101dhayam\u0101no vic\u0101ro, pa\u1e6diladdhavises\u0101dhigamapaccay\u0101 p\u012bti, p\u012btimanassa passaddhisambhavato passaddhi, tannimitta\u1e43 sukha\u1e43, sukhitassa cittasam\u0101dhisambhavato sukhanimitt\u0101 ekaggat\u0101 c\u0101ti jh\u0101na\u1e45g\u0101ni p\u0101tubhavanti. Evamassa pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101napa\u1e6dibimbabh\u016bta\u1e43 upac\u0101rajjh\u0101nampi ta\u1e45kha\u1e47a\xf1\xf1eva nibbattati. Ito para\u1e43 y\u0101va pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nassa appan\u0101 ceva vasippatti ca, t\u0101va sabba\u1e43 pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47e vuttanayeneva veditabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"For one who practices thus, the counterpart sign arises. Herein is the distinction between the two signs: the learning sign appears distorted, repulsive, and frightful to behold. The counterpart sign, however, appears like a man with stout major and minor limbs who, having eaten to his heart's content, is lying down. For him, at the very same time as the acquisition of the counterpart sign, sensual desire is abandoned by way of suppression due to non-attention to external sensual pleasures. And for him, just by the abandonment of attachment, ill will is also abandoned, like pus is removed by the removal of blood. Likewise, due to having aroused energy, sloth and torpor are abandoned; by way of application to peaceful states that cause no remorse, restlessness and remorse are abandoned; and due to the direct experience of the distinction that has been attained, doubt is abandoned regarding the Teacher who teaches the practice, the practice, and the fruit of the practice. In this way, the five hindrances are abandoned. And on that very sign, the absorption factors become manifest: initial application, characterized by directing the mind onto the object; sustained application, accomplishing the task of repeatedly examining the sign; joy, caused by attaining the acquired distinction; and since tranquility arises for one with a joyful mind, there is happiness, which has that tranquility as its cause; and since concentration of mind arises for one who is happy, there is one-pointedness, which has happiness as its cause. Thus, for him, access concentration, which is a reflection of the first absorption, also arises at that very moment. Hereafter, up to the full absorption and mastery of the first absorption, everything should be understood by the same method as was stated in the section on the earth kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"Para ele que age assim, surge o sinal de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta). Aqui reside a diferen\xe7a entre os dois sinais: o sinal de apreens\xe3o (uggahanimitta) aparece com uma apar\xeancia deformada, horr\xedvel e assustadora. O sinal de contraparte, no entanto, aparece como um homem de membros robustos que se deitou para dormir ap\xf3s comer o quanto queria. No mesmo momento em que ele obt\xe9m o sinal de contraparte, devido \xe0 n\xe3o aten\xe7\xe3o aos prazeres sensoriais externos, o desejo sensorial (k\u0101macchanda) \xe9 abandonado por meio da supress\xe3o (vikkhambhana). E pelo pr\xf3prio abandono do apego (anunaya), a malevol\xeancia (by\u0101p\u0101da) tamb\xe9m \xe9 abandonada, assim como o pus \xe9 eliminado com a elimina\xe7\xe3o do sangue. Da mesma forma, devido \xe0 energia aplicada (\u0101raddhav\u012briya), a pregui\xe7a e o torpor (thinamiddha) s\xe3o abandonados; devido \xe0 pr\xe1tica de estados pac\xedficos que evitam o remorso, a agita\xe7\xe3o e a preocupa\xe7\xe3o (uddhaccakukkucca) s\xe3o abandonadas; e devido \xe0 realiza\xe7\xe3o direta do estado especial alcan\xe7ado, a d\xfavida (vicikicch\u0101) em rela\xe7\xe3o ao Mestre que ensina a pr\xe1tica, em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 pr\xf3pria pr\xe1tica e em rela\xe7\xe3o ao fruto da pr\xe1tica \xe9 abandonada. Assim, os cinco obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47a) s\xe3o abandonados. E naquele mesmo sinal, surgem os fatores do jh\u0101na: o pensamento aplicado (vitakka), caracterizado por direcionar a mente ao objeto; o pensamento sustentado (vic\u0101ra), que realiza a fun\xe7\xe3o de examinar repetidamente o sinal; o entusiasmo (p\u012bti), condicionado pela obten\xe7\xe3o do estado especial alcan\xe7ado; a tranquilidade (passaddhi), que surge para aquele que tem a mente entusiasmada; a felicidade (sukha), que tem essa tranquilidade como causa; e a unifica\xe7\xe3o da mente (ekaggat\u0101), que tem a felicidade como causa, pois a concentra\xe7\xe3o mental surge para quem est\xe1 feliz. Assim, o jh\u0101na de acesso (upac\u0101rajjh\u0101na), que \xe9 como um reflexo do primeiro jh\u0101na, tamb\xe9m surge naquele mesmo momento. A partir daqui, at\xe9 a absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101) do primeiro jh\u0101na e a maestria (vasippatti), tudo deve ser compreendido exatamente da mesma maneira descrita no kasi\u1e47a de terra.",es:"A quien act\xfaa as\xed, se le manifiesta el signo reflejo (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta). Aqu\xed radica la diferencia entre los dos signos: el signo de aprendizaje (uggahanimitta) se presenta como algo deforme, asqueroso y de apariencia aterradora; el signo reflejo, en cambio, aparece como un hombre de miembros robustos que yace tras haber comido a su antojo. En el mismo momento en que obtiene el signo reflejo, debido a la falta de atenci\xf3n hacia los deseos sensoriales externos, el deseo sensorial (k\u0101macchando) se abandona mediante la supresi\xf3n. Al abandonar el apego, el odio (by\u0101p\u0101da) tambi\xe9n se abandona, tal como desaparece el pus al desaparecer la sangre. Asimismo, debido a la energ\xeda persistente, desaparece la pereza y el letargo (thinamiddha); debido a la pr\xe1ctica de estados pac\xedficos que no producen remordimiento, desaparece la agitaci\xf3n y la preocupaci\xf3n (uddhaccakukkucca); y debido a la realizaci\xf3n directa de la excelencia alcanzada, desaparece la duda (vicikicch\u0101) respecto al Maestro que ense\xf1a la pr\xe1ctica, respecto a la pr\xe1ctica misma y respecto al fruto de la pr\xe1ctica; as\xed se abandonan los cinco obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101ni). En ese mismo signo surgen los factores del jhana: la aplicaci\xf3n inicial (vitakka) con su caracter\xedstica de dirigir la mente hacia el objeto; el pensamiento sostenido (vic\u0101ra) que realiza la funci\xf3n de examinar repetidamente el signo; el arrebato (p\u012bti) causado por el logro de la excelencia obtenida; la tranquilidad (passaddhi) que surge para quien tiene una mente con arrebato; la felicidad (sukha) causada por esa tranquilidad; y la unificaci\xf3n de la mente (ekaggat\u0101) que tiene a la felicidad como causa. De este modo, en ese mismo instante surge tambi\xe9n la concentraci\xf3n de acceso (upac\u0101rajjh\u0101na), que es como un reflejo del primer jhana. De aqu\xed en adelante, todo lo relativo a la absorci\xf3n (appan\u0101) del primer jhana y al dominio (vasippatti) debe entenderse de la misma manera que se describi\xf3 en el kasina de tierra."}},{id:"vism-6.19",pali:"Aya\u1e43 pana viseso \u2013 vin\u012blake \"vin\u012blakapa\u1e6dikk\u016bla\u1e43 vin\u012blakapa\u1e6dikk\u016bla\"nti manasik\u0101ro pavattetabbo. Uggahanimitta\xf1cettha kabarakabarava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 pana ussadavasena upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"This, however, is the distinction: In the case of the livid one, attention should be directed thus: 'Livid and repulsive, livid and repulsive.' And here, the learning sign appears having a variegated, mottled color. The counterpart sign, however, appears by way of the predominant color.",pt:"Esta, por\xe9m, \xe9 a distin\xe7\xe3o: no caso do cad\xe1ver descolorido (vin\u012blaka), a aten\xe7\xe3o deve ser dirigida pensando: 'repulsivo cad\xe1ver descolorido, repulsivo cad\xe1ver descolorido'. E aqui, o sinal de apreens\xe3o (uggahanimitta) aparece com uma cor manchada e multicolorida. O sinal de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta), no entanto, aparece de acordo com a cor predominante.",es:"Sin embargo, existe esta distinci\xf3n: en el caso del cad\xe1ver c\xe1rdeno (vin\u012blaka), debe aplicarse la atenci\xf3n de la siguiente manera: 'lo repulsivo del cad\xe1ver c\xe1rdeno, lo repulsivo del cad\xe1ver c\xe1rdeno'. En esta meditaci\xf3n, el signo aprendido (uggahanimitta) aparece con una coloraci\xf3n abigarrada o manchada. En cambio, el signo de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta) aparece seg\xfan el color que predomine (entre el rojo, el blanco o el azulado)."}},{id:"vism-6.20",pali:"Vipubbake \"vipubbakapa\u1e6dikk\u016bla\u1e43 vipubbakapa\u1e6dikk\u016bla\"nti manasik\u0101ro pavattetabbo. Uggahanimitta\u1e43 panettha paggharantamiva upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 niccala\u1e43 sannisinna\u1e43 hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"In the case of the festering one, attention should be directed thus: 'Festering and repulsive, festering and repulsive.' Here, the learning sign appears as if oozing. The counterpart sign appears motionless and settled.",pt:"No caso do cad\xe1ver purulento (vipubbaka), a aten\xe7\xe3o deve ser dirigida pensando: 'repulsivo cad\xe1ver purulento, repulsivo cad\xe1ver purulento'. E aqui, o sinal de apreens\xe3o aparece como se estivesse escorrendo pus. O sinal de contraparte aparece im\xf3vel e pacificado.",es:"En el caso del cad\xe1ver putrefacto (vipubbaka), debe aplicarse la atenci\xf3n as\xed: 'lo repulsivo del cad\xe1ver putrefacto, lo repulsivo del cad\xe1ver putrefacto'. Aqu\xed, el signo aprendido aparece como si estuviera supurando o fluyendo. El signo de contraparte aparece inm\xf3vil y estable."}},{id:"vism-6.21",pali:"Lohitaka\u1e43 yuddhama\u1e47\u1e0dal\u0101d\u012bsu laddhappah\u0101r\u0101na\u1e43 hatthap\u0101d\u0101d\u012bsu v\u0101 chinnesu bhinnaga\u1e47\u1e0dap\u012b\u1e37ak\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 v\u0101 mukhato paggharam\u0101nak\u0101le labbhati. Tasm\u0101 ta\u1e43 disv\u0101 \"lohitakapa\u1e6dikk\u016bla\u1e43 lohitakapa\u1e6dikk\u016bla\"nti manasik\u0101ro pavattetabbo. Ettha uggahanimitta\u1e43 v\u0101tappahat\u0101 viya rattapa\u1e6d\u0101k\u0101 calam\u0101n\u0101k\u0101ra\u1e43 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 pana sannisinna\u1e43 hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"The bloody one is found on battlefields and so on, at the time when blood is gushing from the opening of wounds of those who have received blows, or when their hands, feet, and so on, are severed, or from broken boils, pustules, and the like. Therefore, having seen it, attention should be directed thus: 'The bloody one is repulsive, the bloody one is repulsive.' Herein, the learning sign appears in a state of motion, like a red banner struck by the wind. The counterpart sign, however, appears as still.",pt:"O cad\xe1ver ensanguentado (lohitaka) \xe9 obtido em campos de batalha, etc., quando as m\xe3os, p\xe9s, etc., daqueles que receberam ferimentos s\xe3o cortados, ou quando o sangue escorre das aberturas de abscessos, p\xfastulas rompidas, etc. Portanto, ao ver tal cad\xe1ver, a aten\xe7\xe3o deve ser dirigida pensando: 'repulsivo cad\xe1ver ensanguentado, repulsivo cad\xe1ver ensanguentado'. Aqui, o sinal de apreens\xe3o aparece com um aspect em movimento, como uma bandeira vermelha agitada pelo vento. O sinal de contraparte, no entanto, aparece im\xf3vel e pacificado.",es:"El cad\xe1ver sangriento (lohitaka) se encuentra en campos de batalla y lugares similares, ya sea en las manos o pies cortados de quienes han recibido heridas de armas, o cuando la sangre fluye de abscesos, p\xfastulas o llagas que han reventado. Por lo tanto, al ver tal cad\xe1ver, debe aplicarse la atenci\xf3n: 'lo repulsivo del cad\xe1ver sangriento, lo repulsivo del cad\xe1ver sangriento'. En este caso, el signo aprendido aparece con un aspecto oscilante, como una bandera roja agitada por el viento. El signo de contraparte, por el contrario, aparece en un estado de quietud."}},{id:"vism-6.22",pali:"Etesu hi yattha katthaci adhigatajjh\u0101no suvikkhambhitar\u0101gatt\u0101 v\u012btar\u0101go viya nilloluppac\u0101ro hoti. Eva\u1e43 santepi yv\u0101ya\u1e43 asubhappabhedo vutto, so sar\u012brasabh\u0101vappattivasena ca r\u0101gacaritabhedavasena c\u0101ti veditabbo. Chavasar\u012bra\u1e43 hi pa\u1e6dikk\u016blabh\u0101va\u1e43 \u0101pajjam\u0101na\u1e43 uddhum\u0101takasabh\u0101vappatta\u1e43 v\u0101 siy\u0101, vin\u012blak\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atarasabh\u0101vappatta\u1e43. Iti y\u0101disa\u1e43 y\u0101disa\u1e43 sakk\u0101 hoti laddhu\u1e43, t\u0101dise t\u0101dise uddhum\u0101takapa\u1e6dikk\u016bla\u1e43 vin\u012blakapa\u1e6dikk\u016blanti eva\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitabbamev\u0101ti sar\u012brasabh\u0101vappattivasena dasadh\u0101 asubhappabhedo vuttoti veditabbo.",translations:{en:"Indeed, among these, in any one whatsoever, a yogi who has attained jh\u0101na, due to the thorough suppression of lust, is free from fickle behavior, like one who is free from lust. Even so, it should be understood that this division of foulness that has been taught is by way of the state the corpse has reached and by way of the different types of lustful temperament. For a corpse, on becoming repulsive, might reach the state of a bloated one, or it might reach the state of one of the others, such as the livid. Therefore, whatever kind of corpse it is possible to obtain, in that very kind the sign should be grasped thus: 'the foulness of the bloated,' 'the foulness of the livid.' Thus, it should be understood that the tenfold division of foulness is taught by way of the state the corpse has reached.",pt:"Pois o iogue que alcan\xe7ou o jh\u0101na em qualquer uma dessas repulsividades, por ter suprimido bem a cobi\xe7a, torna-se livre de agita\xe7\xe3o, como algu\xe9m livre de paix\xf5es. Mesmo assim, deve-se entender que esta classifica\xe7\xe3o da repulsividade foi ensinada tanto de acordo com o estado natural alcan\xe7ado pelo cad\xe1ver quanto de acordo com os diferentes tipos de temperamento cobi\xe7oso. Pois o corpo de um cad\xe1ver, ao atingir o estado repulsivo, pode alcan\xe7ar o estado de um cad\xe1ver inchado ou qualquer outro estado como o de um cad\xe1ver l\xedvido, etc. Assim, qualquer que seja o tipo de cad\xe1ver que se possa obter, deve-se apreender o sinal em tal cad\xe1ver, pensando: 'repulsivo cad\xe1ver inchado, repulsivo cad\xe1ver l\xedvido', e assim por diante. Portanto, deve-se entender que a classifica\xe7\xe3o da repulsividade em dez tipos foi ensinada de acordo com o estado de decomposi\xe7\xe3o alcan\xe7ado pelo corpo.",es:"Pues aquel que ha alcanzado el jhana en cualquiera de estos asubhas posee el deseo (r\u0101ga) bien suprimido y, al igual que uno libre de pasiones, carece de un comportamiento inestable o codicioso. Aun siendo esto as\xed, esta clasificaci\xf3n de los asubhas que se ha expuesto debe entenderse seg\xfan el estado natural que alcanza el cuerpo muerto y seg\xfan la diversidad de los temperamentos propensos al deseo. Pues un cad\xe1ver, al volverse repulsivo, puede alcanzar el estado de estar hinchado (uddhum\u0101taka), o puede alcanzar cualquiera de los otros estados como el de estar l\xedvido (vin\u012blaka), etc. Por lo tanto, sea cual sea el tipo de cad\xe1ver que se pueda obtener, el signo debe captarse como 'lo repulsivo de lo hinchado' o 'lo repulsivo de lo l\xedvido'. As\xed, debe entenderse que la clasificaci\xf3n de los asubhas en diez tipos se ha expuesto seg\xfan el estado natural alcanzado por el cuerpo."}},{id:"vism-6.23",pali:"Visesato cettha uddhum\u0101taka\u1e43 sar\u012brasa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101navipattippak\u0101sanato sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101nar\u0101gino sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. Vin\u012blaka\u1e43 chavir\u0101gavipattippak\u0101sanato sar\u012brava\u1e47\u1e47ar\u0101gino sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. Vipubbaka\u1e43 k\u0101yava\u1e47apa\u1e6dibaddhassa duggandhabh\u0101vassa pak\u0101sanato m\u0101l\u0101gandh\u0101divasena samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101pitasar\u012bragandhar\u0101gino sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. Vicchiddaka\u1e43 antosusirabh\u0101vappak\u0101sanato sar\u012bre ghanabh\u0101var\u0101gino sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. Vikkh\u0101yitaka\u1e43 ma\u1e43supacayasampattivin\u0101sappak\u0101sanato than\u0101d\u012bsu sar\u012brappadesesu ma\u1e43supacayar\u0101gino sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. Vikkhittaka\u1e43 a\u1e45gapacca\u1e45g\u0101na\u1e43 vikkhepappak\u0101sanato a\u1e45gapacca\u1e45gal\u012bl\u0101r\u0101gino sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. Hatavikkhittaka\u1e43 sar\u012brasa\u1e45gh\u0101tabhedavik\u0101rappak\u0101sanato sar\u012brasa\u1e45gh\u0101tasampattir\u0101gino sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. Lohitaka\u1e43 lohitamakkhitapa\u1e6dikk\u016blabh\u0101vappak\u0101sanato ala\u1e45k\u0101rajanitasobhar\u0101gino sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. Pu\u1e37avaka\u1e43 k\u0101yassa anekakimikulas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47abh\u0101vappak\u0101sanato k\u0101ye mamattar\u0101gino sapp\u0101ya\u1e43. A\u1e6d\u1e6dhika\u1e43 sar\u012bra\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u012bna\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikk\u016blabh\u0101vappak\u0101sanato dantasampattir\u0101gino sapp\u0101yanti eva\u1e43 r\u0101gacaritabhedavasen\u0101pi dasadh\u0101 asubhappabhedo vuttoti veditabbo.",translations:{en:"Here, especially, the bloated corpse is suitable for one with lust for form, as it reveals the destruction of the body\u2019s form. The livid corpse is suitable for one with lust for the body\u2019s complexion, as it reveals the corruption of the skin\u2019s beauty. The festering corpse is suitable for one with lust for bodily scents produced by means of garlands, perfumes, and so on, as it reveals the state of foul smell connected with the body as a wound. The cut-up corpse is suitable for one with lust for the body\u2019s solidity, as it reveals the state of being hollow inside. The gnawed corpse is suitable for one with lust for the accumulation of flesh in regions of the body such as the breasts, as it reveals the destruction of the fullness of the accumulation of flesh. The scattered corpse is suitable for one with lust for the gracefulness of the major and minor limbs, as it reveals the scattering of the limbs. The hacked and scattered corpse is suitable for one with lust for the perfection of the body\u2019s cohesion, as it reveals the alteration which is the breaking of the body\u2019s cohesion. The bloody corpse is suitable for one with lust for beauty produced by adornments, as it reveals the repulsive state of being smeared with blood. The worm-infested corpse is suitable for one with lust for \u2018mineness\u2019 regarding the body, as it reveals the state of being common to many families of worms. The skeleton is suitable for one with lust for the perfection of the teeth, as it reveals the repulsive state of the body\u2019s bones. Thus, it should be understood that the tenfold division of foulness is also taught by way of the different types of lustful temperament.",pt:"Especificamente aqui, o cad\xe1ver inchado \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a pela forma do corpo, pois revela a ru\xedna da forma corporal. O cad\xe1ver l\xedvido \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a pela cor da pele, pois revela a ru\xedna da beleza da pele. O cad\xe1ver purulento \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a pelo odor corporal estimulado por flores, perfumes, etc., pois revela o mau cheiro associado \xe0s feridas do corpo. O cad\xe1ver cortado ao meio \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a pela solidez do corpo, pois revela a natureza oca de seu interior. O cad\xe1ver dilacerado \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a pelo ac\xfamulo de carne em partes do corpo como os seios, etc., pois revela a destrui\xe7\xe3o da plenitude da carne. O cad\xe1ver desmembrado \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a pela gra\xe7a dos membros, pois revela a dispers\xe3o dos membros e partes do corpo. O cad\xe1ver mutilado e desmembrado \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a pela perfei\xe7\xe3o da integridade f\xedsica, pois revela a altera\xe7\xe3o e a quebra da coes\xe3o do corpo. O cad\xe1ver sangrento \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a pela beleza produzida por ornamentos, pois revela a repulsividade de estar coberto de sangue. O cad\xe1ver infestado de vermes \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a de apego ao corpo como 'meu', pois revela que o corpo \xe9 compartilhado com muitas fam\xedlias de vermes. O esqueleto \xe9 adequado para quem tem cobi\xe7a pela perfei\xe7\xe3o dos dentes, pois revela a repulsividade dos ossos do corpo. Assim, deve-se entender que a classifica\xe7\xe3o da repulsividade em dez tipos tamb\xe9m foi ensinada de acordo com os diferentes tipos de temperamento cobi\xe7oso.",es:"Espec\xedficamente, aqu\xed el estado hinchado (uddhum\u0101taka) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por la forma (sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101nar\u0101ga), pues muestra la ruina de la configuraci\xf3n del cuerpo. El estado l\xedvido (vin\u012blaka) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por el color del cuerpo, pues muestra la ruina de la belleza de la piel. El estado purulento (vipubbaka) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por el olor del cuerpo provocado por flores y perfumes, pues muestra la naturaleza maloliente vinculada a las llagas del cuerpo. El estado cortado (vicchiddaka) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por la solidez del cuerpo, pues muestra la naturaleza hueca del interior. El estado devorado (vikkh\u0101yitaka) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por la plenitud de la carne en partes del cuerpo como los senos, pues muestra la destrucci\xf3n de la perfecci\xf3n de la acumulaci\xf3n de carne. El estado disperso (vikkhittaka) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por la gracia de los miembros y extremidades, pues muestra la dispersi\xf3n de estos. El estado mutilado y disperso (hatavikkhittaka) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por la perfecci\xf3n de la integridad del cuerpo, pues muestra la alteraci\xf3n provocada por la ruptura de la uni\xf3n del cuerpo. El estado sangriento (lohitaka) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por la belleza generada por los ornamentos, pues muestra la repulsividad de estar manchado de sangre. El estado infestado de gusanos (pu\u1e37avaka) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por el cuerpo con el sentido de 'es m\xedo', pues muestra que el cuerpo es compartido con numerosas familias de gusanos. El estado de los huesos (a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika) es adecuado para quien tiene deseo por la perfecci\xf3n de los dientes, pues muestra la repulsividad de los huesos del cuerpo. De esta manera, debe entenderse que la clasificaci\xf3n de los asubhas en diez tipos se ha expuesto tambi\xe9n seg\xfan la diversidad de los temperamentos propensos al deseo."}}]},424,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,s,i,n,t){i.exports=[{id:"vism-7.1",pali:"Asubh\u0101nantara\u1e43 uddi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101su pana dasasu anussat\u012bsu punappuna\u1e43 uppajjanato satiyeva anussati, pavattitabba\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101namhiyeva v\u0101 pavattatt\u0101 saddh\u0101pabbajitassa kulaputtassa anur\u016bp\u0101 sat\u012btipi anussati, buddha\u1e43 \u0101rabbha uppann\u0101 anussati buddh\u0101nussati, buddhagu\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43. Dhamma\u1e43 \u0101rabbha uppann\u0101 anussati dhamm\u0101nussati, sv\u0101kkh\u0101tat\u0101didhammagu\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43. Sa\u1e45gha\u1e43 \u0101rabbha uppann\u0101 anussati sa\u1e45gh\u0101nussati, suppa\u1e6dipannat\u0101disa\u1e45ghagu\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43. S\u012bla\u1e43 \u0101rabbha uppann\u0101 anussati s\u012bl\u0101nussati, akha\u1e47\u1e0dat\u0101dis\u012blagu\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43. C\u0101ga\u1e43 \u0101rabbha uppann\u0101 anussati c\u0101g\u0101nussati, muttac\u0101gat\u0101dic\u0101gagu\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43. Devat\u0101 \u0101rabbha uppann\u0101 anussati devat\u0101nussati, devat\u0101 sakkhi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 attano saddh\u0101digu\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43. Mara\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101rabbha uppann\u0101 anussati mara\u1e47\u0101nussati, j\u012bvitindriyupacched\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43. Kes\u0101dibheda\u1e43 r\u016bpak\u0101ya\u1e43 gat\u0101, k\u0101ye v\u0101 gat\u0101ti k\u0101yagat\u0101, k\u0101yagat\u0101 ca s\u0101 sati c\u0101ti k\u0101yagatasat\u012bti vattabbe rassa\u1e43 akatv\u0101 k\u0101yagat\u0101sat\u012bti vutt\u0101, kes\u0101dik\u0101yako\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101sanimitt\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43. \u0100n\u0101p\u0101ne \u0101rabbha uppann\u0101 sati \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassati, ass\u0101sapass\u0101sanimitt\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43. Upasama\u1e43 \u0101rabbha uppann\u0101 anussati upasam\u0101nussati, sabbadukkh\u016bpasam\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya satiy\u0101 etamadhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now, among the ten recollections enumerated after the meditations on foulness, mindfulness itself is recollection (anussati) because it arises again and again. Or, because it occurs only in a suitable place, it is mindfulness appropriate for a clansman who has gone forth out of faith; for this reason also, it is recollection. The recollection that arises with the Buddha as its object is recollection of the Buddha (buddh\u0101nussati); this is a designation for mindfulness that has the qualities of the Buddha as its object. The recollection that arises with the Dhamma as its object is recollection of the Dhamma (dhamm\u0101nussati); this is a designation for mindfulness that has as its object the qualities of the Dhamma, beginning with its being well-proclaimed. The recollection that arises with the Sangha as its object is recollection of the Sangha (sa\u1e45gh\u0101nussati); this is a designation for mindfulness that has as its object the qualities of the Sangha, beginning with their practicing the good way. The recollection that arises with virtue (s\u012bla) as its object is recollection of virtue (s\u012bl\u0101nussati); this is a designation for mindfulness that has as its object the qualities of one's own virtue, beginning with its being unbroken. The recollection that arises with generosity (c\u0101ga) as its object is recollection of generosity (c\u0101g\u0101nussati); this is a designation for mindfulness that has as its object the qualities of one's own generosity, beginning with open-handed generosity. The recollection that arises with the deities as its object is recollection of the deities (devat\u0101nussati); this is a designation for mindfulness that has as its object one's own qualities, beginning with faith, having placed the deities in the position of a witness. The recollection that arises with death as its object is recollection of death (mara\u1e47\u0101nussati); this is a designation for mindfulness that has the cutting off of the life faculty as its object. Mindfulness that has gone to the material body, which is divided into parts beginning with the hair of the head, or has gone into the body, is called k\u0101yagat\u0101 (gone to the body). And since that mindfulness is k\u0101yagat\u0101, it should be called k\u0101yagatasati; but without shortening the vowel, it is called k\u0101yagat\u0101sati. This is a designation for mindfulness that has as its object the sign in the bodily parts, beginning with the hair of the head. The mindfulness that arises with the in-breaths and out-breaths as its object is mindfulness of breathing (\u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassati); this is a designation for mindfulness that has the sign of in-breaths and out-breaths as its object. The recollection that arises with peace (upasama) as its object is recollection of peace (upasam\u0101nussati); this is a designation for mindfulness that has as its object the stilling of all suffering.",pt:"Ap\xf3s as impurezas (asubha), entre as dez recorda\xe7\xf5es (anussati) indicadas, a pr\xf3pria aten\xe7\xe3o (sati) \xe9 chamada de 'recorda\xe7\xe3o' (anussati) por surgir repetidamente; ou tamb\xe9m \xe9 chamada de 'recorda\xe7\xe3o' por ser a aten\xe7\xe3o adequada para um filho de boa fam\xedlia que se ordenou por f\xe9, ocorrendo precisamente naquilo que \xe9 apropriado. A recorda\xe7\xe3o que surge tendo como objeto o Buddha \xe9 a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Buddha (buddh\u0101nussati); este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem as qualidades do Buddha como objeto. A recorda\xe7\xe3o que surge tendo como objeto o Dhamma \xe9 a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Dhamma (dhamm\u0101nussati); este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem como objeto as qualidades do Dhamma, como o fato de ser bem proclamado (sv\u0101kkh\u0101tat\u0101). A recorda\xe7\xe3o que surge tendo como objeto o Sa\u1e45gha \xe9 a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Sa\u1e45gha (sa\u1e45gh\u0101nussati); este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem como objeto as qualidades do Sa\u1e45gha, como o fato de praticar bem (suppa\u1e6dipannat\u0101). A recorda\xe7\xe3o que surge tendo como objeto a virtude \xe9 a recorda\xe7\xe3o da virtude (s\u012bl\u0101nussati); este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem como objeto as qualidades da pr\xf3pria virtude, como o fato de ser ininterrupta (akha\u1e47\u1e0dat\u0101). A recorda\xe7\xe3o que surge tendo como objeto a generosidade \xe9 a recorda\xe7\xe3o da generosidade (c\u0101g\u0101nussati); este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem como objeto as qualidades da pr\xf3pria generosidade, como o desapego na doa\xe7\xe3o (muttac\u0101gat\u0101). A recorda\xe7\xe3o que surge tendo como objeto as divindades \xe9 a recorda\xe7\xe3o das divindades (devat\u0101nussati); este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem como objeto as pr\xf3prias qualidades de f\xe9 e outras, tomando as divindades como testemunhas. A recorda\xe7\xe3o que surge tendo como objeto a morte \xe9 a recorda\xe7\xe3o da morte (mara\u1e47\u0101nussati); este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem como objeto a interrup\xe7\xe3o da faculdade da vida (j\u012bvitindriya). A aten\xe7\xe3o direcionada ao corpo f\xedsico, dividido em partes como cabelos e outras, ou que ocorre no corpo, \xe9 chamada de 'aten\xe7\xe3o direcionada ao corpo' (k\u0101yagat\u0101); sendo ela tanto direcionada ao corpo quanto aten\xe7\xe3o, deveria ser chamada de 'k\u0101yagatasati', mas, sem encurtar a vogal, \xe9 chamada de 'k\u0101yagat\u0101sati'; este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem como objeto o sinal de repulsa das partes do corpo, como cabelos e outras. A aten\xe7\xe3o que surge tendo como objeto a respira\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a aten\xe7\xe3o na respira\xe7\xe3o (\u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassati); este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem como objeto o sinal da inspira\xe7\xe3o e da expira\xe7\xe3o. A recorda\xe7\xe3o que surge tendo como objeto a paz \xe9 a recorda\xe7\xe3o da paz (upasam\u0101nussati); este \xe9 o nome para a aten\xe7\xe3o que tem como objeto o Nibb\u0101na, a pacifica\xe7\xe3o de todo o sofrimento.",es:"Despu\xe9s de las asubhas, respecto a las diez recordaciones (anussati) mencionadas brevemente: se llama 'anussati' a la atenci\xf3n (sati) que surge repetidamente. O bien, se llama 'anussati' a la atenci\xf3n apropiada para un noble hijo que ha renunciado por fe, debido a que ocurre precisamente en el lugar donde debe ser aplicada. La recordaci\xf3n que surge bas\xe1ndose en el Buda es la 'recordaci\xf3n del Buda' (buddh\u0101nussati); este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto las cualidades del Buda. La recordaci\xf3n que surge bas\xe1ndose en el Dhamma es la 'recordaci\xf3n del Dhamma' (dhamm\u0101nussati); este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto las cualidades del Dhamma, tales como su buena proclamaci\xf3n (sv\u0101kkh\u0101tat\u0101). La recordaci\xf3n que surge bas\xe1ndose en el Sa\u1e45gha es la 'recordaci\xf3n del Sa\u1e45gha' (sa\u1e45gh\u0101nussati); este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto las cualidades del Sa\u1e45gha, tales como su buena conducta (suppa\u1e6dipannat\u0101). La recordaci\xf3n que surge bas\xe1ndose en la propia virtud es la 'recordaci\xf3n de la virtud' (s\u012bl\u0101nussati); este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto las cualidades de la propia virtud, tales como su integridad (akha\u1e47\u1e0dat\u0101). La recordaci\xf3n que surge bas\xe1ndose en la propia generosidad es la 'recordaci\xf3n de la generosidad' (c\u0101g\u0101nussati); este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto las cualidades de la propia generosidad, tales como el desprendimiento (muttac\u0101gat\u0101). La recordaci\xf3n que surge bas\xe1ndose en las deidades es la 'recordaci\xf3n de las deidades' (devat\u0101nussati); este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto las propias cualidades de fe y dem\xe1s, tomando a las deidades como testigos. La recordaci\xf3n que surge bas\xe1ndose en la propia muerte es la 'recordaci\xf3n de la muerte' (mara\u1e47\u0101nussati); este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto la cesaci\xf3n de la facultad vital. La atenci\xf3n dirigida al cuerpo f\xedsico, compuesta por partes como el cabello, etc., se llama 'atenci\xf3n dirigida al cuerpo' (k\u0101yagat\u0101sati); aunque gramaticalmente deber\xeda decirse 'k\u0101yagatasati', se dice 'k\u0101yagat\u0101' alargando la vocal; este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto el signo de lo repulsivo en las partes del cuerpo. La atenci\xf3n que surge bas\xe1ndose en la inspiraci\xf3n y la espiraci\xf3n es la 'atenci\xf3n en la respiraci\xf3n' (\u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassati); este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto el signo de la inspiraci\xf3n y la espiraci\xf3n. La recordaci\xf3n que surge bas\xe1ndose en la paz, el Nibb\u0101na que es el apaciguamiento de todas las formaciones, es la 'recordaci\xf3n de la paz' (upasam\u0101nussati); este es un nombre para la atenci\xf3n que tiene como objeto el Nibb\u0101na, que es el apaciguamiento de todo sufrimiento."}},{id:"vism-7.2",pali:"Iti im\u0101su dasasu anussat\u012bsu buddh\u0101nussati\u1e43 t\u0101va bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena aveccappas\u0101dasamann\u0101gatena yogin\u0101 patir\u016bpasen\u0101sane rahogatena pa\u1e6disall\u012bnena \"itipi so bhagav\u0101 araha\u1e43 samm\u0101sambuddho vijj\u0101cara\u1e47asampanno sugato lokavid\u016b anuttaro purisadammas\u0101rathi satth\u0101 devamanuss\u0101na\u1e43 buddho bhagav\u0101\"ti eva\u1e43 buddhassa bhagavato gu\u1e47\u0101 anussaritabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Thus, among these ten recollections, a yog\u012b who wishes to develop the recollection of the Buddha, endowed with unwavering confidence, should first of all, in a suitable dwelling, having gone to a secluded place and being in solitude, recollect the qualities of the Buddha, the Blessed One, in this way: 'For this reason, the Blessed One is an Arahant, a Perfectly Self-Enlightened One, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, a Well-Gone One, a Knower of the World, an Unexcelled Trainer of persons to be tamed, a Teacher of gods and humans, an Enlightened One, a Blessed One.'",pt:"Assim, entre estas dez recorda\xe7\xf5es, o iogue que deseja primeiramente desenvolver a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Buddha, dotado de f\xe9 inabal\xe1vel, tendo se retirado para uma habita\xe7\xe3o adequada e em recolhimento, deve recordar repetidamente as qualidades do Aben\xe7oado Buddha de acordo com esta passagem: 'Assim \xe9 o Aben\xe7oado: Ele \xe9 um Arahat, perfeitamente desperto, dotado de conhecimento claro e conduta virtuosa, sublime, conhecedor do mundo, o insuper\xe1vel guia para as pessoas que podem ser domadas, mestre de divindades e seres humanos, desperto, aben\xe7oado'.",es:"As\xed, entre estas diez recordaciones, el yogui que posee una confianza inquebrantable y desea desarrollar primero la recordaci\xf3n del Buda, en un asiento adecuado, habi\xe9ndose retirado a la soledad y en reclusi\xf3n, debe recordar las cualidades del Buda, el Bienaventurado, de acuerdo con este pasaje: 'Tal es el Bienaventurado: es santo, perfectamente iluminado, dotado de conocimiento y buena conducta, bien ido, conocedor de los mundos, supremo gu\xeda de los hombres que pueden ser domados, maestro de dioses y humanos, el Buda, el Bienaventurado'."}},{id:"vism-7.3",pali:"Tattha \u0101rakatt\u0101 ar\u012bna\u1e43 ar\u0101na\xf1ca hatatt\u0101 paccay\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 arahatt\u0101 p\u0101pakara\u1e47e rah\u0101bh\u0101v\u0101ti imehi t\u0101va k\u0101ra\u1e47ehi so bhagav\u0101 arahanti anussarati. \u0100rak\u0101 hi so sabbakilesehi suvid\u016bravid\u016bre \u1e6dhito maggena sav\u0101san\u0101na\u1e43 kiles\u0101na\u1e43 viddha\u1e43sitatt\u0101ti \u0101rakatt\u0101 araha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Therein, one first of all recollects that the Blessed One is an Arahant for these reasons: because of being far, because of having destroyed the enemies, because of having destroyed the spokes, because of being worthy of requisites and so on, and because of the absence of a secret place for doing evil. Indeed, He is far from all defilements; He stands very, very far away, because the defilements together with their latent tendencies have been destroyed by the path. Thus, because of being far, He is an Arahant.",pt:"Nisso, primeiramente, por estar distante (\u0101rakatt\u0101), por ter destru\xeddo os inimigos (ar\u012bna\u1e43 hatatt\u0101), por ter destru\xeddo os raios da roda (ar\u0101na\u1e43 hatatt\u0101), por ser digno de receber os requisitos e outras oferendas (paccay\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 arahatt\u0101) e por n\xe3o haver segredo na pr\xe1tica do mal (p\u0101pakara\u1e47e rah\u0101bh\u0101v\u0101) \u2014 por estas raz\xf5es ele recorda: 'Aquele Aben\xe7oado \xe9 um Arahat'. Pois ele est\xe1 distante de todas as impurezas mentais, estabelecido em extrema dist\xe2ncia, devido \xe0 destrui\xe7\xe3o das impurezas mentais junto com suas tend\xeancias latentes por meio do Caminho; assim, por estar distante, ele \xe9 um Arahat.",es:"En este contexto, \xe9l recuerda al Bienaventurado como 'santo' (araha\u1e43) primeramente por estas razones: por estar distante de las impurezas, por haber destruido a los enemigos, por haber destruido los radios de la rueda, por ser digno de ofrendas y por la ausencia de secretismo al hacer el mal. Pues \xe9l est\xe1 distante de todas las impurezas, permaneciendo extremadamente lejos de ellas, por haber destruido las impurezas junto con sus impresiones residuales mediante el camino; por estar as\xed distante, es 'araha\u1e43'."}},{id:"vism-7.4",pali:"Tatr\u0101ya\u1e43 ekapadayojan\u0101, jar\u0101mara\u1e47a\u1e43 dukkhasacca\u1e43, j\u0101ti samudayasacca\u1e43, ubhinnampi nissara\u1e47a\u1e43 nirodhasacca\u1e43, nirodhapaj\u0101nan\u0101 pa\u1e6dipad\u0101 maggasaccanti evamekekapaduddh\u0101rena sabbadhamme samm\u0101 s\u0101ma\xf1ca buddho anubuddho pa\u1e6dibuddho. Tena vutta\u1e43 \u2013 \"samm\u0101 s\u0101ma\xf1ca sabbadhamm\u0101na\u1e43 buddhatt\u0101 pana samm\u0101sambuddho\"ti.",translations:{en:"Herein is the application of a single term: aging-and-death is the Truth of Suffering; birth is the Truth of the Origin; the escape from both is the Truth of Cessation; and the practice for the thorough knowledge of cessation is the Truth of the Path. Thus, by the extraction of each single term, He has rightly and by Himself awakened, subsequently awakened, and penetratively awakened to all phenomena. Therefore it is said: \u201cBecause of having rightly and by Himself awakened to all phenomena, He is the Perfectly Self-Enlightened One.\u201d",pt:"Nisso, esta \xe9 a aplica\xe7\xe3o de um \xfanico termo: o envelhecimento e morte \xe9 a verdade do sofrimento; o nascimento \xe9 a verdade da origem; a liberta\xe7\xe3o de ambos \xe9 a verdade da cessa\xe7\xe3o; o caminho que compreende a cessa\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a verdade do caminho. Assim, extraindo cada termo individualmente, Ele compreendeu todos os dhammas de forma correta e por Si mesmo, compreendeu de acordo com a verdade (anubuddho) e realizou plenamente (pa\u1e6dibuddho). Por isso foi dito: 'Por ter compreendido todos os dhammas de forma correta e por Si mesmo, Ele \xe9 chamado de Samm\u0101sambuddho (o Plenamente Desperto por Si Mesmo)'.",es:"En este contexto, esta es la aplicaci\xf3n de un solo t\xe9rmino: la vejez y la muerte son la Verdad del Sufrimiento; el nacimiento es la Verdad del Origen; la liberaci\xf3n de ambos es la Verdad del Cese; la pr\xe1ctica que conoce el cese es la Verdad del Sendero. As\xed, mediante el desglose de cada t\xe9rmino individual, \xe9l es el Buda que ha comprendido todas las cosas de manera correcta y por s\xed mismo, habi\xe9ndolas comprendido plenamente y penetrado. Por ello se dice: 'Debido a que ha despertado a todas las cosas de manera correcta y por s\xed mismo, es llamado el Perfectamente Iluminado (Samm\u0101sambuddho)'."}},{id:"vism-7.5",pali:"Tasm\u0101 have lokavid\u016b sumedho, Lokantag\u016b v\u016bsitabrahmacariyo; Lokassa anta\u1e43 samit\u0101vi \xf1atv\u0101, N\u0101s\u012bsati lokamima\u1e43 para\xf1c\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Therefore, indeed, the wise one, the knower of the world, who has gone to the world's end and lived the holy life; having known the end of the world, the pacified one does not long for this world or the next.",pt:"Portanto, o s\xe1bio conhecedor do mundo, que alcan\xe7ou o fim do mundo e viveu a vida santa, tendo conhecido o fim do mundo e pacificado as impurezas, n\xe3o anseia por este mundo nem pelo outro.",es:"Por lo tanto, el sabio conocedor del mundo, el que ha llegado al fin del mundo y ha culminado la vida santa, habiendo conocido el fin del mundo y habi\xe9ndose calmado, no anhela ni este mundo ni el pr\xf3ximo."}},{id:"vism-7.6",pali:"Yath\u0101 ca sattaloko, eva\u1e43 ok\u0101salokopi. Tath\u0101 hesa eka\u1e43 cakkav\u0101\u1e37a\u1e43 \u0101y\u0101mato ca vitth\u0101rato ca yojan\u0101na\u1e43 dv\u0101dasasatasahass\u0101ni catuti\u1e43sasat\u0101ni ca pa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa\xf1ca yojan\u0101ni. Parikkhepato pana \u2013",translations:{en:"And just as the world of beings, so too the world of location was known to Him. For this single world-system is one million, two hundred and three thousand, four hundred and fifty yojanas in length and breadth. In circumference, however\u2014",pt:"E assim como o mundo dos seres, o mesmo se aplica ao mundo do espa\xe7o (ok\u0101saloko). Pois um \xfanico sistema de mundos (cakkav\u0101\u1e37a) mede, em comprimento e largura, um milh\xe3o duzentas e tr\xeas mil quatrocentas e cinquenta yojanas. E em circunfer\xeancia:",es:"Y as\xed como conoce el mundo de los seres, conoce tambi\xe9n el mundo como localizaci\xf3n (ok\u0101saloka). Pues as\xed, un solo sistema de mundos (cakkav\u0101\u1e37a) mide en longitud y anchura un mill\xf3n doscientas tres mil cuatrocientas cincuenta yoyanas. En cuanto a su circunferencia \u2014"}},{id:"vism-7.7",pali:"Catt\u0101ri satasahass\u0101ni, a\u1e6d\u1e6dheva nahut\u0101ni ca; Ettaka\u1e43 bahalattena, jala\u1e43 v\u0101te pati\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Four hundred thousand and eighty thousand yojanas; of such a thickness, the water is established on the wind.",pt:"A \xe1gua, com uma espessura de quatrocentas e oitenta mil yojanas, estabelecida sobre o ar.",es:"Se encuentra el agua, con un espesor de cuatrocientas ochenta mil yoyanas, apoyada sobre el aire."}},{id:"vism-7.8",pali:"Pa\xf1\xf1\u0101sayojanakkhandha-s\u0101kh\u0101y\u0101m\u0101 samantato; Satayojanavitthi\u1e47\u1e47\u0101, t\u0101vadeva ca uggat\u0101; Jamb\u016b yass\u0101nubh\u0101vena, jambud\u012bpo pak\u0101sito.",translations:{en:"The Jambu tree has a trunk and branches fifty yojanas in length; it is one hundred yojanas wide all around and just as high. By its power, Jambud\u012bpa is proclaimed.",pt:"tem um tronco e galhos que se estendem por cinquenta yojanas em todas as dire\xe7\xf5es, espalhando-se por cem yojanas de largura e elevando-se \xe0 mesma altura. \xc9 devido ao poder desta \xe1rvore Jamb\u016b que este continente \xe9 conhecido como Jambud\u012bpa.",es:"La longitud de su tronco y sus ramas es de cincuenta yoyanas cada uno; su follaje se extiende por cien yoyanas a la redonda y se eleva a la misma altura. Por el poder de este \xe1rbol Jambu, este continente es conocido como Jambud\u012bpa."}},{id:"vism-7.9",pali:"Attan\u0101 pana gu\u1e47ehi visi\u1e6d\u1e6dhatarassa kassaci abh\u0101vato natthi etassa uttaroti anuttaro. Tath\u0101 hesa s\u012blagu\u1e47en\u0101pi sabba\u1e43 lokamabhibhavati, sam\u0101dhipa\xf1\xf1\u0101vimuttivimutti\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanagu\u1e47en\u0101pi. S\u012blagu\u1e47en\u0101pi asamo asamasamo appa\u1e6dimo appa\u1e6dibh\u0101go appa\u1e6dipuggalo\u2026pe\u2026 vimutti\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanagu\u1e47en\u0101pi. Yath\u0101ha \u2013 \"na kho pan\u0101ha\u1e43 samanupass\u0101mi sadevake loke sam\u0101rake\u2026pe\u2026 sadevamanuss\u0101ya paj\u0101ya attan\u0101 s\u012blasampannatara\"nti vitth\u0101ro. Eva\u1e43 aggapas\u0101dasutt\u0101d\u012bni \"na me \u0101cariyo atth\u012b\"ti\u0101dik\u0101 g\u0101th\u0101yo ca vitth\u0101retabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, because there is no one more distinguished than himself in virtues, 'there is no superior to him,' thus he is the Unsurpassed (Anuttara). Indeed, he surpasses the entire world by the virtue of morality, and also by the virtues of concentration, wisdom, liberation, and the knowledge and vision of liberation. By the virtue of morality, he is without equal, equal to the unequalled, without a peer, without a counterpart, and without a rival person... and so on... and also by the virtue of the knowledge and vision of liberation. As it is said: \u201cI do not see anyone in this world with its devas, its M\u0101ra... and so on... in this generation with its devas and humans, who is more accomplished in morality than myself.\u201d This should be elaborated. In this way, the Aggappas\u0101da Sutta and others, and the verses beginning, \u201cThere is no teacher for me,\u201d should also be elaborated.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, por n\xe3o haver ningu\xe9m superior a ele em virtudes, n\xe3o h\xe1 ningu\xe9m acima dele; por isso, ele \xe9 Anuttaro (Incompar\xe1vel). De fato, ele supera o mundo inteiro por sua virtude de moralidade (s\u012bla), e tamb\xe9m por suas virtudes de concentra\xe7\xe3o (sam\u0101dhi), sabedoria (pa\xf1\xf1\u0101), liberta\xe7\xe3o (vimutti) e conhecimento e vis\xe3o da liberta\xe7\xe3o (vimutti\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassana). Mesmo na virtude da moralidade, ele \xe9 inigual\xe1vel (asamo), igual apenas aos inigual\xe1veis (asamasamo), sem paralelo (appa\u1e6dimo), incompar\xe1vel (appa\u1e6dibh\u0101go), sem rival (appa\u1e6dipuggalo)... e assim por diante at\xe9 a virtude do conhecimento e vis\xe3o da liberta\xe7\xe3o. Conforme foi dito: 'N\xe3o vejo, no mundo com seus devas, M\u0101ras... e na popula\xe7\xe3o com seus devas e humanos, ningu\xe9m mais perfeito em moralidade do que eu mesmo', e assim por diante em detalhes. Desse modo, o Aggapas\u0101da Sutta e outros, bem como os versos que come\xe7am com 'N\xe3o tenho mestre', devem ser explicados detalhadamente.",es:"Debido a la inexistencia de alguien superior a \xc9l en cualidades, no tiene superior; por ello es Anuttaro (Insuperable). Pues \xc9l supera a todo el mundo tanto en la cualidad de la virtud, como en las cualidades de la concentraci\xf3n, la sabidur\xeda, la liberaci\xf3n y el conocimiento y visi\xf3n de la liberaci\xf3n. Incluso solo por la cualidad de la virtud es inigualable (asamo), igual solo a los inigualables (asamasamo - los Budas del pasado), sin parang\xf3n (appa\u1e6dimo), sin semejanza (appa\u1e6dibh\u0101go), un individuo sin rival (appa\u1e6dipuggalo)... y as\xed sucesivamente hasta la cualidad del conocimiento y visi\xf3n de la liberaci\xf3n. Como \xc9l mismo dijo: 'No veo, monjes, en este mundo con sus devas, sus Maras... en esta generaci\xf3n con sus ascetas y brahmanes, con sus dioses y hombres, a ning\xfan otro m\xe1s perfecto en virtud que yo mismo', y as\xed se describe extensamente. Del mismo modo deben detallarse el Aggappas\u0101da Sutta y otros, as\xed como los versos que comienzan con 'No tengo maestro'."}},{id:"vism-7.10",pali:"Bhagavati kira gaggar\u0101ya pokkhara\u1e47iy\u0101 t\u012bre camp\u0101nagarav\u0101s\u012bna\u1e43 dhamma\u1e43 desiyam\u0101ne eko ma\u1e47\u1e0d\u016bko bhagavato sare nimitta\u1e43 aggahesi, ta\u1e43 eko vacchap\u0101lako da\u1e47\u1e0da\u1e43 olubbha ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhanto s\u012bse sannirumbhitv\u0101 a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101si. So t\u0101vadeva k\u0101la\u1e45katv\u0101 t\u0101vati\u1e43sabhavane dv\u0101dasayojanike kanakavim\u0101ne nibbatti. Suttappabuddho viya ca tattha acchar\u0101sa\u1e45ghaparivuta\u1e43 att\u0101na\u1e43 disv\u0101 \"are ahampi n\u0101ma idha nibbatto, ki\u1e43 nu kho kammamak\u0101si\"nti \u0101vajjento na a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 ki\xf1ci addasa a\xf1\xf1atra bhagavato sare nimittagg\u0101h\u0101. So t\u0101vadeva saha vim\u0101nena \u0101gantv\u0101 bhagavato p\u0101de siras\u0101 vandi. Bhagav\u0101 j\u0101nantova pucchi \u2013",translations:{en:"It is said that while the Blessed One was teaching the Dhamma to the residents of the city of Camp\u0101 on the bank of the Gaggar\u0101 lotus pond, a certain frog grasped the sign in the Blessed One\u2019s voice. A certain cowherd, while standing leaning on a stick, pressed down on its head with the stick and stood there. That frog, having died at that very moment, was reborn in the T\u0101vati\u1e43sa abode in a golden celestial mansion twelve yojanas in extent. And there, as if awakening from sleep, seeing himself surrounded by a host of celestial nymphs, he reflected, 'Oh! I have indeed been reborn here. What kamma, I wonder, have I done?' Reflecting, he saw no other cause whatsoever apart from grasping the sign in the Blessed One's voice. At that very moment, he came together with his celestial mansion and worshipped the Blessed One\u2019s feet with his head. The Blessed One, although knowing, asked:",pt:"Diz-se que, enquanto o Aben\xe7oado ensinava o Dhamma aos habitantes de Camp\u0101 \xe0s margens do lago Gaggar\u0101, uma r\xe3 captou o sinal da voz do Aben\xe7oado. Um pastor de vacas, de p\xe9 e apoiado em seu cajado, pressionou-o sobre a cabe\xe7a da r\xe3. Ela morreu naquele mesmo instante e renasceu em uma mans\xe3o dourada de doze yojanas no c\xe9u de T\u0101vati\u1e43s\xe3. Despertando como se fosse de um sono, ao ver-se cercado por um grupo de ninfas celestiais, pensou: 'Ora, at\xe9 mesmo eu renasci aqui! Que boa a\xe7\xe3o realizei?'. Ao refletir, n\xe3o viu nenhuma outra causa sen\xe3o o ter captado o sinal da voz do Aben\xe7oado. Ele veio imediatamente com sua mans\xe3o e curvou a cabe\xe7a aos p\xe9s do Aben\xe7oado. O Aben\xe7oado, embora soubesse, perguntou:",es:"Se cuenta que mientras el Bienaventurado ense\xf1aba el Dhamma a los habitantes de la ciudad de Camp\u0101 a orillas del estanque Gaggar\u0101, una rana capt\xf3 el sonido de la voz del Bienaventurado como un objeto de meditaci\xf3n. En ese momento, un pastor que estaba all\xed apoyado sobre su vara la presion\xf3 sobre la cabeza de la rana mientras permanec\xeda de pie. La rana muri\xf3 instant\xe1neamente y renaci\xf3 en un palacio dorado de doce leguas en el reino de los Treinta y Tres Dioses. Al verse all\xed, rodeado por una multitud de ninfas celestiales, como quien despierta de un sue\xf1o, reflexion\xf3: '\xa1Vaya! He nacido aqu\xed, \xbfqu\xe9 acci\xf3n realic\xe9?', y no vio otra causa que el haber captado el sonido de la voz del Bienaventurado. Inmediatamente acudi\xf3 con su palacio celestial y postr\xf3 su cabeza a los pies del Bienaventurado. El Bienaventurado, aun sabi\xe9ndolo, le pregunt\xf3:"}},{id:"vism-7.11",pali:"Ya\u1e43 pana ki\xf1ci atthi \xf1eyya\u1e43 n\u0101ma, sabbasseva buddhatt\u0101 vimokkhantika\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47avasena buddho. Yasm\u0101 v\u0101 catt\u0101ri sacc\u0101ni attan\u0101pi bujjhi, a\xf1\xf1epi satte bodhesi, tasm\u0101 evam\u0101d\u012bhipi k\u0101ra\u1e47ehi buddho. Imassa ca panatthassa vi\xf1\xf1\u0101panattha\u1e43 \"bujjhit\u0101 sacc\u0101n\u012bti buddho. Bodhet\u0101 paj\u0101y\u0101ti buddho\"ti eva\u1e43 pavatto sabbopi niddesanayo pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101nayo v\u0101 vitth\u0101retabbo.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, whatever is called knowable, because he has understood all of it by means of the knowledge that culminates in final liberation, he is the Buddha. Or, because he himself understood the Four Truths and he causes other beings to understand them, for these and similar reasons he is the Buddha. And furthermore, to make this meaning known, this entire method of exposition from the Niddesa or the Pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101magga should be elaborated: 'Because he is one who has understood the truths, he is the Buddha. Because he is one who causes the populace to understand, he is the Buddha.'",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, tudo o que \xe9 cognosc\xedvel (\xf1eyya), por ele ter conhecido tudo isso por meio do conhecimento da liberta\xe7\xe3o final (vimokkhantika\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), ele \xe9 Buddho (o Desperto). Ou, porque ele mesmo compreendeu as Quatro Verdades e fez com que outros seres as compreendessem, por essas raz\xf5es tamb\xe9m ele \xe9 Buddho. Para esclarecer este significado, todo o m\xe9todo de exposi\xe7\xe3o do Niddesa ou do Pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101magga deve ser detalhado: 'Ele \xe9 Buddho porque \xe9 o conhecedor das Verdades. Ele \xe9 Buddho porque faz a gera\xe7\xe3o de seres compreend\xea-las'.",es:"En cuanto a todo lo que es cognoscible (\xf1eyya), se le llama 'Buddho' (el Despierto) porque lo ha comprendido todo mediante el conocimiento al final de la liberaci\xf3n. O bien, es 'Buddho' por tales razones: porque \xe9l mismo comprendi\xf3 las Cuatro Nobles Verdades y porque hace que otros seres las comprendan. Para dar a conocer este significado, debe detallarse todo el m\xe9todo de exposici\xf3n del Niddesa o del Pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101magga que dice: 'Es Buddho porque es el conocedor de las Verdades. Es Buddho porque es el despertador de la generaci\xf3n de seres'."}},{id:"vism-7.12",pali:"Ida\u1e43 t\u0101va buddh\u0101nussatiya\u1e43 vitth\u0101rakath\u0101mukha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"This, for now, is the introduction to the detailed exposition on the recollection of the Buddha.",pt:"Esta \xe9, primeiramente, a introdu\xe7\xe3o detalhada \xe0 recorda\xe7\xe3o do Buda (Buddh\u0101nussati).",es:"Hasta aqu\xed llega la introducci\xf3n a la explicaci\xf3n detallada sobre la recordaci\xf3n del Buddha."}},{id:"vism-7.13",pali:"Dhamm\u0101nussati\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101men\u0101pi rahogatena pa\u1e6disall\u012bnena \"sv\u0101kkh\u0101to bhagavat\u0101 dhammo sandi\u1e6d\u1e6dhiko ak\u0101liko ehipassiko opaneyyiko paccatta\u1e43 veditabbo vi\xf1\xf1\u016bh\u012b\"ti eva\u1e43 pariyattidhammassa ceva navavidhassa ca lokuttaradhammassa gu\u1e47\u0101 anussaritabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"By one who wishes to develop the recollection of the Dhamma, having gone to a secluded place and being in solitude, the qualities of both the scriptural Dhamma and the ninefold supramundane Dhamma should be recollected thus: 'Well-proclaimed is the Dhamma by the Blessed One, visible here and now, timeless, inviting one to come and see, leading onward, to be experienced by the wise for themselves.'",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Dhamma deve, tendo ido para um lugar solit\xe1rio e estando em retiro, recordar as qualidades tanto do Dhamma das escrituras (pariyatti) quanto do Dhamma supramundano de nove tipos (lokuttara), da seguinte maneira: 'O Dhamma \xe9 bem proclamado pelo Aben\xe7oado (sv\u0101kkh\u0101to bhagavat\u0101 dhammo), vis\xedvel aqui e agora (sandi\u1e6d\u1e6dhiko), imediato em seus resultados (ak\u0101liko), que convida a vir e ver (ehipassiko), digno de ser aplicado (opaneyyiko), para ser experimentado pessoalmente pelos s\xe1bios (paccatta\u1e43 veditabbo vi\xf1\xf1\u016bhi)'.",es:"Aquel que desee desarrollar la recordaci\xf3n del Dhamma, habi\xe9ndose retirado a la soledad y al recogimiento, debe recordar las cualidades tanto del Dhamma de las escrituras (pariyatti) como del Dhamma supramundano de nueve clases de la siguiente manera: 'El Dhamma ha sido bien proclamado por el Bienaventurado, es visible por uno mismo, inmediato, que invita a venir y ver, digno de ser aplicado y para ser realizado por los sabios, cada uno por s\xed mismo'."}},{id:"vism-7.14",pali:"Sv\u0101kkh\u0101toti imasmi\u1e43 hi pade pariyattidhammopi sa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 gacchati, itaresu lokuttaradhammova. Tattha pariyattidhammo t\u0101va sv\u0101kkh\u0101to \u0101dimajjhapariyos\u0101nakaly\u0101\u1e47att\u0101 s\u0101tthasabya\xf1janakevalaparipu\u1e47\u1e47aparisuddhabrahmacariyappak\u0101sanatt\u0101 ca. Ya\xf1hi bhagav\u0101 ekag\u0101thampi deseti, s\u0101 samantabhaddakatt\u0101 dhammassa pa\u1e6dhamap\u0101dena \u0101dikaly\u0101\u1e47\u0101, dutiyatatiyap\u0101dehi majjhekaly\u0101\u1e47\u0101, pacchimap\u0101dena pariyos\u0101nakaly\u0101\u1e47\u0101. Ek\u0101nusandhika\u1e43 sutta\u1e43 nid\u0101nena \u0101dikaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, nigamanena pariyos\u0101nakaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, sesena majjhekaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. N\u0101n\u0101nusandhika\u1e43 sutta\u1e43 pa\u1e6dham\u0101nusandhin\u0101 \u0101dikaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, pacchimena pariyos\u0101nakaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, sesehi majjhekaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Apica sanid\u0101nasauppattikatt\u0101 \u0101dikaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, veneyy\u0101na\u1e43 anur\u016bpato atthassa avipar\u012btat\u0101ya ca hetud\u0101hara\u1e47ayuttato ca majjhekaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, sot\u016bna\u1e43 saddh\u0101pa\u1e6dil\u0101bhajananena nigamanena ca pariyos\u0101nakaly\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Indeed, in this term 'well-proclaimed', the scriptural Dhamma is also included, whereas in the others, only the supramundane Dhamma is included. Therein, the scriptural Dhamma is 'well-proclaimed' because it is excellent in the beginning, excellent in the middle, and excellent in the end, and because it proclaims the holy life which is complete with meaning and phrasing, entirely complete, and utterly pure. For whatever single verse the Blessed One teaches, that verse\u2014because the Dhamma is good in all its parts\u2014is excellent in the beginning with the first line, excellent in the middle with the second and third lines, and excellent in the end with the final line. A discourse with a single connection is excellent in the beginning with its introduction, excellent in the end with its conclusion, and excellent in the middle with the remainder. A discourse with various connections is excellent in the beginning with the first connection, excellent in the end with the last, and excellent in the middle with the remaining ones. Furthermore, it is excellent in the beginning because it has an introduction and an origin story; excellent in the middle because of its suitability for the disciples, the non-perversion of its meaning, and its endowment with reason and example; and excellent in the end because it generates the acquisition of faith in the listeners and because of its conclusion.",pt:"Pois, no termo 'bem proclamado' (sv\u0101kkh\u0101to), o Dhamma das escrituras (pariyatti) tamb\xe9m est\xe1 inclu\xeddo; nos outros termos, apenas o Dhamma supramundano (lokuttara) est\xe1 inclu\xeddo. Entre eles, o Dhamma das escrituras \xe9 'bem proclamado' por ser excelente no in\xedcio, excelente no meio e excelente no fim, e por revelar a vida santa (brahmacariya) que \xe9 inteiramente completa, pura, com significado correto e formula\xe7\xe3o correta. De fato, mesmo que o Aben\xe7oado ensine apenas uma \xfanica estrofe, ela \xe9 excelente no in\xedcio com o primeiro verso, excelente no meio com o segundo e o terceiro versos, e excelente no fim com o \xfaltimo verso, devido \xe0 bondade geral do Dhamma. Um discurso com uma \xfanica conex\xe3o (ek\u0101nusandhika) \xe9 excelente no in\xedcio por sua introdu\xe7\xe3o (nid\u0101na), excelente no fim por sua conclus\xe3o (nigamana) e excelente no meio pelo restante. Um discurso com m\xfaltiplas conex\xf5es (n\u0101n\u0101nusandhika) \xe9 excelente no in\xedcio por sua primeira conex\xe3o, excelente no fim por sua \xfaltima conex\xe3o e excelente no meio pelas demais conex\xf5es. Al\xe9m disso, \xe9 excelente no in\xedcio por ser apresentado com sua origem e circunst\xe2ncias hist\xf3ricas; excelente no meio por ser adequado aos que devem ser guiados, pela infalibilidade de seu significado e por ser dotado de causas e ilustra\xe7\xf5es; e excelente no fim por gerar f\xe9 nos ouvintes e por sua conclus\xe3o.",es:"En el t\xe9rmino 'Sv\u0101kkh\u0101to' (bien expuesto), el Dhamma de las escrituras (pariyattidhamma) tambi\xe9n se incluye; en los otros cinco t\xe9rminos, se incluye \xfanicamente el Dhamma supramundano (lokuttaradhamma). En este contexto, el Dhamma de las escrituras es 'bien expuesto' por ser bueno en el inicio, bueno en el medio y bueno en el final, y por proclamar la vida santa (brahmacariya) que es enteramente completa y pura, dotada de sentido y de fraseo. En efecto, incluso cuando el Bendito ense\xf1a un solo verso, este es bueno en el inicio por su primer pie (p\u0101da), bueno en el medio por el segundo y tercer pie, y bueno en el final por el \xfaltimo pie, debido a la excelencia integral del Dhamma. Un discurso (sutta) de una sola conexi\xf3n es bueno en el inicio por su introducci\xf3n (nid\u0101na), bueno en el final por su conclusi\xf3n (nigamana), y bueno en el medio por el resto del texto. Un discurso de m\xfaltiples conexiones es bueno en el inicio por su primera conexi\xf3n, bueno en el final por la \xfaltima, y bueno en el medio por las conexiones restantes. Adem\xe1s, es bueno en el inicio por poseer una introducci\xf3n y un origen; es bueno en el medio por ser adecuado para los que deben ser guiados, por la exactitud de su significado y por estar provisto de razones y ejemplos; y es bueno en el final por generar la adquisici\xf3n de la fe en los oyentes y por su conclusi\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-7.15",pali:"Ida\u1e43 dhamm\u0101nussatiya\u1e43 vitth\u0101rakath\u0101mukha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"This is the introduction to the detailed explanation on the recollection of the Dhamma.",pt:"Esta \xe9 a introdu\xe7\xe3o detalhada \xe0 recorda\xe7\xe3o do Dhamma.",es:"Esta es la introducci\xf3n a la explicaci\xf3n detallada sobre el recuerdo del Dhamma."}},{id:"vism-7.16",pali:"Sa\u1e45gh\u0101nussati\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101men\u0101pi rahogatena pa\u1e6disall\u012bnena \"suppa\u1e6dipanno bhagavato s\u0101vakasa\u1e45gho, ujuppa\u1e6dipanno bhagavato s\u0101vakasa\u1e45gho, \xf1\u0101yappa\u1e6dipanno bhagavato s\u0101vakasa\u1e45gho, s\u0101m\u012bcippa\u1e6dipanno bhagavato s\u0101vakasa\u1e45gho, yadida\u1e43 catt\u0101ri purisayug\u0101ni a\u1e6d\u1e6dha purisapuggal\u0101, esa bhagavato s\u0101vakasa\u1e45gho \u0101huneyyo, p\u0101huneyyo, dakkhi\u1e47eyyo, a\xf1jalikara\u1e47\u012byo, anuttara\u1e43 pu\xf1\xf1akkhetta\u1e43 lokass\u0101\"ti eva\u1e43 ariyasa\u1e45ghagu\u1e47\u0101 anussaritabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"One who wishes to develop the recollection of the Sangha should, having gone to a solitary place and being in seclusion, recollect the qualities of the noble Sangha thus: \"The Sangha of the Blessed One's disciples is practicing the good way, practicing the straight way, practicing the way to Nibb\u0101na, practicing the proper way; that is, the four pairs of persons, the eight types of individuals\u2014this Sangha of the Blessed One's disciples is worthy of offerings, worthy of hospitality, worthy of gifts, worthy of reverential salutation, the unsurpassed field of merit for the world.\"",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver a recorda\xe7\xe3o da Sangha deve ir para um lugar solit\xe1rio, retirar-se em reclus\xe3o e recordar as qualidades da Nobre Sangha da seguinte maneira: 'A Sangha dos disc\xedpulos do Aben\xe7oado pratica o bom caminho (suppa\u1e6dipanno); a Sangha dos disc\xedpulos do Aben\xe7oado pratica o caminho reto (ujuppa\u1e6dipanno); a Sangha dos disc\xedpulos do Aben\xe7oado pratica o caminho verdadeiro (\xf1\u0101yappa\u1e6dipanno); a Sangha dos disc\xedpulos do Aben\xe7oado pratica o caminho adequado (s\u0101m\u012bcippa\u1e6dipanno). Isto \xe9, os quatro pares de homens, as oito pessoas individuais. Esta Sangha dos disc\xedpulos do Aben\xe7oado \xe9 digna de oferendas trazidas de longe (\u0101huneyyo), digna de hospitalidade (p\u0101huneyyo), digna de d\xe1divas (dakkhi\u1e47eyyo), digna de sauda\xe7\xe3o reverente com as m\xe3os unidas (a\xf1jalikara\u1e47\u012byo), o supremo campo de m\xe9rito para o mundo (anuttara\u1e43 pu\xf1\xf1akkhetta\u1e43 lokassa)'.",es:"Aquel que desee desarrollar el recuerdo de la Sangha, habi\xe9ndose retirado a la soledad y al aislamiento, debe rememorar las cualidades de la Noble Sangha de la siguiente manera: \xabLa comunidad de disc\xedpulos del Bienaventurado ha practicado correctamente, la comunidad de disc\xedpulos del Bienaventurado ha practicado rectamente, la comunidad de disc\xedpulos del Bienaventurado ha practicado para la realizaci\xf3n del Nibb\u0101na, la comunidad de disc\xedpulos del Bienaventurado ha practicado con propiedad; es decir, los cuatro pares de hombres, los ocho tipos de individuos; esta comunidad de disc\xedpulos del Bienaventurado es digna de ofrendas, es digna de hospitalidad, es digna de dones, es digna de saludo reverencial, es el campo de m\xe9rito insuperable para el mundo\xbb."}},{id:"vism-7.17",pali:"Tattha suppa\u1e6dipannoti su\u1e6d\u1e6dhu pa\u1e6dipanno, samm\u0101pa\u1e6dipada\u1e43 anivattipa\u1e6dipada\u1e43 anulomapa\u1e6dipada\u1e43 apaccan\u012bkapa\u1e6dipada\u1e43 dhamm\u0101nudhammapa\u1e6dipada\u1e43 pa\u1e6dipannoti vutta\u1e43 hoti. Bhagavato ov\u0101d\u0101nus\u0101sani\u1e43 sakkacca\u1e43 su\u1e47ant\u012bti s\u0101vak\u0101. S\u0101vak\u0101na\u1e43 sa\u1e45gho s\u0101vakasa\u1e45gho, s\u012bladi\u1e6d\u1e6dhis\u0101ma\xf1\xf1at\u0101ya sa\u1e45gh\u0101tabh\u0101vam\u0101panno s\u0101vakasam\u016bhoti attho. Yasm\u0101 pana s\u0101 samm\u0101pa\u1e6dipad\u0101 uju ava\u1e45k\u0101 aku\u1e6dil\u0101 ajimh\u0101, ariyo ca \xf1\u0101yotipi vuccati, anucchavikatt\u0101 ca s\u0101m\u012bc\u012btipi sa\u1e45kha\u1e43 gat\u0101. Tasm\u0101 tampa\u1e6dipanno ariyasa\u1e45gho ujuppa\u1e6dipanno \xf1\u0101yappa\u1e6dipanno s\u0101m\u012bcippa\u1e6dipannotipi vutto.",translations:{en:"Herein, regarding `suppa\u1e6dipanno`, it means one who has practiced well. It is said that one has practiced the right practice, the non-reverting practice, the conforming practice, the non-opposing practice, and the practice in accordance with the Dhamma. They are called `s\u0101vak\u0101` (disciples) because they listen respectfully to the Blessed One's advice and instruction. The community of disciples is the `s\u0101vakasa\u1e45gho`; the meaning is an assembly of disciples that has reached a state of being bound together due to the commonality of noble virtue and noble view. Furthermore, because that right practice is `uju` (straight), being not crooked, not bent, and not curved; and is also called `ariyo \xf1\u0101yo` (the noble methodical way); and has also come to be designated as `s\u0101m\u012bci` (proper) on account of its suitability, therefore the noble Sa\u1e45gha that has practiced it is also called `ujuppa\u1e6dipanno` (one who has practiced the straight way), `\xf1\u0101yappa\u1e6dipanno` (one who has practiced the methodical way), and `s\u0101m\u012bcippa\u1e6dipanno` (one who has practiced properly).",pt:"Nessa passagem, 'pratica o bom caminho' (suppa\u1e6dipanno) significa que eles praticam bem; ou seja, eles praticam o caminho correto, o caminho irrevers\xedvel, o caminho conforme, o caminho n\xe3o hostil, o caminho de acordo com o Dhamma. Aqueles que ouvem com respeito os conselhos e instru\xe7\xf5es do Aben\xe7oado s\xe3o chamados de disc\xedpulos (s\u0101vak\u0101). A comunidade de disc\xedpulos \xe9 a Sangha dos disc\xedpulos (s\u0101vakasa\u1e45gho), o que significa o grupo de disc\xedpulos que alcan\xe7ou a uni\xe3o devido \xe0 igualdade em virtude (s\u012bla) e vis\xe3o (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi). E como essa pr\xe1tica correta \xe9 reta (uju), n\xe3o tortuosa, n\xe3o curva, n\xe3o distorcida; e como \xe9 nobre, \xe9 tamb\xe9m chamada de 'verdadeira' (\xf1\u0101yo); e por ser apropriada, \xe9 tamb\xe9m conhecida como 'adequada' (s\u0101m\u012bc\u012b). Portanto, a Nobre Sangha que pratica esse caminho \xe9 descrita como aquela que pratica o caminho reto (ujuppa\u1e6dipanno), que pratica o caminho verdadeiro (\xf1\u0101yappa\u1e6dipanno) e que pratica o caminho adequado (s\u0101m\u012bcippa\u1e6dipanno).",es:"En ese pasaje, \xabpracticado correctamente\xbb (suppa\u1e6dipanno) significa que ha practicado excelentemente; se dice que ha practicado el sendero correcto, el sendero irreversible, el sendero conforme, el sendero no antagonista y el sendero que sigue al Dhamma. Se llaman \xabdisc\xedpulos\xbb (s\u0101vak\u0101) porque escuchan con respeto las instrucciones y ense\xf1anzas del Bienaventurado. La \xabcomunidad de disc\xedpulos\xbb es la Sangha de los disc\xedpulos; el significado es que es un grupo de disc\xedpulos que ha alcanzado el estado de uni\xf3n mediante la igualdad en la virtud y en la visi\xf3n. Ahora bien, puesto que ese sendero correcto es recto, sin dobleces ni desviaciones, se llama \xabrecto\xbb (uju). Tambi\xe9n se llama \xabm\xe9todo\xbb (\xf1\u0101ya) por ser noble y conducir al Nibb\u0101na. Y debido a su idoneidad, se conoce tambi\xe9n como \xabpropiedad\xbb (s\u0101m\u012bc\u012b). Por lo tanto, la Noble Sangha que ha practicado de esa manera es llamada \xabpracticante de la rectitud\xbb, \xabpracticante del m\xe9todo\xbb y \xabpracticante de la propiedad\xbb."}},{id:"vism-7.18",pali:"Ida\u1e43 sa\u1e45gh\u0101nussatiya\u1e43 vitth\u0101rakath\u0101mukha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"This is the introduction to the detailed discourse on the recollection of the Sangha.",pt:"Esta \xe9 a introdu\xe7\xe3o detalhada \xe0 recorda\xe7\xe3o do Sangha.",es:"Este es el inicio de la explicaci\xf3n detallada sobre el recuerdo del Sangha."}},{id:"vism-7.19",pali:"S\u012bl\u0101nussati\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena pana rahogatena pa\u1e6disall\u012bnena \"aho vata me s\u012bl\u0101ni akha\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101ni acchidd\u0101ni asabal\u0101ni akamm\u0101s\u0101ni bhujiss\u0101ni vi\xf1\xf1uppasatth\u0101ni apar\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ni sam\u0101dhisa\u1e43vattanik\u0101n\u012b\"ti eva\u1e43 akha\u1e47\u1e0dat\u0101digu\u1e47avasena attano s\u012bl\u0101ni anussaritabb\u0101ni. T\u0101ni ca gaha\u1e6d\u1e6dhena gaha\u1e6d\u1e6dhas\u012bl\u0101ni, pabbajitena pabbajitas\u012bl\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, one who wishes to develop the recollection of virtue should, having gone to a solitary place and being in seclusion, recollect one's own virtues by way of their qualities, beginning with being unbroken, thus: 'Oh, indeed my virtues are unbroken, without holes, unvariegated, unmottled, liberating, praised by the wise, unmisappropriated, and conducive to concentration.' And those virtues should be recollected by a householder as the householder's virtues, and by one who has gone forth as the virtues of one who has gone forth.",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver a recorda\xe7\xe3o da virtude, tendo ido para um lugar isolado e retirado, deve recordar suas pr\xf3prias virtudes por meio de suas qualidades, como a de ser inquebr\xe1vel, etc., da seguinte forma: 'Ah, que minhas virtudes sejam de fato inquebr\xe1veis, sem fendas, sem manchas, sem m\xe1culas, libertadoras, elogiadas pelos s\xe1bios, n\xe3o apegadas por desejo ou vis\xf5es e conducentes \xe0 concentra\xe7\xe3o'. E estas s\xe3o as virtudes de um leigo para um leigo, e as virtudes de um mon\xe1stico para um mon\xe1stico.",es:"Quien desee desarrollar el recuerdo de la virtud, retirado en un lugar solitario y en meditaci\xf3n, debe rememorar sus propias virtudes a trav\xe9s de sus cualidades, como el ser \xedntegras y dem\xe1s, de esta manera: \"\xa1Oh, mis virtudes son verdaderamente \xedntegras, sin fisuras, sin manchas, sin motas, liberadoras, elogiadas por los sabios, no aferradas y conducentes a la concentraci\xf3n!\". Estas son las virtudes del laico para el laico, y las virtudes del monje para el monje."}},{id:"vism-7.20",pali:"Gaha\u1e6d\u1e6dhas\u012bl\u0101ni v\u0101 hontu pabbajitas\u012bl\u0101ni v\u0101, yesa\u1e43 \u0101dimhi v\u0101 ante v\u0101 ekampi na bhinna\u1e43, t\u0101ni pariyante chinnas\u0101\u1e6dako viya na kha\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101n\u012bti akha\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101ni. Yesa\u1e43 vemajjhe ekampi na bhinna\u1e43, t\u0101ni majjhe vinividdhas\u0101\u1e6dako viya na chidd\u0101n\u012bti acchidd\u0101ni. Yesa\u1e43 pa\u1e6dip\u0101\u1e6diy\u0101 dve v\u0101 t\u012b\u1e47i v\u0101 na bhinn\u0101ni, t\u0101ni pi\u1e6d\u1e6dhiy\u0101 v\u0101 kucchiy\u0101 v\u0101 u\u1e6d\u1e6dhitena d\u012bghava\u1e6d\u1e6d\u0101disa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101nena visabh\u0101gava\u1e47\u1e47ena k\u0101\u1e37aratt\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1atarasar\u012brava\u1e47\u1e47\u0101 g\u0101v\u012b viya na sabal\u0101n\u012bti asabal\u0101ni. Y\u0101ni antarantar\u0101 na bhinn\u0101ni, t\u0101ni visabh\u0101gabinduvicitr\u0101 g\u0101v\u012b viya na kamm\u0101s\u0101n\u012bti akamm\u0101s\u0101ni. Avisesena v\u0101 sabb\u0101nipi sattavidhena methunasa\u1e43yogena kodhupan\u0101h\u0101d\u012bhi ca p\u0101padhammehi anupahatatt\u0101 akha\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101ni acchidd\u0101ni asabal\u0101ni akamm\u0101s\u0101ni. T\u0101niyeva ta\u1e47h\u0101d\u0101sabyato mocetv\u0101 bhujissabh\u0101vakara\u1e47ena bhujiss\u0101ni. Buddh\u0101d\u012bhi vi\xf1\xf1\u016bhi pasatthatt\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1uppasatth\u0101ni. Ta\u1e47h\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u012bhi apar\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dhat\u0101ya kenaci v\u0101 aya\u1e43 te s\u012blesu dosoti eva\u1e43 par\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dhu\u1e43 asakku\u1e47eyyat\u0101ya apar\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ni. Upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi\u1e43 appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi\u1e43 v\u0101, atha v\u0101 pana maggasam\u0101dhi\u1e43 phalasam\u0101dhi\xf1c\u0101pi sa\u1e43vattent\u012bti sam\u0101dhisa\u1e43vattanik\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"Whether they are the virtues of a householder or the virtues of one gone forth, those in which not even one is broken at the beginning or at the end are unbroken (akha\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101ni), like a cloth not torn at its edges. Those in which not even one is broken in the middle are unperforated (acchidd\u0101ni), like a cloth not pierced in the middle. Those in which two or three are not broken in sequence are unspotted (asabal\u0101ni), like a cow whose body is not marked with patches of a dissimilar color\u2014such as black or dark red\u2014of a long or round shape appearing on its back or belly. Those which are not broken here and there are undappled (akamm\u0101s\u0101ni), like a cow not variegated with spots of a dissimilar color. Alternatively, all of them, without distinction, are unbroken, unperforated, unspotted, and undappled because they are undamaged by the seven kinds of sexual union and by evil states such as anger and resentment. These same virtues are liberating (bhujiss\u0101ni) because they free one from the slavery of craving and make one a free person. They are praised by the wise (vi\xf1\xf1uppasatth\u0101ni) because they are praised by the wise, such as the Buddhas. They are untouched (apar\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ni) because they are not grasped by craving and wrong view, or because no one can find fault with them by saying, \u201cThis is a fault in your virtues.\u201d They are conducive to concentration (sam\u0101dhisa\u1e43vattanik\u0101ni) because they lead to access concentration or absorption concentration, or even to path concentration and fruition concentration.",pt:"Sejam as virtudes de um leigo ou de um mon\xe1stico, aquelas das quais nenhuma regra \xe9 quebrada no in\xedcio ou no fim n\xe3o s\xe3o fragmentadas como uma veste rasgada nas bordas, sendo, portanto, chamadas de 'inquebr\xe1veis' (akha\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101ni). Aquelas das quais nenhuma regra \xe9 quebrada no meio n\xe3o t\xeam furos como uma veste perfurada no centro, sendo chamadas de 'sem fendas' (acchidd\u0101ni). Aquelas das quais duas ou tr\xeas regras consecutivas n\xe3o s\xe3o quebradas n\xe3o s\xe3o malhadas como uma vaca que possui manchas de cores contrastantes, pretas ou vermelhas, de formato longo ou redondo no lombo ou no ventre, sendo chamadas de 'sem manchas' (asabal\u0101ni). Aquelas que n\xe3o s\xe3o quebradas aqui e ali n\xe3o s\xe3o salpicadas como uma vaca variegada com pontos de cores diferentes, sendo chamadas de 'sem m\xe1culas' (akamm\u0101s\u0101ni). Ou, de modo geral, todas elas s\xe3o inquebr\xe1veis, sem fendas, sem manchas e sem m\xe1culas por n\xe3o serem danificadas pelos sete tipos de uni\xe3o sexual e por estados mentais prejudiciais como a raiva e a malevol\xeancia. Essas mesmas virtudes s\xe3o 'libertadoras' (bhujiss\u0101ni) porque libertam a pessoa da escravid\xe3o do desejo, tornando-a livre. S\xe3o 'elogiadas pelos s\xe1bios' (vi\xf1\xf1uppasatth\u0101ni) por serem louvadas pelo Buda e por outros s\xe1bios. S\xe3o 'n\xe3o apegadas' (apar\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ni) por n\xe3o serem contaminadas pelo desejo e por vis\xf5es incorretas, ou porque ningu\xe9m pode critic\xe1-las dizendo: 'este \xe9 um defeito em sua virtude'. S\xe3o 'conducentes \xe0 concentra\xe7\xe3o' (sam\u0101dhisa\u1e43vattanik\u0101ni) porque geram a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso ou a concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o, ou ainda a concentra\xe7\xe3o do caminho e do fruto.",es:"Ya sean virtudes de laico o de monje, aquellas en las que no se ha quebrantado ni un solo precepto al principio ni al final se llaman \"\xedntegras\" (akhandani), como una vestidura que no est\xe1 rota en los bordes. Aquellas en las que ni uno solo se ha roto en el medio se llaman \"sin fisuras\" (acchiddani), como una vestidura que no est\xe1 perforada en el centro. Aquellas en las que dos o tres no se han roto en sucesi\xf3n se llaman \"sin manchas\" (asabalani), a diferencia de una vaca cuyo cuerpo presenta un color distinto en forma de franja larga o c\xedrculo en el lomo o el vientre. Las que no est\xe1n rotas aqu\xed y all\xe1 se llaman \"sin motas\" (akamm\u0101s\u0101ni), a diferencia de una vaca moteada con manchas de colores diversos. O, en general, todas ellas son \xedntegras, sin fisuras, sin manchas y sin motas por no haber sido da\xf1adas por los siete tipos de uni\xf3n sexual ni por estados malvados como la ira y la enemistad. Estas mismas virtudes son \"liberadoras\" (bhujissani) por liberar de la esclavitud del deseo. Son \"elogiadas por los sabios\" (vi\xf1\xf1uppasatth\u0101ni) por ser alabadas por sabios como los Buddhas. Son \"no aferradas\" (apar\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ni) por no ser asidas por el deseo o los puntos de vista, o porque nadie puede atacarlas diciendo: \"Este es un defecto en tus virtudes\". Son \"conducentes a la concentraci\xf3n\" (sam\u0101dhisa\u1e43vattanik\u0101ni) porque originan la concentraci\xf3n de acceso o la de absorci\xf3n, o bien la concentraci\xf3n del sendero y la del fruto."}},{id:"vism-7.21",pali:"C\u0101g\u0101nussati\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena pana pakatiy\u0101 c\u0101g\u0101dhimuttena niccappavattad\u0101nasa\u1e43vibh\u0101gena bhavitabba\u1e43. Atha v\u0101 pana bh\u0101vana\u1e43 \u0101rabhantena ito d\u0101ni pabhuti sati pa\u1e6digg\u0101hake antamaso ek\u0101lopamattampi d\u0101na\u1e43 adatv\u0101 na bhu\xf1jiss\u0101m\u012bti sam\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 katv\u0101 ta\u1e43divasa\u1e43 gu\u1e47avisi\u1e6d\u1e6dhesu pa\u1e6digg\u0101hakesu yath\u0101satti yath\u0101bala\u1e43 d\u0101na\u1e43 datv\u0101 tattha nimitta\u1e43 ga\u1e47hitv\u0101 rahogatena pa\u1e6disall\u012bnena \"l\u0101bh\u0101 vata me suladdha\u1e43 vata me, yoha\u1e43 maccheramalapariyu\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101ya paj\u0101ya vigatamalamaccherena cetas\u0101 vihar\u0101mi muttac\u0101go payatap\u0101\u1e47i vossaggarato y\u0101cayogo d\u0101nasa\u1e43vibh\u0101garato\"ti eva\u1e43 vigatamalamaccherat\u0101digu\u1e47avasena attano c\u0101go anussaritabbo.",translations:{en:"One who wishes to develop the recollection of generosity should, by nature, be inclined towards generosity, constantly engaged in giving and sharing. Alternatively, when beginning the development, one should make the resolution: \u201cFrom this day forward, if there is a recipient, I will not eat without first giving a gift of at least a small morsel.\u201d On that day, one should give according to one\u2019s capacity and strength to recipients distinguished by virtue, then take that as the object for recollection. Having gone into solitude and seclusion, one should recollect one\u2019s own generosity by way of its qualities, such as being free from the stain of stinginess, thus: \u201cTruly, it is a gain for me, truly it is well-gained by me, that I, among a populace overwhelmed by the stain of stinginess, dwell with a mind free from the stain of stinginess\u2014with liberated generosity, with hands ready to give, delighting in relinquishment, fit to be requested, and rejoicing in giving and sharing.\u201d",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver a recorda\xe7\xe3o da generosidade deve, por natureza, ser inclinado \xe0 doa\xe7\xe3o e \xe0 partilha, mantendo uma pr\xe1tica constante de dar e distribuir. Ou ent\xe3o, ao iniciar o desenvolvimento, deve fazer a seguinte resolu\xe7\xe3o: 'A partir de hoje, se houver um receptor presente, n\xe3o comerei sem antes ter feito uma doa\xe7\xe3o, mesmo que seja de apenas um bocado de comida'. Tendo feito essa resolu\xe7\xe3o, naquele dia, deve dar uma doa\xe7\xe3o de acordo com sua capacidade e for\xe7a a receptores que se destacam por suas virtudes e, tendo fixado a marca dessa doa\xe7\xe3o, em um lugar isolado e retirado, deve recordar: '\xc9 um ganho para mim, \xe9 uma grande b\xean\xe7\xe3o para mim, que em meio a seres dominados pela m\xe1cula da avareza, eu viva com a mente livre da m\xe1cula da avareza, generoso, de m\xe3os abertas, deleitando-me em renunciar, acess\xedvel aos pedidos, comprazendo-me em dar e compartilhar'. Assim, deve-se recordar a pr\xf3pria generosidade por meio de suas qualidades, como a de ser livre da m\xe1cula da avareza.",es:"Quien desee desarrollar el recuerdo de la generosidad debe estar naturalmente inclinado a la renuncia y ser constante en la pr\xe1ctica de dar y compartir. O bien, quien comienza el desarrollo debe hacer este compromiso: \"A partir de hoy, mientras haya un receptor, no comer\xe9 ni siquiera un bocado sin haber dado una ofrenda\". Habiendo hecho tal compromiso, en el d\xeda de practicar la meditaci\xf3n, debe dar una ofrenda seg\xfan su capacidad y fuerza a receptores distinguidos por sus virtudes. Habiendo tomado eso como un objeto de atenci\xf3n, retirado en un lugar solitario y en meditaci\xf3n, debe rememorar su propia generosidad mediante sus cualidades, como la ausencia de la mancha de la taca\xf1er\xeda: \"Es una ganancia para m\xed, es una gran ganancia para m\xed, que en medio de una poblaci\xf3n obsesionada por la mancha de la taca\xf1er\xeda, yo viva con una mente libre de ella, generoso, deleit\xe1ndome en el desapego, dispuesto a la caridad, deleit\xe1ndome en dar y compartir\"."}},{id:"vism-7.22",pali:"Devat\u0101nussati\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena pana ariyamaggavasena samud\u0101gatehi saddh\u0101d\u012bhi gu\u1e47ehi samann\u0101gatena bhavitabba\u1e43. Tato rahogatena pa\u1e6disall\u012bnena \"santi dev\u0101 c\u0101tumah\u0101r\u0101jik\u0101, santi dev\u0101 t\u0101vati\u1e43s\u0101, y\u0101m\u0101, tusit\u0101, nimm\u0101naratino, paranimmitavasavattino, santi dev\u0101 brahmak\u0101yik\u0101, santi dev\u0101 tatuttari, yath\u0101r\u016bp\u0101ya saddh\u0101ya samann\u0101gat\u0101 t\u0101 devat\u0101 ito cut\u0101 tattha upapann\u0101, mayhampi tath\u0101r\u016bp\u0101 saddh\u0101 sa\u1e43vijjati. Yath\u0101r\u016bpena s\u012blena. Yath\u0101r\u016bpena sutena. Yath\u0101r\u016bpena c\u0101gena. Yath\u0101r\u016bp\u0101ya pa\xf1\xf1\u0101ya samann\u0101gat\u0101 t\u0101 devat\u0101 ito cut\u0101 tattha upapann\u0101, mayhampi tath\u0101r\u016bp\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 sa\u1e43vijjat\u012b\"ti eva\u1e43 devat\u0101 sakkhi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 attano saddh\u0101digu\u1e47\u0101 anussaritabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Now, one who wishes to develop the recollection of devas should be endowed with the qualities beginning with faith, which have arisen by means of the noble path. Then, having gone to a secluded place and being withdrawn, one should recollect: 'There are the C\u0101tumah\u0101r\u0101jika devas, there are the T\u0101vati\u1e43sa devas, the Y\u0101ma devas, the Tusita devas, the Nimm\u0101narat\u012b devas, the Paranimmitavasavatt\u012b devas, the Brahmak\u0101yika devas, and devas beyond them. Those devas, endowed with faith of such a nature, having passed away from here, were reborn there; for me too, faith of such a nature exists. Those devas, endowed with virtue of such a nature, with learning of such a nature, with generosity of such a nature, and with wisdom of such a nature, having passed away from here, were reborn there; for me too, wisdom of such a nature exists.' Thus, having placed the devas in the position of a witness, one's own qualities beginning with faith should be recollected.",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver a recorda\xe7\xe3o dos devas deve possuir as qualidades de f\xe9, etc., que surgiram por meio do nobre caminho. Ent\xe3o, tendo ido para um lugar isolado e retirado, deve recordar: 'Existem os devas do Reino dos Quatro Reis Grandes, existem os devas do Reino dos Trinta e Tr\xeas, os devas Y\u0101ma, os devas Tusita, os devas que se deleitam na cria\xe7\xe3o, os devas que controlam as cria\xe7\xf5es alheias, existem os devas do reino de Brahma, existem devas al\xe9m desses. Dotados de tal f\xe9, esses devas faleceram daqui e renasceram l\xe1; tal f\xe9 tamb\xe9m se encontra em mim. Dotados de tal virtude... de tal aprendizado... de tal generosidade... de tal sabedoria, esses devas faleceram daqui e renasceram l\xe1; tal sabedoria tamb\xe9m se encontra em mim'. Assim, colocando os devas na posi\xe7\xe3o de testemunhas, o praticante deve recordar suas pr\xf3prias qualidades de f\xe9, etc.",es:"Aquel que desea desarrollar el recuerdo de las deidades debe poseer cualidades como la fe, etc., que han surgido mediante el Sendero Noble. Luego, habi\xe9ndose retirado a la soledad y al recogimiento, debe reflexionar: 'Existen las deidades de los Cuatro Grandes Reyes, existen las deidades de los Treinta y Tres, las deidades Yama, las Tusita, las Nimmanarati, las Paranimmitavasavatti, las deidades del s\xe9quito de Brahma, y existen deidades m\xe1s all\xe1 de esas. Poseyendo tal fe, esas deidades fallecieron de este mundo y renacieron all\xed; tal fe tambi\xe9n existe en m\xed. Poseyendo tal virtud... tal conocimiento... tal generosidad... poseyendo tal sabidur\xeda, esas deidades fallecieron de este mundo y renacieron all\xed; tal sabidur\xeda tambi\xe9n existe en m\xed' (A.N. 6.10). De esta manera, poniendo a las deidades como testigos, uno debe recordar sus propias virtudes de fe, etc."}},{id:"vism-7.23",pali:"Ya\u1e43 pana et\u0101sa\u1e43 vitth\u0101radesan\u0101ya\u1e43 \"ujugatamevassa tasmi\u1e43 samaye citta\u1e43 hoti tath\u0101gata\u1e43 \u0101rabbh\u0101\"ti\u0101d\u012bni vatv\u0101 \"ujugatacitto kho pana, mah\u0101n\u0101ma, ariyas\u0101vako labhati atthaveda\u1e43, labhati dhammaveda\u1e43, labhati dhamm\u016bpasa\u1e43hita\u1e43 p\u0101mojja\u1e43, pamuditassa p\u012bti j\u0101yat\u012b\"ti vutta\u1e43, tattha itipi so bhagav\u0101ti\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 attha\u1e43 niss\u0101ya uppanna\u1e43 tu\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e43 sandh\u0101ya labhati atthavedanti vutta\u1e43. P\u0101\u1e37i\u1e43 niss\u0101ya uppanna\u1e43 tu\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e43 sandh\u0101ya labhati dhammaveda\u1e43. Ubhayavasena labhati dhamm\u016bpasa\u1e43hita\u1e43 p\u0101mojjanti vuttanti veditabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"In the detailed exposition where it is said, \"At that time, his mind is quite upright towards the Tath\u0101gata,\" and further, \"The noble disciple with an upright mind, Mah\u0101n\u0101ma, gains understanding of the meaning, gains understanding of the Dhamma, gains joy associated with the Dhamma, and for one who is joyful, rapture arises\"\u2014here, 'gains understanding of the meaning' is said with reference to the satisfaction arising in dependence on the meaning of phrases such as 'Indeed, the Blessed One...' 'Gains understanding of the Dhamma' refers to the satisfaction arising in dependence on the Pali text. 'Gains joy associated with the Dhamma' should be understood as being said as arising from both aspects.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, no que diz respeito \xe0 exposi\xe7\xe3o detalhada destas [seis recorda\xe7\xf5es], onde foi dito: 'Naquele momento, a mente daquele [nobre disc\xedpulo] torna-se reta, tendo o Tath\u0101gata como objeto...' e assim por diante, e depois: 'O nobre disc\xedpulo de mente reta, Mah\u0101n\u0101ma, obt\xe9m a compreens\xe3o do significado (atthaveda), obt\xe9m a compreens\xe3o do Dhamma (dhammaveda), obt\xe9m o contentamento associado ao Dhamma; naquele que est\xe1 contente, nasce o \xeaxtase' (AN 6.10); deve-se entender que, nessa passagem, a express\xe3o 'obt\xe9m a compreens\xe3o do significado' (labhati atthaveda\u1e43) foi dita em refer\xeancia ao contentamento que surge baseado no significado de termos como 'Itipi so bhagav\u0101' (Assim \xe9 o Aben\xe7oado...). 'Obt\xe9m a compreens\xe3o do Dhamma' (labhati dhammaveda\u1e43) foi dito em refer\xeancia ao contentamento que surge baseado no texto em si (Pali). E 'obt\xe9m o contentamento associado ao Dhamma' foi dito em virtude de ambos.",es:"Sin embargo, en la ense\xf1anza detallada de estas seis recordaciones, despu\xe9s de haber dicho: \u2018En ese momento, la mente [del meditador] est\xe1 ciertamente recta, inspirada en el Tath\u0101gata\u2019, etc., se dice: \u2018Mah\u0101n\u0101ma, el noble disc\xedpulo con la mente recta obtiene la inspiraci\xf3n en el significado (atthaveda), obtiene la inspiraci\xf3n en el Dhamma (dhammaveda), obtiene el j\xfabilo asociado con el Dhamma; en aquel que est\xe1 jubiloso, nace el rapto (p\u0126ti)\u2019 (A. ni. 6.10). En ese pasaje, debe entenderse que se dice \u2018obtiene la inspiraci\xf3n en el significado\u2019 refiri\xe9ndose a la satisfacci\xf3n nacida con base en el significado de los t\xe9rminos como \u2018Itipi so bhagav\u0101\u2019, etc. Se dice \u2018obtiene la inspiraci\xf3n en el Dhamma\u2019 refiri\xe9ndose a la satisfacci\xf3n nacida con base en el texto de la ense\xf1anza (P\u0101\u1137i). Y se dice \u2018obtiene el j\xfabilo asociado con el Dhamma\u2019 bas\xe1ndose en ambos aspectos."}}]},425,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,n,i,t,s){i.exports=[{id:"vism-8.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni ito anantar\u0101ya mara\u1e47assatiy\u0101 bh\u0101van\u0101niddeso anuppatto. Tattha mara\u1e47anti ekabhavapariy\u0101pannassa j\u012bvitindriyassa upacchedo. Ya\u1e43 paneta\u1e43 arahant\u0101na\u1e43 va\u1e6d\u1e6dadukkhasamucchedasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 samucchedamara\u1e47a\u1e43, sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101na\u1e43 kha\u1e47abha\u1e45gasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 kha\u1e47ikamara\u1e47a\u1e43, rukkho mato loha\u1e43 matanti\u0101d\u012bsu sammutimara\u1e47a\xf1ca, na ta\u1e43 idha adhippeta\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now, immediately following this, the explanation of the development of mindfulness of death is taken up. Therein, \u201cdeath\u201d is the cutting off of the life faculty that is included within a single existence. However, that which is the \u201cdeath by cutting off\u201d of the arahants, reckoned as the complete cutting off of the suffering of the round of existence; that which is the \u201cmomentary death,\u201d reckoned as the dissolution of formations at every moment; and that which is \u201cconventional death\u201d in expressions such as \u201cthe tree is dead,\u201d \u201cthe metal is dead,\u201d and so on\u2014these are not intended here.",pt:"Id\u0101ni, logo ap\xf3s esta [recorda\xe7\xe3o das divindades], chegou a vez da exposi\xe7\xe3o do desenvolvimento da recorda\xe7\xe3o da morte. Ali, 'morte' significa a interrup\xe7\xe3o da faculdade da vida (j\u012bvitindriya) contida em uma \xfanica exist\xeancia. No entanto, o que \xe9 chamado de 'morte por corte total' (samucchedamara\u1e47a), que consiste no corte total do sofrimento do ciclo de renascimentos para os arahants; a 'morte moment\xe2nea' (kha\u1e47ikamara\u1e47a), que consiste na dissolu\xe7\xe3o momento a momento das forma\xe7\xf5es (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra); e a 'morte convencional' (sammutimara\u1e47a), como nas express\xf5es 'a \xe1rvore morreu', 'o metal morreu', etc. \u2014 nenhuma dessas \xe9 o que se pretende aqui.",es:"Ahora sigue la explicaci\xf3n del desarrollo de la recordaci\xf3n de la muerte, que viene inmediatamente despu\xe9s de la recordaci\xf3n de las deidades. En ella, \u2018muerte\u2019 significa el corte de la facultad de la vida (j\u0126vitindriya) comprendida dentro de una sola existencia. Sin embargo, no se refiere aqu\xed a la \u2018muerte por aniquilaci\xf3n\u2019 (samucchedamara\u1147a), que es la cesaci\xf3n total del sufrimiento de la ronda para los Arahants; ni a la \u2018muerte moment\xe1nea\u2019 (kha\u1147ikamara\u1147a), que es la disoluci\xf3n de las formaciones en cada momento; ni a la \u2018muerte convencional\u2019 (sammutimara\u1147a), como en expresiones como \u2018el \xe1rbol ha muerto\u2019 o \u2018el metal ha muerto\u2019."}},{id:"vism-8.2",pali:"Yampi ceta\u1e43 adhippeta\u1e43, ta\u1e43 k\u0101lamara\u1e47a\u1e43 ak\u0101lamara\u1e47anti duvidha\u1e43 hoti. Tattha k\u0101lamara\u1e47a\u1e43 pu\xf1\xf1akkhayena v\u0101 \u0101yukkhayena v\u0101 ubhayakkhayena v\u0101 hoti. Ak\u0101lamara\u1e47a\u1e43 kammupacchedakakammavasena.",translations:{en:"And this death which is intended is of two kinds: timely death and untimely death. Therein, timely death occurs through the exhaustion of merit, through the exhaustion of lifespan, or through the exhaustion of both. Untimely death occurs by the force of kamma that cuts off kamma.",pt:"E esta morte que se pretende aqui \xe9 de dois tipos: morte no tempo devido (k\u0101lamara\u1e47a) e morte fora do tempo devido (ak\u0101lamara\u1e47a). Entre elas, a morte no tempo devido ocorre pela exaust\xe3o do m\xe9rito (pu\xf1\xf1akkhaya), pela exaust\xe3o do tempo de vida (\u0101yukkhaya) ou pela exaust\xe3o de ambos. A morte fora do tempo devido ocorre por meio de um kamma interruptor (upacchedakakamma).",es:"Y esta [muerte] que aqu\xed se pretende es de dos clases: muerte oportuna (k\u0101lamara\u1147a) y muerte inoportuna (ak\u0101lamara\u1147a). De ellas, la muerte oportuna ocurre por el agotamiento del m\xe9rito, por el agotamiento de la duraci\xf3n de la vida, o por el agotamiento de ambos. La muerte inoportuna ocurre por la acci\xf3n de un kamma que corta [el kamma que produce los resultados de la vida]."}},{id:"vism-8.3",pali:"Ta\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena rahogatena pa\u1e6disall\u012bnena \"mara\u1e47a\u1e43 bhavissati, j\u012bvitindriya\u1e43 upacchijjissat\u012b\"ti v\u0101, \"mara\u1e47a\u1e43 mara\u1e47a\"nti v\u0101 yoniso manasik\u0101ro pavattetabbo. Ayoniso pavattayato hi i\u1e6d\u1e6dhajanamara\u1e47\u0101nussara\u1e47e soko uppajjati vij\u0101tam\u0101tuy\u0101 piyaputtamara\u1e47\u0101nussara\u1e47e viya. Ani\u1e6d\u1e6dhajanamara\u1e47\u0101nussara\u1e47e p\u0101mojja\u1e43 uppajjati ver\u012bna\u1e43 verimara\u1e47\u0101nussara\u1e47e viya. Majjhattajanamara\u1e47\u0101nussara\u1e47e sa\u1e43vego na uppajjati mataka\u1e37evaradassane chava\u1e0d\u0101hakassa viya. Attano mara\u1e47\u0101nussara\u1e47e sant\u0101so uppajjati ukkhitt\u0101sika\u1e43 vadhaka\u1e43 disv\u0101 bh\u012brukaj\u0101tikassa viya. Tadeta\u1e43 sabbampi satisa\u1e43vega\xf1\u0101\u1e47avirahato hoti. Tasm\u0101 tattha tattha hatamatasatte oloketv\u0101 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhapubbasampatt\u012bna\u1e43 satt\u0101na\u1e43 mat\u0101na\u1e43 mara\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101vajjetv\u0101 sati\xf1ca sa\u1e43vega\xf1ca \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1ca yojetv\u0101 \"mara\u1e47a\u1e43 bhavissat\u012b\"ti\u0101din\u0101 nayena manasik\u0101ro pavattetabbo. Eva\u1e43 pavattento hi yoniso pavatteti, up\u0101yena pavattet\u012bti attho. Eva\u1e43 pavattayatoyeva hi ekaccassa n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101ni vikkhambhanti, mara\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101 sati sa\u1e47\u1e6dh\u0101ti, upac\u0101rappattameva kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"By one who wishes to develop this, having gone to a secluded place and being in solitude, attention should be wisely aroused thus: 'Death will be, the life-faculty will be cut off,' or 'Death, death.' For if one arouses it unwisely, sorrow arises when recollecting the death of a loved one, like a mother recollecting the death of her beloved son. Joy arises when recollecting the death of an unloved person, like recollecting the death of an enemy. A sense of urgency does not arise when recollecting the death of a neutral person, like a corpse-burner seeing a dead body. Terror arises when recollecting one's own death, like a timid person seeing an executioner with an upraised sword. All this occurs due to the absence of mindfulness, sense of urgency, and knowledge. Therefore, having observed here and there beings who have been killed or have died, and having reflected upon the death of beings formerly seen in possession of prosperity, one should combine mindfulness, sense of urgency, and knowledge, and arouse attention by the method beginning with, 'Death will be.' Indeed, one who proceeds in this way, proceeds wisely; the meaning is that one proceeds by a suitable method. For a certain person who proceeds in this way, the hindrances are suppressed, mindfulness with death as its object is established, and the meditation subject reaches access concentration.",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolv\xea-la deve ir para um lugar solit\xe1rio e, em retiro, aplicar a aten\xe7\xe3o s\xe1bia (yoniso manasik\u0101ra) da seguinte forma: 'A morte ocorrer\xe1, a faculdade da vida ser\xe1 interrompida', ou 'Morte, morte'. Pois, para quem aplica a aten\xe7\xe3o de forma inadequada (ayoniso), surge o pesar ao recordar a morte de uma pessoa querida, como no caso de uma m\xe3e que recorda a morte de seu filho amado. Ao recordar a morte de uma pessoa indesejada, surge a alegria, como no caso de inimigos que recordam a morte de seu inimigo. Ao recordar a morte de uma pessoa neutra, n\xe3o surge o senso de urg\xeancia (sa\u1e43vega), como no caso de um coveiro que v\xea um cad\xe1ver. Ao recordar a pr\xf3pria morte, surge o pavor, como no caso de uma pessoa covarde que v\xea um carrasco com a espada erguida. Tudo isso ocorre devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de aten\xe7\xe3o plena, senso de urg\xeancia e conhecimento. Portanto, deve-se observar pessoas mortas ou assassinadas aqui e ali, refletir sobre a morte de seres que outrora possu\xedam prosperidade vis\xedvel, e aplicando a aten\xe7\xe3o plena, o senso de urg\xeancia e o conhecimento, deve-se direcionar a mente da seguinte maneira: 'A morte ocorrer\xe1', e assim por diante. Aquele que direciona a mente dessa forma, direciona-a com aten\xe7\xe3o s\xe1bia, ou seja, de maneira adequada. E para quem direciona a mente dessa forma, os obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47a) s\xe3o suprimidos, a aten\xe7\xe3o plena tendo a morte como objeto se estabelece firmemente, e o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o alcan\xe7a o n\xedvel de acesso (upac\u0101ra).",es:"Aquel que desee cultivarla, debe retirarse a un lugar solitario y, en reclusi\xf3n, aplicar la atenci\xf3n sabia (yoniso manasik\u0101ra) de la siguiente manera: 'La muerte ocurrir\xe1, la facultad vital se interrumpir\xe1' o simplemente 'muerte, muerte'. En efecto, para quien aplica la atenci\xf3n de manera no sabia (ayoniso), surge el dolor al recordar la muerte de una persona querida, como el dolor de una madre que recuerda la muerte de su amado hijo. Al recordar la muerte de una persona no deseada (un enemigo), surge la alegr\xeda, como la alegr\xeda de los enemigos al recordar la muerte de su rival. Al recordar la muerte de una persona indiferente, no surge el sentido de urgencia (sa\u1e43vega), como el enterrador que mira un cad\xe1ver. Al recordar la propia muerte, surge el terror, como el terror que siente una persona cobarde al ver a un verdugo con la espada en alto. Todo esto ocurre por la ausencia de atenci\xf3n plena (sati), de urgencia espiritual (sa\u1e43vega) y de conocimiento (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a). Por lo tanto, uno debe observar a los seres que han muerto en diversos lugares, reflexionar sobre la muerte de seres que anteriormente gozaban de prosperidad y, uniendo la atenci\xf3n, el sentido de urgencia y el conocimiento, aplicar la reflexi\xf3n del modo: 'La muerte ocurrir\xe1'. Al proceder as\xed, se dice que aplica la atenci\xf3n con sabidur\xeda y mediante el m\xe9todo correcto. Para quien reflexiona de esta manera, los obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101ni) se suprimen, la atenci\xf3n se establece firmemente en el objeto de la muerte y el tema de meditaci\xf3n alcanza el nivel de concentraci\xf3n de acceso (upac\u0101ra)."}},{id:"vism-8.4",pali:"Yassa pana ett\u0101vat\u0101 na hoti, tena vadhakapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nato, sampattivipattito, upasa\u1e43hara\u1e47ato, k\u0101yabahus\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47ato, \u0101yudubbalato, animittato, addh\u0101naparicchedato, kha\u1e47aparittatoti imehi a\u1e6d\u1e6dhah\u0101k\u0101rehi mara\u1e47a\u1e43 anussaritabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"But for one for whom this has not yet come about, death should be recollected by these eight aspects: as an executioner ever-present, by the ruin of prosperity, by comparison, by the body being common to many, by the weakness of life, by its signlessness, by the limitation of the life-span, and by the brevity of the moment.",pt:"Mas para quem isso n\xe3o ocorre por esse meio, a morte deve ser recordada por meio destes oito modos: (1) como um carrasco que se apresenta diante de si, (2) pela ru\xedna da prosperidade, (3) por compara\xe7\xe3o, (4) por compartilhar o corpo com muitos seres, (5) pela fragilidade da vida, (6) por ser sem sinais, (7) pela limita\xe7\xe3o do tempo de vida, e (8) pela brevidade do momento presente.",es:"Sin embargo, para aquel a quien no se le manifiesta la meditaci\xf3n mediante el m\xe9todo anterior, debe recordar la muerte a trav\xe9s de estos ocho aspectos: (1) como un verdugo que se presenta frente a uno, (2) por la ruina de la prosperidad, (3) por comparaci\xf3n, (4) por el hecho de que el cuerpo es compartido con muchos seres, (5) por la fragilidad de la vida, (6) por la ausencia de se\xf1ales (incertidumbre), (7) por la limitaci\xf3n de la duraci\xf3n de la vida y (8) por la brevedad del momento presente."}},{id:"vism-8.5",pali:"Tattha vadhakapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101natoti vadhakassa viya paccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nato. Yath\u0101 hi imassa s\u012bsa\u1e43 chindiss\u0101m\u012bti asi\u1e43 gahetv\u0101 g\u012bv\u0101ya c\u0101rayam\u0101no vadhako paccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dhitova hoti, eva\u1e43 mara\u1e47ampi paccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dhitamev\u0101ti anussaritabba\u1e43. Kasm\u0101? Saha j\u0101tiy\u0101 \u0101gatato, j\u012bvitahara\u1e47ato ca. Yath\u0101 hi ahicchattakamaku\u1e37a\u1e43 matthakena pa\u1e43su\u1e43 gahetv\u0101va uggacchati, eva\u1e43 satt\u0101 jar\u0101mara\u1e47a\u1e43 gahetv\u0101va nibbattanti. Tath\u0101 hi nesa\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhicitta\u1e43 upp\u0101d\u0101nantarameva jara\u1e43 patv\u0101 pabbatasikharato patitasil\u0101 viya bhijjati saddhi\u1e43 sampayuttakhandhehi. Eva\u1e43 kha\u1e47ikamara\u1e47a\u1e43 t\u0101va saha j\u0101tiy\u0101 \u0101gata\u1e43. J\u0101tassa pana avassa\u1e43 mara\u1e47ato idh\u0101dhippetamara\u1e47ampi saha j\u0101tiy\u0101 \u0101gata\u1e43. Tasm\u0101 esa satto j\u0101tak\u0101lato pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya yath\u0101 n\u0101ma u\u1e6d\u1e6dhito s\u016briyo atth\u0101bhimukho gacchateva, gatagata\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nato \u012bsakampi na nivattati. Yath\u0101 v\u0101 nad\u012b pabbateyy\u0101 s\u012bghasot\u0101 h\u0101rah\u0101rin\u012b sandateva vattateva \u012bsakampi na nivattati, eva\u1e43 \u012bsakampi anivattam\u0101no mara\u1e47\u0101bhimukhova y\u0101ti. Tena vutta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"Herein, 'as an executioner ever-present' means like the presence of an executioner. Just as an executioner, taking a sword and brandishing it at the neck, thinking, 'I will cut off this person's head,' is ever-present, so too should death be recollected as ever-present. Why? Because it comes together with birth and because it takes away life. Just as a mushroom sprout emerges from the soil already carrying dust on its head, so too beings are born carrying aging and death. Indeed, their rebirth-linking consciousness, immediately after arising, reaches aging and shatters like a stone falling from a mountain peak, along with its associated aggregates. Thus, momentary death comes with birth itself. Moreover, since death is inevitable for one who is born, the death intended here also comes with birth. Therefore, this being, from the moment of birth, is like the rising sun moving toward its setting, never turning back even slightly from the place it has reached. Or like a swift mountain river, carrying all before it, flowing and rolling on, never turning back even a little, it moves inexorably toward death. Hence it is said:",pt:"Ali, 'como um carrasco que se apresenta diante de si' significa que a morte se apresenta como um carrasco. Assim como um carrasco que segura uma espada e a move ao redor do pesco\xe7o de algu\xe9m pensando 'vou cortar a cabe\xe7a deste homem' est\xe1 de fato presente diante dele, da mesma forma deve-se recordar que a morte est\xe1 sempre presente diante de si. Por qu\xea? Porque ela vem junto com o nascimento e porque ela rouba a vida. Assim como o broto de um cogumelo surge carregando terra em sua cabe\xe7a, da mesma forma os seres nascem carregando a velhice e a morte. Pois a mente de renascimento (pa\u1e6disandhicitta) deles, imediatamente ap\xf3s o seu surgimento, atinge a velhice e se dissolve junto com os agregados associados, como uma pedra que cai do topo de uma montanha. Assim, a morte moment\xe2nea (kha\u1e47ikamara\u1e47a) vem junto com o nascimento. E como aquele que nasceu inevitavelmente morrer\xe1, a morte pretendida aqui tamb\xe9m vem junto com o nascimento. Portanto, a partir do momento do nascimento, este ser caminha continuamente em dire\xe7\xe3o ao seu fim, assim como o sol nascente se move inevitavelmente em dire\xe7\xe3o ao poente, sem retroceder nem um pouco de onde quer que passe. Ou como um rio que desce da montanha, com correnteza r\xe1pida e que arrasta tudo, flui e rola continuamente sem retroceder nem um pouco, da mesma forma o ser caminha em dire\xe7\xe3o \xe0 morte sem retroceder nem um pouco. Por isso foi dito:",es:"En este contexto, 'como un verdugo que se presenta frente a uno' significa que la muerte se presenta de forma inminente, como un verdugo. As\xed como un verdugo que sostiene una espada y la dirige hacia el cuello de alguien pensando: 'Cortar\xe9 su cabeza', est\xe1 siempre presente y al acecho, del mismo modo debe recordarse que la muerte es inminente. \xbfPor qu\xe9? Porque viene junto con el nacimiento y porque arrebata la vida. As\xed como el brote de un hongo surge de la tierra llevando polvo en su parte superior, as\xed los seres nacen cargando consigo la vejez y la muerte. Pues su conciencia de renacimiento, inmediatamente despu\xe9s de surgir, alcanza la vejez y se desintegra junto con sus agregados asociados, como una piedra que cae desde la cima de una monta\xf1a. De este modo, la muerte moment\xe1nea (kha\u1e47ika-mara\u1e47a) viene acompa\xf1ada desde el nacimiento. Pero dado que quien ha nacido debe morir inevitablemente, la muerte que se trata aqu\xed (la interrupci\xf3n de la facultad vital) tambi\xe9n se considera que viene junto con el nacimiento. Por lo tanto, este ser, desde el momento de nacer, avanza inevitablemente hacia su ocaso, como el sol que una vez salido se dirige hacia la puesta y no retrocede ni un \xe1pice de cada lugar por donde pasa. O como un r\xedo de monta\xf1a, de corriente r\xe1pida que arrastra todo a su paso, solo fluye hacia adelante y no retrocede ni un poco; as\xed el ser avanza sin detenerse hacia la muerte. Por eso se ha dicho:"}},{id:"vism-8.6",pali:"Sampattivipattitoti idha sampatti n\u0101ma t\u0101vadeva sobhati, y\u0101va na\u1e43 vipatti n\u0101bhibhavati, na ca s\u0101 sampatti n\u0101ma atthi, y\u0101 vipatti\u1e43 atikkamma ti\u1e6d\u1e6dheyya. Tath\u0101 hi \u2013",translations:{en:"As for prosperity and adversity: Here, that which is called prosperity shines only so long as adversity does not overwhelm it. And there is no such thing as a prosperity that could stand, having overcome adversity. For indeed\u2014",pt:"Quanto a 'pela ru\xedna da prosperidade': neste mundo, a prosperidade (sampatti) brilha apenas enquanto a ru\xedna (vipatti) n\xe3o a domina; e n\xe3o existe prosperidade que possa permanecer superando a ru\xedna. Pois de fato:",es:"Respecto a 'por la ruina de la prosperidad': en este mundo, lo que llamamos prosperidad (sampatti) es bella solo mientras la desgracia (vipatti) no la abruma; y no existe prosperidad que pueda permanecer tras haber trascendido la desgracia. En efecto:"}},{id:"vism-8.7",pali:"Upasa\u1e43hara\u1e47atoti parehi saddhi\u1e43 attano upasa\u1e43hara\u1e47ato. Tattha sattah\u0101k\u0101rehi upasa\u1e43hara\u1e47ato mara\u1e47a\u1e43 anussaritabba\u1e43, yasamahattato, pu\xf1\xf1amahattato, th\u0101mamahattato, iddhimahattato, pa\xf1\xf1\u0101mahattato, paccekabuddhato, samm\u0101sambuddhatoti. Katha\u1e43? Ida\u1e43 mara\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u0101ma mah\u0101yas\u0101na\u1e43 mah\u0101pariv\u0101r\u0101na\u1e43 sampannadhanav\u0101han\u0101na\u1e43 mah\u0101sammatamandh\u0101tumah\u0101sudassana da\u1e37hanemi nimippabhut\u012bnampi upari nir\u0101sa\u1e45kameva patita\u1e43, kima\u1e45ga\u1e43 pana mayha\u1e43 upari na patissati?",translations:{en:"By way of comparison means by comparing oneself with others. Therein, death should be recollected by way of comparison in seven aspects: by greatness of fame, by greatness of merit, by greatness of strength, by greatness of psychic power, by greatness of wisdom, by being a Paccekabuddha, and by being a Samm\u0101sambuddha. How? This thing called death has fallen without hesitation even upon those of great fame and large retinues, endowed with wealth and vehicles, such as Mah\u0101sammata, Mandh\u0101tu, Mah\u0101sudassana, Da\u1e37hanemi, Nimi, and others. For what reason, then, will it not fall upon me?",pt:"'Por compara\xe7\xe3o' significa comparar a pr\xf3pria morte com a de outros que j\xe1 faleceram. Nesse sentido, deve-se meditar sobre a morte por meio de sete aspectos comparativos: pela grandeza da fama, pela grandeza do m\xe9rito, pela grandeza da for\xe7a, pela grandeza do poder ps\xedquico, pela grandeza da sabedoria, como um Paccekabuddha e como um Samm\u0101sambuddha. Como? Esta morte abateu-se, sem qualquer hesita\xe7\xe3o, at\xe9 mesmo sobre aqueles de imensa fama, com grandes comitivas e abundantes riquezas e montarias, como os reis Mah\u0101sammata, Mandh\u0101tu, Mah\u0101sudassana, Da\u1e37hanemi, Nimi e outros. Por que, ent\xe3o, ela n\xe3o haveria de se abater sobre mim?",es:"\u2018Mediante la comparaci\xf3n\u2019 (upasa\u1e43hara\u1e47a) significa comparando la propia muerte con la de los dem\xe1s. En este contexto, la muerte debe recordarse mediante la comparaci\xf3n a trav\xe9s de siete aspectos: por la grandeza de la fama, por la grandeza del m\xe9rito, por la grandeza de la fuerza, por la grandeza de los poderes ps\xedquicos, por la grandeza de la sabidur\xeda, por los Budas Solitarios y por los Budas Completamente Iluminados. \xbfC\xf3mo? Esta muerte ha ca\xeddo incluso sobre aquellos de gran renombre, de gran s\xe9quito, poseedores de abundantes riquezas y veh\xedculos, como los reyes Mah\u0101sammata, Mandh\u0101tu, Mah\u0101sudassana, Da\u1e37hanemi y Nimi, cayendo sobre ellos sin vacilaci\xf3n alguna. \xbfC\xf3mo, entonces, no caer\xe1 sobre m\xed?"}},{id:"vism-8.8",pali:"K\u0101yabahus\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47atoti aya\u1e43 k\u0101yo bahus\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47o. As\u012btiy\u0101 t\u0101va kimikul\u0101na\u1e43 s\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47o, tattha chavinissit\u0101 p\u0101\u1e47\u0101 chavi\u1e43 kh\u0101danti, cammanissit\u0101 camma\u1e43 kh\u0101danti, ma\u1e43sanissit\u0101 ma\u1e43sa\u1e43 kh\u0101danti, nh\u0101runissit\u0101 nh\u0101ru\u1e43 kh\u0101danti, a\u1e6d\u1e6dhinissit\u0101 a\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e43 kh\u0101danti, mi\xf1janissit\u0101 mi\xf1ja\u1e43 kh\u0101danti. Tattheva j\u0101yanti j\u012byanti m\u012byanti, ucc\u0101rapass\u0101va\u1e43 karonti. K\u0101yova nesa\u1e43 s\u016btighara\xf1ceva gil\u0101nas\u0101l\u0101 ca sus\u0101na\xf1ca vaccaku\u1e6di ca pass\u0101vado\u1e47ik\u0101 ca. Sv\u0101ya\u1e43 tesampi kimikul\u0101na\u1e43 pakopena mara\u1e47a\u1e43 nigacchatiyeva. Yath\u0101 ca as\u012btiy\u0101 kimikul\u0101na\u1e43, eva\u1e43 ajjhattik\u0101na\u1e43yeva anekasat\u0101na\u1e43 rog\u0101na\u1e43 b\u0101hir\u0101na\xf1ca ahivicchik\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 mara\u1e47assa paccay\u0101na\u1e43 s\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47o.",translations:{en:"This body is common to many. Firstly, it is common to eighty families of worms. Among them, creatures that dwell depending on the outer skin eat the outer skin; those that dwell depending on the inner skin eat the inner skin; those that dwell depending on the flesh eat the flesh; those that dwell depending on the sinews eat the sinews; those that dwell depending on the bones eat the bones; those that dwell depending on the marrow eat the marrow. Right there they are born, grow old, and die; they produce feces and urine. The body itself is for them a maternity home, a hospital, a charnel ground, a toilet, and a urinal. This very body certainly goes to death even by the affliction of those families of worms. And just as it is common to the eighty families of worms, so too it is common to the many hundreds of internal diseases and to external causes of death such as snakes, scorpions, and so on.",pt:"'Por ser compartilhado com muitos' significa que este corpo \xe9 compartilhado com muitos seres. Primeiramente, \xe9 compartilhado com oitenta fam\xedlias de vermes. Nelas, as criaturas que habitam a epiderme comem a epiderme; as que habitam a derme comem a derme; as que habitam a carne comem a carne; as que habitam os tend\xf5es comem os tend\xf5es; as que habitam os ossos comem os ossos; as que habitam a medula comem a medula. Ali mesmo eles nascem, envelhecem, morrem e evacuam fezes e urina. O corpo \xe9 a sua maternidade, o seu hospital, o seu cemit\xe9rio, a sua latrina e o seu mict\xf3rio. Este corpo, devido \xe0 prolifera\xe7\xe3o desses vermes, inevitavelmente caminha para a morte. E assim como \xe9 compartilhado com oitenta fam\xedlias de vermes, tamb\xe9m \xe9 compartilhado com centenas de doen\xe7as internas e perigos externos, como cobras, escorpi\xf5es e outras causas de morte.",es:"En cuanto a 'por ser el cuerpo compartido con muchos': este cuerpo es compartido por muchos seres. En primer lugar, es compartido con ochenta tipos de familias de gusanos; all\xed, los seres que dependen de la epidermis comen la epidermis, los que dependen de la dermis comen la dermis, los que dependen de la carne comen la carne, los que dependen de los tendones comen los tendones, los que dependen de los huesos comen los huesos, y los que dependen de la m\xe9dula \xf3sea comen la m\xe9dula \xf3sea. All\xed mismo nacen, envejecen, mueren y excretan orina y heces. El cuerpo mismo es para ellos su sala de maternidad, su hospital, su cementerio, su letrina y su pozo de orina. Este mismo cuerpo llega a la muerte debido a la alteraci\xf3n de esas mismas familias de gusanos. Y as\xed como es compartido con ochenta familias de gusanos, tambi\xe9n lo es con cientos de enfermedades internas y con causas externas de muerte, como serpientes, escorpiones y otros."}},{id:"vism-8.9",pali:"\u0100yudubbalatoti \u0101yu n\u0101meta\u1e43 abala\u1e43 dubbala\u1e43. Tath\u0101 hi satt\u0101na\u1e43 j\u012bvita\u1e43 ass\u0101sapass\u0101s\u016bpanibaddha\xf1ceva iriy\u0101path\u016bpanibaddha\xf1ca s\u012btu\u1e47h\u016bpanibaddha\xf1ca mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u016bpanibaddha\xf1ca \u0101h\u0101r\u016bpanibaddha\xf1ca. Tadeta\u1e43 ass\u0101sapass\u0101s\u0101na\u1e43 samavuttita\u1e43 labham\u0101nameva pavattati. Bahi nikkhantan\u0101sikav\u0101te pana anto apavisante, pavi\u1e6d\u1e6dhe v\u0101 anikkhamante mato n\u0101ma hoti. Catunna\u1e43 iriy\u0101path\u0101nampi samavuttita\u1e43 labham\u0101nameva pavattati. A\xf1\xf1atara\xf1\xf1atarassa pana adhimattat\u0101ya \u0101yusa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 upacchijjanti. S\u012btu\u1e47h\u0101nampi samavuttita\u1e43 labham\u0101nameva pavattati. Atis\u012btena pana atiu\u1e47hena v\u0101 abhibh\u016btassa vipajjati. Mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101nampi samavuttita\u1e43 labham\u0101nameva pavattati. Pathav\u012bdh\u0101tuy\u0101 pana \u0101podh\u0101tu\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atara\xf1\xf1atarassa pakopena balasampannopi puggalo patthaddhak\u0101yo v\u0101 atis\u0101r\u0101divasena kilinnap\u016btik\u0101yo v\u0101 mah\u0101\u1e0d\u0101hapareto v\u0101 sambhijjam\u0101nasandhibandhano v\u0101 hutv\u0101 j\u012bvitakkhaya\u1e43 p\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101ti. Kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101r\u0101h\u0101rampi yuttak\u0101le labhantasseva j\u012bvita\u1e43 pavattati, \u0101h\u0101ra\u1e43 alabham\u0101nassa pana parikkhaya\u1e43 gacchat\u012bti. Eva\u1e43 \u0101yudubbalato mara\u1e47a\u1e43 anussaritabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"By way of the weakness of life: this which is called life is without strength and is feeble. For the life of beings is dependent upon the in-breath and out-breath, the postures, cold and heat, the great elements, and food. This life continues only when it obtains a balanced occurrence of the in-breaths and out-breaths. But when the nasal breath that has gone out does not enter within, or when the breath that has entered does not go out, one is called dead. It continues only when obtaining a balanced occurrence of the four postures as well. But through the excess of any one of them, the life-formations are cut off. It continues only when obtaining a balanced occurrence of cold and heat as well. But for one who is overcome by extreme cold or extreme heat, it perishes. It continues only when obtaining a balanced occurrence of the great elements as well. But through the disturbance of the earth element, or of one or another of the water element and so on, even a person endowed with strength reaches the destruction of life, having become one with a stiff body, or one with a moist and putrid body due to diarrhea and so on, or one overcome by a great burning fever. Life continues only for one who obtains physical food at the proper time; but for one not obtaining food, it goes to destruction. Thus, death should be recollected by way of the weakness of life.",pt:"'Pela fragilidade da vida' significa que esta vida \xe9 sem for\xe7a, fr\xe1gil. Pois a vida dos seres est\xe1 vinculada \xe0 inspira\xe7\xe3o e \xe0 expira\xe7\xe3o, vinculada \xe0s posturas corporais, vinculada ao frio e ao calor, vinculada aos grandes elementos e vinculada ao alimento. Esta vida prossegue apenas quando obt\xe9m o funcionamento equilibrado da inspira\xe7\xe3o e da expira\xe7\xe3o. Se o ar que sai pelas narinas n\xe3o retornar para dentro, ou se o ar que entrou n\xe3o sair, a pessoa \xe9 considerada morta. Ela prossegue apenas quando obt\xe9m o funcionamento equilibrado das quatro posturas corporais. Pelo excesso de qualquer uma das posturas, as forma\xe7\xf5es vitais s\xe3o interrompidas. Ela prossegue apenas quando obt\xe9m o funcionamento equilibrado do frio e do calor. Se for subjugada pelo frio extremo ou pelo calor extremo, ela falha. Ela prossegue apenas quando obt\xe9m o funcionamento equilibrado dos grandes elementos. Pela perturba\xe7\xe3o do elemento terra, ou do elemento \xe1gua, etc., mesmo uma pessoa forte, ficando com o corpo r\xedgido, ou com o corpo \xfamido e putrefato devido \xe0 diarreia, etc., ou atormentada por um calor intenso, ou com as articula\xe7\xf5es e ligamentos rompidos, chega ao fim da vida. At\xe9 mesmo o alimento f\xedsico sustenta a vida apenas quando obtido no momento adequado; para quem n\xe3o obt\xe9m alimento, a vida chega ao fim. Assim, deve-se meditar sobre a morte pela fragilidade da vida.",es:"En cuanto a 'por la debilidad de la vida': esto que se llama vida no tiene fuerza, es d\xe9bil. Pues la vida de los seres est\xe1 ligada a la inhalaci\xf3n y exhalaci\xf3n, a las posturas, al fr\xedo y al calor, a los grandes elementos y al alimento. Esta vida contin\xfaa solo mientras se mantiene el equilibrio entre la inhalaci\xf3n y la exhalaci\xf3n. Si el aire de la nariz sale pero no entra, o si entra pero no sale, se dice que uno est\xe1 muerto. Tambi\xe9n contin\xfaa solo mientras se mantiene el equilibrio de las cuatro posturas; por el exceso de una u otra, las formaciones vitales se interrumpen. Tambi\xe9n contin\xfaa solo mientras se mantiene el equilibrio entre el fr\xedo y el calor; si uno es subyugado por el fr\xedo extremo o el calor extremo, la vida perece. Tambi\xe9n contin\xfaa solo mientras se mantiene el equilibrio de los grandes elementos; por la alteraci\xf3n del elemento tierra o de uno de los elementos como el agua, etc., incluso una persona dotada de gran fuerza llega al fin de la vida, ya sea con el cuerpo r\xedgido, o con el cuerpo descompuesto y purulento debido a la disenter\xeda u otras causas, o consumido por un gran calor, o con las conexiones de sus articulaciones rompi\xe9ndose. Incluso la vida contin\xfaa para aquel que obtiene alimento material en el momento adecuado; para quien no obtiene alimento, llega a su fin. De esta manera, se debe rememorar la muerte por la debilidad de la vida."}},{id:"vism-8.10",pali:"Animittatoti avavatth\u0101nato, paricched\u0101bh\u0101vatoti attho. Satt\u0101na\u1e43 hi \u2013",translations:{en:"By way of being without a sign: this means because of non-determination, that is, because of the absence of limitation. For of beings\u2014",pt:"'Por ser imprevis\xedvel' significa sem defini\xe7\xe3o, sem limite estabelecido. Pois, para os seres vivos:",es:"En cuanto a 'por la ausencia de signos': el significado es que no hay una delimitaci\xf3n o una duraci\xf3n fija. Pues para los seres:"}},{id:"vism-8.11",pali:"Addh\u0101naparicchedatoti manuss\u0101na\u1e43 j\u012bvitassa n\u0101ma etarahi paritto addh\u0101. Yo cira\u1e43 j\u012bvati, so vassasata\u1e43, appa\u1e43 v\u0101 bhiyyo. Ten\u0101ha bhagav\u0101 \u2013 \"appamida\u1e43, bhikkhave, manuss\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101yu, gaman\u012byo sampar\u0101yo, kattabba\u1e43 kusala\u1e43, caritabba\u1e43 brahmacariya\u1e43, natthi j\u0101tassa amara\u1e47a\u1e43. Yo, bhikkhave, cira\u1e43 j\u012bvati, so vassasata\u1e43, appa\u1e43 v\u0101 bhiyyoti.",translations:{en:"By way of the limited span of life: for humans, the length of life at present is indeed short. One who lives long lives a hundred years or a little more. Therefore, the Blessed One said: \u201cBrief, bhikkhus, is the life of humans\u2014the next world is to be gone to. What is wholesome should be done, the holy life should be lived, for there is no not-dying for one who is born. One who lives long, bhikkhus, lives a hundred years or a little more.\u201d",pt:"'Pela limita\xe7\xe3o do tempo de vida' significa que, atualmente, o tempo de vida dos seres humanos \xe9 muito curto. Aquele que vive muito vive cem anos, ou um pouco mais ou menos. Por isso, o Aben\xe7oado disse: 'Monges, este tempo de vida dos seres humanos \xe9 curto; deve-se partir para o pr\xf3ximo mundo; o que \xe9 ben\xe9fico deve ser praticado; a vida santa deve ser vivida; n\xe3o existe o n\xe3o-morrer para quem nasceu. Monges, aquele que vive muito vive cem anos, ou um pouco mais ou menos'.",es:"En cuanto a 'por la limitaci\xf3n del tiempo': la duraci\xf3n de la vida de los humanos en la actualidad es muy corta. Aquel que vive mucho tiempo, vive cien a\xf1os, o un poco m\xe1s. Por eso dijo el Sublime: 'Monjes, esta vida de los humanos es corta; el m\xe1s all\xe1 debe ser alcanzado, se debe hacer lo que es bueno y se debe vivir la vida santa; no hay inmortalidad para el que ha nacido. Monjes, aquel que vive mucho tiempo, vive cien a\xf1os, o un poco m\xe1s'."}},{id:"vism-8.12",pali:"Kha\u1e47aparittatoti paramatthato hi atiparitto satt\u0101na\u1e43 j\u012bvitakkha\u1e47o ekacittappavattimattoyeva. Yath\u0101 n\u0101ma rathacakka\u1e43 pavattam\u0101nampi ekeneva nemippadesena pavattati, ti\u1e6d\u1e6dham\u0101nampi ekeneva ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhati, evameva ekacittakkha\u1e47ika\u1e43 satt\u0101na\u1e43 j\u012bvita\u1e43. Tasmi\u1e43 citte niruddhamatte satto niruddhoti vuccati. Yath\u0101ha \u2013 \"at\u012bte cittakkha\u1e47e j\u012bvittha, na j\u012bvati, na j\u012bvissati. An\u0101gate cittakkha\u1e47e na j\u012bvittha, na j\u012bvati, j\u012bvissati. Paccuppanne cittakkha\u1e47e na j\u012bvittha, j\u012bvati, na j\u012bvissati.",translations:{en:"Regarding the brevity of the moment: indeed, in the ultimate sense, the life-moment of beings is exceedingly brief; it is merely the duration of the occurrence of a single mind-moment. Just as a chariot wheel, even when rolling, rolls on only one point of its rim, and even when standing still, stands on only one point, even so, the life of beings has the duration of a single mind-moment. When that mind has just ceased, the being is said to have ceased. As it is said: 'In a past mind-moment, one lived; one does not live, nor will one live. In a future mind-moment, one did not live, nor does one live; one will live. In the present mind-moment, one did not live; one lives, but one will not live.'",pt:"\"Pela brevidade do momento\" significa que, no sentido \xfaltimo, a dura\xe7\xe3o da vida dos seres \xe9 extremamente curta, durando apenas a ocorr\xeancia de um \xfanico momento mental. Assim como a roda de uma carruagem, ao girar, gira apenas sobre um \xfanico ponto do aro e, ao parar, para apenas sobre um \xfanico ponto; da mesma forma, a vida dos seres dura apenas um \xfanico momento mental. Assim que esse momento mental cessa, diz-se que o ser cessou (morreu). Como foi dito: \"No momento mental passado, o ser viveu, n\xe3o vive agora, nem viver\xe1 no futuro. No momento mental futuro, o ser n\xe3o viveu no passado, n\xe3o vive agora, mas viver\xe1 no futuro. No momento mental presente, o ser n\xe3o viveu no passado, vive agora, mas n\xe3o viver\xe1 no futuro.\"",es:"Por la brevedad del momento significa que, en el sentido \xfaltimo, el momento de vida de los seres es extremadamente breve, durando solo lo que dura el surgimiento de un solo pensamiento. As\xed como la rueda de un carro, tanto al rodar como al estar detenida, se apoya solo sobre un punto de su llanta, de la misma manera la vida de los seres dura solo un momento de conciencia. En cuanto esa conciencia cesa, se dice que el ser ha cesado. Como se ha dicho: \"En el momento de conciencia pasado se ha vivido, no se vive, ni se vivir\xe1. En el momento de conciencia futuro no se ha vivido, no se vive, pero se vivir\xe1. En el momento de conciencia presente no se ha vivido, se vive, pero no se vivir\xe1."}},{id:"vism-8.13",pali:"Tasm\u0101 have appam\u0101da\u1e43, kayir\u0101tha sumedhaso; Eva\u1e43 mah\u0101nubh\u0101v\u0101ya, mara\u1e47assatiy\u0101 sad\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Therefore, let the wise indeed always practice heedfulness in this mindfulness of death of such great power.",pt:"\"Portanto, de fato, uma pessoa s\xe1bia deve sempre praticar a dilig\xeancia na medita\xe7\xe3o sobre a morte, que possui t\xe3o grande poder.\"",es:"Por lo tanto, ciertamente, el sabio debe practicar siempre la diligencia en la recordaci\xf3n de la muerte, que posee tan gran poder."}},{id:"vism-8.14",pali:"Id\u0101ni ya\u1e43 ta\u1e43 bhagavat\u0101 \"ayampi kho, bhikkhave, \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassatisam\u0101dhi bh\u0101vito bahul\u012bkato santo ceva pa\u1e47\u012bto ca asecanako ca sukho ca vih\u0101ro, uppannuppanne ca p\u0101pake akusale dhamme \u1e6dh\u0101naso antaradh\u0101peti v\u016bpasamet\u012b\"ti eva\u1e43 pasa\u1e43sitv\u0101 \u2013",translations:{en:"Now, that concentration through mindfulness of breathing which the Blessed One praised thus: 'Bhikkhus, when this concentration through mindfulness of breathing is developed and much cultivated, it is peaceful and sublime, unadulterated and a blissful abiding; and it instantly causes arisen evil, unwholesome states to disappear and be calmed'\u2014",pt:"Agora, quanto \xe0quilo que foi elogiado pelo Aben\xe7oado da seguinte maneira: 'Monjes, esta concentra\xe7\xe3o atrav\xe9s da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o, quando cultivada e desenvolvida, \xe9 pac\xedfica e sublime, uma morada pura e prazerosa, e faz desaparecer e acalma imediatamente os dhammas prejudiciais e insalubres que surgem' \u2014",es:"Ahora, el Bienaventurado, despu\xe9s de elogiar esta pr\xe1ctica diciendo: 'Monjes, esta concentraci\xf3n mediante el mindfulness de la respiraci\xf3n, cuando se desarrolla y se cultiva, es ciertamente pac\xedfica y sublime, una morada inmaculada y placentera, que hace desaparecer y calma inmediatamente los estados perjudiciales y no saludables que surgen'..."}},{id:"vism-8.15",pali:"\"Katha\u1e43 bh\u0101vito ca, bhikkhave, \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassatisam\u0101dhi katha\u1e43 bahul\u012bkato santo ceva pa\u1e47\u012bto ca asecanako ca sukho ca vih\u0101ro, uppannuppanne ca p\u0101pake akusale dhamme \u1e6dh\u0101naso antaradh\u0101peti v\u016bpasameti? Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu ara\xf1\xf1agato v\u0101 rukkham\u016blagato v\u0101 su\xf1\xf1\u0101g\u0101ragato v\u0101 nis\u012bdati palla\u1e45ka\u1e43 \u0101bhujitv\u0101 uju\u1e43 k\u0101ya\u1e43 pa\u1e47idh\u0101ya parimukha\u1e43 sati\u1e43 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhapetv\u0101, so satova assasati sato passasati. D\u012bgha\u1e43 v\u0101 assasanto d\u012bgha\u1e43 assas\u0101m\u012bti paj\u0101n\u0101ti. D\u012bgha\u1e43 v\u0101 passasanto\u2026pe\u2026 rassa\u1e43 v\u0101 assasanto\u2026pe\u2026 rassa\u1e43 v\u0101 passasanto rassa\u1e43 passas\u0101m\u012bti paj\u0101n\u0101ti. Sabbak\u0101yapa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b assasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhati. Sabbak\u0101yapa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b passasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhati. Passambhaya\u1e43 k\u0101yasa\u1e45kh\u0101ra\u1e43 assasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhati. Passambhaya\u1e43 k\u0101yasa\u1e45kh\u0101ra\u1e43 passasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhati. P\u012btipa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b\u2026 sukhapa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b\u2026 cittasa\u1e45kh\u0101rapa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b\u2026 passambhaya\u1e43 cittasa\u1e45kh\u0101ra\u1e43\u2026 cittapa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b\u2026 abhippamodaya\u1e43 citta\u1e43\u2026 sam\u0101daha\u1e43 citta\u1e43\u2026 vimocaya\u1e43 citta\u1e43 \u2026 anicc\u0101nupass\u012b\u2026 vir\u0101g\u0101nupass\u012b\u2026 nirodh\u0101nupass\u012b. Pa\u1e6dinissagg\u0101nupass\u012b assasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhati. Pa\u1e6dinissagg\u0101nupass\u012b passasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhat\u012b\"ti \u2013",translations:{en:"\u2018How, bhikkhus, is concentration through mindfulness of breathing developed and cultivated so that it is peaceful and sublime, unadulterated, and a pleasant abiding, and on the spot causes evil, unwholesome states that have arisen to disappear and be stilled? Here, bhikkhus, a bhikkhu, having gone to the forest or to the root of a tree or to an empty dwelling, sits down, folds his legs crosswise, sets his body erect, and establishes mindfulness before him. Mindful he breathes in, mindful he breathes out. Breathing in long, he understands, \u201cI breathe in long.\u201d Breathing out long\u2026 and so on\u2026 breathing in short\u2026 breathing out short, he understands, \u201cI breathe out short.\u201d He trains himself, \u201cI will breathe in experiencing the whole body.\u201d He trains himself, \u201cI will breathe out experiencing the whole body.\u201d He trains himself, \u201cI will breathe in calming the bodily formation.\u201d He trains himself, \u201cI will breathe out calming the bodily formation.\u201d He trains himself, \u201cI will breathe in experiencing rapture\u201d\u2026 \u201cexperiencing pleasure\u201d\u2026 \u201cexperiencing the mental formation\u201d\u2026 \u201ccalming the mental formation\u201d\u2026 \u201cexperiencing the mind\u201d\u2026 \u201cgladdening the mind\u201d\u2026 \u201cconcentrating the mind\u201d\u2026 \u201cliberating the mind\u201d\u2026 \u201ccontemplating impermanence\u201d\u2026 \u201ccontemplating fading away\u201d\u2026 \u201ccontemplating cessation.\u201d He trains himself, \u201cI will breathe in contemplating relinquishment.\u201d He trains himself, \u201cI will breathe out contemplating relinquishment.\u201d\u2019",pt:"\u201cE como, monges, a concentra\xe7\xe3o da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o (\u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassatisam\u0101dhi), quando desenvolvida e cultivada, \xe9 pac\xedfica e sublime, uma morada pura e feliz, e faz desaparecer e pacificar imediatamente os dhammas prejudiciais e insalubres que surgem? Aqui, monges, um monge que foi para a floresta, para o p\xe9 de uma \xe1rvore ou para uma cabana vazia, senta-se, cruzando as pernas, mantendo o corpo ereto e estabelecendo a aten\xe7\xe3o plena \xe0 sua frente. Atento ele inspira, atento ele expira. Inspirando longamente, ele compreende: \u2018Inspiro longamente\u2019; ou expirando longamente... [pe]... inspirando curto... [pe]... ou expirando curto, ele compreende: \u2018Expiro curto\u2019. Ele treina: \u2018Inspirarei experienciando todo o corpo\u2019; ele treina: \u2018Expirarei experienciando todo o corpo\u2019. Ele treina: \u2018Inspirarei tranquilizando a forma\xe7\xe3o corporal\u2019; ele treina: \u2018Expirarei tranquilizando a forma\xe7\xe3o corporal\u2019. Ele treina: \u2018Inspirarei experienciando o \xeaxtase\u2019... \u2018experienciando a felicidade\u2019... \u2018experienciando a forma\xe7\xe3o mental\u2019... \u2018tranquilizando a forma\xe7\xe3o mental\u2019... \u2018experienciando a mente\u2019... \u2018alegrando a mente\u2019... \u2018concentrando a mente\u2019... \u2018libertando a mente\u2019... \u2018observando a imperman\xeancia\u2019... \u2018observando o desapego\u2019... \u2018observando a cessa\xe7\xe3o\u2019. Ele treina: \u2018Inspirarei observando o abandono\u2019; ele treina: \u2018Expirarei observando o abandono\u2019.\u201d",es:"...indic\xf3 el tema de meditaci\xf3n sobre la respiraci\xf3n con sus diecis\xe9is etapas de la siguiente manera: '\xbfY c\xf3mo, monjes, se desarrolla la concentraci\xf3n mediante el mindfulness de la respiraci\xf3n?... Un monje, habiendo ido al bosque, al pie de un \xe1rbol o a un lugar solitario, se sienta con las piernas cruzadas, el cuerpo erguido y establece la atenci\xf3n plena frente a \xe9l... Inhalando largo, comprende: inhalo largo... Se entrena as\xed: experimentando todo el cuerpo inhalar\xe9... tranquilizando la formaci\xf3n corporal inhalar\xe9... experimentando el gozo... experimentando la felicidad... experimentando la formaci\xf3n mental... tranquilizando la formaci\xf3n mental... experimentando la mente... regocijando la mente... concentrando la mente... liberando la mente... contemplando la impermanencia... contemplando el desapasionamiento... contemplando el cese... Se entrena as\xed: contemplando la renuncia inhalar\xe9, contemplando la renuncia exhalar\xe9'."}},{id:"vism-8.16",pali:"Eva\u1e43 so\u1e37asavatthuka\u1e43 \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassatikamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 niddi\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43. Tassa bh\u0101van\u0101nayo anuppatto. So pana yasm\u0101 p\u0101\u1e37iva\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101nus\u0101reneva vuccam\u0101no sabb\u0101k\u0101raparip\u016bro hoti. Tasm\u0101 ayamettha p\u0101\u1e37iva\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101pubba\u1e45gamo niddeso.",translations:{en:"Thus, the sixteen-faceted meditation subject of mindfulness of breathing has been indicated. The method of its development is next in sequence. However, since that method becomes complete in all aspects only when explained in accordance with the P\u0101\u1e37i commentary, this exposition here is therefore preceded by the P\u0101\u1e37i commentary.",pt:"Assim foi indicado o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o com suas dezesseis bases. O m\xe9todo para o seu desenvolvimento chegou \xe0 sua vez. No entanto, visto que esse m\xe9todo de desenvolvimento, quando explicado seguindo estritamente o coment\xe1rio do texto em P\u0101li, torna-se completo em todos os aspectos, esta \xe9, portanto, a exposi\xe7\xe3o detalhada que tem como guia a explica\xe7\xe3o do texto em P\u0101li neste tema de medita\xe7\xe3o da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o.",es:"De esta manera se ha expuesto el tema de meditaci\xf3n del mindfulness de la respiraci\xf3n con sus diecis\xe9is bases. El m\xe9todo de su desarrollo ha llegado a su turno de ser explicado. No obstante, dado que dicho m\xe9todo resulta completo en todos sus aspectos cuando se explica siguiendo la interpretaci\xf3n del Canon, esta exposici\xf3n tiene como prioridad la explicaci\xf3n de las palabras del Canon."}},{id:"vism-8.17",pali:"Ara\xf1\xf1agato v\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 su\xf1\xf1\u0101g\u0101ragato v\u0101ti idamassa \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassatisam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101nur\u016bpasen\u0101sanapariggahaparid\u012bpana\u1e43. Imassa hi bhikkhuno d\u012bgharatta\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101d\u012bsu \u0101ramma\u1e47esu anuvisa\u1e6da\u1e43 citta\u1e43 \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassatisam\u0101dhi\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 abhiruhitu\u1e43 na icchati, k\u016b\u1e6dago\u1e47ayuttaratho viya uppathameva dh\u0101vati. Tasm\u0101 seyyath\u0101pi n\u0101ma gopo k\u016b\u1e6dadhenuy\u0101 sabba\u1e43 kh\u012bra\u1e43 pivitv\u0101 va\u1e0d\u1e0dhita\u1e43 k\u016b\u1e6davaccha\u1e43 dametuk\u0101mo dhenuto apanetv\u0101 ekamante mahanta\u1e43 thambha\u1e43 nikha\u1e47itv\u0101 tattha yottena bandheyya, athassa so vaccho ito cito ca vipphanditv\u0101 pal\u0101yitu\u1e43 asakkonto tameva thambha\u1e43 upanis\u012bdeyya v\u0101 upanipajjeyya v\u0101, evameva imin\u0101pi bhikkhun\u0101 d\u012bgharatta\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101dirasap\u0101nava\u1e0d\u1e0dhita\u1e43 du\u1e6d\u1e6dhacitta\u1e43 dametuk\u0101mena r\u016bp\u0101di\u0101ramma\u1e47ato apanetv\u0101 ara\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 v\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 su\xf1\xf1\u0101g\u0101ra\u1e43 v\u0101 pavesetv\u0101 tattha ass\u0101sapass\u0101sathambhe satiyottena bandhitabba\u1e43. Evamassa ta\u1e43 citta\u1e43 ito cito ca vipphanditv\u0101pi pubbe \u0101ci\u1e47\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 alabham\u0101na\u1e43 satiyotta\u1e43 chinditv\u0101 pal\u0101yitu\u1e43 asakkonta\u1e43 tamev\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 upac\u0101rappan\u0101vasena upanis\u012bdati ceva upanipajjati ca. Ten\u0101hu por\u0101\u1e47\u0101 \u2013",translations:{en:"Whether he has gone to the forest... or to an empty dwelling\u2014this is the explanation of the selection of a dwelling suitable for the development of concentration through mindfulness of breathing. For this bhikkhu's mind, which for a long time has run about among objects such as forms, does not wish to ascend to the object of concentration through mindfulness of breathing; like a cart yoked to a crooked ox, it runs only along the wrong path. Therefore, just as a cowherd wishing to tame a crooked calf\u2014one that has grown by drinking all the milk of a crooked cow\u2014would take it away from its mother, drive a large post into the ground in a secluded spot, and tie it there with a rope; and then that calf, after struggling here and there, unable to escape, would sit down or lie down by that very post; even so, this bhikkhu, wishing to tame his unruly mind\u2014one that has grown for a long time by drinking the flavor of objects such as forms\u2014should take it away from objects like forms, make it enter the forest... or an empty dwelling, and there bind it with the rope of mindfulness to the post of in-and-out breathing. Thus his mind, though struggling here and there, not obtaining its formerly habitual object and being unable to escape by breaking the rope of mindfulness, settles down and rests upon that very object by way of access and absorption. Therefore, the ancients have said:",pt:"A frase \u2018foi para a floresta... [pe]... ou para uma cabana vazia\u2019 indica a escolha de uma habita\xe7\xe3o adequada para o desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o por parte desse monge. Pois a mente deste monge, que por muito tempo correu atr\xe1s de objetos como formas vis\xedveis e outros, n\xe3o deseja focar no objeto da concentra\xe7\xe3o da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o, correndo fora do caminho como uma carruagem puxada por um boi indom\xe1vel. Portanto, assim como um pastor de vacas que deseja domar um bezerro selvagem, que cresceu bebendo todo o leite de uma vaca selvagem, o afasta da m\xe3e, finca um grande poste em um local isolado e o amarra ali com uma corda; e ent\xe3o aquele bezerro, debatendo-se para l\xe1 e para c\xe1, incapaz de fugir, acaba por se sentar ou deitar junto \xe0quele mesmo poste; da mesma forma, este monge, desejando domar sua mente rebelde que cresceu por muito tempo bebendo o sabor dos prazeres dos objetos como formas vis\xedveis e outros, deve afast\xe1-la de tais objetos, lev\xe1-la para a floresta... [pe]... ou para uma cabana vazia, e amarr\xe1-la ali ao poste das inspira\xe7\xf5es e expira\xe7\xf5es com a corda da aten\xe7\xe3o plena. Assim, mesmo que sua mente se debate para l\xe1 e para c\xe1, n\xe3o encontrando o objeto ao qual estava habituada anteriormente e sendo incapaz de quebrar a corda da aten\xe7\xe3o plena para fugir, ela se estabelece e repousa apenas naquele mesmo objeto por meio do acesso e da absor\xe7\xe3o. Por isso disseram os antigos:",es:"'Se ha ido al bosque... (hasta)... o a una morada vac\xeda': esto indica la elecci\xf3n de un lugar de residencia adecuado para el desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n mediante la atenci\xf3n en la respiraci\xf3n por parte del monje. Pues la mente de este monje, que durante mucho tiempo ha divagado entre objetos como las formas y otros est\xedmulos, no desea aplicarse al objeto de la atenci\xf3n en la respiraci\xf3n; corre fuera del camino como un carro enganchado a bueyes ind\xf3mitos. Por lo tanto, as\xed como un pastor que desea domar a un ternero ind\xf3mito que ha crecido bebiendo toda la leche de una vaca salvaje, lo apartar\xeda de la madre, clavar\xeda un gran poste en un lugar apartado y lo atar\xeda all\xed con una soga; entonces, ese ternero, forcejeando de un lado a otro y siendo incapaz de escapar, terminar\xeda sent\xe1ndose o ech\xe1ndose junto a ese mismo poste; del mismo modo, este monje, deseando domar su mente rebelde que ha crecido durante mucho tiempo deleit\xe1ndose en el sabor de los objetos de los sentidos, debe apartarla de tales objetos, llevarla al bosque o a una morada vac\xeda, y all\xed atarla al poste de la inhalaci\xf3n y la exhalaci\xf3n con la soga de la atenci\xf3n. As\xed, aunque su mente forcejee de un lado a otro, al no encontrar los objetos a los que antes estaba habituada y ser incapaz de romper la soga de la atenci\xf3n y escapar, se asienta y descansa en ese mismo objeto mediante la concentraci\xf3n de acceso y de absorci\xf3n. Por eso dijeron los antiguos:"}},{id:"vism-8.18",pali:"\"Yath\u0101 thambhe nibandheyya, vaccha\u1e43 dama\u1e43 naro idha; Bandheyyeva\u1e43 saka\u1e43 citta\u1e43, satiy\u0101ramma\u1e47e da\u1e37ha\"nti.",translations:{en:"\u201cJust as a man wishing to tame a calf would bind it to a post, even so, here, one should firmly bind one's own mind to the object with mindfulness.\u201d",pt:"\u201c\u2018Assim como um homem amarra um bezerro a um poste para dom\xe1-lo aqui; assim o monge deve amarrar firmemente sua pr\xf3pria mente ao objeto de medita\xe7\xe3o com a aten\xe7\xe3o plena\u2019.\u201d",es:"'Tal como un hombre aqu\xed atar\xeda a un poste a un ternero para domarlo, del mismo modo uno debe atar firmemente su propia mente al objeto de meditaci\xf3n con la soga de la atenci\xf3n'."}},{id:"vism-8.19",pali:"Tattha d\u012bgha\u1e43 v\u0101 assasantoti d\u012bgha\u1e43 v\u0101 ass\u0101sa\u1e43 pavattayanto. Ass\u0101soti bahi nikkhamanav\u0101to. Pass\u0101soti anto pavisanav\u0101toti vinaya\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101ya\u1e43 vutta\u1e43. Suttanta\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101su pana uppa\u1e6dip\u0101\u1e6diy\u0101 \u0101gata\u1e43. Tattha sabbesampi gabbhaseyyak\u0101na\u1e43 m\u0101tukucchito nikkhamanak\u0101le pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 abbhantarav\u0101to bahi nikkhamati. Pacch\u0101 b\u0101hirav\u0101to sukhumaraja\u1e43 gahetv\u0101 abbhantara\u1e43 pavisanto t\u0101lu\u1e43 \u0101hacca nibb\u0101yati. Eva\u1e43 t\u0101va ass\u0101sapass\u0101s\u0101 veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Herein, 'breathing in long' means producing a long in-breath. 'In-breath' is the wind going out, and 'out-breath' is the wind coming in; so it is said in the Vinaya commentary. In the Sutta commentaries, however, it is given in the opposite order. There, for all beings lying in the womb, at the time of emerging from the mother\u2019s womb, first the internal wind goes out; then the external wind, carrying subtle dust, enters inside and, striking the palate, ceases. Thus, in the first place, are the in-breaths and out-breaths to be understood.",pt:"Ali, 'ou inspirando longamente' (d\u012bgha\u1e43 v\u0101 assasanto) significa produzindo uma inspira\xe7\xe3o longa. No Coment\xe1rio do Vinaya (Vinaya-a\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101), diz-se: 'Ass\u0101sa \xe9 o ar que sai para fora; pass\u0101sa \xe9 o ar que entra para dentro'. Nos Coment\xe1rios dos Suttas (Suttanta-a\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101), por\xe9m, isso vem na ordem inversa. A esse respeito, para todos os seres nascidos de \xfatero, no momento de sair do \xfatero materno, primeiro o ar interno sai para fora. Depois, o ar externo, carregando poeira fina, entra no interior, toca o palato e cessa. Assim, primeiramente, devem ser compreendidas a inspira\xe7\xe3o e a expira\xe7\xe3o.",es:"En ese pasaje, 'inhalando largo' (d\u012bgha\u1e43 v\u0101 assasanto) se refiere a quien produce una inhalaci\xf3n de larga duraci\xf3n. Seg\xfan se afirma en el Comentario del Vinaya, 'ass\u0101sa' es el aire que sale hacia afuera y 'pass\u0101sa' es el aire que entra hacia adentro. Sin embargo, en los Comentarios de los Suttas, el orden aparece invertido. En ese contexto, para todos los seres que nacen del vientre materno, al momento de salir del vientre de la madre, primero el aire interno sale hacia afuera. Despu\xe9s, el aire externo, trayendo consigo part\xedculas finas de polvo, entra al interior y, tras tocar el paladar, se extingue. De esta manera deben entenderse inicialmente la inhalaci\xf3n y la exhalaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-8.20",pali:"Sabbak\u0101yapa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b assasiss\u0101mi\u2026pe\u2026 passasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhat\u012bti sakalassa ass\u0101sak\u0101yassa \u0101dimajjhapariyos\u0101na\u1e43 vidita\u1e43 karonto p\u0101ka\u1e6da\u1e43 karonto assasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhati. Sakalassa pass\u0101sak\u0101yassa \u0101dimajjhapariyos\u0101na\u1e43 vidita\u1e43 karonto p\u0101ka\u1e6da\u1e43 karonto passasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhati. Eva\u1e43 vidita\u1e43 karonto p\u0101ka\u1e6da\u1e43 karonto \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayuttacittena assasati ceva passasati ca. Tasm\u0101 \"assasiss\u0101mi passasiss\u0101m\u012b\"ti sikkhat\u012bti vuccati. Ekassa hi bhikkhuno cu\u1e47\u1e47avicu\u1e47\u1e47avisa\u1e6de ass\u0101sak\u0101ye pass\u0101sak\u0101ye v\u0101 \u0101di p\u0101ka\u1e6do hoti, na majjhapariyos\u0101na\u1e43. So \u0101dimeva pariggahetu\u1e43 sakkoti, majjhapariyos\u0101ne kilamati. Ekassa majjha\u1e43 p\u0101ka\u1e6da\u1e43 hoti, na \u0101dipariyos\u0101na\u1e43. Ekassa pariyos\u0101na\u1e43 p\u0101ka\u1e6da\u1e43 hoti, na \u0101dimajjha\u1e43. So pariyos\u0101na\u1e43yeva pariggahetu\u1e43 sakkoti, \u0101dimajjhe kilamati. Ekassa sabbampi p\u0101ka\u1e6da\u1e43 hoti, so sabbampi pariggahetu\u1e43 sakkoti, na katthaci kilamati, t\u0101disena bhavitabbanti dassento \u0101ha \u2013 \"sabbak\u0101yapa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b assasiss\u0101m\u012bti\u2026pe\u2026 passasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhat\u012b\"ti.",translations:{en:"\u2018I will breathe in experiencing the whole body\u2026 and so on\u2026 I will breathe out experiencing the whole body,\u2019 thus he trains. He trains thus: \u2018I will breathe in,\u2019 making known and making manifest the beginning, middle, and end of the entire in-breath body. He trains thus: \u2018I will breathe out,\u2019 making known and making manifest the beginning, middle, and end of the entire out-breath body. Thus making them known and manifest, he breathes in and out with a mind conjoined with knowledge. Therefore, he is said to be one who trains thus: \u2018I will breathe in, I will breathe out.\u2019 For one bhikkhu, with an in-breath body or out-breath body that is broken up and dispersed, the beginning is manifest, but not the middle and end. He is able to grasp only the beginning; he struggles with the middle and end. For another, the middle is manifest, but not the beginning and end. For another, the end is manifest, but not the beginning and middle. He is able to grasp only the end; he struggles with the beginning and middle. For another, the whole of it is manifest; he is able to grasp the whole of it and does not struggle anywhere. To show that one should become like this, it is said: \u2018He trains, \u201cI will breathe in experiencing the whole body\u2026 and so on\u2026 I will breathe out experiencing the whole body.\u201d\u2019",pt:"A frase 'Treinando-se assim: Experienciando todo o corpo, inspirarei... [pe]... expirarei' significa que ele treina para inspirar tornando conhecido e claro o in\xedcio, o meio e o fim de todo o corpo da inspira\xe7\xe3o. Ele treina para expirar tornando conhecido e claro o in\xedcio, o meio e o fim de todo o corpo da expira\xe7\xe3o. Tornando-os assim conhecidos e claros, ele inspira e expira com uma mente associada ao conhecimento (\xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayuttacitta). Por isso se diz: 'ele treina: inspirarei, expirarei'. Pois, para um certo monge, no corpo da inspira\xe7\xe3o ou no corpo da expira\xe7\xe3o que se dispersa em part\xedculas extremamente sutis, apenas o in\xedcio \xe9 claro, mas n\xe3o o meio e o fim. Ele \xe9 capaz de apreender apenas o in\xedcio, e se cansa no meio e no fim. Para outro, apenas o meio \xe9 claro, mas n\xe3o o in\xedcio e o fim. Para outro, apenas o fim \xe9 claro, mas n\xe3o o in\xedcio e o meio; ele \xe9 capaz de apreender apenas o fim, e se cansa no in\xedcio e no meio. Para outro, tudo \xe9 claro; ele \xe9 capaz de apreender tudo e n\xe3o se cansa em parte alguma. Para mostrar que se deve ser como este \xfaltimo tipo de pessoa, [o Buda] disse: 'Treinando-se assim: Experienciando todo o corpo, inspirarei... [pe]... expirarei'.",es:"'Experimentando todo el cuerpo inhalar\xe9... exhalar\xe9', as\xed entrena; esto significa que hace conocido y claro el principio, el medio y el fin de todo el cuerpo de la inhalaci\xf3n mientras entrena diciendo 'inhalar\xe9'. Hace conocido y claro el principio, el medio y el fin de todo el cuerpo de la exhalaci\xf3n mientras entrena diciendo 'exhalar\xe9'. Haci\xe9ndolo conocido y claro de esta manera, inhala y exhala con una mente asociada al conocimiento. Por eso se dice que entrena diciendo 'inhalar\xe9 y exhalar\xe9'. Pues para un monje, cuando el cuerpo de la inhalaci\xf3n o exhalaci\xf3n se dispersa en m\xfaltiples part\xedculas, el principio es claro, pero no el medio ni el fin. \xc9l puede captar solo el principio y se fatiga en el medio y el fin. Para otro monje, el medio es claro, pero no el principio ni el fin. Para otro, el fin es claro, pero no el principio ni el medio. \xc9l puede captar solo el fin y se fatiga en el principio y el medio. Para otro monje, todo es claro; \xe9l puede captar todo y no se fatiga en ninguna parte. Para mostrar que uno debe llegar a ser como este \xfaltimo, se dijo: 'Experimentando todo el cuerpo inhalar\xe9... exhalar\xe9, as\xed entrena'."}},{id:"vism-8.21",pali:"Passambhaya\u1e43 k\u0101yasa\u1e45kh\u0101ra\u1e43 assasiss\u0101m\u012bti\u2026pe\u2026 passasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhat\u012bti o\u1e37\u0101rika\u1e43 k\u0101yasa\u1e45kh\u0101ra\u1e43 passambhento pa\u1e6dippassambhento nirodhento v\u016bpasamento assasiss\u0101mi passasiss\u0101m\u012bti sikkhati. Tatra eva\u1e43 o\u1e37\u0101rikasukhumat\u0101 ca passaddhi ca veditabb\u0101. Imassa hi bhikkhuno pubbe apariggahitak\u0101le k\u0101yo ca citta\xf1ca sadarath\u0101 honti o\u1e37\u0101rik\u0101. K\u0101yacitt\u0101na\u1e43 o\u1e37\u0101rikatte av\u016bpasante ass\u0101sapass\u0101s\u0101pi o\u1e37\u0101rik\u0101 honti, balavatar\u0101 hutv\u0101 pavattanti, n\u0101sik\u0101 nappahoti, mukhena assasantopi passasantopi ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhati. Yad\u0101 panassa k\u0101yopi cittampi pariggahit\u0101 honti, tad\u0101 te sant\u0101 honti v\u016bpasant\u0101. Tesu v\u016bpasantesu ass\u0101sapass\u0101s\u0101 sukhum\u0101 hutv\u0101 pavattanti, \"atthi nu kho natth\u012b\"ti vicetabbat\u0101k\u0101rappatt\u0101 honti.",translations:{en:"'I will breathe in calming the bodily formation... I will breathe out calming the bodily formation,' thus he trains. He trains thus: 'I will breathe in... I will breathe out,' while calming, tranquillizing, causing to cease, and pacifying the gross bodily formation. Herein, grossness, subtlety, and tranquillity should be understood thus. For before this bhikkhu has apprehended the meditation subject, his body and mind are agitated and gross. When the grossness of body and mind is unpacified, the in-breaths and out-breaths are also gross; they occur with great force. The nose is not sufficient, and he stands breathing in and out through the mouth. But when his body and mind are apprehended, they become peaceful and especially pacified. When they are pacified, the in-breaths and out-breaths occur subtly, reaching a state where one must investigate whether they exist or not.",pt:"A frase 'Tranquilizando a forma\xe7\xe3o do corpo (k\u0101yasa\u1e45kh\u0101ra), inspirarei... [pe]... expirarei' significa que ele treina para inspirar e expirar acalmando, tranquilizando ainda mais, cessando e apaziguando a forma\xe7\xe3o grosseira do corpo. A esse respeito, a natureza grosseira e sutil, bem como a tranquiliza\xe7\xe3o, devem ser compreendidas da seguinte forma: anteriormente, no momento em que este monge ainda n\xe3o havia apreendido [o objeto de medita\xe7\xe3o], seu corpo e sua mente estavam cansados e eram grosseiros. Quando a natureza grosseira do corpo e da mente n\xe3o est\xe1 apaziguada, a inspira\xe7\xe3o e a expira\xe7\xe3o tamb\xe9m s\xe3o grosseiras, ocorrendo com mais for\xe7a; as narinas n\xe3o s\xe3o suficientes, e ele permanece inspirando e expirando pela boca. No entanto, quando seu corpo e sua mente s\xe3o apreendidos, eles se tornam calmos e apaziguados. Com o apaziguamento deles, a inspira\xe7\xe3o e a expira\xe7\xe3o ocorrem de forma sutil, chegando a um estado em que se deve investigar: 'Ser\xe1 que existem ou n\xe3o?'.",es:"'Tranquilizando la formaci\xf3n corporal inhalar\xe9... exhalar\xe9', as\xed entrena; esto significa que entrena para inhalar y exhalar calmando, apaciguando, cesando y tranquilizando la formaci\xf3n corporal densa (o\u1e37\u0101rika, las respiraciones bastas). En este punto, debe entenderse la naturaleza de lo denso y lo sutil, y la tranquilidad de la siguiente manera: antes de que este monje haya captado el objeto de meditaci\xf3n, tanto su cuerpo como su mente est\xe1n inquietos y son densos. Al no estar calmada la densidad del cuerpo y la mente, las inhalaciones y exhalaciones tambi\xe9n son densas, ocurren con gran fuerza, las fosas nasales no son suficientes y llega a respirar incluso por la boca. Pero cuando su cuerpo y mente han sido captados por la meditaci\xf3n, entonces est\xe1n en paz y tranquilos. Al estar estos tranquilos, las inhalaciones y exhalaciones ocurren de manera sutil, llegando a un estado en el que uno debe examinar y preguntarse: '\xbfexisten realmente o no existen?'."}},{id:"vism-8.22",pali:"Ga\u1e47an\u0101 anubandhan\u0101, phusan\u0101 \u1e6dhapan\u0101 sallakkha\u1e47\u0101; Viva\u1e6d\u1e6dan\u0101 p\u0101risuddhi, tesa\xf1ca pa\u1e6dipassan\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Counting and following, touching and fixing, observing, turning away, purification, and the reviewing of them.",pt:"Contagem, acompanhamento, toque, fixa\xe7\xe3o, observa\xe7\xe3o; desapego, purifica\xe7\xe3o e a revis\xe3o de cada um deles.",es:"Conteo (ga\u1e47an\u0101), seguimiento (anubandhan\u0101), contacto (phusan\u0101), fijaci\xf3n (\u1e6dhapan\u0101), observaci\xf3n (sallakkha\u1e47\u0101), giro (viva\u1e6d\u1e6dan\u0101), purificaci\xf3n (p\u0101risuddhi) y la revisi\xf3n de estos (pa\u1e6dipassan\u0101)."}},{id:"vism-8.23",pali:"Tattha imin\u0101 \u0101dikammikena kulaputtena pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 ga\u1e47an\u0101ya ida\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 manasi k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Ga\u1e47entena ca pa\xf1canna\u1e43 he\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101 na \u1e6dhapetabba\u1e43. Dasanna\u1e43 upari na netabba\u1e43. Antar\u0101 kha\u1e47\u1e0da\u1e43 na dassetabba\u1e43. Pa\xf1canna\u1e43 he\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101 \u1e6dhapentassa hi samb\u0101dhe ok\u0101se cittupp\u0101do vipphandati samb\u0101dhe vaje sanniruddhagoga\u1e47o viya. Dasannampi upari nentassa ga\u1e47ananissitako cittupp\u0101do hoti. Antar\u0101 kha\u1e47\u1e0da\u1e43 dassentassa \"sikh\u0101ppatta\u1e43 nu kho me kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, no\"ti citta\u1e43 vikampati. Tasm\u0101 ete dose vajjetv\u0101 ga\u1e47etabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Here, this clansman who is a beginner should first apply his mind to this meditation subject by means of counting. When counting, he should not stop below five and should not go beyond ten. He should not show a break in the middle. For one who stops below five, the mind flutters in the confined space like a herd of cattle shut up in a narrow pen. For one who goes beyond ten, the mind becomes dependent on the counting. For one who shows a break in the middle, his mind wavers, wondering: \u2018Has my meditation subject reached its culmination or not?\u2019 Therefore, one should count avoiding these faults.",pt:"Nisso, o jovem de boa fam\xedlia que \xe9 iniciante deve primeiro aplicar a aten\xe7\xe3o a este tema de medita\xe7\xe3o por meio da contagem. E, ao contar, ele n\xe3o deve parar abaixo de cinco, n\xe3o deve ir al\xe9m de dez, e n\xe3o deve permitir nenhuma interrup\xe7\xe3o no intervalo. Pois, para quem para abaixo de cinco, o surgimento da mente agita-se em um espa\xe7o estreito, como um rebanho de vacas trancado em um curral apertado. Para quem vai al\xe9m de dez, o surgimento da mente torna-se dependente apenas da contagem. E para quem permite uma interrup\xe7\xe3o no intervalo, a mente vacila pensando: \u2018Ser\xe1 que meu tema de medita\xe7\xe3o atingiu o \xe1pice ou n\xe3o?\u2019. Portanto, deve-se contar evitando esses defeitos.",es:"En ese proceso, este hijo de buena familia que es principiante debe aplicar la mente a este objeto de meditaci\xf3n primero mediante el conteo. Al contar, no debe detenerse por debajo de cinco ni exceder de diez. No debe dejar huecos en medio. Pues para quien se detiene por debajo de cinco, el pensamiento se agita en un espacio confinado, como un grupo de vacas encerradas en un establo estrecho. Para quien excede de diez, el pensamiento se vuelve dependiente \xfanicamente del conteo. Para quien deja un hueco en medio, la mente vacila pensando: '\xbfHa llegado mi meditaci\xf3n a su culminaci\xf3n o no?'. Por lo tanto, debe contar evitando estos defectos."}},{id:"vism-8.24",pali:"\"Nimitta\u1e43 ass\u0101sapass\u0101s\u0101, an\u0101ramma\u1e47amekacittassa; Aj\u0101nato ca tayo dhamme, bh\u0101van\u0101 nupalabbhati.",translations:{en:"'The sign, the in-breaths and out-breaths, are not the object of a single consciousness; and for one who does not know these three things, development is not obtained.'",pt:"\u201cO sinal, a inspira\xe7\xe3o e a expira\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o s\xe3o o objeto de uma \xfanica mente; para quem n\xe3o conhece esses tr\xeas fatores, o desenvolvimento da medita\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o \xe9 obtido.\u201d",es:"\xabEl signo, la inhalaci\xf3n y la exhalaci\xf3n no son objetos de una sola mente; para quien no conoce estos tres fealidades, la meditaci\xf3n no se obtiene\xbb."}},{id:"vism-8.25",pali:"Tassevamanuyu\xf1jato na cirasseva nimitta\u1e43 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Ta\u1e43 paneta\u1e43 na sabbesa\u1e43 ekasadisa\u1e43 hoti. Apica kho kassaci sukhasamphassa\u1e43 upp\u0101dayam\u0101no t\u016blapicu viya kapp\u0101sapicu viya v\u0101tadh\u0101r\u0101 viya ca upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101t\u012bti ekacce \u0101hu.",translations:{en:"For one who applies himself in this way, the sign appears in no long time. This sign, however, is not the same for everyone. Moreover, some say that for a certain person it appears producing a pleasant contact, like silk-cotton, like cotton, or like a current of wind.",pt:"Para aquele que se aplica dessa maneira, em pouco tempo o sinal (nimitta) se manifesta. No entanto, esse sinal n\xe3o \xe9 id\xeantico para todos. De fato, alguns dizem que, para certos praticantes, ele se manifesta produzindo uma sensa\xe7\xe3o de toque agrad\xe1vel, como um tufo de algod\xe3o de seda, um tufo de algod\xe3o comum ou uma corrente de vento.",es:"A aquel que practica de esta manera, en poco tiempo se le manifiesta el signo (nimitta). Sin embargo, este signo no es id\xe9ntico para todos. Por el contrario, algunos maestros afirman que para algunos se manifiesta produciendo una sensaci\xf3n placentera, como una mota de algod\xf3n, como una fibra de seda o como una corriente de aire."}}]},426,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,s,i,t,n){i.exports=[{id:"vism-9.1",pali:"Anussatikamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101nantara\u1e43 uddi\u1e6d\u1e6dhesu pana mett\u0101, karu\u1e47\u0101, mudit\u0101, upekkh\u0101ti imesu cat\u016bsu brahmavih\u0101resu metta\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena t\u0101va \u0101dikammikena yog\u0101vacarena upacchinnapalibodhena gahitakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nena bhattakicca\u1e43 katv\u0101 bhattasammada\u1e43 pa\u1e6divinodetv\u0101 vivitte padese supa\xf1\xf1atte \u0101sane sukhanisinnena \u0101dito t\u0101va dose \u0101d\u012bnavo, khantiya\xf1ca \u0101nisa\u1e43so paccavekkhitabbo.",translations:{en:"Now, following the recollection meditation subjects that were taught, among these four divine abidings\u2014loving-kindness, compassion, appreciative joy, and equanimity\u2014a beginner yogi who wishes to develop loving-kindness should first, having cut off the impediments and taken up a meditation subject from a teacher, having completed his duties concerning the meal and dispelled his drowsiness from the meal, sit down comfortably in a secluded place on a well-prepared seat. To begin with, the danger in aversion and the benefit in patience should be reviewed.",pt:"Entre as quatro moradas divinas mencionadas logo ap\xf3s os temas de medita\xe7\xe3o das recorda\xe7\xf5es \u2014 a saber, amor-bondade (mett\u0101), compaix\xe3o (karu\u1e47\u0101), alegria altru\xedsta (mudit\u0101) e equanimidade (upekkh\u0101) \u2014, o praticante iniciante (\u0101dikammika yog\u0101vacara) que deseja desenvolver o amor-bondade deve primeiro cortar os seus impedimentos (palibodha), receber o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o de seu mestre, realizar a sua refei\xe7\xe3o di\xe1ria, afastar a sonol\xeancia p\xf3s-prandial e, sentando-se confortavelmente em um assento bem preparado em um local solit\xe1rio, refletir primeiramente sobre os perigos da avers\xe3o (dosa) e os benef\xedcios da paci\xeancia (khanti).",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s de los temas de meditaci\xf3n de los recuerdos, entre las cuatro moradas divinas mencionadas \u2014amor benevolente, compasi\xf3n, alegr\xeda altruista y ecuanimidad\u2014, el practicante principiante que desea desarrollar el amor benevolente, habiendo cortado sus impedimentos y habiendo recibido el tema de meditaci\xf3n, despu\xe9s de terminar su comida y disipar la somnolencia posterior, sentado c\xf3modamente en un lugar solitario en un asiento bien preparado, debe primero reflexionar sobre el peligro del odio y los beneficios de la paciencia."}},{id:"vism-9.2",pali:"Aya\xf1hi mett\u0101 appiyapuggale, atippiyasah\u0101yake, majjhatte, ver\u012bpuggaleti imesu cat\u016bsu puggalesu \u0101dito na bh\u0101vetabb\u0101. Li\u1e45gavisabh\u0101ge ca ekantato \u0101rabbha na bh\u0101vetabb\u0101. K\u0101lakate ca na bh\u0101vetabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"For this loving-kindness should not be developed at first towards these four kinds of persons: an unloved person, an overly dear companion, a neutral person, and a hostile person. And it should definitely not be developed specifically towards a person of the opposite sex, nor should it be developed towards a dead person.",pt:"Pois esta medita\xe7\xe3o sobre o amor-bondade n\xe3o deve ser desenvolvida de in\xedcio em rela\xe7\xe3o a quatro tipos de pessoas: uma pessoa desagrad\xe1vel, um companheiro excessivamente querido, uma pessoa neutra e uma pessoa hostil (inimigo). E, de modo absoluto, n\xe3o deve ser desenvolvida individualmente em rela\xe7\xe3o a uma pessoa do sexo oposto, nem em rela\xe7\xe3o a uma pessoa falecida.",es:"Pues el amor benevolente no debe desarrollarse al principio hacia cuatro tipos de personas: una persona que no sea grata, un amigo excesivamente querido, una persona neutral o una persona enemiga. Tampoco debe desarrollarse de manera espec\xedfica hacia alguien del sexo opuesto, ni hacia una persona fallecida."}},{id:"vism-9.3",pali:"Tasm\u0101 sakkhibh\u0101vattha\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 att\u0101na\u1e43 mett\u0101ya pharitv\u0101 tadanantara\u1e43 sukhasampattiy\u0101 paccakkhibh\u0101vattha\u1e43 p\u0101s\u0101dikat\u0101ya ca garubh\u0101van\u012byapuggale t\u0101va \u0101cariyupajjh\u0101yas\u0101disu pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 mett\u0101 bh\u0101vetabb\u0101 \u2018\u2018aya\u1e43 sappuriso sukh\u012b hotu, niddukkho\u2019\u2019ti\u0101din\u0101 nayena. Evar\u016bpe hi puggale mett\u0101 bh\u0101ventassa sukheneva sam\u0101dhi uppajjati.",translations:{en:"Therefore, for the sake of being a witness, one should first pervade oneself with loving-kindness; immediately following that, for the sake of making happiness and success evident, and because they inspire confidence and reverence, loving-kindness should first be developed towards a venerable person, such as a teacher or preceptor, in this manner: 'May this good person be happy and free from suffering.' For one developing loving-kindness towards such a person, concentration arises with ease.",pt:"Portanto, a t\xedtulo de testemunha (sakkhibh\u0101va), deve-se primeiro impregnar a si mesmo com o amor-bondade. Imediatamente a seguir, a fim de tornar evidente a realiza\xe7\xe3o da felicidade e por inspirar f\xe9 e rever\xeancia, o amor-bondade deve ser desenvolvido inicialmente para com uma pessoa vener\xe1vel, semelhante a um mestre ou preceptor, da seguinte forma: 'Que este nobre indiv\xedduo seja feliz e livre do sofrimento'. Pois para quem desenvolve o amor-bondade em rela\xe7\xe3o a uma pessoa desse tipo, a concentra\xe7\xe3o surge com muita facilidade.",es:"Por lo tanto, para servir de testigo directo a uno mismo, primero se debe impregnar a uno mismo con amor benevolente. Inmediatamente despu\xe9s, para hacer patente la obtenci\xf3n de la felicidad y por su cualidad inspiradora, se debe desarrollar primero el amor benevolente hacia personas dignas de reverencia, como el maestro o el preceptor, de esta manera: 'Que esta persona noble sea feliz y est\xe9 libre de sufrimiento'. En efecto, para quien desarrolla el amor benevolente hacia una persona de tal condici\xf3n, la concentraci\xf3n surge con facilidad."}},{id:"vism-9.4",pali:"Sace panassa verimhi cittamupasa\u1e43harato tena kat\u0101par\u0101dh\u0101nussara\u1e47ena pa\u1e6digha\u1e43 uppajjati, tena punappuna\u1e43 purimup\u0101yena ekasmi\u1e43 puggale mett\u0101sam\u0101patti\u1e43 upp\u0101detv\u0101 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya \u2018\u2018yato me ver\u012bpuggale kopo uppajjati, hand\u0101ha\u1e43 ta\u1e43 pa\u1e6digha\u1e43 v\u016bpasameyy\u0101\u2019\u2019ti tassa satthu ov\u0101do paccavekkhitabbo.",translations:{en:"If, however, while directing his mind toward an enemy, resentment arises in him through recollecting wrongs done by that person, he should repeatedly enter the attainment of loving-kindness towards one of the previously mentioned persons, emerge from it, and reflect on the advice of the Teacher: 'Whenever anger arises in me towards an enemy, let me pacify that resentment.'",pt:"Se, no entanto, ao direcionar a mente para uma pessoa hostil, surgir ressentimento pela lembran\xe7a das ofensas por ela cometidas, o praticante deve reiteradamente alcan\xe7ar a absor\xe7\xe3o de amor-bondade com rela\xe7\xe3o a uma das pessoas anteriormente mencionadas, emergir dela e refletir na exorta\xe7\xe3o do Mestre: 'Visto que em mim surge a raiva para com uma pessoa hostil, deverei eu agora apaziguar esse ressentimento'.",es:"Si al dirigir la mente hacia el enemigo surge el enojo por el recuerdo de las ofensas cometidas por \xe9l, el monje debe alcanzar repetidamente la absorci\xf3n de benevolencia hacia las personas mencionadas anteriormente y, al salir de ella, debe reflexionar en las instrucciones del Maestro pensando: 'Puesto que me surge ira hacia una persona enemiga, ciertamente calmar\xe9 ese resentimiento'."}},{id:"vism-9.5",pali:"Sace pana evampi citta\u1e43 nibb\u0101petu\u1e43 na sakkotiyeva, ath\u0101nena eva\u1e43 mett\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101ya va\u1e47\u1e47abha\u1e47ane bhagavato paricita\xf1ca bahula\xf1ca katv\u0101 sucarita\u1e43 suttanta\u1e43 mah\u0101nubh\u0101va\u1e43 kakac\u016bpamasutta\u1e43 (ma. ni. 1.237 \u0101dayo) anussaritabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"But if one is still unable to appease one\u2019s mind even in this way, one should then recollect the Kakac\u016bpama Sutta (The Simile of the Saw), a discourse of great power thoroughly familiarized and frequently practiced in praising the development of loving-kindness by the Blessed One.",pt:"Se, contudo, mesmo assim n\xe3o for poss\xedvel acalmar a mente, deve-se ent\xe3o recordar o Kakac\u016bpama Sutta (O Discurso sobre o S\xedmile da Serra), um sutta de grande poder, amplamente conhecido e praticado, no qual o Aben\xe7oado louva o desenvolvimento do amor-bondade.",es:"Si a pesar de ello todav\xeda no puede apaciguar la mente, entonces debe recordar el kakac\u016bpamasutta (el s\xedmil de la sierra), un discurso de gran poder, ampliamente familiar y frecuentado por el Bienaventurado para alabar el desarrollo del amor benevolente."}},{id:"vism-9.6",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 ver\u012bpuggale v\u016bpasantapa\u1e6dighassa yath\u0101 piy\u0101tippiyasah\u0101yakamajjhattesu, eva\u1e43 ver\u012bpuggale ca muducitta\u1e43 sampajjati mett\u0101ppavattiya\u1e43. Tato para\u1e43 tena attani, piye, majjhatte, verimhiti imesu cat\u016bsu puggalesu samacittat\u0101ya s\u012bm\u0101sambhedo k\u0101tabbo.",translations:{en:"For that yogi, when aversion towards a hostile person has been pacified, his mind becomes pliant in radiating loving-kindness towards the hostile person, just as towards the dear, the very dear companion, and the neutral person. Thereafter, he should break down the barriers by achieving impartiality towards these four persons: himself, the dear person, the neutral person, and the hostile person.",pt:"Para aquele iogue, quando a avers\xe3o em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 pessoa hostil estiver assim apaziguada, a sua mente torna-se male\xe1vel no fluxo do amor-bondade para com a pessoa hostil, exatamente como para com o amigo querido, o companheiro muito querido e a pessoa neutra. Depois disso, ele deve realizar a quebra de fronteiras (s\u012bm\u0101sambheda), desenvolvendo equanimidade mental para com estas quatro pessoas: a si mesmo, o amigo, a pessoa neutra e a pessoa hostil.",es:"Para ese yogui, habi\xe9ndose apaciguado la aversi\xf3n hacia el enemigo de este modo, su mente se vuelve d\xf3cil en la irradiaci\xf3n del amor benevolente hacia el enemigo tanto como hacia el amigo, el amigo entra\xf1able y la persona neutral. A partir de entonces, mediante la ecuanimidad mental hacia estas cuatro clases de personas: \xe9l mismo, el querido, el neutral y el enemigo, debe llevar a cabo la disoluci\xf3n de los l\xedmites (s\u012bm\u0101sambheda)."}},{id:"vism-9.7",pali:"So hi pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101n\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataravasena mett\u0101sahagatena cetas\u0101 eka\u1e43 disa\u1e43 pharitv\u0101 viharati, tath\u0101 dutiya\u1e43, tath\u0101 tatiya\u1e43, tath\u0101 catuttha\u1e43. Iti uddhamadho tiriya\u1e43 sabbadhi sabbattat\u0101ya sabb\u0101vanta\u1e43 loka\u1e43 mett\u0101sahagatena cetas\u0101 vipulena mahaggatena appam\u0101\u1e47ena averena aby\u0101pajjena pharitv\u0101 viharati.",translations:{en:"Truly, that yogi dwells pervading one direction with a mind accompanied by loving-kindness by means of one of the jh\u0101nas such as the first, likewise the second, the third, and the fourth. Thus above, below, around, everywhere, identifying oneself with all, he pervades the all-encompassing world with a mind accompanied by loving-kindness, vast, exalted, immeasurable, free from enmity, free from affliction.",pt:"Deveras, aquele iogue habita permeando uma dire\xe7\xe3o com uma mente acompanhada de amor-bondade, por meio de qualquer um dos jh\u0101nas a partir do primeiro, assim como a segunda dire\xe7\xe3o, a terceira e a quarta. Assim para cima, para baixo, transversalmente, em toda a extens\xe3o, identificando-se com todos, ele habita permeando o mundo inteiro com uma mente acompanhada de amor-bondade, ampla, sublime, ilimitada, livre de inimizade e livre de afli\xe7\xe3o.",es:"En verdad, aquel yogui mora habiendo impregnado una direcci\xf3n con una mente acompa\xf1ada de amor benevolente mediante alguno de los jh\u0101nas, a saber, el primero u otros; del mismo modo la segunda direcci\xf3n, del mismo modo la tercera, del mismo modo la cuarta. As\xed, hacia arriba, hacia abajo, alrededor, en todas partes, reconoci\xe9ndose id\xe9ntico a todos, mora habiendo impregnado al mundo entero con una mente acompa\xf1ada de amor benevolente, amplia, sublime, ilimitada, sin enemistad y libre de aflicci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-9.8",pali:"Tattha ca sabbe satt\u0101 aver\u0101 aby\u0101pajj\u0101 an\u012bgh\u0101 sukh\u012b att\u0101na\u1e43 pariharant\u016bti ayamek\u0101 anodhiso phara\u1e47\u0101 mett\u0101cetovimutti. Sabbe p\u0101\u1e47\u0101\u2026 sabbe bh\u016bt\u0101\u2026 sabbe puggal\u0101\u2026 sabbe attabh\u0101vapariy\u0101pann\u0101 aver\u0101 aby\u0101pajj\u0101 an\u012bgh\u0101 sukh\u012b att\u0101na\u1e43 pariharant\u016bti im\u0101 pa\xf1ca anodhiso phara\u1e47\u0101 mett\u0101cetovimuttiyo.",translations:{en:"And therein, 'May all beings be free from enmity, free from affliction, free from trouble, and maintain themselves in happiness': this is one unspecified pervasion of loving-kindness as mental liberation. 'May all living beings... all creatures... all persons... all those who have an individuality be free from enmity, free from affliction, free from trouble, and maintain themselves in happiness': these are the five unspecified pervasions of loving-kindness as mental liberation.",pt:"E nisso: 'Que todos os seres estejam livres de inimizade, livres de afli\xe7\xe3o, livres de sofrimento, que vivam felizes cuidando de si mesmos' \u2014 esta \xe9 uma das formas de irradia\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o delimitada (anodhiso phara\u1e47\u0101) da liberta\xe7\xe3o mental pelo amor-bondade. 'Que todos os seres que respiram... todos os que foram gerados... todas as pessoas... todos os que possuem uma individualidade estejam livres de inimizade, livres de afli\xe7\xe3o, livres de sofrimento, que vivam felizes cuidando de si mesmos' \u2014 estas s\xe3o as cinco irradia\xe7\xf5es n\xe3o delimitadas da liberta\xe7\xe3o mental pelo amor-bondade.",es:"Y en ello: \xabQue todos los seres est\xe9n libres de enemistad, libres de aflicci\xf3n, libres de angustia y cuiden de s\xed mismos con felicidad\xbb: esta es una de las liberaciones de la mente mediante el amor benevolente de irradiaci\xf3n inespec\xedfica. \xabQue todos los seres con aliento... todos los seres creados... todas las personas... todos los poseedores de una individualidad est\xe9n libres de enemistad, libres de aflicci\xf3n, libres de angustia y cuiden de s\xed mismos con felicidad\xbb: estas son las cinco liberaciones de la mente mediante el amor benevolente de irradiaci\xf3n inespec\xedfica."}},{id:"vism-9.9",pali:"N\u0101ssa aggi v\u0101 visa\u1e43 v\u0101 sattha\u1e43 v\u0101 kamat\u012bti mett\u0101vih\u0101rissa sar\u012bre aggi v\u0101 visa\u1e43 v\u0101 sattha\u1e43 v\u0101 na kramati, na pavisati, anupak\u0101rakameva hutv\u0101 patati. Sukha\u1e43 supati, sukha\u1e43 pa\u1e6dibujjhati, na p\u0101paka\u1e43 supina\u1e43 passati, manuss\u0101na\u1e43 piyo hoti, amanuss\u0101na\u1e43 piyo hoti, devat\u0101 rakkhanti, tuva\u1e6da\u1e43 citta\u1e43 sam\u0101dhiyati, mukhava\u1e47\u1e47o vippas\u012bdati, asamm\u016b\u1e37ho k\u0101la\u1e43 karoti, uttari\u1e43 appa\u1e6divijjhanto brahmalok\u016bpago hoti.",translations:{en:"'Fire, poison, or a weapon does not affect him' means: For one who dwells in loving-kindness, neither fire, poison, nor a weapon harms or penetrates the body; falling harmlessly, it has no effect. He sleeps in comfort, wakes in comfort, sees no bad dreams, is dear to human beings, is dear to non-human beings, the devas protect him, his mind is quickly concentrated, his complexion is clear, he dies unconfused, and if he penetrates no higher, he is destined for the Brahma world.",pt:"'Fogo, veneno ou arma n\xe3o o atingem': no corpo daquele que habita no amor-bondade, nem o fogo, nem o veneno, nem a arma causam dano ou penetram; caem sem produzir efeito. Ele dorme feliz, acorda feliz, n\xe3o tem sonhos ruins, \xe9 querido pelos seres humanos, \xe9 querido pelos seres n\xe3o humanos, os devas o protegem, a sua mente se concentra com rapidez, a sua complei\xe7\xe3o facial \xe9 radiante, morre sem confus\xe3o e, se n\xe3o alcan\xe7ar realiza\xe7\xf5es superiores, renasce no mundo de Brahma.",es:"\xabNi el fuego, ni el veneno, ni el arma le hieren\xbb: en el cuerpo de quien mora en el amor benevolente, ni el fuego, ni el veneno, ni las armas causan efecto o penetran, sino que caen haci\xe9ndose inocuos. Duerme feliz, despierta feliz, no tiene malos sue\xf1os, es querido por los humanos, es querido por los no humanos, los devas lo protegen, la mente se le concentra r\xe1pidamente, el semblante se le apacigua, muere sin confusi\xf3n y, si no penetra m\xe1s alto, renace en el mundo de Brahma."}},{id:"vism-9.10",pali:"Karu\u1e47a\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena pana nikkaru\u1e47at\u0101ya \u0101d\u012bnava\u1e43 karu\u1e47\u0101ya ca \u0101nisa\u1e43sa\u1e43 paccavekkhitv\u0101 karu\u1e47\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101yeva kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101d\u0101t\u0101yya d\u0101\u1e37iddiyaappas\u0101dikabh\u0101v\u0101divasena asmi\u1e43 loke d\u012bnadukkhite apaviddhe puggale pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 karu\u1e47\u0101 upp\u0101detabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, one who wishes to develop compassion should reflect on the danger of cruelty and the benefit of compassion, take up the meditation subject through the development of compassion itself, and first arouse compassion towards a miserable, suffering, abandoned person in this world, due to poverty, deformities, and the like.",pt:"Aquele que deseja cultivar a compaix\xe3o deve, ap\xf3s refletir sobre os perigos da crueldade e os benef\xedcios da compaix\xe3o, assumir o pr\xf3prio desenvolvimento da compaix\xe3o como tema de medita\xe7\xe3o. Inicialmente, ele deve despertar a compaix\xe3o em rela\xe7\xe3o a um indiv\xedduo desamparado e aflito neste mundo, abatido pela pobreza, desgra\xe7a e mis\xe9ria extrema.",es:"Por su parte, quien desea desarrollar la compasi\xf3n, tras reflexionar sobre los peligros de la falta de piedad y los beneficios de la compasi\xf3n, habiendo tomado el tema de meditaci\xf3n a trav\xe9s del desarrollo de la compasi\xf3n misma, debe suscitar compasi\xf3n en primer t\xe9rmino hacia una persona desvalida y sufriente en este mundo, a causa de la pobreza, la deformidad y el infortunio."}},{id:"vism-9.11",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Seyyath\u0101pi saha bha\u1e47\u1e0dena gahitacora\u1e43 \u2018\u2018vadhetha na\u2019\u2019nti ra\xf1\xf1o \u0101\u1e47\u0101ya vadhak\u0101 pacch\u0101b\u0101ha\u1e43 b\u0101\u1e37habandhana\u1e43 bandhitv\u0101 pa\u1e6dikha\xf1jehi kas\u0101hi t\u0101\u1e37etv\u0101 pacchim\u0101ya v\u012bthiy\u0101 \u0101gh\u0101tana\u1e43 nenti, tamena\u1e43 passanto manusso \u2018\u2018aho vata ima\u1e43 dukkha\u1e43 p\u0101papunno anubhava\u2019\u2019ti karu\u1e47a\u1e43 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101peti, tatheva sabbasattesu k\u0101yavac\u012bmanokammehi dukkhit\u0101 an\u0101th\u0101 ete dukkhinoti karu\u1e47\u0101 pavattitabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"How so? Suppose royal men have caught a thief with the stolen goods. On the king's order, 'Execute him,' the executioners tie his arms tightly behind him, beat him with whips at every step, and take him through the western street to the place of execution. A person seeing him arouses compassion: 'Alas! This wretch undergoes great suffering!' Even so, compassion should be directed towards all beings who through bodily, verbal, and mental actions are subject to suffering and without refuge.",pt:"Como isso se d\xe1? Suponha que os carrascos, sob a ordem real 'executai-o', tenham capturado um ladr\xe3o em posse do fruto de seu roubo. Amarram-lhe firmemente os bra\xe7os para tr\xe1s e, a\xe7oitando-o duramente a cada esquina, conduzem-no pela rua oeste ao local de execu\xe7\xe3o. Uma pessoa que v\xea isso desperta compaix\xe3o: 'Ah, qu\xe3o terr\xedvel \xe9 o sofrimento que este infeliz suporta!'. Da mesma forma, deve-se estender a compaix\xe3o a todos os seres que, por a\xe7\xf5es do corpo, fala e mente, s\xe3o afligidos pelo sofrimento e encontram-se desamparados.",es:"\xbfC\xf3mo es esto? As\xed como cuando los verdugos, habiendo capturado a un ladr\xf3n con lo robado, por orden del rey 'matadlo', le atan fuertemente los brazos a la espalda y azot\xe1ndolo con l\xe1tigos a cada paso lo llevan por la calle occidental al lugar de ejecuci\xf3n, una persona que lo ve siente compasi\xf3n diciendo: '\xa1Ay, qu\xe9 sufrimiento padece este infeliz!'; as\xed tambi\xe9n se debe manifestar compasi\xf3n hacia todos los seres, reconociendo que a trav\xe9s de las acciones de cuerpo, habla y mente est\xe1n afligidos y sin amparo."}},{id:"vism-9.12",pali:"Mudit\u0101bh\u0101vana\u1e43 \u0101rabhanten\u0101pi na pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 piyapuggal\u0101d\u012bsu \u0101rabhitabb\u0101. Atippiyasah\u0101yako pana siy\u0101 pada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, ta\u1e43 disv\u0101 v\u0101 sutv\u0101 v\u0101 \u2018\u2018aya\u1e43 satto sukhito modati, s\u0101dhu vata, aho su\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u016b\u2019\u2019ti mudit\u0101 upp\u0101detabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Even when beginning the development of sympathetic joy, one should not begin with an unloved person and so forth. However, a very dear companion can be a proximate cause. Having seen or heard of him, one should arouse sympathetic joy: 'This being is happy and rejoices; how good indeed! How wonderful!'",pt:"Aquele que come\xe7a o cultivo da alegria altru\xedsta tamb\xe9m n\xe3o deve inici\xe1-lo por uma pessoa odiada e demais. Contudo, um amigo extremamente querido pode servir como causa pr\xf3xima. Ao v\xea-lo ou ao ouvir sobre ele, deve-se suscitar a alegria altru\xedsta: 'Este ser \xe9 feliz e se alegra! Qu\xe3o excelente, qu\xe3o maravilhoso!'.",es:"Aquel que comienza el cultivo de la alegr\xeda altruista tampoco debe empezar por una persona odiada o similares. Sin embargo, un amigo muy entra\xf1able puede servir de base. Al verlo o al o\xedr hablar de \xe9l, debe despertar el gozo altruista: '\xa1Este ser es feliz y se regocija! \xa1Qu\xe9 bueno, qu\xe9 maravilloso!'."}},{id:"vism-9.13",pali:"Atippiyasah\u0101yako pana siy\u0101 pada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, yo a\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101ya\u1e43 so\u1e47\u1e0dasah\u0101yoti vutto, so hi paha\u1e6d\u1e6dhataro hoti, hasitapubba\u1e45gamo. Tasm\u0101 tameva pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 mudit\u0101ya pharitabba\u1e43 \u2018\u2018aya\u1e43 mah\u0101satto sukhito, aho s\u0101dhu, modat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti. Tato para\u1e43 piyapuggale, majjhatte, verimhiti eva\u1e43 anukkamena sabbasattesu mudit\u0101 pavattetabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"However, a very dear companion can be a proximate cause; he is called a 'convivial companion' in the commentary, for he is consistently cheerful and always greets one with a smile. Therefore, one should first pervade him with sympathetic joy: 'This great being is happy, ah, how good! He rejoices!' Thereafter, sympathetic joy should be aroused towards the dear person, the neutral person, and the hostile person, and thus gradually towards all beings.",pt:"No entanto, um companheiro muito querido pode servir de base; ele \xe9 chamado nas linhagens dos coment\xe1rios de 'companheiro alegre', pois \xe9 sempre alegre e expansivo, acolhendo com um sorriso. Por conseguinte, deve-se primeiro envolv\xea-lo na alegria altru\xedsta: 'Este nobre ser \xe9 feliz! Qu\xe3o espl\xeandido! Ele se regozija!'. A seguir, a alegria altru\xedsta deve ser sucessivamente direcionada ao amigo querido, \xe0 pessoa neutra e ao inimigo, estendendo-se gradualmente a todos os seres.",es:"Por su parte, un amigo muy entra\xf1able puede ser la causa pr\xf3xima; en los comentarios se le llama 'compa\xf1ero alegre', pues siempre est\xe1 contento y risue\xf1o. Por consiguiente, se le debe impregnar a \xe9l en primer lugar con el gozo altruista pensando: 'Este gran ser es dichoso; \xa1ay, qu\xe9 bueno, se alegra!'. Despu\xe9s de ello, se debe extender paulatinamente el gozo altruista a la persona querida, a la persona neutral, a la persona enemiga y a todos los seres."}},{id:"vism-9.14",pali:"Upekkh\u0101bh\u0101vana\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena pana mett\u0101d\u012bsu pa\u1e6diladdhatikacatukkajjh\u0101nena mett\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 \u0101d\u012bnava\u1e43 upekkh\u0101ya ca \u0101nisa\u1e43sa\u1e43 disv\u0101 majjhattapuggale pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 upekkh\u0101 upp\u0101detabb\u0101 \u2018\u2018kammasak\u0101 satt\u0101, kassa bhogena sukhit\u0101 v\u0101 bhavissanti dukkh\u0101 v\u0101 muccissanti, yath\u0101kammameva gamissant\u012b\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, one who wishes to develop equanimity, who has attained the first three or four jh\u0101nas in loving-kindness and the others, having seen the danger in loving-kindness and the rest and the benefit in equanimity, should first arouse equanimity towards a neutral person: 'Beings are owners of their actions. By whose wish will they become happy or be freed from suffering? They will go according to their own actions.'",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, aquele que deseja cultivar a equanimidade e que j\xe1 obteve os jh\u0101nas correspondentes atrav\xe9s de mett\u0101 e demais, tendo discernido os inconvenientes presentes nas realiza\xe7\xf5es anteriores e os benef\xedcios supremos da equanimidade, deve suscitar a equanimidade primeiramente para com uma pessoa neutra: 'Os seres s\xe3o donos de seus pr\xf3prios atos (kamma). Pelo desejo de quem eles se tornar\xe3o felizes ou se libertar\xe3o do sofrimento? Eles seguir\xe3o exatamente conforme o seu kamma'.",es:"Asimismo, aquel que desea cultivar la ecuanimidad, habiendo obtenido las absorciones previas en el amor benevolente y las dem\xe1s moradas, al discernir los peligros de las primeras y las ventajas de la ecuanimidad, debe suscitar la ecuanimidad primero hacia una persona neutral: 'Los seres son due\xf1os de sus propias acciones. \xbfPor deseo de qui\xe9n se volver\xe1n felices o se liberar\xe1n del sufrimiento? Conforme a sus propias acciones continuar\xe1n su destino'."}},{id:"vism-9.15",pali:"Et\u0101su hi mett\u0101karu\u1e47\u0101mudit\u0101upekkh\u0101su atthato t\u0101va mejjat\u012bti mett\u0101, siniyhat\u012bti attho. Sneho v\u0101 mett\u0101. Paradukkhe sati s\u0101dh\u016bna\u1e43 hadayakampana\u1e43 karot\u012bti karu\u1e47\u0101. K\u012b\u1e47\u0101ti v\u0101 paradukkha\u1e43 hi\u1e43sat\u012bti karu\u1e47\u0101. Modanti t\u0101ya, saya\u1e43 v\u0101 modati, modanamattameva v\u0101 es\u0101ti mudit\u0101. Upatipattiya\u1e43 ikkhati, pekkhitabbavasena upapann\u0101 v\u0101 pavatt\u0101 upekkh\u0101, majjhatt\u0101k\u0101rappavattiy\u0101 eta\u1e43 adhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"For in these\u2014loving-kindness, compassion, appreciative joy, and equanimity\u2014as to their meaning: it loves (mejjati), thus it is loving-kindness (mett\u0101); the meaning is that it softens. Or loving-kindness is affection. When there is suffering in others, it makes the hearts of the good tremble, thus it is compassion (karu\u1e47\u0101); or it destroys (k\u012b\u1e47\u0101ti), strikes down others' suffering, thus it is compassion. By it they rejoice, or it rejoices of itself, or it is merely rejoicing, thus it is appreciative joy (mudit\u0101). It views impartially (upatipattiya\u1e43 ikkhati), or arises as looking on with detachment, thus it is equanimity (upekkh\u0101); this is a term for neutrality of mode.",pt:"Pois, entre estas \u2014 mett\u0101, karu\u1e47\u0101, mudit\u0101 e upekkh\u0101 \u2014, quanto ao significado literal: tem afinidade (mejjati), portanto \xe9 mett\u0101; significa que torna brando, ou \xe9 afei\xe7\xe3o pura. Diante da dor alheia, faz vibrar o cora\xe7\xe3o dos nobres, logo \xe9 karu\u1e47\u0101; ou consome e dispersa o sofrimento dos outros, logo \xe9 karu\u1e47\u0101. Atrav\xe9s dela eles se alegram, ou ela mesma se alegra, ou \xe9 o puro regozijo, portanto \xe9 mudit\u0101. Olha com imparcialidade e sem apego, manifestando-se como contempla\xe7\xe3o neutra, logo \xe9 upekkh\u0101; este \xe9 um termo para o modo de neutralidade.",es:"En estas cuatro moradas \u2014amor benevolente, compasi\xf3n, alegr\xeda altruista y ecuanimidad\u2014, en cuanto al significado literal: porque se encari\xf1a (mejjati), es benevolencia (mett\u0101); esto significa que produce afinidad o es afecto sincero. Ante el dolor ajeno hace temblar el coraz\xf3n de los buenos, por eso es compasi\xf3n (karu\u1e47\u0101); o combate y destruye el dolor ajeno, por eso es compasi\xf3n. Con ella se regocijan, o ella misma se goza, o es puro gozo, por eso es alegr\xeda altruista (mudit\u0101). Observa con ecuanimidad y sin parcialidad, surgiendo como contemplaci\xf3n imparcial, por eso es ecuanimidad (upekkh\u0101); esta es una designaci\xf3n para el modo neutro de actuar."}},{id:"vism-9.16",pali:"Lakkha\u1e47\u0101dito panettha hit\u0101k\u0101rappavattilakkha\u1e47\u0101 mett\u0101, hit\u016bpasa\u1e43h\u0101raras\u0101, \u0101gh\u0101tavinayapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, satt\u0101na\u1e43 man\u0101pabh\u0101vadassanapada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101. By\u0101p\u0101dav\u016bpasamo tass\u0101 sampatti, sinehasambhavo vipatti. Dukk\u8bbe\u5b9aapanayak\u0101rappavattilakkha\u1e47\u0101 karu\u1e47\u0101, paradukkh\u0101sahanaras\u0101, avihi\u1e43s\u0101paccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, dukkh\u0101bhibh\u016bt\u0101na\u1e43 an\u0101thabh\u0101vadassanapada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101. Vihes\u0101v\u016bpasamo tass\u0101 sampatti, sokasambhavo vipatti. Modan\u0101lakkha\u1e47\u0101 mudit\u0101, aniss\u0101yanaras\u0101, aratividdha\u1e43sanapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, satt\u0101na\u1e43 sampattidassanapada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101. Arativ\u016bpasamo tass\u0101 sampatti, pah\u0101sasambhavo vipatti. Majjhatt\u0101k\u0101rappavattilakkha\u1e47\u0101 upekkh\u0101, sattesu samabh\u0101vadassanaras\u0101, pa\u1e6digh\u0101nunayav\u016bpasamapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, kammasakat\u0101dassanapada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101. Pa\u1e6digh\u0101nunayav\u016bpasamo tass\u0101 sampatti, a\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47upekkh\u0101sambhavo vipatti.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, as to their characteristics and so on, among these: Loving-kindness has the characteristic of promoting the welfare of others; its function is to provide for their benefit; it is manifested as the removal of resentment; its proximate cause is seeing the lovableness of beings. Its success is the pacification of ill will; its failure is the arising of selfish affection. Compassion has the characteristic of promoting the removal of others' suffering; its function is not being able to bear others' suffering; it is manifested as non-cruelty; its proximate cause is seeing the helplessness of those overwhelmed by suffering. Its success is the pacification of cruelty; its failure is the arising of sorrow. Sympathetic joy has the characteristic of rejoicing; its function is non-envy; it is manifested as the destruction of discontent; its proximate cause is seeing the success of beings. Its success is the pacification of discontent; its failure is the arising of exhilaration. Equanimity has the characteristic of proceeding with impartiality towards beings; its function is seeing the equality of beings; it is manifested as the pacification of resentment and affection; its proximate cause is seeing the ownership of kamma. Its success is the pacification of resentment and affection; its failure is the arising of ignorant indifference.",pt:"Quanto \xe0s suas caracter\xedsticas e demais fatores: o amor-bondade tem como caracter\xedstica a promo\xe7\xe3o do bem-estar; sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 proporcionar o benef\xedcio; manifesta-se como a elimina\xe7\xe3o da avers\xe3o; sua causa pr\xf3xima \xe9 a percep\xe7\xe3o das qualidades am\xe1veis dos seres. O seu \xeaxito \xe9 o apaziguamento da malevol\xeancia; o seu fracasso \xe9 o surgimento do apego ego\xedsta. A compaix\xe3o tem como caracter\xedstica a elimina\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento; sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a recusa em tolerar o sofrimento alheio; manifesta-se como a n\xe3o crueldade; sua causa pr\xf3xima \xe9 ver o desamparo dos oprimidos pela dor. O seu \xeaxito \xe9 a pacifica\xe7\xe3o da crueldade; o seu fracasso \xe9 o surgimento da tristeza. A alegria altru\xedsta tem como caracter\xedstica o regozijo; sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a aus\xeancia de inveja; manifesta-se como a destrui\xe7\xe3o do descontentamento; sua causa pr\xf3xima \xe9 ver a prosperidade dos seres. O seu \xeaxito \xe9 a pacifica\xe7\xe3o da inveja; o seu fracasso \xe9 o surgimento da frivolidade mundana. A equanimidade tem como caracter\xedstica a neutralidade em rela\xe7\xe3o aos seres; sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 enxergar a igualdade fundamental entre eles; manifesta-se como o apaziguamento da avers\xe3o e do favoritismo; sua causa pr\xf3xima \xe9 a reflex\xe3o sobre o fato de os seres serem herdeiros de suas a\xe7\xf5es. O seu \xeaxito \xe9 a cessa\xe7\xe3o da animosidade e do favoritismo; o seu fracasso \xe9 o aparecimento da indiferen\xe7a ignorante.",es:"En cuanto a sus caracter\xedsticas y dem\xe1s propiedades: el amor benevolente (mett\u0101) tiene como caracter\xedstica el promover el bienestar; su funci\xf3n es procurar el beneficio; se manifiesta como la eliminaci\xf3n del resentimiento y tiene como causa pr\xf3xima el ver el aspecto amable de los seres. Su \xe9xito es la pacificaci\xf3n de la malevolencia; su fracaso es el surgimiento del afecto ego\xedsta. La compasi\xf3n (karu\u1e47\u0101) tiene como caracter\xedstica el promover la eliminaci\xf3n del sufrimiento; su funci\xf3n es la incapacidad de tolerar el sufrimiento ajeno; se manifiesta como la no crueldad y tiene como causa pr\xf3xima el ver la desprotecci\xf3n de quienes est\xe1n abrumados por el dolor. Su \xe9xito es la pacificaci\xf3n de la crueldad; su fracaso es el surgimiento del pesar (soka). La alegr\xeda altruista (mudit\u0101) tiene como caracter\xedstica el regocijo; su funci\xf3n es la ausencia de envidia; se manifiesta como la eliminaci\xf3n del descontento y tiene como causa pr\xf3xima el ver la prosperidad de los seres. Su \xe9xito es la pacificaci\xf3n del descontento (arati); su fracaso es el surgimiento de la algarab\xeda mundana. La ecuanimidad (upekkh\u0101) tiene como caracter\xedstica el proceder con neutralidad hacia los seres; su funci\xf3n es ver la igualdad entre los seres; se manifiesta como la pacificaci\xf3n de la aversi\xf3n y el favoritismo, y tiene como causa pr\xf3xima el ver la propiedad de las acciones (kammassakat\u0101) de esta manera: 'Los seres son due\xf1os de sus actos; \xbfpor voluntad de qui\xe9n llegar\xe1n a ser felices, o se liberar\xe1n del sufrimiento, o no perder\xe1n la prosperidad alcanzada?'. Su \xe9xito es la pacificaci\xf3n de la aversi\xf3n y el favoritismo; su fracaso es el surgimiento de la indiferencia ignorante basada en la vida mundana."}},{id:"vism-9.17",pali:"Ekekassa cettha \u0101sannad\u016bravasena dve dve paccatthik\u0101. Mett\u0101brahmavih\u0101rassa hi sam\u012bpac\u0101ro viya purisassa sapatto gu\u1e47adassanasabh\u0101gat\u0101ya r\u0101go \u0101sannapaccatthiko, so lahu\u1e43 ot\u0101ra\u1e43 labhati, tasm\u0101 tato su\u1e6d\u1e6dhu mett\u0101 rakkhitabb\u0101. Pabbat\u0101digahananissito viya purisassa sapatto sabh\u0101gavisabh\u0101gat\u0101ya by\u0101p\u0101do d\u016brapaccatthiko, tasm\u0101 tato nibbhayena mett\u0101yitabba\u1e43. Mett\u0101yissati ca n\u0101ma, kopa\xf1ca karissat\u012bti a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nameta\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Herein, for each of these divine abidings, there are two enemies each by way of a near one and a far one. For the divine abiding of loving-kindness, lust is the near enemy due to the similarity of seeing good qualities, like a rival of a person who moves about nearby. It finds an opening quickly; therefore, loving-kindness must be well guarded from it. Ill will is the far enemy due to the dissimilarity in nature, like a rival of a person who relies on a difficult place such as a mountain. Therefore, from it, loving-kindness should be developed fearlessly. For it is an impossible case that one would develop loving-kindness and also produce anger.",pt:"Cada um deles tem dos inimigos: um pr\xf3ximo e um distante. Para o estado sublime da amorosidade (mett\u0101), a cobi\xe7a (r\u0101go) \xe9 o inimigo pr\xf3ximo, devido \xe0 sua semelhan\xe7a em ver as qualidades positivas, assim como um inimigo que ronda perto de um homem. Ela encontra facilmente uma oportunidade de entrar; portanto, mett\u0101 deve ser bem protegida contra ela. A malevol\xeancia (by\u0101p\u0101do) \xe9 o inimigo distante, devido \xe0 sua total incompatibilidade de natureza, assim como um inimigo escondido em uma floresta montanhosa. Portanto, deve-se praticar mett\u0101 sem medo dela. \xc9 imposs\xedvel que algu\xe9m desenvolva mett\u0101 e, ao mesmo tempo, sinta raiva.",es:"Para cada uno de ellos, existen dos enemigos: uno cercano y otro lejano. Para el amor benevolente, el apego (r\u0101ga) es el enemigo cercano, debido a que comparte la naturaleza de ver cualidades positivas, similar a un enemigo que se mueve cerca de un hombre; este encuentra una oportunidad de entrada r\xe1pidamente. Por lo tanto, el amor benevolente debe protegerse bien del apego. La malevolencia (by\u0101p\u0101da) es el enemigo lejano debido a su naturaleza opuesta, similar a un enemigo de un hombre que se oculta en un lugar inaccesible como una monta\xf1a; por ello, se debe practicar el amor benevolente sin temor a la malevolencia. Es imposible que alguien desarrolle amor benevolente y, al mismo tiempo, d\xe9 lugar a la ira."}},{id:"vism-9.18",pali:"Ettha siy\u0101, kasm\u0101 panet\u0101 mett\u0101karu\u1e47\u0101mudit\u0101upekkh\u0101 brahmavih\u0101r\u0101ti vuccanti? Kasm\u0101 ca catassova? Ko ca et\u0101sa\u1e43 kamo, abhidhamme ca kasm\u0101 appama\xf1\xf1\u0101ti vutt\u0101ti? Vuccate, se\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e6d\u1e6dhena t\u0101va niddosabh\u0101vena cettha brahmavih\u0101rat\u0101 veditabb\u0101. Sattesu samm\u0101pa\u1e6dipattibh\u0101vena hi se\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101 ete vih\u0101r\u0101. Yath\u0101 ca brahm\u0101no niddosacitt\u0101 viharanti, eva\u1e43 etehi sampayutt\u0101 yogino brahmasam\u0101 hutv\u0101 viharant\u012bti se\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e6d\u1e6dhena niddosabh\u0101vena ca brahmavih\u0101r\u0101ti vuccanti.",translations:{en:"Herein, this reflection might arise: Why, then, are these\u2014loving-kindness, compassion, sympathetic joy, and equanimity\u2014called the divine abidings? And why are they said to be only four? And what is their sequence? And in the Abhidhamma, why are they called the 'immeasurables'? It is said: Herein, their nature as divine abidings should be known, firstly, in the sense of being sublime and by their faultless nature. For, because they are the state of right conduct towards beings, these abidings are sublime. And just as brahm\u0101s dwell with faultless minds, so too, yogis endowed with these dwell having become like brahm\u0101s. Thus, they are called divine abidings in the sense of being sublime and by their faultless nature.",pt:"Aqui pode surgir a pergunta: 'Por que estas, a saber, mett\u0101, karu\u1e47\u0101, mudit\u0101 e upekkh\u0101, s\xe3o chamadas de dhammas sublimes (brahmavih\u0101ras)? E porque s\xe3o exatamente quatro? Qual \xe9 a sua ordem? E porque no Abhidhamma s\xe3o chamadas de imensur\xe1veis (appama\xf1\xf1\u0101)?' Responde-se: Primeiro, a sua natureza de brahmavih\u0101ra deve ser compreendida no sentido de excel\xeancia (se\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e6d\u1e6dhena) e de pureza de falhas (niddosabh\u0101vena). Pois estas moradas s\xe3o excelentes por serem a conduta correta em rela\xe7\xe3o aos seres. E assim como os grandes Brahma habitam com mentes livres de falhas, da mesma forma os iogues associados a estas qualidades habitam como os Brahma. Portanto, devido ao sentido de excel\xeancia e de pureza de falhas, s\xe3o chamadas de brahmavih\u0101ras.",es:"En este punto, podr\xeda surgir la pregunta: \xbfPor qu\xe9 estas cualidades \u2014benevolencia, compasi\xf3n, alegr\xeda altruista y ecuanimidad\u2014 se llaman \"moradas divinas\" (brahmavih\u0101ras)? \xbfY por qu\xe9 son solo cuatro? \xbfCu\xe1l es su orden y por qu\xe9 en el Abhidhamma se llaman \"inconmensurables\" (appama\xf1\xf1\u0101)? Se responde: En primer lugar, su condici\xf3n de moradas divinas debe entenderse en el sentido de excelencia y de ausencia de tacha. Pues estas moradas son excelentes por ser la conducta correcta hacia los seres. Adem\xe1s, as\xed como los Grandes Brahmas moran con mentes sin tacha, de la misma manera, los yoguis asociados con estas cualidades moran como iguales a los Brahmas; por lo tanto, se llaman moradas divinas por su excelencia y su estado libre de tacha."}}]},427,[]);
__d(function(a,e,i,n,o,t,s){o.exports=[{id:"vism-10.1",pali:"Brahmavih\u0101r\u0101nantara\u1e43 uddi\u1e6d\u1e6dhesu pana cat\u016bsu \u0101ruppesu \u0101k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatana\u1e43 t\u0101va bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena kulaputtena \u2018\u2018ida\u1e43 me kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 s\u0101vasesa\u1e43, asa\u1e45khata\u1e43 santanti upasa\u1e43haritv\u0101\u2019\u2019ti eva\u1e43 brahmavih\u0101resu \u0101d\u012bnava\u1e43 disv\u0101 sesakasi\u1e47\u0101na\u1e43 v\u0101 nava\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 pattharitabba\u1e43, pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47ameva v\u0101 pattharitv\u0101 tadanur\u016bpampi jh\u0101na\u1e43 nibbattetv\u0101 tasm\u0101 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya catutthajjh\u0101nassa nimittabh\u016bt\u0101 kasi\u1e47ar\u016bp\u0101 nibbijjitabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now, among the four formless states mentioned after the divine abodes, one who wishes to develop the base of the infinitude of space should, having seen the danger in the divine abodes by reflecting, 'This meditation subject of mine still has a remainder, it is not unconditioned peace,' expand either one of the remaining nine kasi\u1e47as, or having expanded the earth kasi\u1e47a itself and produced the corresponding jh\u0101na, emerge from it and become disenchanted with the kasi\u1e47a-form that serves as the sign of the fourth jh\u0101na.",pt:"Entre as quatro realiza\xe7\xf5es imateriais (\u0101ruppas) mencionadas logo ap\xf3s os Brahmavih\u0101ras, aquele nobre praticante que deseja desenvolver a esfera do espa\xe7o infinito deve, tendo percebido os limites dos Brahmavih\u0101ras por refletir que 'este meu objeto de medita\xe7\xe3o ainda possui res\xedduos, n\xe3o \xe9 a verdadeira paz incondicionada', expandir qualquer um dos outros nove kasi\u1e47as, ou expandir o pr\xf3prio kasi\u1e47a da terra e realizar a correspondente quarta absor\xe7\xe3o; depois de emergir dela, deve se desencantar da forma material do kasi\u1e47a que serve como base desse quarto jh\u0101na.",es:"Despu\xe9s de las moradas divinas, entre los cuatro estados inmateriales mencionados, el disc\xedpulo que desee desarrollar la esfera del espacio infinito, habiendo visto el defecto en las moradas divinas al reflexionar: 'este objeto de meditaci\xf3n todav\xeda tiene remanentes, no es la paz incondicionada', debe expandir alguno de los otros nueve kasi\u1e47as o, habiendo expandido el propio kasi\u1e47a de la tierra y habiendo obtenido la absorci\xf3n correspondiente, emerger de ella y desilusionarse de la forma del kasi\u1e47a que sirve de objeto para el cuarto jh\u0101na."}},{id:"vism-10.2",pali:"Tassa ki\xf1c\u0101pi r\u016bp\u0101vacaracatutthajjh\u0101navasena karajar\u016bpa\u1e43 atikkanta\u1e43 hoti, atha kho kasi\u1e47ar\u016bpa\u1e43 anatikkantatt\u0101 r\u016bpatikkamo n\u0101ma na hoti. Yath\u0101 cassa karajar\u016bpassa atikkamo na hoti, eva\u1e43 tadup\u0101dik\u0101na\u1e43 da\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101bhigh\u0101t\u0101disabbadukkh\u0101na\u1e43 na hoti atikkamo. R\u016bpa\xf1ca n\u0101ma eta\u1e43 bahus\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Although his physical body has been transcended by means of the fourth jh\u0101na belonging to the fine-material sphere, still, because the kasi\u1e47a-form has not been transcended, there is no real transcending of materiality. And just as there is no real transcending of the physical body, so too there is no transcending of all the suffering that has it as its cause, such as strikes with sticks and so forth. Moreover, this materiality is common to many.",pt:"Embora o corpo f\xedsico j\xe1 tenha sido transcendido pelo quarto jh\u0101na do plano da mat\xe9ria sutil, ainda assim, pelo fato de a forma visual do kasi\u1e47a n\xe3o ter sido superada, n\xe3o h\xe1 a supera\xe7\xe3o completa da mat\xe9ria. E da mesma forma que n\xe3o h\xe1 a supera\xe7\xe3o definitiva do corpo material, assim tamb\xe9m n\xe3o h\xe1 supera\xe7\xe3o de todos os sofrimentos decorrentes dele, tais como golpes de bast\xe3o e semelhantes. Al\xe9m disso, a mat\xe9ria \xe9 comum a muitos perigos.",es:"Aunque el cuerpo f\xedsico haya sido trascendido por medio del cuarto jh\u0101na del plano de la forma sutil, dado que la forma del kasi\u1e47a no ha sido trascendida, no existe una trascendencia real de la forma material. Y as\xed como no existe una superaci\xf3n completa del cuerpo f\xedsico, de igual manera no hay trascendencia de todos los sufrimientos causados por \xe9l, como los golpes de palos y dem\xe1s aflicciones. Adem\xe1s, la materia es compartida por muchos peligros."}},{id:"vism-10.3",pali:"Eva\u1e43 so tasm\u0101 catutthajjh\u0101nassa \u0101ramma\u1e47abh\u016bt\u0101 kasi\u1e47ar\u016bp\u0101 nibbijja pakkamitu\u1e43 v\u0101yamanto \u2018\u2018ida\u1e43 catutthajjh\u0101na\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101ramma\u1e47at\u0101ya r\u016bpasabh\u0101gapaccatthika\u1e43, r\u016bpappabhav\u0101ya ca pa\u1e6dighasa\xf1\xf1\u0101ya \u0101sanna\u2019\u2019nti tassa \u0101d\u012bnava\u1e43 disv\u0101 nikanti\u1e43 pariy\u0101d\u0101ya \u0101k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatana\u1e43 santato manasik\u0101tabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"So, being disgusted with the kasi\u1e47a-form that is the object of the fourth jh\u0101na, and striving to depart from it, he should see the danger in that fourth jh\u0101na: 'Because it has a form as its object, it has a material counterpart as an enemy, and it is close to the perception of resistance that originates from form'; having dispelled attachment to it, he should attend to the base of the infinitude of space as peaceful.",pt:"Desse modo, estando desiludido com a forma do kasi\u1e47a que constitui o objeto do quarto jh\u0101na e empenhando-se em super\xe1-la, ele deve perceber o perigo inerente ao quarto jh\u0101na: 'Por ter a mat\xe9ria como objeto, este possui um inimigo similar que \xe9 a forma material, e est\xe1 perigosamente pr\xf3ximo da percep\xe7\xe3o de resist\xeancia originada da forma'. Tendo superado o apego a ele, deve prestar aten\xe7\xe3o \xe0 esfera do espa\xe7o infinito como um estado pac\xedfico.",es:"De ese modo, estando desilusionado de la forma del kasi\u1e47a que sirve de objeto al cuarto jh\u0101na y esforz\xe1ndose por trascenderla, debe ver el peligro de ese cuarto jh\u0101na pensando: 'por tener la forma como objeto, tiene como enemigo a la materia misma, y se encuentra muy cerca de la percepci\xf3n de resistencia nacida de la forma'. Habiendo agotado su apego a \xe9l, debe prestar atenci\xf3n a la esfera del espacio infinito como algo sumamente pac\xedfico."}},{id:"vism-10.4",pali:"So ta\u1e43 kasi\u1e47uggh\u0101\u1e6dim\u0101k\u0101sanimitta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018\u0101k\u0101so \u0101k\u0101so\u2019\u2019ti punappuna\u1e43 \u0101vajjeti, tattha citta\u1e43 c\u0101reti, tassa tatra punappuna\u1e43 citta\u1e43 c\u0101rentassa n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101ni vikkhambhanti, sati santi\u1e6d\u1e6dhati, upac\u0101rena citta\u1e43 sam\u0101dhiyati. So ta\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 \u0101sevati bh\u0101veti bahul\u012bkaroti. Tasseva\u1e43 karoto ar\u016bp\u0101vacaracitte appan\u0101 uppajjati.",translations:{en:"He repeatedly adverts to that sign of space from which the kasi\u1e47a was removed, thinking, 'Space, space.' He directs his mind towards it. As he repeatedly directs his mind there, the hindrances are suppressed, mindfulness is established, and the mind is concentrated through access. He frequents that sign, develops it, and makes much of it. As he does so, absorption arises in the immaterial-sphere mind.",pt:"Ele orienta repetidamente sua aten\xe7\xe3o para esse sinal do espa\xe7o aberto resultante da remo\xe7\xe3o mental do kasi\u1e47a, pensando: 'espa\xe7o, espa\xe7o'. Direciona sua mente para ele. E \xe0 medida que conduz a mente repetidamente para l\xe1, os obst\xe1culos s\xe3o suprimidos, a aten\xe7\xe3o se estabelece e a mente se concentra pelo est\xe1gio de acesso. Ele cultiva esse sinal, o desenvolve e o pratica com frequ\xeancia. Conforme procede assim, surge a absor\xe7\xe3o na consci\xeancia do plano imaterial.",es:"\xc9l orienta su mente una y otra vez hacia esa se\xf1al del espacio abierto dejada por la remoci\xf3n del kasi\u1e47a, pensando: 'espacio, espacio'. Conduce su mente hacia all\xed. Al conducir su mente repetidamente hacia ese objeto, los obst\xe1culos se suprimen, la atenci\xf3n plena se establece y la mente se concentra en la proximidad del acceso. \xc9l cultiva esa se\xf1al, la desarrolla y la frecuenta. Mientras procede as\xed, surge la absorci\xf3n en la mente del plano inmaterial."}},{id:"vism-10.5",pali:"Tattha sabb\u0101soti sabb\u0101k\u0101rena, sabb\u0101sa\u1e43 v\u0101 anavases\u0101nanti attho. R\u016bpasa\xf1\xf1\u0101nanti r\u016bp\u0101vacarajjh\u0101nasampayutt\u0101na\u1e43 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43, r\u016bp\u0101vacar\u0101na\xf1ca r\u016bp\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101na\xf1ca sa\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43. Samatikkam\u0101ti atikkam\u0101, v\u012btivattan\u0101, appavattiy\u0101. Na hi r\u016bp\u0101vacaradhamm\u0101 ar\u016bp\u0101vacaracittassa \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 honti.",translations:{en:"Herein, 'completely' means in every way, or of all, without remainder. 'Of perceptions of form' means of perceptions associated with the fine-material sphere jh\u0101nas, and of perceptions that belong to the fine-material sphere and have form as their object. 'By the transcendence' means by overcoming, by passing beyond, by non-occurrence. For phenomena of the fine-material sphere cannot be the object of an immaterial-sphere consciousness.",pt:"Ali, 'completamente' significa de todos os modos, ou de todas as percep\xe7\xf5es sem exce\xe7\xe3o. 'Das percep\xe7\xf5es de forma' refere-se \xe0s percep\xe7\xf5es associadas aos jh\u0101nas do plano da mat\xe9ria sutil, e \xe0s percep\xe7\xf5es que pertencem ao plano da forma e tomam a forma material como objeto. 'Pela supera\xe7\xe3o' significa pela ultrapassagem, por transpor, pela n\xe3o ocorr\xeancia. Pois os fen\xf4menos do plano da forma n\xe3o podem ser o objeto da consci\xeancia pertencente ao plano imaterial.",es:"All\xed, 'completamente' significa en todos los modos, o de todas las percepciones sin excepci\xf3n. 'De las percepciones de la forma' se refiere a las percepciones asociadas a los jh\u0101nas del plano de la forma sutil, y a las percepciones que pertenecen a dicho plano y tienen a la forma como objeto. 'Por la trascendencia' significa por haberlas superado, por haberlas traspasado, por su cesaci\xf3n. Pues los dhammas del plano de la forma no pueden constituir el objeto de la mente del plano inmaterial."}},{id:"vism-10.6",pali:"Pa\u1e6dighasa\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43 attha\u1e45gam\u0101ti cakkh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 vatth\u016bna\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101na\xf1ca pa\u1e6digh\u0101tavasena uppann\u0101na\u1e43 r\u016bpasaddagandharasapho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbasa\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43 attha\u1e45gam\u0101, appavattiy\u0101, pah\u0101n\u0101ti attho. K\u0101ma\xf1cet\u0101 pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101n\u0101d\u012bni sam\u0101pannass\u0101pi na santi, atha kho na pah\u012bnatt\u0101 anattha\u1e45gat\u0101 n\u0101ma honti, imin\u0101 pana jh\u0101nena pah\u012bnatt\u0101 attha\u1e45gat\u0101 n\u0101ma hont\u012bti.",translations:{en:"The cessation of perceptions of resistance: Perception arising from the impact of bases such as the eye and objects such as forms, that is, perceptions of forms, sounds, odors, tastes, and tangibles\u2014their cessation means their non-occurrence, their abandoning. Although these do not exist for one who has entered the first jh\u0101na and so on, they are not called ceased because they have not been abandoned; but because they are abandoned by this attainment, they are said to have ceased.",pt:"'Pelo desaparecimento das percep\xe7\xf5es de resist\xeancia' refere-se ao fim das percep\xe7\xf5es de formas, sons, odores, sabores e contatos corporais, que surgem do impacto entre as bases dos sentidos, como o olho, e os seus objetos, como as formas. 'Desaparecimento' significa a sua n\xe3o ocorr\xeancia, o seu abandono efetivo. Embora tais percep\xe7\xf5es n\xe3o estejam presentes mesmo naquele que atingiu o primeiro jh\u0101na e os seguintes, elas n\xe3o s\xe3o consideradas verdadeiramente 'desaparecidas' porque ainda n\xe3o foram erradicadas; mas, por terem sido superadas atrav\xe9s desta realiza\xe7\xe3o imaterial, diz-se verdadeiramente que desapareceram.",es:"'Por el cese de las percepciones de resistencia': se refiere a las percepciones de formas, sonidos, olores, sabores y contactos t\xe1ctiles surgidas por el choque entre las bases sensoriales como el ojo y sus objetos correspondientes; su cese significa su no concurrencia, su abandono. Aunque ciertamente tales percepciones tampoco existen en quien ha entrado en el primer jh\u0101na y los siguientes, no se consideran desaparecidas puesto que a\xfan no han sido eliminadas; pero al haber sido erradicadas por medio de este jh\u0101na inmaterial, se dice con propiedad que han cesado."}},{id:"vism-10.7",pali:"N\u0101nattasa\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43 amanasik\u0101r\u0101ti n\u0101natte v\u0101 gocare pavatt\u0101na\u1e43 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43, n\u0101n\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 v\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43 amanasik\u0101r\u0101 appavattiy\u0101. K\u0101m\u0101vacaravitakkavic\u0101rasahagat\u0101na\u1e43 v\u0101 n\u0101n\u0101vidh\u0101na\u1e43 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43 avy\u0101p\u0101rabh\u0101v\u0101.",translations:{en:"'By not attending to perceptions of diversity' means not attending to perceptions operating in a diverse field, or not attending to perceptions diverse in nature, through their non-occurrence; or through the non-functioning of the diverse kinds of perceptions associated with applied and sustained thought in the sensuous sphere.",pt:"'Pela falta de aten\xe7\xe3o \xe0s percep\xe7\xf5es da diversidade' significa n\xe3o dar aten\xe7\xe3o \xe0s percep\xe7\xf5es que operam em m\xfaltiplos campos sensoriais, ou pela n\xe3o ocorr\xeancia das percep\xe7\xf5es caracterizadas pela multiplicidade; ou pelo cessar do funcionamento das diversas percep\xe7\xf5es acompanhadas de pensamento aplicado e sustentado pertencentes \xe0 esfera sensorial.",es:"'Por la no atenci\xf3n a las percepciones de la diversidad' significa por no prestar atenci\xf3n a las percepciones que operan en un \xe1mbito m\xfaltiple o a las percepciones distinguidas por su diversidad, mediante su no manifestaci\xf3n; o por la inactividad de las diversas clases de percepci\xf3n asociadas con el pensamiento aplicado y sostenido del plano sensorial."}},{id:"vism-10.8",pali:"Ananto \u0101k\u0101soti ettha n\u0101ssa upp\u0101danto v\u0101 vayanto v\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101yat\u012bti ananto. Na sakk\u0101 tassa puratthimopi anto pa\xf1\xf1\u0101petu\u1e43, pacchimopi, dakkhi\u1e47opi, uttaropi, majjhepi anto pa\xf1\xf1\u0101petu\u1e43. Tasm\u0101 ananto \u0101k\u0101soti \u0101k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatana\u1e43 upasampajja viharati.",translations:{en:"Herein, regarding 'infinite space,' because its limit of arising or limit of cessation is not known, it is infinite. It is not possible to point out an eastern limit of it, or a western, southern, northern, or central limit. Therefore, having attained the base of the infinitude of space, thinking 'Space is infinite,' he dwells.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 express\xe3o 'o espa\xe7o \xe9 infinito', ela \xe9 chamada infinita porque n\xe3o se pode discernir nela um limite de surgimento ou de cessa\xe7\xe3o. N\xe3o \xe9 poss\xedvel determinar um limite leste para ele, nem oeste, nem sul, nem norte, nem tampouco um centro. Portanto, diz-se que ele permanece tendo realizado a esfera do espa\xe7o infinito, pensando: 'o espa\xe7o \xe9 ilimitado'.",es:"En cuanto a 'el espacio es infinito': porque no se conoce en \xe9l ni un l\xedmite de surgimiento ni de disoluci\xf3n, se le llama infinito. No es posible se\xf1alar en \xe9l un l\xedmite oriental, ni occidental, ni meridional, ni septentrional, ni tampoco un l\xedmite central. Por consiguiente, habiendo alcanzado la esfera del espacio infinito pensando 'el espacio es infinito', el meditador permanece."}},{id:"vism-10.9",pali:"Vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatana\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena pana pa\xf1cah\u0101k\u0101rehi \u0101k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatanasam\u0101pattiy\u0101 vasi\u1e43 katv\u0101 tamatikkamituk\u0101mena tesa\u1e43 \u0101k\u0101sapharakacitt\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101d\u012bnava\u1e43 disv\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatana\u1e43 santato manasik\u0101tabba\u1e43. So ta\u1e43 \u0101k\u0101saphara\u1e47ena pavattavij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 \u2018\u2018vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti punappuna\u1e43 manasikaroti.",translations:{en:"However, one who wishes to develop the base of the infinitude of consciousness, having achieved mastery over the attainment of the base of the infinitude of space in five ways, wishing to transcend it, having seen the danger in those thoughts that pervaded space, should attend to the base of the infinitude of consciousness as peaceful. He repeatedly attends to that consciousness characterized by cognizance that occurred through pervading the space, thinking, 'Consciousness, consciousness.'",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver a esfera da consci\xeancia infinita deve primeiro dominar a realiza\xe7\xe3o da esfera do espa\xe7o infinito de cinco maneiras. Desejando super\xe1-la e tendo discernido as limita\xe7\xf5es daquela mente que perpassou o espa\xe7o, deve contemplar a esfera da consci\xeancia infinita como pac\xedfica. Ele direciona sua aten\xe7\xe3o repetidamente para aquela mesma consci\xeancia que conheceu a imensid\xe3o do espa\xe7o, pensando: 'consci\xeancia, consci\xeancia'.",es:"Aquel que desea desarrollar la esfera de la conciencia infinita debe haber dominado el logro de la esfera del espacio infinito de cinco maneras. Deseando trascenderla y habiendo visto los defectos de los estados mentales que abarcaron el espacio, debe prestar atenci\xf3n a la esfera de la conciencia infinita como un estado de quietud. As\xed, atiende una y otra vez a esa conciencia que se manifest\xf3 abarcando el espacio, pensando: 'conciencia, conciencia'."}},{id:"vism-10.10",pali:"Sabbaso \u0101k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatana\u1e43 samatikkamm\u0101ti \u0101k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatanampi ta\u1e43sam\u0101pattampi sabba\u1e43 atikkamma, an\u0101lambitv\u0101, ta\u1e43samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nasa\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43 atikkam\u0101 v\u012btivattan\u0101ti attho.",translations:{en:"'Completely transcending the base of the infinitude of space' means having completely transcended that base of the infinitude of space together with that attainment, not taking it as an object; the meaning is through the transcending, the surpassing of perceptions originating therefrom.",pt:"'Superando completamente a esfera do espa\xe7o infinito' significa ter ultrapassado inteiramente a esfera do espa\xe7o infinito e a sua realiza\xe7\xe3o, sem tom\xe1-la mais como objeto; o significado \xe9 atrav\xe9s da supera\xe7\xe3o e cessa\xe7\xe3o das percep\xe7\xf5es originadas dela.",es:"'Habiendo trascendido completamente la esfera del espacio infinito' significa habiendo superado por completo tanto la esfera del espacio infinito como su propio logro, sin tomarlo ya como objeto; es decir, mediante la trascendencia y el abandono de las percepciones que de \xe9l surgen."}},{id:"vism-10.11",pali:"Ananta\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47anti ta\u1e43yeva ananto \u0101k\u0101soti eva\u1e43 pharitv\u0101 pavattavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 anantanti manasikaroti, ananta\u1e43 v\u0101 gocara\u1e43 karitv\u0101 pavattatt\u0101 ananta\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47anti vuccati. Tameta\u1e43 ananta\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatana\u1e43 upasampajja viharat\u012bti attho.",translations:{en:"'Consciousness is infinite' means that one attends to the consciousness that occurred pervading space, thinking 'Consciousness is infinite'; or it is called infinite consciousness because it operates having made an infinite object its field. The meaning is that, having taken this infinite consciousness as object, one dwells having attained the base of the infinitude of consciousness.",pt:"'A consci\xeancia \xe9 infinita' significa que o praticante contempla como infinita a pr\xf3pria consci\xeancia que perpassou o espa\xe7o infinito; ou \xe9 chamada de consci\xeancia infinita porque atua tendo tornado um objeto ilimitado o seu dom\xednio. O significado \xe9 que, tendo tomado essa consci\xeancia infinita como objeto, ele permanece tendo realizado a esfera da consci\xeancia infinita.",es:"'La conciencia es infinita' significa que atiende como infinita a esa misma conciencia que surgi\xf3 impregnando el espacio; o bien se llama conciencia infinita porque act\xfaa habiendo hecho de un \xe1mbito infinito su objeto. El significado es que, habiendo tomado esa conciencia infinita como objeto, permanece tras alcanzar la esfera de la conciencia infinita."}},{id:"vism-10.12",pali:"\u0100ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena pana pa\xf1cah\u0101k\u0101rehi vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatanasam\u0101pattiy\u0101 vasi\u1e43 katv\u0101 tato para\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47assa abh\u0101va\u1e43, su\xf1\xf1ata\u1e43, vivittabh\u0101va\u1e43 manasik\u0101tabba\u1e43. So ta\u1e43 \u0101k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatanapharakavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 \u2018\u2018natthi natthi, su\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 su\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, vivitta\u1e43 vivitta\u2019\u2019nti punappuna\u1e43 manasikaronto \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanacitte appana\u1e43 p\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, one who wishes to develop the base of nothingness, having achieved mastery over the attainment of the base of the infinitude of consciousness in five ways, should thereafter attend to the non-existence, emptiness, and seclusion of that consciousness. Repeatedly attending to the absence of that consciousness which pervaded the base of the infinitude of space, thinking 'There is nothing, nothing; empty, empty; secluded, secluded,' he attains absorption in the mind of the base of nothingness.",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver a esfera do nada deve primeiro dominar a realiza\xe7\xe3o da esfera da consci\xeancia infinita de cinco maneiras; depois disso, deve prestar aten\xe7\xe3o \xe0 n\xe3o exist\xeancia, vacuidade e isolamento dessa mesma consci\xeancia. Atentando repetidamente para a aus\xeancia daquela consci\xeancia que perpassava o espa\xe7o, pensando: 'n\xe3o h\xe1 nada, n\xe3o h\xe1 nada; vazio, vazio; retirado, retirado', ele atinge a absor\xe7\xe3o mental na esfera do nada.",es:"Aquel que desea desarrollar la esfera de la nada debe dominar el logro de la esfera de la conciencia infinita de cinco maneras; despu\xe9s de ello, debe prestar atenci\xf3n a la inexistencia, a la vacuidad y al aislamiento de esa conciencia. Al atender repetidamente a la ausencia de esa conciencia que abarcaba la esfera del espacio infinito, pensando: 'no hay nada, no hay nada; vac\xedo, vac\xedo; apartado, apartado', alcanza la absorci\xf3n en la mente de la esfera de la nada."}},{id:"vism-10.13",pali:"Natthi ki\xf1c\u012bti natthi natthi, su\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 su\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, vivitta\u1e43 vivittanti eva\u1e43 ta\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 vigata\xf1ceva antaradhita\xf1ca manasi karoti. Tassa eva\u1e43 bh\u0101ventassa tass\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47assa natthibh\u0101va\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 ar\u016bp\u0101vacaracitte appan\u0101 uppajjati. Tasm\u0101 \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana\u1e43 upasampajja viharat\u012bti vuccati.",translations:{en:"'There is nothing whatsoever' means 'nothing, nothing,' 'empty, empty,' 'secluded, secluded'; in this way he attends to that consciousness as departed and disappeared. For him who develops it in this way, absorption in the immaterial-sphere mind arises, having made the non-existence of that consciousness its object. Therefore it is said: 'He dwells having attained the base of nothingness.'",pt:"'N\xe3o h\xe1 nada' significa 'nada, nada', 'vazio, vazio', 'afastado, afastado'; deste modo, ele reflete sobre aquela consci\xeancia como algo que se extinguiu e desapareceu por completo. Para quem medita assim, surge a absor\xe7\xe3o na mente da esfera imaterial, tendo como objeto a n\xe3o exist\xeancia daquela consci\xeancia anterior. Por isso, diz-se: 'ele habita tendo realizado a esfera do nada'.",es:"'No hay nada en absoluto' significa 'nada, nada', 'vac\xedo, vac\xedo', 'aislado, aislado'; de esta manera reflexiona en esa conciencia como algo que se ha disipado y desaparecido. Para quien practica de este modo, surge la absorci\xf3n en la mente del plano inmaterial tomando como objeto la inexistencia de dicha conciencia. Por lo tanto, se dice: 'permanece habiendo alcanzado la esfera de la nada'."}},{id:"vism-10.14",pali:"Nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena pana pa\xf1cah\u0101k\u0101rehi \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanasam\u0101pattiy\u0101 vasi\u1e43 katv\u0101 \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanassa \u0101d\u012bnava\u1e43 nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanassa ca santa\u1e43 disv\u0101 tasmi\u1e43 natthibh\u0101ve pavattacittassa abh\u0101va\u1e43 paramasukhuma\u1e43 santato manasik\u0101tabba\u1e43. So ta\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101vasesasa\xf1\xf1\u0101bh\u0101va\u1e43 santato manasikaronto nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanacitte appana\u1e43 p\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Now, one who wishes to develop the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception, having mastered the attainment of the base of nothingness in five ways, having seen the danger in the base of nothingness and the peace in the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception, should attend as peaceful to that extremely subtle non-functioning of mind that took non-existence as its object. Attending to that state of perception with residual formations as peaceful, he attains absorption in the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception.",pt:"Aquele que deseja desenvolver a esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o percep\xe7\xe3o, tendo alcan\xe7ado o dom\xednio sobre a realiza\xe7\xe3o da esfera do nada de cinco maneiras, tendo discernido os defeitos da esfera do nada e a paz da esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o percep\xe7\xe3o, deve atentar como pac\xedfico para aquele estado sumamente sutil de aus\xeancia de mente ativa que tomava a inexist\xeancia como objeto. Contemplando esse estado de percep\xe7\xe3o com res\xedduos de forma\xe7\xf5es mentais como algo pac\xedfico, ele atinge a absor\xe7\xe3o na esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o percep\xe7\xe3o.",es:"Aquel que desea desarrollar la esfera de la ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n, habiendo dominado el logro de la esfera de la nada de cinco maneras, habiendo visto el defecto en la esfera de la nada y la quietud en la esfera de la ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n, debe prestar atenci\xf3n como algo sumamente pac\xedfico a ese estado extremadamente sutil donde cesa la mente activa que tomaba la inexistencia como objeto. Al contemplar ese estado de percepci\xf3n residual como algo pac\xedfico, alcanza la absorci\xf3n en la mente de la esfera de la ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-10.15",pali:"Nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatananti ettha pana y\u0101ya sa\xf1\xf1\u0101ya bh\u0101vato ta\u1e43 nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatananti vuccati. Yath\u0101 pa\u1e6dipannassa s\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101 hoti, ta\u1e43 t\u0101va dassetu\u1e43 vibha\u1e45ge \u2018\u2018nevasa\xf1\xf1\u012bn\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u012b\u2019\u2019ti uddharitv\u0101 \u2018\u2018ta\xf1\xf1eva \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana\u1e43 santato manasi karoti, sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101vasesasam\u0101patti\u1e43 bh\u0101veti, tena vuccati nevasa\xf1\xf1\u012bn\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (vibha. 619) vutta\u1e43. Tattha santato manasi karot\u012bti \u2018\u2018sant\u0101 vat\u0101ya\u1e43 sam\u0101patti, yatra hi n\u0101ma natthibh\u0101vampi \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 karitv\u0101 \u1e6dhassat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti eva\u1e43 sant\u0101ramma\u1e47at\u0101ya ta\u1e43 sant\u0101ti manasi karoti.",translations:{en:"Now, in this term 'the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception', it is so called because of the existence of a certain kind of perception. In order to first show how that perception arises for one who is practicing, the Vibha\u1e45ga cites the term 'one with neither perception nor non-perception' and states: 'He attends to that very base of nothingness as peaceful, he develops the attainment that has residual formations; therefore he is called one with neither perception nor non-perception' (Vibh. \xa7619). Therein, 'he attends to it as peaceful' means that because of its peaceful object, he attends to that base of nothingness as 'peaceful,' thinking thus: 'Peaceful indeed is this attainment, that it can abide having made even the state of non-existence its object!'",pt:"Quanto ao termo 'esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o percep\xe7\xe3o', ele \xe9 assim chamado devido \xe0 presen\xe7a de uma percep\xe7\xe3o de tal natureza. Para mostrar primeiro como essa percep\xe7\xe3o ocorre naquele que pratica, o Vibhanga, destacando o termo 'nem com percep\xe7\xe3o, nem sem percep\xe7\xe3o', afirma: 'Ele presta aten\xe7\xe3o a essa mesma esfera do nada como pac\xedfica e desenvolve a realiza\xe7\xe3o com res\xedduos de forma\xe7\xf5es mentais; por isso \xe9 chamado de nem com percep\xe7\xe3o, nem sem percep\xe7\xe3o'. Ali, 'presta aten\xe7\xe3o como pac\xedfica' significa que ele a considera pac\xedfica devido ao seu objeto pac\xedfico, pensando: 'Qu\xe3o pac\xedfica \xe9 esta realiza\xe7\xe3o, que pode se estabelecer tomando at\xe9 mesmo a n\xe3o exist\xeancia como objeto!'.",es:"En cuanto a 'esfera de la ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n', se llama as\xed a aquel jhana debido a la presencia de una percepci\xf3n de tal naturaleza. Para mostrar primero c\xf3mo es esa percepci\xf3n para quien la practica, el Vibha\u1e45ga, tras citar el t\xe9rmino 'ni-percipiente-ni-no-percipiente', dice: '\xe9l presta atenci\xf3n a esa misma esfera de la nada como pac\xedfica, desarrolla el logro donde solo restan las formaciones, por eso se dice ni-percipiente-ni-no-percipiente'. All\xed, 'presta atenci\xf3n como pac\xedfica' significa que la considera como algo pac\xedfico debido a que su objeto es pac\xedfico, pensando: '\xa1qu\xe9 pac\xedfico es este logro, pues puede permanecer tomando como objeto incluso el estado de inexistencia!'."}},{id:"vism-10.16",pali:"S\u0101ma\u1e47ero kira telena patta\u1e43 makkhetv\u0101 \u1e6dhapesi, ta\u1e43 y\u0101gup\u0101nak\u0101le thero pattam\u0101har\u0101ti \u0101ha. So \u2018\u2018patte telamatthi, bhante\u2019\u2019ti \u0101ha. Tato \u2018\u2018\u0101hara, s\u0101ma\u1e47era, tela\u1e43, n\u0101\u1e37i\u1e43 p\u016bress\u0101m\u012b\u2019\u2019ti vutte \u2018\u2018natthi, bhante, tela\u2019\u2019nti \u0101ha. Tattha yath\u0101 antovutthatt\u0101 y\u0101guy\u0101 saddhi\u1e43 akappiya\u1e6d\u1e6dhena \u2018\u2018telamatth\u012b\u2019\u2019ti hoti. N\u0101\u1e37ip\u016bra\u1e47\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 vasena \u2018\u2018natth\u012b\u2019\u2019ti hoti. Eva\u1e43 s\u0101pi sa\xf1\xf1\u0101 pa\u1e6dusa\xf1\xf1\u0101kicca\u1e43 k\u0101tu\u1e43 asamatthat\u0101ya nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101, sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101vasesasukhumabh\u0101vena vijjam\u0101natt\u0101 n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"A novice, it is said, having smeared a bowl with oil, put it aside. At the time for drinking rice-gruel, the elder said to him, \u201cBring the bowl.\u201d He replied, \u201cVenerable sir, there is oil in the bowl.\u201d Then, when it was said, \u201cBring the oil, novice, I will fill a n\u0101\u1e37i,\u201d he replied, \u201cVenerable sir, there is no oil.\u201d Therein, just as it is said, 'There is oil,' on account of its being stored inside and its unsuitability to be taken together with the gruel, and it is said, 'There is no oil,' with regard to filling a n\u0101\u1e37i and so on; in the same way, that perception, due to its inability to perform the function of a clear perception, is 'not perception,' and due to its existence in a very subtle state as a remainder of formations, it is 'not non-perception'.",pt:"Diz-se que um novi\xe7o untou uma tigela com \xf3leo e a guardou. Na hora de beber o mingau, o anci\xe3o lhe disse: 'Traga a tigela'. O novi\xe7o respondeu: 'H\xe1 \xf3leo na tigela, vener\xe1vel senhor'. Ent\xe3o, quando lhe foi dito: 'Traga o \xf3leo, novi\xe7o, vou encher o recipiente de \xf3leo', ele respondeu: 'N\xe3o h\xe1 \xf3leo, vener\xe1vel senhor'. Nessa analogia, diz-se 'h\xe1 \xf3leo' no sentido de que, por ter sido guardado dentro da tigela, seria impr\xf3prio mistur\xe1-lo com o mingau; mas diz-se 'n\xe3o h\xe1' no sentido de que n\xe3o h\xe1 quantidade suficiente para encher um recipiente de \xf3leo. Da mesma forma, essa percep\xe7\xe3o, por ser incapaz de realizar a fun\xe7\xe3o ativa da percep\xe7\xe3o, \xe9 'nem percep\xe7\xe3o'; e por existir como um res\xedduo sutil de forma\xe7\xf5es mentais, \xe9 'nem n\xe3o percep\xe7\xe3o'.",es:"Se cuenta que un novicio, tras ungir un cuenco con aceite, lo dej\xf3 aparte. En el momento de tomar las gachas, el anciano le dijo: 'Trae el cuenco'. \xc9l respondi\xf3: 'Se\xf1or, hay aceite en el cuenco'. Luego, cuando se le dijo: 'Tr\xe1elo, novicio, llenar\xe9 el recipiente de aceite con \xe9l', respondi\xf3: 'Se\xf1or, no hay aceite'. En este ejemplo, se dice 'hay aceite' por el hecho de ser inapropiado para mezclarlo con las gachas al haber permanecido all\xed; y se dice 'no hay' en el sentido de llenar un recipiente. Del mismo modo, esa percepci\xf3n es 'ni percepci\xf3n' por su incapacidad para realizar la funci\xf3n clara de la percepci\xf3n, y es 'no no-percepci\xf3n' por existir en un estado sutil de formaciones residuales."}},{id:"vism-10.17",pali:"\u0100ramma\u1e47\u0101tikkamato, catassopi bhavantim\u0101; A\u1e45g\u0101tikkamamet\u0101sa\u1e43, na icchanti vibh\u0101vino.",translations:{en:"These four arise by way of transcending the object; the discerning do not admit the transcending of factors in these.",pt:"Todas estas quatro ocorrem pela supera\xe7\xe3o do objeto; os s\xe1bios n\xe3o aceitam a supera\xe7\xe3o de fatores para elas.",es:"Estas cuatro surgen mediante la trascendencia del objeto; los sabios no aceptan para ellas la trascendencia de los factores."}},{id:"vism-10.18",pali:"Suppa\u1e47\u012btatar\u0101 honti, pacchim\u0101 pacchim\u0101 idha; Upam\u0101 tattha vi\xf1\xf1eyy\u0101, p\u0101s\u0101datalas\u0101\u1e6dik\u0101.",translations:{en:"Here, each succeeding attainment is progressively more sublime. Therein, the similes of the palace terrace and the fine cloth should be understood.",pt:"Cada uma das realiza\xe7\xf5es subsequentes aqui \xe9 progressivamente mais sublime; a esse respeito, devem-se compreender as analogias dos andares de um pal\xe1cio e das vestes.",es:"Aqu\xed, cada una de las absorciones posteriores es m\xe1s sublime; en esto deben conocerse los s\xedmiles del piso del palacio y del pa\xf1o."}}]},428,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,n,t,i,s){t.exports=[{id:"vism-11.1",pali:"Tatrida\u1e43 vissajjana\u1e43. Ko sam\u0101dh\u012bti sam\u0101dhi bahuvidho n\u0101nappak\u0101rako. Ta\u1e43 sabba\u1e43 vibh\u0101vayitu\u1e43 \u0101rabbham\u0101na\u1e43 vissajjana\u1e43 adhippeta\xf1ceva attha\u1e43 na s\u0101dheyya, uttari ca vikkhep\u0101ya sa\u1e43vatteyya, tasm\u0101 idh\u0101dhippetameva sandh\u0101ya vad\u0101ma, kusalacittekaggat\u0101 sam\u0101dhi.",translations:{en:"Here is the answer. As to 'What is concentration?': Concentration is of many kinds and of various modes. An answer that undertook to explain all of that would not accomplish the intended purpose and would lead to further distraction; therefore, referring only to what is intended here, we say: Concentration is wholesome one-pointedness of mind.",pt:"Aqui est\xe1 a resposta. Quanto a 'O que \xe9 a concentra\xe7\xe3o?': a concentra\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de muitos tipos e de v\xe1rios modos. Uma resposta que se propusesse a explicar tudo isso n\xe3o realizaria o prop\xf3sito pretendido e levaria a uma distra\xe7\xe3o ainda maior; portanto, referindo-nos apenas ao que se pretende aqui, dizemos: a concentra\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a unifica\xe7\xe3o salutar da mente (kusalacittekaggat\u0101).",es:"Aqu\xed est\xe1 la respuesta. En cuanto a '\xbfQu\xe9 es la concentraci\xf3n?': la concentraci\xf3n es de muchas clases y de diversos tipos. Una respuesta que intentara explicarlo todo no lograr\xeda el prop\xf3sito deseado y conducir\xeda a una mayor dispersi\xf3n mental. Por consiguiente, refiri\xe9ndonos \xfanicamente a lo que aqu\xed se pretende, decimos: la concentraci\xf3n es la unificaci\xf3n de la mente sana (kusalacittekaggat\u0101)."}},{id:"vism-11.2",pali:"Kena\u1e6d\u1e6dhena sam\u0101dh\u012bti sam\u0101dh\u0101na\u1e6d\u1e6dhena sam\u0101dhi. Kimida\u1e43 sam\u0101dh\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101ma? Ek\u0101ramma\u1e47e cittacetasik\u0101na\u1e43 sama\u1e43 samm\u0101 ca \u0101dh\u0101na\u1e43, \u1e6dhapananti vutta\u1e43 hoti. Tasm\u0101 yassa dhammass\u0101nubh\u0101vena ek\u0101ramma\u1e47e cittacetasik\u0101 sama\u1e43 samm\u0101 ca avikkhipam\u0101n\u0101 avippaki\u1e47\u1e47\u0101 ca hutv\u0101 ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhanti, ida\u1e43 sam\u0101dh\u0101nanti veditabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"As to 'In what sense is it concentration?': It is concentration in the sense of centering (sam\u0101dh\u0101na). What is this centering? It is said to be the even and proper placing, the fixing of consciousness and its mental factors upon a single object. Therefore, that state through whose efficacy consciousness and its mental factors remain on a single object evenly and properly, unscattered and undistracted, is to be known as centering.",pt:"Quanto a 'Em que sentido \xe9 concentra\xe7\xe3o?': \xe9 concentra\xe7\xe3o no sentido de centraliza\xe7\xe3o (sam\u0101dh\u0101na). O que \xe9 essa centraliza\xe7\xe3o? Diz-se que \xe9 o posicionamento e a fixa\xe7\xe3o correta e equilibrada da mente e dos fatores mentais em um \xfanico objeto. Portanto, deve-se entender por centraliza\xe7\xe3o aquele fen\xf4meno por cuja influ\xeancia a mente e os fatores mentais permanecem em um \xfanico objeto de modo equilibrado e correto, sem dispers\xe3o e sem agita\xe7\xe3o.",es:"En cuanto a '\xbfEn qu\xe9 sentido es concentraci\xf3n?': es concentraci\xf3n en el sentido de concentraci\xf3n o asentamiento (sam\u0101dh\u0101na). \xbfA qu\xe9 se llama este asentamiento? Se dice que es el asentamiento y fijaci\xf3n correcta y equilibrada de la conciencia y los factores mentales en un \xfanico objeto. Por lo tanto, debe entenderse por asentamiento aquel fen\xf3meno por cuya eficacia la conciencia y los factores mentales permanecen en un \xfanico objeto de forma equilibrada y correcta, sin dispersarse ni agitarse."}},{id:"vism-11.3",pali:"K\u0101nassa lakkha\u1e47arasapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101n\u012bti ettha pana avikkhepalakkha\u1e47o sam\u0101dhi, vikkhepaviddha\u1e43sanaraso, avikampanapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101no. \u2018\u2018Sukhino citta\u1e43 sam\u0101dhiyat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti vacanato pana sukhamassa pada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Here, as to 'What are its characteristic, function, manifestation, and proximate cause?': Concentration has the characteristic of non-distraction, its function is the dispelling of distraction, its manifestation is non-wavering. And on account of the saying, 'The mind of one who is happy becomes concentrated,' happiness is its proximate cause.",pt:"Aqui, quanto a 'Quais s\xe3o as suas caracter\xedsticas, fun\xe7\xe3o, manifesta\xe7\xe3o e causa pr\xf3xima?': a concentra\xe7\xe3o tem a n\xe3o distra\xe7\xe3o como caracter\xedstica, a elimina\xe7\xe3o da distra\xe7\xe3o como fun\xe7\xe3o e a firmeza inabal\xe1vel como manifesta\xe7\xe3o. E devido \xe0 passagem que diz 'a mente de quem \xe9 feliz se concentra', a felicidade (sukha) \xe9 a sua causa pr\xf3xima.",es:"Aqu\xed, en cuanto a '\xbfCu\xe1les son sus caracter\xedsticas, funci\xf3n, manifestaci\xf3n y causa pr\xf3xima?': la concentraci\xf3n tiene como caracter\xedstica la no distracci\xf3n, como funci\xf3n la eliminaci\xf3n de la dispersi\xf3n mental y como manifestaci\xf3n la firmeza inamovible. Y debido a la ense\xf1anza que dice 'la mente de quien es feliz se concentra', la felicidad es su causa pr\xf3xima."}},{id:"vism-11.4",pali:"Katividho sam\u0101dh\u012bti avikkhepalakkha\u1e47ena t\u0101va ekavidho. Upac\u0101raappan\u0101vasena duvidho, tath\u0101 lokiyalokuttaravasena sapp\u012btikanipp\u012btikavasena sukhasahagataupekkh\u0101sahagatavasena ca. Tividho h\u012bnamajjhimapa\u1e47\u012btavasena, tath\u0101 savitakkasavic\u0101r\u0101divasena p\u012btisahagat\u0101divasena parittamahaggatappam\u0101\u1e47avasena ca. Catubbidho dukkh\u0101pa\u1e6dipad\u0101dandh\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101divasena, tath\u0101 parittaparitt\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101divasena catujh\u0101na\u1e45gavasena h\u0101nabh\u0101giy\u0101divasena k\u0101m\u0101vacar\u0101divasena adhipativasena ca. Pa\xf1cavidho pa\xf1cakanaye pa\xf1cajh\u0101na\u1e45gavasen\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"As to the question, 'How many kinds of concentration are there?': First, by the characteristic of non-distraction, it is of one kind. It is of two kinds by way of access and absorption, and likewise by way of mundane and supramundane, with zest and without zest, accompanied by pleasure and accompanied by equanimity. It is of three kinds by way of inferior, middling, and superior; and likewise by way of accompanied by applied and sustained thought, etc., accompanied by rapture, etc., and with a limited, exalted, and immeasurable object. It is of four kinds by way of painful progress with sluggish direct knowledge, etc., and likewise by way of limited with a limited object, etc., by way of the four jh\u0101na factors, by way of partaking of decline, etc., by way of the realm of sense desires, etc., and by way of predominance. It is of five kinds by way of the five jh\u0101na factors in the fivefold method.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 pergunta: 'Quantos tipos de concentra\xe7\xe3o existem?': Em primeiro lugar, pela caracter\xedstica de n\xe3o distra\xe7\xe3o, \xe9 de um s\xf3 tipo. \xc9 de dois tipos pela distin\xe7\xe3o entre acesso e absor\xe7\xe3o; da mesma forma, pelas distin\xe7\xf5es entre mundana e supramundana, com \xeaxtase e sem \xeaxtase, acompanhada de felicidade e acompanhada de equanimidade. \xc9 de tr\xeas tipos pela divis\xe3o em inferior, m\xe9dia e superior; igualmente, pelas divis\xf5es entre acompanhada de pensamento aplicado e sustentado, etc., acompanhada de arroubo, etc., e com objeto limitado, sublime ou imensur\xe1vel. \xc9 de quatro tipos pela divis\xe3o entre pr\xe1tica dolorosa de intui\xe7\xe3o lenta, etc.; e igualmente, pela divis\xe3o entre limitada com objeto limitado, etc., pelos fatores dos quatro jh\u0101nas, por tender ao decl\xednio, etc., pelo plano dos sentidos, etc., e pelo fator predominante. \xc9 de cinco tipos, no m\xe9todo qu\xedntuplo, pelos fatores dos cinco jh\u0101nas.",es:"En cuanto a la pregunta: '\xbfDe cu\xe1ntas clases es la concentraci\xf3n?': en primer lugar, por la caracter\xedstica de la no distracci\xf3n, es de una sola clase. Es de dos clases seg\xfan el acceso y la absorci\xf3n; del mismo modo, seg\xfan sea mundana o supramundana, con gozo o sin gozo, acompa\xf1ada de placer o acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad. Es de tres clases seg\xfan sea inferior, media o superior; asimismo, seg\xfan est\xe9 acompa\xf1ada de pensamiento aplicado y sostenido, etc., seg\xfan est\xe9 acompa\xf1ada de arrobamiento, etc., o seg\xfan tenga un objeto limitado, sublime o inconmensurable. Es de cuatro clases seg\xfan el progreso doloroso y la captaci\xf3n lenta, etc.; asimismo, seg\xfan sea limitada con un objeto limitado, etc., seg\xfan los factores de los cuatro jh\u0101nas, seg\xfan favorezca el declive, etc., seg\xfan pertenezca a la esfera sensorial, etc., y seg\xfan el factor predominante. Es de cinco clases seg\xfan los factores de los cinco jh\u0101nas en el m\xe9todo qu\xedntuplo."}},{id:"vism-11.5",pali:"Id\u0101ni \u0101rupp\u0101nantara\u1e43 ek\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101ti eva\u1e43 uddi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya \u0101h\u0101re pa\u1e6dikk\u016blasa\xf1\xf1\u0101ya bh\u0101van\u0101niddeso anuppatto. Tattha \u0101harat\u012bti \u0101h\u0101ro. So catubbidho kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101r\u0101h\u0101ro, phass\u0101h\u0101ro, manosa\xf1cetan\u0101h\u0101ro, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101h\u0101roti. Tattha ima\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 bh\u0101vetuk\u0101mena kulaputtena gamanapariyesanabhoga\u0101sayaniddh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101divasena kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101re \u0101h\u0101re pa\u1e6dikk\u016blat\u0101 paccavekkhitabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Now, immediately after the immaterial attainments, the detailed exposition of the development of the perception of repulsiveness in nutriment\u2014which was pointed out in brief as 'one perception'\u2014has come in due course. Therein, 'nutriment' (\u0101h\u0101ra) is so called because it brings (\u0101harati) [its fruit]. It is of four kinds: physical nutriment, contact as nutriment, mental volition as nutriment, and consciousness as nutriment. Therein, one who wishes to develop this meditation subject should review the repulsiveness in physical nutriment by way of going, seeking, consuming, receptacle, digestion, and so forth.",pt:"Agora, imediatamente ap\xf3s os estados imateriais, a exposi\xe7\xe3o do desenvolvimento da percep\xe7\xe3o da repulsividade no alimento, que foi mencionada brevemente como 'uma percep\xe7\xe3o', chegou em sua devida ordem. Nele, \xe9 chamado de 'alimento' (\u0101h\u0101ra) porque traz (\u0101harati) seu pr\xf3prio fruto. \xc9 de quatro tipos: alimento f\xedsico (kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101r\u0101h\u0101ra), contato (phass\u0101h\u0101ra), voli\xe7\xe3o mental (manosa\xf1cetan\u0101h\u0101ra) e consci\xeancia (vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101h\u0101ra). Aquele que deseja cultivar este tema de medita\xe7\xe3o deve refletir sobre a repulsividade do alimento f\xedsico quanto ao ato de ir busc\xe1-lo, \xe0 procura, ao consumo, ao recept\xe1culo estomacal, \xe0 digest\xe3o e demais aspectos.",es:"Ahora, inmediatamente despu\xe9s de los estados inmateriales, ha llegado el turno de la exposici\xf3n del desarrollo de la percepci\xf3n de lo repulsivo en la comida, mencionada como 'una percepci\xf3n'. En ese contexto, se llama nutrimento a aquello que sustenta. Este es de cuatro clases: nutrimento f\xedsico, del contacto, de la volici\xf3n mental y de la conciencia. Quien desee desarrollar este tema de meditaci\xf3n debe reflexionar sobre lo repulsivo del nutrimento f\xedsico considerando el desplazamiento, la b\xfasqueda, la ingesti\xf3n, el recept\xe1culo estomacal, la digesti\xf3n y dem\xe1s fases."}},{id:"vism-11.6",pali:"Mah\u0101hatthipad\u016bpame pana \u2013 \u2018\u2018katam\u0101 c\u0101vuso, ajjhattik\u0101 pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu? Ya\u1e43 ajjhatta\u1e43 paccatta\u1e43 kakkhala\u1e43 kharigata\u1e43 up\u0101dinna\u1e43, seyyathida\u1e43 \u2013 kes\u0101 lom\u0101 nakh\u0101 dant\u0101 taco ma\u1e43sa\u1e43 nh\u0101ru a\u1e6d\u1e6dhi a\u1e6d\u1e6dhimi\xf1ja\u1e43 vakka\u1e43 hadaya\u1e43 yakana\u1e43 kilomaka\u1e43 pihaka\u1e43 papph\u0101sa\u1e43 anta\u1e43 antagu\u1e47a\u1e43 udariya\u1e43 kar\u012bsa\u1e43, ya\u1e43 v\u0101 pana\xf1\xf1ampi atthi ajjhatta\u1e43 paccatta\u1e43 kakkhala\u1e43 kharigata\u1e43 up\u0101dinna\u1e43 \u2013 aya\u1e43 vuccat\u0101vuso, ajjhattik\u0101 pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu\u2019\u2019ti (ma. ni. 1.300).",translations:{en:"Furthermore, in the Mah\u0101hatthipadopama Sutta (The Great Elephant Footprint Simile): 'And what, friends, is the internal earth element? Whatever is internal, belonging to oneself, hard, solid, clung to; that is to say: head hairs, body hairs, nails, teeth, skin, flesh, sinews, bones, bone marrow, kidneys, heart, liver, diaphragm, spleen, lungs, large intestine, small intestine, contents of the stomach, feces, or whatever else internal, belonging to oneself, is hard, solid, clung to\u2014this, friends, is called the internal earth element.'",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, no Mah\u0101hatthipadopama Sutta (O Grande Discurso sobre o S\xedmile da Pegada do Elefante): 'E o que \xe9, amigos, o elemento terra interno? Tudo o que \xe9 interno, pertencente a si mesmo, duro, s\xf3lido, objeto de apego, a saber: cabelos, pelos, unhas, dentes, pele, carne, tend\xf5es, ossos, medula \xf3ssea, rins, cora\xe7\xe3o, f\xedgado, diafragma, ba\xe7o, pulm\xf5es, intestino grosso, intestino delgado, alimento n\xe3o digerido, fezes, ou qualquer outra coisa interna que seja s\xf3lida \u2014 a isto se chama elemento terra interno'.",es:"Asimismo, en el Mah\u0101hatthipadopama Sutta: '\xbfY qu\xe9 es, amigos, el elemento tierra interno? Cualquier cosa interna, propia, dura, s\xf3lida y apropiada, como cabellos, vellos, u\xf1as, dientes, piel, carne, tendones, huesos, m\xe9dula \xf3sea, ri\xf1ones, coraz\xf3n, h\xedgado, membranas, bazo, pulmones, intestinos, mesenterio, contenido estomacal, heces, o cualquier otra cosa interna que sea dura o s\xf3lida: esto, amigos, se llama el elemento tierra interno'."}},{id:"vism-11.7",pali:"Katam\u0101 c\u0101vuso, ajjhattik\u0101 \u0101podh\u0101tu? Ya\u1e43 ajjhatta\u1e43 paccatta\u1e43 \u0101po \u0101pogata\u1e43 up\u0101dinna\u1e43, seyyathida\u1e43 \u2013 pitta\u1e43 semha\u1e43 pubbo lohita\u1e43 sedo medo assu vas\u0101 khe\u1e37o si\u1e45gh\u0101\u1e47ik\u0101 lasik\u0101 mutta\u1e43, ya\u1e43 v\u0101 pana\xf1\xf1ampi atthi ajjhatta\u1e43 paccatta\u1e43 \u0101po \u0101pogata\u1e43 up\u0101dinna\u1e43 \u2013 aya\u1e43 vuccat\u0101vuso, ajjhattik\u0101 \u0101podh\u0101t\u016bti (ma. ni. 1.302).",translations:{en:"'And what, friends, is the internal water element? Whatever is internal, belonging to oneself, water, watery, clung to; that is to say: bile, phlegm, pus, blood, sweat, fat, tears, grease, spit, snot, synovial fluid, urine, or whatever else internal, belonging to oneself, is water, watery, clung to\u2014this, friends, is called the internal water element.'",pt:"'E o que \xe9, amigos, o elemento \xe1gua interno? Tudo o que \xe9 interno, pertencente a si mesmo, l\xedquido, aquoso, objeto de apego, a saber: b\xedlis, fleuma, pus, sangue, suor, gordura, l\xe1grimas, sebo, saliva, muco nasal, l\xedquido sinovial, urina, ou qualquer outra coisa interna, pertencente a si mesmo, que seja l\xedquida, aquosa, objeto de apego \u2014 a isto, amigos, chama-se o elemento \xe1gua interno'.",es:"'\xbfY qu\xe9 es, amigos, el elemento agua interno? Cualquier cosa interna, propia, fluida, acuosa y apropiada, a saber: bilis, flema, pus, sangre, sudor, grasa, l\xe1grimas, unto, saliva, mucosidad, l\xedquido sinovial, orina, o cualquier otra cosa interna propia que sea l\xedquida o fluida: esto, amigos, se llama el elemento agua interno'."}},{id:"vism-11.8",pali:"Katam\u0101 c\u0101vuso, ajjhattik\u0101 tejodh\u0101tu? Ya\u1e43 ajjhatta\u1e43 paccatta\u1e43 tejo tejogata\u1e43 up\u0101dinna\u1e43, seyyathida\u1e43 \u2013 yena ca santappati, yena ca j\u012br\u012byati, yena ca pari\u1e0dayhati, yena ca asitap\u012btakh\u0101yitas\u0101yita\u1e43 samm\u0101 pari\u1e47\u0101ma\u1e43 gacchati, ya\u1e43 v\u0101 pana\xf1\xf1ampi atthi ajjhatta\u1e43 paccatta\u1e43 tejo tejogata\u1e43 up\u0101dinna\u1e43 \u2013 aya\u1e43 vuccat\u0101vuso, ajjhattik\u0101 tejodh\u0101t\u016bti (ma. ni. 1.304).",translations:{en:"'And what, friends, is the internal fire element? Whatever is internal, belonging to oneself, fire, fiery, clung to; that is to say: that by which one is warmed, that by which one ages, that by which one is burned up, and that by which what is eaten, drunk, chewed, and tasted is fully digested, or whatever else internal, belonging to oneself, is fire, fiery, clung to\u2014this, friends, is called the internal fire element.'",pt:"'E o que \xe9, amigos, o elemento fogo interno? Tudo o que \xe9 interno, pertencente a si mesmo, calor, \xedgneo, objeto de apego, a saber: aquilo pelo qual se \xe9 aquecido, pelo qual se envelhece, pelo qual se queima de febre e pelo qual o que foi comido, bebido, mastigado e saboreado \xe9 devidamente digerido, ou qualquer outra coisa interna que seja calor \u2014 a isto, amigos, chama-se o elemento fogo interno'.",es:"'\xbfY qu\xe9 es, amigos, el elemento fuego interno? Cualquier cosa interna, propia, \xedgnea, caliente y apropiada, a saber: aquello por lo cual uno entra en calor, por lo cual uno envejece, por lo cual uno se quema y por lo cual lo comido, bebido, masticado y saboreado se digiere por completo, o cualquier otra cosa interna que sea fuego o calor: esto se llama el elemento fuego interno'."}},{id:"vism-11.9",pali:"Katam\u0101 c\u0101vuso, ajjhattik\u0101 v\u0101yodh\u0101tu? Ya\u1e43 ajjhatta\u1e43 paccatta\u1e43 v\u0101yo v\u0101yogata\u1e43 up\u0101dinna\u1e43, seyyathida\u1e43 \u2013 uddha\u1e45gam\u0101 v\u0101t\u0101, adhogam\u0101 v\u0101t\u0101, kucchisay\u0101 v\u0101t\u0101, ko\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101say\u0101 v\u0101t\u0101, a\u1e45gama\u1e45g\u0101nus\u0101rino v\u0101t\u0101, ass\u0101so pass\u0101so iti v\u0101, ya\u1e43 v\u0101 pana\xf1\xf1ampi atthi ajjhatta\u1e43 paccatta\u1e43 v\u0101yo v\u0101yogata\u1e43 up\u0101dinna\u1e43 \u2013 aya\u1e43 vuccat\u0101vuso, ajjhattik\u0101 v\u0101yodh\u0101t\u016bti (ma. ni. 1.306).",translations:{en:"'And what, friends, is the internal air element? Whatever is internal, belonging to oneself, air, airy, clung to; that is to say: upward-moving winds, downward-moving winds, winds in the stomach, winds in the belly, winds coursing through the limbs, in-breath and out-breath, or whatever else internal, belonging to oneself, is air, airy, clung to\u2014this, friends, is called the internal air element.'",pt:"'E o que \xe9, amigos, o elemento ar interno? Tudo o que \xe9 interno, pertencente a si mesmo, ar, gasoso, objeto de apego, a saber: os ventos que sobem, os ventos que descem, os ventos no est\xf4mago, os ventos nos intestinos, os ventos que percorrem os membros, a inspira\xe7\xe3o e a expira\xe7\xe3o, ou qualquer outra coisa interna que seja ar ou movimento \u2014 a isto, amigos, chama-se o elemento ar interno'.",es:"'\xbfY qu\xe9 es, amigos, el elemento aire interno? Cualquier cosa interna, propia, e\xf3lica, m\xf3vil y apropiada, a saber: vientos ascendentes, vientos descendentes, vientos en el est\xf3mago, vientos en el vientre, vientos que recorren los miembros, la respiraci\xf3n entrante y saliente, o cualquier otra cosa interna que sea aire o movimiento: esto se llama el elemento aire interno'."}},{id:"vism-11.10",pali:"Iti v\u012bsatiy\u0101 \u0101k\u0101rehi pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu, dv\u0101dasahi \u0101podh\u0101tu, cat\u016bhi tejodh\u0101tu, chahi v\u0101yodh\u0101t\u016bti vitth\u0101rato catubbidh\u0101 dh\u0101tuyo vavatthapetabb\u0101. Eva\u1e43 vavatthapento ca t\u0101sa\u1e43 catunna\u1e43 dh\u0101t\u016bna\u1e43 salakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 pariggahetv\u0101 nissattasabh\u0101va\u1e43 su\xf1\xf1ata\u1e43 passati.",translations:{en:"Thus, in twenty aspects the earth element, in twelve the water element, in four the fire element, and in six the air element: in this way the four elements should be determined in detail. Determining them thus and comprehending their individual characteristics, one sees their nature as devoid of a being, seeing their emptiness.",pt:"Assim, o elemento terra deve ser discriminado em vinte aspectos, o elemento \xe1gua em doze, o elemento fogo em quatro e o elemento ar em seis: desse modo os quatro elementos devem ser definidos detalhadamente. Ao delimit\xe1-los assim e discernir as suas caracter\xedsticas individuais, o praticante compreende a aus\xeancia de uma entidade substancial (nissatta) e contempla a sua vacuidade inerente (su\xf1\xf1at\u0101).",es:"As\xed, el elemento tierra debe delimitarse en veinte aspectos, el elemento agua en doce, el elemento fuego en cuatro y el elemento aire en seis: de este modo deben distinguirse detalladamente los cuatro elementos. Al determinarlos as\xed y captar sus caracter\xedsticas individuales, el monje contempla la vaciedad y la ausencia de una entidad individual sustancial en ellos."}},{id:"vism-11.11",pali:"Lakkha\u1e47\u0101ditoti pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu ki\u1e43 lakkha\u1e47\u0101, ki\u1e43 ras\u0101, ki\u1e43 paccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101? Kakkhalalakkha\u1e47\u0101 pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu, pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nakaras\u0101, sampa\u1e6dicchanapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101. Pagghara\u1e47alakkha\u1e47\u0101 \u0101podh\u0101tu, br\u016bhanaras\u0101, sa\u1e45gahapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101. U\u1e47hattalakkha\u1e47\u0101 tejodh\u0101tu, parip\u0101canaras\u0101, samann\u0101h\u0101rapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101. Vitthambhanalakkha\u1e47\u0101 v\u0101yodh\u0101tu, samud\u012bra\u1e47aras\u0101, abhinih\u0101raparip\u0101lanapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101.",translations:{en:"By way of characteristics, etc.: What are the characteristic, function, and manifestation of the earth element? The earth element has the characteristic of hardness, its function is serving as a foundation, its manifestation is receiving. The water element has the characteristic of trickling, its function is intensifying, its manifestation is cohesion. The fire element has the characteristic of heat, its function is maturing, its manifestation is supplying softness. The air element has the characteristic of distension, its function is causing movement, its manifestation is conveying and supporting.",pt:"Quanto \xe0s caracter\xedsticas e demais aspectos: qual \xe9 a caracter\xedstica, a fun\xe7\xe3o e a manifesta\xe7\xe3o do elemento terra? O elemento terra tem a rigidez como caracter\xedstica, sustentar como fun\xe7\xe3o e receber como manifesta\xe7\xe3o. O elemento \xe1gua tem a fluidez como caracter\xedstica, intensificar como fun\xe7\xe3o e a coes\xe3o como manifesta\xe7\xe3o. O elemento fogo tem o calor como caracter\xedstica, amadurecer como fun\xe7\xe3o e propiciar maleabilidade como manifesta\xe7\xe3o. O elemento ar tem a distens\xe3o como caracter\xedstica, impulsionar o movimento como fun\xe7\xe3o e sustentar o deslocamento como manifesta\xe7\xe3o.",es:"Por sus caracter\xedsticas y propiedades: \xbfcu\xe1l es la caracter\xedstica, la funci\xf3n y la manifestaci\xf3n del elemento tierra? El elemento tierra tiene la dureza por caracter\xedstica, servir de base por funci\xf3n y la recepci\xf3n por manifestaci\xf3n. El elemento agua tiene la fluidez por caracter\xedstica, hacer crecer por funci\xf3n y la cohesi\xf3n por manifestaci\xf3n. El elemento fuego tiene el calor por caracter\xedstica, madurar por funci\xf3n y aportar docilidad por manifestaci\xf3n. El elemento aire tiene la distensi\xf3n por caracter\xedstica, impulsar el movimiento por funci\xf3n y sostener por manifestaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-11.12",pali:"Ida\xf1ca pana catudh\u0101tuvavatth\u0101na\u1e43 anuyutto bhikkhu su\xf1\xf1ata\u1e43 avag\u0101hati, amanasikaronto sattasa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 jahitv\u0101 cat\u016bsu dh\u0101t\u016bsu citta\u1e43 \u1e6dhapeti. Tassa su\xf1\xf1at\u0101nupassan\u0101 vu\u1e0d\u1e0dhi\u1e43 gacchati, pariyod\u0101yanti \u0101sav\u0101, nibb\u0101nasa\xf1\xf1ino citta\u1e43 nibb\u0101n\u0101bhimukha\u1e43 namati.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, a monk devoted to this analysis of the four elements plunges into emptiness; abandoning the perception of a living being through non-attention to it, he establishes his mind upon the four elements. His contemplation of emptiness grows, his taints are purified, and his mind, perceiving Nibb\u0101na, inclines towards Nibb\u0101na.",pt:"O monge dedicado a esta discrimina\xe7\xe3o dos quatro elementos mergulha na vacuidade; abandonando a ilus\xe3o de um ser individual atrav\xe9s da cessa\xe7\xe3o dessa falsa percep\xe7\xe3o, ele fixa sua mente nos quatro elementos fundamentais. O seu discernimento da vacuidade se aprofunda, as impurezas mentais se extinguem e a sua mente, reconhecendo o Nibb\u0101na, inclina-se resolutamente em dire\xe7\xe3o ao Nibb\u0101na.",es:"Asimismo, el monje consagrado a esta delimitaci\xf3n de los cuatro elementos se sumerge en la vaciedad; abandonando la percepci\xf3n de un ser sustancial al dejar de prestarle atenci\xf3n, fija su mente en los cuatro elementos. Su contemplaci\xf3n de la vaciedad madura, sus impurezas se disipan y su mente, atenta al Nibbana, se inclina resueltamente hacia el Nibbana."}},{id:"vism-11.13",pali:"Ett\u0101vat\u0101 ca ya\u1e43 sam\u0101dhissa vitth\u0101ra\u1e43 bh\u0101van\u0101naya\xf1ca dassetu\u1e43 \u2018\u2018ko sam\u0101dhi, kena\u1e6d\u1e6dhena sam\u0101dh\u012b\u2019\u2019ti\u0101din\u0101 nayena pa\xf1h\u0101kamma\u1e43 kata\u1e43, tattha \u2018\u2018katha\u1e43 bh\u0101vetabbo\u2019\u2019ti imassa padassa sabbappak\u0101rato atthava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101 samatt\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"And thus far, regarding the task of questioning undertaken by the method beginning with, 'What is concentration? In what sense is it concentration?' in order to show the details of concentration and the method of its development, the explanation of the meaning of this phrase, 'How is it to be developed?' has been completed in every respect.",pt:"E assim, no que diz respeito \xe0s perguntas formuladas pelo m\xe9todo que come\xe7a com 'O que \xe9 a concentra\xe7\xe3o? Em que sentido \xe9 concentra\xe7\xe3o?', com o prop\xf3sito de expor os detalhes da concentra\xe7\xe3o e o m\xe9todo de seu desenvolvimento, a explica\xe7\xe3o do significado da frase 'Como deve ser desenvolvida?' foi conclu\xedda em todos os seus aspectos.",es:"Y hasta este punto, en cuanto a las cuestiones planteadas comenzando por: '\xbfQu\xe9 es la concentraci\xf3n? \xbfEn qu\xe9 sentido es concentraci\xf3n?', con el prop\xf3sito de mostrar el detalle de la concentraci\xf3n y el m\xe9todo de desarrollo, se ha completado en todos sus aspectos la explicaci\xf3n del sentido de la frase: '\xbfC\xf3mo debe ser desarrollada?'."}},{id:"vism-11.14",pali:"Duvidhoyeva haya\u1e43 idha adhippeto upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi ceva appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi ca. Tattha dasasu kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu, appan\u0101pubbabh\u0101gacittesu ca ekaggat\u0101 upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi. Avasesakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu cittekaggat\u0101 appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi. So duvidhopi tesa\u1e43 kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101na\u1e43 bh\u0101vitatt\u0101 bh\u0101vito hoti.",translations:{en:"Here, this concentration is intended as only of two kinds: access concentration and absorption concentration. Therein, one-pointedness in the ten meditation subjects and in the thoughts preliminary to absorption is access concentration. One-pointedness of mind in the remaining meditation subjects is absorption concentration. And both kinds are developed through the development of those meditation subjects.",pt:"A concentra\xe7\xe3o aqui pretendida \xe9 de apenas dois tipos: a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso (upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi) e a concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi). Dentre estas, a unifica\xe7\xe3o mental nos dez primeiros temas de medita\xe7\xe3o e nos momentos que antecedem a absor\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso. A unifica\xe7\xe3o da mente nos temas restantes \xe9 a concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o. Ambos os tipos s\xe3o desenvolvidos atrav\xe9s da pr\xe1tica desses respectivos temas de medita\xe7\xe3o.",es:"Aqu\xed, la concentraci\xf3n a la que se aspira es \xfanicamente de dos clases: la concentraci\xf3n de acceso y la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n. Entre ellas, la unificaci\xf3n de la mente en los diez temas de meditaci\xf3n y en los pensamientos previos a la absorci\xf3n es la concentraci\xf3n de acceso. La unificaci\xf3n mental en los temas de meditaci\xf3n restantes es la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n. Y ambas clases quedan desarrolladas gracias al desarrollo de dichos objetos meditativos."}},{id:"vism-11.15",pali:"Ya\u1e43 pana vutta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101ya ko \u0101nisa\u1e43so\u2019\u2019ti, tattha di\u1e6d\u1e6dhadhammasukhavih\u0101r\u0101dipa\xf1cavidho sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101ya \u0101nisa\u1e43so. Kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sav\u0101na\u1e43 t\u0101va arahattaphalasam\u0101pattisampayuttasam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhadhammasukhavih\u0101r\u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"Now, regarding what was said, 'What is the benefit of the development of concentration?': Therein, the benefit of the development of concentration is fivefold, beginning with pleasant abiding in the present life. For the Arahants whose taints are destroyed, the development of concentration associated with the attainment of the fruition of Arahantship has pleasant abiding in the present life as its benefit.",pt:"Quanto ao que foi perguntado: 'Qual \xe9 o benef\xedcio do cultivo da concentra\xe7\xe3o?': nele, o benef\xedcio do desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o \xe9 qu\xedntuplo, come\xe7ando pela viv\xeancia feliz no presente momento (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhadhammasukhavih\u0101ra). Para os Arahants que destru\xedram as impurezas, o cultivo da concentra\xe7\xe3o associado \xe0 realiza\xe7\xe3o do fruto do estado de Arahant tem como benef\xedcio a viv\xeancia pac\xedfica e feliz no momento presente.",es:"En cuanto a lo que se dijo: '\xbfCu\xe1l es el fruto del desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n?': en ello, el beneficio del desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n es qu\xedntuple, comenzando por el gozoso vivir en el presente. Para los Arahants con las impurezas destruidas, el desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n asociada a la realizaci\xf3n del fruto de Arahant tiene como beneficio el gozoso vivir en el presente."}},{id:"vism-11.16",pali:"Sekkhaputhujjan\u0101na\u1e43 sam\u0101pattito vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya sam\u0101hitena cittena vipassiss\u0101m\u0101ti bh\u0101vayata\u1e43 vipassan\u0101ya pada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101natt\u0101 appan\u0101sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101pi samb\u0101dhe ok\u0101s\u0101dhigamanayena upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101pi vipassan\u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101 hoti. Ten\u0101ha bhagav\u0101 \u2018\u2018sam\u0101dhi\u1e43, bhikkhave, bh\u0101vetha. Sam\u0101hito, bhikkhave, bhikkhu yath\u0101bh\u016bta\u1e43 paj\u0101n\u0101t\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (sa\u1e43. ni. 3.5).",translations:{en:"For learners and worldlings who develop concentration, thinking, 'Having arisen from attainment, we will practice insight with a concentrated mind,' both the development of absorption concentration\u2014because it is the proximate cause for insight\u2014and the development of access concentration\u2014by the method of gaining an opportunity in confinement\u2014have the benefit of insight. Therefore the Blessed One said: 'Monks, develop concentration. A monk who is concentrated, monks, understands things as they really are' (SN 22.5).",pt:"Para os disc\xedpulos em treinamento e as pessoas comuns que, tendo emergido da realiza\xe7\xe3o, desenvolvem a concentra\xe7\xe3o pensando: 'Praticaremos a vis\xe3o meditativa com a mente concentrada', tanto o desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o quanto o desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso \u2014 por meio da obten\xe7\xe3o de uma oportunidade em meio ao confinamento \u2014 t\xeam a vis\xe3o meditativa como benef\xedcio, por ser a causa pr\xf3xima para a vis\xe3o meditativa. Por isso o Aben\xe7oado disse: 'Monges, desenvolvei a concentra\xe7\xe3o. O monge concentrado, monges, compreende as coisas como elas realmente s\xe3o'.",es:"Para los aprendices (sekha) y los hombres comunes (puthujjana) que, tras emerger de la absorci\xf3n, desarrollan la concentraci\xf3n pensando: 'Practicaremos la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassan\u0101) con la mente concentrada', el desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n \u2014e incluso el desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n de acceso al obtener una oportunidad en medio de las limitaciones\u2014 tiene como beneficio la visi\xf3n cabal, por ser su causa pr\xf3xima. Por eso dijo el Bendito: 'Monjes, desarrollen la concentraci\xf3n. El monje que est\xe1 concentrado comprende las cosas tal como son'."}},{id:"vism-11.17",pali:"Ye pana a\u1e6d\u1e6dha sam\u0101pattiyo nibbattetv\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101p\u0101daka\u1e43 jh\u0101na\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjitv\u0101 sam\u0101pattito vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya ekopi hutv\u0101 bahudh\u0101 hot\u012bti vuttanay\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101yo patthento nibbattenti, tesa\u1e43 sati sati \u0101yatane abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101pada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101natt\u0101 appan\u0101sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101 hoti. Ten\u0101ha bhagav\u0101 \u2013 \u2018\u2018so yassa yassa abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101sacchikara\u1e47\u012byassa dhammassa citta\u1e43 abhininn\u0101meti abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101sacchikiriy\u0101ya, tatra tatreva sakkhibhabbata\u1e43 p\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101ti sati sati \u0101yatane\u2019\u2019ti (ma. ni. 3.158; a. ni. 3.102).",translations:{en:"For those who, having produced the eight attainments, enter the jh\u0101na that is the basis for the super-knowledges, and emerging from that attainment, desire and produce the super-knowledges in the manner taught as, 'Having been one, he becomes many,' for them, when the supporting condition exists, because it is the proximate cause for the super-knowledges, the development of absorption concentration has the super-knowledges as its benefit. Therefore, the Blessed One said: 'He directs his mind towards whatever phenomenon is to be directly realized by super-knowledge, for the sake of direct realization by super-knowledge; when the supporting condition exists, he attains the state of being capable of directly witnessing it in that very phenomenon.'",pt:"Para aqueles que, tendo produzido as oito realiza\xe7\xf5es e entrado no jh\u0101na que serve de base para o conhecimento direto, emergem da realiza\xe7\xe3o e produzem os conhecimentos diretos desejando-os \u2014 conforme o m\xe9todo descrito em 'sendo um, ele se torna muitos' \u2014, o desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o tem o conhecimento direto como benef\xedcio, por ser a causa pr\xf3xima para o conhecimento direto, desde que as condi\xe7\xf5es necess\xe1rias estejam presentes. Por isso o Aben\xe7oado disse: 'Para qualquer estado realiz\xe1vel por meio do conhecimento direto ao qual ele incline a sua mente para a realiza\xe7\xe3o por meio do conhecimento direto, ele alcan\xe7a a capacidade de testemunh\xe1-lo pessoalmente ali mesmo, desde que as condi\xe7\xf5es necess\xe1rias estejam presentes'.",es:"Para aquellos que, habiendo producido las ocho realizaciones y entrado en el jhana que sirve de base para el conocimiento directo, emergen de la absorci\xf3n y producen los conocimientos directos anhelados, seg\xfan el m\xe9todo descrito como 'siendo uno, se vuelve muchos', su desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n tiene como beneficio el conocimiento directo, por ser su causa pr\xf3xima siempre que exista la base necesaria. Por eso dijo el Bendito: 'Cualquier estado realizable mediante el conocimiento directo hacia el cual \xe9l incline su mente para realizarlo por conocimiento directo, alcanza la capacidad de atestiguarlo en ese mismo aspecto, siempre que exista la base necesaria'."}},{id:"vism-11.18",pali:"Ye pana ariy\u0101 a\u1e6d\u1e6dha sam\u0101pattiyo nibbattetv\u0101 nirodhasam\u0101patti\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjitv\u0101 satta divas\u0101ni acitt\u0101 hutv\u0101 di\u1e6d\u1e6dheva dhamme nirodha\u1e43 nibb\u0101na\u1e43 patv\u0101 sukha\u1e43 vihariss\u0101m\u0101ti sam\u0101dhi\u1e43 bh\u0101venti, tesa\u1e43 appan\u0101sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101 nirodh\u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101 hoti. Ten\u0101ha \u2013 \u2018\u2018so\u1e37asahi \xf1\u0101\u1e47acariy\u0101hi navahi sam\u0101dhicariy\u0101hi vas\u012bbh\u0101vat\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 nirodhasam\u0101pattiy\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti (pa\u1e6di. ma. 1.34).",translations:{en:"Furthermore, for those noble ones who, having produced the eight attainments, enter the attainment of cessation and, having been without mind for seven days, having reached cessation\u2014Nibb\u0101na\u2014in this very life, develop concentration thinking, 'We will dwell happily,' for them, the development of absorption concentration has the attainment of cessation as its benefit. Therefore, it is said: 'Wisdom which is mastery through the sixteen courses of knowledge and the nine courses of concentration is the knowledge regarding the attainment of cessation.'",pt:"Para os nobres que, tendo produzido as os oito realiza\xe7\xf5es e entrado na realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o, permanecem sem mente por sete dias e desenvolvem a concentra\xe7\xe3o pensando 'Viveremos felizes tendo alcan\xe7ado a cessa\xe7\xe3o, o Nibb\u0101na, nesta mesma vida', o desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o deles tem a cessa\xe7\xe3o como benef\xedcio. Por isso foi dito: 'A sabedoria que consiste no dom\xednio de dezesseis comportamentos de conhecimento e nove comportamentos de concentra\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o conhecimento da realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o'.",es:"Por otra parte, aquellos Nobles que, habiendo alcanzado los ocho logros (sam\u0101patti), entran en el logro de la cesaci\xf3n (nirodhasam\u0101patti) y permanecen sin conciencia durante siete d\xedas, diciendo: \xabMoraremos felices habiendo alcanzado en esta misma vida la cesaci\xf3n, que es el Nibbana\xbb, para ellos el desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n tiene como beneficio la cesaci\xf3n. Por eso se dijo: \xabEl conocimiento de la maestr\xeda a trav\xe9s de diecis\xe9is tipos de conducta del conocimiento y nueve tipos de conducta de la concentraci\xf3n es el conocimiento del logro de la cesaci\xf3n\xbb."}},{id:"vism-11.19",pali:"\u2018\u2018Tasm\u0101 nek\u0101nisa\u1e43samhi, kilesamalasodhane; Sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101yoge, nappamajjeyya pa\u1e47\u1e0dito\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"Therefore, in the practice of developing concentration, which has many benefits and cleanses the stains of defilements, a wise person should not be negligent.",pt:"\u201cPortanto, em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 pr\xe1tica do desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o, que traz in\xfameros benef\xedcios e purifica as impurezas mentais, o s\xe1bio jamais deve ser negligente.\u201d",es:"\xabPor lo tanto, en la pr\xe1ctica del desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n, que posee m\xfaltiples beneficios y purifica las impurezas de las aflicciones (kilesas), el sabio no debe ser negligente\xbb."}}]},429,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,i,n,t,s){n.exports=[{id:"vism-12.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni y\u0101sa\u1e43 lokik\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43 vasena aya\u1e43 sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101ti vutt\u0101, t\u0101sa\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101panattha\u1e43 iddhividh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 pa\xf1canna\u1e43 lokik\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101na\u1e43 uddeso vutto. Bhagavat\u0101 hi adhigatacatutthajjh\u0101nasam\u0101dh\u012bna\u1e43 kulaputt\u0101na\u1e43 sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101nisa\u1e43sadassanattha\u1e43 pa\xf1ca lokiy\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101yo desit\u0101, t\u0101su pa\u1e6dham\u0101 t\u0101va iddhividh\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101.",translations:{en:"Now, this development of concentration was said to have the benefit of direct knowledge by virtue of the worldly direct knowledges; in order to explain them, the exposition of the five worldly direct knowledges, beginning with the kinds of psychic power, was stated. For the Blessed One, in order to show the benefits of the development of concentration to those clansmen who had attained the concentration of the fourth jh\u0101na, taught five mundane direct knowledges; of these, the first is the direct knowledge of the kinds of psychic power.",pt:"Agora, visto que foi dito que este desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o tem como benef\xedcio as intelig\xeancias diretas (abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101), gra\xe7as aos conhecimentos diretos mundanos, a exposi\xe7\xe3o das cinco faculdades supranormais mundanas, come\xe7ando pelas modalidades de poder ps\xedquico (iddhi), foi apresentada para esclarec\xea-las. Pois o Aben\xe7oado ensinou cinco conhecimentos diretos mundanos para mostrar os frutos do cultivo da concentra\xe7\xe3o aos nobres praticantes que alcan\xe7aram a estabilidade do quarto jh\u0101na; entre elas, a primeira \xe9 a realiza\xe7\xe3o das v\xe1rias formas de poder ps\xedquico.",es:"Ahora, para llevar a cabo aquellos conocimientos directos mundanos por cuya causa se dijo que este desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n tiene como fruto el conocimiento directo, se presenta la explicaci\xf3n de los cinco conocimientos directos mundanos, comenzando por las modalidades de poder ps\xedquico. Pues el Bienaventurado, con el fin de mostrar los beneficios del desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n a los nobles que hab\xedan alcanzado la concentraci\xf3n del cuarto jh\u0101na, ense\xf1\xf3 cinco conocimientos directos mundanos; entre ellos, el primero es el conocimiento directo de las clases de poder ps\xedquico."}},{id:"vism-12.2",pali:"Bhagavat\u0101 hi adhigatacatutthajjh\u0101nasam\u0101dh\u012bna\u1e43 kulaputt\u0101na\u1e43 sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101nisa\u1e43sadassanattha\u1e43 pa\xf1ca lokiy\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101yo desit\u0101, t\u0101su pa\u1e6dham\u0101 t\u0101va iddhividh\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101. T\u0101ya ca anantar\u0101 dibbasotadh\u0101tu\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, cut\u016bpap\u0101ta\xf1\u0101\u1e47anti im\u0101 pa\xf1ca abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101yo veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"For the Blessed One, in order to show the benefits of the development of concentration to clansmen who have reached the concentration of the fourth jh\u0101na, taught five mundane direct knowledges. Of these, the first is the knowledge of the kinds of psychic power; and following that, the divine ear element, the knowledge of encompassing minds, the knowledge of recollecting past abodes, and the knowledge of passing away and rebirth of beings\u2014these five direct knowledges should be understood.",pt:"Pois o Aben\xe7oado, para mostrar aos nobres disc\xedpulos que alcan\xe7aram a concentra\xe7\xe3o do quarto jh\u0101na os benef\xedcios do cultivo da mente, ensinou cinco intelig\xeancias diretas mundanas. Entre estas, a primeira \xe9 o conhecimento das classes de poder ps\xedquico; e depois dela v\xeam o elemento do ouvido divino, a penetra\xe7\xe3o nos cora\xe7\xf5es alheios, a rememora\xe7\xe3o de vidas passadas e a vis\xe3o da morte e renascimento dos seres \u2014 estas cinco faculdades supranormais devem ser compreendidas.",es:"El Bienaventurado ense\xf1\xf3 los cinco conocimientos directos mundanos a los nobles disc\xedpulos que hab\xedan alcanzado la concentraci\xf3n del cuarto jh\u0101na para mostrarles los beneficios del cultivo mental. De ellos, el primero es el conocimiento de las clases de poderes ps\xedquicos; y a continuaci\xf3n deben comprenderse el elemento del o\xeddo divino, el conocimiento que abarca la mente ajena, la memoria de las moradas previas y la visi\xf3n del morir y renacer de los seres: estos son los cinco conocimientos directos mundanos."}},{id:"vism-12.3",pali:"Tattha ekopi hutv\u0101 bahudh\u0101 hot\u012bti\u0101dika\u1e43 iddhivikubbana\u1e43 k\u0101tuk\u0101mena \u0101dikammikena kulaputtena cuddasahi \u0101k\u0101rehi citta\u1e43 paridametabba\u1e43. Kasi\u1e47\u0101nulomato, kasi\u1e47apa\u1e6dilomato, kasi\u1e47\u0101nulomapa\u1e6dilomato, jh\u0101n\u0101nulomato, jh\u0101napa\u1e6dilomato, jh\u0101n\u0101nulomapa\u1e6dilomato, jh\u0101nukkantikato, kasi\u1e47ukkantikato, jh\u0101nangukkantikato, a\u1e45gukkantikato, \u0101ramma\u1e47ukkantikato, a\u1e45g\u0101ramma\u1e47ukkantikato, a\u1e45gavavatth\u0101panato, \u0101ramma\u1e47avavatth\u0101panatoti.",translations:{en:"Therein, a beginner yogin who wishes to perform the psychic transformations, such as having been one, he becomes many, must tame his mind in fourteen ways: in conformity with the kasi\u1e47as, in reverse of the kasi\u1e47as, in conformity and reverse of the kasi\u1e47as; in conformity with the jh\u0101nas, in reverse of the jh\u0101nas, in conformity and reverse of the jh\u0101nas; by skipping jh\u0101nas, by skipping kasi\u1e47as, by skipping jh\u0101nas and kasi\u1e47as; by skipping factors, by skipping objects, by skipping factors and objects; by determining the factors, and by determining the objects.",pt:"Ali, o praticante iniciante que deseja realizar as transforma\xe7\xf5es ps\xedquicas \u2014 tais como 'sendo um, tornar-se muitos' e assim por diante \u2014 deve disciplinar a sua mente de quatorze maneiras: na ordem direta dos kasi\u1e47as, na ordem inversa dos kasi\u1e47as, na ordem direta e inversa dos kasi\u1e47as; na ordem direta dos jh\u0101nas, na ordem inversa dos jh\u0101nas, na ordem direta e inversa dos jh\u0101nas; saltando jh\u0101nas, saltando kasi\u1e47as, saltando jh\u0101nas e kasi\u1e47as conjuntamente; saltando fatores, saltando objetos, saltando fatores e objetos; determinando os fatores dos jh\u0101nas e determinando os objetos.",es:"All\xed, el noble principiante que desee llevar a cabo la transformaci\xf3n ps\xedquica descrita como 'siendo uno, se multiplica en muchos', debe dominar su mente mediante catorce modalidades: en orden directo de los kasi\u1e47as, en orden inverso de los kasi\u1e47as, en orden directo e inverso de los kasi\u1e47as; en orden directo de los jh\u0101nas, en orden inverso de los jh\u0101nas, en orden directo e inverso de los jh\u0101nas; salteando jh\u0101nas, salteando kasi\u1e47as, salteando jh\u0101nas y kasi\u1e47as conjuntamente; salteando factores, salteando objetos, salteando factores y objetos conjuntamente; discriminando los factores de las absorciones y discriminando los objetos meditativos."}},{id:"vism-12.4",pali:"Imehi pana cuddasahi \u0101k\u0101rehi citta\u1e43 aparidametv\u0101 pubbe abh\u0101vitabh\u0101vanova \u0101dikammikassa bhikkhuno iddhividha\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 upp\u0101detu\u1e43 na sakk\u0101. Kasm\u0101? Asant\u0101na\u1e43 parikamm\u0101na\u1e43 abh\u0101v\u0101. Yath\u0101 hi cheko tantav\u0101yo tantavit\u0101na\u1e43 sam\u0101netv\u0101 cittasutta\u1e43 sa\u1e45kharonto ya\u1e43 ya\u1e43 dussa\u1e43 icchati, ta\u1e43 tameva samp\u0101deti, evameva cuddasahi \u0101k\u0101rehi cittadamane kate yog\u0101vacarassa citta\u1e43 mudu hoti kammaniya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, for a beginner yogin who has not tamed the mind in these fourteen ways and who has not previously developed meditation, it is impossible to produce the knowledge of the kinds of psychic power. Why? Because the preparatory tasks do not exist. For just as a skilled weaver, having set up the loom and preparing the warp threads, produces whatever kind of cloth he wishes, even so, when the taming of the mind in the fourteen ways has been accomplished, the yogi's mind becomes malleable and wieldy.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, sem dominar a mente dessas quatorze maneiras, \xe9 imposs\xedvel para um monge iniciante que n\xe3o tenha desenvolvido a medita\xe7\xe3o anteriormente fazer surgir o conhecimento das v\xe1rias modalidades de poder ps\xedquico. Por qual raz\xe3o? Pela aus\xeancia das etapas preparat\xf3rias necess\xe1rias. Pois assim como um tecel\xe3o habilidoso, preparando o seu tear e organizando os fios, confecciona com perfei\xe7\xe3o qualquer tipo de tecido que desejar, da mesma forma, quando o dom\xednio da mente atrav\xe9s desses quatorze modos \xe9 completado, a mente do meditador se torna extraordinariamente d\xf3cil, male\xe1vel e male\xe1vel.",es:"Asimismo, sin haber dominado la mente mediante estas catorce modalidades, es imposible para un monje principiante que no haya cultivado la absorci\xf3n previamente suscitar el conocimiento de las diversas clases de poderes ps\xedquicos. \xbfPor qu\xe9 raz\xf3n? Por faltar las pr\xe1cticas preparatorias indispensables. As\xed como un h\xe1bil tejedor que, tras preparar el telar y disponer con esmero los hilos, elabora cualquier clase de tela que desee, de la misma manera, habi\xe9ndose completado el adiestramiento mental en las catorce modalidades, la mente del yogui se vuelve sumamente d\xf3cil y maleable."}},{id:"vism-12.5",pali:"Aparo nayo, catutthajjh\u0101nasam\u0101dhin\u0101 sam\u0101hite. N\u012bvara\u1e47ad\u016brabh\u0101vena parisuddhe pariyod\u0101te ana\u1e45ga\u1e47e vigat\u016bpakkilese mudubh\u016bte kammaniye \u1e6dhite \u0101ne\xf1jappatte. So eva\u1e43 sam\u0101hite citte parisuddhe pariyod\u0101te iddhividh\u0101ya citta\u1e43 abhin\u012bharati abhininn\u0101meti.",translations:{en:"Another method: When the mind is composed with the concentration of the fourth jh\u0101na; purified, bright, unblemished, rid of imperfection by being far removed from hindrances, malleable, wieldy, steady, attained to imperturbability. With the mind thus concentrated, purified, and bright, he directs and inclines his mind to the knowledge of the kinds of psychic power.",pt:"Por outro m\xe9todo: estando a mente concentrada atrav\xe9s da estabilidade do quarto jh\u0101na; purificada, luminosa, sem m\xe1cula e liberta de imperfei\xe7\xf5es pelo total afastamento dos obst\xe1culos mentais, tornada male\xe1vel, d\xf3cil, est\xe1vel e tendo atingido a imperturbabilidade. Com a mente assim concentrada, perfeitamente purificada e l\xedmpida, ele inclina e dirige sua mente para a realiza\xe7\xe3o dos m\xfaltiplos poderes ps\xedquicos.",es:"Otro m\xe9todo: estando la mente concentrada mediante la serenidad del cuarto jh\u0101na; purificada, di\xe1fana, sin mancha y libre de imperfecciones por el alejamiento de los obst\xe1culos, flexible, manejable, firme y habiendo alcanzado la imperturbabilidad. Con la mente as\xed concentrada, pura y luminosa, dirige e inclina su mente hacia las diversas modalidades de poderes ps\xedquicos."}},{id:"vism-12.6",pali:"Iddhividh\u0101ya citta\u1e43 abhin\u012bharati abhininn\u0101met\u012bti ettha ijjhana\u1e6d\u1e6dhena iddhi. S\u0101 samijjhana\u1e6d\u1e6dhena sampattiy\u0101 adhivacana\u1e43. Ya\xf1hi ki\xf1ci siddhi\u1e43 p\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101ti, ta\u1e43 sabba\u1e43 \u2018\u2018iddh\u012b\u2019\u2019ti vuccati. Tath\u0101 hi \u2018\u2018iddha\u1e43 ph\u012bta\u2019\u2019nti (d\u012b. ni. 1.284) labbhati.",translations:{en:"In the phrase 'one directs and inclines the mind towards the kinds of psychic power': Here, iddhi is in the sense of succeeding. It is an expression for accomplishment in the sense of succeeding completely. For whatever success one achieves, all of that is called 'iddhi.' Accordingly, the phrase 'successful and prosperous' is found.",pt:"Na passagem 'ele inclina e direciona a mente para as v\xe1rias modalidades de poderes': neste ponto, \xe9 chamada de iddhi no sentido de realiza\xe7\xe3o bem-sucedida (ijjhana). \xc9 uma designa\xe7\xe3o para o \xeaxito consumado no sentido de completa perfei\xe7\xe3o. Pois qualquer sucesso ou realiza\xe7\xe3o espiritual plenamente alcan\xe7ada \xe9 chamada de 'iddhi'. Por conseguinte, usa-se a express\xe3o 'bem-sucedido e pr\xf3spero'.",es:"En la frase 'dirige e inclina la mente hacia las modalidades de poder ps\xedquico': aqu\xed iddhi se entiende en el sentido de consumaci\xf3n o logro exitoso. Es una designaci\xf3n para la plenitud lograda en el sentido de realizaci\xf3n perfecta. Pues cualquier logro extraordinario que se alcance se denomina 'iddhi'. De ah\xed que se use la expresi\xf3n tradicional 'pr\xf3spero y floreciente'."}},{id:"vism-12.7",pali:"Tattha \u2018\u2018pakatiy\u0101 eko bahuka\u1e43 \u0101vajjati. Sata\u1e43 v\u0101 sahassa\u1e43 v\u0101 satasahassa\u1e43 v\u0101 \u0101vajjati. \u0100vajjitv\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47ena adhimuccati \u2018bahuko hom\u012b\u2019ti, bahuko hoti. Seyyath\u0101pi \u0101yasm\u0101 c\u016b\u1e37apanthako eko hutv\u0101 bahuko ahos\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (pa\u1e6di. ma. 2.196) eva\u1e43 ekopi hutv\u0101 bahudh\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"Therein: 'Being one by nature, one adverts to many. Having adverted, one resolves with knowledge: 'Let me be many.' One becomes many, just as the Venerable C\u016b\u1e37apanthaka, having been one, became many.' In this way, having been one, he becomes many.",pt:"A esse respeito: 'Sendo naturalmente um, o meditador projeta a sua mente para a multiplicidade. Projeta para cem, para mil ou para cem mil indiv\xedduos. Tendo projetado, ele determina firmemente com conhecimento: que eu me torne muitos; e ele se torna muitos. Exatamente como o vener\xe1vel C\u016b\u1e37apanthaka que, sendo um s\xf3, se multiplicou em uma multid\xe3o'. Deste modo, tendo sido um s\xf3 indiv\xedduo, ele se torna muitos.",es:"A este respecto: 'Siendo uno por naturaleza, orienta su mente hacia la multiplicidad. Orienta la mente hacia cien, hacia mil o hacia cien mil formas. Habiendo orientado la mente, resuelve con conocimiento: '\xa1que me vuelva muchos!', y se vuelve muchos. As\xed como el venerable C\u016b\u1e37apanthaka, que siendo uno solo, se multiplic\xf3 en muchos'. De esta manera, habiendo sido uno solo, se convierte en multitud."}},{id:"vism-12.8",pali:"\u2018\u2018So pakativa\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 vijahitv\u0101 kum\u0101rakava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 dasseti n\u0101gava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 supa\u1e47\u1e47ava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 asurava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 indava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 brahmava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 samuddava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 pabbatava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 vanava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 s\u012bhava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 byagghava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 d\u012bpiva\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 hatthiva\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 assava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 rathava\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 pattiva\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101 n\u0101n\u0101vidha\xf1ca sen\u0101by\u016bha\u2019\u2019nti (pa\u1e6di. ma. 2.196) eva\u1e43 vikubbanaiddhi hoti.",translations:{en:"'Having abandoned one\u2019s natural appearance, one displays the appearance of a boy, or of a serpent, or of a garu\u1e0da, or of an asura, or of Indra, or of a Brahm\u0101, or of an ocean, or of a mountain, or of a forest, or of a lion, or of a tiger, or of a leopard, or of an elephant, or of a horse, or of a chariot, or of a foot-soldier, or of various military arrays'\u2014thus is psychic power by transformation.",pt:"'Renunciando \xe0 sua apar\xeancia habitual, ele manifesta a forma de uma crian\xe7a, a forma de uma serpente divina (n\u0101ga), de uma ave m\xedstica (garu\u1e0da), de um asura, do deus Indra, de um Grande Brahma, a vastid\xe3o do oceano, a solidez de uma montanha, a extens\xe3o de uma floresta, a apar\xeancia de um le\xe3o, de um tigre, de um leopardo, de um elefante real, de um cavalo nobre, de uma carruagem de guerra, de guerreiros de infantaria ou de ex\xe9rcitos em forma\xe7\xe3o de combate' \u2014 assim opera o poder ps\xedquico de transforma\xe7\xe3o.",es:"'Renunciando a su forma ordinaria, manifiesta la apariencia de un muchacho, o la apariencia de un n\u0101ga, de un garu\u1e0da, de un asura, del dios Indra, de un Brahma, la inmensidad del oc\xe9ano, la figura de una monta\xf1a, la de una selva, la de un le\xf3n, la de un tigre, de un leopardo, de un elefante, de un corcel, de un carro de guerra, de soldados de infanter\xeda o de diversas formaciones de combate': tal es el poder ps\xedquico por transformaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-12.9",pali:"\u2018\u2018Idha bhikkhu imamh\u0101 k\u0101y\u0101 a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 k\u0101ya\u1e43 abhinimmin\u0101ti r\u016bpi\u1e43 manomaya\u1e43 sabba\u1e45gapacca\u1e45ga\u1e43 ah\u012bnindriya\u2019\u2019nti (d\u012b. ni. 1.239) eva\u1e43 manomay\u0101 iddhi veditabb\u0101. So ima\u1e43 k\u0101ya\u1e43 mu\xf1citv\u0101 tato a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 manomaya\u1e43 k\u0101ya\u1e43 nimm\u0101ti, seyyath\u0101pi puriso mu\xf1jamh\u0101 \u012bsika\u1e43 pabb\u0101heyya, asimh\u0101 v\u0101 kosi\u1e43 pabb\u0101heyya, uragamh\u0101 v\u0101 taco nipphu\u1e6do kareyya.",translations:{en:"'Here a bhikkhu creates from this body another body, having form, mind-made, complete in all its limbs and parts, not lacking any sense faculty'\u2014thus should mind-made psychic power be understood. Leaving this physical body aside, he creates another mind-made body from it, just as a man might draw out a reed from mu\xf1ja grass, or draw out a sword from its scabbard, or as a snake might slough off its skin.",pt:"'Aqui um monge cria a partir deste corpo material outro corpo, dotado de forma vis\xedvel, criado pela mente, completo em todos os seus membros e \xf3rg\xe3os, sem que lhe falte faculdade alguma' \u2014 deste modo deve ser compreendido o poder ps\xedquico da cria\xe7\xe3o pelo poder da mente. Deixando este corpo de lado, ele produz a partir dele outro corpo feito pela mente, exatamente como um homem que retira a haste central de uma folha de junco, ou saca uma espada de sua bainha, ou como uma serpente que se desvencilha de sua pele antiga.",es:"'Aqu\xed un monje crea a partir de este cuerpo otro cuerpo provisto de forma, hecho por la mente, completo en todos sus miembros y partes, sin que le falte facultad alguna': as\xed debe comprenderse el poder ps\xedquico producido por la mente. Dejando a un lado este cuerpo, produce a partir de \xe9l otro cuerpo creado por la mente, tal como un hombre que extrae una espiga de ca\xf1a de su vaina, o desenvaina una espada de su funda, o como una serpiente que se desprende de su piel."}},{id:"vism-12.10",pali:"Pa\u1e6dikk\u016bl\u0101d\u012bsu appa\u1e6dikk\u016blasa\xf1\xf1ivih\u0101r\u0101dik\u0101 pana ariy\u0101 iddhi n\u0101ma. Yath\u0101ha \u2013 \u2018\u2018pa\u1e6dikk\u016ble ce \u0101ka\u1e45khati appa\u1e6dikk\u016blasa\xf1\xf1\u012b vihareyya\u1e43, appa\u1e6dikk\u016blasa\xf1\xf1\u012b tattha viharat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (d\u012b. ni. 3.156). Et\u0101ya hi samann\u0101gato kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101savo bhikkhu pa\u1e6dikk\u016ble ani\u1e6d\u1e6dhe vatthusmi\u1e43 mett\u0101phara\u1e47ena v\u0101 dh\u0101tumanasik\u0101rena v\u0101 appa\u1e6dikk\u016blasa\xf1\xf1\u012b viharati.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, the practice of dwelling with the perception of the unrepulsive in what is repulsive, and so on, is called 'noble psychic power.' As it is said: 'If he wishes, \"May I dwell with the perception of the unrepulsive in what is repulsive,\" he dwells there perceiving the unrepulsive' (D\u012b. Ni. 3.156). Endowed with this, an arahant monk with taints destroyed dwells perceiving the unrepulsive in a repulsive, disagreeable object through the pervasion of loving-kindness or by attending to it as elements.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, a pr\xe1tica de permanecer com a percep\xe7\xe3o do n\xe3o repulsivo naquilo que \xe9 repulsivo e vice-versa \xe9 chamada de 'poder ps\xedquico nobre'. Conforme foi ensinado: 'Se ele desejar: que eu permane\xe7a com a percep\xe7\xe3o do n\xe3o repulsivo perante o repulsivo, ele permanece ali percebendo o n\xe3o repulsivo'. Dotado deste poder supremo, o monge com as impurezas extintas (kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sava) habita percebendo o puro e belo num objeto desagrad\xe1vel por meio da irradia\xe7\xe3o do amor-bondade ou pela discrimina\xe7\xe3o dos elementos materiais fundamentais.",es:"Por su parte, el permanecer con la percepci\xf3n de lo no repugnante en lo repugnante, y viceversa, es llamado 'poder ps\xedquico noble'. Como dijo el Bienaventurado: 'Si desea: que habite percibiendo lo no repugnante en lo repugnante, all\xed habita percibiendo lo no repugnante'. Dotado de este poder, el monje que ha destruido todas las impurezas mora percibiendo lo no desagrad\xe1vel en un objeto desagradable mediante la irradiaci\xf3n de la benevolencia universal o atendiendo a \xe9l como meros elementos naturales."}},{id:"vism-12.11",pali:"Tiroku\u1e6d\u1e6da\u1e43 tirop\u0101k\u0101ra\u1e43 tiropabbata\u1e43 asajjam\u0101no gacchati seyyath\u0101pi \u0101k\u0101seti ettha \u0101k\u0101sakasi\u1e47asam\u0101pattiy\u0101 l\u0101bh\u012b hoti. So tiroku\u1e6d\u1e6d\u0101digantuk\u0101mo ku\u1e6d\u1e6dhap\u0101k\u0101rapabbat\u0101na\u1e43 vivaramattampi oloketv\u0101 \u0101k\u0101santi adhimuccati, sabbo so ku\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101diko padeso \u0101k\u0101so hoti, tena asajjam\u0101no gacchati.",translations:{en:"\u201cHe goes unimpeded through a wall, through an enclosure, through a mountain, as if through empty space\u201d: herein, he is an obtainer of the attainment of the space-kasi\u1e47a. Wishing to go through a wall and so forth, he adverts even to a mere cleft in the wall, fence, or mountain, and resolves, 'Let it be space.' That entire place, wall and all, becomes space, and through it he goes unimpeded.",pt:"\u201cEle passa atrav\xe9s de muros, atrav\xe9s de cercas e atrav\xe9s de montanhas sem qualquer impedimento, exatamente como atrav\xe9s do espa\xe7o vazio\u201d: nisso, ele domina a absor\xe7\xe3o do kasi\u1e47a do espa\xe7o. Querendo atravessar muros e obst\xe1culos semelhantes, ele contempla at\xe9 mesmo uma fresta no muro ou na montanha e determina firmemente: 'que seja espa\xe7o'. Toda aquela estrutura s\xf3lida se converte em espa\xe7o aberto, e atrav\xe9s dela ele passa sem nenhuma resist\xeancia f\xedsica.",es:"\u201cPasa a trav\xe9s de un muro, a trav\xe9s de una muralla o a trav\xe9s de una monta\xf1a sin detenerse, como a trav\xe9s del espacio vac\xedo\u201d: en este logro, el monje posee el dominio del kasi\u1e47a del espacio. Queriendo atravesar un muro u obst\xe1culo, contempla incluso una peque\xf1a hendidura en la pared o monte y determina con resoluci\xf3n: '\xa1que sea espacio!'. Todo ese sitio s\xf3lido se transforma en espacio libre, y pasa a trav\xe9s de \xe9l sin ning\xfan obst\xe1culo."}},{id:"vism-12.12",pali:"Pathaviy\u0101pi ummujjanimujjanti ettha ummujjanti u\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 vuccati, nimujjanti paveso. \u0100pokasi\u1e47asam\u0101pattiy\u0101 l\u0101bh\u012b hoti. So pathavi\u1e43 \u0101vajjati. \u0100vajjitv\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47ena adhimuccati \u2018\u2018udaka\u1e43 hot\u016b\u2019\u2019ti, udaka\u1e43 hoti. So tasmi\u1e43 ummujjanimujja\u1e43 karoti seyyath\u0101pi udake.",translations:{en:"Regarding \u201cemerging from and diving into the earth\u201d: here \u201cemerging\u201d means rising up, and \u201cdiving\u201d means entering. He is an obtainer of the attainment of the water-kasi\u1e47a. He adverts to the earth. Having adverted, he resolves with knowledge: 'Let it be water.' It becomes water. He dives in and out of it just as in water.",pt:"Quanto a \u201cmergulhar e emergir da terra firme\u201d: aqui \u201cemergir\u201d significa subir e \u201cmergulhar\u201d significa submergir. O meditador domina a realiza\xe7\xe3o do kasi\u1e47a da \xe1gua. Ele orienta sua aten\xe7\xe3o para a terra firme. Tendo orientado a mente, determina resolutamente pelo conhecimento: 'que seja \xe1gua'; e a terra se torna \xe1gua fluida. Ele mergulha e emerge dela como se estivesse na \xe1gua.",es:"En cuanto a \u201cemerger y sumergirse en la tierra\u201d: aqu\xed \u201cemerger\u201d significa salir a la superficie y \u201csumergirse\u201d significa penetrar. El meditador posee el dominio de la absorci\xf3n del kasi\u1e47a del agua. Orienta su mente hacia la tierra. Habiendo orientado la mente, resuelve con conocimiento: '\xa1que sea agua!', y la tierra se vuelve agua. \xc9l emerge y se zambulle en ella tal como en el agua."}},{id:"vism-12.13",pali:"Udakepi abhijjam\u0101ne gacchati seyyath\u0101pi pathaviy\u0101ti pakatiy\u0101 pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47asam\u0101pattiy\u0101 l\u0101bh\u012b hoti. So udaka\u1e43 \u0101vajjati. \u0100vajjitv\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47ena adhimuccati \u2018\u2018pathav\u012b hot\u016b\u2019\u2019ti, udakampi pathav\u012b hoti. So tasmi\u1e43 abhijjam\u0101ne udake gacchati seyyath\u0101pi pathaviy\u0101.",translations:{en:"\u201cHe walks upon water without sinking, just as on dry land\u201d: he is by nature an obtainer of the attainment of the earth-kasi\u1e47a. He adverts to the water. Having adverted, he resolves with knowledge: 'Let it be earth.' Even water becomes firm earth. He walks upon that unbroken water just as on dry land.",pt:"\u201cEle caminha sobre as \xe1guas sem afundar, exatamente como em terra firme\u201d: ele domina naturalmente a realiza\xe7\xe3o do kasi\u1e47a da terra. Ele orienta sua mente para a \xe1gua. Tendo orientado a mente, determina pelo conhecimento: 'que seja terra firme'; e a \xe1gua se torna terra s\xf3lida. Ele caminha sobre a superf\xedcie ininterrupta da \xe1gua como se caminhasse em terra firme.",es:"\u201cCamina sobre el agua sin hundirse, exactamente igual que sobre la tierra firme\u201d: posee el dominio de la absorci\xf3n del kasi\u1e47a de la tierra. Orienta su mente hacia las aguas. Habi\xe9ndola orientado, resuelve mediante su conocimiento: '\xa1que sea tierra firme!', y el agua se convierte en suelo firme. \xc9l camina sobre esa agua sin romper su superficie como si caminara en tierra firme."}},{id:"vism-12.14",pali:"\u0100k\u0101sepi palla\u1e45kena kamati, seyyath\u0101pi pakkh\u012b saku\u1e47oti. Pakatiy\u0101 pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47asam\u0101pattiy\u0101 l\u0101bh\u012b hoti. So \u0101k\u0101se pathavibh\u0101va\u1e43 adhimuccitv\u0101 tattha ca\u1e45kamati ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhati nis\u012bdati nipajjati, seyyath\u0101pi pakkh\u012b saku\u1e47o \u0101k\u0101se carati.",translations:{en:"\u201cIn the sky, he travels cross-legged, just as a bird with wings.\u201d He is by nature an obtainer of the attainment of the earth-kasi\u1e47a. Having resolved on the nature of earth in the sky, he walks there, stands, sits, and lies down, just as a winged bird flies through the sky.",pt:"\u201cNo espa\xe7o do c\xe9u, ele viaja de pernas cruzadas, exatamente como uma ave com asas.\u201d Ele possui naturalmente o dom\xednio da realiza\xe7\xe3o do kasi\u1e47a da terra. Tendo determinado a solidez da terra no ar do c\xe9u, ele caminha, fica de p\xe9, senta-se e deita-se ali, do mesmo modo que um p\xe1ssaro alado se desloca no ar.",es:"\u201cEn el espacio del cielo, viaja con las piernas cruzadas, exactamente igual que un ave con alas\u201d. Domina por naturaleza el logro del kasi\u1e47a de la tierra. Habiendo resuelto la naturaleza s\xf3lida de la tierra en el aire del cielo, camina, permanece de pie, se sienta y se recuesta all\xed, del mismo modo que un ave alada vuela por el espacio."}},{id:"vism-12.15",pali:"Imepi candimas\u016briye eva\u1e43mahiddhike eva\u1e43mah\u0101nubh\u0101ve p\u0101\u1e47in\u0101 par\u0101masati parimajjat\u012bti so iddhim\u0101 cetovasippatto candimas\u016briye \u0101vajjati. \u0100vajjitv\u0101 attano santike katv\u0101 adhimuccitv\u0101 nisinnakova v\u0101 nipannakova v\u0101 hattha\u1e43 pas\u0101retv\u0101 t\u0101la\u1e6d\u1e6dhik\u0101 viya dh\u0101vati p\u0101\u1e47in\u0101 parimasati parimajjati.",translations:{en:"\u201cEven these moon and sun, so powerful and mighty, he touches and strokes with his hand\u201d: that possessor of psychic power who has attained mastery of mind adverts to the moon and sun. Having adverted, resolving to make them near to himself, whether sitting or lying down, he stretches out his hand and touches and strokes them as if touching a palm kernel.",pt:"\u201cMesmo o sol e a lua, de t\xe3o imenso poder e majestade, ele toca e acaricia com a pr\xf3pria m\xe3o\u201d: aquele mestre de poderes espirituais que alcan\xe7ou o completo dom\xednio sobre a mente orienta sua aten\xe7\xe3o para a lua e o sol. Tendo orientado a mente, determina resolutamente traz\xea-los para perto de si; e permanecendo sentado ou recostado, estende a m\xe3o e os toca e afaga como se tocasse uma semente redonda de palmeira.",es:"\u201cIncluso a la luna y al sol, dotados de tan inmenso poder y majestad, los toca y acaricia con su mano\u201d: aquel que posee los poderes ps\xedquicos y ha logrado la maestr\xeda mental orienta su mente hacia la luna y el sol. Habi\xe9ndola orientado, resuelve hacerlos cercanos a s\xed mismo; y permaneciendo sentado o recostado, extiende su mano y los toca y acaricia como quien toca una semilla de palma."}},{id:"vism-12.16",pali:"Y\u0101va brahmalok\u0101pi k\u0101yena vasa\u1e43 vattet\u012bti. Sace so iddhim\u0101 cetovasippatto brahmaloka\u1e43 gantuk\u0101mo hoti, d\u016brepi santike adhimuccati \u2018\u2018santike hot\u016b\u2019\u2019ti, santike hoti. Bahukampi thoka\u1e43 adhimuccati, thoka\u1e43 hoti. So a\xf1\xf1atarava\u1e47\u1e47ena v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atarar\u016bpena v\u0101 brahmaloka\u1e43 upasa\u1e45kamitv\u0101 brahm\u0101na\u1e43 saddhi\u1e43 s\u0101kaccha\u1e43 samp\u0101deti.",translations:{en:"\u201cAs for the saying, \u2018He wields mastery with the body even up to the world of Brahm\u0101\u2019: If that possessor of psychic power who has achieved mastery over the mind wishes to go to the Brahm\u0101 world, he resolves the distant into the near, thinking, \u2018Let it be near,\u2019 and it becomes near. He resolves the much into little, and it becomes little. Approaching the Brahm\u0101 world with any desired appearance or form, he engages in conversation with the Brahm\u0101s.",pt:"\u201cQuanto ao que foi dito: \u2018Ele exerce dom\xednio com o corpo at\xe9 mesmo no mundo de Brahma\u2019: se aquele mestre dotado de poder ps\xedquico que alcan\xe7ou o controle da mente desejar ir ao mundo de Brahma, ele determina que o distante se torne pr\xf3ximo, pensando \u2018que seja pr\xf3ximo\u2019, e se torna pr\xf3ximo. Determina que a imensid\xe3o se torne pequena, e se torna pequena. Aproximando-se do mundo de Brahma com qualquer apar\xeancia ou forma desejada, ele realiza di\xe1logos sublimes com os Grandes Brahmas.\u201d",es:"\u201cEn cuanto a la expresi\xf3n: \u2018Ejerce dominio con su cuerpo incluso hasta el mundo de Brahma\u2019: si aquel maestro que posee poderes ps\xedquicos y ha alcanzado el control mental desea ir al mundo de Brahma, resuelve que lo lejano sea cercano pensando: \u2018\xa1que sea cercano!\u2019, y se vuelve cercano. Resuelve que la inmensidad sea peque\xf1a, y se vuelve peque\xf1a. Acerc\xe1ndose al mundo de Brahma con cualquier apariencia o figura que desee, entabla conversaci\xf3n con los Brahmas.\u201d"}},{id:"vism-12.17",pali:"Id\u0101ni dibbasotadh\u0101tuy\u0101 niddesakkamo anuppatto. Tattha tato par\u0101su ca t\u012bsu abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101su so eva\u1e43 sam\u0101hite citteti\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 (d\u012b. ni. 1.240 \u0101dayo) attho vuttanayeneva veditabbo. Sabbattha pana visesamattameva va\u1e47\u1e47ayiss\u0101ma. Tatra dibb\u0101ya sotadh\u0101tuy\u0101ti ettha dibbasadisatt\u0101 dibb\u0101. Dev\u0101na\u1e43 hi sucaritakammanibbatt\u0101 pittasemharuhir\u0101d\u012bhi apalibuddh\u0101 upakkilesavimuttat\u0101ya d\u016brepi \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 sampa\u1e6dicchanasamatth\u0101 dibbapas\u0101dasotadh\u0101tu hoti. Aya\xf1c\u0101pi imassa bhikkhuno v\u012briyabh\u0101van\u0101balanibbatt\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asotadh\u0101tu t\u0101dis\u0101yev\u0101ti dibbasadisatt\u0101 dibb\u0101. Apica dibbavih\u0101ravasena pa\u1e6diladdhatt\u0101 attan\u0101 ca dibbavih\u0101rasannissitatt\u0101pi dibb\u0101. Savana\u1e6d\u1e6dhena nijj\u012bva\u1e6d\u1e6dhena ca sotadh\u0101tu. Sotadh\u0101tukiccakara\u1e47ena ca sotadh\u0101tu viy\u0101tipi sotadh\u0101tu. T\u0101ya dibb\u0101ya sotadh\u0101tuy\u0101.",translations:{en:"Now the turn for the exposition of the divine ear element has come. In this and in the three direct knowledges that follow, the meaning of the passage beginning 'With his mind thus concentrated...' (D\u012b. Ni. 1.240, etc.) should be understood in the way already stated. We shall, however, comment only on the specific points in each case. Herein, in the phrase 'with the divine ear element': it is 'divine' (dibba) because it is like the divine. For the devas have a sensitive ear element produced by wholesome kamma, which is unimpeded by bile, phlegm, blood, etc., and is capable of receiving even distant objects because it is free from defilements. And this bhikkhu\u2019s knowledge-ear-element, produced by the power of the development of energy, is also of the same kind; hence it is called 'divine' because it is like the divine. Furthermore, it is 'divine' because it is obtained by means of the divine abiding and because it is itself dependent on the divine abiding. It is an 'ear element' (sotadh\u0101tu) in the sense of hearing and in the sense of being non-sentient. And because it performs the function of the ear element, it is like an ear element, thus it is an 'ear element.' With that divine ear element...",pt:"Agora chegou a vez da exposi\xe7\xe3o do elemento do ouvido divino. Nela, e nas tr\xeas intelig\xeancias diretas subsequentes, o significado de passagens como 'com a mente assim concentrada', e assim por diante, deve ser entendido exatamente pelo m\xe9todo j\xe1 explicado. No entanto, em todos os casos, descreveremos apenas as particularidades. Ali, na express\xe3o 'com o elemento do ouvido divino': \xe9 chamado de 'divino' por ser semelhante ao dos devas. Pois o elemento do ouvido sens\xedvel divino dos devas, nascido de a\xe7\xf5es de boa conduta, n\xe3o \xe9 obstru\xeddo por bile, fleuma, sangue, etc., e, por estar livre de imperfei\xe7\xf5es, \xe9 capaz de receber objetos mesmo distantes. E este elemento do ouvido de conhecimento deste monge, nascido da for\xe7a do desenvolvimento do esfor\xe7o, \xe9 exatamente semelhante a ele; por ser semelhante ao dos devas, \xe9 chamado de 'divino'. Al\xe9m disso, \xe9 chamado de 'divino' por ser obtido por meio das moradas divinas e por ele pr\xf3prio se apoiar nas moradas divinas. \xc9 chamado de 'elemento do ouvido' no sentido de ouvir e no sentido de ser sem alma. E \xe9 chamado de 'elemento do ouvido' tamb\xe9m por realizar a fun\xe7\xe3o de um elemento do ouvido. 'Com esse elemento do ouvido divino'.",es:"Ahora ha llegado el turno de la exposici\xf3n del elemento del o\xeddo divino. En este caso y en los tres conocimientos superiores siguientes, el significado de frases como 'con el pensamiento as\xed concentrado' debe entenderse mediante el m\xe9todo ya explicado en la exposici\xf3n de los modos de poder. No obstante, describiremos solo los puntos espec\xedficos en cada caso. En la expresi\xf3n 'mediante el elemento del o\xeddo divino', se llama 'divino' porque es similar al de los devas. El elemento del o\xeddo sensible de los devas, nacido de sus acciones meritorias, no est\xe1 obstruido por la bilis, la flema, la sangre, etc., y por estar libre de impurezas, es capaz de captar objetos incluso lejanos. Este elemento del o\xeddo del conocimiento de este monje, nacido de la fuerza del desarrollo de la energ\xeda, es similar al de ellos; por tanto, es 'divino'. Adem\xe1s, es 'divino' por haber sido obtenido mediante la morada divina (dibbavih\u0101ra) y por depender de ella. Se llama 'elemento del o\xeddo' en el sentido de o\xedr y en el sentido de carecer de un ser (nijj\u012bva). Tambi\xe9n se llama as\xed porque realiza la funci\xf3n de un elemento del o\xeddo. 'Mediante ese elemento del o\xeddo divino'."}},{id:"vism-12.18",pali:"Cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47akath\u0101ya cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101y\u0101ti ettha pariy\u0101t\u012bti pariya\u1e43, paricchindat\u012bti attho. Cetaso pariya\u1e43 cetopariya\u1e43. Cetopariya\xf1ca ta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101ti cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Tadatth\u0101y\u0101ti vutta\u1e43 hoti. Parasatt\u0101nanti att\u0101na\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 sesasatt\u0101na\u1e43. Parapuggal\u0101nanti idampi imin\u0101 ekatthameva. Veneyyavasena pana desan\u0101vil\u0101sena ca bya\xf1janan\u0101natta\u1e43 kata\u1e43. Cetas\u0101 cetoti attano cittena tesa\u1e43 citta\u1e43. Paricca paj\u0101n\u0101t\u012bti paricchinditv\u0101 sar\u0101g\u0101divasena n\u0101nappak\u0101rato j\u0101n\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"In the account of the knowledge of encompassing mind (cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), in the phrase 'for the knowledge of encompassing mind' (cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ya), 'pariya' is from 'pariy\u0101ti' (he encompasses), and means 'he delimits.' 'Cetaso pariya\u1e43' is 'cetopariya\u1e43' (the encompassing of mind). And that which is both an encompassing of mind and a knowledge is 'knowledge of encompassing mind' (cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43). 'For that purpose' is the meaning. By 'other beings' (parasatt\u0101na\u1e43) is meant beings other than oneself. By 'other individuals' (parapuggal\u0101na\u1e43) is meant the same thing. However, the difference in expression is made according to the suitability for the audience and the elegance of the teaching. By 'mind with mind' (cetas\u0101 ceto) is meant 'their mind with one's own mind'. By 'he discerns by encompassing' (paricca paj\u0101n\u0101ti) is meant 'he knows by delimiting it in various ways, such as with or without passion'.",pt:"Na exposi\xe7\xe3o sobre o conhecimento da penetra\xe7\xe3o nos cora\xe7\xf5es alheios, em rela\xe7\xe3o ao termo \u201ccetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ya\u201d: \u201cpariya\u201d significa aquilo que delimita ou conhece delimitando (paricchindati). \u201cCetaso pariya\u1e43\u201d \xe9 a delimita\xe7\xe3o da mente alheia. Aquilo que \xe9 tanto a delimita\xe7\xe3o da mente quanto o conhecimento \xe9 o \u201ccetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u201d (conhecimento da penetra\xe7\xe3o nos cora\xe7\xf5es alheios). \u201cTadatth\u0101ya\u201d significa para o benef\xedcio desse conhecimento. \u201cParasatt\u0101na\u1e43\u201d significa de outros seres, excluindo a si mesmo. \u201cParapuggal\u0101nanti\u201d (de outros indiv\xedduos) tem o mesmo significado que o termo anterior. No entanto, a varia\xe7\xe3o de termos \xe9 feita para se adequar \xe0queles que devem ser guiados (veneyya) e pela eleg\xe2ncia da instru\xe7\xe3o (desan\u0101vil\u0101sa). \u201cCetas\u0101 ceto\u201d significa com a pr\xf3pria mente, a mente deles. \u201cParicca paj\u0101n\u0101ti\u201d significa que, tendo delimitado, ele conhece de v\xe1rias maneiras, de acordo com a presen\xe7a de cobi\xe7a (sar\u0101ga), etc.",es:"En la explicaci\xf3n del conocimiento de la penetraci\xf3n en las mentes ajenas, el t\xe9rmino \xabcetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ya\xbb se analiza as\xed: \xabpariya\xbb significa que delimita o conoce exhaustivamente; este es el significado. \xabCetopariya\xbb es la delimitaci\xf3n de la mente ajena. Aquello que es tanto una delimitaci\xf3n de la mente como un conocimiento se denomina \xabcetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xbb (conocimiento de la penetraci\xf3n en las mentes ajenas). Se dice \xabpara su prop\xf3sito\xbb (tadatth\u0101ya). Con \xabparasatt\u0101na\u1e43\xbb (de otros seres) se refiere a todos los dem\xe1s seres excepto a uno mismo. \xabParapuggal\u0101na\u1e43\xbb (de otros individuos) tiene el mismo significado que el t\xe9rmino anterior. La diferencia en la terminolog\xeda se debe a la disposici\xf3n de los seres que han de ser guiados (veneyya) o a la elegancia de la ense\xf1anza (desan\u0101vil\u0101sa). \xabCetas\u0101 ceto\xbb significa conocer la mente de otros mediante la propia mente. \xabParicca paj\u0101n\u0101ti\xbb significa que conoce de diversas maneras tras haber delimitado el estado mental como \xabcon apego\xbb, etc."}}]},430,[]);
__d(function(e,a,o,s,i,t,n){i.exports=[{id:"vism-13.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni dibbasotadh\u0101tuy\u0101 niddesakkamo anuppatto. Tattha tato par\u0101su ca t\u012bsu abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101su so eva\u1e43 sam\u0101hite citteti\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 (d\u012b. ni. 1.240 \u0101dayo) attho vuttanayeneva veditabbo. Sabbattha pana visesamattameva va\u1e47\u1e47ayiss\u0101ma. Tatra dibb\u0101ya sotadh\u0101tuy\u0101ti ettha dibbasadisatt\u0101 dibb\u0101. Dev\u0101na\u1e43 hi sucaritakammanibbatt\u0101 pittasemharuhir\u0101d\u012bhi apalibuddh\u0101 upakkilesavimuttat\u0101ya d\u016brepi \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 sampa\u1e6dicchanasamatth\u0101 dibbapas\u0101dasotadh\u0101tu hoti. Aya\xf1c\u0101pi imassa bhikkhuno v\u012briyabh\u0101van\u0101balanibbatt\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asotadh\u0101tu t\u0101dis\u0101yev\u0101ti dibbasadisatt\u0101 dibb\u0101. Apica dibbavih\u0101ravasena pa\u1e6diladdhatt\u0101 attan\u0101 ca dibbavih\u0101rasannissitatt\u0101pi dibb\u0101. Savana\u1e6d\u1e6dhena nijj\u012bva\u1e6d\u1e6dhena ca sotadh\u0101tu. Sotadh\u0101tukiccakara\u1e47ena ca sotadh\u0101tu viy\u0101tipi sotadh\u0101tu. T\u0101ya dibb\u0101ya sotadh\u0101tuy\u0101.",translations:{en:"Now the turn for the exposition of the divine ear element has come. In this and in the three direct knowledges that follow, the meaning of the passage beginning 'With his mind thus concentrated...' (D\u012b. Ni. 1.240, etc.) should be understood in the way already stated. We shall, however, comment only on the specific points in each case. Herein, in the phrase 'with the divine ear element': it is 'divine' (dibba) because it is like the divine. For the devas have a sensitive ear element produced by wholesome kamma, which is unimpeded by bile, phlegm, blood, etc., and is capable of receiving even distant objects because it is free from defilements. And this bhikkhu\u2019s knowledge-ear-element, produced by the power of the development of energy, is also of the same kind; hence it is called 'divine' because it is like the divine. Furthermore, it is 'divine' because it is obtained by means of the divine abiding and because it is itself dependent on the divine abiding. It is an 'ear element' (sotadh\u0101tu) in the sense of hearing and in the sense of being non-sentient. And because it performs the function of the ear element, it is like an ear element, thus it is an 'ear element.' With that divine ear element...",pt:"Agora chegou a vez da exposi\xe7\xe3o do elemento do ouvido divino. Nela, e nas tr\xeas intelig\xeancias diretas subsequentes, o significado de passagens como 'com a mente assim concentrada', e assim por diante, deve ser entendido exatamente pelo m\xe9todo j\xe1 explicado. No entanto, em todos os casos, descreveremos apenas as particularidades. Ali, na express\xe3o 'com o elemento do ouvido divino': \xe9 chamado de 'divino' por ser semelhante ao dos devas. Pois o elemento do ouvido sens\xedvel divino dos devas, nascido de a\xe7\xf5es de boa conduta, n\xe3o \xe9 obstru\xeddo por bile, fleuma, sangue, etc., e, por estar livre de imperfei\xe7\xf5es, \xe9 capaz de receber objetos mesmo distantes. E este elemento do ouvido de conhecimento deste monge, nascido da for\xe7a do desenvolvimento do esfor\xe7o, \xe9 exatamente semelhante a ele; por ser semelhante ao dos devas, \xe9 chamado de 'divino'. Al\xe9m disso, \xe9 chamado de 'divino' por ser obtido por meio das moradas divinas e por ele pr\xf3prio se apoiar nas moradas divinas. \xc9 chamado de 'elemento do ouvido' no sentido de ouvir e no sentido de ser sem alma. E \xe9 chamado de 'elemento do ouvido' tamb\xe9m por realizar a fun\xe7\xe3o de um elemento do ouvido. 'Com esse elemento do ouvido divino'.",es:"Ahora ha llegado el turno de la exposici\xf3n del elemento del o\xeddo divino. En este caso y en los tres conocimientos superiores siguientes, el significado de frases como 'con el pensamiento as\xed concentrado' debe entenderse mediante el m\xe9todo ya explicado en la exposici\xf3n de los modos de poder. No obstante, describiremos solo los puntos espec\xedficos en cada caso. En la expresi\xf3n 'mediante el elemento del o\xeddo divino', se llama 'divino' porque es similar al de los devas. El elemento del o\xeddo sensible de los devas, nacido de sus acciones meritorias, no est\xe1 obstruido por la bilis, la flema, la sangre, etc., y por estar libre de impurezas, es capaz de captar objetos incluso lejanos. Este elemento del o\xeddo del conocimiento de este monje, nacido de la fuerza del desarrollo de la energ\xeda, es similar al de ellos; por tanto, es 'divino'. Adem\xe1s, es 'divino' por haber sido obtenido mediante la morada divina (dibbavih\u0101ra) y por depender de ella. Se llama 'elemento del o\xeddo' en el sentido de o\xedr y en el sentido de carecer de un ser (nijj\u012bva). Tambi\xe9n se llama as\xed porque realiza la funci\xf3n de un elemento del o\xeddo. 'Mediante ese elemento del o\xeddo divino'."}},{id:"vism-13.2",pali:"Katha\u1e43 pan\u0101ya\u1e43 upp\u0101detabb\u0101ti? Tena bhikkhun\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101p\u0101dakajjh\u0101na\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjitv\u0101 tato vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya saddanimitta\u1e43 manasik\u0101tabba\u1e43. Upac\u0101rajjh\u0101nagocara\u1e43 katv\u0101 \u0101sanno v\u0101 d\u016bro v\u0101 mahanto v\u0101 a\u1e47uko v\u0101 yobbo saddo ta\u1e43 manasikaroti, tasm\u0101 sadd\u0101 nimitta\u1e43 gahetv\u0101 puna abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101p\u0101dakajjh\u0101na\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjitv\u0101 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya \u2018\u2018aya\u1e43 saddo kuto \u0101gacchati, ki\u1e43 v\u0101 bhanat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti \u0101vajjitabba\u1e43. Tasseva\u1e43 \u0101vajjayato dibbasotadh\u0101tu uppajjati.",translations:{en:"But how is this to be produced? That bhikkhu, having attained the jh\u0101na that serves as the basis for the direct knowledges and having emerged from it, should attend to the sign of sound. Having made it the object of access concentration, he attends to whatever sound is heard, whether near or far, loud or subtle; taking the sound as the sign, he should again enter the basic jh\u0101na, emerge from it, and advert: 'From where does this sound come? What is being spoken?' As he adverts in this way, the divine ear element arises.",pt:"Mas como isso deve ser gerado? Aquele monge, tendo alcan\xe7ado o jh\u0101na que serve de fundamento para os conhecimentos diretos e tendo emergido dele, deve prestar aten\xe7\xe3o ao sinal do som. Fazendo disso o objeto do est\xe1gio de acesso, ele direciona sua aten\xe7\xe3o a qualquer som que se fa\xe7a ouvir, seja pr\xf3ximo ou distante, alto ou sutil; tomando esse som como objeto e entrando novamente no jh\u0101na de base, ele deve emergir e refletir: 'De onde vem este som? O que est\xe1 sendo dito?'. Conforme ele reflete dessa forma, surge nele o elemento do ouvido divino.",es:"\xbfC\xf3mo debe suscitarse este conocimiento? El monje, tras entrar en la absorci\xf3n que sirve de base para los conocimientos directos y haber emergido de ella, debe prestar atenci\xf3n al signo del sonido. Tom\xe1ndolo como objeto del estado de acceso, presta atenci\xf3n a cualquier sonido perceptible, ya sea cercano o lejano, intenso o sutil; tomando ese sonido como se\xf1al, debe ingresar de nuevo en la absorci\xf3n b\xe1sica, emerger de ella y advertir: '\xbfDe d\xf3nde proviene este sonido? \xbfQu\xe9 se est\xe1 diciendo?'. Conforme reflexiona de este modo, surge en \xe9l el elemento del o\xeddo divino."}},{id:"vism-13.3",pali:"Cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47akath\u0101ya cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101y\u0101ti ettha pariy\u0101t\u012bti pariya\u1e43, paricchindat\u012bti attho. Cetaso pariya\u1e43 cetopariya\u1e43. Cetopariya\xf1ca ta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101ti cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Tadatth\u0101y\u0101ti vutta\u1e43 hoti. Parasatt\u0101nanti att\u0101na\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 sesasatt\u0101na\u1e43. Parapuggal\u0101nanti idampi imin\u0101 ekatthameva. Veneyyavasena pana desan\u0101vil\u0101sena ca bya\xf1janan\u0101natta\u1e43 kata\u1e43. Cetas\u0101 cetoti attano cittena tesa\u1e43 citta\u1e43. Paricca paj\u0101n\u0101t\u012bti paricchinditv\u0101 sar\u0101g\u0101divasena n\u0101nappak\u0101rato j\u0101n\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"In the account of the knowledge of encompassing mind (cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), in the phrase 'for the knowledge of encompassing mind' (cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ya), 'pariya' is from 'pariy\u0101ti' (he encompasses), and means 'he delimits.' 'Cetaso pariya\u1e43' is 'cetopariya\u1e43' (the encompassing of mind). And that which is both an encompassing of mind and a knowledge is 'knowledge of encompassing mind' (cetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43). 'For that purpose' is the meaning. By 'other beings' (parasatt\u0101na\u1e43) is meant beings other than oneself. By 'other individuals' (parapuggal\u0101na\u1e43) is meant the same thing. However, the difference in expression is made according to the suitability for the audience and the elegance of the teaching. By 'mind with mind' (cetas\u0101 ceto) is meant 'their mind with one's own mind'. By 'he discerns by encompassing' (paricca paj\u0101n\u0101ti) is meant 'he knows by delimiting it in various ways, such as with or without passion'.",pt:"Na exposi\xe7\xe3o sobre o conhecimento da penetra\xe7\xe3o nos cora\xe7\xf5es alheios, em rela\xe7\xe3o ao termo \u201ccetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ya\u201d: \u201cpariya\u201d significa aquilo que delimita ou conhece delimitando (paricchindati). \u201cCetaso pariya\u1e43\u201d \xe9 a delimita\xe7\xe3o da mente alheia. Aquilo que \xe9 tanto a delimita\xe7\xe3o da mente quanto o conhecimento \xe9 o \u201ccetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u201d (conhecimento da penetra\xe7\xe3o nos cora\xe7\xf5es alheios). \u201cTadatth\u0101ya\u201d significa para o benef\xedcio desse conhecimento. \u201cParasatt\u0101na\u1e43\u201d significa de outros seres, excluindo a si mesmo. \u201cParapuggal\u0101nanti\u201d (de outros indiv\xedduos) tem o mesmo significado que o termo anterior. No entanto, a varia\xe7\xe3o de termos \xe9 feita para se adequar \xe0queles que devem ser guiados (veneyya) e pela eleg\xe2ncia da instru\xe7\xe3o (desan\u0101vil\u0101sa). \u201cCetas\u0101 ceto\u201d significa com a pr\xf3pria mente, a mente deles. \u201cParicca paj\u0101n\u0101ti\u201d significa que, tendo delimitado, ele conhece de v\xe1rias maneiras, de acordo com a presen\xe7a de cobi\xe7a (sar\u0101ga), etc.",es:"En la explicaci\xf3n del conocimiento de la penetraci\xf3n en las mentes ajenas, el t\xe9rmino \xabcetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ya\xbb se analiza as\xed: \xabpariya\xbb significa que delimita o conoce exhaustivamente; este es el significado. \xabCetopariya\xbb es la delimitaci\xf3n de la mente ajena. Aquello que es tanto una delimitaci\xf3n de la mente como un conocimiento se denomina \xabcetopariya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xbb (conocimiento de la penetraci\xf3n en las mentes ajenas). Se dice \xabpara su prop\xf3sito\xbb (tadatth\u0101ya). Con \xabparasatt\u0101na\u1e43\xbb (de otros seres) se refiere a todos los dem\xe1s seres excepto a uno mismo. \xabParapuggal\u0101na\u1e43\xbb (de otros individuos) tiene el mismo significado que el t\xe9rmino anterior. La diferencia en la terminolog\xeda se debe a la disposici\xf3n de los seres que han de ser guiados (veneyya) o a la elegancia de la ense\xf1anza (desan\u0101vil\u0101sa). \xabCetas\u0101 ceto\xbb significa conocer la mente de otros mediante la propia mente. \xabParicca paj\u0101n\u0101ti\xbb significa que conoce de diversas maneras tras haber delimitado el estado mental como \xabcon apego\xbb, etc."}},{id:"vism-13.4",pali:"Katha\u1e43 paneta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 upp\u0101detabbanti? Eta\xf1hi dibbacakkhuvasena ijjhati, ta\u1e43 niss\u0101ya pavattati. Tasm\u0101 dibbacakkhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena parassa va\u1e47\u1e47adh\u0101tuparivattana\u1e43 sallakkhetv\u0101 tadanus\u0101rena citta\u1e43 j\u0101n\u0101ti. Somanassupp\u0101dak\u0101ramma\u1e47e hi pas\u0101dar\u016bpa\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhak\u0101le va\u1e47\u1e47adh\u0101tu virocati, domanassupp\u0101dak\u0101ramma\u1e47e di\u1e6d\u1e6dhak\u0101le kalamburoti. Eva\u1e43 hadayavatthu\xf1\xf1ut\u0101ya r\u016bpassa parivattana\u1e43 disv\u0101 parassa citta\u1e43 sar\u0101ga\u1e43 v\u0101 v\u012btar\u0101ga\u1e43 v\u0101ti paj\u0101n\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"But how is this knowledge to be produced? Indeed, this is achieved by means of the divine eye; it operates dependent upon that. Therefore, having observed the alteration of the color of physical elements in another by means of the knowledge of the divine eye, he knows the mind in accordance with that. For when an object that arouses joy is seen, the color of the physical elements glows bright; when an object that arouses displeasure is seen, it dims. Having seen the alteration of form through understanding the heart-base in this way, he discerns another's mind as with passion or without passion.",pt:"Mas como esse conhecimento deve ser produzido? De fato, ele se realiza por meio do olho divino; opera com base nele. Portanto, tendo observado a altera\xe7\xe3o na cor dos elementos f\xedsicos em outra pessoa atrav\xe9s do conhecimento do olho divino, ele conhece a mente dela em conformidade com isso. Pois, quando se percebe um objeto que desperta alegria, a cor dos elementos corporais resplandece luminosa; quando se v\xea um objeto que desperta pesar, ela se torna sombria. Tendo discernido a mudan\xe7a no corpo atrav\xe9s do conhecimento da base do cora\xe7\xe3o desse modo, ele reconhece se a mente alheia est\xe1 tomada de paix\xe3o ou livre de paix\xe3o.",es:"\xbfC\xf3mo se produce este conocimiento? En verdad, esto se logra mediante el ojo divino; opera apoy\xe1ndose en \xe9l. Por lo tanto, habiendo observado el cambio en el color de los elementos f\xedsicos en otra persona mediante el conocimiento del ojo divino, conoce su mente en conformidad con ello. Pues cuando se percibe un objeto que despierta alegr\xeda, el color de los elementos corporais brilla con claridad; cuando se percibe un objeto que suscita disgusto, se opaca. Habiendo observado la alteraci\xf3n de la forma mediante la comprensi\xf3n de la base del coraz\xf3n de este modo, discierne si la mente ajena est\xe1 con pasi\xf3n o libre de pasi\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-13.5",pali:"Pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati\xf1\u0101\u1e47akath\u0101ya\u1e43 pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101y\u0101ti (d\u012b. ni. 1.244) ettha pubbe nivasit\u0101ti pubbeniv\u0101so. At\u012btasu j\u0101t\u012bsu khandhasant\u0101nassa nibbattaniv\u0101so. Pubbeniv\u0101sassa anussara\u1e47a\u1e43 pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati. S\u0101 ca ta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101ti pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Tadatth\u0101y\u0101ti vutta\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"In the exposition of the knowledge of recollection of past lives, regarding the phrase 'for the knowledge of recollection of past lives' (D\u012b. Ni. 1.244): Herein, 'pubbeniv\u0101sa' means that which was lived in previously; that is, the abodes where the continuum of aggregates arose in past births. The recollection of that past abode is 'pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati' (recollection of past lives). And that which is both such recollection and knowledge is 'pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati\xf1\u0101\u1e47a' (knowledge of recollection of past lives). 'For the purpose of that' is what is stated.",pt:"Na exposi\xe7\xe3o do conhecimento da rememora\xe7\xe3o de vidas passadas, quanto \xe0 express\xe3o 'para o conhecimento da rememora\xe7\xe3o de vidas passadas': 'pubbeniv\u0101sa' refere-se \xe0quilo que foi vivido anteriormente; isto \xe9, as moradas onde o fluxo cont\xednuo dos agregados surgiu nas vidas passadas. A recorda\xe7\xe3o dessas moradas anteriores \xe9 'pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati'. E aquilo que \xe9 tanto a recorda\xe7\xe3o quanto o conhecimento \xe9 'pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati\xf1\u0101\u1e47a'. 'Com o prop\xf3sito de realizar esse conhecimento' \xe9 o que foi dito.",es:"En la explicaci\xf3n del conocimiento del recuerdo de las vidas pasadas, respecto a la frase 'para el conocimiento del recuerdo de las vidas pasadas': 'pubbeniv\u0101sa' significa aquello que fue vivido previamente; es decir, las moradas donde surgi\xf3 la continuidad de los agregados en los renacimientos pasados. El recuerdo de esa morada previa es 'pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati'. Y aquello que es tanto ese recuerdo como un conocimiento es 'pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati\xf1\u0101\u1e47a'. 'Con el prop\xf3sito de lograrlo' es lo que se declara."}},{id:"vism-13.6",pali:"Anekavihitanti anekavidha\u1e43, anekehi v\u0101 pak\u0101rehi pavattita\u1e43, sa\u1e43va\u1e47\u1e47ita\u1e43 v\u0101. Pubbeniv\u0101santi purimenayena vuttappak\u0101ra\u1e43 pubbeniv\u0101sa\u1e43. Anussarat\u012bti anugantv\u0101 anugantv\u0101 sarati, anupubbena v\u0101 sarati. Ekamp\u012bti\u0101din\u0101 panassa anussara\u1e47appak\u0101ro dassito. Tattha ekamp\u012bti eko eva ga\u1e47anavasena, anek\u0101mapi ekatt\u0101pekkh\u0101ya.",translations:{en:"'Many kinds' means manifold, or occurring in many aspects, or fully described. 'Past abodes' means past abodes in the manner already explained. 'He recollects' means that he remembers by continually following after, or remembers in regular succession. By the passage beginning with 'Even one [birth],' the manner of his recollecting is shown. Therein, 'even one' is just one by way of counting, or many by reference to unity.",pt:"'M\xfaltiplos modos' significa variado, ou que ocorre sob m\xfaltiplos aspectos, ou detalhadamente descrito. 'Vidas anteriores' refere-se \xe0s vidas pregressas pelo m\xe9todo j\xe1 mencionado. 'Rememora' significa que se lembra seguindo continuamente o rastro, ou que se lembra em ordem sucessiva. Pela passagem que come\xe7a com 'mesmo um [renascimento]', mostra-se o modo de sua rememora\xe7\xe3o. Nisso, 'mesmo um' refere-se a um \xfanico renascimento por contagem direta, ou a muitos no sentido de uma unidade.",es:"'M\xfaltiples clases' significa variado, o que se manifiesta bajo diversos aspectos, o que est\xe1 descrito extensamente. 'Moradas pasadas' se refiere a las vidas anteriores en el modo antes expuesto. 'Recuerda' significa que rememora siguiendo una y otra vez la huella, o recuerda en debida sucesi\xf3n. Mediante el pasaje que comienza por 'incluso un [nacimiento]', se muestra el modo de su rememoraci\xf3n. En ello, 'incluso un' denota uno solo en cuanto al c\xf3mputo, o muchos respecto a la unidad de conjunto."}},{id:"vism-13.7",pali:"Imesu ca pana pubbeniv\u0101sa\u1e43 anussara\u1e47asattesu titthiy\u0101na\u1e43 pubbeniv\u0101sadassana\u1e43 khandhamatteyeva pavattati, n\u0101magott\u0101diparicchedavasena na pavattati. Pakatis\u0101vak\u0101na\u1e43 pana n\u0101magott\u0101dik\u0101yapi khandhappavattiy\u0101pi anussara\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti, te pana ekasmi\xf1\xf1eva kappe anussaranti, na tato uttari. Mah\u0101s\u0101vak\u0101na\u1e43 as\u012bti mah\u0101kapp\u0101 gocaro. Dvinna\u1e43 aggas\u0101vak\u0101na\u1e43 eka\u1e43 asa\u1e45khyeyya\u1e43 kappasatasahassa\xf1ca. Paccekabuddh\u0101na\u1e43 dve asa\u1e45khyeyy\u0101ni kappasatasahassa\xf1ca. Buddh\u0101na\u1e43 pana paricchedo natthi.",translations:{en:"Among those beings who recollect past lives, the recollection of past lives by sectarian ascetics operates only upon the mere aggregates; it does not operate by way of determining names, clans, and so forth. But the recollection of ordinary disciples occurs regarding both the occurrence of aggregates and by way of names, clans, and so forth; yet they recollect only within a single eon, not beyond that. The range of the great disciples is eighty great eons. For the two chief disciples, it is one incalculable period and one hundred thousand eons. For paccekabuddhas, it is two incalculable periods and one hundred thousand eons. But for the Buddhas, there is no limit.",pt:"Entre os que relembram vidas passadas, a vis\xe3o dos ascetas de outras tradi\xe7\xf5es opera apenas sobre os meros agregados corporais e mentais, n\xe3o discernindo linhagens de nomes e cl\xe3s. Os disc\xedpulos comuns conseguem recordar tanto a sucess\xe3o dos agregados quanto os nomes e cl\xe3s, mas relembram apenas no \xe2mbito de um \xfanico grande ciclo c\xf3smico (kappa), n\xe3o al\xe9m disso. O alcance dos grandes disc\xedpulos abrange oitenta grandes kappas. O dos dois principais disc\xedpulos alcan\xe7a um per\xedodo incalcul\xe1vel e cem mil ciclos. O dos Paccekabuddhas alcan\xe7a dois per\xedodos incalcul\xe1veis e cem mil ciclos. J\xe1 para os Supremos Budas, n\xe3o existe limite algum.",es:"Entre los seres que recuerdan vidas pasadas, la visi\xf3n de los ascetas de otras escuelas act\xfaa \xfanicamente sobre los meros agregados, sin discernir nombres ni linajes familiares. Los disc\xedpulos comunes pueden recordar tanto la continuidad de los agregados como los nombres y familias, pero recuerdan \xfanicamente dentro de un solo e\xf3n, no m\xe1s all\xe1. El \xe1mbito de los grandes disc\xedpulos abarca ochenta grandes eones. El de los dos disc\xedpulos principales abarca un per\xedodo incalculable y cien mil eones. El de los Paccekabuddhas abarca dos per\xedodos incalculables y cien mil eones. Pero para los Supremos Budas, no existe l\xedmite alguno."}},{id:"vism-13.8",pali:"Tasm\u0101 evamanussarituk\u0101mena \u0101dikammikena bhikkhun\u0101 pacch\u0101bhatta\u1e43 pi\u1e47\u1e0dap\u0101tapa\u1e6dikkantena vivitte padese pa\u1e6disall\u012bnena catutthajjh\u0101na\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjitv\u0101 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya pacchimanisajjato pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya y\u0101va pa\u1e6disandhito ta\u1e43 ta\u1e43 kiriy\u0101pariccheda\u1e43 anulomena v\u0101 pa\u1e6dilomena v\u0101 anussaritabba\u1e43. Tato cutikkha\u1e47e pavattakamma\xf1ca ta\u1e43samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 ca khandh\u0101 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 anantarabh\u0101ve pavattakhandh\u0101 anussaritabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Therefore, a beginner monk wishing to recollect in this way, having returned from almsround after the meal, secluded in a quiet place, having entered the fourth jh\u0101na and emerged from it, should recollect each action performed in succession, forward or backward, from his last seated posture all the way back to rebirth-linking. Then, taking as object the kamma that occurred at the moment of death and the aggregates originating therefrom, he should recollect the aggregates that occurred in the immediately preceding existence.",pt:"Portanto, o monge principiante que deseja recordar dessa maneira, ap\xf3s regressar da ronda de esmolas e fazer sua refei\xe7\xe3o, recolhido em um local solit\xe1rio, deve entrar no quarto jh\u0101na e, emergindo dele, recordar cada a\xe7\xe3o realizada em sequ\xeancia, para tr\xe1s ou para frente, desde a sua \xfaltima postura sentada at\xe9 o momento da concep\xe7\xe3o. A seguir, tomando como objeto a a\xe7\xe3o executada no momento do falecimento e os agregados originados desse kamma, deve recordar os agregados que existiam na vida imediatamente anterior.",es:"Por consiguiente, el monje principiante que desee recordar de este modo, tras regresar de la recolecci\xf3n de limosnas despu\xe9s de la comida, retirado en un sitio solitario, debe entrar en el cuarto jh\u0101na y, al salir de \xe9l, rememorar cada acci\xf3n llevada a cabo en debida sucesi\xf3n, en orden directo o inverso, desde su \xfaltima postura sentada hasta el renacimiento mismo. Luego, tomando como objeto la acci\xf3n que operaba en el instante de la muerte y los agregados originados por ella, debe recordar los agregados que exist\xedan en la existencia inmediatamente precedente."}},{id:"vism-13.9",pali:"Eva\u1e43 karonto hi seyyath\u0101pi n\u0101ma balav\u0101 puriso k\u016b\u1e6d\u0101g\u0101raka\u1e47\u1e47ikatth\u0101ya mah\u0101rukkha\u1e43 chinditv\u0101 rukkham\u016blato pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya y\u0101va agga\xf1ca s\u0101kha\xf1ca v\u0101sipara\u015b\u016bhi taccheyya, agge sampatte punadeva m\u016bl\u0101bhimukha\u1e43 gaccheyya, evameva aya\u1e43 bhikkhu attano kiriy\u0101pariccheda\u1e43 anupubbena anulomapa\u1e6dilomato anussaranto pa\u1e6disandhi\xf1ca cuti\xf1ca anussarati.",translations:{en:"Doing so, he is just like a strong man who, having cut down a huge tree for the ridge-pole of a gabled house, planes it with adze and axe from the base to the top and branches, and having reached the top, returns again towards the base. Even so, this monk, recollecting the course of his actions successively, forward and backward, recollects conception and death.",pt:"Ao proceder assim, ele se assemelha a um homem robusto que, tendo derrubado uma grande \xe1rvore para esculpir a viga mestra de um edif\xedcio nobre, desbasta-a com o machado desde a raiz at\xe9 o topo e os galhos e, ao alcan\xe7ar a extremidade superior, retorna trabalhando em dire\xe7\xe3o \xe0 raiz. Exatamente dessa forma, este monge, recordando o desdobramento de seus atos em ordem direta e inversa, recorda a concep\xe7\xe3o e a morte anterior.",es:"Al obrar as\xed, se asemeja a un hombre fuerte que, habiendo talado un gran \xe1rbol para la viga cumbrera de un edificio, lo desbasta con el hacha desde la base hasta la c\xfaspide y las ramas, y tras llegar a la copa, regresa trabajando hacia la ra\xedz. De la misma manera, este monje, al recordar el curso de sus actos en orden directo e inverso, recuerda la concepci\xf3n y la muerte pasada."}},{id:"vism-13.10",pali:"Tattha pacchimanisajjato pabhuti y\u0101va pa\u1e6disandhito \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 pavatta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u0101ma na hoti, parikamma\xf1\u0101\u1e47ameva n\u0101ma hoti. Yato pana cutikhane kammaja\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43 atikkamitv\u0101 anantarabh\u0101ve pa\u1e6disandhikkha\u1e47e pavattan\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti, tato pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u0101ma hoti.",translations:{en:"Therein, the knowledge that occurs having taken as object the period from the last seated posture back to rebirth-linking is not called the knowledge of recollection of past lives; it is called preliminary-work knowledge. But from the moment it transcends the kamma-born form at the time of death and takes as object the mentality-materiality occurring at the moment of rebirth-linking in the immediately preceding existence, from then on it is called the knowledge of recollection of past lives.",pt:"Nesse processo, o conhecimento que opera tendo como objeto os momentos que v\xe3o desde a \xfaltima postura sentada at\xe9 a concep\xe7\xe3o no ventre materno ainda n\xe3o \xe9 chamado de conhecimento de recorda\xe7\xe3o de vidas passadas; \xe9 chamado apenas de conhecimento preparat\xf3rio. Mas a partir do momento em que ultrapassa a mat\xe9ria gerada por kamma na hora da morte e toma como objeto a mente e a mat\xe9ria atuantes no instante da concep\xe7\xe3o da vida imediatamente anterior, a partir da\xed passa a ser chamado legitimamente de conhecimento de recorda\xe7\xe3o de vidas passadas.",es:"En ese proceso, el conocimiento que opera tomando como objeto el lapso que va desde la \xfaltima postura sentada hasta el instante de la concepci\xf3n no se denomina todav\xeda conocimiento del recuerdo de vidas pasadas; se llama \xfanicamente conocimiento preparatorio. Pero a partir del momento en que trasciende la materia nacida de las acciones en el instante de la muerte y toma como objeto el nombre y la forma que surgieron en la concepci\xf3n de la existencia previa, a partir de entonces se llama propiamente conocimiento del recuerdo de vidas pasadas."}},{id:"vism-13.11",pali:"Apica yasm\u0101 amutr\u0101si\u1e43 eva\u1e43n\u0101mo eva\u1e45gotto eva\u1e43va\u1e47\u1e47o evam\u0101h\u0101ro eva\u1e43sukhadukkhapa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b evam\u0101yupariyanto, so tato cuto amutra udap\u0101di\u1e43, tatr\u0101p\u0101si\u1e43 eva\u1e43n\u0101mo eva\u1e45gotto eva\u1e43va\u1e47\u1e47o evam\u0101h\u0101ro eva\u1e43sukhadukkhapa\u1e6disa\u1e43ved\u012b evam\u0101yupariyanto, so tato cuto idh\u016bpapannoti (d\u012b. ni. 1.244) eva\u1e43 s\u0101k\u0101ra\u1e43 sauddesa\u1e43 anekavihita\u1e43 pubbeniv\u0101sa\u1e43 anussarati, tasm\u0101 etena \u0101k\u0101rena anussaritabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Moreover, since it is said: 'There I was, of such name, of such clan, of such complexion, with such food, experiencing such pleasure and pain, with such a lifespan; having passed away from there, I reappeared elsewhere; there too I was, of such name, of such clan, of such complexion, with such food, experiencing such pleasure and pain, with such a lifespan; having passed away from there, I have reappeared here' (D\u012b. Ni. 1.244); in this way he recollects his manifold past abodes with their modes and details; therefore, in this manner should he recollect.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, porque foi ensinado: 'Ali eu estive, com tal nome, de tal linhagem familiar, com tal complei\xe7\xe3o corporal, nutrindo-me de tal alimento, experimentando tais prazeres e tais dores, com tal dura\xe7\xe3o de vida; tendo falecido daquele estado, renasci em outro lugar; ali tamb\xe9m estive, com tal nome, de tal cl\xe3, de tal apar\xeancia, consumindo tal alimento, sentindo tais alegrias e sofrimentos, tendo tal longevidade; e tendo falecido dali, renasci aqui'; dessa forma ele rememora as suas m\xfaltiplas exist\xeancias passadas com todas as suas caracter\xedsticas e particularidades; por conseguinte, \xe9 exatamente sob esses aspectos que ele deve recordar.",es:"Asimismo, puesto que se ense\xf1a: 'All\xed estuve, con tal nombre, de tal linaje, con tal tez, aliment\xe1ndome de tal comida, experimentando tal placer y dolor, y con tal duraci\xf3n de vida; habiendo fallecido de all\xed, renac\xed en otra parte; all\xed tambi\xe9n estuve, con tal nombre, de tal linaje, de tal apariencia, tomando tales alimentos, experimentando tal dicha y aflicci\xf3n, y con tal longevidad; habiendo fallecido de all\xed, he renacido aqu\xed'; de esta manera recuerda sus m\xfaltiples vidas pasadas con todos sus modos y pormenores; por lo tanto, es en conformidad con estos aspectos como debe rememorar."}},{id:"vism-13.12",pali:"Satt\u0101na\u1e43 cut\u016bpap\u0101ta\xf1\u0101\u1e47akath\u0101ya cut\u016bpap\u0101ta\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101y\u0101ti (d\u012b. ni. 1.247) cuti ca upap\u0101to ca cut\u016bpap\u0101to. Cuti\xf1ceva upap\u0101ta\xf1ca j\u0101nana\u1e6d\u1e6dhena cut\u016bpap\u0101ta\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Satt\u0101na\u1e43 cuti\xf1ceva upap\u0101ta\xf1ca j\u0101nana\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101y\u0101ti attho. Dibben\u0101ti dibbasadisena. Dev\u0101na\u1e43 hi pas\u0101dacakkhu r\u016bp\u0101bhigh\u0101t\u0101p\u0101thagat\u0101namiva d\u016brepi tirobh\u0101vagatepi r\u016bpe passati, aya\xf1c\u0101pi imassa bhikkhuno \xf1\u0101\u1e47acakkhu t\u0101dis\u0101yev\u0101ti dibbasadisatt\u0101 dibba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"In the account of the knowledge of the passing away and reappearance of beings, regarding the phrase 'for the knowledge of the passing away and reappearance' (D\u012b. Ni. 1.247): 'Passing away and reappearance' means passing away and reappearing. It is the knowledge of passing away and reappearance in the sense of knowing passing away and reappearance; the meaning is: for the knowledge that knows the passing away and reappearance of beings. 'With the divine [eye]' means: with that which is like the divine. For the sensitive eye of the devas sees forms even though distant or concealed, just as if they had struck the range of sight; and this bhikkhu's eye of knowledge is of that very kind, hence it is called 'divine' because it is like the divine.",pt:"Na exposi\xe7\xe3o do conhecimento da morte e do renascimento dos seres, na express\xe3o 'para o conhecimento da morte e do renascimento': 'cut\u016bpap\u0101to' significa o falecimento e o posterior renascimento. \xc9 o conhecimento da morte e do renascimento no sentido de compreender plenamente o morrer e o renascer; o significado \xe9: para o conhecimento que discerne o falecimento e o reaparecimento dos seres. 'Com o olho divino' significa: com aquele que \xe9 semelhante ao dos devas. Pois o olho luminoso dos devas contempla formas mesmo distantes ou ocultas atr\xe1s de obst\xe1culos como se estivessem imediatamente presentes no seu campo de vis\xe3o; e este olho da sabedoria do monge possui a mesma excel\xeancia l\xedmpida, sendo chamado de 'divino' pela sua semelhan\xe7a com a vis\xe3o dos deuses.",es:"En la explicaci\xf3n del conocimiento del morir y el renacer de los seres, respecto a la frase 'para el conocimiento del morir y el renacer': 'cut\u016bpap\u0101ta' significa la muerte y el renacimiento. Se llama conocimiento del morir y el renacer en el sentido de conocer la muerte y el renacer; el sentido es: para el conocimiento que conoce la muerte y el renacimiento de los seres. 'Mediante el ojo divino' significa: con aquel que es similar al de los dioses. Pues el ojo luminoso de los devas percibe formas lejanas u ocultas tras obst\xe1culos tal como si estuvieran a la vista; y este ojo de sabidur\xeda del monje posee esa misma cualidad, por lo que se llama 'divino' debido a su parecido con el de los dioses."}},{id:"vism-13.13",pali:"Dassana\u1e6d\u1e6dhena cakkhu. Cakkhukiccakara\u1e47ena cakkhumiv\u0101tipi cakkhu. Dibba\xf1ca ta\u1e43 cakkhu\xf1c\u0101ti dibbacakkhu. Tena dibbacakkhun\u0101. Visuddhen\u0101ti pariyod\u0101tena \u0101lokabh\u0101van\u0101nubh\u0101vena tamavinodanena nirupakkilesena. Atikkantam\u0101nusik\u0113n\u0101ti manuss\u0101na\u1e43 cakkhu\u1e43 up\u0101d\u0101ya d\u016bradassan\u0101dit\u0101ya atikkantam\u0101nusika\u1e43.",translations:{en:"It is an 'eye' (cakkhu) in the sense of seeing. And because it performs the function of the eye, it is like an eye, thus it is an 'eye.' And that which is both divine and an eye is the 'divine eye' (dibbacakkhu). With that divine eye. 'Purified' means cleansed, free from defilement by the dispelling of darkness through the power of developing light. 'Surpassing that of humans' means surpassing the human eye by its seeing at a distance and so forth.",pt:"\xc9 chamado de 'olho' no sentido de ver. E por desempenhar a fun\xe7\xe3o do olho, \xe9 semelhante a um olho e por isso \xe9 chamado de 'olho'. Aquilo que \xe9 ao mesmo tempo divino e olho \xe9 o 'olho divino'. 'Com esse olho divino'. 'Purificado' significa l\xedmpido, inteiramente livre de imperfei\xe7\xf5es pela dissipa\xe7\xe3o da escurid\xe3o mediante o poder do cultivo da percep\xe7\xe3o luminosa. 'Que ultrapassa a vis\xe3o humana' significa que supera a vis\xe3o dos homens comuns por enxergar a grandes dist\xe2ncias, atrav\xe9s de obst\xe1culos s\xf3lidos e em todas as dire\xe7\xf5es.",es:"Se llama 'ojo' en el sentido de ver. Y por realizar la funci\xf3n del ojo, es como un ojo, por eso se llama 'ojo'. Aquello que es al mismo tiempo divino y ojo es el 'ojo divino'. 'Mediante ese ojo divino'. 'Purificado' significa limpio, libre de imperfecciones gracias a la disipaci\xf3n de las tinieblas por la fuerza del desarrollo de la luz. 'Que sobrepasa la visi\xf3n humana' significa que supera el ojo humano por su capacidad de ver a gran distancia y en la oscuridad."}},{id:"vism-13.14",pali:"Cavam\u0101ne upapajjam\u0101neti ettha cutikkha\u1e47e upapattikkha\u1e47e v\u0101 dibbacakkhussa visayo na hoti. Cut\u0101bhimukhe pana cavam\u0101neti, upapattiy\u0101 abhimukhe upapajjam\u0101neti vuccati. H\u012bne pa\u1e47\u012bte suva\u1e47\u1e47e dubba\u1e47\u1e47e sugate duggate yath\u0101kammupage satte paj\u0101n\u0101ti. Yath\u0101 hi puriso uparip\u0101s\u0101de \u1e6dhito v\u012bthiy\u0101 carante manusse passati, evameva dibbacakkhun\u0101 satte passati.",translations:{en:"Regarding 'passing away and reappearing': Herein, at the exact moment of death or the moment of rebirth, there is no domain for the divine eye. But those who are facing death are said to be 'passing away,' and those facing rebirth are said to be 'reappearing.' He discerns beings as inferior, superior, beautiful, ugly, fortunate, unfortunate, faring according to their actions. Just as a man standing on the upper terrace of a palace sees people walking in the street, even so he sees beings with the divine eye.",pt:"Quanto a 'morrendo e renascendo': no exato instante da morte ou da concep\xe7\xe3o, n\xe3o h\xe1 campo para a vis\xe3o do olho divino. Mas aqueles que est\xe3o prestes a morrer s\xe3o chamados de 'morrendo', e aqueles prestes a renascer s\xe3o chamados de 'renascendo'. Ele discerne os seres como inferiores ou nobres, belos ou disformes, afortunados ou desafortunados, seguindo de acordo com as suas pr\xf3prias a\xe7\xf5es (kamma). Do mesmo modo que um homem situado no terra\xe7o superior de um pal\xe1cio contempla as pessoas caminhando pelas ruas, assim tamb\xe9m ele contempla os seres pelo olho divino.",es:"En cuanto a 'muriendo y renaciendo': en el instante preciso de la muerte o en el del renacimiento, no opera el \xe1mbito del ojo divino. Pero los que est\xe1n a punto de morir se llaman 'muriendo', y los que est\xe1n a punto de renacer se llaman 'renaciendo'. Discierne a los seres como inferiores, superiores, bellos, feos, afortunados o desdichados, seg\xfan el curso de sus acciones. As\xed como un hombre de pie en la terraza alta de un palacio contempla a las personas que caminan por la calle, de la misma manera contempla a los seres con el ojo divino."}},{id:"vism-13.15",pali:"Eva\u1e43 passituk\u0101mena pana \u0101dikammikena kulaputtena kasi\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101p\u0101dakajjh\u0101na\u1e43 sabb\u0101k\u0101rena abhin\u012bh\u0101rakkhama\u1e43 katv\u0101 \u2018\u2018tejokasi\u1e47a\u1e43, od\u0101takasi\u1e47a\u1e43, \u0101lokakasi\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti imesu t\u012bsu kasi\u1e47esu a\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 \u0101sanna\u1e43 k\u0101tabba\u1e43. Upac\u0101rajjh\u0101nagocara\u1e43 katv\u0101 va\u1e0d\u1e0dhetv\u0101 \u1e6dhapetabba\u1e43. Na tattha appan\u0101 upp\u0101detabb\u0101ti adhipp\u0101yo. Sace hi upp\u0101deti, p\u0101dakajjh\u0101nanissaya\u1e43 hoti, na parikammanissaya\u1e43. Imesu ca pana t\u012bsu \u0101lokakasi\u1e47a\u1e43yeva se\u1e6d\u1e6dhatara\u1e43. Tasm\u0101 ta\u1e43 v\u0101 itaresa\u1e43 v\u0101 a\xf1\xf1atara\u1e43 kasi\u1e47aniddese vuttanayena upp\u0101detv\u0101 upac\u0101rabh\u016bmiya\u1e43yeva \u1e6dhatv\u0101 va\u1e0d\u1e0dhetabba\u1e43. Va\u1e0d\u1e0dhan\u0101nayopi cassa tattha vuttanayeneva veditabbo.",translations:{en:"However, a clansman who is a beginner and wishes to see in this way should make the jh\u0101na that is the basis for the direct knowledges, with a kasi\u1e47a as its object, capable of being directed in every way. Then he should take up one of these three kasi\u1e47as: the fire kasi\u1e47a, the white kasi\u1e47a, or the light kasi\u1e47a. Having made it the object of access concentration, he should develop and establish it. The intention is that absorption should not be produced there. For if he produces it, the object becomes the support for the basic jh\u0101na, not the support for the preliminary work. Among these three, the light kasi\u1e47a is the most excellent. Therefore, having produced that one or one of the others in the way stated in the Exposition on the Kasi\u1e47as, he should develop it while remaining right in the plane of access. The method for its development should also be understood in the way stated there.",pt:"No entanto, o filho de boa fam\xedlia que \xe9 um iniciante (\u0101dikammika) e deseja ver dessa forma deve primeiro dominar, em todos os aspects, o jh\u0101na que serve de base para o conhecimento direto (abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101p\u0101dakajjh\u0101na), tendo como objeto um kasina, tornando a mente apta para a proje\xe7\xe3o. Em seguida, ele deve aproximar-se de um dos tr\xeas kasinas: o kasina de fogo (tejokasi\u1e47a), o kasina branco (od\u0101takasi\u1e47a) ou o kasina de luz (\u0101lokakasi\u1e47a). Ele deve fazer disso o objeto do jh\u0101na de acesso (upac\u0101rajjh\u0101na), expandi-lo e mant\xea-lo. O significado \xe9 que ele n\xe3o deve produzir a absor\xe7\xe3o total (appan\u0101) nesse kasina espec\xedfico. Pois, se ele produzir a absor\xe7\xe3o, isso se tornar\xe1 a base para o jh\u0101na de base (p\u0101dakajjh\u0101na), e n\xe3o a base para a prepara\xe7\xe3o preliminar (parikamma). E, entre esses tr\xeas, o kasina de luz \xe9 o mais excelente. Portanto, ele deve produzir esse kasina de luz, ou um dos outros dois, conforme o m\xe9todo descrito na se\xe7\xe3o sobre os kasinas (Kasi\u1e47aniddese), e expandi-lo permanecendo apenas no n\xedvel do jh\u0101na de acesso. O m\xe9todo para expandir o sinal contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta) tamb\xe9m deve ser entendido conforme o m\xe9todo descrito naquela mesma se\xe7\xe3o.",es:"Para un noble hijo de familia que es principiante (\u0101dikammika) y desea ver de esta manera, habiendo hecho que el jh\u0101na que sirve de base para el conocimiento directo (p\u0101dakajjh\u0101na) \u2014el cual tiene un kasina como objeto\u2014 sea capaz de ser dirigido en todos sus aspectos, debe acercarse a uno de estos tres kasinas: el kasina de fuego, el kasina blanco o el kasina de luz. Debe convertirlo en el objeto del jh\u0101na de acceso (upac\u0101rajjh\u0101na), desarrollarlo y mantenerlo. El significado es que no se debe producir la absorci\xf3n (appan\u0101) en ese kasina en particular. Pues si se produce la absorci\xf3n, se convierte en la base de un jh\u0101na (p\u0101dakajjh\u0101na) y no en el sustento para el trabajo preliminar (parikamma). Entre estos tres, el kasina de luz es el m\xe1s excelente. Por lo tanto, habiendo producido ese o cualquiera de los otros seg\xfan el m\xe9todo descrito en la explicaci\xf3n de los kasinas, debe desarrollarse permaneciendo \xfanicamente en la etapa de acceso (upac\u0101rabh\u016bmi). El m\xe9todo de desarrollo debe entenderse de la misma manera que se describe en esa secci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-13.16",pali:"Iti pa\xf1cakkhandhavid\u016b, pa\xf1ca abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101 avoca y\u0101 n\u0101tho; T\u0101 \xf1atv\u0101 t\u0101su aya\u1e43, paki\u1e47\u1e47akakath\u0101pi vi\xf1\xf1eyy\u0101.",translations:{en:"Thus the Protector, knower of the five aggregates, declared the five direct knowledges. Having known them, in regard to them this miscellaneous discourse should also be understood.",pt:"Assim, o Protetor, conhecedor dos cinco agregados, ensinou as cinco superconhecimentos; tendo-as conhecido, esta discuss\xe3o miscel\xe2nea sobre elas tamb\xe9m deve ser compreendida.",es:"As\xed, el Protector, conocedor de los cinco agregados, declar\xf3 los cinco conocimientos superiores. Habi\xe9ndolos comprendido, debe entenderse tambi\xe9n esta explicaci\xf3n miscel\xe1nea sobre ellos."}},{id:"vism-13.17",pali:"Pubbeniv\u0101sa\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 parittamahaggataappam\u0101\u1e47amaggaat\u012btaajjhattabahiddh\u0101navattabb\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena a\u1e6d\u1e6dhasu \u0101ramma\u1e47esu pavattati. Katha\u1e43? Ta\xf1hi k\u0101m\u0101vacarakkhandh\u0101nussara\u1e47ak\u0101le paritt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti. R\u016bp\u0101vacar\u0101r\u016bp\u0101vacarakkhandh\u0101nussara\u1e47ak\u0101le mahaggat\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43. At\u012bte attan\u0101 parehi v\u0101 bh\u0101vitamagga\u1e43 sacchikataphala\xf1ca anussara\u1e47ak\u0101le appam\u0101\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43. Bh\u0101vitamaggameva anussara\u1e47ak\u0101le magg\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43. Niyamato paneta\u1e43 at\u012bt\u0101ramma\u1e47ameva.",translations:{en:"The knowledge of recollecting past lives operates in regard to eight kinds of objects: limited, exalted, immeasurable, the path, past, internal, external, and inexpressible. How so? When it recollects the aggregates of the sense sphere, it has a limited object. When it recollects the aggregates of the fine-material sphere or the immaterial sphere, it has an exalted object. When it recollects a path developed or a fruit realized by oneself or by others in the past, it has an immeasurable object. When it recollects only a developed path, it has the path as its object. As a rule, however, it has only a past object.",pt:"O conhecimento de recorda\xe7\xe3o de vidas passadas (pubbeniv\u0101sa\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) ocorre em rela\xe7\xe3o a oito tipos de objetos, a saber: limitado (paritta), sublime (mahaggata), imensur\xe1vel (appam\u0101\u1e47a), caminho (magga), passado (at\u012bta), interno (ajjhatta), externo (bahiddh\u0101) e indescrit\xedvel [conceito] (navattabba). Como? Pois, no momento de recordar os agregados da esfera sensorial, ele tem um objeto limitado. No momento de recordar os agregados da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil ou imaterial, ele tem um objeto sublime. No momento de recordar o caminho desenvolvido ou o fruto realizado no passado por si mesmo ou por outrem, ele tem um objeto imensur\xe1vel. No momento de recordar apenas o caminho desenvolvido, ele tem o caminho como objeto. Por regra fixa, no entanto, ele tem apenas o passado como objeto.",es:"417. El conocimiento de vidas pasadas (pubbeniv\u0101sa\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) opera sobre ocho tipos de objetos, en virtud de objetos limitados, sublimes, incalculables, del camino, pasados, internos, externos y no manifestables. \xbfC\xf3mo? Al recordar los agregados de la esfera de los sentidos, tiene un objeto limitado (paritta). Al recordar los agregados de las esferas de materia fina o inmaterial, tiene un objeto sublime (mahaggata). Al recordar el camino cultivado o el fruto realizado por uno mismo o por otros en el pasado, tiene un objeto incalculable (appam\u0101\u1e47a). Al recordar espec\xedficamente el camino cultivado, tiene al camino como objeto. No obstante, por regla fija, este conocimiento tiene \xfanicamente un objeto pasado."}},{id:"vism-13.18",pali:"Yath\u0101kammupaga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 parittamahaggataat\u012btaajjhattabahiddh\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena pa\xf1casu \u0101ramma\u1e47esu pavattati. Katha\u1e43? Ta\xf1hi k\u0101m\u0101vacarakammaj\u0101nanak\u0101le paritt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti. R\u016bp\u0101vacar\u0101r\u016bp\u0101vacarakammaj\u0101nanak\u0101le mahaggat\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43. At\u012btameva j\u0101n\u0101t\u012bti at\u012bt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43. Attano kamma\u1e43 j\u0101nanak\u0101le ajjhatt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43. Parassa kamma\u1e43 j\u0101nanak\u0101le bahiddh\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti. Eva\u1e43 yath\u0101kammupaga\xf1\u0101\u1e47assa pa\xf1casu \u0101ramma\u1e47esu pavatti veditabb\u0101. Ya\xf1cettha ajjhatt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\xf1ceva bahiddh\u0101ramma\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101ti vutta\u1e43, ta\u1e43 k\u0101lena ajjhatta\u1e43 k\u0101lena bahiddh\u0101 j\u0101nanak\u0101le ajjhattabahiddh\u0101ramma\u1e47ampi hotiyev\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"The knowledge of beings\u2019 faring according to their kamma operates in regard to five kinds of objects, by way of the limited, the exalted, the past, the internal, and the external. How so? For when it knows kamma of the sense-sphere, it has a limited object. When it knows kamma of the fine-material and immaterial spheres, it has an exalted object. Since it knows only the past, it has a past object. When it knows its own kamma, it has an internal object. When it knows another\u2019s kamma, it has an external object. Thus, the operation of the knowledge of beings\u2019 faring according to their kamma in regard to these five kinds of objects should be understood. And as for what is stated herein as \u2018both an internal object and an external object,\u2019 this is said because when it knows the internal at one time and the external at another, it can indeed also have an internal-and-external object.",pt:"O conhecimento de passagem de acordo com as a\xe7\xf5es (yath\u0101kammupaga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) ocorre em rela\xe7\xe3o a cinco tipos de objetos, a saber: limitado (paritta), sublime (mahaggata), passado (at\u012bta), interno (ajjhatta) e externo (bahiddh\u0101). Como? Pois, no momento de conhecer o kamma da esfera sensorial, ele tem um objeto limitado. No momento de conhecer o kamma da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil ou imaterial, ele tem um objeto sublime. Visto que ele conhece apenas o passado, ele tem um objeto passado. No momento de conhecer o pr\xf3prio kamma, ele tem um objeto interno. No momento de conhecer o kamma de outrem, ele tem um objeto externo. Assim deve ser entendida a ocorr\xeancia do conhecimento de passagem de acordo com as a\xe7\xf5es em rela\xe7\xe3o aos cinco tipos de objetos. E o que \xe9 dito aqui sobre ter 'objeto interno e objeto externo' significa que, por conhecer ora o interno, ora o externo, ele tamb\xe9m pode ter um objeto interno-externo.",es:"El conocimiento de los seres que pasan de acuerdo con sus acciones act\xfaa sobre cinco tipos de objetos: limitado, excelso, pasado, interno y externo. \xbfC\xf3mo? Al conocer una acci\xf3n de la esfera de los sentidos, tiene un objeto limitado. Al conocer una acci\xf3n de la esfera de la forma o sin forma, tiene un objeto excelso. Puesto que conoce solo el pasado, tiene un objeto pasado. Al conocer la propia acci\xf3n, tiene un objeto interno. Al conocer la acci\xf3n de otro, tiene un objeto externo. As\xed debe entenderse la actividad del conocimiento de los seres que pasan de acuerdo con sus acciones respecto a los cinco tipos de objetos. Y lo que se dice aqu\xed sobre 'objeto interno y objeto externo', se refiere a que, al conocer en un momento lo interno y en otro momento lo externo, tambi\xe9n tiene objetos tanto internos como externos."}}]},431,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,i,s,t,n){s.exports=[{id:"vism-14.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni yasm\u0101 eva\u1e43 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101vasena adhigat\u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101ya thiratar\u0101ya sam\u0101dhibh\u0101van\u0101ya samp\u0101dit\u0101dhicittena \u2018\u2018s\u012ble pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya naro sapa\xf1\xf1o, citta\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1a\xf1ca bh\u0101vaya\u2019\u2019nti vacanato cittas\u012bsena niddi\u1e6d\u1e6dhe sam\u0101dhimhi bh\u0101vite tadanantar\u0101 pana pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 bh\u0101vetabb\u0101. S\u0101 ca atisa\u1e45khepadesitatt\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101tumpi t\u0101va na sukar\u0101, pageva bh\u0101vetu\u1e43. Tasm\u0101 tass\u0101 vitth\u0101ra\xf1ca bh\u0101van\u0101naya\xf1ca dassetu\u1e43 ayamaparo pa\xf1h\u0101kamo \u2013 k\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101? Kena\u1e6d\u1e6dhena pa\xf1\xf1\u0101? K\u0101nass\u0101 lakkha\u1e47arasapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni? Katividh\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101? Katha\u1e43 bh\u0101vetabb\u0101? Pa\xf1\xf1\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101ya ko \u0101nisa\u1e43soti?",translations:{en:"Now, a bhikkhu endowed with the development of concentration that is very firm, whose benefit was attained through the direct knowledges in this way, who has accomplished the higher consciousness\u2014when concentration, indicated under the heading of 'mind' in accordance with the saying, 'A wise man, established in virtue, should develop mind and wisdom,' has been developed\u2014understanding should be developed immediately following that. And because it has been taught in an extremely concise manner, it is not easy even to understand, let alone to develop. Therefore, in order to show its details and the method of its development, here is another series of questions: What is understanding? In what sense is it understanding? What are its characteristic, function, manifestation, and proximate cause? How many kinds of understanding are there? How is it to be developed? What is the benefit of the development of understanding?",pt:"Agora, visto que, por meio do desenvolvimento da concentra\xe7\xe3o que se tornou extremamente firme e cujo benef\xedcio foi obtido por meio dos conhecimentos diretos (abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101), a mente superior foi realizada pelo nobre praticante \u2014 tendo sido a concentra\xe7\xe3o desenvolvida sob o t\xedtulo de 'mente' (citta), de acordo com a passagem 'O homem s\xe1bio, estabelecido na virtude, deve desenvolver a mente e o entendimento' \u2014, a compreens\xe3o (pa\xf1\xf1\u0101) deve ser desenvolvida logo em seguida. E, como ela foi ensinada de modo extremamente conciso, n\xe3o \xe9 f\xe1cil sequer de ser compreendida, quanto mais de ser desenvolvida. Portanto, para expor os seus detalhes e o m\xe9todo de seu desenvolvimento, apresenta-se a seguinte ordem de perguntas: O que \xe9 o entendimento? Em que sentido \xe9 entendimento? Quais s\xe3o as suas caracter\xedsticas, fun\xe7\xf5es, manifesta\xe7\xf5es e causas pr\xf3ximas? Quantos tipos de entendimento existem? Como deve ser desenvolvido? Qual \xe9 o benef\xedcio do desenvolvimento do entendimento?",es:"Ahora, puesto que el monje que posee el desarrollo de la concentraci\xf3n m\xe1s firme mediante los conocimientos directos ha cumplido con el adiestramiento de la mente superior seg\xfan el verso: 'El hombre sabio, establecido en la virtud, que desarrolla la mente y el entendimiento', habi\xe9ndose desarrollado la concentraci\xf3n indicada bajo el nombre de mente, debe cultivarse seguidamente el entendimiento (pa\xf1\xf1\u0101). Y como ha sido ense\xf1ada de manera sumamente resumida, no es f\xe1cil ni siquiera comprenderla, y mucho menos desarrollarla. Por lo tanto, para mostrar sus detalles y el m\xe9todo de desarrollo, se presenta la siguiente serie de preguntas: \xbfQu\xe9 es el entendimiento? \xbfEn qu\xe9 sentido es entendimiento? \xbfCu\xe1les son sus caracter\xedsticas, funciones, manifestaciones y causas pr\xf3ximas? \xbfCu\xe1ntas clases de entendimiento existen? \xbfC\xf3mo debe desarrollarse? \xbfCu\xe1l es el beneficio de su desarrollo?"}},{id:"vism-14.2",pali:"Katha\u1e43 bh\u0101vetabb\u0101ti ettha pana yasm\u0101 im\u0101ya pa\xf1\xf1\u0101ya khandh\u0101yatanadh\u0101tuindriyasaccapa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101d\u0101dibhed\u0101 dhamm\u0101 bh\u016bmi, s\u012blavisuddhi ceva cittavisuddhi c\u0101ti im\u0101 dve visuddhiyo m\u016bla\u1e43, di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddhi, ka\u1e45kh\u0101vitara\u1e47avisuddhi, magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi, pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi, \xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddh\u012bti im\u0101 pa\xf1ca visuddhiyo sar\u012bra\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Regarding 'How is it to be developed?': Herein, since the phenomena differentiated as the aggregates, the bases, the elements, the faculties, the truths, dependent origination, and so forth, are the ground of this understanding; the two purifications, namely, purification of virtue and purification of mind, are its root; and the five purifications, namely, purification of view, purification by overcoming doubt, purification by knowledge and vision of what is path and not-path, purification by knowledge and vision of the way, and purification by knowledge and vision, are its body.",pt:"Quanto a 'Como deve ser desenvolvido?': nele, visto que as realidades distinguidas como os agregados (khandhas), as bases (\u0101yatanas), os elementos (dh\u0101tus), as faculdades (indriyas), as verdades (saccas), a origina\xe7\xe3o dependente (pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101da) e outras s\xe3o o solo deste entendimento; a purifica\xe7\xe3o da virtude (s\u012blavisuddhi) e a purifica\xe7\xe3o da mente (cittavisuddhi) s\xe3o a sua raiz; e as cinco purifica\xe7\xf5es \u2014 a saber, a purifica\xe7\xe3o da vis\xe3o (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddhi), a purifica\xe7\xe3o pela supera\xe7\xe3o da d\xfavida (ka\u1e45kh\u0101vitara\u1e47avisuddhi), a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o do caminho e do n\xe3o caminho (magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi), a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o da pr\xe1tica (pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi) e a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o (\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi) \u2014 constituem o seu corpo.",es:"En cuanto a '\xbfC\xf3mo debe ser desarrollado?': en este contexto, dado que los fen\xf3menos clasificados como los agregados (khandha), las bases (\u0101yatana), los elementos (dh\u0101tu), las facultades (indriya), las nobles verdades (sacca) y el origen dependiente (pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101da) son el terreno de este entendimiento; y que la purificaci\xf3n de la virtud y la purifica\xe7\xe3o de la mente son las dos ra\xedces de este entendimiento; y que las cinco purificaciones restantes \u2014a saber, la purificaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n, la purificaci\xf3n por superaci\xf3n de la duda, la purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y visi\xf3n del camino y no camino, la purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y visi\xf3n del sendero de pr\xe1ctica, y la purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y visi\xf3n\u2014 son su cuerpo."}},{id:"vism-14.3",pali:"Tattha ya\u1e43 ki\xf1ci s\u012bt\u0101d\u012bhi ruppanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 dhammaj\u0101ta\u1e43, sabba\u1e43 ta\u1e43 ekato katv\u0101 r\u016bpakkhandhoti vuccati. Ruppat\u012bti kho, bhikkhave, tasm\u0101 r\u016bpanti vuccat\u012bti (sa\u1e43. ni. 3.79) vacanato ruppanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43. Kena ruppati? S\u012btenapi ruppati, u\u1e47henapi ruppati, jighacch\u0101yapi ruppati, pip\u0101s\u0101yapi ruppati, \u1e0da\u1e43samakasav\u0101t\u0101tapasiri\u1e43sapasamphassenapi ruppati.",translations:{en:"Herein, whatever kind of phenomenon has the characteristic of being afflicted by cold, etc., all that taken together is called the aggregate of form. Form has the characteristic of being afflicted, in accordance with the saying: 'It is afflicted, monks, therefore it is called form' (SN 22.79). Afflicted by what? It is afflicted by cold, it is afflicted by heat, it is afflicted by hunger, it is afflicted by thirst, it is afflicted by the contact of horseflies, mosquitoes, wind, the sun, and creeping things.",pt:"Ali, qualquer tipo de fen\xf4meno que tenha a caracter\xedstica de ser alterado ou afetado por frio, calor, etc., tudo isso tomado em conjunto \xe9 chamado de o agregado da mat\xe9ria (r\u016bpakkhandha). A mat\xe9ria tem a caracter\xedstica de ser suscet\xedvel \xe0 altera\xe7\xe3o, conforme a passagem: '\xc9 afetada, monges; por isso \xe9 chamada de mat\xe9ria'. Afetada por qu\xea? \xc9 afetada pelo frio, afetada pelo calor, afetada pela fome, afetada pela sede, afetada pelo contato com mutucas, mosquitos, vento, sol e r\xe9pteis.",es:"All\xed, cualquier clase de fen\xf3meno que tenga la caracter\xedstica de ser alterado por el fr\xedo y dem\xe1s condiciones, todo eso considerado en conjunto se denomina el agregado de la forma o materia (r\u016bpakkhandha). La forma tiene la caracter\xedstica de la alterabilidad, de acuerdo con el pasaje que dice: 'Es alterada, monjes, por eso se llama forma'. \xbfPor qu\xe9 es alterada? Es alterada por el fr\xedo, es alterada por el calor, es alterada por el hambre, es alterada por la sed, es alterada por el contacto con t\xe1banos, mosquitos, viento, sol y animales que se arrastran."}},{id:"vism-14.4",pali:"Tadeta\u1e43 ruppanalakkha\u1e47ena ekavidhampi bh\u016btop\u0101d\u0101yabhedato duvidha\u1e43 hoti. Tattha bh\u016btar\u016bpa\u1e43 catubbidha\u1e43 \u2013 pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu, \u0101podh\u0101tu, tejodh\u0101tu, v\u0101yodh\u0101t\u016bti. T\u0101sa\u1e43 lakkha\u1e47arasapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni catudh\u0101tuvavatth\u0101ne vutt\u0101neva.",translations:{en:"This form, though onefold by its characteristic of being afflicted, is twofold by the division into primary and derived. Therein, primary form is fourfold: the earth element, the water element, the fire element, and the air element. Their characteristics, functions, manifestations, and proximate causes have already been stated in the Analysis of the Four Elements.",pt:"Esta mat\xe9ria, embora seja de um s\xf3 tipo por sua caracter\xedstica de ser afetada, \xe9 de dois tipos pela divis\xe3o entre mat\xe9ria prim\xe1ria e mat\xe9ria derivada. Ali, a mat\xe9ria prim\xe1ria \xe9 de quatro tipos: o elemento terra, o elemento \xe1gua, o elemento fogo e o elemento ar. As suas caracter\xedsticas, fun\xe7\xf5es, manifesta\xe7\xf5es e causas pr\xf3ximas j\xe1 foram explicadas na Determina\xe7\xe3o dos Quatro Elementos.",es:"Esta forma, aunque es de una sola clase por su caracter\xedstica de alterabilidad, se divide en dos clases: elementos fundamentales (bh\u016btar\u016bpa) y materia derivada (up\u0101d\u0101r\u016bpa). Entre ellos, la materia fundamental es de cuatro clases: el elemento tierra, el elemento agua, el elemento fuego y el elemento aire. Sus caracter\xedsticas, funciones, manifestaciones y causas pr\xf3ximas ya han sido explicadas en la Determinaci\xf3n de los Cuatro Elementos."}},{id:"vism-14.5",pali:"Up\u0101d\u0101r\u016bpa\u1e43 catuv\u012bsatividha\u1e43 \u2013 cakkhu, sota\u1e43, gh\u0101na\u1e43, jivh\u0101, k\u0101yo, r\u016bpa\u1e43, saddo, gandho, raso, itthindriya\u1e43, purisindriya\u1e43, j\u012bvitindriya\u1e43, hadayavatthu, k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1atti, vac\u012bvi\xf1\xf1atti, \u0101k\u0101sadh\u0101tu, r\u016bpassa lahut\u0101, mudut\u0101, kamma\xf1\xf1at\u0101, upacayo, santati, jarat\u0101, aniccat\u0101, kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101ro \u0101h\u0101roti.",translations:{en:"Derived form is twenty-fourfold: the eye, the ear, the nose, the tongue, the body; visible form, sound, odor, taste; the female sex-faculty, the male sex-faculty, the life faculty, the heart-basis; bodily intimation, vocal intimation, the space element; lightness of form, malleability of form, wieldiness of form; growth of form, continuity of form, aging of form, impermanence of form, and physical nutriment.",pt:"A mat\xe9ria derivada \xe9 de vinte e quatro tipos: o olho, o ouvido, o nariz, a l\xedngua, o corpo; a forma vis\xedvel, o som, o odor, o sabor; a feminilidade, a masculinidade, a faculdade vital, a base material do cora\xe7\xe3o; a comunica\xe7\xe3o corporal, a comunica\xe7\xe3o verbal, o elemento espa\xe7o; a leveza da mat\xe9ria, a maleabilidade da mat\xe9ria, a flexibilidade da mat\xe9ria; o crescimento da mat\xe9ria, a continuidade da mat\xe9ria, a decad\xeancia da mat\xe9ria, a imperman\xeancia da mat\xe9ria e o alimento f\xedsico.",es:"La materia derivada es de veinticuatro clases: el ojo, el o\xeddo, la nariz, la lengua, el cuerpo; la forma visible, el sonido, el olor, el sabor; la facultad femenina, la facultad masculina, la facultad de la vida, la base del coraz\xf3n; la expresi\xf3n corporal, la expresi\xf3n verbal, el elemento espacio; la ligereza de la forma, la docilidad de la forma, la maleabilidad de la forma; la acumulaci\xf3n de la forma, la continuidad de la forma, la decadencia de la forma, la impermanencia de la forma y el alimento f\xedsico."}},{id:"vism-14.6",pali:"Itaresu pana ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci vedayitalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, sabba\u1e43 ta\u1e43 ekato katv\u0101 vedan\u0101kkhandho; ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci sa\xf1j\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, sabba\u1e43 ta\u1e43 ekato katv\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101kkhandho; ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci abhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ralakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, sabba\u1e43 ta\u1e43 ekato katv\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandho; ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci vij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, sabba\u1e43 ta\u1e43 ekato katv\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47akkhandho veditabbo.",translations:{en:"As for the remaining aggregates, whatever has the characteristic of being felt, all that taken together is the aggregate of feeling; whatever has the characteristic of perceiving, all that taken together is the aggregate of perception; whatever has the characteristic of forming, all that taken together is the aggregate of formations; whatever has the characteristic of cognizing, all that taken together should be understood as the aggregate of consciousness.",pt:"Quanto aos outros agregados, tudo aquilo que tem a caracter\xedstica de experienciar uma sensa\xe7\xe3o, tomado em conjunto, \xe9 o agregado da sensa\xe7\xe3o; tudo aquilo que tem a caracter\xedstica de reconhecer ou perceber, tomado em conjunto, \xe9 o agregado da percep\xe7\xe3o; tudo aquilo que tem a caracter\xedstica de construir ou condicionar, tomado em conjunto, \xe9 o agregado das forma\xe7\xf5es mentais; tudo aquilo que tem a caracter\xedstica de cognizar, tomado em conjunto, deve ser compreendido como o agregado da consci\xeancia.",es:"En cuanto a los dem\xe1s agregados, todo aquello que tiene la caracter\xedstica de experimentar una sensaci\xf3n, considerado en conjunto, es el agregado de la sensaci\xf3n; todo aquello que tiene la caracter\xedstica de percibir, considerado en conjunto, es el agregado de la percepci\xf3n; todo aquello que tiene la caracter\xedstica de conformar o elaborar, considerado en conjunto, es el agregado de las formaciones; todo aquello que tiene la caracter\xedstica de conocer o ser consciente, considerado en conjunto, debe entenderse como el agregado de la conciencia."}},{id:"vism-14.7",pali:"Ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci vij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, sabba\u1e43 ta\u1e43 ekato katv\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47akkhandho veditabboti hi vutta\u1e43. Ki\xf1ca vij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43? Vij\u0101n\u0101ti vij\u0101n\u0101t\u012bti kho, bhikkhave, tasm\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47anti vuccat\u012bti (sa\u1e43. ni. 3.79) vacanato vij\u0101nanameva vij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43. Ta\xf1ca kho \u0101ramma\u1e47a\xf1\xf1ut\u0101yeva vuccati. Na hi \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1\u0101ya vij\u0101n\u0101ti n\u0101ma natthi.",translations:{en:"For it was said: 'Whatever has the characteristic of cognizing, all that taken together is to be known as the aggregate of consciousness.' And what is the characteristic of cognizing? According to the passage: 'It cognizes, monks, therefore it is called consciousness' (SN 22.79), cognizing itself is the characteristic of cognizing. And that is simply said to be knowing the object. For there is no consciousness that cognizes without knowing an object.",pt:"Pois foi dito que qualquer coisa que tenha a caracter\xedstica de cogni\xe7\xe3o, reunida em conjunto, deve ser conhecida como o agregado da consci\xeancia. E o que \xe9 essa caracter\xedstica de cogni\xe7\xe3o? De acordo com a passagem que diz 'Ela cogniza, monges; por isso \xe9 chamada de consci\xeancia', a pr\xf3pria cogni\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a caracter\xedstica de cogni\xe7\xe3o. E isso \xe9 expressado simplesmente como o conhecimento do objeto, pois n\xe3o existe nenhuma consci\xeancia que cognize sem conhecer um objeto.",es:"Pues se ha dicho que todo aquello que posee la caracter\xedstica de conocer o cognizar, reunido en conjunto, debe entenderse como el agregado de la conciencia. \xbfY qu\xe9 es la caracter\xedstica de cognici\xf3n? De acuerdo con el pasaje que dice: 'Conoce, monjes, por eso se llama conciencia', el conocimiento mismo es la caracter\xedstica de cognici\xf3n. Y esto se refiere exclusivamente al hecho de aprehender el objeto, ya que no existe una conciencia que conozca sin aprehender un objeto."}},{id:"vism-14.8",pali:"Tattha kusala\u1e43 bh\u016bmibhedato catubbidha\u1e43 k\u0101m\u0101vacara\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101vacara\u1e43 ar\u016bp\u0101vacara\u1e43 lokuttara\xf1ca. Akusala\u1e43 pana k\u0101m\u0101vacarameva, m\u016blato tividha\u1e43 lobham\u016bla\u1e43 dosam\u016bla\u1e43 moham\u016bla\xf1ca. Vip\u0101ka\xf1ca kriy\u0101 ca cat\u016bsu bh\u016bm\u012bsu labbhati. Iti te pa\xf1c\u0101s\u012bti citt\u0101ni v\u0101 ek\u016bnasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi citt\u0101ni v\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47akkhandhoti vuccanti.",translations:{en:"Therein, wholesome consciousness is fourfold by the division of planes: of the sensuous plane, of the fine-material plane, of the immaterial plane, and supramundane. Unwholesome consciousness belongs to the sensuous plane only, and is threefold by its roots: rooted in greed, rooted in hatred, and rooted in delusion. Resultant and functional consciousness are found in all four planes. Thus, these eighty-nine types of consciousness or one hundred and twenty-one are called the aggregate of consciousness.",pt:"Ali, a consci\xeancia salutar (kusala citta) \xe9 de quatro tipos pela divis\xe3o dos planos: do plano sensorial, do plano da mat\xe9ria sutil, do plano imaterial e do plano supramundano. A consci\xeancia prejudicial (akusala citta) pertence apenas ao plano sensorial e \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos pelas suas ra\xedzes: com raiz na cobi\xe7a, com raiz na avers\xe3o e com raiz na delus\xe3o. A consci\xeancia resultante e a funcional ocorrem nos quatro planos. Assim, esses oitenta e nove tipos de consci\xeancia ou cento e vinte e um s\xe3o chamados de agregado da consci\xeancia.",es:"All\xed, la conciencia sana (kusala) se divide en cuatro clases seg\xfan los planos: de la esfera de los sentidos, de la esfera de la forma sutil, de la esfera inmaterial y supramundana. La conciencia insana (akusala) pertenece \xfanicamente al plano sensorial y es de tres clases seg\xfan sus ra\xedces: con ra\xedz en el apego, con ra\xedz en el odio y con ra\xedz en la ignorancia. La conciencia resultante y la funcional se encuentran en los cuatro planos. As\xed, estos ochenta y nueve tipos de conciencia (o ciento veintiuno) reciben el nombre de agregado de la conciencia."}},{id:"vism-14.9",pali:"Id\u0101ni ya\u1e43 vutta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci vedayitalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, sabba\u1e43 ta\u1e43 ekato katv\u0101 vedan\u0101kkhandho\u2019\u2019ti, tattha katha\u1e43 veditabba\u1e43? Cakkhusamphassaj\u0101 vedan\u0101, sotasamphassaj\u0101 vedan\u0101, gh\u0101nasamphassaj\u0101 vedan\u0101, jivh\u0101samphassaj\u0101 vedan\u0101, k\u0101yasamphassaj\u0101 vedan\u0101, manosamphassaj\u0101 vedan\u0101ti eva\u1e43 chabbidh\u0101 hoti. S\u0101 panes\u0101 anubhavanalakkha\u1e47\u0101, anubhanaras\u0101, cetasik\u0101ss\u0101dapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, passapada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101.",translations:{en:"Now, as to what was said: \u2018Whatever has the characteristic of being felt, all that taken together is the aggregate of feeling,\u2019 how is it to be understood therein? Feeling born of eye-contact, feeling born of ear-contact, feeling born of nose-contact, feeling born of tongue-contact, feeling born of body-contact, feeling born of mind-contact: thus it is sixfold. This feeling has the characteristic of experiencing, its function is the tasting of the object's flavor, its manifestation is mental gratification, and its proximate cause is contact.",pt:"Agora, quanto ao que foi dito: 'Tudo aquilo que tem a caracter\xedstica de experienciar uma sensa\xe7\xe3o, tomado em conjunto, \xe9 o agregado da sensa\xe7\xe3o', como deve ser compreendido isso? H\xe1 a sensa\xe7\xe3o nascida do contato no olho, a sensa\xe7\xe3o nascida do contato no ouvido, a sensa\xe7\xe3o nascida do contato no nariz, a sensa\xe7\xe3o nascida do contato na l\xedngua, a sensa\xe7\xe3o nascida do contato no corpo e a sensa\xe7\xe3o nascida do contato na mente: assim, ela \xe9 de seis tipos. Essa sensa\xe7\xe3o tem como caracter\xedstica a experi\xeancia direta do objeto; sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 saborear o est\xedmulo do objeto; manifesta-se como gratifica\xe7\xe3o mental e tem o contato sensorial como sua causa pr\xf3xima.",es:"Ahora, respecto a lo expresado: 'Todo aquello que posee la caracter\xedstica de la sensaci\xf3n, reunido en conjunto, es el agregado de la sensaci\xf3n', \xbfc\xf3mo debe entenderse esto? Existe la sensaci\xf3n nacida del contacto del ojo, del o\xeddo, de la nariz, de la lengua, del cuerpo y de la mente: as\xed es de seis clases. Esta sensaci\xf3n tiene como caracter\xedstica el experimentar; su funci\xf3n es disfrutar o saborear el objeto; se manifiesta como satisfacci\xf3n mental y tiene el contacto como su causa pr\xf3xima."}},{id:"vism-14.10",pali:"Id\u0101ni ya\u1e43 vutta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci sa\xf1j\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, sabba\u1e43 ta\u1e43 ekato katv\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101kkhandho\u2019\u2019ti, s\u0101pi cakkhusamphassaj\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 manosamphassaj\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101ti eva\u1e43 chabbidh\u0101 hoti. S\u0101 panes\u0101 sa\xf1j\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47\u0101, pacc\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47aras\u0101 puna sa\xf1j\u0101nanapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 abbh\u016bt\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101bhinivesapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 v\u0101, yath\u0101sagatasabh\u0101vapada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101. Yath\u0101 kassako ti\u1e47apurise purisasampaccayo hoti, evames\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101 nimittagg\u0101hik\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"Now, as to what was said: \u2018Whatever has the characteristic of perceiving, all that taken together is the aggregate of perception\u2019\u2014that too is sixfold as perception born of eye-contact, and so on, up to perception born of mind-contact. This perception has the characteristic of recognizing, its function is recognizing again what has previously been perceived, its manifestation is the apprehension of a sign or a conviction regarding an unreal object, and its proximate cause is the objective datum as it has presented itself. Just as a farmer perceives a scarecrow as a man, even so this perception grasps signs.",pt:"Agora, quanto ao que foi dito: 'Tudo aquilo que tem a caracter\xedstica de reconhecer ou perceber, tomado em conjunto, \xe9 o agregado da percep\xe7\xe3o' \u2014 esta tamb\xe9m \xe9 de seis tipos: a percep\xe7\xe3o nascida do contato no olho, at\xe9 a percep\xe7\xe3o nascida do contato na mente. Essa percep\xe7\xe3o tem como caracter\xedstica o ato de reconhecer; sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 reconhecer novamente algo percebido anteriormente; manifesta-se como a apreens\xe3o de um sinal conceitual ou como uma convic\xe7\xe3o baseada num objeto aparente; e tem como causa pr\xf3xima o objeto tal como ele se apresenta aos sentidos. Assim como um campon\xeas percebe um espantalho feito de palha como se fosse um homem verdadeiro, do mesmo modo a percep\xe7\xe3o apreende os sinais superficiais das coisas.",es:"Ahora bien, en cuanto a lo que se dijo: 'Todo aquello que posee la caracter\xedstica de percibir, considerado en conjunto, es el agregado de la percepci\xf3n': este es de seis clases, a saber, la percepci\xf3n nacida del contacto en el ojo, y as\xed sucesivamente hasta la percepci\xf3n nacida del contacto en la mente. Esta percepci\xf3n tiene por caracter\xedstica el percibir o reconocer; su funci\xf3n es reconocer de nuevo lo ya percibido; se manifiesta como la captaci\xf3n de un signo conceptual o como la convicci\xf3n ante un objeto ilusorio; y tiene como causa pr\xf3xima el objeto tal como se presenta. As\xed como un agricultor toma un espantap\xe1jaros por un ser humano, de esa misma manera la percepci\xf3n capta las se\xf1ales exteriores."}},{id:"vism-14.11",pali:"Id\u0101ni ya\u1e43 vutta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci abhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ralakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, sabba\u1e43 ta\u1e43 ekato katv\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandho\u2019\u2019ti, tattha sa\u1e45kharont\u012bti sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101. Te abhisa\u1e45khara\u1e47alakkha\u1e47\u0101, \u0101y\u016bhanaras\u0101, cetan\u0101pubba\u1e45gam\u0101. Phasso, cetan\u0101, vitakko, vic\u0101ro, p\u012bti, v\u012briya\u1e43, j\u012bvita\u1e43, sam\u0101dhi, saddh\u0101, sati, hiri, ottappa\u1e43, alobho, adoso, amoho ca etehi bhed\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandho veditabbo.",translations:{en:"Now, as to what was said: \u2018Whatever has the characteristic of constructing, all that taken together is the aggregate of formations\u2019\u2014herein, formations are so called because they construct. They have the characteristic of constructing, the function of accumulating, and are preceded by volition. Contact, volition, applied thought, sustained thought, rapture, energy, life faculty, concentration, faith, mindfulness, shame, fear of wrongdoing, non-greed, non-hatred, and non-delusion: by these divisions should the aggregate of formations be understood.",pt:"Agora, quanto ao que foi ensinado: 'Tudo aquilo que tem a caracter\xedstica de construir ou condicionar, tomado em conjunto, \xe9 o agregado das forma\xe7\xf5es mentais' \u2014 nesse ponto, s\xe3o chamadas de forma\xe7\xf5es (sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101) porque constroem. Elas t\xeam a caracter\xedstica de construir, a fun\xe7\xe3o de acumular kamma e s\xe3o lideradas pela voli\xe7\xe3o (cetan\u0101). O contato, a voli\xe7\xe3o, o pensamento aplicado, o pensamento sustentado, o \xeaxtase, a energia, a faculdade vital, a concentra\xe7\xe3o, a f\xe9, a aten\xe7\xe3o plena, a vergonha moral, o temor moral, o desapego, a benevol\xeancia e a sabedoria: atrav\xe9s destas divis\xf5es deve ser compreendido o agregado das forma\xe7\xf5es mentais.",es:"Ahora, respecto a lo dicho: 'Todo aquello que posee la caracter\xedstica de conformar o elaborar, tomado en conjunto, es el agregado de las formaciones': aqu\xed se llaman formaciones porque conforman los estados condicionados. Tienen por caracter\xedstica la elaboraci\xf3n activa; su funci\xf3n es acumular acciones (kamma) y est\xe1n precedidas por la volici\xf3n. El contacto, la volici\xf3n, el pensamiento aplicado, el pensamiento sostenido, el entusiasmo, la energ\xeda, la facultad vital, la concentraci\xf3n, la fe, la atenci\xf3n plena, la verg\xfcenza moral, el temor moral, el desapego, la benevolencia y la sabidur\xeda: mediante estas divisiones debe entenderse el agregado de las formaciones."}},{id:"vism-14.12",pali:"Tattha phusat\u012bti phasso. Sv\u0101ya\u1e43 phusanalakkha\u1e47o. Sa\u1e45gha\u1e6d\u1e6danaraso, sannip\u0101tapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101no, \u0101p\u0101thagatavisayapada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101no. So hi ar\u016bpadhammopi sam\u0101no \u0101ramma\u1e47e phusam\u0101nova pavattati. Na ca ekadesena laggo hutv\u0101, yath\u0101 cakkhussa r\u016bpa\u1e43, sotassa saddo, eva\u1e43 manassa \u0101ramma\u1e47assa ca sa\u1e45gha\u1e6d\u1e6danamano viya hutv\u0101 pavattati. Sannip\u0101tapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101no ca tividhasannip\u0101tena vuttatt\u0101 veditabbo.",translations:{en:"Herein, \u2018it touches,\u2019 thus it is contact. This has the characteristic of touching. Its function is impingement, its manifestation is concurrence of base, object, and consciousness, and its proximate cause is an objective datum that has entered the field of awareness. For contact, even though it is an immaterial state, occurs in the object by touching it. And not adhering to one part, like form to the eye or sound to the ear, it occurs as an impingement of mind and object.",pt:"Entre estes, o contato (phassa) \xe9 assim chamado porque toca. Ele tem a caracter\xedstica de tocar. Sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o impacto (sa\u1e45gha\u1e6d\u1e6dana); manifesta-se como a uni\xe3o (sannip\u0101ta) [da base, do objeto e da consci\xeancia]; e tem o objeto que entrou no campo de foco como sua causa pr\xf3xima. Pois este, embora seja um dhamma imaterial, ocorre no objeto precisamente tocando-o. E embora n\xe3o se apegue a uma parte espec\xedfica, ele impacta a mente e o objeto, assim como a forma vis\xedvel impacta o olho e o som impacta o ouvido.",es:"All\xed, se llama contacto porque toca. Este tiene la caracter\xedstica de tocar. Su funci\xf3n es el impacto; se manifiesta como concurrencia; su causa pr\xf3xima es el objeto que ha entrado en el campo de la experiencia. Pues, aunque es un estado inmaterial, ocurre en el objeto precisamente mediante el acto de tocar. Y aunque no se adhiere a una parte, impacta la mente y el objeto, as\xed como el color al ojo y el sonido al o\xeddo."}},{id:"vism-14.13",pali:"Cetayat\u012bti cetan\u0101. Abhisandahat\u012bti attho. S\u0101 cetan\u0101bh\u0101valakkha\u1e47\u0101, \u0101y\u016bhanaras\u0101, sa\u1e43vidahanapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 sakiccaparakiccas\u0101dhik\u0101 je\u1e6d\u1e6dhasissamah\u0101va\u1e0d\u1e0dhak\u012b\u0101dayo viya. Acc\u0101yikakamm\u0101nussara\u1e47\u0101d\u012bsu ca pan\u0101ya\u1e43 sampayutt\u0101na\u1e43 ussahanabh\u0101vena pavattam\u0101n\u0101 p\u0101ka\u1e6d\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"\u2018It wills,\u2019 thus it is volition; the meaning is that it coordinates. It has the characteristic of the state of willing, the function of striving, and manifestation as coordinating, accomplishing its own task and the tasks of others, like a senior pupil or a master carpenter. Moreover, in such instances as the urgent recollection of a deed, this volition becomes manifest through its occurring with the nature of an urge to its associated states.",pt:"A voli\xe7\xe3o (cetan\u0101) \xe9 assim chamada porque coordena. O significado \xe9 que ela re\xfane. Ela tem a caracter\xedstica do estado de voli\xe7\xe3o; sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 acumular (\u0101y\u016bhana); manifesta-se como coordena\xe7\xe3o (sa\u1e43vidahana); e realiza sua pr\xf3pria tarefa e a dos dhammas associados, assim como um disc\xedpulo s\xeanior ou um mestre carpinteiro e outros. E ela se torna claramente evidente atrav\xe9s do estado de esfor\xe7o que imp\xf5e aos dhammas associados em tarefas como a recorda\xe7\xe3o de a\xe7\xf5es urgentes e afins.",es:"Se llama voluntad porque coordina. El significado es que une. Ella tiene la caracter\xedstica del estado de voluntad; su funci\xf3n es esforzarse por acumular; se manifiesta como el acto de ordenar; es como un estudiante mayor o un maestro carpintero que cumplen tanto sus propias tareas como las de otros. Adem\xe1s, se vuelve evidente a trav\xe9s del estado de esforzarse por los estados asociados en actos tales como el recuerdo de acciones urgentes."}},{id:"vism-14.14",pali:"Vitakkavic\u0101rap\u012bt\u012bsu ya\u1e43 vattabba\u1e43 siy\u0101, ta\u1e43 sabba\u1e43 pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47aniddese pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101ya\u1e43 (visuddhi. 1.71) vuttameva.",translations:{en:"Whatever should be said about initial application, sustained application, and joy, all that has already been said in the description of the first jh\u0101na in the exposition of the earth kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"Tudo o que deveria ser dito sobre o pensamento aplicado (vitakka), o pensamento sustentado (vic\u0101ra) e o arrebatamento (p\u012bti) j\xe1 foi dito na explica\xe7\xe3o do primeiro jh\u0101na na exposi\xe7\xe3o do kasina de terra.",es:"Todo lo que deba decirse sobre el pensamiento aplicado, el pensamiento sostenido y la alegr\xeda, ya ha sido dicho en la descripci\xf3n del primer jh\u0101na dentro de la exposici\xf3n de la totalidad de tierra."}},{id:"vism-14.15",pali:"Saranti t\u0101ya, saya\u1e43 v\u0101 sarati sara\u1e47amattameva v\u0101 es\u0101ti sati. S\u0101 apil\u0101panalakkha\u1e47\u0101, asammosaras\u0101, \u0101rakkhapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, visay\u0101bhimukhabh\u0101vapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 v\u0101, thirasa\xf1\xf1\u0101pada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, k\u0101y\u0101disatipa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 v\u0101. \u0100ramma\u1e47e da\u1e37hapati\u1e6d\u1e6dhitatt\u0101 pana esik\u0101 viya, cakkhudv\u0101r\u0101dirakkha\u1e47ato dov\u0101riko viya ca da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"\u2018One remembers by means of it,\u2019 or \u2018it remembers by itself,\u2019 or \u2018it is simply the act of remembering\u2019\u2014this is mindfulness. It has the characteristic of not floating away, its function is non-confusion, and it is manifested as guarding, or as the state of facing the object. Its proximate cause is firm perception, or the foundations of mindfulness concerning the body, etc. Because it is firmly established on the object, it should be seen as like a pillar; and because it guards the eye-door and so on, it should be seen as like a gatekeeper.",pt:"A aten\xe7\xe3o plena (sati) \xe9 aquilo por meio do qual eles se lembram, ou que se lembra por si mesma, ou que \xe9 o mero ato de lembrar. Ela tem a caracter\xedstica de n\xe3o flutuar (apil\u0101pana); sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a n\xe3o confus\xe3o ou n\xe3o esquecimento (asammosa); manifesta-se como prote\xe7\xe3o (\u0101rakkha) ou como o estado de estar face a face com o objeto; e tem a percep\xe7\xe3o firme (thirasa\xf1\xf1\u0101) como sua causa pr\xf3xima, ou tem os fundamentos da aten\xe7\xe3o plena, como o corpo e outros, como sua causa pr\xf3xima. No entanto, por estar firmemente estabelecida no objeto, deve ser vista como um pilar, e por proteger a porta do olho e outras, deve ser vista como um guardi\xe3o do portal.",es:"Sati es aquello mediante lo cual se recuerda, o aquello que por s\xed mismo recuerda, o bien es simplemente el acto de recordar. Tiene como caracter\xedstica el no flotar superficialmente (sino sumergirse firmemente en el objeto). Su funci\xf3n es la ausencia de confusi\xf3n u olvido. Se manifiesta como protecci\xf3n de la mente o como el estado de estar orientado hacia el objeto. Tiene como causa pr\xf3xima una percepci\xf3n firme o los fundamentos de la atenci\xf3n plena (satipa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na) como el cuerpo. Debe entenderse como un poste firme debido a su estabilidad en el objeto, y como un portero por su labor de proteger las puertas de los sentidos."}},{id:"vism-14.16",pali:"Tattha ya\u1e43ki\xf1c\u012bti anavasesapariy\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43. R\u016bpanti atippasa\u1e45ganiyamana\u1e43. Eva\u1e43 padadvayen\u0101pi r\u016bpassa anavasesapariggaho kato hoti. Athassa at\u012bt\u0101din\u0101 vibh\u0101ga\u1e43 \u0101rabhati. Ta\xf1hi ki\xf1ci at\u012bta\u1e43, ki\xf1ci an\u0101gat\u0101dibhedanti. Esa nayo vedan\u0101d\u012bsu.",translations:{en:"Herein, 'whatever' signifies exhaustive inclusion. 'Form' is a restriction to prevent over-extension. Thus by these two terms an exhaustive comprehension of form is effected. Then its division by way of past, etc., is undertaken. For some of it is past, and some is of the division of future, etc. This is the method for feeling and the other aggregates.",pt:"Ali, 'qualquer que seja' (ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci) \xe9 uma express\xe3o que abrange tudo sem exce\xe7\xe3o. 'Forma' (r\u016bpa) \xe9 uma palavra que restringe a extens\xe3o excessiva. Assim, por meio de ambas as palavras juntas, realiza-se a inclus\xe3o completa da forma, sem restar nada. Em seguida, inicia-se a sua divis\xe3o em passado, etc. Pois parte dela \xe9 passada, parte tem a divis\xe3o de futura, etc. Este mesmo m\xe9todo aplica-se \xe0 sensa\xe7\xe3o, etc.",es:"En ese pasaje, la expresi\xf3n 'cualquier' (ya\u1e43 ki\xf1ci) indica una inclusi\xf3n total sin excepci\xf3n. La palabra 'forma' (r\u016bpa) sirve para delimitar el significado y evitar una extensi\xf3n excesiva a otros fealidades. As\xed, mediante la combinaci\xf3n de estas dos palabras, se realiza la aprehensi\xf3n completa de la forma sin residuo. Luego, comienza la divisi\xf3n de dicha forma por el pasado y otros tiempos. Pues esa forma es en parte pasada, en parte futura, y as\xed sucesivamente. Este mismo m\xe9todo debe aplicarse a la sensaci\xf3n y a los dem\xe1s agregados."}},{id:"vism-14.17",pali:"Tattha kamatoti idha uppattikkamo, pah\u0101nakkamo, pa\u1e6dipattikkamo, bh\u016bmikkamo, desan\u0101kkamoti bahuvidho kamo.",translations:{en:"Here, as to 'by sequence,' this means sequence of arising, sequence of abandoning, sequence of practice, sequence of planes, and sequence of teaching; thus, sequence is of many kinds.",pt:"Nisso, 'por meio da ordem' significa que aqui a ordem \xe9 de muitos tipos: ordem de surgimento, ordem de abandono, ordem de pr\xe1tica, ordem de planos e ordem de ensinamento.",es:"En este contexto, en cuanto al \xaborden\xbb (kama), existen diversos tipos de orden: el orden de surgimiento, el orden de abandono, el orden de pr\xe1ctica, el orden de los planos de existencia y el orden de la ense\xf1anza."}},{id:"vism-14.18",pali:"Upam\u0101toti ettha hi gil\u0101nas\u0101lupamo r\u016bpup\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho, gil\u0101nupamassa vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47up\u0101d\u0101nakkhandhassa vatthudv\u0101r\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena niv\u0101sa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nato. Gela\xf1\xf1upamo vedanup\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho, \u0101b\u0101dhakatt\u0101. Gela\xf1\xf1asamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nupamo sa\xf1\xf1up\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho, k\u0101masa\xf1\xf1\u0101divasena r\u0101g\u0101disampayuttavedan\u0101sabbh\u0101v\u0101. Asapp\u0101yasevanupamo sa\u1e45kh\u0101rup\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho, vedan\u0101gela\xf1\xf1assa nid\u0101natt\u0101. \u2018\u2018Vedana\u1e43 vedanatth\u0101ya abhisa\u1e45kharont\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (sa\u1e43. ni. 3.79) hi vutta\u1e43. Tath\u0101 \u2018\u2018akusalassa kammassa katatt\u0101 upacitatt\u0101 vip\u0101ka\u1e43 k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 uppanna\u1e43 hoti dukkhasahagata\u2019\u2019nti (dha. sa. 556). Gil\u0101nupamo vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47up\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho, vedan\u0101gela\xf1\xf1ena aparimuttatt\u0101. Apica c\u0101rakak\u0101ra\u1e47aapar\u0101dhak\u0101ra\u1e47ak\u0101rakaapar\u0101dhikupam\u0101 ete bh\u0101janabhojanabya\xf1janaparivesakabhu\xf1jak\u016bpam\u0101 c\u0101ti eva\u1e43 upam\u0101to vinicchayanayo vi\xf1\xf1\u0101tabbo.",translations:{en:"As to 'by simile': Here the aggregate of clinging to material form is like a sick-hall, because it is the dwelling place\u2014by way of physical basis, door, and object\u2014for the aggregate of clinging to consciousness, which is like a sick person. The aggregate of clinging to feeling is like the illness, because it is an affliction. The aggregate of clinging to perception is like the cause of the illness, because of the existence of feeling connected with lust, etc., by way of sensual perception, etc. The aggregate of clinging to formations is like the partaking of what is unsuitable, because it is the source of the illness of feeling. For it is said: \u201cThey generate formations for the purpose of feeling\u201d (SN 22.81). And similarly: \u201cBecause of unwholesome kamma that has been done and accumulated, resultant body-consciousness accompanied by pain arises\u201d (Dhs \xa7556). The aggregate of clinging to consciousness is like the sick person, because it is not freed from the illness of feeling. Moreover, these are like the prison, the torture, the crime, the torturer, and the criminal; and like the bowl, the food, the curry, the server, and the eater. Thus the method of determination by way of simile should be understood.",pt:"Quanto a 'por meio de met\xe1foras' (upam\u0101to): aqui, o agregado da mat\xe9ria sujeito ao apego \xe9 semelhante a um hospital, pois serve como local de resid\xeancia, por meio das bases, portas e objetos, para o agregado da consci\xeancia sujeito ao apego, que \xe9 semelhante a um doente. O agregado da sensa\xe7\xe3o sujeito ao apego \xe9 semelhante \xe0 doen\xe7a, devido \xe0 sua natureza aflitiva. O agregado da percep\xe7\xe3o sujeito ao apego \xe9 semelhante \xe0 causa da doen\xe7a, pois, por meio da percep\xe7\xe3o sensual e de outras percep\xe7\xf5es, d\xe1 origem a sensa\xe7\xf5es associadas \xe0 cobi\xe7a e a outras afli\xe7\xf5es. O agregado das forma\xe7\xf5es mentais sujeito ao apego \xe9 semelhante ao consumo de coisas inadequadas, pois \xe9 a causa prim\xe1ria da doen\xe7a da sensa\xe7\xe3o. Pois foi dito: 'Eles condicionam a sensa\xe7\xe3o para o prop\xf3sito de produzir sensa\xe7\xe3o'. E tamb\xe9m: 'Devido \xe0 realiza\xe7\xe3o e ao ac\xfamulo de a\xe7\xf5es prejudiciais, surge a consci\xeancia corporal resultante, acompanhada de dor'. O agregado da consci\xeancia sujeito ao apego \xe9 semelhante ao doente, pois n\xe3o est\xe1 livre da doen\xe7a da sensa\xe7\xe3o. Al\xe9m disso, estes agregados s\xe3o semelhantes, respectivamente, a uma pris\xe3o, \xe0 puni\xe7\xe3o, ao crime, ao carrasco e ao criminoso; e tamb\xe9m s\xe3o semelhantes a um prato, ao alimento, ao condimento, ao servidor e ao comedor. Assim deve ser compreendido o m\xe9todo de determina\xe7\xe3o por meio de met\xe1foras.",es:"En cuanto a 'por medio de comparaciones': el agregado de la materia afectado por el apego es como un hospital, ya que es el lugar de residencia para el agregado de la conciencia (que es como un enfermo) a trav\xe9s de las bases de los sentidos y sus objetos. El agregado de la sensaci\xf3n es como una enfermedad, debido a su naturaleza aflictiva. El agregado de la percepci\xf3n es como el origen o la causa de la enfermedad, pues mediante la percepci\xf3n de los deseos sensoriales y dem\xe1s, surgen sensaciones asociadas con la pasi\xf3n y otros estados. El agregado de las formaciones es como el consumo de lo que no es saludable, por ser la causa ra\xedz de la enfermedad de la sensaci\xf3n. Como se ha dicho: 'Ellos producen la sensaci\xf3n con el prop\xf3sito de la sensaci\xf3n'. Asimismo: 'Debido a que el kamma insalubre ha sido realizado y acumulado, surge la conciencia corporal resultante acompa\xf1ada de dolor'. El agregado de la conciencia es como el enfermo, por no estar libre de la enfermedad de la sensaci\xf3n. Adem\xe1s, se debe conocer el m\xe9todo de determinaci\xf3n mediante comparaciones como una prisi\xf3n, el castigo, el delito, el ejecutor del castigo y el delincuente; y tambi\xe9n como el plato, la comida, el condimento, el que sirve y el comensal."}}]},432,[]);
__d(function(e,a,o,n,s,t,i){s.exports=[{id:"vism-15.1",pali:"\u0100yatan\u0101n\u012bti dv\u0101das\u0101yatan\u0101ni \u2013 cakkh\u0101yatana\u1e43, r\u016bp\u0101yatana\u1e43, sot\u0101yatana\u1e43, sadd\u0101yatana\u1e43, gh\u0101n\u0101yatana\u1e43, gandh\u0101yatana\u1e43, jivh\u0101yatana\u1e43, ras\u0101yatana\u1e43, k\u0101y\u0101yatana\u1e43, pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101yatana\u1e43, man\u0101yatana\u1e43, dhamm\u0101yatananti.",translations:{en:"\u201cBases\u201d means the twelve bases: the eye-base, form-base, ear-base, sound-base, nose-base, odor-base, tongue-base, taste-base, body-base, tangible-base, mind-base, and mental-object base.",pt:"As bases (\u0101yatan\u0101ni) s\xe3o as doze bases: a base do olho (cakkh\u0101yatana), a base da forma (r\u016bp\u0101yatana), a base do ouvido (sot\u0101yatana), a base do som (sadd\u0101yatana), a base do nariz (gh\u0101n\u0101yatana), a base do odor (gandh\u0101yatana), a base da l\xedngua (jivh\u0101yatana), a base do sabor (ras\u0101yatana), a base do corpo (k\u0101y\u0101yatana), a base do tang\xedvel (pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101yatana), a base da mente (man\u0101yatana) e a base dos objetos mentais (dhamm\u0101yatana).",es:"Respecto a 'las bases': son doce bases: la base del ojo, la base de la forma, la base del o\xeddo, la base del sonido, la base de la nariz, la base del olor, la base de la lengua, la base del sabor, la base del cuerpo, la base de lo tangible, la base de la mente y la base de los objetos mentales."}},{id:"vism-15.2",pali:"Tattha visesato t\u0101va cakkhat\u012bti cakkhu, r\u016bpa\u1e43 ass\u0101deti vibh\u0101veti c\u0101ti attho. R\u016bpayat\u012bti r\u016bpa\u1e43, va\u1e47\u1e47avik\u0101ra\u1e43 \u0101pajjanto cakkhussa gocara\u1e43 hot\u012bti attho. Su\u1e47\u0101t\u012bti sota\u1e43. Sappat\u012bti saddo. Gh\u0101yat\u012bti gh\u0101na\u1e43. Gandhayat\u012bti gandho. J\u012bvita\u1e43 avh\u0101t\u012bti jivh\u0101. Rasat\u012bti raso. Kucchit\u0101na\u1e43 kes\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 \u0101yo pavattidesoti k\u0101yo. Phus\u012byat\u012bti pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43. Manat\u012bti mano. Dh\u0101rent\u012bti dhamm\u0101.",translations:{en:"Therein, specifically: It sees (cakkhati), thus it is the eye (cakkhu); the meaning is that it relishes and reveals form. It changes appearance (r\u016bpayati), thus it is form (r\u016bpa); the meaning is that, undergoing alterations of color, it becomes the range of the eye. It hears (su\u1e47\u0101ti), thus it is the ear (sota). It sounds (sappati), thus it is sound (sadda). It smells (gh\u0101yati), thus it is the nose (gh\u0101na). It smells (gandhayati), thus it is odor (gandha). It invokes life (j\u012bvita\u1e43 avh\u0101ti), thus it is the tongue (jivh\u0101). It tastes (rasati), thus it is taste (rasa). The origin or place of occurrence of loathsome things like hairs and so forth is the body (k\u0101ya). It is touched (phus\u012byati), thus it is tangible (pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba). It cognizes (manati), thus it is the mind (mano). They preserve their own nature (dh\u0101renti), thus they are mental objects (dhamm\u0101).",pt:"Nesse sentido, de modo espec\xedfico: O olho \xe9 chamado de cakkhu porque 'v\xea' (cakkhati), no sentido de que percebe e desfruta da forma e a manifesta. A forma \xe9 chamada de r\u016bpa porque 'manifesta forma' (r\u016bpayati), significando que, sofrendo varia\xe7\xf5es de cor, torna-se o objeto do olho. O ouvido \xe9 chamado de sota porque 'ouve' (su\u1e47\u0101ti). O som \xe9 chamado de sadda porque 'se faz ouvir' (sappati). O nariz \xe9 chamado de gh\u0101na porque 'cheira' (gh\u0101yati). O odor \xe9 chamado de gandha porque 'emite cheiro' (gandhayati). A l\xedngua \xe9 chamada de jivh\u0101 porque 'chama a vida' (j\u012bvita\u1e43 avh\u0101ti). O sabor \xe9 chamado de rasa porque 'tem gosto' (rasati). O corpo \xe9 chamado de k\u0101ya porque \xe9 o 'lugar de origem' (\u0101yo) de coisas impuras, como cabelos e outros. O tang\xedvel \xe9 chamado de pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba porque '\xe9 tocado' (phus\u012byati). A mente \xe9 chamada de mano porque 'pensa' ou 'compreende' (manati). Os fen\xf4menos mentais s\xe3o chamados de dhamm\u0101 porque 'sustentam' (dh\u0101renti) a sua pr\xf3pria natureza.",es:"All\xed, en particular, se llama ojo (cakkhu) porque ve (cakkhati); el significado es que saborea y manifiesta la forma. Se llama forma (r\u016bpa) porque muestra apariencia (r\u016bpayati); el significado es que, al sufrir alteraciones de color, se convierte en el campo del ojo. Se llama o\xeddo (sota) porque oye (su\u1e47\u0101ti). Se llama sonido (sadda) porque se emite o suena (sappati). Se llama nariz (gh\u0101na) porque huele (gh\u0101yati). Se llama olor (gandha) porque difunde fragancia (gandhayati). Se llama lengua (jivh\u0101) porque convoca la vida (j\u012bvita\u1e43 avh\u0101ti). Se llama sabor (rasa) porque es saboreado (rasati). Se llama cuerpo (k\u0101ya) porque es el lugar de concurrencia o residencia (\u0101yo) de cosas repugnantes como cabellos, etc. Se llama tangible (pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba) porque es tocado (phus\u012byati). Se llama mente (mano) porque piensa o discierne (manati). Se llaman objetos mentales (dhamm\u0101) porque sostienen o mantienen (dh\u0101renti) su propia naturaleza espec\xedfica."}},{id:"vism-15.3",pali:"Avisesato pana \u0101yatanato, \u0101y\u0101na\u1e43 tananato, \u0101yatassa ca nayanato \u0101yatananti veditabba\u1e43. Cakkh\u0101d\u012bni hi manodh\u0101tu\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 uppattidesatt\u0101 sayampi \u0101yatan\u0101ni honti. Cittacetasik\u0101 pana tattha \u0101yanti, ettha v\u0101 te \u0101yanti, etehi v\u0101 \u0101yant\u012bti \u0101yo. Tassa \u0101yassa tananato pavattanato vitth\u0101ranatopi \u0101yatana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"In general, however, it should be known as a base (\u0101yatana) because of: extending (\u0101yatanato), expanding that which extends (\u0101y\u0101na\u1e43 tananato), and leading what has extended (\u0101yatassa ca nayanato). For the eye and the rest are themselves bases because they are the place of origin for the mind-element, etc. Moreover, 'range' or 'income' (\u0101ya) is that in which, or from which, or by means of which, consciousness and mental factors arise; because of extending, continuing, and expanding that range, it is called a 'base' (\u0101yatana).",pt:"Em geral, no entanto, deve ser entendido como base (\u0101yatana) por sua fun\xe7\xe3o de estender (\u0101yatanato), por expandir aquilo que se estende (\u0101y\u0101na\u1e43 tananato) e por conduzir o que foi estendido (\u0101yatassa ca nayanato). Pois o olho e as outras faculdades s\xe3o eles mesmos bases porque s\xe3o o local de origem do elemento mental, etc. Al\xe9m disso, 'entrada' ou 'alcance' (\u0101ya) \xe9 aquilo onde, ou de onde, ou por meio do qual a mente e os fatores mentais surgem; e por estender, continuar e expandir esse alcance, \xe9 chamado de 'base' (\u0101yatana).",es:"De manera general, debe entenderse como base (\u0101yatana) por extender (\u0101yatanato), por desplegar lo que se extiende (\u0101y\u0101na\u1e43 tananato) y por guiar lo extendido (\u0101yatassa ca nayanato). Pues el ojo y los dem\xe1s son ellos mismos bases porque son el lugar de origen del elemento de la mente, etc. Adem\xe1s, se llama 'ingreso' (\u0101ya) a aquello en lo cual, desde lo cual o mediante lo cual surgen la mente y los factores mentales; y por desplegar, prolongar y expandir ese ingreso, se llama 'base' (\u0101yatana)."}},{id:"vism-15.4",pali:"Apica niv\u0101sa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e6d\u1e6dhena \u0101kara\u1e6d\u1e6dhena samosara\u1e47a\u1e6d\u1e6dhena sa\xf1j\u0101tidesa\u1e6d\u1e6dhena k\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e6d\u1e6dhena ca \u0101yatananti veditabba\u1e43. Yath\u0101 hi \u2018\u2018issar\u0101yatana\u1e43, v\u0101sudev\u0101yatana\u2019\u2019nti\u0101disu niv\u0101sa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101yatananti vuccati. \u2018\u2018Suva\u1e47\u1e47\u0101yatana\u1e43, rajat\u0101yatana\u2019\u2019nti\u0101disu \u0101karoti. \u2018\u2018K\u0101y\u0101yatan\u0101disu pana cittacetasik\u0101na\u1e43 niv\u0101sa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nat\u0101 \u0101karat\u0101 samosara\u1e47at\u0101 sa\xf1j\u0101tidesat\u0101 k\u0101ra\u1e47at\u0101 ca yath\u0101yoga\u1e43 veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, it should be understood as a base (\u0101yatana) in the sense of a dwelling place, a mine, a place of meeting, a birthplace, and a cause. For just as in such phrases as 'the abode of the Lord' or 'the abode of V\u0101sudeva,' a dwelling place is called an \u0101yatana; and in such phrases as 'a gold mine' or 'a silver mine,' a mine is called an \u0101yatana; even so, in the case of the eye-base and so on, their being a dwelling place, a mine, a meeting place, a birthplace, and a cause for consciousness and mental factors should be understood appropriately.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, 'base' deve ser entendida no sentido de local de moradia, no sentido de mina (fonte), no sentido de local de reuni\xe3o, no sentido de local de nascimento e no sentido de causa. Pois, assim como em express\xf5es como 'morada do Senhor' ou 'morada de V\u0101sudeva', o local de habita\xe7\xe3o \xe9 chamado de \u0101yatana; e em express\xf5es como 'mina de ouro' ou 'mina de prata', a mina \xe9 chamada de \u0101yatana; da mesma forma, no olho e nas outras bases, sua fun\xe7\xe3o como morada, mina, local de encontro, local de nascimento e causa para a mente e os fatores mentais deve ser compreendida conforme o caso.",es:"Adem\xe1s, debe entenderse como base (\u0101yatana) en el sentido de morada, en el sentido de mina (yacimiento), en el sentido de punto de encuentro, en el sentido de lugar de nacimiento y en el sentido de causa. As\xed como en frases como 'la morada del Se\xf1or' o 'la morada de V\u0101sudeva' se llama \u0101yatana a una morada; y en frases como 'mina de oro' o 'mina de plata' se llama \u0101yatana a una mina; de la misma manera, en el caso de la base del ojo y dem\xe1s, debe entenderse adecuadamente su condici\xf3n de morada, mina, lugar de encuentro, lugar de nacimiento y causa para la mente y los factores mentales."}},{id:"vism-15.5",pali:"Lakkha\u1e47\u0101ti cakkh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 lakkha\u1e47atopettha vi\xf1\xf1\u0101tabbo vinicchayo. T\u0101ni panet\u0101ni khandhaniddese vutt\u0101nur\u016bp\u0101neva. Tattha hi cakkh\u0101yatan\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 t\u0101va pas\u0101dalakkha\u1e47at\u0101, r\u016bp\u0101yatan\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 gocarasabh\u0101vat\u0101, man\u0101yatanassa vij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47at\u0101, dhamm\u0101yatanassa khandhattay\u0101dibh\u0101vo ca vuttoti na puna vitth\u0101riyati.",translations:{en:"\u201cIn terms of characteristics\u201d: The determination here should also be understood in terms of the characteristics of the eye and so on. These are just as stated in the Exposition of the Aggregates. For there, the nature of the eye-base, etc., as sensitive matter, the nature of the form-base, etc., as their objective fields, the nature of the mind-base as cognizing, and the nature of the mental-object base as the three mental aggregates, etc., were already stated; therefore, it is not elaborated again here.",pt:"Quanto \xe0s caracter\xedsticas (lakkha\u1e47\u0101): a determina\xe7\xe3o aqui tamb\xe9m deve ser compreendida com base nas caracter\xedsticas do olho, etc. Estas correspondem exatamente ao que j\xe1 foi explicado na Exposi\xe7\xe3o dos Agregados (Khandhaniddesa). Pois ali, a natureza da base do olho, etc., como mat\xe9ria sens\xedvel l\xedmpida; a natureza da base da forma, etc., como seus campos de objeto; a caracter\xedstica da base mental como cogni\xe7\xe3o; e a natureza da base dos fen\xf4menos como compreendendo os tr\xeas agregados imateriais, etc., j\xe1 foram devidamente explicadas, de modo que n\xe3o precisam ser detalhadas novamente aqui.",es:"\xabPor sus caracter\xedsticas\xbb: la decisi\xf3n aqu\xed tambi\xe9n debe entenderse por las caracter\xedsticas del ojo y los dem\xe1s sentidos. Estas caracter\xedsticas son exactamente iguales a las expuestas en la Explicaci\xf3n de los Agregados (Khandhaniddesa). Pues all\xed ya se declar\xf3 que la base del ojo y las dem\xe1s tienen la naturaleza de materia sensitiva; que la base de la forma y las dem\xe1s tienen la naturaleza de campos u objetos; que la base de la mente tiene la caracter\xedstica de conocer; y que la base de los objetos mentales comprende los tres agregados restantes, etc.; por lo tanto, no se detalla de nuevo."}},{id:"vism-15.6",pali:"Kamatoti idh\u0101pi pubbe vuttesu uppattikkam\u0101d\u012bsu desan\u0101kkamova yujjati. Ajjhattik\u0101na\xf1hi cakkh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 desan\u0101nupubb\u012b hetusampann\u0101na\u1e43 atth\u0101vahabh\u0101vato hoti. B\u0101hir\u0101na\u1e43 pana r\u016bp\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 cakkh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 gocarasabh\u0101vatoti ayamettha desan\u0101kkamo.",translations:{en:"\u201cIn terms of sequence\u201d: here too, among the sequences of arising and so forth stated previously, only the sequence of teaching is appropriate. For the sequential order in the teaching of the internal bases, such as the eye, is because they bring about benefit when endowed with their conditions; and that of the external bases, such as visible forms, is because they are the objective fields of the eye and the rest. This is the sequence of teaching here.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 ordem (kamato): aqui tamb\xe9m, entre as ordens de surgimento e outras explicadas anteriormente, apenas a ordem da instru\xe7\xe3o \xe9 apropriada. Pois a ordem na instru\xe7\xe3o das bases internas, como o olho, deve-se ao fato de que elas trazem benef\xedcios quando dotadas de suas condi\xe7\xf5es; e a das bases externas, como a forma vis\xedvel, deve-se ao fato de serem o campo de objeto do olho e das demais faculdades. Esta \xe9 a ordem da instru\xe7\xe3o neste ponto.",es:"\xabPor el orden\xbb: aqu\xed tambi\xe9n, entre los \xf3rdenes de surgimiento y dem\xe1s explicados anteriormente, solo se aplica el orden de la ense\xf1anza. Pues el orden en la ense\xf1anza de las bases internas, como el ojo, se debe a que conducen al beneficio cuando poseen sus condiciones; y el de las bases externas, como la forma, se debe a que constituyen los campos objetivos del ojo y de los dem\xe1s sentidos. Este es el orden de la ense\xf1anza en este caso."}},{id:"vism-15.7",pali:"Da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbatoti ettha pana sabb\u0101neva sa\u1e45khat\u0101ni \u0101yatan\u0101ni an\u0101gamanato agamanato ca da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101ni. Na hi et\u0101ni pure upp\u0101d\u0101 kuto\xf1ci \u0101gacchanti, na niruddhopettha katthaci gacchanti. Atha kho pure upp\u0101d\u0101 appa\u1e6diladdhasabh\u0101v\u0101ni, pacch\u0101 ca nirodh\u0101 parikkh\u012b\u1e47asabh\u0101v\u0101ni pubbant\u0101parantavivitt\u0101ni avasavattit\u0101ya nir\u012bhakatt\u0101 ca su\xf1\xf1\u0101ni da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"\u201cIn terms of how they should be seen\u201d: Here, all conditioned bases should be seen as not coming from anywhere and not going anywhere. For before their arising, they do not come from anywhere, nor after their cessation do they go anywhere. Rather, before their arising they are devoid of own-nature, and after their cessation their own-nature is completely exhausted; they should be seen as empty of a past and future end, and empty because they are devoid of exertion, not subject to anyone's mastery.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 maneira como devem ser vistas (da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbato): aqui, todas as bases condicionadas devem ser vistas como n\xe3o tendo vindo de lugar algum e como n\xe3o indo para lugar nenhum. Pois antes de seu surgimento elas n\xe3o v\xeam de parte alguma, e ao cessarem n\xe3o v\xe3o para lugar algum. Pelo contr\xe1rio: antes do surgimento, s\xe3o destitu\xeddas de natureza pr\xf3pria, e ap\xf3s a cessa\xe7\xe3o, sua natureza pr\xf3pria esgota-se completamente; devem ser vistas como desprovidas de um come\xe7o e de um fim, e como vazias de controle pessoal por n\xe3o possu\xedrem agente algum.",es:"\xabSeg\xfan c\xf3mo deben ser vistas\xbb: aqu\xed, todas las bases condicionadas deben ser vistas como no viniendo de ninguna parte ni yendo a ninguna parte. Pues antes de su surgimiento no vienen de ning\xfan sitio, ni al cesar van a sitio alguno. M\xe1s bien, antes de su surgimiento carecen de naturaleza propia, y despu\xe9s de su cesaci\xf3n su naturaleza propia queda completamente extinta; deben ser vistas como vac\xedas de un principio y de un fin, y como vac\xedas de un hacedor por no responder al deseo de nadie."}},{id:"vism-15.8",pali:"Tadanantar\u0101 pana dh\u0101tuyoti a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa dh\u0101tuyo \u2013 cakkhudh\u0101tu, r\u016bpadh\u0101tu, cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu; sotadh\u0101tu, saddadh\u0101tu, sotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu; gh\u0101nadh\u0101tu, gandhadh\u0101tu, gh\u0101navi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu; jivh\u0101dh\u0101tu, rasadh\u0101tu, jivh\u0101vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu; k\u0101yadh\u0101tu, pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbadh\u0101tu, k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu; manodh\u0101tu, dhammadh\u0101tu, manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101t\u016bti.",translations:{en:"Immediately after them, \u201celements\u201d means the eighteen elements: the eye element, form element, eye-consciousness element; ear element, sound element, ear-consciousness element; nose element, odor element, nose-consciousness element; tongue element, taste element, tongue-consciousness element; body element, tangible element, body-consciousness element; mind element, mental-object element, and mind-consciousness element.",pt:"Imediatamente a seguir, os 'elementos' (dh\u0101tuyo) referem-se aos dezoito elementos: elemento do olho, elemento das formas, elemento da consci\xeancia visual; elemento do ouvido, elemento dos sons, elemento da consci\xeancia auditiva; elemento do nariz, elemento dos odores, elemento da consci\xeancia olfativa; elemento da l\xedngua, elemento dos sabores, elemento da consci\xeancia gustativa; elemento do corpo, elemento do tang\xedvel, elemento da consci\xeancia corporal; elemento da mente, elemento dos objetos mentais e elemento da consci\xeancia mental.",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s, los 'elementos' son los dieciocho elementos: el elemento ojo, el elemento forma, el elemento conciencia visual; el elemento o\xeddo, el elemento sonido, el elemento conciencia auditiva; el elemento nariz, el elemento olor, el elemento conciencia olfativa; el elemento lengua, el elemento sabor, el elemento conciencia gustativa; el elemento cuerpo, el elemento tangible, el elemento conciencia corporal; el elemento mente, el elemento objetos mentales y el elemento conciencia mental."}},{id:"vism-15.9",pali:"Tattha atthatoti cakkhat\u012bti cakkhu. R\u016bpayat\u012bti r\u016bpa\u1e43. Cakkhussa vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Esa nayo sabbattha. Dh\u0101rent\u012bti dh\u0101tuyo. Attano pana sabh\u0101va\u1e43 dh\u0101rent\u012bti dh\u0101tuyo. Dh\u0101riyanti v\u0101 paccayehi, dh\u012byati v\u0101 etesu sa\u1e43s\u0101radukkha\u1e43, dh\u0101namatta\u1e43 v\u0101 etanti dh\u0101tuyo.",translations:{en:"Therein, as to meaning: It sees, thus it is the eye. It presents a visible appearance, thus it is form. The consciousness of the eye is eye-consciousness. This is the method everywhere. They bear, thus they are elements. That is, they bear their own nature, thus they are elements. Or they are borne by conditions, or the suffering of sa\u1e43s\u0101ra is placed upon them, or they are a mere depositing; thus they are elements.",pt:"Ali, em rela\xe7\xe3o ao significado literal: Porque v\xea, \xe9 chamado de olho. Porque apresenta uma forma vis\xedvel, \xe9 chamado de forma. A consci\xeancia pertencente ao olho \xe9 chamada de consci\xeancia visual. Esse \xe9 o m\xe9todo em todos os casos. Porque 'sustentam' (dh\u0101renti), s\xe3o chamados de elementos (dh\u0101tuyo). Isto \xe9, sustentam a sua pr\xf3pria natureza individual; por isso s\xe3o elementos. Ou s\xe3o sustentados por condi\xe7\xf5es; ou o sofrimento do sa\u1e43s\u0101ra \xe9 depositado sobre eles; ou s\xe3o meros dep\xf3sitos sem subst\xe2ncia duradoura; por isso s\xe3o chamados de elementos.",es:"All\xed, en cuanto al significado literal: porque ve, es ojo. Porque se manifiesta con color y forma, es forma. La conciencia del ojo es la conciencia visual. Este m\xe9todo se aplica a todos los casos. Porque sostienen, son elementos. Es decir, porque sostienen su propia naturaleza individual intr\xednseca, son elementos. O bien, son sostenidos por condiciones, o en ellos se deposita el sufrimiento del sa\u1e43s\u0101ra, o son un mero recept\xe1culo de fen\xf3menos; por eso se llaman elementos."}},{id:"vism-15.10",pali:"Apica yath\u0101 titthiy\u0101na\u1e43 att\u0101 n\u0101ma sabh\u0101vato natthi, na evamet\u0101, et\u0101 pana attano sabh\u0101va\u1e43 dh\u0101rent\u012bti dh\u0101tuyo. Yath\u0101 v\u0101 loke harit\u0101lamanas\u012bl\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 n\u0101n\u0101dh\u0101t\u016bna\u1e43 sam\u016bho dh\u0101t\u016bti vuccati, tath\u0101 et\u0101pi n\u0101nappak\u0101rakassa sa\u1e45khatassa sar\u012bradhammasa\xf1\xf1itassa dukkhassa dh\u0101tuyo n\u0101n\u0101sabh\u0101vadhammasam\u016bhoti dh\u0101tuyo.",translations:{en:"Moreover, just as the 'self' of other sectarian teachers does not exist by own-nature, these are not like that; rather, they bear their own intrinsic nature, thus they are elements. Or just as in the world a collection of various minerals like orpiment and realgar is called an 'element,' so too these are elements of the suffering known as the conditioned bodily phenomena of various kinds, because they are a collection of phenomena with various intrinsic natures; thus they are elements.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, da mesma forma que o suposto 'eu' das outras escolas filos\xf3ficas n\xe3o possui exist\xeancia real por natureza pr\xf3pria, os elementos n\xe3o s\xe3o ilus\xf3rios dessa maneira: eles sustentam a sua pr\xf3pria ess\xeancia individual; por isso s\xe3o elementos. Ou como no mundo uma reuni\xe3o de diversos min\xe9rios, como o orpimento e o realgar, \xe9 chamada de 'elemento', da mesma forma estes s\xe3o os elementos daquele sofrimento complexo composto de m\xfaltiplas naturezas intr\xednsecas, conhecido sob a designa\xe7\xe3o de fen\xf4menos corporais e mentais condicionados.",es:"Adem\xe1s, as\xed como el supuesto 'yo' de los maestros de otras doctrinas no existe por naturaleza propia, estos elementos no son irreales de esa manera; por el contrario, sustentan su propia naturaleza individual y por eso se llaman elementos. O como en el mundo una colecci\xf3n de diversos minerales como el oropimente y el rejalgar se denomina 'elemento', de igual modo estos son los elementos de ese sufrimiento m\xfaltiple llamado fen\xf3menos corporales y mentales condicionados, por constituir una colecci\xf3n de fen\xf3menos dotados de diversas naturalezas intr\xednsecas."}},{id:"vism-15.11",pali:"Lakkha\u1e47\u0101ditoti cakkh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 lakkha\u1e47\u0101ditopettha veditabbo vinicchayo. Tatth\u0101pi cakkhussa pas\u0101dalakkha\u1e47at\u0101 vuttanayeneva veditabb\u0101. Tath\u0101 r\u016bpassa gocarasabh\u0101vat\u0101, cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47assa vij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47at\u0101. Sot\u0101d\u012bsupi eseva nayo. Manodh\u0101tu pana \u0101vajjanasampa\u1e6dicchanalakkha\u1e47\u0101, dhammadh\u0101tu khandhattay\u0101dibh\u0101v\u0101, manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu sant\u012bra\u1e47\u0101divij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47\u0101ti eva\u1e43 sabb\u0101sampi lakkha\u1e47\u0101divibh\u0101go veditabbo.",translations:{en:"\u201cIn terms of characteristics, etc.\u201d: Here the determination should be understood by way of the characteristics, etc., of the eye and the rest. There too, the eye's characteristic of sensitivity should be understood in the manner already stated. Likewise, the form's nature as objective field, and the eye-consciousness's characteristic of cognizing. This is the method for the ear and the rest as well. The mind-element has the characteristic of adverting and receiving; the mental-object element consists of the three mental aggregates, etc.; and the mind-consciousness element has the characteristic of cognizing by way of investigating, determining, and so forth. Thus the division by way of characteristics, etc., of all of them should be understood.",pt:"Quanto \xe0s caracter\xedsticas e outros aspectos (lakkha\u1e47\u0101dito): a decis\xe3o aqui tamb\xe9m deve ser compreendida atrav\xe9s das caracter\xedsticas, etc., do olho e dos demais. Neles tamb\xe9m, a caracter\xedstica do olho como sensibilidade l\xedmpida deve ser entendida do modo j\xe1 explicado. Da mesma forma, a natureza da forma como campo objetivo e a caracter\xedstica da consci\xeancia visual como cogni\xe7\xe3o. O mesmo m\xe9todo se aplica ao ouvido e demais faculdades. O elemento da mente tem como caracter\xedstica advertir e receber os est\xedmulos; o elemento dos objetos mentais abrange os tr\xeas agregados imateriais e outros fen\xf4menos; e o elemento da consci\xeancia mental tem a caracter\xedstica de cogni\xe7\xe3o sob as modalidades de investigar, decidir, etc. Assim deve ser compreendida a classifica\xe7\xe3o por caracter\xedsticas de todos os elementos.",es:"\xabPor sus caracter\xedsticas y propiedades\xbb: aqu\xed tambi\xe9n debe entenderse la determinaci\xf3n por medio de las caracter\xedsticas del ojo y los dem\xe1s elementos. En este punto, la caracter\xedstica de sensibilidad pura del ojo debe entenderse en la forma ya dicha. Del mismo modo, la naturaleza de objeto visible de la forma y la caracter\xedstica de cognici\xf3n de la conciencia visual. Este mismo m\xe9todo rige para el o\xeddo y dem\xe1s sentidos. El elemento de la mente tiene la caracter\xedstica de advertencia y recepci\xf3n; el elemento de los objetos mentales comprende los tres agregados mentales y otros fen\xf3menos; y el elemento de la conciencia mental tiene la caracter\xedstica de cognici\xf3n mediante la investigaci\xf3n, determinaci\xf3n y dem\xe1s funciones. As\xed debe entenderse la distin\xe7\xe3o de todos ellos por sus caracter\xedsticas."}},{id:"vism-15.12",pali:"Sattarasa dh\u0101tuyo dhammadh\u0101tuekadeso ca sa\u1e45khatadh\u0101tu, asa\u1e45khat\u0101 pana dh\u0101tu dhammadh\u0101tuekadesova. Sa\u1e45khatadh\u0101tu hi hetupaccayasa\u1e45gaten\u0101pi sa\u1e45kh\u0101rena sa\u1e45khatatt\u0101 sa\u1e45khat\u0101. Nibb\u0101nadh\u0101tu pana na kehici paccayehi sa\u1e45khat\u0101, tasm\u0101 asa\u1e45khatadh\u0101t\u016bti vuccati.",translations:{en:"Seventeen elements and a portion of the mental-object element are the conditioned element; but the unconditioned element is just a portion of the mental-object element. For the conditioned element is conditioned because it has been constructed by formations brought together by causes and conditions. But the element of Nibb\u0101na is not constructed by any conditions whatsoever; therefore, it is called the unconditioned element.",pt:"Dezessete elementos e uma parte do elemento dos objetos mentais constituem o elemento condicionado (sa\u1e45khatadh\u0101tu); mas o elemento incondicionado (asa\u1e45khatadh\u0101tu) \xe9 exclusivamente uma por\xe7\xe3o do elemento dos objetos mentais. Pois o elemento condicionado \xe9 chamado de condicionado por ser constru\xeddo por forma\xe7\xf5es produzidas pela conjun\xe7\xe3o de causas e condi\xe7\xf5es. Mas o elemento de Nibb\u0101na n\xe3o \xe9 constru\xeddo por nenhuma condi\xe7\xe3o existente; por essa raz\xe3o, ele \xe9 chamado de o elemento incondicionado.",es:"Diecisiete elementos y una porci\xf3n del elemento de los objetos mentales son el elemento condicionado (sa\u1e45khatadh\u0101tu); pero el elemento incondicionado (asa\u1e45khatadh\u0101tu) es \xfanicamente una porci\xf3n del elemento de los objetos mentales. Pues el elemento condicionado se llama as\xed por haber sido elaborado mediante formaciones reunidas por causas y condiciones. Pero el elemento del Nibbana no es elaborado por ninguna condici\xf3n en absoluto; por eso se llama el elemento incondicionado."}},{id:"vism-15.13",pali:"Apica vij\u0101nanasabh\u0101ve vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47e j\u012bvasa\xf1\xf1\u012bna\u1e43 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101sam\u016bhananatthampi a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101raseva dh\u0101tuyo vutt\u0101. Yath\u0101 hi ekena vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47akkhandhena niddis\u012byam\u0101no vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47appabhedo j\u012bvassa ekattag\u0101ha\u1e43 na pajahati, tath\u0101 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47asotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101didh\u0101tubhedena vibh\u0101jiyam\u0101no vividh\u016bp\u0101d\u0101nanimitt\u0101bh\u0101vato su\u1e6d\u1e6dhutara\u1e43 j\u012bvasa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 vinodeti.",translations:{en:"Moreover, the eighteen elements were taught specifically to dismantle the perception of a soul in those who perceive a living entity in consciousness, which has the nature of cognizing. For just as the variety of consciousness, when indicated simply as the single aggregate of consciousness, does not abandon the grasping at the oneness of a soul, so when analyzed into the division of elements as eye-consciousness, ear-consciousness, etc., it thoroughly dispels the perception of a soul due to the absence of a unified basis for clinging.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, os dezoito elementos foram ensinados especificamente para desmantelar a ilus\xe3o de uma alma individual (j\u012bva) naqueles que tomam a consci\xeancia, cuja natureza \xe9 apenas cognizar, como se fosse um ser real. Pois assim como a multiplicidade da consci\xeancia, quando descrita apenas como o \xfanico agregado da consci\xeancia, n\xe3o erradica o apego \xe0 ideia de uma alma una, ao ser dividida na distin\xe7\xe3o de elementos como consci\xeancia visual, consci\xeancia auditiva, etc., dissipa com muito mais efic\xe1cia a ideia de uma entidade pessoal, pela aus\xeancia de qualquer base que sustente essa ilus\xe3o.",es:"Asimismo, los dieciocho elementos fueron ense\xf1ados con el fin expreso de desarticular la percepci\xf3n de un alma o entidad viva (j\u012bva) en aquellos que consideran que la conciencia, cuya naturaleza es simplemente conocer, es un ser permanente. Pues as\xed como la variedad de la conciencia, cuando se presenta \xfanicamente bajo el \xfanico agregado de la conciencia, no logra eliminar el apego a la unidad de un yo, al ser clasificada en la distinci\xf3n de elementos como conciencia visual, conciencia auditiva, etc., disipa de ra\xedz la falsa creencia de un alma, al carecer de un sustento unificado para la apropiaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-15.14",pali:"Paccay\u0101ti ettha ca cakkhudh\u0101tu t\u0101va cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tuy\u0101 vippayuttapaccayena, nissayapaccayena, purej\u0101tapaccayena, atthipaccayena, avigatapacc\u0101yena c\u0101ti pa\xf1cadh\u0101 paccayo hoti. R\u016bpadh\u0101tu pana \u0101ramma\u1e47apaccayena, purej\u0101tapaccayena, atthipaccayena, avigatapaccayen\u0101ti catudh\u0101 paccayo hoti. Esa nayo sotadh\u0101tu\u0101d\u012bsupi.",translations:{en:"\u201cIn terms of conditions\u201d: And herein, the eye-element is a condition for the eye-consciousness element in five ways: as dissociated condition, support condition, prenascence condition, presence condition, and non-disappearance condition. But the form-element is a condition for it in four ways: as object condition, prenascence condition, presence condition, and non-disappearance condition. This is the method for the ear-element and so on as well.",pt:"Quanto \xe0s condi\xe7\xf5es (paccay\u0101): e aqui, o elemento do olho \xe9 uma condi\xe7\xe3o para o elemento da consci\xeancia visual de cinco maneiras: por condi\xe7\xe3o dissociada (vippayutta), condi\xe7\xe3o de suporte (nissaya), condi\xe7\xe3o pr\xe9-nascida (purej\u0101ta), condi\xe7\xe3o de presen\xe7a (atthi) e condi\xe7\xe3o de n\xe3o desaparecimento (avigata). Mas o elemento da forma \xe9 uma condi\xe7\xe3o para ela de quatro maneiras: por condi\xe7\xe3o de objeto (\u0101ramma\u1e47a), condi\xe7\xe3o pr\xe9-nascida, condi\xe7\xe3o de presen\xe7a e condi\xe7\xe3o de n\xe3o desaparecimento. Este \xe9 o m\xe9todo tamb\xe9m para o elemento do ouvido, etc.",es:"\xabPor sus condiciones\xbb: aqu\xed el elemento ojo es condici\xf3n para el elemento conciencia visual de cinco maneras: como condici\xf3n de disociaci\xf3n, como condici\xf3n de apoyo, como condici\xf3n prenacida, como condici\xf3n de presencia y como condici\xf3n de no desaparici\xf3n. Pero el elemento forma es condici\xf3n para \xe9l de cuatro maneras: como condici\xf3n de objeto, como condici\xf3n prenacida, como condici\xf3n de presencia y como condici\xf3n de no desaparici\xf3n. Este mismo m\xe9todo rige tambi\xe9n para el elemento o\xeddo y los dem\xe1s."}},{id:"vism-15.15",pali:"\u2018\u2018Cakkhur\u016bp\u0101lokamanasik\u0101re pa\u1e6dicca uppajjati cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Sotasaddavivaramanasik\u0101re pa\u1e6dicca uppajjati sotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Gh\u0101nagandhav\u0101yumanasik\u0101re pa\u1e6dicca uppajjati gh\u0101navi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Jivh\u0101rasa\u0101pamanasik\u0101re pa\u1e6dicca uppajjati jivh\u0101vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. K\u0101yapho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbapathav\u012bmanasik\u0101re pa\u1e6dicca uppajjati k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Bhava\u1e45gamanadhammamanasik\u0101re pa\u1e6dicca uppajjati manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti.",translations:{en:"\u201cDependent on the eye, forms, light, and attention, eye-consciousness arises. Dependent on the ear, sounds, the aperture, and attention, ear-consciousness arises. Dependent on the nose, odors, air, and attention, nose-consciousness arises. Dependent on the tongue, tastes, the water element, and attention, tongue-consciousness arises. Dependent on the body, tangibles, the earth element, and attention, body-consciousness arises. Dependent on the life-continuum mind, dhammas, and attention, mind-consciousness arises.\u201d",pt:"\u201cDependendo do olho, das formas, da luz e da aten\xe7\xe3o, surge a consci\xeancia visual. Dependendo do ouvido, dos sons, do canal auditivo e da aten\xe7\xe3o, surge a consci\xeancia auditiva. Dependendo do nariz, dos cheiros, do vento e da aten\xe7\xe3o, surge a consci\xeancia olfativa. Dependendo da l\xedngua, dos sabores, da umidade e da aten\xe7\xe3o, surge a consci\xeancia gustativa. Dependendo do corpo, do tang\xedvel, do elemento terra e da aten\xe7\xe3o, surge a consci\xeancia corporal. Dependendo do fluxo vital (mente), dos objetos mentais e da aten\xe7\xe3o, surge a consci\xeancia mental.\u201d",es:"\xabEn dependencia del ojo, de las formas, de la luz y de la atenci\xf3n, surge la conciencia visual. En dependencia del o\xeddo, de los sonidos, del espacio y de la atenci\xf3n, surge la conciencia auditiva. En dependencia de la nariz, de los olores, del aire y de la atenci\xf3n, surge la conciencia olfativa. En dependencia de la lengua, de los sabores, del agua y de la atenci\xf3n, surge la conciencia gustativa. En dependencia del cuerpo, de lo tangible, de la tierra y de la atenci\xf3n, surge la conciencia corporal. En dependencia del coraz\xf3n (base), de los objetos mentales y de la atenci\xf3n, surge la conciencia mental\xbb."}},{id:"vism-15.16",pali:"Da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbatoti da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbatopettha vinicchayo veditabboti attho. Sabb\u0101 eva hi sa\u1e45khatadh\u0101tuyo pubbant\u0101parantavivittato dhuvasubhasukhattabh\u0101vasu\xf1\xf1ato paccay\u0101yattavuttito ca da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"\u201cIn terms of how they should be seen\u201d: this means the analysis here should be understood in terms of how they are to be seen. For all conditioned elements should be seen as devoid of a past end and a future end, as void of permanence, beauty, pleasure, and self, and as having their occurrence dependent on conditions.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 forma como devem ser vistos (da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbato): o significado \xe9 que, neste contexto, a decis\xe3o deve ser compreendida tamb\xe9m de acordo com a forma como devem ser vistos. Pois todos os elementos condicionados devem ser vistos como vazios de um passado e de um futuro, vazios de perman\xeancia, beleza, felicidade e de um eu, e como ocorrendo na depend\xeancia de condi\xe7\xf5es.",es:"\xabComo deben ser vistos\xbb: el significado es que aqu\xed tambi\xe9n debe entenderse la determinaci\xf3n seg\xfan c\xf3mo deben ser vistos. Pues todos los elementos condicionados deben ser vistos como vac\xedos de un pasado y un futuro, vac\xedos de permanencia, belleza, felicidad y un yo, y como procesos dependientes de condiciones."}},{id:"vism-15.17",pali:"Visesato panettha bheritala\u1e43 viya cakkhudh\u0101tu da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101, da\u1e47\u1e0do viya r\u016bpadh\u0101tu, saddo viya cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu. Tath\u0101 \u0101d\u0101satala\u1e43 viya cakkhudh\u0101tu, mukha\u1e43 viya r\u016bpadh\u0101tu, mukhanimitta\u1e43 viya cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu. Atha v\u0101 ucchutil\u0101 viya cakkhudh\u0101tu, yantacakkaya\u1e6d\u1e6dhi viya r\u016bpadh\u0101tu, ucchurasatel\u0101ni viya cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu. Tath\u0101 adhar\u0101ra\u1e47\u012b viya cakkhudh\u0101tu, uttar\u0101ra\u1e47\u012b viya r\u016bpadh\u0101tu, aggi viya cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu. Esa nayo sotadh\u0101tu\u0101d\u012bsu.",translations:{en:"Specifically, herein, the eye-element should be seen as like the surface of a drum, the form-element as like the drumstick, and the eye-consciousness element as like the sound. Similarly, the eye-element is like the surface of a mirror, the form-element as like the face, and the eye-consciousness element as like the reflection of the face. Or, the eye-element is like sugarcane and sesame seeds, the form-element is like the rod of the press, and the eye-consciousness element is like sugarcane juice and sesame oil. Likewise, the eye-element is like the lower fire-stick, the form-element is like the upper fire-stick, and the eye-consciousness element is like the fire. This is the method for the ear-element and so on.",pt:"Especificamente, neste contexto, o elemento do olho deve ser visto como a pele de um tambor, o elemento das formas como a baqueta, e o elemento da consci\xeancia visual como o som. Da mesma forma, o elemento do olho deve ser visto como a superf\xedcie de um espelho, o elemento das formas como o rosto, e o elemento da consci\xeancia visual como o reflexo do rosto. Ou ainda, o elemento do olho como a cana-de-a\xe7\xfacar ou sementes de gergelim, o elemento das formas como a prensa ou o moinho, e o elemento da consci\xeancia visual como o caldo de cana ou o \xf3leo. Da mesma forma, o elemento do olho como a pe\xe7a inferior de madeira para fazer fogo, o elemento das formas como a pe\xe7a superior, e o elemento da consci\xeancia visual como o fogo. Este \xe9 o m\xe9todo para o elemento do ouvido, etc.",es:"Espec\xedficamente, entre estos dieciocho elementos, el elemento ojo debe ser visto como la superficie de un tambor; el elemento forma, como el palillo del tambor; y el elemento conciencia visual, como el sonido. Del mismo modo, el elemento ojo debe verse como la superficie de un espejo; el elemento forma, como el rostro; y el elemento conciencia visual, como el reflejo del rostro. O bien, el elemento ojo es como la ca\xf1a de az\xfacar o las semillas de s\xe9samo; el elemento forma, como la prensa o el molino; y el elemento conciencia visual, como el jugo de la ca\xf1a o el aceite de s\xe9samo. Asimismo, el elemento ojo es como la tabla inferior para encender fuego; el elemento forma, como el madero superior; y el elemento conciencia visual, como el fuego resultante. Este mismo m\xe9todo se aplica al elemento o\xeddo, etc."}},{id:"vism-15.18",pali:"Manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu \u0101ramma\u1e47esu vavatth\u0101n\u0101bh\u0101vato ara\xf1\xf1amakka\u1e6do viya, duddamanato assakha\u1e37u\u1e45ko viya, yatthak\u0101manip\u0101tito veh\u0101sakkhittada\u1e47\u1e0do viya, lobhados\u0101din\u0101nappak\u0101rakilesavesayogato ra\u1e45gana\u1e6do viya da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"The mind-consciousness element should be seen as a forest monkey because it does not stay settled on its objects; as an untamed colt because it is difficult to tame; as a stick thrown into the air because it falls wherever it wants; and as an actor on a stage because it is associated with the guises of various defilements such as greed and hatred.",pt:"O elemento da consci\xeancia mental deve ser visto como um macaco da floresta, por n\xe3o se fixar nos objetos; como um cavalo selvagem, por ser dif\xedcil de domar; como um bast\xe3o lan\xe7ado ao ar, por cair onde quer que seja; e como um ator de teatro, por assumir as formas de v\xe1rios tipos de impurezas mentais, como a gan\xe2ncia, o \xf3dio, etc.",es:"El elemento de conciencia mental debe verse como un mono de la selva por su falta de estabilidad en los objetos; como un caballo salvaje por ser dif\xedcil de domar; como un palo lanzado al aire por caer donde quiere; y como un actor de teatro por su asociaci\xf3n con los diversos disfraces de las impurezas como la codicia, el odio, etc."}}]},433,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,i,n,s,t){n.exports=[{id:"vism-16.1",pali:"Dh\u0101t\u016bna\u1e43 anantara\u1e43 uddi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ni pana indriy\u0101n\u012bti b\u0101v\u012bsatindriy\u0101ni \u2013 cakkhundriya\u1e43, sotindriya\u1e43, gh\u0101nindriya\u1e43, jivhindriya\u1e43, k\u0101yindriya\u1e43, manindriya\u1e43, itthindriya\u1e43, purisindriya\u1e43, j\u012bvitindriya\u1e43, sukhindriya\u1e43, dukkhindriya\u1e43, somanassindriya\u1e43, domanassindriya\u1e43, upekkhindriya\u1e43, saddhindriya\u1e43, v\u012briyindriya\u1e43, satindriya\u1e43, sam\u0101dhindriya\u1e43, pa\xf1\xf1indriya\u1e43, ana\xf1\xf1\u0101ta\xf1\xf1ass\u0101m\u012btindriya\u1e43, a\xf1\xf1indriya\u1e43, a\xf1\xf1\u0101t\u0101vindriyanti.",translations:{en:"Now, the faculties were pointed out immediately after the elements. There are twenty-two faculties: the eye faculty, the ear faculty, the nose faculty, the tongue faculty, the body faculty, the mind faculty, the female sex faculty, the male sex faculty, the life faculty, the bodily pleasure faculty, the bodily pain faculty, the mental joy faculty, the mental grief faculty, the equanimity faculty, the faith faculty, the energy faculty, the mindfulness faculty, the concentration faculty, the wisdom faculty, the faculty 'I shall come to know the unknown,' the faculty of final knowledge, and the faculty of one who has final knowledge.",pt:"Imediatamente ap\xf3s os elementos, as faculdades que foram brevemente indicadas s\xe3o as vinte e duas faculdades: a faculdade do olho (cakkhundriya), a faculdade do ouvido (sotindriya), a faculdade do nariz (gh\u0101nindriya), a faculdade da l\xedngua (jivhindriya), a faculdade do corpo (k\u0101yindriya), a faculdade da mente (manindriya), a faculdade feminina (itthindriya), a faculdade masculina (purisindriya), a faculdade vital (j\u012bvitindriya), a faculdade do prazer f\xedsico (sukhindriya), a faculdade da dor f\xedsica (dukkhindriya), a faculdade da alegria mental (somanassindriya), a faculdade da tristeza mental (domanassindriya), a faculdade da equanimidade (upekkhindriya), a faculdade da f\xe9 (saddhindriya), a faculdade da energia (v\u012briyindriya), a faculdade da aten\xe7\xe3o plena (satindriya), a faculdade da concentra\xe7\xe3o (sam\u0101dhindriya), a faculdade da sabedoria (pa\xf1\xf1indriya), a faculdade 'conhecerei o desconhecido' (ana\xf1\xf1\u0101ta\xf1\xf1ass\u0101m\u012btindriya), a faculdade do conhecimento pleno (a\xf1\xf1indriya) e a faculdade daquele que possui o conhecimento pleno (a\xf1\xf1\u0101t\u0101vindriya).",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s de los elementos, las facultades que fueron mencionadas brevemente son veintid\xf3s facultades: la facultad del ojo, la facultad del o\xeddo, la facultad de la nariz, la facultad de la lengua, la facultad del cuerpo, la facultad de la mente, la facultad de la feminidad, la facultad de la masculinidad, la facultad de la vida, la facultad del placer, la facultad del dolor, la facultad de la alegr\xeda mental, la facultad del pesar mental, la facultad de la ecuanimidad, la facultad de la fe, la facultad de la energ\xeda, la facultad de la atenci\xf3n, la facultad de la concentraci\xf3n, la facultad de la sabidur\xeda, la facultad de 'conocer\xe9 lo no conocido', la facultad del conocimiento directo y la facultad del que posee el conocimiento directo."}},{id:"vism-16.2",pali:"Ko pana nesa\u1e43 indriya\u1e6d\u1e6dho n\u0101m\u0101ti? Indali\u1e45ga\u1e6d\u1e6dho indriya\u1e6d\u1e6dho. Indadesita\u1e6d\u1e6dho indriya\u1e6d\u1e6dho. Indadi\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e6d\u1e6dho indriya\u1e6d\u1e6dho. Indaju\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e6d\u1e6dho indriya\u1e6d\u1e6dho. Indakata\u1e6d\u1e6dho indriya\u1e6d\u1e6dho. So sabbo yath\u0101yoga\u1e43 yojetabbo. Bhagav\u0101 hi samm\u0101sambuddho paramissariyabh\u0101vena indo, kusal\u0101kusalakamma\xf1ca kammassakat\u0101ya. Teneva ca kamm\u0101na\u1e43 parivattana\u1e43 hoti, na a\xf1\xf1esa\u1e43.",translations:{en:"What is the meaning of 'faculty' (indriya) here? The characteristic of the Lord (Indra) is the meaning of faculty. Being taught by the Lord is the meaning of faculty. Being seen by the Lord is the meaning of faculty. Being enjoyed by the Lord is the meaning of faculty. Being created by the Lord is the meaning of faculty. All these should be applied where appropriate. For the Blessed One, the Perfectly Enlightened One, is the Lord on account of his supreme sovereignty, and wholesome and unwholesome kamma is the lord on account of beings being the owners of their kamma. And precisely on that account does the revolution of deeds take place, and not on account of others.",pt:"Qual \xe9, afinal, o significado de 'faculdade' (indriya)? O significado de faculdade \xe9 a caracter\xedstica de um senhor (inda); o significado de faculdade \xe9 o que foi ensinado por um senhor; o significado de faculdade \xe9 o que foi visto por um senhor; o significado de faculdade \xe9 o que foi desfrutado por um senhor; o significado de faculdade \xe9 o que foi criado por um senhor. Todos esses significados devem ser aplicados de acordo com a conveni\xeancia. Pois o Aben\xe7oado, o Perfeitamente Desperto, \xe9 um senhor (inda) em raz\xe3o de sua soberania suprema; e o kamma salutar e insalubre \xe9 o senhor no sentido de os seres serem herdeiros de suas pr\xf3prias a\xe7\xf5es. E \xe9 precisamente por causa disso que a rota\xe7\xe3o das a\xe7\xf5es k\xe1rmicas acontece, e n\xe3o por causa de outros agentes.",es:"\xbfCu\xe1l es el significado de 'facultad' (indriya)? El significado de facultad es la caracter\xedstica de un se\xf1or (inda); el significado de facultad es haber sido ense\xf1ado por un se\xf1or; el significado de facultad es haber sido visto por un se\xf1or; el significado de facultad es haber sido disfrutado por un se\xf1or; el significado de facultad es haber sido hecho por un se\xf1or. Todos estos sentidos deben aplicarse de acuerdo con la pertinencia. Pues el Bienaventurado, el Plenamente Iluminado, es un se\xf1or supremo por su soberan\xeda trascendente; y el kamma sano y perjudicial es tambi\xe9n se\xf1or porque los seres son due\xf1os de sus acciones. Y es precisamente por causa de esto que ocurre la rotaci\xf3n de los actos, y no por otros factores."}},{id:"vism-16.3",pali:"Apica \u0101dhipaccasa\u1e45kh\u0101tena issariya\u1e6d\u1e6dhen\u0101pi et\u0101ni indriy\u0101ni. Cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 hi cakkh\u0101d\u012bsu pavattam\u0101n\u0101na\u1e43 tesa\u1e43 tesa\u1e43 pas\u0101dar\u016bp\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 \u0101dhipacca\u1e43 labbhati. Tasm\u0101 yath\u0101vuttena indassa li\u1e45g\u0101dibh\u0101vena \u0101dhipaccena ca indriyanti veditabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Moreover, these are called faculties also in the sense of sovereignty (issariya), which is designated as predominance (\u0101dhipacca). For the eye and the other transparent organs exercise predominance over the states of eye-consciousness and so forth that occur in them. Therefore, an indriya should be understood as a faculty both through the aforementioned states of being the mark of the Lord, etc., and through predominance.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, essas faculdades s\xe3o assim chamadas tamb\xe9m no sentido de soberania (issariya), que \xe9 definida como preponder\xe2ncia ou dom\xednio (\u0101dhipacca). Pois o olho e as outras bases materiais exercem dom\xednio soberano sobre as consci\xeancias visuais e demais processos que nelas operam. Portanto, deve-se compreender que uma faculdade (indriya) \xe9 assim chamada tanto pela sua condi\xe7\xe3o de marca de um senhor, etc., conforme mencionado anteriormente, quanto pelo seu poder de dom\xednio preponderante.",es:"Asimismo, estas facultades se denominan as\xed tambi\xe9n en el sentido de soberan\xeda (issariya), entendida como predominio directo (\u0101dhipacca). Pues el ojo y las dem\xe1s bases sensoriales ejercen predominio sobre las conciencias visuales y dem\xe1s procesos que operan en ellos. Por lo tanto, debe entenderse que una facultad (indriya) se llama as\xed tanto por su condici\xf3n de marca de un se\xf1or como por su poder de gobierno o soberan\xeda sobre sus respectivos dominios."}},{id:"vism-16.4",pali:"Bhed\u0101bhed\u0101ti j\u012bvitindriyasseva cettha bhedo. Ta\xf1hi r\u016bpaj\u012bvitindriya\u1e43 ar\u016bpaj\u012bvitindriyanti eva\u1e43 duvidha\u1e43 hoti. Ses\u0101ni panettha abhed\u0101neva. Ekeka\u1e43 hi attano sabh\u0101vena abhinnatt\u0101 abhedatveva da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Regarding 'distinction and non-distinction': Herein, distinction applies to the life faculty alone. For that is twofold as the physical life faculty and the mental life faculty. The rest, however, are non-distinct; for each one, being indivisible in its own nature, should be regarded simply as non-distinct.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 'divis\xe3o e n\xe3o divis\xe3o' (bhed\u0101bhed\u0101): aqui, a divis\xe3o aplica-se unicamente \xe0 faculdade da vida (j\u012bvitindriya). Pois esta \xe9 de dois tipos: a faculdade da vida material (r\u016bpaj\u012bvitindriya) e a faculdade da vida imaterial (ar\u016bpaj\u012bvitindriya). As restantes, no entanto, n\xe3o se dividem; pois cada uma deve ser considerada indivis\xedvel por sua pr\xf3pria natureza intr\xednseca.",es:"\xabPor distinci\xf3n y no distinci\xf3n\xbb: aqu\xed la distinci\xf3n se aplica \xfanicamente a la facultad de la vida. Pues esta es de dos clases: la facultad de la vida material y la facultad de la vida inmaterial. Las dem\xe1s, en cambio, no tienen divisi\xf3n; pues cada una, al no estar dividida en su propia naturaleza, debe considerarse como no dividida."}},{id:"vism-16.5",pali:"Kicc\u0101ti ki\u1e43 indriy\u0101na\u1e43 kiccanti ce. Cakkhundriyassa t\u0101va \u2018\u2018cakkh\u0101yatana\u1e43 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tuy\u0101 ta\u1e43sampayuttak\u0101na\xf1ca dhamm\u0101na\u1e43 nissayapaccayena paccayo\u2019\u2019ti (pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na 1.1.424) vacanato cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47uppatti\u0101d\u012bsu pas\u0101dabh\u0101vo kicca\u1e43. Sotaghy\u0101najivh\u0101k\u0101yindriy\u0101nampi eseva nayo.",translations:{en:"Regarding 'functions': If it is asked, 'What is the function of the faculties?'\u2014firstly, for the eye faculty, according to the passage, 'The eye base is a condition by way of support condition for the eye-consciousness element and its associated phenomena' (Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na 1.1.424), its function is clarity in the arising of eye-consciousness and so on. The same method applies to the ear, nose, tongue, and body faculties.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 'fun\xe7\xe3o' (kicc\u0101): se for perguntado: 'Qual \xe9 a fun\xe7\xe3o das faculdades?' \u2014 primeiramente, para a faculdade do olho, de acordo com o texto can\xf4nico que diz: 'A base do olho \xe9 uma condi\xe7\xe3o por meio de suporte para o elemento da consci\xeancia visual e para os fen\xf4menos a ele associados', sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 atuar como sensibilidade clara no surgimento da consci\xeancia visual, etc. O mesmo m\xe9todo se aplica \xe0s faculdades do ouvido, nariz, l\xedngua e corpo.",es:"\xabPor su funci\xf3n\xbb: si se pregunta cu\xe1l es la funci\xf3n de las facultades, en primer lugar, para la facultad del ojo, seg\xfan la ense\xf1anza can\xf3nica: 'La base del ojo es una condici\xf3n de apoyo para el elemento de la conciencia visual y los estados asociados con ella', su funci\xf3n es servir de claridad sensitiva para el surgimiento de la conciencia visual, etc. Este mismo principio se aplica a las facultades del o\xeddo, nariz, lengua y cuerpo."}},{id:"vism-16.6",pali:"Tadanantar\u0101ni pana sacc\u0101n\u012bti catt\u0101ri ariyasacc\u0101ni \u2013 dukkha\u1e43 ariyasacca\u1e43, dukkhasamudayo ariyasacca\u1e43, dukkhanirodho ariyasacca\u1e43, dukkhanirodhag\u0101min\u012b pa\u1e6dipad\u0101 ariyasaccanti.",translations:{en:"Immediately after them, 'the truths' are the four Noble Truths: the Noble Truth of Suffering, the Noble Truth of the Origin of Suffering, the Noble Truth of the Cessation of Suffering, and the Noble Truth of the Path Leading to the Cessation of Suffering.",pt:"Imediatamente depois delas, 'as verdades' s\xe3o as quatro Nobres Verdades: a Nobre Verdade do Sofrimento (dukkha), a Nobre Verdade da Origem do Sofrimento (dukkhasamudaya), a Nobre Verdade da Cessa\xe7\xe3o do Sofrimento (dukkhanirodha) e a Nobre Verdade do Caminho que Conduz \xe0 Cessa\xe7\xe3o do Sofrimento (dukkhanirodhag\u0101min\u012b pa\u1e6dipad\u0101).",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s, 'las verdades' son las cuatro nobles verdades: la noble verdad del sufrimiento, la noble verdad del origen del sufrimiento, la noble verdad del cese del sufrimiento y la noble verdad del sendero que conduce al cese del sufrimiento."}},{id:"vism-16.7",pali:"Tattha vibh\u0101gototi dukkh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 hi catt\u0101ro catt\u0101ro atth\u0101 vibhatt\u0101 tattha tattha bhagavat\u0101. Yath\u0101ha \u2013 \u2018\u2018catt\u0101ro me, bhikkhave, dukkhassa tath\u0101 avitath\u0101 ana\xf1\xf1ath\u0101. Katame catt\u0101ro? P\u012b\u1e37ana\u1e6d\u1e6dho, sa\u1e45khata\u1e6d\u1e6dho, sant\u0101pa\u1e6d\u1e6dho, vipari\u1e47\u0101ma\u1e6d\u1e6dho\u2019\u2019ti (pa\u1e6di. ma. 2.158). Samudayassa pana \u2013 \u2018\u2018\u0101y\u016bhana\u1e6d\u1e6dho, nid\u0101na\u1e6d\u1e6dho, sa\u1e43yoga\u1e6d\u1e6dho, palibodha\u1e6d\u1e6dho\u2019\u2019ti. Nirodhassa \u2013 \u2018\u2018nissara\u1e47a\u1e6d\u1e6dho, paviveka\u1e6d\u1e6dho, asa\u1e45khata\u1e6d\u1e6dho, amata\u1e6d\u1e6dho\u2019\u2019ti. Maggassa \u2013 \u2018\u2018niyy\u0101na\u1e6d\u1e6dho, hetu\u1e6d\u1e6dho, dassana\u1e6d\u1e6dho, adhipateyya\u1e6d\u1e6dho\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"Therein, 'by way of division': The Blessed One divided four aspects each for suffering and the others in various places. As he said: 'Monks, these four aspects of suffering are real, not unreal, not otherwise. Which four? The aspect of oppressing, the aspect of being conditioned, the aspect of burning, and the aspect of changing' (Pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101magga 2.158). For origin: 'The aspect of accumulating, the aspect of source, the aspect of bondage, and the aspect of impediment.' For cessation: 'The aspect of escape, the aspect of seclusion, the aspect of the unconditioned, and the aspect of the deathless.' For the path: 'The aspect of leading out, the aspect of cause, the aspect of seeing, and the aspect of dominance.'",pt:"Ali, 'por meio da divis\xe3o': o Aben\xe7oado dividiu quatro significados para o sofrimento e para os outros fatores em v\xe1rias passagens. Como ele mesmo disse: '\xd3 monges, estes quatro aspectos do sofrimento s\xe3o verdadeiros, n\xe3o ilus\xf3rios, n\xe3o alter\xe1veis. Quais quatro? O aspecto de opress\xe3o, o aspecto de ser condicionado, o aspecto de tormento e o aspecto de transforma\xe7\xe3o cont\xednua'. Para a origem do sofrimento: 'O aspecto de acumula\xe7\xe3o, o aspecto de causa prim\xe1ria, o aspecto de aprisionamento e o aspecto de obst\xe1culo'. Para a cessa\xe7\xe3o: 'O aspecto de escape definitivo, o aspecto de isolamento, o aspecto do incondicionado e o aspecto do imortal'. Para o caminho: 'O aspecto de liberta\xe7\xe3o (conduzir para fora), o aspecto de causa, o aspecto de vis\xe3o e o aspecto de soberania'.",es:"All\xed, 'por su divisi\xf3n': el Bienaventurado clasific\xf3 cuatro aspectos para cada una de las verdades del sufrimiento y las dem\xe1s en diversos lugares. Como dijo: 'Monjes, estos cuatro aspectos del sufrimiento son reales, no falsos, no diferentes. \xbfCu\xe1les cuatro? El aspecto de opresi\xf3n, el aspecto de ser condicionado, el aspecto de quemaz\xf3n o tormento y el aspecto de cambio continuo'. En cuanto al origen: 'El aspecto de acumulaci\xf3n, el aspecto de fuente causal, el aspecto de atadura y el aspecto de impedimento'. En cuanto al cese: 'El aspecto de escape, el aspecto de aislamiento, el aspecto de lo incondicionado y el aspecto de la inmortalidad'. En cuanto al sendero: 'El aspecto de conducir hacia la liberaci\xf3n, el aspecto de causa fundamental, el aspecto de visi\xf3n y el aspecto de supremac\xeda'."}},{id:"vism-16.8",pali:"Nibbacanalakkha\u1e47\u0101dippabhedatoti ettha pana nibbacanato t\u0101va idha du-iti aya\u1e43 saddo kucchiye dissati. Kha-iti aya\u1e43 saddo tucche. Kucchita\u1e43 v\u0101 eta\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 sacca\u1e43 garahitasabbh\u0101vat\u0101, tucchampi nir\u012bhakanissattavuttito. Tasm\u0101 kucchitatt\u0101 tucchatt\u0101 ca dukkhanti vuccati.",translations:{en:"Regarding 'analysis by way of etymology, characteristics, etc.': Herein, firstly, by way of etymology: Here, the prefix 'du' is seen in the sense of vile or contemptible. The word 'kha' is in the sense of empty. And this first truth is vile because it is the state of all things blameworthy, and it is empty because it occurs without an agent or an enduring living being. Therefore, because it is vile and empty, it is called 'dukkha' (suffering).",pt:"Quanto \xe0 'an\xe1lise por meio da etimologia, caracter\xedsticas e outras distin\xe7\xf5es': aqui, primeiramente, pela etimologia: o prefixo 'du-' \xe9 usado no sentido de vil, indigno ou desprez\xedvel. A palavra 'kha' \xe9 usada no sentido de vazio ou oco. Esta primeira verdade \xe9 vil porque abrange tudo o que \xe9 digno de censura pelo seu sofrimento intr\xednseco, e \xe9 vazia porque ocorre sem qualquer agente ou entidade duradoura permanente. Portanto, por ser ao mesmo tempo vil e vazia, \xe9 chamada de 'dukkha' (sofrimento).",es:"En cuanto al 'an\xe1lisis por etimolog\xeda, caracter\xedsticas y dem\xe1s distinciones': en primer lugar, por la etimolog\xeda: el prefijo 'du-' se utiliza en el sentido de vil o despreciable. La palabra 'kha' se emplea en el sentido de vac\xedo. Esta primera verdad es vil por su naturaleza reprochable en el sa\u1e43s\u0101ra, y es vac\xeda porque ocurre sin un hacedor ni un alma permanente. Por lo tanto, por ser vil y vac\xeda, se llama 'dukkha' (sufrimiento)."}},{id:"vism-16.9",pali:"Sa\u1e43-iti ca aya\u1e43 saddo sam\u0101game dissati, u-iti aya\u1e43 uppattismi\u1e43, aya-iti \u0101yasm\u0101 paccaye. Sam\u0101gantv\u0101 uppat\u012bti samudayo. Paccay\u0101 sam\u0101gantv\u0101 dukkhassa uppatti etasm\u0101ti samudayo. Dutiyassa panassa saccassa dukkhupp\u0101dak\u0101ranatt\u0101 samudayoti sacca\u1e6d\u1e6dho.",translations:{en:"And this prefix 'sa\u1e43' is seen in the sense of coming together; 'u' is in the sense of arising; 'aya' is in the sense of condition or source. Coming together, it arises, thus it is 'origin' (samudaya). Conditions having come together, the arising of suffering is from this, thus it is 'samudaya.' Because this second truth is the cause that generates suffering, its meaning as a truth is 'origin' (samudaya).",pt:"O prefixo 'sa\u1e43-' \xe9 empregado no sentido de converg\xeancia ou reuni\xe3o; 'u-' tem o sentido de surgimento ou eleva\xe7\xe3o; e 'aya' tem o sentido de causa, condi\xe7\xe3o ou fonte. Surgindo atrav\xe9s da converg\xeancia de fatores, \xe9 chamada de 'origem' (samudaya). As causas tendo convergido conjuntamente, o surgimento do sofrimento prov\xe9m disto; logo, \xe9 'samudaya'. Porque esta segunda verdade \xe9 a causa produtora do sofrimento, o seu sentido como verdade \xe9 'origem'.",es:"El prefijo 'sa\u1e43-' se usa en el sentido de convergencia o reuni\xf3n; 'u-' se usa en el sentido de surgimiento o aparici\xf3n; 'aya' se usa en el sentido de causa o condici\xf3n. Surgiendo por convergencia, es 'origen' (samudaya). Habi\xe9ndose reunido las causas, el surgimiento del sufrimiento proviene de esto; por tanto, es 'samudaya'. Porque esta segunda verdad es la causa productora del sufrimiento, su sentido como verdad es 'origen'."}},{id:"vism-16.10",pali:"Tatiyasacca\u1e43 pana yasm\u0101 ni-saddo abh\u0101va\u1e43, rodha-saddo ca c\u0101raka\u1e43 sa\u1e43s\u0101rac\u0101rakassa etth\u0101bh\u0101v\u0101ti nirodho. Sabba\u1e43 v\u0101 ta\u1e43 sa\u1e43s\u0101radukkha\u1e43 ettha nirujjhati, na punuppattivasena pavattat\u012bti nirodho. Tasm\u0101 anupp\u0101danirodhasabh\u0101vatt\u0101 nirodhoti vuccati.",translations:{en:"As for the third truth: since the syllable 'ni' signifies absence, and the word 'rodha' signifies a prison, and here there is the absence of the prison of sa\u1e43s\u0101ra, it is 'nirodha' (cessation). Or all that suffering of sa\u1e43s\u0101ra ceases here and does not proceed again by way of renewed existence; therefore it is 'nirodha'. Hence, because its nature is cessation without further arising, it is called 'nirodha'.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 terceira verdade: visto que a s\xedlaba 'ni-' denota aus\xeancia e a palavra 'rodha' denota uma pris\xe3o, e aqui ocorre a aus\xeancia total da pris\xe3o do sa\u1e43s\u0101ra, ela \xe9 'nirodha' (cessa\xe7\xe3o). Ou todo aquele sofrimento do sa\u1e43s\u0101ra cessa plenamente aqui e n\xe3o torna a ocorrer mediante um novo renascimento; logo, \xe9 'nirodha'. Portanto, por ser a natureza da cessa\xe7\xe3o definitiva de todo renascimento, \xe9 chamada de 'nirodha'.",es:"En cuanto a la tercera verdad: dado que la part\xedcula 'ni-' expresa ausencia y la palabra 'rodha' denota una c\xe1rcel, y aqu\xed se encuentra la ausencia de la prisi\xf3n del sa\u1e43s\u0101ra, se llama 'nirodha' (cese). O bien, todo ese sufrimiento del sa\u1e43s\u0101ra cesa aqu\xed y no prosigue mediante un nuevo renacimiento; por eso es 'nirodha'. As\xed, por tener la naturaleza de la cesaci\xf3n sin nuevo surgimiento, se llama 'nirodha'."}},{id:"vism-16.11",pali:"Catutthasacca\u1e43 pana yasm\u0101 eta\u1e43 dukkhanirodha\u1e43 gacchati \u0101ramma\u1e47avasena tadabhimukha\u1e43 y\u0101ti, maggo viya v\u0101 nibb\u0101napura\u1e43 p\u0101pet\u012bti dukkhanirodhag\u0101min\u012b pa\u1e6dipad\u0101 maggotipi vuccati. Magg\u012byati v\u0101 kilese m\u0101rento khemanta\u1e43 p\u0101pet\u012bti maggo.",translations:{en:"As for the fourth truth: because it goes to the cessation of suffering, heading towards it by way of object, or because, like a path, it leads to the city of Nibb\u0101na, it is called the path leading to the cessation of suffering, and also 'the path' (magga). Or it is called a path because it is sought after, or because, slaying the defilements, it leads to security.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 quarta verdade: visto que ela se dirige \xe0 cessa\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento, caminhando ao seu encontro atrav\xe9s de seu objeto sublime, ou porque, semelhante a uma estrada r\xe9gia, conduz \xe0 cidade gloriosa do Nibb\u0101na, ela \xe9 chamada de a pr\xe1tica que conduz \xe0 cessa\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento e tamb\xe9m de 'o caminho' (magga). Ou ainda, \xe9 chamada de caminho porque \xe9 buscada ardentemente por quem deseja a paz, ou porque, aniquilando as impurezas mentais, conduz ao ref\xfagio seguro.",es:"En cuanto a la cuarta verdad: dado que se dirige a la cesaci\xf3n del sufrimiento, marchando hacia ella por medio de su objeto, o porque, al igual que una senda, conduce a la ciudad del Nibbana, se llama pr\xe1ctica que conduce al cese del sufrimiento, y tambi\xe9n 'sendero' (magga). O bien se llama sendero porque es buscado por los sabios, o porque, destruyendo las impurezas, conduce a la seguridad suprema."}},{id:"vism-16.12",pali:"Yasm\u0101 panet\u0101ni buddh\u0101dayo ariy\u0101 pa\u1e6divijjhanti, tasm\u0101 ariyasacc\u0101n\u012bti vuccanti. Ariyassa sacc\u0101n\u012bti v\u0101 ariyasacc\u0101ni. Tath\u0101 heta\u1e43 vutta\u1e43 \u2013 \u2018\u2018catt\u0101rim\u0101ni, bhikkhave, ariyasacc\u0101ni. Katam\u0101ni catt\u0101ri? Dukkha\u1e43 ariyasacca\u1e43\u2026pe\u2026 dukkhanirodhag\u0101min\u012b pa\u1e6dipad\u0101 ariyasacca\u1e43. Im\u0101ni kho, bhikkhave, catt\u0101ri ariyasacc\u0101ni tath\u0101ni avitath\u0101ni ana\xf1\xf1ath\u0101ni, tasm\u0101 ariyasacc\u0101n\u012bti vuccant\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (sa\u1e43. ni. 5.1095).",translations:{en:"Because the Buddhas and other Noble Ones penetrate them, they are called 'Noble Truths.' Or they are the Noble Truths because they are the truths of the Noble One. For this has been said: 'Monks, these four are the Noble Truths. Which four? The Noble Truth of Suffering... the Noble Truth of the Path Leading to the Cessation of Suffering. These four Noble Truths, monks, are real, not unreal, not otherwise; therefore they are called Noble Truths' (SN 56.27).",pt:"Porque os Budas e os outros Nobres Disc\xedpulos as penetram com profunda sabedoria, s\xe3o chamadas de 'Nobres Verdades'. Ou s\xe3o chamadas de Nobres Verdades por serem as verdades pertencentes ao Nobre por excel\xeancia. Pois foi dito: '\xd3 monges, estas quatro s\xe3o as Nobres Verdades. Quais quatro? A Nobre Verdade do Sofrimento... a Nobre Verdade do Caminho que Conduz \xe0 Cessa\xe7\xe3o do Sofrimento. Estas quatro Nobres Verdades, monges, s\xe3o reais, n\xe3o s\xe3o ilus\xf3rias, n\xe3o s\xe3o mut\xe1veis; por isso s\xe3o chamadas de Nobres Verdades'.",es:"Puesto que los Budas y los dem\xe1s Nobles las penetran con sabidur\xeda, se llaman 'Nobles Verdades'. O bien se llaman Nobles Verdades porque son las verdades propias del Noble. Como se dijo: 'Monjes, estas cuatro son las Nobles Verdades. \xbfCu\xe1les cuatro? La noble verdad del sufrimiento... la noble verdad del sendero que conduce al cese del sufrimiento. Estas cuatro nobles verdades, monjes, son reales, no irreales, no diferentes; por lo tanto, se llaman Nobles Verdades'."}},{id:"vism-16.13",pali:"Katha\u1e43 lakkha\u1e47\u0101dippabhedato? Ettha hi b\u0101dhanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 dukkhasacca\u1e43, sant\u0101panarasa\u1e43, pavattipaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43. Pabhavalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 samudayasacca\u1e43, anupacchedarasa\u1e43, palibodhapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43. Santilakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 nirodhasacca\u1e43, accutirasa\u1e43, nimittapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43. Niyy\u0101nalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 maggasacca\u1e43, kilesappah\u0101narasa\u1e43, vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanti.",translations:{en:"How by way of characteristics and so on? Herein, the truth of suffering has the characteristic of oppressing, its function is tormenting, and its manifestation is continuous occurrence. The truth of origin has the characteristic of producing, its function is non-interruption, and its manifestation is impediment. The truth of cessation has the characteristic of peace, its function is not dying, and its manifestation is the unconditioned sign. The truth of the path has the characteristic of leading out, its function is the abandoning of defilements, and its manifestation is emergence.",pt:"Como se dividem por meio de caracter\xedsticas e outros fatores? Aqui, a verdade do sofrimento tem a caracter\xedstica de opress\xe3o constante, sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o tormento e sua manifesta\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a continuidade do ciclo de renascimentos. A verdade da origem tem como caracter\xedstica a produ\xe7\xe3o, sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a n\xe3o interrup\xe7\xe3o da dor e sua manifesta\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o impedimento do progresso espiritual. A verdade da cessa\xe7\xe3o tem a paz como caracter\xedstica, sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a imortalidade inabal\xe1vel e sua manifesta\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a aus\xeancia de sinais condicionados. A verdade do caminho tem a caracter\xedstica de liberta\xe7\xe3o (conduzir para fora), sua fun\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o abandono das impurezas mentais e sua manifesta\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a emerg\xeancia de todas as afli\xe7\xf5es do mundo.",es:"\xbfC\xf3mo se diferencian seg\xfan las caracter\xedsticas y dem\xe1s propiedades? Aqu\xed, la verdad del sufrimiento tiene la caracter\xedstica de oprimir, la funci\xf3n de atormentar y la manifestaci\xf3n de la continuidad del proceso. La verdad del origen tiene la caracter\xedstica de producir, la funci\xf3n de no interrupci\xf3n y la manifestaci\xf3n de ser un obst\xe1culo. La verdad del cese tiene la caracter\xedstica de la paz, la funci\xf3n de la inmortalidad y la manifestaci\xf3n de lo incondicionado. La verdad del camino tiene la caracter\xedstica de liberar, la funci\xf3n de abandonar las aflicciones y la manifestaci\xf3n de salir del sa\u1e43s\u0101ra."}},{id:"vism-16.14",pali:"N\u0101b\u0101dhaka\u1e43 yato dukkha\u1e43, dukkh\u0101 a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 na b\u0101dhaka\u1e43; Bh\u016btassatthassa d\u012bpan\u0101, sacca\u1e43 dukkha\u1e43 tato mata\u1e43. Na c\u0101pabhava\u1e43 samudayo, samuday\u0101 a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 na pabhava\u1e43; Bh\u016btassatthassa d\u012bpan\u0101, sacca\u1e43 samudayo tato mato. N\u0101\xf1\xf1\u0101 nibb\u0101nato santi, santa\u1e43 na ca na ta\u1e43 yato; Tasm\u0101 nirodho nibb\u0101na\u1e43, sacca\u1e43 saccavid\u016b mata\u1e43. Magg\u0101 a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 na niyy\u0101na\u1e43, aniyy\u0101no na c\u0101pi so; Tasm\u0101 maggo ariyasacca\u1e43, bh\u016btassatthassa d\u012bpan\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Since suffering is not non-oppressive, and nothing other than suffering is oppressive, by illuminating the real state of affairs, suffering is known as a truth. Origin is not non-producing, and nothing other than origin produces suffering; by illuminating the real state of affairs, origin is known as a truth. Since there is no peace other than Nibb\u0101na, and that Nibb\u0101na is not non-peaceful; therefore Nibb\u0101na as cessation is known as a truth by knowers of the truth. There is no deliverance other than the Path, and that Path is not non-deliverance; therefore the Path is a Noble Truth, illuminating the real state of affairs.",pt:"Visto que o sofrimento nunca deixa de ser opressivo, e nada al\xe9m do sofrimento \xe9 verdadeiramente opressivo, por revelar a realidade das coisas como elas s\xe3o, o sofrimento \xe9 reconhecido como uma verdade indiscut\xedvel. A origem nunca deixa de produzir sofrimento, e nada al\xe9m dela produz a dor; por iluminar a realidade dos fatos, a origem \xe9 conhecida como uma verdade. Visto que n\xe3o existe outra paz aut\xeantica al\xe9m do Nibb\u0101na, e esse Nibb\u0101na nunca \xe9 destitu\xeddo de paz; por conseguinte, a cessa\xe7\xe3o no Nibb\u0101na \xe9 considerada verdade suprema por aqueles que compreendem a verdade. N\xe3o existe outra liberta\xe7\xe3o al\xe9m do Nobre Caminho, e esse Caminho jamais deixa de libertar; por isso o Caminho \xe9 uma Nobre Verdade, por desvelar a verdade irrefut\xe1vel.",es:"Puesto que el sufrimiento no deja de ser aflictivo, y nada fuera del sufrimiento es aflictivo, por revelar el estado real de las cosas, el sufrimiento es conocido como una verdad. Puesto que el origen no deja de ser causante, y nada fuera del origen produce el sufrimiento, por revelar la verdad de las cosas, el origen se reconoce como una verdad. Dado que no hay otra paz fuera del Nibbana, y ese Nibbana no carece de paz, por eso el cese es tenido por verdad por los conocedores de la verdad. No hay otra liberaci\xf3n fuera del sendero, y ese sendero nunca deja de liberar; por lo tanto, el sendero es una noble verdad que revela la realidad aut\xe9ntica."}},{id:"vism-16.15",pali:"Samudayaniddese pana y\u0101ya\u1e43 ta\u1e47h\u0101 ponobbhavik\u0101 nand\u012br\u0101gasahagat\u0101 tatratatr\u0101bhinandin\u012b, seyyathida\u1e43 \u2013 k\u0101mata\u1e47h\u0101, bhavata\u1e47h\u0101, vibhavata\u1e47h\u0101ti eva\u1e43 samudayasacca\u1e43 vitth\u0101rita\u1e43. S\u0101 cettha ponobbhavik\u0101ti punabbhavajanik\u0101. Nand\u012br\u0101gasahagat\u0101ti nandiy\u0101 ca r\u0101gena ca saddhi\u1e43 ekakkha\u1e47e uppann\u0101. Tatratatr\u0101bhinandin\u012bti tasmi\u1e43 tasmi\u1e43 attabh\u0101ve abhinandan\u0101. K\u0101mata\u1e47h\u0101ti k\u0101m\u0101vacaradhammesu uppannata\u1e47h\u0101. Bhavata\u1e47h\u0101ti sassatadi\u1e6d\u1e6dhisahagato bhavapattik\u0101mat\u0101. Vibhavata\u1e47h\u0101ti ucchedadi\u1e6d\u1e6dhisahagat\u0101 bhavapah\u0101nak\u0101mat\u0101.",translations:{en:"In the Exposition of the Origin, the truth of origin is detailed thus: 'It is this craving that leads to renewed existence, accompanied by delight and lust, finding delight here and there; that is, sensual craving, craving for existence, and craving for non-existence.' Therein, 'leading to renewed existence' means causing rebirth. 'Accompanied by delight and lust' means arisen in a single moment with delight and lust. 'Finding delight here and there' means rejoicing in this or that individuality. 'Sensual craving' is craving that arises for sensuous-realm phenomena. 'Craving for existence' is desire for existence accompanied by the eternalist view. 'Craving for non-existence' is desire for annihilation accompanied by the annihilationist view.",pt:"Na exposi\xe7\xe3o sobre a origem do sofrimento, a verdade da origem \xe9 assim detalhada: '\xc9 este desejo que conduz a novos renascimentos, acompanhado pelo deleite e pela paix\xe3o, encontrando prazer aqui e acol\xe1; a saber: o desejo pelos prazeres sensoriais (k\u0101mata\u1e47h\u0101), o desejo pela continuidade da exist\xeancia (bhavata\u1e47h\u0101) e o desejo pela aniquila\xe7\xe3o da exist\xeancia (vibhavata\u1e47h\u0101)'. Nisto, 'que conduz a novos renascimentos' significa que gera continuamente o ciclo do vir-a-ser. 'Acompanhado pelo deleite e pela paix\xe3o' significa nascido simultaneamente com a complac\xeancia e o apego cego. 'Encontrando prazer aqui e acol\xe1' significa deleitar-se em cada uma das exist\xeancias corporais assumidas. O desejo pelos prazeres sensoriais \xe9 o anseio pelos objetos dos sentidos. O desejo pela exist\xeancia \xe9 o apego \xe0 continuidade acompanhado pela vis\xe3o err\xf4nea do eternalismo. O desejo pela aniquila\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o anseio pela destrui\xe7\xe3o total acompanhado pela vis\xe3o err\xf4nea do aniquilacionismo.",es:"En la explicaci\xf3n del origen, la verdad del origen se detalla as\xed: 'Es esta sed o avidez que conduce a un nuevo renacimiento, acompa\xf1ada de deleite y pasi\xf3n, que encuentra gozo aqu\xed y all\xe1; es decir, el apego a los placeres sensuales, el apego a la existencia y el apego a la no existencia'. En este pasaje, 'que conduce a un nuevo renacimiento' significa que produce nuevas vidas. 'Acompa\xf1ada de deleite y pasi\xf3n' denota que surge junto con el apego gozoso. 'Que encuentra gozo aqu\xed y all\xe1' denota que se complace en cada individualidad asumida. El deseo de placeres sensuales es el anhelo hacia los objetos sensoriales. El deseo de existencia es el anhelo acompa\xf1ado de la creencia en la eternidad del yo. El deseo de no existencia es el anhelo de aniquilaci\xf3n total acompa\xf1ado de la doctrina aniquilacionista."}},{id:"vism-16.16",pali:"Dukkhanirodhaniddese yo tass\u0101yeva ta\u1e47h\u0101ya asesavir\u0101ganirodho c\u0101go pa\u1e6dinissaggo mutti an\u0101layoti aya\u1e43 dukkhanirodhoti eva\u1e43 nirodhasacca\u1e43 vitth\u0101rita\u1e43. Asesavir\u0101ganirodhoti ettha pana vir\u0101go cettha nirodho ca, tasm\u0101 vir\u0101ganirodho. Aseso vir\u0101ganirodho asesavir\u0101ganirodho. C\u0101goti ta\u1e47h\u0101ya vissajjana\u1e43. Pa\u1e6dinissaggoti tass\u0101yeva cat\u016bhi maggehi pa\u1e6dinissajjana\u1e43. Mutt\u012bti ta\u1e47h\u0101bandhan\u0101 muttat\u0101. An\u0101layoti ta\u1e47h\u0101ya \u0101l\u012byanatth\u0101nassa abh\u0101v\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"In the Exposition of the Cessation of Suffering, the truth of cessation is detailed thus: 'It is the remainderless fading away and cessation of that very craving, the giving up, the relinquishment, the release, the non-reliance; this is the cessation of suffering.' Herein, 'remainderless fading away and cessation': it is fading away and it is cessation, hence fading-cessation; remainderless fading-cessation is 'asesavir\u0101ganirodho.' 'Giving up' is the abandoning of craving. 'Relinquishment' is the giving up of craving through the four noble paths. 'Release' is freedom from the bond of craving. 'Non-reliance' is the absence of any resting place for craving.",pt:"Na exposi\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento, a verdade da cessa\xe7\xe3o \xe9 assim detalhada: '\xc9 o desvanecimento e a cessa\xe7\xe3o sem res\xedduos desse mesmo desejo, o seu abandono, a sua ren\xfancia, a liberta\xe7\xe3o e a aus\xeancia de apego a ele; isto \xe9 a cessa\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento'. Ali, 'cessa\xe7\xe3o sem res\xedduos': \xe9 ao mesmo tempo desapego absoluto e cessa\xe7\xe3o definitiva; portanto, \xe9 a cessa\xe7\xe3o pelo desapego desprovida de qualquer res\xedduo. 'Abandono' (c\u0101ga) \xe9 a ren\xfancia total ao desejo. 'Ren\xfancia' (pa\u1e6dinissagga) \xe9 a erradica\xe7\xe3o definitiva do anseio pelos quatro nobres caminhos. 'Liberta\xe7\xe3o' (mutti) \xe9 estar liberto dos grilh\xf5es do desejo. 'Aus\xeancia de apego' (an\u0101laya) \xe9 a inexist\xeancia de qualquer abrigo ou base na mente onde o desejo possa se alojar.",es:"En la explicaci\xf3n del cese del sufrimiento, la verdad de la cesaci\xf3n se detalla as\xed: 'Es el desvanecimiento y cese sin residuo de esa misma sed, su renuncia, su abandono, su liberaci\xf3n y su desapego total; esto es el cese del sufrimiento'. En este contexto, 'cese sin residuo': es tanto desapego como extinci\xf3n total. 'Renuncia' significa el desprendimiento del apego. 'Abandono' es la erradicaci\xf3n del anhelo mediante los cuatro nobles senderos. 'Liberaci\xf3n' es quedar libre de las ataduras de la sed. 'Desapego total' significa la ausencia de cualquier asiento o morada donde el deseo pueda apoyarse."}},{id:"vism-16.17",pali:"Apica nibb\u0101na\u1e43 natth\u012bti na vattabba\u1e43, kasm\u0101? Pa\u1e6dipattiy\u0101 va\xf1jhabh\u0101v\u0101pajjanato. Sace hi nibb\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101ma na bhaveyya, samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhipubba\u1e45gam\u0101 s\u012blasam\u0101dhipa\xf1\xf1\u0101sampann\u0101 maggasama\u1e45gino pa\u1e6dipatti va\xf1jh\u0101 siy\u0101, na ca va\xf1jh\u0101, adhigam\u0101vahatt\u0101. Tasm\u0101 atthi nibb\u0101na\u1e43. Tayida\u1e43 asa\u1e45khata\u1e43, amata\u1e43, santa\u1e43, pa\u1e47\u012bta\u1e43, dhuva\u1e43, ananta\u1e43, khemanti vuccati.",translations:{en:"Moreover, it should not be said that Nibb\u0101na does not exist. Why? Because that would entail the fruitlessness of the spiritual practice. For if Nibb\u0101na did not exist, the practice endowed with virtue, concentration, and understanding, preceded by right view for those on the path, would be sterile. But it is not sterile, because it brings about the attainment. Therefore, Nibb\u0101na exists. And this is called the unconditioned, the deathless, peace, the sublime, the stable, the infinite, the secure.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, n\xe3o se deve afirmar de modo algum que o Nibb\u0101na n\xe3o existe. Por qual raz\xe3o? Porque isso implicaria a inutilidade e esterilidade de toda a pr\xe1tica espiritual. Se o Nibb\u0101na n\xe3o existisse como uma realidade aut\xeantica, a pr\xe1tica disciplinada dotada de virtude, concentra\xe7\xe3o e sabedoria, guiada pelo correto entendimento, seria est\xe9ril para os disc\xedpulos no caminho. Mas ela n\xe3o \xe9 est\xe9ril, pois conduz de fato \xe0 realiza\xe7\xe3o libertadora. Portanto, o Nibb\u0101na \xe9 real e existe. E este Nibb\u0101na \xe9 chamado de incondicionado, imortal, pac\xedfico, sublime, inabal\xe1vel, infinito e supremo ref\xfagio.",es:"Adem\xe1s, no debe sostenerse de ninguna manera que el Nibbana no existe. \xbfPor qu\xe9 raz\xf3n? Porque ello implicar\xeda la inutilidad de toda la pr\xe1ctica espiritual. Si el Nibbana no existiera, la pr\xe1ctica que consta de virtud, concentraci\xf3n y sabidur\xeda, encabezada por el recto entendimiento, resultar\xeda infructuosa para quienes transitan el sendero. Mas no es infructuosa, puesto que conduce efectivamente a la realizaci\xf3n. Por lo tanto, el Nibbana existe. Y se llama lo incondicionado, lo inmortal, la paz suprema, lo sublime, lo imperecedero, lo infinito y el refugio inexpugnable."}},{id:"vism-16.18",pali:"Dukkhanirodhag\u0101minipa\u1e6dipad\u0101niddese vutt\u0101 pana a\u1e6d\u1e6dha dhamm\u0101 k\u0101ma\u1e43 khandhaniddese vutt\u0101, idh\u0101pi ekakkha\u1e47e pavattam\u0101n\u0101na\u1e43 tesa\u1e43 visesaj\u0101nana\xf1ca dassetu\u1e43 vad\u0101ma. Sa\u1e45khepato hi catunna\u1e43 sacc\u0101na\u1e43 pa\u1e6divedh\u0101ya pa\u1e6dipannassa yog\u0101vacarassa nibb\u0101n\u0101ramma\u1e47o avijj\u0101nusayasamuggh\u0101tako pa\xf1\xf1\u0101cakkhubh\u016bto maggo samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi. Sv\u0101ya\u1e43 samm\u0101dassanakkha\u1e47o, saccavibh\u0101vanaraso, avijjandhak\u0101raviddha\u1e43sanapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101no. Tass\u0101 ca sampayuttassa samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhissa tadanur\u016bpo micch\u0101sa\u1e45kappaviddha\u1e43sako nibb\u0101ne citt\u0101bhiniropanabh\u016bto maggo samm\u0101sa\u1e45kappo. So samm\u0101abhiniropanalakkha\u1e47o, appan\u0101raso, micch\u0101sa\u1e45kappappah\u0101napaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101no.",translations:{en:"The eight factors mentioned in the Exposition of the Path Leading to the Cessation of Suffering are, to be sure, also explained in substance in the Exposition of the Aggregates; here, however, we speak in order to make known the distinctions among them as they occur in a single moment. Briefly, for the yogin who has entered upon the path for the penetration of the four truths, right view is the eye of wisdom that has Nibb\u0101na as its object and uproots the underlying tendency to ignorance. It has the characteristic of right seeing, its function is to illuminate the elements, and it is manifested as the dispelling of the darkness of ignorance. For one accomplished in such a view, the associated right intention is the directing of the mind onto the state of Nibb\u0101na, which strikes down wrong intention. It has the characteristic of rightly directing the mind, its function is absorption, and it is manifested as the abandoning of wrong intention.",pt:"Embora os oito fatores mencionados na exposi\xe7\xe3o do caminho que conduz \xe0 cessa\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento j\xe1 tenham sido explicados em termos de significado na exposi\xe7\xe3o dos agregados (khandhaniddesa), n\xf3s os explicamos aqui para dar a conhecer as suas distin\xe7\xf5es especiais conforme ocorrem em um \xfanico momento mental. Brevemente, para o iogue que pratica para a penetra\xe7\xe3o das Quatro Verdades, o olho da sabedoria que tem o Nibb\u0101na como objeto e erradica a tend\xeancia latente da ignor\xe2ncia (avijj\u0101nusaya) \xe9 o entendimento correto (samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi). Ele tem a caracter\xedstica de ver corretamente, a fun\xe7\xe3o de revelar a natureza das coisas (ou as verdades) e manifesta-se como a destrui\xe7\xe3o da escurid\xe3o da ignor\xe2ncia. Para aquele que \xe9 dotado de tal entendimento, o fator associado a ele, que destr\xf3i o pensamento incorreto (micch\u0101sa\u1e45kappa) e direciona a mente em dire\xe7\xe3o ao estado do Nibb\u0101na, \xe9 o pensamento correto (samm\u0101sa\u1e45kappa). Ele tem a caracter\xedstica de direcionar corretamente a mente [ao objeto], a fun\xe7\xe3o de focar ou aplicar a mente [no Nibb\u0101na] e manifesta-se como o abandono do pensamento incorreto.",es:"Los ocho factores mencionados en la exposici\xf3n de la pr\xe1ctica que conduce a la cesaci\xf3n del sufrimiento ya han sido explicados en esencia en la exposici\xf3n de los agregados; sin embargo, aqu\xed los explicamos para dar a conocer su distinci\xf3n cuando ocurren en un solo momento. En resumen, para el yogui que practica para la penetraci\xf3n de las cuatro verdades, el ojo de la sabidur\xeda que tiene al Nibb\u0101na como objeto y que arranca la tendencia latente a la ignorancia es el recto entendimiento (samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi). Este tiene la caracter\xedstica de ver correctamente, la funci\xf3n de manifestar los elementos y la manifestaci\xf3n de la destrucci\xf3n de la oscuridad de la ignorancia. Para quien posee tal entendimiento, el factor del camino que erradica el pensamiento incorrecto concomitante y que aplica la mente al estado del Nibb\u0101na es el recto pensamiento (samm\u0101sa\u1e45kappa). Este tiene la caracter\xedstica de aplicar correctamente la mente, la funci\xf3n de la absorci\xf3n y la manifestaci\xf3n del abandono del pensamiento incorrecto."}},{id:"vism-16.19",pali:"Upam\u0101toti bh\u0101ro viya hi dukkhasacca\u1e43 da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43, bh\u0101r\u0101d\u0101namiva samudayasacca\u1e43, bh\u0101ranikkhepanamiva nirodhasacca\u1e43, bh\u0101ranikkhepanup\u0101yo viya maggasacca\u1e43. Rogo viya ca dukkhasacca\u1e43, roganid\u0101namiva samudayasacca\u1e43, rogav\u016bpasamo viya nirodhasacca\u1e43, bhesajjamiva maggasacca\u1e43. Dubbhikkhamiva v\u0101 dukkhasacca\u1e43, dubbu\u1e6d\u1e6dhi viya samudayasacca\u1e43, subhikkhamiva nirodhasacca\u1e43, suvu\u1e6d\u1e6dhi viya maggasacca\u1e43. Apica ver\u012b-veram\u016bla-verasamuggh\u0101ta-verasamuggh\u0101tup\u0101yehi, visarukkha-rukkham\u016bla-m\u016blupaccheda-tadupacchedup\u0101yehi, bhaya-bhayam\u016bla-nibbhaya-tadadhigamup\u0101yehi, orimat\u012bra-mahoghap\u0101rimat\u012bra-ta\u1e43samp\u0101pakav\u0101y\u0101mehi ca yojetv\u0101pet\u0101ni upam\u0101to veditabb\u0101n\u012bti evamettha upam\u0101to vinicchayo veditabbo.",translations:{en:"By way of analogy: The truth of suffering should be seen as a burden, the truth of the origin as the taking up of the burden, the truth of cessation as the laying down of the burden, and the truth of the path as the means to lay down the burden. And the truth of suffering is like a disease, the truth of the origin like the cause of the disease, the truth of cessation like the subsiding of the disease, and the truth of the path like the medicine. Or the truth of suffering is like a famine, the truth of the origin like a drought, the truth of cessation like abundance, and the truth of the path like good rain. Furthermore, these truths should be understood by way of analogy by applying them to: an enemy, the root of the enemy, the eradication of the enemy, and the means to eradicate the enemy; a poisonous tree, the root of the tree, the cutting off of the root, and the means to cut it off; fear, the root of fear, fearlessness, and the means to attain it; and the near shore, the great flood, the far shore, and the effort to reach it. Thus, the determination should be understood here also by way of analogy.",pt:"Por meio de analogias: a verdade do sofrimento deve ser vista como um fardo; a verdade da origem, como o ato de carregar o fardo; a verdade da cessa\xe7\xe3o, como o ato de depor o fardo; e a verdade do caminho, como o meio para depor o fardo. E a verdade do sofrimento \xe9 como uma doen\xe7a; a verdade da origem, como a causa da doen\xe7a; a verdade da cessa\xe7\xe3o, como a cura da doen\xe7a; e a verdade do caminho, como o rem\xe9dio. Ou ainda, a verdade do sofrimento \xe9 como uma fome generalizada; a verdade da origem, como uma seca; a verdade da cessa\xe7\xe3o, como a abund\xe2ncia de alimentos; e a verdade do caminho, como uma chuva favor\xe1vel. Al\xe9m disso, estas quatro verdades devem ser compreendidas por meio de analogias, associando-as respectivamente com: um inimigo, a raiz da inimizade, a erradica\xe7\xe3o da inimizade e o meio para essa erradica\xe7\xe3o; uma \xe1rvore venenosa, a raiz da \xe1rvore, o corte da raiz e o meio para esse corte; o perigo, a raiz do perigo, a aus\xeancia de perigo e o meio para alcan\xe7\xe1-la; a margem pr\xf3xima, a grande inunda\xe7\xe3o, a margem oposta e o esfor\xe7o para alcan\xe7\xe1-la. Assim deve ser compreendida aqui a decis\xe3o por meio de analogias.",es:"565. 'Por comparaciones': la verdad del sufrimiento debe verse como una carga, la verdad del origen como el acto de tomar la carga, la verdad del cese como el acto de dejar la carga y la verdad del camino como el medio para dejar la carga. Y la verdad del sufrimiento es como una enfermedad, la verdad del origen como la causa de la enfermedad, la verdad del cese como el alivio de la enfermedad y la verdad del camino como la medicina. O bien, la verdad del sufrimiento es como una hambruna, la verdad del origen como la sequ\xeda, la verdad del cese como la abundancia y la verdad del camino como la lluvia adecuada. Adem\xe1s, estas cuatro verdades deben entenderse a trav\xe9s de comparaciones aplic\xe1ndolas al enemigo, la ra\xedz de la enemistad, la erradicaci\xf3n de la enemistad y el medio para erradicar la enemistad; al \xe1rbol venenoso, su ra\xedz, el corte de la ra\xedz y el medio para cortar la ra\xedz; al peligro, la causa del peligro, la ausencia de peligro y el medio para alcanzarla; y a la orilla cercana, la gran corriente, la orilla lejana y el esfuerzo que conduce a ella. De esta manera debe entenderse aqu\xed la determinaci\xf3n por comparaciones."}}]},434,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,s,n,i,t){n.exports=[{id:"vism-17.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni \u2018\u2018khandh\u0101yatanadh\u0101tuindriyasaccapa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101d\u0101dibhed\u0101 dhamm\u0101 bh\u016bm\u012b\u2019\u2019ti eva\u1e43 vuttesu imiss\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101ya bh\u016bmibh\u016btesu dhammesu yasm\u0101 pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101doceva, \u0101disaddena sa\u1e45gahit\u0101 pa\u1e6diccasamuppann\u0101 dhamm\u0101 ca avases\u0101 honti, tasm\u0101 tesa\u1e43 va\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101kkamo anuppatto.",translations:{en:"Now, it was said: 'The phenomena classified as aggregates, bases, elements, faculties, truths, dependent origination, etc., are the ground.' Since, among these phenomena that have become the ground for this wisdom, what remain are dependent origination itself and the dependently arisen phenomena included by the word 'etc.', the turn for their description has now come.",pt:"Agora, tendo sido dito que 'os estados divididos em agregados, bases, elementos, faculdades, verdades, origina\xe7\xe3o dependente, etc., constituem o solo', e visto que, entre os estados que servem de solo para esta sabedoria, a origina\xe7\xe3o dependente e os estados originados de forma dependente (inclu\xeddos pela palavra 'etc.') s\xe3o os que restam, a ordem de sua explica\xe7\xe3o agora chegou.",es:"Ahora, habi\xe9ndose dicho que \xablos estados clasificados como agregados, bases, elementos, facultades, verdades, origen dependiente, etc., son el suelo de la sabidur\xeda\xbb, y puesto que entre los estados que constituyen el suelo de esta sabidur\xeda, el origen dependiente y los estados nacidos por dependencia (incluidos por la palabra \xabetc.\xbb) son los que quedan por explicar, ha llegado el turno para su descripci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-17.2",pali:"Tattha avijj\u0101dayo t\u0101va dhamm\u0101 pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101do ti veditabb\u0101. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 bhagavat\u0101 \u2013",translations:{en:"Herein, the phenomena beginning with ignorance should first be understood as dependent origination. For this was said by the Blessed One:",pt:"Entre estes, primeiramente, os estados que come\xe7am com a ignor\xe2ncia devem ser compreendidos como a origina\xe7\xe3o dependente. Pois isso foi dito pelo Aben\xe7oado:",es:"En ese contexto, los estados que comienzan con la ignorancia deben entenderse primero como el \xaborigen dependiente\xbb. Pues esto fue dicho por el Sublime:"}},{id:"vism-17.3",pali:"\u2018\u2018Katamo ca, bhikkhave, pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101do? Avijj\u0101paccay\u0101, bhikkhave, sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101, sa\u1e45kh\u0101rapaccay\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47apaccay\u0101 n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43, n\u0101mar\u016bpapaccay\u0101 sa\u1e37\u0101yatana\u1e43, sa\u1e37\u0101yatanapaccay\u0101 phasso, phassapaccay\u0101 vedan\u0101, vedan\u0101paccay\u0101 ta\u1e47h\u0101, ta\u1e47h\u0101paccay\u0101 up\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43, up\u0101d\u0101napaccay\u0101 bhavo, bhavapaccay\u0101 j\u0101ti, j\u0101tipaccay\u0101 jar\u0101mara\u1e47a\u1e43 sokaparidevadukkhadomanassup\u0101y\u0101s\u0101 sambhavanti. Evametassa kevalassa dukkhakkhandhassa samudayo hoti. Aya\u1e43 vuccati, bhikkhave, pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101do\u2019\u2019ti (sa\u1e43. ni. 2.1).",translations:{en:"\"And what, bhikkhus, is dependent origination? With ignorance as condition, bhikkhus, volitional formations; with volitional formations as condition, consciousness; with consciousness as condition, name-and-form; with name-and-form as condition, the six sense bases; with the six sense bases as condition, contact; with contact as condition, feeling; with feeling as condition, craving; with craving as condition, clinging; with clinging as condition, existence; with existence as condition, birth; with birth as condition, aging-and-death, sorrow, lamentation, pain, grief, and despair come to be. Such is the origin of this whole mass of suffering. This, bhikkhus, is called dependent origination.\"",pt:"\u201cE o que, monges, \xe9 a origina\xe7\xe3o dependente? Com a ignor\xe2ncia como condi\xe7\xe3o, monges, surgem as forma\xe7\xf5es volitivas; com as forma\xe7\xf5es volitivas como condi\xe7\xe3o, a consci\xeancia; com a consci\xeancia como condi\xe7\xe3o, a mente-e-corpo; com a mente-e-corpo como condi\xe7\xe3o, as seis bases dos sentidos; com as seis bases dos sentidos como condi\xe7\xe3o, o contato; com o contato como condi\xe7\xe3o, a sensa\xe7\xe3o; com a sensa\xe7\xe3o como condi\xe7\xe3o, o desejo; com o desejo como condi\xe7\xe3o, o apego; com o apego como condi\xe7\xe3o, o devir; com o devir como condi\xe7\xe3o, o nascimento; com o nascimento como condi\xe7\xe3o, surgem o envelhecimento e morte, tristeza, lamenta\xe7\xe3o, dor, afli\xe7\xe3o e desespero. Assim se d\xe1 a origem de toda esta massa de sofrimento. Isto, monges, \xe9 chamado de origina\xe7\xe3o dependente\u201d.",es:"\xab\xbfY qu\xe9 es, monjes, el origen dependiente? Con la ignorancia como condici\xf3n, monjes, surgen las formaciones; con las formaciones como condici\xf3n, la conciencia; con la conciencia como condici\xf3n, la mente y la materia; con la mente y la materia como condici\xf3n, las seis bases de los sentidos; con las seis bases de los sentidos como condici\xf3n, el contacto; con el contacto como condici\xf3n, la sensaci\xf3n; con la sensaci\xf3n como condici\xf3n, la avidez; con la avidez como condici\xf3n, el apego; con el apego como condici\xf3n, la existencia; con la existencia como condici\xf3n, el nacimiento; con el nacimiento como condici\xf3n, surgen la vejez y la muerte, la pena, el lamento, el dolor, la aflicci\xf3n y la desesperaci\xf3n. Tal es el origen de toda esta masa de sufrimiento. Esto, monjes, es llamado el origen dependiente\xbb."}},{id:"vism-17.4",pali:"Aya\u1e43 panettha sa\u1e45khepo. Pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101do ti paccayadhamm\u0101 veditabb\u0101. Pa\u1e6diccasamuppann\u0101 dhamm\u0101 ti tehi tehi paccayehi nibbattadhamm\u0101. Kathamida\u1e43 j\u0101nitabbanti ce? Bhagavato vacanena. Bhagavat\u0101 hi pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101dapa\u1e6diccasamuppannadhammadesan\u0101sutte \u2013",translations:{en:"This is the summary here. Dependent origination is to be understood as the conditioning phenomena. Dependently arisen phenomena are to be understood as the phenomena produced by those various conditions. If it is asked, 'How is this to be known?' By the word of the Blessed One. For in the Sutta on the Teaching of Dependent Origination and Dependently Arisen Phenomena, the Blessed One said:",pt:"Aqui est\xe1 o resumo disso. Deve-se entender que a 'origina\xe7\xe3o dependente' refere-se aos dhammas condicionantes. E os 'dhammas originados dependentemente' s\xe3o os dhammas produzidos por essas respectivas condi\xe7\xf5es. Se algu\xe9m perguntar: 'Como isso deve ser conhecido?', responde-se: 'Pelas palavras do Aben\xe7oado'. Pois, no Discurso sobre o Ensinamento da Origina\xe7\xe3o Dependente e dos Dhammas Originados Dependentemente, o Aben\xe7oado disse:",es:"He aqu\xed el resumen: Por \xaborigen dependiente\xbb deben entenderse los estados condicionales. Por \xabestados nacidos por dependencia\xbb deben entenderse los estados producidos por dichas condiciones. \xbfC\xf3mo se sabe esto? Por las palabras del Sublime. Pues en el Sutta sobre la Ense\xf1anza del Origen Dependiente y los Estados Nacidos por Dependencia, el Sublime dijo:"}},{id:"vism-17.5",pali:"So pan\u0101ya\u1e43 tehi tehi paccayehi an\u016bn\u0101dhikeheva tassa tassa dhammassa sambhavato tathat\u0101 ti, s\u0101maggi\u1e43 upagatesu paccayesu muhuttampi tato nibbattadhamm\u0101na\u1e43 asambhav\u0101bh\u0101vato avitathat\u0101 ti, a\xf1\xf1adhammapaccayehi a\xf1\xf1adhamm\u0101nuppattito ana\xf1\xf1athat\u0101 ti, yath\u0101vutt\u0101na\u1e43 etesa\u1e43 jar\u0101mara\u1e47\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 paccayato v\u0101 paccayasam\u016bhato v\u0101 idappaccayat\u0101 ti vutto.",translations:{en:"And this is called 'suchness' because of the arising of a specific phenomenon from its specific conditions without deficiency or excess. It is called 'undeviatingness' because when the conditions have come together, there is no non-arising, even for a moment, of the phenomena that should be produced from them. It is called 'unalterableness' because another phenomenon does not arise from the conditions for a different one. And it is called 'specific conditionality' because it is the condition, or the collection of conditions, for these phenomena mentioned, that is, aging-and-death, etc.",pt:"Esta mesma origina\xe7\xe3o dependente \xe9 chamada de 'realidade' porque cada dhamma surge de suas respectivas condi\xe7\xf5es, nem mais nem menos; \xe9 chamada de 'infalibilidade' porque, uma vez reunidas as condi\xe7\xf5es, n\xe3o h\xe1 sequer um momento em que os dhammas produzidos por elas deixem de surgir; \xe9 chamada de 'invariabilidade' porque um dhamma n\xe3o surge a partir de condi\xe7\xf5es que pertencem a outro dhamma; e \xe9 chamada de 'condicionalidade espec\xedfica' porque atua como a condi\xe7\xe3o ou o conjunto de condi\xe7\xf5es para os j\xe1 mencionados envelhecimento, morte e demais fatores.",es:"Adem\xe1s, este origen dependiente se denomina 'talidad' (tathat\u0101) porque cada fealidade surge de sus causas espec\xedficas, ni m\xe1s ni menos; se llama 'no-falsidad' (avitathat\u0101) porque, una vez que las causas han alcanzado su plenitud, no hay ni un solo momento en que los fealidades que deben surgir de ellas dejen de aparecer; se llama 'invariabilidad' (ana\xf1\xf1athat\u0101) porque un fealidade no surge de las condiciones que pertenecen a otro fealidade; y se denomina 'condicionalidad espec\xedfica' (idappaccayat\u0101) por ser la condici\xf3n o el conjunto de condiciones de estos fealidades antes mencionados, como la vejez y la muerte."}},{id:"vism-17.6",pali:"Aya\u1e43 pana vitth\u0101ranayo \u2013 avijj\u0101 ti suttantapariy\u0101yena dukkh\u0101d\u012bsu cat\u016bsu \u1e6dh\u0101nesu a\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, abhidhammapariy\u0101yena pubbant\u0101d\u012bhi saddhi\u1e43 a\u1e6d\u1e6dhasu. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018tattha katam\u0101 avijj\u0101, dukkhe a\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43\u2026pe\u2026 dukkhanirodhag\u0101miniy\u0101 pa\u1e6dipad\u0101ya a\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, pubbante a\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, aparante, pubbant\u0101parante, idappaccayat\u0101pa\u1e6diccasamuppannesu dhammesu a\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti (dha. sa. 1106). Tattha ki\xf1c\u0101pi \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 lokuttara\u1e43 saccadvaya\u1e43 sesa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu \u0101ramma\u1e47avasena avijj\u0101 uppajjati, eva\u1e43 santepi pa\u1e6dicch\u0101danavaseneva idha adhippet\u0101. S\u0101 hi uppann\u0101 dukkhasacca\u1e43 pa\u1e6dicch\u0101detv\u0101 ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhati, y\u0101th\u0101vasarasalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 pa\u1e6divijjhitu\u1e43 na deti, tath\u0101 samudaya\u1e43, nirodha\u1e43, magga\u1e43, pubbantasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 at\u012bta\u1e43 khandhapa\xf1caka\u1e43, aparantasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 an\u0101gata\u1e43 khandhapa\xf1caka\u1e43, pubbant\u0101parantasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 tadubhaya\u1e43, idappaccayat\u0101pa\u1e6diccasamuppannadhammasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 idappaccayata\xf1ceva pa\u1e6diccasamuppannadhamme ca pa\u1e6dicch\u0101detv\u0101 ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhati. \u2018\u2018Aya\u1e43 avijj\u0101, ime sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101\u2019\u2019ti eva\u1e43 y\u0101th\u0101vasarasalakkha\u1e47amettha pa\u1e6divijjhitu\u1e43 na deti. Tasm\u0101 dukkhe a\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43\u2026pe\u2026 idappaccayat\u0101pa\u1e6diccasamuppannesu dhammesu a\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47anti vuccati.",translations:{en:"Now, this is the detailed explanation. Ignorance (avijj\u0101), according to the Suttanta method, is the lack of knowledge in four instances beginning with suffering; according to the Abhidhamma method, it is the lack of knowledge in eight instances including the past ends. For it is said: 'Herein, what is ignorance? Lack of knowledge concerning suffering... lack of knowledge concerning the path leading to the cessation of suffering; lack of knowledge concerning the past end, the future end, both the past and future ends; lack of knowledge concerning this-conditionality and dependently arisen phenomena.' Here, although ignorance arises by way of taking as object the remaining six instances, setting aside the two supramundane truths, it is nevertheless intended here only in the sense of concealment. For when it arises, it stands concealing the truth of suffering, not allowing its true, inherent characteristic to be penetrated. Similarly, it stands concealing the origin, cessation, and path; the past five aggregates reckoned as the past end; the future five aggregates reckoned as the future end; both of these reckoned as both the past and future ends; and both this-conditionality and the dependently arisen phenomena, which are reckoned as 'this-conditionality and dependently arisen phenomena.' It does not allow one to penetrate herein their true, inherent characteristic, as in: 'This is ignorance, these are volitional formations.' Therefore, it is called 'lack of knowledge concerning suffering... lack of knowledge concerning this-conditionality and dependently arisen phenomena.'",pt:"Este, por\xe9m, \xe9 o m\xe9todo detalhado: a ignor\xe2ncia (avijj\u0101), de acordo com o m\xe9todo dos Suttas, \xe9 o n\xe3o saber em quatro bases, a saber, no sofrimento, etc.; de acordo com o m\xe9todo do Abhidhamma, \xe9 em oito bases, junto com o passado, etc. Pois foi dito: 'Aqui, o que \xe9 a ignor\xe2ncia? O n\xe3o saber no sofrimento... [pe]... o n\xe3o saber no caminho que leva \xe0 cessa\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento, o n\xe3o saber no passado, no futuro, no passado e futuro, e o n\xe3o saber nos dhammas da origina\xe7\xe3o dependente e condicionalidade'. Entre estas, embora a ignor\xe2ncia surja por meio de tomar como objeto as seis bases restantes (excluindo as duas verdades supramundanas), mesmo assim, ela \xe9 pretendida aqui apenas por meio de sua fun\xe7\xe3o de encobrir. Pois, quando surge, ela permanece encobrindo a verdade do sofrimento, n\xe3o permitindo que se penetre em sua caracter\xedstica real e intr\xednseca; da mesma forma, ela permanece encobrindo a origem, a cessa\xe7\xe3o, o caminho, o passado (os cinco agregados passados), o futuro (os cinco agregados futuros), ambos (passado e futuro), e a condicionalidade e os dhammas originados dependentemente. Ela n\xe3o permite que se penetre na caracter\xedstica real e intr\xednseca aqui, como 'esta \xe9 a ignor\xe2ncia, estas s\xe3o as forma\xe7\xf5es'. Portanto, \xe9 chamada de 'n\xe3o saber no sofrimento... [pe]... n\xe3o saber nos dhammas da origina\xe7\xe3o dependente e condicionalidade'.",es:"Esta es la explicaci\xf3n detallada: 'Ignorancia' (avijj\u0101) significa, seg\xfan el m\xe9todo de los Suttas (suttantapariy\u0101yena), el no-conocimiento en relaci\xf3n con las cuatro bases, comenzando por el sufrimiento; y seg\xfan el m\xe9todo del Abhidhamma, en relaci\xf3n con ocho bases, incluyendo el pasado y dem\xe1s. Pues se ha dicho: 'All\xed, \xbfqu\xe9 es la ignorancia? Es el no-conocimiento en el sufrimiento... pe... el no-conocimiento en el camino que conduce al cese del sufrimiento, el no-conocimiento en el pasado, en el futuro, en el pasado y futuro, y el no-conocimiento en los fealidades de la condicionalidad espec\xedfica y el origen dependiente' (Dhs. 1106). En este contexto, aunque la ignorancia surge por el poder del objeto en las otras seis bases, exceptuando las dos verdades supramundanas, aqu\xed se entiende espec\xedficamente por su poder de ocultamiento (pa\u1e6dicch\u0101danavasena). Pues esta, al surgir, permanece ocultando la verdad del sufrimiento y no permite penetrar su caracter\xedstica de naturaleza real (y\u0101th\u0101vasarasalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43); del mismo modo, permanece ocultando el origen, el cese, el camino, los cinco agregados del pasado llamados 'el extremo anterior' (pubbanta), los cinco agregados del futuro llamados 'el extremo posterior' (aparanta), ambos llamados 'el extremo anterior y posterior', y los fealidades llamados 'condicionalidad espec\xedfica y origen dependiente', es decir, tanto la condicionalidad espec\xedfica como los fealidades originados dependientemente. No permite penetrar la caracter\xedstica de naturaleza real en estas cosas, tales como: 'esta es la ignorancia, estas son las formaciones'. Por lo tanto, se denomina 'no-conocimiento en el sufrimiento... pe... no-conocimiento en los fealidades de la condicionalidad espec\xedfica y el origen dependiente'."}},{id:"vism-17.7",pali:"Sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 ti pu\xf1\xf1\u0101dayo tayo k\u0101yasa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101dayo tayoti eva\u1e43 pubbe sa\u1e45khepato vutt\u0101 cha, vitth\u0101rato panettha pu\xf1\xf1\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ro d\u0101nas\u012bl\u0101divasena pavatt\u0101 a\u1e6d\u1e6dha k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalacetan\u0101 ceva bh\u0101van\u0101vasena pavatt\u0101 pa\xf1ca r\u016bp\u0101vacarakusalacetan\u0101 c\u0101ti terasa cetan\u0101 honti. Apu\xf1\xf1\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ro p\u0101\u1e47\u0101tip\u0101t\u0101divasena pavatt\u0101 dv\u0101dasa akusalacetan\u0101. \u0100ne\xf1j\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ro bh\u0101van\u0101vaseneva pavatt\u0101 catasso ar\u016bp\u0101vacarakusalacetan\u0101 c\u0101ti tayopi sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 ek\u016bnati\u1e43sa cetan\u0101 honti.",translations:{en:"The formations (sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101) are the three, namely, meritorious formations and so on, and the three, namely, bodily formations and so on; thus, six were briefly stated before. But here in detail, the meritorious formation (pu\xf1\xf1\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ra) consists of thirteen volitions: the eight wholesome sense-sphere volitions occurring through giving, virtue, and so on, and the five wholesome form-sphere volitions occurring through meditation. The demeritorious formation (apu\xf1\xf1\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ra) consists of the twelve unwholesome volitions occurring through killing living beings and so on. The imperturbable formation (\u0101ne\xf1j\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ra) consists of the four wholesome formless-sphere volitions occurring through meditation alone. Thus, these three formations amount to twenty-nine volitions.",pt:"As forma\xe7\xf5es (sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101) s\xe3o as seis mencionadas anteriormente de forma resumida, a saber, as tr\xeas de m\xe9rito, etc., e as tr\xeas do corpo, etc. Em detalhes, por\xe9m, aqui: a forma\xe7\xe3o de m\xe9rito (pu\xf1\xf1\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ra) consiste em treze voli\xe7\xf5es (cetan\u0101), a saber, as oito voli\xe7\xf5es salutares da esfera dos sentidos que ocorrem por meio de generosidade, moralidade, etc., e as cinco voli\xe7\xf5es salutares da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil que ocorrem apenas por meio do cultivo mental (medita\xe7\xe3o). A forma\xe7\xe3o de dem\xe9rito (apu\xf1\xf1\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ra) consiste em doze voli\xe7\xf5es insalutares que ocorrem por meio de tirar a vida, etc. A forma\xe7\xe3o de imperturbabilidade (\u0101ne\xf1j\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ra) consiste em quatro voli\xe7\xf5es salutares da esfera imaterial que ocorrem apenas por meio do cultivo mental. Assim, as tr\xeas forma\xe7\xf5es totalizam vinte e nove voli\xe7\xf5es.",es:"Respecto a 'formaciones' (sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101), estas son las seis mencionadas brevemente antes: las tres que comienzan con la meritoria y las tres que comienzan con la corporal. En detalle, aqu\xed la 'formaci\xf3n meritoria' (pu\xf1\xf1\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ro) consiste en trece voliciones: las ocho voliciones sanas de la esfera de los sentidos que operan mediante la generosidad, la virtud, etc., y las cinco voliciones sanas de la esfera de la forma fine que operan \xfanicamente mediante la meditaci\xf3n. La 'formaci\xf3n no meritoria' (apu\xf1\xf1\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ro) consiste en las doce voliciones insanas que operan mediante el matar, etc. La 'formaci\xf3n imperturbable' (\u0101ne\xf1j\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ro) consiste en las cuatro voliciones sanas de la esfera inmaterial que operan \xfanicamente mediante la meditaci\xf3n. As\xed, estas tres formaciones constituyen las veintinueve voliciones."}},{id:"vism-17.8",pali:"Sa\u1e45kh\u0101rapaccay\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47apade \u2013 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a nti cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101di chabbidha\u1e43. Tattha cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 kusalavip\u0101ka\u1e43 akusalavip\u0101kanti duvidha\u1e43 hoti. Tath\u0101 sotagh\u0101najivh\u0101ka\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni. Manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 kusal\u0101kusalavip\u0101k\u0101 dve manodh\u0101tuyo, tisso ahetukamanovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tuyo, a\u1e6d\u1e6dha sahetuk\u0101ni k\u0101m\u0101vacaravip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni, pa\xf1ca r\u016bp\u0101vacar\u0101ni, catt\u0101ri ar\u016bp\u0101vacar\u0101n\u012bti b\u0101v\u012bsatividha\u1e43 hoti. Iti imehi chahi vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47ehi sabb\u0101nipi b\u0101tti\u1e43sa lokiyavip\u0101kavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni sa\u1e45gahit\u0101ni honti. Lokuttar\u0101ni pana va\u1e6d\u1e6dakath\u0101ya na yujjant\u012bti na gahit\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"In the phrase 'With formations as condition, consciousness,' consciousness is sixfold, beginning with eye-consciousness. Among these, eye-consciousness is twofold: wholesome-resultant and unwholesome-resultant. Likewise for ear-, nose-, tongue-, and body-consciousness. Mind-consciousness is of twenty-two kinds: the two mind-elements that are wholesome- and unwholesome-resultant, the three rootless mind-consciousness-elements, the eight sense-sphere resultant consciousnesses with roots, the five form-sphere resultants, and the four formless-sphere resultants. Thus, by these six kinds of consciousness, all thirty-two mundane resultant consciousnesses are included. The supramundane ones, however, are not included as they are not appropriate to the discussion of the round of existence.",pt:"Na frase \"com as forma\xe7\xf5es como condi\xe7\xe3o, a consci\xeancia\", \"consci\xeancia\" refere-se aos seis tipos de consci\xeancia, come\xe7ando pela consci\xeancia visual. Entre eles, a consci\xeancia visual \xe9 de dois tipos: resultante de a\xe7\xf5es ben\xe9ficas e resultante de a\xe7\xf5es prejudiciais. O mesmo se aplica \xe0s consci\xeancias auditiva, olfativa, gustativa e corporal. A consci\xeancia mental \xe9 de vinte e dois tipos: duas mentes-elemento resultantes de a\xe7\xf5es ben\xe9ficas e prejudiciais, tr\xeas mentes-elemento de consci\xeancia sem causa, oito consci\xeancias resultantes da esfera dos sentidos com causa, cinco da esfera da mat\xe9ria e quatro da esfera imaterial. Assim, com esses seis tipos de consci\xeancia, todas as trinta e duas consci\xeancias resultantes mundanas est\xe3o inclu\xeddas. As consci\xeancias supramundanas, no entanto, n\xe3o s\xe3o inclu\xeddas aqui por n\xe3o serem apropriadas para a explica\xe7\xe3o do ciclo de exist\xeancias.",es:"En el t\xe9rmino \xabcon las formaciones como condici\xf3n, la conciencia\xbb, por \xabconciencia\xbb se entiende los seis tipos: conciencia visual, etc. Entre estos, la conciencia visual es de dos tipos: resultado de m\xe9rito y resultado de dem\xe9rito. Lo mismo ocurre con las conciencias auditiva, olfativa, gustativa y t\xe1ctil. La conciencia mental es de veintid\xf3s tipos: dos elementos mentales (manodh\u0101tu) de resultado de m\xe9rito y dem\xe9rito, tres elementos de conciencia mental sin ra\xedz (ahetuka), ocho conciencias de resultado de la esfera de los sentidos con ra\xedz (sahetuka), cinco del reino de la forma y cuatro del reino inmaterial. As\xed, mediante estos seis tipos de conciencia, quedan incluidas las treinta y dos conciencias de resultado mundanas (lokiya-vip\u0101ka). Las supramundanas no se incluyen por no ser apropiadas en el contexto de la explicaci\xf3n del ciclo de existencias (va\u1e6d\u1e6da)."}},{id:"vism-17.9",pali:"Vibh\u0101g\u0101 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43, bhav\u0101d\u012bsu pavattito; Sa\u1e45gah\u0101 paccayanay\u0101, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101tabbo vinicchayo.",translations:{en:"The determination should be known through: the analysis of name-and-form, its occurrence in existences and so on, its summary, and the method of conditionality.",pt:"A decis\xe3o deve ser compreendida por meio da divis\xe3o de mentalidade-materialidade, de sua ocorr\xeancia nos reinos de exist\xeancia e outros, de sua inclus\xe3o e dos m\xe9todos de condicionamento.",es:"La conclusi\xf3n debe conocerse mediante la divisi\xf3n del nombre y la forma, su ocurrencia en las existencias y dem\xe1s categor\xedas, su clasificaci\xf3n y el m\xe9todo de condicionalidad."}},{id:"vism-17.10",pali:"N\u0101ma\u1e43 khandhattaya\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43, bh\u016btavatth\u0101dika\u1e43 mata\u1e43; Katekasesa\u1e43 ta\u1e43 tassa, t\u0101disasseva paccayo.",translations:{en:"N\u0101ma is the three aggregates; r\u016bpa is considered the primary elements, the bases, and so forth. That n\u0101mar\u016bpa, treated by single remainder, is a condition for that sa\u1e37\u0101yatana, which is treated in the same way.",pt:"O nome \xe9 considerado como a tr\xedade de agregados [sensa\xe7\xe3o, percep\xe7\xe3o, forma\xe7\xf5es]; a forma \xe9 considerada como os elementos prim\xe1rios, a base, etc. Esse [nome-e-forma], tendo sido reduzido a um termo remanescente (katekasesa), \xe9 a condi\xe7\xe3o para aquela [base dos sentidos] que foi similarmente reduzida a um termo remanescente.",es:"Se considera \xabnombre\xbb a la tr\xedada de agregados y \xabforma\xbb a los elementos, las bases, etc. Ese [nombre-forma], tras la elisi\xf3n de uno de los t\xe9rminos, es condici\xf3n para aquellas [seis bases] de su misma clase."}},{id:"vism-17.11",pali:"Sa\u1e37eva phass\u0101 sa\u1e45khep\u0101, cakkhusamphassa\u0101dayo; Vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47amiva b\u0101tti\u1e43sa, vitth\u0101rena bhavanti te.",translations:{en:"In brief, there are just six contacts, beginning with eye-contact. In detail, like consciousness, they become thirty-two.",pt:"Em resumo, existem apenas seis tipos de contato, a come\xe7ar pelo contato visual; em detalhes, eles s\xe3o trinta e dois, assim como a consci\xeancia.",es:"En resumen, hay solo seis tipos de contacto, comenzando por el contacto visual; en detalle, estos son treinta y dos, al igual que la conciencia."}},{id:"vism-17.12",pali:"Dv\u0101rato vedan\u0101 vutt\u0101, cakkhusamphassaj\u0101dik\u0101; Sa\u1e37eva t\u0101 pabhedena, ek\u016bnanavut\u012b mat\u0101.",translations:{en:"Feelings are spoken of by way of the doors, beginning with that born of eye-contact; they are just six. But by way of detailed division, they are considered to be eighty-nine.",pt:"As sensa\xe7\xf5es s\xe3o ditas ser seis de acordo com as portas sensoriais, a come\xe7ar pela nascida do contato visual; em detalhes, elas s\xe3o consideradas oitenta e nove.",es:"Las sensaciones han sido declaradas por el Bienaventurado seg\xfan las puertas de los sentidos, comenzando con la nacida del contacto visual. Son solo seis, pero se consideran ochenta y nueve seg\xfan su clasificaci\xf3n detallada."}},{id:"vism-17.13",pali:"R\u016bpata\u1e47h\u0101dibhedena, cha ta\u1e47h\u0101 idha d\u012bpit\u0101; Ekek\u0101 tividh\u0101 tattha, pavatt\u0101k\u0101rato mat\u0101.",translations:{en:"Here, six kinds of craving are shown, divided as craving for forms and so on; each of these is considered threefold according to its mode of occurrence.",pt:"Seis tipos de desejo s\xe3o mostrados aqui, divididos em desejo por formas vis\xedveis e os demais; cada um deles \xe9 considerado de tr\xeas tipos de acordo com o modo de ocorr\xeancia.",es:"En esta ense\xf1anza, el Bendito ha mostrado seis tipos de avidez seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de la avidez por las formas y dem\xe1s objetos; en ella se entiende que cada una es de tres tipos seg\xfan el modo de su manifestaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-17.14",pali:"Up\u0101d\u0101n\u0101ni catt\u0101ri, t\u0101ni atthavibh\u0101gato; Dhammasa\u1e45khepavitth\u0101r\u0101, kamato ca vibh\u0101vaye.",translations:{en:"The four kinds of clinging should be clarified according to their analysis by meaning, according to the teaching in brief and in detail, and according to their sequence.",pt:"Os apegos s\xe3o quatro; deve-se explic\xe1-los por meio da an\xe1lise de seus significados, do resumo e detalhamento de seus dhammas, e de sua ordem.",es:"Los apegos son cuatro; estos deben explicarse mediante el an\xe1lisis de su significado, la brevedad y extensi\xf3n de los estados (dhammas), y su orden sucesivo."}},{id:"vism-17.15",pali:"Atthato dhammato ceva, s\u0101tthato bhedasa\u1e45gah\u0101; Ya\u1e43 yassa paccayo ceva, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101tabbo vinicchayo.",translations:{en:"The determination should be understood: by meaning and by phenomenon, by its meaningfulness, by division and combination, and by what is a condition for what.",pt:"A decis\xe3o deve ser compreendida atrav\xe9s do significado, da natureza intr\xednseca, do prop\xf3sito, da diferencia\xe7\xe3o e da s\xedntese, e de qual apego \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para qual devir.",es:"Se debe conocer la determinaci\xf3n por el significado, por su naturaleza intr\xednseca, por su prop\xf3sito, por su clasificaci\xf3n y s\xedntesis, y por qu\xe9 factor es condici\xf3n de cu\xe1l."}},{id:"vism-17.16",pali:"Bhavapaccay\u0101 j\u0101t\u012bti\u0101d\u012bsu j\u0101ti\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 vinicchayo saccaniddese vuttanayeneva veditabbo. Bhavo ti panettha kammabhavova adhippeto. So hi j\u0101tiy\u0101 paccayo, na upapattibhavo. So ca pana kammapaccayaupanissayapaccayavasena dvedh\u0101 paccayo hot\u012bti.",translations:{en:"In the passage 'with becoming as condition, birth,' etc., the determination of birth and so on should be understood in the same way as stated in the Exposition of the Truths. Here, 'becoming' is intended only as kamma-becoming. For it is the condition for birth, not rebirth-becoming. And it is a condition in two ways: as kamma-condition and as decisive-support condition.",pt:"Nas frases 'com a exist\xeancia como condi\xe7\xe3o, surge o nascimento' e seguintes, a decis\xe3o a respeito do nascimento e demais fatores deve ser compreendida exatamente pelo m\xe9todo j\xe1 exposto na Explica\xe7\xe3o das Verdades (saccaniddesa). No entanto, neste contexto, por 'exist\xeancia' (bhava), entende-se apenas o processo ativo da exist\xeancia (kammabhava). Pois \xe9 ele que serve de condi\xe7\xe3o para o nascimento (j\u0101ti), e n\xe3o o processo passivo do renascimento (upapattibhava). E esse processo ativo \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o de duas maneiras: por meio da condi\xe7\xe3o de kamma (kammapaccayo) e da condi\xe7\xe3o de suporte decisivo (upanissayapaccayo).",es:"En los t\xe9rminos 'con el devenir como condici\xf3n, el nacimiento', etc., la conclusi\xf3n sobre el nacimiento y otros debe entenderse de la misma manera explicada en la Exposici\xf3n de las Verdades (Saccaniddese). Sin embargo, aqu\xed, por 'devenir' se entiende \xfanicamente el devenir de la acci\xf3n (kammabhavova). Pues este es condici\xf3n para el nacimiento, no as\xed el devenir de renacimiento (upapattibhavo). Y ese [devenir de la acci\xf3n] es condici\xf3n de dos maneras: a trav\xe9s de la condici\xf3n de la acci\xf3n y de la condici\xf3n de apoyo decisivo."}},{id:"vism-17.17",pali:"Yasm\u0101 ca asati j\u0101tiy\u0101 jar\u0101mara\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u0101ma, sok\u0101dayo v\u0101 dhamm\u0101 na honti. J\u0101tiy\u0101 pana sati jar\u0101mara\u1e47a\xf1ceva, jar\u0101mara\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101tadukkhadhammaphu\u1e6d\u1e6dhassa ca b\u0101lajanassa jar\u0101mara\u1e47\u0101bhisambandh\u0101 v\u0101 tena tena dukkhadhammena phu\u1e6d\u1e6dhassa anabhisambandh\u0101 v\u0101 sok\u0101dayo ca dhamm\u0101 honti. Tasm\u0101 ayampi j\u0101ti jar\u0101mara\u1e47assa ceva sok\u0101d\u012bna\xf1ca paccayo hot\u012bti veditabb\u0101. S\u0101 pana upanissayako\u1e6diy\u0101 ekadh\u0101va paccayo hot\u012bti.",translations:{en:"And because, when there is no birth, there is no such thing as aging-and-death, nor are there states such as sorrow and the like. But when birth exists, there is aging-and-death; and for the foolish person afflicted by the painful states reckoned as aging-and-death, states such as sorrow and the like arise, whether connected with that aging-and-death or unconnected, when afflicted by this or that painful state. Therefore, this birth should be understood as a condition for both aging-and-death and for sorrow and the rest. But it is a condition in only one way, in the category of decisive support.",pt:"E visto que, na aus\xeancia do nascimento, o envelhecimento e a morte (jar\u0101mara\u1e47a), bem como o sofrimento e outros estados mentais dolorosos, n\xe3o ocorrem; mas, havendo o nascimento, ocorrem tanto o envelhecimento e a morte quanto, para a pessoa tola afligida pelo sofrimento do envelhecimento e da morte, os dhammas de tristeza e outros \u2014 quer estejam diretamente relacionados ao envelhecimento e \xe0 morte, quer n\xe3o estejam diretamente relacionados a eles, mas sim a outros dhammas de sofrimento que a afligem \u2014, deve-se compreender que este nascimento tamb\xe9m \xe9 a condi\xe7\xe3o para o envelhecimento e a morte, bem como para a tristeza e os demais estados. E ele \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o de uma \xfanica maneira: sob o aspecto de suporte decisivo (upanissaya).",es:"Adem\xe1s, dado que si no hay nacimiento, no existen la vejez y la muerte, ni estados como el pesar, etc. Pero habiendo nacimiento, ocurren tanto la vejez y la muerte, como \u2014para la persona ignorante afligida por el estado de sufrimiento denominado vejez y muerte\u2014 el pesar y otros estados, ya sea que est\xe9n relacionados con la vejez y la muerte o no lo est\xe9n, al ser afligida por diversos estados de sufrimiento. Por lo tanto, debe entenderse que este nacimiento es tambi\xe9n condici\xf3n tanto para la vejez y la muerte como para el pesar y otros. Y este es condici\xf3n de una sola manera, a trav\xe9s del aspecto de apoyo decisivo (upanissayako\u1169iy\u0101)."}},{id:"vism-17.18",pali:"Tassa kho panetassa bhavacakkassa avijj\u0101 ta\u1e47h\u0101 c\u0101ti dve dhamm\u0101 m\u016bla nti veditabb\u0101. Tadeta\u1e43 pubbant\u0101hara\u1e47ato avijj\u0101m\u016bla\u1e43 vedan\u0101vas\u0101na\u1e43, aparantasant\u0101nato ta\u1e47h\u0101m\u016bla\u1e43 jar\u0101mara\u1e47\u0101vas\u0101nanti duvidha\u1e43 hoti. Tattha purima\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhicaritavasena vutta\u1e43, pacchima\u1e43 ta\u1e47h\u0101caritavasena. Di\u1e6d\u1e6dhicarit\u0101na\u1e43 hi avijj\u0101, ta\u1e47h\u0101carit\u0101na\xf1ca ta\u1e47h\u0101 sa\u1e43s\u0101ran\u0101yik\u0101. Ucchedadi\u1e6d\u1e6dhisamuggh\u0101t\u0101ya v\u0101 pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43, phaluppattiy\u0101 het\u016bna\u1e43 anupacchedappak\u0101sanato, sassatadi\u1e6d\u1e6dhisamuggh\u0101t\u0101ya dutiya\u1e43, uppann\u0101na\u1e43 jar\u0101mara\u1e47appak\u0101sanato. Gabbhaseyyakavasena v\u0101 purima\u1e43, anupubbapavattid\u012bpanato, opap\u0101tikavasena pacchima\u1e43, sahuppattid\u012bpanato.",translations:{en:"It should be understood that the root of this wheel of becoming is two things: ignorance and craving. This is twofold: when traced back to the past end, it is rooted in ignorance and ends with feeling; in the continuity of the future end, it is rooted in craving and ends with aging-and-death. Here, the former is stated for one of speculative temperament, the latter for one of craving temperament. For those of speculative temperament, ignorance is the leader in sa\u1e43s\u0101ra; for those of craving temperament, craving is the leader. Alternatively, the first is for the eradication of the annihilationist view, by showing the non-interruption of causes for the arising of fruit; the second is for the eradication of the eternalist view, by showing the aging-and-death of what has come to be. Or, the former is stated by way of womb-birth, showing a gradual process; the latter by way of spontaneous birth, showing simultaneous arising.",pt:"Deve-se compreender que esses dois fatores, a ignor\xe2ncia e o desejo, s\xe3o as ra\xedzes desta roda da exist\xeancia. Ela \xe9 de dois tipos: a roda da exist\xeancia que tem a ignor\xe2ncia como raiz e termina na sensa\xe7\xe3o, por trazer o efeito presente a partir do limite do passado; e a roda da exist\xeancia que tem o desejo como raiz e termina no envelhecimento e morte, por conectar e estender o limite do futuro. Dessas duas, a primeira foi dita de acordo com o temperamento daqueles propensos a vis\xf5es incorretas, e a segunda de acordo com o temperamento daqueles propensos ao desejo. Pois, para os propensos a vis\xf5es incorretas, a ignor\xe2ncia \xe9 a condutora do sa\u1e43s\u0101ra; e para os propensos ao desejo, o desejo \xe9 o condutor do sa\u1e43s\u0101ra. Ou ainda, a primeira foi dita para erradicar a vis\xe3o de aniquila\xe7\xe3o, ao mostrar a continuidade ininterrupta das causas atrav\xe9s do surgimento dos efeitos; a segunda foi dita para erradicar a vis\xe3o de eternidade, ao mostrar o envelhecimento e a morte daquilo que surgiu. Ou ainda, a primeira foi dita de acordo com os seres de nascimento uterino, ao ilustrar o desenvolvimento gradual; e a segunda de acordo com os seres de nascimento espont\xe2neo, ao ilustrar o surgimento simult\xe2neo.",es:"Debe entenderse que la ignorancia y la sed son los dos factores que constituyen las ra\xedces de esta Rueda de la Existencia. Esta es de dos tipos: una con la ignorancia como ra\xedz que termina en la sensaci\xf3n, al traer los efectos desde el pasado; y otra con la sed como ra\xedz que termina en la vejez y la muerte, al conectar con la continuidad futura. De estas, la primera se ense\xf1\xf3 en virtud de aquellos con temperamento de puntos de vista, y la segunda en virtud de aquellos con temperamento de sed. Pues para los de temperamento de puntos de vista, la ignorancia es la gu\xeda del samsara, y para los de temperamento de sed, lo es la sed. O bien, la primera se ense\xf1\xf3 para la erradicaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n nihilista, al mostrar que las causas no se interrumpen mediante el surgimiento de los frutos; y la segunda para la erradicaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n eternalista, al mostrar la vejez y la muerte de lo que ha surgido. O bien, la primera se ense\xf1\xf3 en virtud de los seres de nacimiento uterino, al mostrar el proceso gradual; y la \xfaltima en virtud de los seres de nacimiento espont\xe1neo, al mostrar el surgimiento simult\xe1neo."}},{id:"vism-17.19",pali:"Tiva\u1e6d\u1e6damanava\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43 bhamat\u012b ti ettha pana sa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhav\u0101 kammava\u1e6d\u1e6da\u1e43, avijj\u0101ta\u1e47hup\u0101d\u0101n\u0101ni kilesava\u1e6d\u1e6da\u1e43, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47an\u0101mar\u016bpasa\u1e37\u0101yatanaphassavedan\u0101 vip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6danti imehi t\u012bhi va\u1e6d\u1e6dehi tiva\u1e6d\u1e6damida\u1e43 bhavacakka\u1e43 y\u0101va kilesava\u1e6d\u1e6da\u1e43 na upacchijjati, t\u0101va anupacchinnapaccayatt\u0101 anava\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43 punappuna\u1e43 parivattanato bhamatiyev\u0101ti veditabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Here, as to the statement that it revolves with three rounds, without stop: formations and existence are the round of kamma; ignorance, craving, and clinging are the round of defilements; consciousness, name-and-form, the six sense bases, contact, and feeling are the round of results. It should be understood that this wheel of existence has three rounds because of these three rounds. For as long as the round of defilements is not cut off, for so long, because its condition is not cut off, it revolves without stop, turning again and again.",pt:"Na frase 'gira sem cessar com tr\xeas ciclos', as forma\xe7\xf5es volunt\xe1rias e o devir constituem o ciclo do kamma. A ignor\xe2ncia, o desejo e o apego constituem o ciclo das impurezas. A consci\xeancia, a mente-e-mat\xe9ria, as seis bases dos sentidos, o contato e a sensa\xe7\xe3o constituem o ciclo dos resultados. Deve-se compreender que, por meio desses tr\xeas ciclos, esta roda da exist\xeancia, que possui tr\xeas ciclos, gira continuamente sem cessar e de forma repetida, visto que suas condi\xe7\xf5es n\xe3o s\xe3o interrompidas enquanto o ciclo das impurezas n\xe3o for cortado.",es:"En cuanto a la frase 'gira sin cesar en tres rondas', se debe entender que las formaciones y el proceso de existencia son la ronda del kamma; la ignorancia, el anhelo y el apego son la ronda de las defilecciones; la conciencia, la mente y la materia, las seis bases sensoriales, el contacto y la sensaci\xf3n son la ronda de los resultados. As\xed, esta rueda de la existencia, compuesta por estas tres rondas, gira continuamente debido a que sus condiciones no se han interrumpido mientras no se corte la ronda de las defilecciones, rotando una y otra vez sin detenerse."}},{id:"vism-17.20",pali:"Vuttampi heta\u1e43 bhagavat\u0101 \u2013 \u2018\u2018gambh\u012bro c\u0101ya\u1e43, \u0101nanda, pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101do gambh\u012br\u0101vabh\u0101so ca. Etassa c\u0101nanda, dhammassa ananubodh\u0101 appa\u1e6divedh\u0101 evamaya\u1e43 paj\u0101 tant\u0101kulakaj\u0101t\u0101 kul\u0101ga\u1e47\u1e6dhikaj\u0101t\u0101 mu\xf1japabbajabh\u016bt\u0101 ap\u0101ya\u1e43 duggati\u1e43 vinip\u0101ta\u1e43 sa\u1e43s\u0101ra\u1e43 n\u0101tivattat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (mah\u0101va. 95; sa\u1e43. ni. 2.60). Tasm\u0101 attano v\u0101 paresa\u1e43 v\u0101 hit\u0101ya ca sukh\u0101ya ca pa\u1e6dipanno avasesakicc\u0101ni pah\u0101ya,",translations:{en:"This was also spoken by the Blessed One: 'Deep, \u0100nanda, is this dependent origination, and it appears deep. It is through not understanding and not penetrating this Dhamma, \u0100nanda, that this generation has become a tangled skein, a knotted ball of thread, like matted mu\xf1ja and babbaja grass; it does not pass beyond the plane of misery, the bad destination, the nether world, sa\u1e43s\u0101ra' (DN 15.1; SN 12.60). Therefore, having abandoned other duties, one who is practicing for the welfare and happiness of oneself or others,",pt:"Pois isso foi dito pelo Aben\xe7oado: 'Profundo \xe9 este surgimento dependente, Ananda, e profunda \xe9 a sua apar\xeancia. \xc9 por n\xe3o compreender e n\xe3o penetrar este ensinamento, Ananda, que esta gera\xe7\xe3o de seres se tornou emaranhada como um novelo de linha, coberta de n\xf3s como um ninho de p\xe1ssaros, semelhante ao capim-mu\xf1ja e \xe0 palha, e n\xe3o consegue superar os dhammas de priva\xe7\xe3o, os destinos infelizes, a ru\xedna e o sa\u1e43s\u0101ra'. Portanto, aquele que pratica para o benef\xedcio e felicidade de si mesmo ou dos outros, abandonando as demais tarefas,",es:"De hecho, esto fue dicho por el Bienaventurado: 'Este origen dependiente, Ananda, es profundo y profundo en su apariencia. Debido a la falta de comprensi\xf3n y de penetraci\xf3n de esta doctrina, Ananda, esta generaci\xf3n se ha vuelto como una madeja de hilo enredada, como un nido de p\xe1jaros cubierto de nudos, como juncos y ca\xf1as, y no supera el estado de perdici\xf3n, el mal destino, la ruina y el sa\u1e43s\u0101ra'. Por lo tanto, aquel que se ha dedicado a su propio bienestar y felicidad, o al de los dem\xe1s, debe abandonar las tareas restantes y,"}}]},435,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,t,i,s,n){i.exports=[{id:"vism-18.1",pali:"Id\u0101ni y\u0101 \u2018\u2018imesu bh\u016bmibh\u016btesu dhammesu uggahaparipucch\u0101vasena \xf1\u0101\u1e47aparicaya\u1e43 katv\u0101 \u2018s\u012blavisuddhi ceva cittavisuddhi c\u0101\u2019ti dve m\u016blabh\u016bt\u0101 visuddhiyo samp\u0101detabb\u0101\u2019\u2019ti vutt\u0101. Tattha s\u012blavisuddhi n\u0101ma suparisuddha\u1e43 p\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43var\u0101dicatubbidha\u1e43 s\u012bla\u1e43, ta\xf1ca s\u012blaniddese vitth\u0101ritameva. Cittavisuddhi n\u0101ma saupac\u0101r\u0101 a\u1e6d\u1e6dha sam\u0101pattiyo, t\u0101pi cittas\u012bsena vutta sam\u0101dhiniddese sabb\u0101k\u0101rena vitth\u0101rit\u0101 eva. Tasm\u0101 t\u0101 tattha vitth\u0101ritanayeneva veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Now, it was said: 'Having gained acquaintance with knowledge of these states that are the ground by way of study and questioning, two purifications that are the root should be accomplished, namely, purification of virtue and purification of mind.' Herein, purification of virtue is the fourfold utterly pure virtue beginning with the P\u0101timokkha restraint, and that has been explained in detail in the Exposition of Virtue. Purification of mind is the eight attainments together with their access concentration, and these too have been explained in every way in the Exposition of Concentration, which was stated under the heading of mind. Therefore, they should be understood in the way they were explained in detail there.",pt:"Agora, foi dito anteriormente: 'Tendo adquirido familiaridade com o conhecimento por meio do aprendizado e da indaga\xe7\xe3o a respeito destes estados que constituem o solo, devem ser realizadas as duas purifica\xe7\xf5es fundamentais: a purifica\xe7\xe3o da conduta e a purifica\xe7\xe3o da mente'. Entre estas, a purifica\xe7\xe3o da conduta \xe9 a conduta extremamente pura de quatro tipos, come\xe7ando com a restri\xe7\xe3o do Patimokkha, e essa conduta j\xe1 foi detalhada na Exposi\xe7\xe3o da Conduta (S\u012blaniddesa). A purifica\xe7\xe3o da mente consiste nas oito realiza\xe7\xf5es meditativas junto com o acesso; estas tamb\xe9m foram detalhadas em todos os seus aspectos na Exposi\xe7\xe3o da Concentra\xe7\xe3o (Sam\u0101dhiniddesa), que foi ensinada sob o aspecto da mente. Portanto, estas devem ser compreendidas exatamente da maneira como foram detalhadas naquelas se\xe7\xf5es.",es:"Se ha dicho anteriormente: 'Habiendo cultivado el conocimiento mediante el estudio y la indagaci\xf3n sobre estos fealidades que constituyen el terreno, deben completarse las dos purificaciones que son la ra\xedz, a saber: la purificaci\xf3n de la conducta (s\u012blavisuddhi) y la purificaci\xf3n de la mente (cittavisuddhi)'. All\xed, la purificaci\xf3n de la conducta consiste en los cuatro tipos de moralidad, como la moderaci\xf3n del Patimokkha, la cual ha sido detallada en la 'Descripci\xf3n de la Conducta'. La purificaci\xf3n de la mente consiste en los ocho logros con sus concentraciones de acceso, los cuales han sido detallados en todos sus aspectos en la 'Descripci\xf3n de la Concentraci\xf3n' bajo el encabezado de la mente. Por lo tanto, deben entenderse seg\xfan lo detallado en esos lugares."}},{id:"vism-18.2",pali:"Ya\u1e43 pana vutta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddhi, ka\u1e45kh\u0101vitara\u1e47avisuddhi, magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi, pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi, \xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddh\u012bti im\u0101 pana pa\xf1ca visuddhiyo sar\u012bra\u2019\u2019nti, tattha n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43 y\u0101th\u0101vadassana\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddhi n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"But as to what was said: 'Purification of view, purification by overcoming doubt, purification by knowledge and vision of path and not-path, purification by knowledge and vision of the way, and purification by knowledge and vision\u2014these five purifications are the body.' Herein, the seeing of mentality-materiality as it really is is called purification of view.",pt:"Quanto ao que foi dito: 'A purifica\xe7\xe3o da vis\xe3o, a purifica\xe7\xe3o pela supera\xe7\xe3o da d\xfavida, a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o do que \xe9 e do que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho, a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o do caminho da pr\xe1tica, e a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o \u2014 estas cinco purifica\xe7\xf5es constituem o corpo', entre estas, a vis\xe3o correta da mente e da mat\xe9ria de acordo com a realidade \xe9 chamada de purifica\xe7\xe3o da vis\xe3o (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddhi).",es:"En cuanto a lo que se ha dicho: 'La purificaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n, la purificaci\xf3n mediante la superaci\xf3n de la duda, la purificaci\xf3n mediante el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n de lo que es el sendero y lo que no lo es, la purificaci\xf3n mediante el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n del progreso, y la purificaci\xf3n mediante el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n: estas cinco purificaciones son el cuerpo [de la sabidur\xeda]', de ellas, la visi\xf3n de la mentalidad y la materialidad tal como son en realidad se denomina purificaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-18.3",pali:"Ta\u1e43 samp\u0101detuk\u0101mena samathay\u0101nikena t\u0101va \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana\u1e43 avasesar\u016bp\u0101r\u016bp\u0101vacarajjh\u0101n\u0101na\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1atarato vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya vitakk\u0101d\u012bni jh\u0101na\u1e45g\u0101ni, ta\u1e43sampayutt\u0101 ca dhamm\u0101 lakkha\u1e47aras\u0101divasena pariggahetabb\u0101. Pariggahetv\u0101 sabbampeta\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101bhimukha\u1e43 namanato namana\u1e6d\u1e6dhena n\u0101ma nti vavatthapetabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"A serenity-vehicle meditator who wishes to accomplish this should first, setting aside the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception, emerge from any of the remaining fine-material or immaterial jh\u0101nas. Then the jh\u0101na factors, such as applied thought, and the states associated with them, should be comprehended by way of their characteristic, function, etc. Having comprehended them, all this should be defined as 'mentality' on the ground of bending, in the sense of its inclining towards an object.",pt:"Aquele que tem o ve\xedculo da tranquilidade e deseja realizar essa purifica\xe7\xe3o deve, primeiramente, excetuando a esfera da nem-percep\xe7\xe3o-nem-n\xe3o-percep\xe7\xe3o, emergir de qualquer uma das demais absor\xe7\xf5es meditativas pertencentes \xe0s esferas da mat\xe9ria e da n\xe3o-mat\xe9ria, e definir os fatores da absor\xe7\xe3o, como a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial, etc., bem como os dhammas associados a eles, por meio de suas caracter\xedsticas, fun\xe7\xf5es, etc. Tendo-os definido, ele deve determinar que todo esse conjunto de estados \xe9 'mente' (n\u0101ma), no sentido de inclinar-se, por se inclinar em dire\xe7\xe3o ao objeto.",es:"El practicante que utiliza la tranquilidad como veh\xedculo (samathay\u0101nika), deseando perfeccionar dicha [pureza de visi\xf3n], debe primero emerger de cualquiera de las absorciones de las esferas de la forma o sin forma \u2014exceptuando la esfera de la ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n\u2014 y discernir los factores de la absorci\xf3n como la aplicaci\xf3n inicial (vitakka) y los dem\xe1s, as\xed como los estados asociados, mediante sus caracter\xedsticas, funciones, y as\xed sucesivamente. Tras haberlos discernido, debe definir todo aquello como \xabmente\xbb (n\u0101ma), en el sentido de inclinarse, debido a que se inclina hacia el objeto."}},{id:"vism-18.4",pali:"Suddhavipassan\u0101y\u0101niko pana ayameva v\u0101 samathay\u0101niko catudh\u0101tuvavatth\u0101ne vutt\u0101na\u1e43 tesa\u1e43 tesa\u1e43 dh\u0101tupariggahamukh\u0101na\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ataramukhavasena sa\u1e45khepato v\u0101 vitth\u0101rato v\u0101 catasso dh\u0101tuyo parigga\u1e47h\u0101ti. Athassa y\u0101th\u0101vasarasalakkha\u1e47ato \u0101vibh\u016bt\u0101su dh\u0101t\u016bsu kammasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101namhi t\u0101va kese \u2018\u2018catasso dh\u0101tuyo, va\u1e47\u1e47o, gandho, raso, oj\u0101, j\u012bvita\u1e43, k\u0101yappas\u0101do\u2019\u2019ti eva\u1e43 k\u0101yadasakavasena dasa r\u016bp\u0101ni, tattheva bh\u0101vassa atthit\u0101ya bh\u0101vadasakavasena dasa, tattheva \u0101h\u0101rasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 oja\u1e6d\u1e6dhamaka\u1e43, utusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, cittasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanti apar\u0101nipi catuv\u012bsat\u012bti eva\u1e43 catusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu catuv\u012bsatiko\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101sesu catucatt\u0101l\u012bsa catucatt\u0101l\u012bsa r\u016bp\u0101ni, sedo, assu, khe\u1e37o, si\u1e45gh\u0101\u1e47ik\u0101ti imesu pana cat\u016bsu utucittasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu dvinna\u1e43 oja\u1e6d\u1e6dhamak\u0101na\u1e43 vasena so\u1e37asa so\u1e37asa r\u016bp\u0101ni, udariya\u1e43, kar\u012bsa\u1e43, pubbo, muttanti imesu cat\u016bsu utusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu utusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nasseva oja\u1e6d\u1e6dhamakassa vasena a\u1e6d\u1e6dha a\u1e6d\u1e6dha r\u016bp\u0101ni p\u0101ka\u1e6d\u0101ni hont\u012bti. Esa t\u0101va dvatti\u1e43s\u0101k\u0101re nayo.",translations:{en:"But a pure-insight-vehicle meditator, or this same serenity-vehicle meditator, comprehends the four great elements either briefly or in detail by one of the approaches to the comprehension of elements stated in the Definition of the Four Elements. Then, when the elements have become manifest to him with their individual characteristics as appropriate, there become evident to him: first, in the kamma-born hair of the head, ten material phenomena by way of the body-decad\u2014'the four great elements, color, odor, flavor, nutritive essence, life, and body-sensitivity'; and there also, because of the presence of sex-materiality, ten by way of the sex-decad; and there also, the nutriment-born, temperature-born, and consciousness-born octads with nutritive essence as the eighth, thus another twenty-four. So in each of the twenty-four parts with fourfold origination, there are forty-four material phenomena. But in these four\u2014sweat, tears, saliva, and snot\u2014which are born of temperature and consciousness, there are sixteen material phenomena each by way of two octads with nutritive essence as the eighth. And in these four\u2014stomach contents, feces, pus, and urine\u2014which are born of temperature only, there are eight material phenomena each by way of the temperature-born octad with nutritive essence as the eighth, become manifest. This, for now, is the method regarding the thirty-two parts.",pt:"Por outro lado, o praticante que tem a pura introspec\xe7\xe3o como ve\xedculo (suddhavipassan\u0101y\u0101niko), ou este mesmo praticante que tem a tranquilidade como ve\xedculo (samathay\u0101niko), apreende os quatro elementos, de forma breve ou detalhada, por meio de uma das v\xe1rias portas de apreens\xe3o dos elementos descritas na defini\xe7\xe3o dos quatro elementos (catudh\u0101tuvavatth\u0101na). Ent\xe3o, quando os elementos se tornam manifestos para ele de acordo com suas caracter\xedsticas e fun\xe7\xf5es reais (y\u0101th\u0101vasarasalakkha\u1e47ato), primeiramente no cabelo (kese), que \xe9 originado pelo kamma (kammasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na): h\xe1 dez tipos de mat\xe9ria por meio da d\xe9cada do corpo (k\u0101yadasaka), a saber, \"os quatro elementos, cor, odor, sabor, ess\xeancia nutritiva, faculdade da vida e sensibilidade corporal\"; no mesmo local, devido \xe0 presen\xe7a do g\xeanero, h\xe1 dez tipos de mat\xe9ria por meio da d\xe9cada do g\xeanero (bh\u0101vadasaka); e no mesmo local, h\xe1 outras vinte e quatro mat\xe9rias, a saber, o octeto que tem a ess\xeancia nutritiva como oitava (oja\u1e6d\u1e6dhamaka) originado pelo alimento, o originado pela temperatura e o originado pela mente. Assim, nas vinte e quatro partes do corpo originadas pelas quatro causas (catusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na), h\xe1 quarenta e quatro mat\xe9rias em cada uma. No entanto, nestas quatro partes originadas pela temperatura e pela mente, a saber, suor, l\xe1grimas, saliva e secre\xe7\xe3o nasal, h\xe1 dezesseis mat\xe9rias em cada uma, por meio de dois octetos que t\xeam a ess\xeancia nutritiva como oitava. Nestas quatro partes originadas apenas pela temperatura, a saber, conte\xfado estomacal, fezes, pus e urina, h\xe1 oito mat\xe9rias em cada uma, por meio do octeto que tem a ess\xeancia nutritiva como oitava originado apenas pela temperatura. Este \xe9, primeiramente, o m\xe9todo em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s trinta e duas partes do corpo.",es:"Pero el practicante que utiliza la visi\xf3n cabal pura como veh\xedculo (suddhavipassan\u0101y\u0101niko), o ese mismo practicante que utiliza la tranquilidad como veh\xedculo, discierne los cuatro elementos, ya sea de forma resumida o detallada, mediante uno de los m\xe9todos para discernir los elementos expuestos en la definici\xf3n de los cuatro elementos. Cuando los elementos se le manifiestan a trav\xe9s de sus caracter\xedsticas y funciones reales, discierne primero en el cabello, originado por el kamma, diez tipos de materia mediante el dec\xe1dodo del cuerpo: los cuatro elementos, color, olor, sabor, esencia nutritiva, vida y la sensibilidad corporal; otros diez mediante el dec\xe1dodo del sexo, debido a la presencia del sexo all\xed mismo; y otras veinticuatro mediante el oct\xe1dodo de la esencia nutritiva originado por el alimento, el originado por la temperatura y el originado por la conciencia. As\xed, en las veinticuatro partes originadas por las cuatro causas, se manifiestan cuarenta y cuatro tipos de materia en cada una. En las cuatro partes \u2014sudor, l\xe1grimas, saliva y mucosidad\u2014 originadas por la temperatura y la conciencia, se manifiestan diecis\xe9is tipos de materia en cada una mediante los dos oct\xe1dodos de la esencia nutritiva. En las cuatro partes \u2014contenido del est\xf3mago, excremento, pus y orina\u2014 originadas \xfanicamente por la temperatura, se manifiestan ocho tipos de materia en cada una mediante el oct\xe1dodo de la esencia nutritiva. Este es el m\xe9todo para las treinta y dos partes."}},{id:"vism-18.5",pali:"Ye pana imasmi\u1e43 dvatti\u1e43s\u0101k\u0101re \u0101vibh\u016bte apare dasa \u0101k\u0101r\u0101 \u0101vibhavanti. Tattha asit\u0101diparip\u0101cake t\u0101va kammaje tejoko\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101samhi oja\u1e6d\u1e6dhamaka\xf1ceva j\u012bvita\xf1c\u0101ti nava r\u016bp\u0101ni, tath\u0101 cittaje ass\u0101sapass\u0101sako\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101sepi oja\u1e6d\u1e6dhamaka\xf1ceva saddo c\u0101ti nava, sesesu catusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu a\u1e6d\u1e6dhasu j\u012bvitanavaka\xf1ceva t\u012b\u1e47i ca oja\u1e6d\u1e6dhamak\u0101n\u012bti tetti\u1e43sa r\u016bp\u0101ni p\u0101ka\u1e6d\u0101ni honti.",translations:{en:"But when these thirty-two parts have become manifest, another ten parts become manifest. Therein, first, in the kamma-born fire-element part that digests what is eaten, drunk, etc., there are nine material phenomena: the octad with nutritive essence as the eighth and life. Similarly, in the consciousness-born in-and-out-breathing part, there are nine: the octad with nutritive essence as the eighth and sound. In the remaining eight parts with fourfold origination, thirty-three material phenomena become manifest: the life-nonad and three octads with nutritive essence as the eighth.",pt:"Quando estas trinta e duas partes se tornam manifestas, outras dez partes se manifestam. Dessas, primeiramente, na parte do elemento fogo nascida do kamma que digere o que \xe9 comido, etc. (asit\u0101diparip\u0101cake), h\xe1 nove mat\xe9rias, a saber, o octeto que tem a ess\xeancia nutritiva como oitava e a faculdade da vida. Da mesma forma, na parte da respira\xe7\xe3o (ass\u0101sapass\u0101sa) nascida da mente, h\xe1 nove mat\xe9rias, a saber, o octeto que tem a ess\xeancia nutritiva como oitava e o som. Nas restantes oito partes originadas pelas quatro causas, trinta e tr\xeas mat\xe9rias tornam-se manifestas, a saber, a n\xf4nada da vida (j\u012bvitanavaka) e tr\xeas octetos que t\xeam a ess\xeancia nutritiva como oitava.",es:"Cuando se han manifestado estas treinta y dos partes, aparecen otras diez partes adicionales. En la parte del elemento fuego originado por el kamma que digiere lo ingerido y dem\xe1s, se manifiestan nueve tipos de materia: el oct\xe1dodo de la esencia nutritiva y la facultad de la vida. Del mismo modo, en la parte de la inhalaci\xf3n y exhalaci\xf3n originada por la conciencia, se manifiestan nueve: el oct\xe1dodo de la esencia nutritiva y el sonido. En las ocho partes restantes originadas por las cuatro causas, se manifiestan treinta y tres tipos de materia mediante el non\xe1dodo de la vida y tres oct\xe1dodos de la esencia nutritiva."}},{id:"vism-18.6",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 vitth\u0101rato dv\u0101catt\u0101l\u012bs\u0101k\u0101ravasena imesu bh\u016btup\u0101d\u0101yar\u016bpesu p\u0101ka\u1e6desu j\u0101tesu vatthudv\u0101ravasena pa\xf1ca cakkhudasak\u0101dayo, hadayavatthudasaka\xf1c\u0101ti apar\u0101nipi sa\u1e6d\u1e6dhir\u016bp\u0101ni p\u0101ka\u1e6d\u0101ni honti. So sabb\u0101nipi t\u0101ni ruppanalakkha\u1e47ena ekato katv\u0101 \u2018\u2018eta\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u2019\u2019 nti passati.",translations:{en:"When for him in this way, by way of the forty-two parts in detail, these primary and derived material phenomena have become manifest, then by way of the bases and doors, another sixty material phenomena also become manifest: the five decad-groups beginning with the eye-decad, and the heart-base-decad. Having grouped them all together by the characteristic of being afflicted, he sees: 'This is materiality.'",pt:"Quando estas mat\xe9rias primordiais e derivadas se tornam manifestas para ele em detalhes, por meio das quarenta e duas partes, outras sessenta mat\xe9rias tornam-se manifestas por meio das bases e portas, a saber, as cinco d\xe9cadas que come\xe7am com a d\xe9cada do olho (cakkhudasaka) e a d\xe9cada da base do cora\xe7\xe3o (hadayavatthudasaka). Ele re\xfane todas elas sob a caracter\xedstica de sofrer altera\xe7\xe3o (ruppanalakkha\u1e47a) e v\xea: \"Isto \xe9 mat\xe9ria\".",es:"Una vez que se han manifestado as\xed estos elementos y la materia derivada detalladamente a trav\xe9s de las cuarenta y dos partes, se manifiestan otros sesenta tipos de materia mediante las bases y las puertas: los cinco dec\xe1dodos que comienzan con el del ojo y el dec\xe1dodo de la base del coraz\xf3n. El practicante agrupa todos estos tipos de materia bajo la caracter\xedstica de verse afectados y observa: \xabesto es materia\xbb."}},{id:"vism-18.7",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 pariggahitar\u016bpassa dv\u0101ravasena ar\u016bpadhamm\u0101 p\u0101ka\u1e6d\u0101 honti. Seyyathida\u1e43 \u2013 dvepa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni, tisso manodh\u0101tuyo, a\u1e6d\u1e6dhasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tuyoti ek\u0101s\u012bti lokiyacitt\u0101ni, avisesena ca tehi cittehi sahaj\u0101to phasso, vedan\u0101, sa\xf1\xf1\u0101, cetan\u0101, j\u012bvita\u1e43, citta\u1e6d\u1e6dhiti, manasik\u0101roti ime satta satta cetasik\u0101ti. Lokuttaracitt\u0101ni pana neva suddhavipassakassa, na samathay\u0101nikassa pariggaha\u1e43 gacchanti anadhigatatt\u0101ti. So sabbepi te ar\u016bpadhamme namanalakkha\u1e47ena ekato katv\u0101 \u2018\u2018eta\u1e43 n\u0101ma\u2019\u2019 nti passati. Evameko catudh\u0101tuvavatth\u0101namukhena vitth\u0101rato n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43 vavatthapeti .",translations:{en:"For one who has thus comprehended materiality, the immaterial phenomena become manifest by way of the doors. That is to say: the two sets of five consciousnesses, the three mind-elements, and the sixty-eight mind-consciousness-elements\u2014thus eighty-one mundane consciousnesses; and, without exception, associated with these consciousnesses are these seven mental factors: contact, feeling, perception, volition, life, one-pointedness, and attention. However, the supramundane consciousnesses are not comprehended by either the pure-insight-vehicle meditator or the serenity-vehicle meditator because they have not been attained. Having grouped all these immaterial phenomena together by the characteristic of bending, he sees: 'This is mentality.' Thus someone defines mentality-materiality in detail by the approach of the definition of the four elements.",pt:"Quando a mat\xe9ria \xe9 assim apreendida, os estados n\xe3o f\xedsicas (ar\u016bpadhamm\u0101) tornam-se manifestos para ele por meio das portas. A saber: as oitenta e uma consci\xeancias mundanas, que consistem nos dois conjuntos de cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais (dvepa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni), nos tr\xeas elementos da mente (manodh\u0101tuyo) e nos sessenta e oito elementos da consci\xeancia da mente (manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tuyo); e, sem distin\xe7\xe3o, os sete fatores mentais (cetasika) que surgem junto com essas consci\xeancias, a saber, contato (phassa), sensa\xe7\xe3o (vedan\u0101), percep\xe7\xe3o (sa\xf1\xf1\u0101), voli\xe7\xe3o (cetan\u0101), faculdade da vida (j\u012bvita), estabilidade mental (citta\u1e6d\u1e6dhiti) e aten\xe7\xe3o (manasik\u0101ra). No entanto, as consci\xeancias supramundanas (lokuttaracitt\u0101ni) n\xe3o entram na apreens\xe3o nem do praticante de pura introspec\xe7\xe3o, nem do praticante de tranquilidade, por n\xe3o terem sido alcan\xe7adas. Ele re\xfane todos esses estados n\xe3o f\xedsicas sob a caracter\xedstica de inclinar-se (namanalakkha\u1e47a) e v\xea: \"Isto \xe9 mente (n\u0101ma)\". Assim, um praticante define mente e mat\xe9ria em detalhes por meio da defini\xe7\xe3o dos quatro elementos.",es:"Habiendo discernido as\xed la materia, los estados inmateriales se le manifiestan a trav\xe9s de las puertas. A saber: las diez conciencias de los cinco sentidos, las tres esferas de la mente y las sesenta y ocho esferas de la conciencia de la mente, que son las ochenta y una conciencias mundanas; y, de manera general, los siete factores mentales que surgen junto con estas conciencias: contacto, sensaci\xf3n, percepci\xf3n, volici\xf3n, vida, estabilidad mental y atenci\xf3n. Sin embargo, las conciencias supramundanas no entran en el discernimiento ni del practicante de la visi\xf3n cabal pura ni del que utiliza la tranquilidad, por no haber sido a\xfan alcanzadas. \xc9l agrupa todos estos estados inmateriales bajo la caracter\xedstica de inclinarse y observa: \xabesto es mente\xbb. De este modo, un tipo de practicante define detalladamente la mentalidad y la materialidad mediante el m\xe9todo de la definici\xf3n de los cuatro elementos."}},{id:"vism-18.8",pali:"Aparo \u2018\u2018ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci r\u016bpa\u1e43 sabba\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43 catt\u0101ri mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101ni catunna\xf1ca mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101na\u1e43 up\u0101d\u0101yar\u016bpa\u2019\u2019nti (ma. ni. 1.347; a. ni. 11.17) eva\u1e43 sa\u1e43khitteneva imasmi\u1e43 attabh\u0101ve r\u016bpa\u1e43 pariggahetv\u0101, tath\u0101 man\u0101yatana\xf1ceva dhamm\u0101yatanekadesa\xf1ca n\u0101manti pariggahetv\u0101 \u2018\u2018iti ida\xf1ca n\u0101ma\u1e43 ida\xf1ca r\u016bpa\u1e43, ida\u1e43 vuccati n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u2019\u2019nti sa\u1e45khepato n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43 vavatthapeti.",translations:{en:"Another, having briefly grasped materiality in this individual existence with the concise definition, 'Whatever materiality there is, all materiality is the four great elements and the materiality derived from the four great elements,' and having likewise grasped the mind-base and a portion of the Dhamma-base as mentality, defines mentality-materiality concisely thus: 'This is mentality and this is materiality; this is called mentality-materiality.'",pt:"Outro praticante, apreendendo a mat\xe9ria nesta personalidade de forma muito breve: \"Qualquer mat\xe9ria que exista, toda mat\xe9ria consiste nos quatro grandes elementos e na mat\xe9ria derivada que depende dos quatro grandes elementos\"; e da mesma forma apreendendo a mente como a base da mente e uma parte da base dos objetos mentais, define brevemente mente e mat\xe9ria: \"Assim, isto \xe9 mente e isto \xe9 mat\xe9ria; isto \xe9 chamado de mente e mat\xe9ria\".",es:"Otro define la mentalidad y la materia de forma abreviada: \"Cualquier clase de materia que exista, toda ella consiste en los cuatro grandes elementos y la materia derivada de los cuatro grandes elementos\", comprendiendo as\xed la materia en este cuerpo de forma concisa; y comprendiendo la base de la mente y una parte de la base de los fealidades como mentalidad, concluye: \"as\xed, esto es mentalidad y esto es materia; a esto se le llama mentalidad y materia\"."}},{id:"vism-18.9",pali:"Eva\u1e43 suvisuddhar\u016bpapariggahassa panassa ar\u016bpadhamm\u0101 t\u012bhi \u0101k\u0101rehi upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhahanti phassavasena v\u0101 vedan\u0101vasena v\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47avasena v\u0101. Katha\u1e43? Ekassa t\u0101va \u2018\u2018pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu kakkha\u1e37alakkha\u1e47\u0101\u2019\u2019ti\u0101din\u0101 nayena dh\u0101tuyo parigga\u1e47hantassa pa\u1e6dham\u0101bhinip\u0101to phasso, ta\u1e43sampayutt\u0101 vedan\u0101 vedan\u0101kkhandho, sa\xf1\xf1\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101kkhandho, saddhi\u1e43 phassena cetan\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandho, citta\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47akkhandhoti upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Tath\u0101 \u2018\u2018kese pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu kakkha\u1e37alakkha\u1e47\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 ass\u0101sapass\u0101se pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu kakkha\u1e37alakkha\u1e47\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (visuddhi. 1.307) pa\u1e6dham\u0101bhinip\u0101to phasso, ta\u1e43sampayutt\u0101 vedan\u0101 vedan\u0101kkhandho\u2026pe\u2026 citta\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47akkhandhoti upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Eva\u1e43 ar\u016bpadhamm\u0101 phassavasena upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhahanti.",translations:{en:"To one who has thus grasped materiality with thorough purity, immaterial phenomena become apparent in three ways: by way of contact, by way of feeling, or by way of consciousness. How so? For one who is grasping the elements by the method beginning, \u2018The earth element has the characteristic of hardness,\u2019 the initial impact is contact. The feeling associated with it is the feeling aggregate; perception is the perception aggregate; volition together with contact is the formations aggregate; and consciousness is the consciousness aggregate\u2014thus they become apparent. Similarly, when considering, \u2018In the hair of the head, the earth element has the characteristic of hardness\u2026 and so on \u2026 in the in-breaths and out-breaths, the earth element has the characteristic of hardness,\u2019 the initial impact is contact. The feeling associated with it is the feeling aggregate\u2026 and so on \u2026 consciousness is the consciousness aggregate\u2014thus they become apparent. In this way, immaterial phenomena become apparent by way of contact.",pt:"Para aquele que assim purificou completamente a sua apreens\xe3o da mat\xe9ria, os estados n\xe3o f\xedsicas tornam-se manifestos de tr\xeas maneiras: por meio do contato, por meio da sensa\xe7\xe3o ou por meio da consci\xeancia. Como? Primeiramente, para quem apreende os elementos desta maneira: \"O elemento terra tem a caracter\xedstica de dureza\", etc., o contato (phasso) como o primeiro impacto (pa\u1e6dham\u0101bhinip\u0101to) torna-se manifesto. A sensa\xe7\xe3o associada a ele \xe9 o agregado da sensa\xe7\xe3o; a percep\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o agregado da percep\xe7\xe3o; a voli\xe7\xe3o junto com o contato \xe9 o agregado das forma\xe7\xf5es mentais; a mente \xe9 o agregado da consci\xeancia \u2014 assim eles se tornam manifestos. Da mesma forma, no cabelo: \"O elemento terra tem a caracter\xedstica de dureza... at\xe9... na inspira\xe7\xe3o e expira\xe7\xe3o, o elemento terra tem a caracter\xedstica de dureza\", o contato como o primeiro impacto torna-se manifesto. A sensa\xe7\xe3o associada a ele \xe9 o agregado da sensa\xe7\xe3o... at\xe9... a mente \xe9 o agregado da consci\xeancia \u2014 assim eles se tornam manifestos. Desta forma, os estados n\xe3o f\xedsicas tornam-se manifestos por meio do contato.",es:"Para quien ha purificado completamente la comprensi\xf3n de la materia, los fealidades inmateriales se manifiestan de tres maneras: a trav\xe9s del contacto, de la sensaci\xf3n o de la conciencia. \xb1C\xf3mo? Para uno, al comprender los elementos mediante el m\xe9todo \"el elemento tierra tiene la caracter\xedstica de la dureza\", etc., se manifiesta el contacto como el primer encuentro con el objeto; la sensaci\xf3n asociada a \xe9l es el agregado de la sensaci\xf3n, la percepci\xf3n es el agregado de la percepci\xf3n, la voluntad junto con el contacto es el agregado de las formaciones, y la mente es el agregado de la conciencia. Del mismo modo, al comprender \"en el cabello, el elemento tierra tiene la caracter\xedstica de la dureza... en la inhalaci\xf3n y exhalaci\xf3n, el elemento tierra tiene la caracter\xedstica de la dureza\", se manifiesta el primer encuentro como el contacto, la sensaci\xf3n asociada como el agregado de la sensaci\xf3n... y la mente como el agregado de la conciencia. As\xed, los fealidades inmateriales se manifiestan a trav\xe9s del contacto."}},{id:"vism-18.10",pali:"So eva\u1e43 phass\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 vasena upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhite catt\u0101ro ar\u016bpino khandhe n\u0101manti, tesa\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47abh\u016bt\u0101ni catt\u0101ri mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101ni, catunna\xf1ca mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101na\u1e43 up\u0101d\u0101yar\u016bpa\u1e43 r\u016bpanti vavatthapeti. Iti a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa dh\u0101tuyo dv\u0101das\u0101yatan\u0101ni pa\xf1cakkhandh\u0101ti sabbepi tebh\u016bmake dhamme khaggena samugga\u1e43 vivaram\u0101no viya yamakat\u0101lakanda\u1e43 ph\u0101layam\u0101no viya ca n\u0101ma\xf1ca r\u016bpa\xf1c\u0101ti dvedh\u0101 vavatthapeti. N\u0101mar\u016bpamattato uddha\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1o satto v\u0101 puggalo v\u0101 devo v\u0101 brahm\u0101 v\u0101 natth\u012bti ni\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43 gacchati.",translations:{en:"He thus determines the four immaterial aggregates, which have become apparent by way of contact and so on, as \u2018mentality\u2019; and he determines the four great elements that are their object, along with the derived materiality dependent on the four great elements, as \u2018materiality.\u2019 Thus, like one opening a casket with a sword or splitting a twin palm shoot, he divides all these phenomena of the three planes\u2014the eighteen elements, the twelve bases, and the five aggregates\u2014into two parts as \u2018mentality and materiality.\u2019 He comes to the conclusion: \u2018Beyond mere mentality-and-materiality, there is no other being or person, no deva or brahm\u0101.\u2019",pt:"Ele define assim os quatro agregados imateriais que se manifestam por meio do contato e outros fatores como 'mente' (n\u0101ma), e define como 'mat\xe9ria' (r\u016bpa) os quatro grandes elementos que servem de objeto para eles, bem como a mat\xe9ria derivada dos quatro grandes elementos. Assim, ele define em duas partes, como mente e mat\xe9ria, todos os dhammas dos tr\xeas planos de exist\xeancia \u2014 a saber, os dezoito elementos, as doze bases e os cinco agregados \u2014, como quem abre uma caixa com uma espada ou como quem fende ao meio um broto duplo de palmeira. Ele chega \xe0 conclus\xe3o de que, al\xe9m de mera mente e mat\xe9ria, n\xe3o existe nenhum outro ser, pessoa, deva ou brahm\u0101.",es:"\xc9l define as\xed como 'nombre' (n\u0101ma) a los cuatro agregados inmateriales que se manifiestan mediante el contacto y dem\xe1s; y define como 'forma' (r\u016bpa) a los cuatro grandes elementos que son sus objetos, as\xed como a la materia derivada de los cuatro grandes elementos. De este modo, define en dos partes, como nombre y forma, a todos los fealidades de los tres planos \u2014las dieciocho esferas, los doce campos sensoriales y los cinco agregados\u2014, como si abriera una caja con una espada o como si partiera el brote de una palmera gemela. Llega a la conclusi\xf3n de que, m\xe1s all\xe1 de mero nombre y forma, no existe ning\xfan ser, persona, deva o brahma."}},{id:"vism-18.11",pali:"So eva\u1e43 y\u0101th\u0101vasarasato n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43 vavatthapetv\u0101 su\u1e6d\u1e6dhutara\u1e43 \u2018\u2018satto puggalo\u2019\u2019ti imiss\u0101 lokasama\xf1\xf1\u0101ya pah\u0101natth\u0101ya sattasammohassa samatikkamatth\u0101ya asammohabh\u016bmiya\u1e43 citta\u1e43 \u1e6dhapanatth\u0101ya sambahulasuttantavasena \u2018\u2018n\u0101mar\u016bpamattamevida\u1e43, na satto, na puggalo atth\u012b\u2019\u2019ti etamattha\u1e43 sa\u1e43sandetv\u0101 vavatthapeti. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"Having thus determined mentality-and-materiality according to its true nature, in order to more thoroughly abandon the worldly convention \u2018a being,\u2019 \u2018a person,\u2019 in order to overcome the delusion about a being, and in order to establish the mind in the domain of non-delusion, he correlates this meaning with many suttas and determines it thus: \u2018This is merely mentality-and-materiality; there is no being, no person.\u2019 For it is said:",pt:"Tendo assim definido a mente e a mat\xe9ria de acordo com a sua verdadeira natureza essencial, a fim de abandonar ainda melhor essa designa\xe7\xe3o mundana de 'ser' ou 'pessoa', para superar a ilus\xe3o de um ser e estabelecer a mente no est\xe1gio da n\xe3o ilus\xe3o, ele define e confirma esse significado de acordo com numerosos suttas: 'Isto \xe9 apenas mente e mat\xe9ria; n\xe3o existe ser, n\xe3o existe pessoa'. Pois foi dito:",es:"Habiendo definido as\xed el nombre y la forma seg\xfan su naturaleza real, para abandonar m\xe1s eficazmente la designaci\xf3n convencional de 'ser' y 'persona', para trascender la confusi\xf3n respecto a los seres y para establecer la mente en el terreno de la no-confusi\xf3n, \xe9l correlaciona y define este significado mediante numerosos Suttas: 'Esto es solo nombre y forma, no existe un ser ni una persona'. Pues se ha dicho:"}},{id:"vism-18.12",pali:"\u2018\u2018Yath\u0101pi a\u1e45gasambh\u0101r\u0101, hoti saddo ratho iti; Eva\u1e43 khandhesu santesu, hoti sattoti sammut\u012b\u2019\u2019ti. (sa\u1e43. ni. 1.171);",translations:{en:"\u201cJust as with an assemblage of parts, The word \u2018chariot\u2019 is used; So, when the aggregates are present, There is the convention \u2018a being.\u2019\u201d",pt:"'Assim como, pela reuni\xe3o de suas partes, surge o nome \"carruagem\", da mesma forma, existindo os agregados, h\xe1 a conven\xe7\xe3o de \"um ser\".'",es:"\u201cAs\xed como por el conjunto de las partes surge el nombre de \u2018carro\u2019, as\xed cuando existen los agregados, surge la convenci\xf3n de \u2018ser\u2019.\u201d"}},{id:"vism-18.13",pali:"\u2018\u2018Dukkhameva hi sambhoti, dukkha\u1e43 ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhati veti ca; N\u0101\xf1\xf1atra dukkh\u0101 sambhoti, n\u0101\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 dukkh\u0101 nirujjhat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti. (sa\u1e43. ni. 1.171);",translations:{en:"\u201cIt is only suffering that comes to be, Suffering that persists and passes away. Nothing other than suffering comes to be, Nothing other than suffering ceases.\u201d",pt:"'Apenas o sofrimento surge, o sofrimento permanece e desaparece; nada al\xe9m do sofrimento surge, nada al\xe9m do sofrimento cessa.'",es:"\u201cSolo el sufrimiento surge, el sufrimiento permanece y se desvanece; nada m\xe1s que el sufrimiento surge, nada m\xe1s que el sufrimiento cesa\u201d."}},{id:"vism-18.14",pali:"Tasm\u0101 yath\u0101 d\u0101ruyanta\u1e43 su\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 nijj\u012bva\u1e43 nir\u012bhaka\u1e43, atha ca pana d\u0101rurajjukasam\u0101yogavasena gacchatipi ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhatipi. Sa\u012bhaka\u1e43 saby\u0101p\u0101ra\u1e43 viya kh\u0101yati, evamida\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bpampi su\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 nijj\u012bva\u1e43 nir\u012bhaka\u1e43, atha ca pana a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1asam\u0101yogavasena gacchatipi ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhatipi. Sa\u012bhaka\u1e43 saby\u0101p\u0101ra\u1e43 viya kh\u0101yat\u012bti da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43. Ten\u0101hu por\u0101\u1e47\u0101 \u2013",translations:{en:"Therefore, just as a wooden automaton is empty, lifeless, and inert, yet by means of the connection of wood and strings it moves and stands and appears as if it has volition and is active, so too this name-and-form is empty, lifeless, and inert, yet by means of their mutual connection it moves and stands and appears as if it has volition and is active. Thus it should be understood. Therefore the ancients have said:",pt:"Portanto, assim como um boneco de madeira \xe9 vazio, sem vida e sem iniciativa pr\xf3pria, mas, devido \xe0 combina\xe7\xe3o de madeira e cordas, ele caminha e permanece de p\xe9, parecendo ter iniciativa e atividade pr\xf3pria; exatamente da mesma forma, esta mente e mat\xe9ria tamb\xe9m s\xe3o vazias, sem vida e sem iniciativa pr\xf3pria, mas, devido \xe0 sua m\xfatua combina\xe7\xe3o, caminham e permanecem de p\xe9, parecendo ter iniciativa e atividade pr\xf3pria. Assim deve ser visto. Por isso disseram os antigos:",es:"Por lo tanto, as\xed como una marioneta de madera est\xe1 vac\xeda, carece de vida y de voluntad propia, pero camina y se detiene debido a la combinaci\xf3n de la madera y las cuerdas, y parece que tuviera voluntad y actividad; del mismo modo, este nombre y forma (mente y cuerpo) est\xe1 vac\xedo, carece de vida y de voluntad propia, pero camina y se detiene mediante la combinaci\xf3n mutua. Debe verse como si tuviera voluntad y actividad. Por eso dijeron los antiguos:"}},{id:"vism-18.15",pali:"\u2018\u2018N\u0101ma\xf1ca r\u016bpa\xf1ca idhatthi saccato, Na hettha satto manujo ca vijjati; Su\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 ida\u1e43 yantamiv\u0101bhisa\u1e45khata\u1e43, Dukkhassa pu\xf1jo ti\u1e47aka\u1e6d\u1e6dhas\u0101diso\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"\"Here there truly are but name and form, / No being is found herein, no person; / This is void, constructed like an automaton, / A mass of suffering, like grass and sticks.\"",pt:"'Mente e mat\xe9ria existem aqui em verdade, mas nenhum ser ou homem \xe9 encontrado aqui. Isto \xe9 vazio, constru\xeddo como um boneco mec\xe2nico, um mero ac\xfamulo de sofrimento, semelhante a grama e madeira.'",es:"\xabEl nombre y la forma existen aqu\xed en verdad, pero aqu\xed no se encuentra ning\xfan ser ni humano; esto est\xe1 vac\xedo, como una marioneta construida, un mont\xf3n de sufrimiento similar a la hierba y la madera\xbb."}},{id:"vism-18.16",pali:"\u2018\u2018Yamaka\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bpa\xf1ca, ubho a\xf1\xf1o\xf1\xf1anissit\u0101; Ekasmi\u1e43 bhijjam\u0101nasmi\u1e43, ubho bhijjanti paccay\u0101\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"\"Name-and-form are a pair, both mutually dependent. When one is broken, both conditions break.\"",pt:"'A mente e a mat\xe9ria s\xe3o um par, ambas dependentes uma da outra; quando uma se desintegra, ambas se desintegram devido \xe0 cessa\xe7\xe3o de suas condi\xe7\xf5es.'",es:"\xabEl nombre y la forma son un par, ambos dependen el uno del otro; al romperse uno, ambos se rompen debido a su condici\xf3n\xbb."}},{id:"vism-18.17",pali:"Yath\u0101 ca da\u1e47\u1e0d\u0101bhihata\u1e43 bheri\u1e43 niss\u0101ya sadde pavattam\u0101ne a\xf1\xf1\u0101 bher\u012b, a\xf1\xf1o saddo, bherisadd\u0101 asammiss\u0101, bher\u012b saddena su\xf1\xf1\u0101, saddo bheriy\u0101 su\xf1\xf1o, evameva\u1e43 vatthudv\u0101r\u0101ramma\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43 niss\u0101ya n\u0101me pavattam\u0101ne a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43, a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 n\u0101ma\u1e43, n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101 asammiss\u0101, n\u0101ma\u1e43 r\u016bpena su\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, r\u016bpa\u1e43 n\u0101mena su\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, apica kho bheri\u1e43 pa\u1e6dicca saddo viya r\u016bpa\u1e43 pa\u1e6dicca n\u0101ma\u1e43 pavattati. Ten\u0101hu por\u0101\u1e47\u0101 \u2013",translations:{en:"And just as when a drum is struck with a stick, sound occurs in dependence on it, the drum is one thing and the sound another; the drum and sound are unmixed; the drum is void of sound, and the sound is void of the drum. So too, when name occurs in dependence on form\u2014that is, the physical basis, door, and object\u2014form is one thing and name another; name and form are unmixed; name is void of form, and form is void of name. And yet, just as sound occurs in dependence on a drum, so name occurs in dependence on form. Therefore the ancients have said:",pt:"E assim como, quando o som surge dependendo de um tambor golpeado por uma baqueta, o tambor \xe9 uma coisa e o som \xe9 outra, o tambor e o som n\xe3o se misturam, o tambor \xe9 vazio de som e o som \xe9 vazio de tambor; exatamente da mesma forma, quando a mente surge dependendo da mat\xe9ria constitu\xedda pela base f\xedsica, pela porta e pelo objeto, a mat\xe9ria \xe9 uma coisa e a mente \xe9 outra, a mente e a mat\xe9ria n\xe3o se misturam, a mente \xe9 vazia de mat\xe9ria e a mat\xe9ria \xe9 vazia de mente. Contudo, assim como o som surge dependendo do tambor, a mente surge dependendo da mat\xe9ria. Por isso disseram os antigos:",es:"Y as\xed como cuando surge el sonido dependiendo de un tambor golpeado por un mazo, el tambor es una cosa y el sonido es otra, el tambor y el sonido no est\xe1n mezclados, el tambor est\xe1 vac\xedo de sonido y el sonido est\xe1 vac\xedo de tambor; de la misma manera, cuando surge el nombre dependiendo de la materia conocida como base, puerta y objeto, la materia es una cosa y el nombre es otra, el nombre y la forma no est\xe1n mezclados, el nombre est\xe1 vac\xedo de la forma y la forma est\xe1 vac\xeda del nombre. Sin embargo, as\xed como el sonido depende del tambor, el nombre procede dependiendo de la forma. Por eso dijeron los antiguos:"}},{id:"vism-18.18",pali:"Imassa panatthassa vibh\u0101vanatth\u0101ya ima\u1e43 upama\u1e43 ud\u0101haranti \u2013 yath\u0101 jaccandho ca p\u012b\u1e6dhasapp\u012b ca dis\u0101pakkamituk\u0101m\u0101 assu, jaccandho p\u012b\u1e6dhasappi\u1e43 evam\u0101ha \u2018\u2018aha\u1e43 kho bha\u1e47e, sakkomi p\u0101dehi p\u0101dakara\u1e47\u012bya\u1e43 k\u0101tu\u1e43, natthi ca me cakkh\u016bni yehi samavisama\u1e43 passeyya\u2019\u2019nti. P\u012b\u1e6dhasapp\u012bpi jaccandha\u1e43 evam\u0101ha \u2018\u2018aha\u1e43 kho bha\u1e47e, sakkomi cakkhun\u0101 cakkhukara\u1e47\u012bya\u1e43 k\u0101tu\u1e43, natthi ca me p\u0101d\u0101ni yehi abhikkameyya\u1e43 v\u0101 pa\u1e6dikkameyya\u1e43 v\u0101\u2019\u2019ti. So tu\u1e6d\u1e6dhaha\u1e6d\u1e6dho jaccandho p\u012b\u1e6dhasappi\u1e43 a\u1e43sak\u016b\u1e6da\u1e43 \u0101ropesi. P\u012b\u1e6dhasapp\u012b jaccandhassa a\u1e43sak\u016b\u1e6de nis\u012bditv\u0101 evam\u0101ha \u2018\u2018v\u0101ma\u1e43 mu\xf1ca dakkhi\u1e47a\u1e43 ga\u1e47ha, dakkhi\u1e47a\u1e43 mu\xf1ca v\u0101ma\u1e43 ga\u1e47h\u0101\u2019\u2019ti. Tattha jaccandhopi nittejo dubbalo na sakena tejena sakena balena gacchati, p\u012b\u1e6dhasapp\u012bpi nittejo dubbalo na sakena tejena sakena balena gacchati, na ca tesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 niss\u0101ya gamana\u1e43 nappavattati, evameva\u1e43 n\u0101mampi nitteja\u1e43 na sakena tejena uppajjati, na t\u0101su t\u0101su kiriy\u0101su pavattati. R\u016bpampi nitteja\u1e43 na sakena tejena uppajjati, na t\u0101su t\u0101su kiriy\u0101su pavattati, na ca tesa\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 niss\u0101ya uppatti v\u0101 pavatti v\u0101 na hoti. Teneta\u1e43 vuccati \u2013",translations:{en:"To elucidate this meaning, they cite the following simile. Suppose a man born blind and a cripple wanted to go on a journey. The man born blind said to the cripple: 'Friend, I can do with my feet what needs to be done by feet, but I have no eyes with which to see the even and uneven ground.' The cripple, too, said to the man born blind: 'Friend, I can do with my eyes what needs to be done by eyes, but I have no feet with which to go forward or back.' The man born blind, glad and delighted, mounted the cripple on his shoulders. And the cripple, sitting on the shoulders of the man born blind, directed him, saying: 'Leave the left and take the right; leave the right and take the left.' Here, the man born blind is powerless and weak; he cannot go by his own power and strength. The cripple, too, is powerless and weak; he cannot go by his own power and strength. Yet it is not the case that their journey does not proceed when they are dependent on each other. In the same way, name is powerless; it cannot arise by its own power, nor can it proceed in this or that activity. Form, too, is powerless; it cannot arise by its own power, nor can it proceed in this or that activity. Yet it is not the case that their arising or proceeding does not happen when they are dependent on each other. Therefore it is said:",pt:"Para esclarecer este significado, os antigos mestres apresentam a seguinte par\xe1bola: Suponha que um cego de nascen\xe7a e um paral\xedtico desejassem partir para alguma dire\xe7\xe3o. O cego disse ao paral\xedtico: 'Olha, meu amigo, eu posso, com as minhas pernas, realizar a a\xe7\xe3o de caminhar, mas n\xe3o tenho olhos com os quais possa ver o que \xe9 plano ou acidentado'. O paral\xedtico tamb\xe9m disse ao cego: 'Olha, meu amigo, eu posso, com os meus olhos, realizar a a\xe7\xe3o de ver, mas n\xe3o tenho pernas com as quais possa avan\xe7ar ou recuar'. Satisfeito e alegre, o cego colocou o paral\xedtico sobre os seus ombros. O paral\xedtico, sentado nos ombros do cego, disse-lhe: 'Deixe a esquerda, pegue a direita; deixe a direita, pegue a esquerda'. Nessa situa\xe7\xe3o, o cego, sendo desprovido de poder e fraco, n\xe3o caminha por sua pr\xf3pria for\xe7a ou poder; o paral\xedtico tamb\xe9m, sendo desprovido de poder e fraco, n\xe3o caminha por sua pr\xf3pria for\xe7a ou poder. No entanto, a caminhada deles n\xe3o deixa de ocorrer quando dependem um do outro. Da mesma forma, a mente (nama) tamb\xe9m \xe9 desprovida de poder; n\xe3o surge por sua pr\xf3pria for\xe7a, nem atua nesta ou naquela atividade. A mat\xe9ria (rupa) tamb\xe9m \xe9 desprovida de poder; n\xe3o surge por sua pr\xf3pria for\xe7a, nem atua nesta ou naquela atividade. Contudo, o surgimento ou a continuidade de ambos n\xe3o deixa de ocorrer quando dependem um do outro. Por isso, foi dito:",es:"Para aclarar este punto, citan esta analog\xeda: supongamos que un ciego de nacimiento y un lisiado desearan emprender un viaje. El ciego de nacimiento le dice al lisiado: \xabAmigo, yo puedo realizar con mis piernas la tarea de caminar, pero no tengo ojos con los que pueda ver lo que es terreno llano o escabroso\xbb. El lisiado tambi\xe9n le dice al ciego: \xabAmigo, yo puedo realizar con mi ojo la tarea de ver, pero no tengo piernas con las que pueda avanzar o retroceder\xbb. Entonces, el ciego, complacido y alegre, subi\xf3 al lisiado sobre sus hombros. El lisiado, sentado sobre los hombros del ciego, le dec\xeda: \xabDeja la izquierda, toma la derecha; deja la derecha, toma la izquierda\xbb. All\xed, el ciego carece de poder, es d\xe9bil y no puede caminar por su propio poder y fuerza. El lisiado tambi\xe9n carece de poder, es d\xe9bil y no puede caminar por su propio poder y fuerza. Pero no es que el acto de caminar no ocurra cuando dependen el uno del otro. Del mismo modo, el nombre carece de poder y no surge por su propio poder, ni procede en tales y cuales acciones. La forma tambi\xe9n carece de poder y no surge por su propio poder, ni procede en tales y cuales funciones. Pero no es que su surgimiento o procedencia no ocurra cuando dependen el uno del otro. Por eso se dice:"}},{id:"vism-18.19",pali:"\u2018\u2018Yath\u0101pi n\u0101va\u1e43 niss\u0101ya, manuss\u0101 yanti a\u1e47\u1e47ave; Evameva r\u016bpa\u1e43 niss\u0101ya, n\u0101mak\u0101yo pavattati.",translations:{en:"\"Just as people travel on the ocean depending on a boat, So too, the mental body proceeds depending on form.",pt:"\u201cAssim como, dependendo de um barco, os homens navegam no oceano; da mesma forma, dependendo da mat\xe9ria, o corpo mental prossegue.",es:"\xabAs\xed como los hombres cruzan el oc\xe9ano apoy\xe1ndose en un barco, del mismo modo el grupo del nombre procede apoy\xe1ndose en la forma\xbb."}},{id:"vism-18.20",pali:"Eva\u1e43 n\u0101n\u0101nayehi n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43 vavatth\u0101payato sattasa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 abhibhavitv\u0101 asammohabh\u016bmiya\u1e43 \u1e6dhita\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43 y\u0101th\u0101vadassana\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddh\u012b ti veditabba\u1e43. N\u0101mar\u016bpavavatth\u0101na ntipi sa\u1e45kh\u0101raparicchedo tipi etasseva adhivacana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Thus, the seeing of name-and-form as it really is\u2014by one who defines it in these various ways, has overcome the perception of a being, and is established in the domain of non-delusion\u2014should be known as the purification of view. 'Definition of name-and-form' and 'delimitation of formations' are also designations for this very thing.",pt:"Assim, para quem define a mente e a mat\xe9ria atrav\xe9s de v\xe1rios m\xe9todos, superando a percep\xe7\xe3o de um ser e estabelecendo-se no solo da n\xe3o ilus\xe3o, a vis\xe3o correta da mente e da mat\xe9ria como elas realmente s\xe3o deve ser entendida como purifica\xe7\xe3o da vis\xe3o. 'Defini\xe7\xe3o de mente e mat\xe9ria' e 'delimita\xe7\xe3o das forma\xe7\xf5es' s\xe3o tamb\xe9m sin\xf4nimos para esta mesma realiza\xe7\xe3o.",es:"As\xed, la visi\xf3n correcta de aquel que define el nombre y la forma mediante diversos m\xe9todos, habiendo superado la percepci\xf3n de \xabser\xbb y establecido en el terreno de la no confusi\xf3n, debe conocerse como purificaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddhi). Los t\xe9rminos \xabdefinici\xf3n de nombre y forma\xbb y \xabdelimitaci\xf3n de las formaciones\xbb son sin\xf3nimos de esta misma purificaci\xf3n."}}]},436,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,i,s,n,t){s.exports=[{id:"vism-19.1",pali:"Etasseva pana n\u0101mar\u016bpassa paccayapariggaha\u1e47ena t\u012bsu addh\u0101su ka\u1e45kha\u1e43 vitaritv\u0101 \u1e6dhita\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 ka\u1e45kh\u0101vitara\u1e47avisuddhi n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"The knowledge that is established by having overcome doubt about the three periods of time through the comprehension of the conditions for this very name-and-form is called the purification by overcoming doubt.",pt:"O conhecimento estabelecido ao superar a d\xfavida nos tr\xeas per\xedodos de tempo atrav\xe9s da compreens\xe3o das condi\xe7\xf5es desta mesma mente e mat\xe9ria \xe9 chamado de purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo superamento da d\xfavida.",es:"El conocimiento que se establece tras haber superado la duda en los tres periodos de tiempo mediante la comprensi\xf3n de las condiciones de esta misma mentalidad y materialidad se denomina Purificaci\xf3n por la Superaci\xf3n de la Duda."}},{id:"vism-19.2",pali:"Ta\u1e43 samp\u0101detuk\u0101mo bhikkhu yath\u0101 n\u0101ma kusalo bhisakko roga\u1e43 disv\u0101 tassa samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 pariyesati. Yath\u0101 v\u0101 pana anukampako puriso dahara\u1e43 kum\u0101ra\u1e43 manda\u1e43 utt\u0101naseyyaka\u1e43 rathik\u0101ya nipanna\u1e43 disv\u0101 \u2018\u2018kassa nu kho aya\u1e43 puttako\u2019\u2019ti tassa m\u0101t\u0101pitaro \u0101vajjati, evameva tassa n\u0101mar\u016bpassa hetupaccayapariyesana\u1e43 \u0101pajjati.",translations:{en:"A bhikkhu who wishes to accomplish this undertakes the investigation of the causes and conditions of that name-and-form, just as a skilled physician, upon seeing a disease, seeks its origin; or just as a compassionate man who, upon seeing a tender, helpless infant lying on its back in the street, wonders, \"Whose child is this?\" and considers its parents.",pt:"O bhikkhu que deseja realizar isso, assim como um m\xe9dico habilidoso que, ao ver uma doen\xe7a, busca a sua origem, ou como um homem compassivo que, ao ver um beb\xea pequeno, fr\xe1gil e deitado de costas na rua, pensa: 'De quem ser\xe1 este filho?' e investiga quem s\xe3o os seus pais, da mesma forma ele se empenha na busca pelas causas e condi\xe7\xf5es daquela mente e mat\xe9ria.",es:"El monje que desea lograr esto, tal como un m\xe9dico experto que, habiendo visto una enfermedad, busca su origen; o como un hombre compasivo que, al ver a un ni\xf1o peque\xf1o e indefenso acostado de espaldas en la calle, reflexiona: \"\xbfDe qui\xe9n ser\xe1 este hijo?\", y busca a sus padres; del mismo modo, se dedica a buscar las causas y condiciones de esa mentalidad y materialidad."}},{id:"vism-19.3",pali:"So \u0101ditova iti pa\u1e6disa\xf1cikkhati \u2018\u2018na t\u0101vidha\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43 ahetuka\u1e43, sabbattha sabbad\u0101 sabbesa\xf1ca ekasadisabh\u0101v\u0101pattito, na issar\u0101dihetuka\u1e43, n\u0101mar\u016bpato uddha\u1e43 issar\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 abh\u0101vato. Yepi n\u0101mar\u016bpamattameva issar\u0101dayoti vadanti, tesa\u1e43 issar\u0101disa\u1e45kh\u0101tan\u0101mar\u016bpassa ahetukabh\u0101vappattito. Tasm\u0101 bhavitabbamassa hetupaccayehi, ke nu kho te\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"From the very beginning, he reflects thus: \"This name-and-form is not without a cause, for that would entail that it would have a single, uniform nature everywhere, at all times, and for all beings. Nor is it caused by a creator god (Issara), etc., for there are no such creators apart from name-and-form. And for those who say that a creator, etc., is nothing but name-and-form, it would follow that the name-and-form designated as 'creator' is itself without a cause. Therefore, it must have causes and conditions. Now, what are they?\"",pt:"Ele primeiro reflete da seguinte maneira: 'Esta mente e mat\xe9ria n\xe3o s\xe3o sem causa, pois em todos os lugares, em todos os tempos e para todos os seres, elas apresentam uma uniformidade semelhante. Elas tamb\xe9m n\xe3o s\xe3o causadas por um Criador (Issara) ou algo semelhante, pois n\xe3o existe nenhum Criador al\xe9m da mente e da mat\xe9ria. Mesmo para aqueles que afirmam que o Criador \xe9 apenas mente e mat\xe9ria, a mente e a mat\xe9ria chamadas de \"Criador\" seriam, nesse caso, sem causa. Portanto, elas devem ter causas e condi\xe7\xf5es. Quais seriam elas?'",es:"Al principio, \xe9l reflexiona as\xed: \"Esta mentalidad y materialidad no carecen de causa, porque si no la tuvieran, todas las cosas ser\xedan iguales para todos, en todo lugar y en todo momento. Tampoco son creadas por un Se\xf1or (Issara) o causas similares, porque m\xe1s all\xe1 de la mentalidad y la materialidad no existe tal Se\xf1or. Incluso para quienes dicen que el Se\xf1or y otros son solo mentalidad y materialidad, su supuesta causa carecer\xeda de fundamento. Por lo tanto, deben existir causas y condiciones; \xbfcu\xe1les podr\xedan ser?\"."}},{id:"vism-19.4",pali:"So eva\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bpassa hetupaccaye \u0101vajjetv\u0101 imassa t\u0101va r\u016bpak\u0101yassa eva\u1e43 hetupaccaye parigga\u1e47h\u0101ti \u2013 \u2018\u2018aya\u1e43 k\u0101yo nibbattam\u0101no neva uppalapadumapu\u1e47\u1e0dar\u012bkasogandhik\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 abbhantare nibbattati, na ma\u1e47imutt\u0101h\u0101r\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43, atha kho \u0101m\u0101sayapakk\u0101say\u0101na\u1e43 antare udarapa\u1e6dala\u1e43 pacchato pi\u1e6d\u1e6dhika\u1e47\u1e6daka\u1e43 purato katv\u0101 antaantagu\u1e47apariv\u0101rito sayampi duggandhajegucchapa\u1e6dikk\u016blo duggandhajegucchapa\u1e6dikk\u016ble paramasamb\u0101dhe ok\u0101se p\u016btimacchap\u016btikumm\u0101sao\u1e37igallacandanik\u0101d\u012bsu kimiva nibbattati. Tasseva\u1e43 nibbattam\u0101nassa \u2018avijj\u0101 ta\u1e47h\u0101 up\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 kamma\u2019nti ime catt\u0101ro dhamm\u0101 nibbattakatt\u0101 hetu, \u0101h\u0101ro upatthambhakatt\u0101 paccayo ti pa\xf1ca dhamm\u0101 hetupaccay\u0101 honti. Tesupi avijj\u0101dayo tayo imassa k\u0101yassa m\u0101t\u0101 viya d\u0101rakassa upanissay\u0101 honti. Kamma\u1e43 pit\u0101 viya puttassa janaka\u1e43. \u0100h\u0101ro dh\u0101ti viya d\u0101rakassa sandh\u0101rako\u2019\u2019ti. Eva\u1e43 r\u016bpak\u0101yassa paccayapariggaha\u1e43 katv\u0101, puna \u2018\u2018cakkhu\xf1ca pa\u1e6dicca r\u016bpe ca uppajjati cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti\u0101din\u0101 (sa\u1e43. ni. 2.43) nayena n\u0101mak\u0101yassa paccayapariggaha\u1e43 karoti.",translations:{en:"Having thus adverted to the causes and conditions of name-and-form, he first comprehends the causes and conditions of this material body as follows: 'This body, when it is produced, is not produced inside a blue lotus, red lotus, white lotus, water lily, or the like, nor inside jewels, pearls, necklaces, or the like. Rather, it is produced between the stomach and the intestines, with the belly-lining behind and the backbone in front, surrounded by the entrails and mesentery, itself foul-smelling, disgusting, and repulsive, in an extremely confined, foul-smelling, disgusting, and repulsive place, like a worm in rotting fish, in putrid gruel, in a cesspool, or in a sewer. When it is thus produced, these four things\u2014ignorance, craving, clinging, and kamma\u2014are its causes because they are its producers, while nutriment is its condition because it is its supporter. Thus, these five things are its causes and conditions. Among them, the three beginning with ignorance are the support for this body, like a mother is for her child. Kamma is the generator, like a father is for his son. Nutriment is the sustainer, like a wet-nurse is for the infant.' Having thus comprehended the conditions of the material body, he then comprehends the conditions of the mental body by the method beginning: 'Dependent on the eye and forms, eye-consciousness arises' (SN 12.43).",pt:"Tendo assim refletido sobre as causas e condi\xe7\xf5es da mente e da mat\xe9ria, ele primeiro compreende as causas e condi\xe7\xf5es deste corpo material da seguinte forma: 'Este corpo, ao nascer, n\xe3o nasce no interior de l\xf3tus azuis, vermelhos ou brancos, nem dentro de colares de joias e p\xe9rolas. Pelo contr\xe1rio, ele nasce entre o est\xf4mago e o intestino grosso, tendo a membrana abdominal atr\xe1s e a espinha dorsal \xe0 frente, cercado pelas entranhas e intestinos, sendo ele pr\xf3prio f\xe9tido, repugnante e asqueroso, em um espa\xe7o extremamente confinado, como um verme em peixe podre, mingau azedo, uma fossa ou um esgoto. Para este corpo que assim nasce, estes quatro fatores \u2014 a ignor\xe2ncia, o desejo, o apego e o kamma \u2014 s\xe3o as causas (hetu) porque o produzem; e o alimento \xe9 a condi\xe7\xe3o (paccaya) porque o sustenta. Assim, estes cinco fatores s\xe3o as suas causas e condi\xe7\xf5es. Entre estes, os tr\xeas que come\xe7am com a ignor\xe2ncia s\xe3o o seu apoio decisivo (upanissaya), como uma m\xe3e para um filho. O kamma \xe9 o gerador (janaka), como um pai para um filho. O alimento \xe9 o sustentador (sandh\u0101rako), como uma ama de leite para uma crian\xe7a'. Tendo assim compreendido as condi\xe7\xf5es do corpo material, ele novamente compreende as condi\xe7\xf5es do corpo mental por meio do m\xe9todo: 'Dependendo do olho e das formas vis\xedveis, surge a consci\xeancia visual', e assim por diante.",es:"Habiendo reflexionado as\xed sobre las causas y condiciones de la mentalidad y la materialidad, primero comprende las causas y condiciones del cuerpo f\xedsico de esta manera: \"Este cuerpo, al nacer, no surge dentro de lotos azules, rojos o blancos, ni entre perlas o joyas. Al contrario, surge entre el recept\xe1culo del alimento digerido y el del no digerido, con la membrana abdominal detr\xe1s y la columna vertebral delante, rodeado por los intestinos y el mesenterio, siendo \xe9l mismo maloliente, asqueroso y repulsivo, en un lugar extremadamente estrecho, como un gusano que nace en pescado podrido, en masa fermentada, en un pozo negro o en una alcantarilla. Para este cuerpo que as\xed se produce, estos cuatro factores: la ignorancia, el deseo, el apego y el kamma, son las causas (hetu) porque lo producen; y el alimento es la condici\xf3n (paccaya) porque lo sostiene. As\xed, estos cinco factores son sus causas y condiciones. Entre estos, los tres primeros, como la ignorancia y dem\xe1s, son para este cuerpo como una madre para un ni\xf1o (su apoyo); el kamma es como un padre (quien lo genera); y el alimento es como una nodriza que lo sustenta\". Habiendo comprendido as\xed las condiciones del cuerpo f\xedsico, comprende luego las de la mentalidad mediante el m\xe9todo: \"En dependencia del ojo y de las formas surge la conciencia visual\", etc."}},{id:"vism-19.5",pali:"So eva\u1e43 paccayato n\u0101mar\u016bpassa pavatti\u1e43 disv\u0101 yath\u0101 ida\u1e43 etarahi, eva\u1e43 at\u012btepi addh\u0101ne paccayato pavattittha, an\u0101gatepi paccayato pavattissat\u012bti samanupassati.",translations:{en:"Having thus seen the occurrence of name-and-form from conditions, he understands that just as it occurs now from conditions, so too in the past it occurred from conditions, and in the future it will occur from conditions.",pt:"Ao ver assim a ocorr\xeancia da mente e da mat\xe9ria devido a condi\xe7\xf5es, ele contempla: 'Assim como ocorre agora, da mesma forma no tempo passado ocorreu devido a condi\xe7\xf5es, e no futuro tamb\xe9m ocorrer\xe1 devido a condi\xe7\xf5es'.",es:"Habiendo visto as\xed el proceso de la mentalidad y la materialidad a partir de sus condiciones, \xe9l percibe que, tal como ocurre ahora, tambi\xe9n en el pasado este proceso se dio por condiciones, y en el futuro tambi\xe9n se dar\xe1 por condiciones."}},{id:"vism-19.6",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 samanupassato y\u0101 s\u0101 pubbanta\u1e43 \u0101rabbha \u2018\u2018ahosi\u1e43 nu kho aha\u1e43 at\u012btamaddh\u0101na\u1e43, na nu kho ahosi\u1e43 at\u012btamaddh\u0101na\u1e43, ki\u1e43 nu kho ahosi\u1e43 at\u012btamaddh\u0101na\u1e43, katha\u1e43 nu kho ahosi\u1e43 at\u012btamaddh\u0101na\u1e43, ki\u1e43 hutv\u0101 ki\u1e43 ahosi\u1e43 nu kho aha\u1e43 at\u012btamaddh\u0101na\u2019\u2019nti (ma. ni. 1.18; sa\u1e43. ni. 2.20) pa\xf1cavidh\u0101 vicikicch\u0101 vutt\u0101, y\u0101pi aparanta\u1e43 \u0101rabbha \u2018\u2018bhaviss\u0101mi nu kho aha\u1e43 an\u0101gatamaddh\u0101na\u1e43, na nu kho bhaviss\u0101mi an\u0101gatamaddh\u0101na\u1e43, ki\u1e43 nu kho bhaviss\u0101mi an\u0101gatamaddh\u0101na\u1e43, katha\u1e43 nu kho bhaviss\u0101mi an\u0101gatamaddh\u0101na\u1e43, ki\u1e43 hutv\u0101 ki\u1e43 bhaviss\u0101mi nu kho aha\u1e43 an\u0101gatamaddh\u0101na\u2019\u2019nti pa\xf1cavidh\u0101 vicikicch\u0101 vutt\u0101, y\u0101pi paccuppanna\u1e43 \u0101rabbha \u2018\u2018etarahi v\u0101 pana paccuppanna\u1e43 addh\u0101na\u1e43 ajjhatta\u1e43 katha\u1e43kath\u012b hoti \u2013 aha\u1e43 nu khosmi, no nu khosmi, ki\u1e43 nu khosmi, katha\u1e43 nu khosmi, aya\u1e43 nu kho satto kuto \u0101gato, so kuhi\u1e43 g\u0101m\u012b bhavissat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (ma. ni. 1.18) chabbidh\u0101 vicikicch\u0101 vutt\u0101, s\u0101 sabb\u0101pi pah\u012byati.",translations:{en:"For one who understands in this way, the five kinds of doubt concerning the past, spoken of thus: 'Did I exist in the past? Did I not exist in the past? What was I in the past? How was I in the past? Having been what, what did I become in the past?' (MN 2); and the five kinds of doubt concerning the future, spoken of thus: 'Will I exist in the future? Will I not exist in the future? What will I be in the future? How will I be in the future? Having been what, what will I become in the future?'; and also the six kinds of doubt concerning the present, spoken of thus: 'Now, in the present time, he is inwardly perplexed: \u201cDo I exist? Do I not exist? What am I? How am I? From where has this being come? Where will it go?\u201d' (MN 2)\u2014all this doubt is abandoned.",pt:"Para ele, que assim contempla, s\xe3o abandonadas todas as cinco formas de d\xfavida sobre o passado: 'Eu existi no passado? Eu n\xe3o existi no passado? O que eu fui no passado? Como eu fui no passado? Tendo sido o qu\xea, o que me tornei no passado?'; e tamb\xe9m as cinco formas de d\xfavida sobre o futuro: 'Eu existirei no futuro? Eu n\xe3o existirei no futuro? O que serei no futuro? Como serei no futuro? Tendo sido o qu\xea, o que me tornarei no futuro?'; e tamb\xe9m as seis formas de d\xfavida sobre o presente: 'Eu existo agora? Eu n\xe3o existo agora? O que sou eu? Como sou eu? De onde veio este ser? Para onde ele ir\xe1?'. Todas essas d\xfavidas s\xe3o completamente eliminadas.",es:"Mientras \xe9l percibe esto de tal manera, se abandonan por completo los cinco tipos de duda referentes al pasado: \"\xbfFui yo en el pasado? \xbfNo fui yo en el pasado? \xbfQu\xe9 fui yo en el pasado? \xbfC\xf3mo fui yo en el pasado? \xbfHabiendo sido qu\xe9, en qu\xe9 me convert\xed en el pasado?\"; tambi\xe9n los cinco tipos de duda referentes al futuro: \"\xbfSer\xe9 yo en el futuro? \xbfNo ser\xe9 yo en el futuro? \xbfQu\xe9 ser\xe9 yo en el futuro? \xbfC\xf3mo ser\xe9 yo en el futuro? \xbfHabiendo sido qu\xe9, en qu\xe9 me convert\xed en el futuro?\"; y tambi\xe9n los seis tipos de duda referentes al presente: \"\xbfSoy yo ahora? \xbfNo soy yo? \xbfQu\xe9 soy? \xbfC\xf3mo soy? \xbfDe d\xf3nde ha venido este ser? \xbfA d\xf3nde ir\xe1?\"."}},{id:"vism-19.7",pali:"R\u016bpassa pana kamma\u1e43 citta\u1e43 utu \u0101h\u0101roti aya\u1e43 kamm\u0101diko catubbidho paccayo. Tattha kamma\u1e43 at\u012btameva kammasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nassa r\u016bpassa paccayo hoti. Citta\u1e43 cittasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nassa uppajjam\u0101na\u1e43. Utu\u0101h\u0101r\u0101 utu\u0101h\u0101rasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nassa \u1e6dhitikkha\u1e47e paccay\u0101 hont\u012bti. Evameveko n\u0101mar\u016bpassa paccayapariggaha\u1e43 karoti.",translations:{en:"For form, the condition is fourfold: kamma, consciousness, temperature, and nutriment. Herein, only past kamma is the condition for kamma-originated form. Consciousness, when arising, is the condition for consciousness-originated form. Temperature and nutriment are conditions for temperature-originated and nutriment-originated form at the moment of presence. In this way a certain one comprehends the conditions for name-and-form.",pt:"Para a mat\xe9ria, no entanto, existe esta condi\xe7\xe3o qu\xe1drupla que come\xe7a com o kamma: o kamma, a mente, a temperatura (utu) e o alimento. Entre estes, apenas o kamma passado \xe9 a condi\xe7\xe3o para a mat\xe9ria produzida pelo kamma. A mente, \xe0 medida que surge, \xe9 a condi\xe7\xe3o para a mat\xe9ria produzida pela mente. A temperatura e o alimento s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para a mat\xe9ria produzida pela temperatura e pelo alimento no seu momento de presen\xe7a (thitikkhana). Dessa forma, o praticante realiza a compreens\xe3o das condi\xe7\xf5es da mente e da mat\xe9ria.",es:"Para la materialidad, sin embargo, existen estas cuatro condiciones: kamma, consciencia, clima y alimento. De estas, solo el kamma pasado es la condici\xf3n para la materialidad originada por el kamma. La consciencia en el momento de su surgimiento es la condici\xf3n para la materialidad originada por la consciencia. El clima y el alimento son condiciones para la materialidad originada por el clima y por el alimento en el momento de su presencia. De esta manera, este tipo de yogui comprende las condiciones de la mentalidad y la materialidad."}},{id:"vism-19.8",pali:"Aparo \u2018\u2018purimakammabhavasmi\u1e43 moho avijj\u0101, \u0101y\u016bhan\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101, nikanti ta\u1e47h\u0101, upagamana\u1e43 up\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43, cetan\u0101 bhavoti ime pa\xf1ca dhamm\u0101 purimakammabhavasmi\u1e43 idha pa\u1e6disandhiy\u0101 paccay\u0101, idha pa\u1e6disandhi vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, okkanti n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43, pas\u0101do \u0101yatana\u1e43, phu\u1e6d\u1e6dho phasso, vedayita\u1e43 vedan\u0101ti ime pa\xf1ca dhamm\u0101 idh\u016bpapattibhavasmi\u1e43 purekatassa kammassa paccay\u0101. Idha paripakkatt\u0101 \u0101yatan\u0101na\u1e43 moho avijj\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 cetan\u0101 bhavoti ime pa\xf1ca dhamm\u0101 idha kammabhavasmi\u1e43 \u0101yati\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhiy\u0101 paccay\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (pa\u1e6di. ma. 1.47) eva\u1e43 kammava\u1e6d\u1e6davip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6davasena n\u0101mar\u016bpassa paccayapariggaha\u1e43 karoti.",translations:{en:"Another comprehends the conditions for name-and-form by way of the round of kamma and the round of results, as follows: \"In a previous kamma-existence, delusion was ignorance; accumulation was volitional formations; delight was craving; approaching was clinging; and volition was becoming. These five things in a previous kamma-existence were the conditions for rebirth-linking here. Here, in this resultant-existence, rebirth-linking is consciousness; descent is name-and-form; sensitivity is the sense base; the touched is contact; the felt is feeling. These five things are the result here of kamma done previously. Here, due to the maturing of the sense bases, delusion is ignorance\u2026 volition is becoming. These five things in this kamma-existence here are the conditions for future rebirth-linking\" (Pa\u1e6dis I 47).",pt:"Outro praticante compreende as condi\xe7\xf5es da mente e da mat\xe9ria por meio do ciclo do kamma e do ciclo do resultado da seguinte forma: 'Na exist\xeancia de kamma anterior, a ilus\xe3o \xe9 a ignor\xe2ncia, o esfor\xe7o acumulador s\xe3o as forma\xe7\xf5es, o apego sutil \xe9 o desejo, a aproxima\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o apego, a voli\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a exist\xeancia \u2014 estes cinco fatores na exist\xeancia de kamma anterior s\xe3o as condi\xe7\xf5es para o renascimento aqui. O renascimento aqui \xe9 a consci\xeancia, a descida \xe9 a mente e a mat\xe9ria, a sensibilidade s\xe3o as bases dos sentidos, o toque \xe9 o contato, a experi\xeancia \xe9 a sensa\xe7\xe3o \u2014 estes cinco fatores na presente exist\xeancia de renascimento s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es decorrentes do kamma realizado no passado. Aqui, devido ao amadurecimento das bases dos sentidos, a ilus\xe3o \xe9 a ignor\xe2ncia... a voli\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a exist\xeancia \u2014 estes cinco fatores na presente exist\xeancia de kamma s\xe3o as condi\xe7\xf5es para o renascimento no futuro'. Assim, ele compreende as condi\xe7\xf5es da mente e da mat\xe9ria por meio do ciclo do kamma e do ciclo do resultado.",es:"Otro [yogui comprende]: \u2018La confusi\xf3n en el momento de realizar el kamma-bhava (proceso del kamma) en una existencia pasada es la ignorancia (avijj\u0101); las acumulaciones de esfuerzo son las formaciones (sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101); el anhelo es la avidez (ta\u1e47h\u0101); el aferramiento es el apego (up\u0101d\u0101na); la intenci\xf3n volitiva es el proceso del kamma (kammabhava). Estos cinco estados en el kamma-bhava pasado son las condiciones para el renacimiento aqu\xed. La conciencia de renacimiento aqu\xed es la conciencia (vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a); el descenso [en el \xfatero] es la mentalidad-materialidad (n\u0101mar\u016bpa); la sensibilidad es la base sensorial (\u0101yatana); el contacto es el contacto (phassa); lo experimentado es la sensaci\xf3n (vedan\u0101). Estos cinco estados en el proceso de surgimiento (upapattibhava) aqu\xed son los resultados de kamma realizado en el pasado. Debido a la madurez de las bases sensoriales aqu\xed, la confusi\xf3n es la ignorancia (avijj\u0101)... etc... la intenci\xf3n volitiva es el proceso del kamma (kammabhava). Estos cinco estados en el proceso del kamma aqu\xed son las condiciones para el renacimiento en el futuro\u2019 (Pa\u1e6dis. M. 1.47). De esta manera, mediante el ciclo del kamma (kammava\u1e6d\u1e6da) y el ciclo del resultado (vip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6da), realiza la aprehensi\xf3n de la condici\xf3n de la mentalidad-materialidad."}},{id:"vism-19.9",pali:"Tattha catubbidha\u1e43 kamma\u1e43 \u2013 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhadhammavedan\u012bya\u1e43, upapajjavedan\u012bya\u1e43, apar\u0101pariyavedan\u012bya\u1e43, ahosikammanti. Tesu ekajavanav\u012bthiya\u1e43 sattasu cittesu kusal\u0101 v\u0101 akusal\u0101 v\u0101 pa\u1e6dhamajavanacetan\u0101 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhidhammavedan\u012byakamma\u1e43 n\u0101ma. Ta\u1e43 imasmi\xf1\xf1eva attabh\u0101ve vip\u0101ka\u1e43 deti. Tath\u0101 asakkonta\u1e43 pana \u2018\u2018ahosikamma\u1e43 n\u0101hosi kammavip\u0101ko, na bhavissati kammavip\u0101ko, natthi kammavip\u0101ko\u2019\u2019ti (pa\u1e6di. ma. 1.234) imassa tikassa vasena ahosikamma\u1e43 n\u0101ma hoti. Atthas\u0101dhik\u0101 pana sattamajavanacetan\u0101 upapajjavedan\u012byakamma\u1e43 n\u0101ma. Ta\u1e43 anantare attabh\u0101ve vip\u0101ka\u1e43 deti. Tath\u0101 asakkonta\u1e43 vuttanayeneva ahosikamma\u1e43 n\u0101ma hoti. Ubhinna\u1e43 antare pa\xf1ca javanacetan\u0101 apar\u0101pariyavedan\u012byakamma\u1e43 n\u0101ma. Ta\u1e43 an\u0101gate yad\u0101 ok\u0101sa\u1e43 labhati, tad\u0101 vip\u0101ka\u1e43 deti. Sati sa\u1e43s\u0101rappavattiy\u0101 ahosikamma\u1e43 n\u0101ma na hoti.",translations:{en:"Herein, kamma is fourfold: immediately effective kamma, subsequently effective kamma, indefinitely effective kamma, and defunct kamma. Among these, the volition of the first impulsion in a single cognitive series of seven cittas, whether wholesome or unwholesome, is called immediately effective kamma. It yields its result in this very existence. If it is unable to do so, it becomes defunct kamma, in the sense of the triad: 'There was kamma, but there was no kamma-result, there will be no kamma-result, and there is no kamma-result.' The volition of the seventh impulsion that accomplishes its purpose is called subsequently effective kamma. It yields its result in the immediately following existence. If it is unable to do so, it becomes defunct kamma in the way just stated. The volitions of the five intermediate impulsions are called indefinitely effective kamma. They yield their result in the future whenever an opportunity arises. As long as the round of existence continues, this kamma does not become defunct.",pt:"Nesse contexto, o kamma \xe9 de quatro tipos: o kamma a ser vivenciado nesta mesma vida (ditthadhamma-vedaniya), o kamma a ser vivenciado na pr\xf3xima vida (upapajja-vedaniya), o kamma a ser vivenciado em alguma vida subsequente (aparapariya-vedaniya) e o kamma ineficaz (ahosikamma). Entre estes, em um \xfanico processo cognitivo de impuls\xe3o (javana) de sete momentos mentais, a voli\xe7\xe3o ben\xe9fica ou prejudicial da primeira impuls\xe3o \xe9 chamada de kamma a ser vivenciado nesta mesma vida. Ele amadurece o seu resultado nesta mesma exist\xeancia. No entanto, se for incapaz de faz\xea-lo, torna-se kamma ineficaz, de acordo com a tr\xedade: 'Houve kamma, n\xe3o houve resultado de kamma, n\xe3o haver\xe1 resultado de kamma, n\xe3o h\xe1 resultado de kamma'. Mas a voli\xe7\xe3o da s\xe9tima impuls\xe3o, que realiza o prop\xf3sito, \xe9 chamada de kamma a ser vivenciado na pr\xf3xima vida. Ele amadurece o seu resultado na exist\xeancia imediatamente seguinte. Si for incapaz de faz\xea-lo, torna-se kamma ineficaz da mesma maneira descrita. As cinco voli\xe7\xf5es de impuls\xe3o intermedi\xe1rias entre as duas s\xe3o chamadas de kamma a ser vivenciado em alguma vida subsequente. Ele amadurece o seu resultado no futuro sempre que encontrar uma oportunidade. Enquanto continuar a continuidade do ciclo de renascimentos (sa\u1e43s\u0101ra), este kamma nunca se torna ineficaz.",es:"En ese contexto, el kamma es de cuatro tipos: kamma que se experimenta en esta misma vida (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhadhammavedan\u012bya), kamma que se experimenta en el siguiente renacimiento (upapajjavedan\u012bya), kamma que se experimenta en vidas sucesivas (apar\u0101pariyavedan\u012bya) y kamma inoperante (ahosikamma). Entre ellos, en un \xfanico proceso cognitivo de impulsos (javanav\u012bthi), de los siete momentos de conciencia, la intenci\xf3n del primer impulso (javana), ya sea de naturaleza beneficiosa o no beneficiosa, se denomina kamma que se experimenta en esta misma vida. Este da su fruto \xfanicamente en esta existencia actual. Si no puede hacerlo, se convierte en kamma inoperante bajo el principio de: \u2018Hubo kamma, pero no hubo resultado de kamma; no habr\xe1 resultado de kamma; no hay resultado de kamma\u2019 (Pa\u1e6dis. M. 1.234). Por otro lado, la intenci\xf3n del s\xe9ptimo impulso, que consuma el acto, se denomina kamma que se experimenta en el siguiente renacimiento. Este da su fruto en la existencia inmediatamente posterior. Si no puede hacerlo, se convierte en kamma inoperante de la manera ya mencionada. Las intenciones de los cinco impulsos intermedios se denominan kamma que se experimenta en vidas sucesivas. Este da su fruto en el futuro cada vez que encuentra una oportunidad. Mientras contin\xfae el proceso del sa\u1e43s\u0101ra, este kamma nunca llega a ser inoperante."}},{id:"vism-19.10",pali:"Aparampi catubbidha\u1e43 kamma\u1e43 \u2013 ya\u1e43 garuka\u1e43, ya\u1e43 bahula\u1e43, yad\u0101sanna\u1e43, ka\u1e6datt\u0101 v\u0101 pana kammanti. Tattha kusala\u1e43 v\u0101 hotu akusala\u1e43 v\u0101, garuk\u0101garukesu ya\u1e43 garuka\u1e43 m\u0101tugh\u0101t\u0101dikamma\u1e43 v\u0101 mahaggatakamma\u1e43 v\u0101, tadeva pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 vipaccati. Tath\u0101 bahul\u0101bahulesupi ya\u1e43 bahula\u1e43 hoti sus\u012blya\u1e43 v\u0101 duss\u012blya\u1e43 v\u0101, tadeva pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 vipaccati. Yad\u0101sanna\u1e43 n\u0101ma mara\u1e47ak\u0101le anussaritakamma\u1e43. Ya\xf1hi \u0101sannamara\u1e47o anussaritu\u1e43 sakkoti, teneva upapajjati. Etehi pana t\u012bhi mutta\u1e43 punappuna\u1e43 laddh\u0101sevana\u1e43 ka\u1e6datt\u0101 v\u0101 pana kamma\u1e43 n\u0101ma hoti, tesa\u1e43 abh\u0101ve ta\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhi\u1e43 \u0101ka\u1e0d\u1e0dhati.",translations:{en:"There is another fourfold classification of kamma: weighty kamma, habitual kamma, proximate kamma, and reserve kamma. Herein, whether wholesome or unwholesome, among weighty and non-weighty kammas, that which is weighty\u2014such as matricide or a sublime kamma pertaining to the fine-material and immaterial spheres\u2014ripens first. Similarly, among habitual and non-habitual kammas, that which is habitual\u2014whether virtuous or unvirtuous conduct\u2014ripens first. Proximate kamma is that which is recollected at the time of death. For one is reborn by whatever kamma one who is near death is able to recollect. Apart from these three, kamma that has been repeatedly practiced is called reserve kamma. In the absence of the former three, it is this kamma that brings about rebirth-linking.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, o kamma \xe9 de quatro tipos: o kamma pesado (garuka), o kamma habitual (bahula), o kamma pr\xf3ximo da morte (\u0101sanna) e o kamma residual (ka\u1e6datt\u0101). Dentre estes, seja ben\xe9fico ou prejudicial, entre as a\xe7\xf5es pesadas e n\xe3o pesadas, aquela que \xe9 pesada \u2014 como o matric\xeddio, etc., ou um kamma sublime \u2014 amadurece primeiro. Da mesma forma, entre as a\xe7\xf5es habituais e n\xe3o habituais, aquela que \xe9 habitual \u2014 seja de boa conduta ou de m\xe1 conduta \u2014 amadurece primeiro. O kamma pr\xf3ximo da morte \xe9 aquele lembrado no momento da morte. Pois aquilo que a pessoa prestes a morrer \xe9 capaz de lembrar, por meio disso ela renasce. Livre desses tr\xeas, o kamma que foi repetidamente praticado \xe9 chamado de kamma residual; na aus\xeancia daqueles tr\xeas, este atrai o renascimento.",es:"Tambi\xe9n hay otros cuatro tipos de kamma: kamma pesado (garuka), kamma habitual (bahula), kamma pr\xf3ximo a la muerte (\u0101sanna) y kamma residual (ka\u1e6datt\u0101). Entre ellos, sea beneficioso o no beneficioso, de entre los actos pesados y leves, aquel que es pesado \u2014como el matricidio (m\u0101tugh\u0101ta), etc., o un kamma de naturaleza sublime (mahaggata)\u2014 madura primero. Asimismo, de entre los actos habituales y no habituales, aquel que es habitual \u2014ya sea de buena conducta (sus\u012blya) o mala conducta (duss\u012blya)\u2014 madura primero. El kamma pr\xf3ximo a la muerte es el kamma recordado en el momento de morir; pues aquello que uno puede recordar estando pr\xf3ximo a la muerte, por eso mismo renace. Pero el kamma que se ha practicado repetidamente y que es diferente de los tres anteriores se denomina kamma residual; en ausencia de los otros tres, este atrae el renacimiento."}},{id:"vism-19.11",pali:"Aparampi catubbidha\u1e43 kamma\u1e43 \u2013 janaka\u1e43, upatthambhaka\u1e43, upap\u012b\u1e37aka\u1e43, upagh\u0101takanti. Tattha janaka\u1e43 n\u0101ma kusalampi hoti akusalampi. Ta\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhiyampi pavattepi r\u016bp\u0101r\u016bpavip\u0101kakkhandhe janeti. Upatthambhaka\u1e43 pana vip\u0101ka\u1e43 janetu\u1e43 na sakkoti, a\xf1\xf1ena kammena dinn\u0101ya pa\u1e6disandhiy\u0101 janite vip\u0101ke uppajjam\u0101nakasukhadukkha\u1e43 upatthambheti, addh\u0101na\u1e43 pavatteti. Upap\u012b\u1e37aka\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1ena kammena dinn\u0101ya pa\u1e6disandhiy\u0101 janite vip\u0101ke uppajjam\u0101nakasukhadukkha\u1e43 p\u012b\u1e37eti b\u0101dhati, addh\u0101na\u1e43 pavattitu\u1e43 na deti. Upagh\u0101taka\u1e43 pana saya\u1e43 kusalampi akusalampi sam\u0101na\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 dubbalakamma\u1e43 gh\u0101tetv\u0101 tassa vip\u0101ka\u1e43 pa\u1e6dib\u0101hitv\u0101 attano vip\u0101kassa ok\u0101sa\u1e43 karoti. Eva\u1e43 pana kammena kate ok\u0101se ta\u1e43 vip\u0101ka\u1e43 uppanna\u1e43 n\u0101ma vuccati.",translations:{en:"There is still another fourfold kamma: generative, supportive, oppressive, and destructive. Herein, generative kamma, which can be either wholesome or unwholesome, generates the material and immaterial resultant aggregates both at rebirth-linking and during the course of existence. Supportive kamma cannot generate a result itself; rather, when rebirth-linking has been given by another kamma, it supports and prolongs the pleasure and pain that arise in the generated result. Oppressive kamma oppresses and obstructs the pleasure and pain that arise in the result generated by another kamma, not allowing it to continue. Destructive kamma, being itself wholesome or unwholesome, destroys another weaker kamma, wards off its result, and creates an opportunity for its own result. When an opportunity has thus been created by a kamma, its result is said to have arisen.",pt:"Al\xe9m disso, o kamma \xe9 de quatro tipos: o kamma produtor (janaka), o kamma apoiador (upatthambhaka), o kamma obstrutor (upap\u012b\u1e37aka) e o kamma destrutivo (upagh\u0101taka). Dentre estes, o kamma produtor pode ser ben\xe9fico ou prejudicial. Ele gera os agregados materiais e imateriais resultantes tanto no momento do renascimento quanto durante o curso da vida. O kamma apoiador, por sua vez, n\xe3o pode gerar um resultado por si mesmo; quando o renascimento \xe9 dado por outro kamma e o resultado \xe9 gerado, ele apoia a felicidade ou o sofrimento que surge, fazendo-os durar por muito tempo. O kamma obstrutor, quando o renascimento \xe9 dado por outro kamma e o resultado \xe9 gerado, obstrui e aflige a felicidade ou o sofrimento que surge, n\xe3o permitindo que durem por muito tempo. O kamma destrutivo, por sua vez, sendo ele pr\xf3prio ben\xe9fico ou prejudicial, destr\xf3i outro kamma mais fraco, impede o seu resultado e abre espa\xe7o para o seu pr\xf3prio resultado. Quando o espa\xe7o \xe9 assim aberto pelo kamma, diz-se que esse resultado surgiu.",es:"Hay otros cuatro tipos de kamma: kamma productor (janaka), kamma sustentador (upatthambhaka), kamma opresor (upap\u012b\u1e37aka) y kamma destructor (upagh\u0101taka). En ellos, el kamma productor puede ser tanto beneficioso como no beneficioso; este genera los agregados del resultado material e inmaterial tanto en el renacimiento como durante el curso de la vida. El kamma sustentador, por su parte, no puede generar un resultado, pero sostiene el placer o el dolor que surge en el resultado generado por otro kamma en el renacimiento y le permite durar por largo tiempo. El kamma opresor oprime y aflige el placer o el dolor que surge en el resultado generado por otro kamma en el renacimiento, impidi\xe9ndole continuar por mucho tiempo. El kamma destructor, siendo \xe9l mismo beneficioso o no beneficioso, anula otro kamma m\xe1s d\xe9bil, impide su resultado y crea una oportunidad para su propio fruto. Cuando el kamma crea tal oportunidad, se dice que ese resultado ha surgido."}},{id:"vism-19.12",pali:"Iti ima\u1e43 dv\u0101dasavidha\u1e43 kamma\u1e43 kammava\u1e6d\u1e6de pakkhipitv\u0101 eva\u1e43 eko kammava\u1e6d\u1e6davip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6davasena n\u0101mar\u016bpassa paccayapariggaha\u1e43 karoti. So eva\u1e43 kammava\u1e6d\u1e6davip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6davasena paccayato n\u0101mar\u016bpassa pavatti\u1e43 disv\u0101 \u2018\u2018yath\u0101 ida\u1e43 etarahi, eva\u1e43 at\u012btepi addh\u0101ne kammava\u1e6d\u1e6davip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6davasena paccayato pavattittha, an\u0101gatepi kammava\u1e6d\u1e6davip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6davaseneva paccayato pavattissat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti. Iti kamma\xf1ceva kammavip\u0101ko ca, kammava\u1e6d\u1e6da\xf1ca vip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6da\xf1ca, kammapavatta\xf1ca vip\u0101kapavatta\xf1ca, kammasantati ca vip\u0101kasantati ca, kiriy\u0101 ca kiriy\u0101phala\xf1ca.",translations:{en:"Thus, having included this twelvefold kamma in the round of kamma, one in this way discerns the conditions for name-and-form by way of the round of kamma and the round of result. Having seen the occurrence of name-and-form as conditioned by the round of kamma and the round of result, one understands: 'Just as it is now, so too in the past time it occurred conditioned by the round of kamma and the round of result; and in the future time it will occur conditioned by the round of kamma and the round of result.' Thus: kamma and kamma-result; the round of kamma and the round of result; the process of kamma and the process of result; the continuity of kamma and the continuity of result; action and the fruit of action.",pt:"Assim, inserindo este kamma de doze tipos no ciclo do kamma, um iogue realiza a apreens\xe3o das condi\xe7\xf5es do nome-e-forma por meio do ciclo do kamma e do ciclo do resultado. Ele, vendo assim a ocorr\xeancia do nome-e-forma a partir de condi\xe7\xf5es por meio do ciclo do kamma e do ciclo do resultado, compreende: 'Assim como este ocorre agora, da mesma forma ocorreu no passado a partir de condi\xe7\xf5es por meio do ciclo do kamma e do ciclo do resultado, e no futuro tamb\xe9m ocorrer\xe1 a partir de condi\xe7\xf5es por meio do ciclo do kamma e do ciclo do resultado'. Assim, h\xe1 apenas o kamma e o resultado do kamma, o ciclo do kamma e o ciclo do resultado, o processo do kamma e o processo do resultado, a continuidade do kamma e a continuidade do resultado, a a\xe7\xe3o funcional e o fruto da a\xe7\xe3o funcional.",es:"As\xed, integrando estos doce tipos de kamma en el ciclo del kamma, un yogui realiza la aprehensi\xf3n de la condici\xf3n de la mentalidad-materialidad mediante el ciclo del kamma y el ciclo del resultado. Al ver el curso de la mentalidad-materialidad a partir de sus condiciones de esta manera, comprende: \u2018Tal como es esto ahora, as\xed en el pasado el curso procedi\xf3 a trav\xe9s de condiciones mediante el ciclo del kamma y el ciclo del resultado, y en el futuro tambi\xe9n proceder\xe1 a trav\xe9s de condiciones mediante el ciclo del kamma y el ciclo del resultado\u2019. As\xed existen el kamma y el resultado del kamma, el ciclo del kamma y el ciclo del resultado, la continuidad del kamma y la continuidad del resultado, la acci\xf3n y el fruto de la acci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-19.13",pali:"Kamm\u0101 vip\u0101k\u0101 vattanti, vip\u0101ko kammasambhavo; Kamm\u0101 punabbhavo hoti, eva\u1e43 loko pavattat\u012bti. \u2013",translations:{en:"From kamma results proceed, a result has kamma for its source; From kamma comes renewed existence; thus the world revolves.",pt:"A partir do kamma os resultados procedem; o resultado tem sua origem no kamma. A partir do kamma ocorre o renascimento; assim o mundo prossegue.",es:"\u2018Los resultados fluyen del kamma, el kamma se origina en los resultados; del kamma surge el renacimiento, y as\xed es como el mundo procede\u2019."}},{id:"vism-19.14",pali:"Samanupassati. Tasseva\u1e43 samanupassato y\u0101 s\u0101 pubbant\u0101dayo \u0101rabbha \u2018\u2018ahosi\u1e43 nu kho aha\u2019\u2019nti\u0101din\u0101 nayena vutt\u0101 so\u1e37asavidh\u0101 vicikicch\u0101, s\u0101 sabb\u0101 pah\u012byati. Sabbabhavayonigati\u1e6d\u1e6dhitiniv\u0101sesu hetuphalasambandhavasena pavattam\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bpamattameva kh\u0101yati. So neva k\u0101ra\u1e47ato uddha\u1e43 k\u0101raka\u1e43 passati, na vip\u0101kappavattito uddha\u1e43 vip\u0101kapa\u1e6disa\u1e43vedaka\u1e43. K\u0101ra\u1e47e pana sati \u2018\u2018k\u0101rako\u2019\u2019ti, vip\u0101kappavattiy\u0101 sati \u2018\u2018pa\u1e6disa\u1e43vedako\u2019\u2019ti sama\xf1\xf1\u0101mattena pa\u1e47\u1e0dit\u0101 voharanticcevassa sammappa\xf1\xf1\u0101ya sudi\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"He sees this. For one who sees in this way, the sixteen kinds of doubt concerning the past, etc., stated in the way beginning, 'Did I exist in the past?' are all abandoned. In all kinds of existence, generation, destiny, station, and abode, only mere name-and-form is apparent, occurring by way of the connection between cause and effect. He sees no doer apart from the condition, no experiencer apart from the occurrence of the result. And it is well seen by him with right wisdom that the wise use mere conventional expressions when, there being a condition, they speak of a 'doer,' and when, there being an occurrence of a result, they speak of an 'experiencer.'",pt:"Ele v\xea claramente. Para aquele que assim v\xea claramente, toda aquela d\xfavida de dezesseis tipos descrita em rela\xe7\xe3o ao passado, etc., come\xe7ando com 'Ser\xe1 que eu existi?', \xe9 completamente abandonada. Em todas as exist\xeancias, modos de gera\xe7\xe3o, destinos, esta\xe7\xf5es da consci\xeancia e moradas dos seres, aparece apenas o nome-e-forma ocorrendo por meio da rela\xe7\xe3o de causa e efeito. Ele n\xe3o v\xea nenhum agente criador al\xe9m da causa, nem v\xea nenhum experienciador do resultado al\xe9m do processo do resultado. No entanto, quando h\xe1 uma causa, os s\xe1bios usam a mera designa\xe7\xe3o convencional de 'agente', e quando h\xe1 a ocorr\xeancia do resultado, usam a designa\xe7\xe3o de 'experienciador' \u2014 isso \xe9 bem visto por ele com sabedoria correta.",es:"As\xed lo observa. Mientras observa de esta manera, toda aquella duda de diecis\xe9is tipos que ha sido descrita respecto al pasado, etc., de la forma: \u2018\xbfFui yo en el pasado?\u2019, queda totalmente abandonada. En todos los tipos de existencia, formas de nacimiento, destinos, estaciones de la conciencia y moradas de los seres, solo aparece la mera mentalidad-materialidad fluyendo mediante la conexi\xf3n entre causa y efecto. \xc9l no ve a ning\xfan \u2018hacedor\u2019 por encima de la causa, ni ve a nadie que experimente por encima del flujo del resultado. Pero cuando hay una causa, los sabios usan la designaci\xf3n convencional de \u2018hacedor\u2019, y cuando hay un flujo de resultados, usan la designaci\xf3n de \u2018quien experimenta\u2019; esto es bien visto por \xe9l con el conocimiento correcto."}},{id:"vism-19.15",pali:"\u2018\u2018Kammassa k\u0101rako natthi, vip\u0101kassa ca vedako; Suddhadhamm\u0101 pavattanti, eveta\u1e43 sammadassana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"No doer of the kamma can be found, no one who reaps the fruit of it; mere phenomena flow on\u2014this is right seeing.",pt:"\"N\xe3o h\xe1 um agente do kamma, nem um experienciador do resultado; apenas puros dhammas ocorrem. Esta \xe9 a vis\xe3o correta.\"",es:"\u2018No hay hacedor del kamma, ni hay quien experimente el resultado; solo fluyen fealidades puros; esta es la visi\xf3n correcta\u2019."}},{id:"vism-19.16",pali:"\u2018\u2018Eva\u1e43 kamme vip\u0101ke ca, vattam\u0101ne sahetuke; B\u012bjarukkh\u0101dik\u0101na\u1e43va, pubb\u0101 ko\u1e6di na n\u0101yati; An\u0101gatepi sa\u1e43s\u0101re, appavatta\u1e43 na dissati.",translations:{en:"With kamma and result thus turning, together with their causal source, like seeds and trees and so on, no first beginning can be known. And in the future round of births, non-occurrence is not seen.",pt:"\"Assim, enquanto o kamma e o resultado ocorrem com suas causas, tal como no caso da semente e da \xe1rvore, etc., o limite inicial n\xe3o \xe9 conhecido; e no futuro do sa\u1e43s\u0101ra, a n\xe3o ocorr\xeancia deles n\xe3o \xe9 vista.\"",es:"\u2018As\xed, mientras el kamma y su resultado fluyen junto con sus causas, al igual que con la semilla y el \xe1rbol, no se conoce un punto inicial; ni siquiera en el futuro se vislumbra el cese de este sa\u1e43s\u0101ra mientras el proceso contin\xfae\u2019."}},{id:"vism-19.17",pali:"\u2018\u2018Yath\u0101 na s\u016briye aggi, na ma\u1e47imhi na gomaye; Na tesa\u1e43 bahi so atthi, sambh\u0101rehi ca j\u0101yati.",translations:{en:"Just as fire is not in the sun, nor in the crystal, nor in cow dung; nor does it exist outside of them, but is born from their components.",pt:"\"Assim como o fogo n\xe3o est\xe1 no sol, nem na joia, nem no esterco de vaca, nem existe fora deles, mas surge atrav\xe9s da combina\xe7\xe3o de condi\xe7\xf5es;\"",es:"As\xed como el fuego no reside en el sol, ni en la gema, ni en el esti\xe9rcol de vaca, ni existe fuera de ellos, sino que surge mediante la conjunci\xf3n de condiciones."}},{id:"vism-19.18",pali:"\u2018\u2018Na hettha devo brahm\u0101 v\u0101, sa\u1e43s\u0101rassatthik\u0101rako; Suddhadhamm\u0101 pavattanti, hetusambh\u0101rapaccay\u0101\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"There is no god or Brahm\u0101 here who is the maker of this round; mere phenomena flow on, conditioned by their causal base.",pt:"\"N\xe3o h\xe1 aqui nenhum deus ou Brahma que seja o criador do sa\u1e43s\u0101ra; apenas puros dhammas ocorrem, condicionados pela combina\xe7\xe3o de causas.\"",es:"No hay aqu\xed un dios ni un Brahma que sea el creador del ciclo de renacimientos (sa\u1e43s\u0101ra); solo fluyen puros fealidades (dhamma) producidos por la conjunci\xf3n de causas y condiciones."}},{id:"vism-19.19",pali:"Imin\u0101 pana \xf1\u0101\u1e47ena samann\u0101gato vipassako buddhas\u0101sane laddhass\u0101so laddhapati\u1e6d\u1e6dho niyatagatiko c\u016b\u1e37asot\u0101panno n\u0101ma hoti.",translations:{en:"Endowed with this knowledge, the insight meditator gains confidence and a firm footing in the Buddha's Dispensation. He is fixed in his destiny and is called a 'lesser stream-enterer.'",pt:"O praticante de vipassan\u0101 dotado deste conhecimento obt\xe9m al\xedvio e uma base firme na dispensa\xe7\xe3o do Buda, tem um destino seguro e \xe9 chamado de 'pequeno que entra na corrente' (c\u016b\u1e37asot\u0101panna).",es:"El practicante de la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassaka) dotado de este conocimiento, habiendo encontrado consuelo y apoyo en la ense\xf1anza del Buddha (Buddhas\u0101sana), posee un destino seguro y es llamado un 'Peque\xf1o Sot\u0101panna' (c\u016b\u1e37asot\u0101panna)."}},{id:"vism-19.20",pali:"Tasm\u0101 bhikkhu sad\u0101 sato, n\u0101mar\u016bpassa sabbaso; Paccaye parigga\u1e47heyya, ka\u1e45kh\u0101vitara\u1e47atthikoti.",translations:{en:"Therefore a bhikkhu, ever mindful, Of mentality-materiality in every way, Should comprehend its conditions, If he would overcome his doubt.",pt:"\"Portanto, o monge, sempre atento, desejando superar a d\xfavida, deve apreender as condi\xe7\xf5es do nome-e-forma em todos os aspectos.\"",es:"Por lo tanto, el monje, siempre atento, debe aprehender en su totalidad las condiciones de la mentalidad y la materialidad, deseando la superaci\xf3n de la duda."}}]},437,[]);
__d(function(a,e,i,n,o,s,t){o.exports=[{id:"vism-20.1",pali:"Aya\u1e43 maggo, aya\u1e43 na maggoti eva\u1e43 magga\xf1ca amagga\xf1ca \xf1atv\u0101 \u1e6dhita\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 pana magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"The knowledge that stands firm, having known the path and the not-path thus, 'This is the path, this is not the path,' is called the purification by knowledge and vision of path and not-path.",pt:"O conhecimento estabelecido ao compreender o que \xe9 o caminho e o que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho, na forma de 'este \xe9 o caminho, este n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho', \xe9 chamado de purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o do que \xe9 o caminho e do que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho (magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi).",es:"'Esta es la senda, esta no es la senda'; el conocimiento que permanece habiendo distinguido as\xed lo que es la senda y lo que no es la senda, se denomina Purificaci\xf3n por el Conocimiento y la Visi\xf3n de lo que es Senda y lo que no es Senda."}},{id:"vism-20.2",pali:"Ta\u1e43 samp\u0101detuk\u0101mena kal\u0101pasammasana sa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101ya nayavipassan\u0101ya t\u0101va yogo kara\u1e47\u012byo. Kasm\u0101? \u0100raddhavipassakassa obh\u0101s\u0101disambhave magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47asambhavato. \u0100raddhavipassakassa hi obh\u0101s\u0101d\u012bsu sambh\u016btesu magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti, vipassan\u0101ya ca kal\u0101pasammasana\u1e43 \u0101di. Tasm\u0101 eta\u1e43 ka\u1e45kh\u0101vitara\u1e47\u0101nantara\u1e43 uddi\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43. Apica yasm\u0101 t\u012bra\u1e47apari\xf1\xf1\u0101ya vattam\u0101n\u0101ya magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 uppajjati, t\u012bra\u1e47apari\xf1\xf1\u0101 ca \xf1\u0101tapari\xf1\xf1\u0101nantar\u0101, tasm\u0101pi ta\u1e43 magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi\u1e43 samp\u0101detuk\u0101mena kal\u0101pasammasane t\u0101va yogo k\u0101tabbo.",translations:{en:"To accomplish that, one who wishes to do so should first apply himself to the methodical insight known as the comprehension of groups (kal\u0101pasammasana). Why? Because for an insight meditator who has undertaken the practice, the knowledge of path and not-path arises with the occurrence of illumination and so on. For when illumination, etc., have occurred for an insight meditator who has undertaken the practice, the knowledge of path and not-path arises, and comprehension of groups is the beginning of insight. That is why this was described immediately after the overcoming of doubt. Furthermore, since the knowledge of path and not-path arises while full understanding by scrutinizing is occurring, and full understanding by scrutinizing is subsequent to full understanding as the known, therefore one who wishes to accomplish that purification by knowledge and vision of path and not-path should first apply himself to the comprehension of groups.",pt:"Aquele que deseja realizar essa purifica\xe7\xe3o deve primeiro aplicar-se ao m\xe9todo de vipassan\u0101 conhecido como compreens\xe3o por grupos (kal\u0101pasammasana). Por qu\xea? Porque o conhecimento do que \xe9 o caminho e do que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho surge quando as imperfei\xe7\xf5es da medita\xe7\xe3o, como a aura de luz (obh\u0101sa), etc., ocorrem para aquele que iniciou a medita\xe7\xe3o de insight. Pois, quando a aura de luz, etc., surgem para aquele que iniciou a medita\xe7\xe3o de insight, ocorre o conhecimento do que \xe9 o caminho e do que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho; e a compreens\xe3o por grupos \xe9 o in\xedcio da medita\xe7\xe3o de insight. Por isso, ela foi indicada imediatamente ap\xf3s o superamento da d\xfavida. Al\xe9m disso, visto que o conhecimento do que \xe9 o caminho e do que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho surge quando a compreens\xe3o plena por investiga\xe7\xe3o (t\u012bra\u1e47apari\xf1\xf1\u0101) est\xe1 ocorrendo, e a compreens\xe3o plena por investiga\xe7\xe3o vem imediatamente ap\xf3s a compreens\xe3o plena do que \xe9 conhecido (\xf1\u0101tapari\xf1\xf1\u0101), por essa raz\xe3o tamb\xe9m, aquele que deseja realizar a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o do que \xe9 o caminho e do que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho deve primeiro aplicar-se \xe0 compreens\xe3o por grupos.",es:"Quien desee perfeccionar esa [Purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n de lo que es y lo que no es el camino] debe primero aplicarse a la introspecci\xf3n de m\xe9todo conocida como comprensi\xf3n por grupos (kal\u0101pasammasana). \xbfPor qu\xe9? Porque el conocimiento de lo que es y lo que no es el camino surge cuando aparecen las luces, etc., en quien ha comenzado la introspecci\xf3n. Pues el conocimiento de lo que es y lo que no es el camino ocurre cuando surgen luces y dem\xe1s fealidades en quien ha comenzado la introspecci\xf3n, y la comprensi\xf3n por grupos es el comienzo de la introspecci\xf3n. Por lo tanto, esto se indica inmediatamente despu\xe9s de la superaci\xf3n de la duda. Adem\xe1s, dado que el conocimiento de lo que es y lo que no es el camino surge mientras se desarrolla el pleno entendimiento por el juicio, y el pleno entendimiento por el juicio sigue al pleno entendimiento de lo conocido, tambi\xe9n por esta raz\xf3n, quien desee perfeccionar esa purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n de lo que es y lo que no es el camino debe primero aplicarse a la comprensi\xf3n por grupos."}},{id:"vism-20.3",pali:"Tatr\u0101ya\u1e43 vinicchayo \u2013 tisso hi lokiyapari\xf1\xf1\u0101 \xf1\u0101tapari\xf1\xf1\u0101 t\u012bra\u1e47apari\xf1\xf1\u0101 pah\u0101napari\xf1\xf1\u0101 ca. Y\u0101 sandh\u0101ya vutta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 \xf1\u0101ta\u1e6d\u1e6dhe \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Pari\xf1\xf1\u0101pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 t\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e6d\u1e6dhe \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Pah\u0101napa\xf1\xf1\u0101 paricc\u0101ga\u1e6d\u1e6dhe \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti (pa\u1e6di. ma. 1.75). Tattha \u2018\u2018ruppanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43, vedayitalakkha\u1e47\u0101 vedan\u0101\u2019\u2019ti eva\u1e43 tesa\u1e43 tesa\u1e43 dhamm\u0101na\u1e43 paccattalakkha\u1e47asallakkha\u1e47avasena pavatt\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 \xf1\u0101tapari\xf1\xf1\u0101 n\u0101ma. \u2018\u2018R\u016bpa\u1e43 anicca\u1e43, vedan\u0101 anicc\u0101\u2019\u2019ti\u0101din\u0101 nayena tesa\u1e43yeva dhamm\u0101na\u1e43 s\u0101ma\xf1\xf1alakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101ropetv\u0101 pavatt\u0101 lakkha\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47ikavipassan\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 t\u012bra\u1e47apari\xf1\xf1\u0101 n\u0101ma. Tesuyeva pana dhammesu niccasa\xf1\xf1\u0101dipajahanavasena pavatt\u0101 lakkha\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47ikavipassan\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 pah\u0101napari\xf1\xf1\u0101 n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"Herein, this is the detailed analysis: There are three mundane kinds of full understanding: full understanding as the known, full understanding by scrutinizing, and full understanding by abandoning. With reference to this it is said: 'Wisdom of direct knowledge is knowledge in the sense of the known. Wisdom of full understanding is knowledge in the sense of scrutinizing. Wisdom of abandoning is knowledge in the sense of relinquishing' (Pa\u1e6dis I 75). Herein, the wisdom that proceeds by way of discerning the individual characteristics of the several phenomena, such as 'Form has the characteristic of being afflicted, feeling has the characteristic of being felt,' is called full understanding as the known. The wisdom of insight that has the characteristics of phenomena as its object, which proceeds by ascribing the general characteristics to those same phenomena in the way beginning, 'Form is impermanent, feeling is impermanent,' is called full understanding by scrutinizing. The wisdom of insight that has the characteristics of phenomena as its object, which proceeds by way of abandoning the perception of permanence, etc., in those same phenomena, is called full understanding by abandoning.",pt:"A este respeito, esta \xe9 a determina\xe7\xe3o: pois existem tr\xeas compreens\xf5es plenas mundanas: a compreens\xe3o plena do conhecido, a compreens\xe3o plena por meio da investiga\xe7\xe3o e a compreens\xe3o plena pelo abandono. Em refer\xeancia \xe0s quais foi dito: 'A sabedoria do conhecimento direto \xe9 conhecimento no sentido de conhecer. A sabedoria da compreens\xe3o plena \xe9 conhecimento no sentido de investigar. A sabedoria do abandono \xe9 conhecimento no sentido de renunciar.' Entre elas, a sabedoria que surge por meio da observa\xe7\xe3o das caracter\xedsticas individuais de cada dhamma, como 'a mat\xe9ria tem a caracter\xedstica de se alterar, a sensa\xe7\xe3o tem a caracter\xedstica de experienciar', \xe9 chamada de compreens\xe3o plena do conhecido. A sabedoria de insight que tem as caracter\xedsticas como objeto, surgindo ao aplicar a caracter\xedstica comum a esses mesmos dhammas, da seguinte maneira: 'a mat\xe9ria \xe9 impermanente, a sensa\xe7\xe3o \xe9 impermanente', etc., \xe9 chamada de compreens\xe3o plena por meio da investiga\xe7\xe3o. E a sabedoria de insight que tem as caracter\xedsticas como objeto, surgindo nesses mesmos dhammas por meio do abandono da percep\xe7\xe3o de perman\xeancia, etc., \xe9 chamada de compreens\xe3o plena pelo abandono.",es:"Aqu\xed est\xe1 la conclusi\xf3n: existen tres tipos de pleno entendimiento mundano: el pleno entendimiento de lo conocido (\xf1\u0101tapari\xf1\xf1\u0101), el pleno entendimiento por el juicio (t\u012bra\u1e47apari\xf1\xf1\u0101) y el pleno entendimiento por el abandono (pah\u0101napari\xf1\xf1\u0101). Refiri\xe9ndose a ellos, se ha dicho: \xabEl conocimiento como comprensi\xf3n directa tiene el sentido de lo conocido; el conocimiento como pleno entendimiento tiene el sentido del juicio; el conocimiento como abandono tiene el sentido del renunciamiento\xbb (Pa\u1e6di. I, 75). All\xed, el conocimiento que procede mediante la observaci\xf3n de las caracter\xedsticas individuales de tales y cuales fealidades, como \xabla materia tiene la caracter\xedstica de alterarse, la sensaci\xf3n tiene la caracter\xedstica de sentir\xbb, se llama pleno entendimiento de lo conocido. El conocimiento de introspecci\xf3n que tiene como objeto las caracter\xedsticas [universales] y procede atribuyendo las caracter\xedsticas comunes a esos mismos fealidades mediante el m\xe9todo de \xabla materia es impermanente, la sensaci\xf3n es impermanente\xbb, etc., se llama pleno entendimiento por el juicio. Sin embargo, el conocimiento de introspecci\xf3n que tiene como objeto las caracter\xedsticas [universales] y procede mediante el abandono de la percepci\xf3n de permanencia, etc., en esos mismos fealidades, se llama pleno entendimiento por el abandono."}},{id:"vism-20.4",pali:"\u2018\u2018R\u016bpa\u1e43 at\u012bt\u0101n\u0101gatapaccuppanna\u1e43 anicca\u1e43 khaya\u1e6d\u1e6dhena, dukkha\u1e43 bhaya\u1e6d\u1e6dhena, anatt\u0101 as\u0101raka\u1e6d\u1e6dhen\u0101ti sa\u1e45khipitv\u0101 vavatth\u0101ne pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 sammasane \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Vedana\u1e43\u2026 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43\u2026 cakkhu\u1e43\u2026pe\u2026 jar\u0101mara\u1e47a\u1e43\u2026pe\u2026 sammasane \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"'Form\u2014past, future, and present\u2014is impermanent in the sense of decay, suffering in the sense of fear, non-self in the sense of being without substance': wisdom in defining by summarizing thus, knowledge in comprehending. Feeling... consciousness... the eye...pe... aging-and-death...pe... knowledge in comprehending.",pt:"\u201cA sabedoria em definir resumidamente que a mat\xe9ria passada, futura ou presente \xe9 impermanente no sentido de esgotamento, sofrimento no sentido de perigo, n\xe3o-eu no sentido de aus\xeancia de ess\xeancia, \xe9 o conhecimento da investiga\xe7\xe3o. A sensa\xe7\xe3o... a consci\xeancia... o olho... [pe]... o envelhecimento e morte... [pe]... \xe9 o conhecimento da investiga\xe7\xe3o.",es:"\xabLa materia pasada, futura y presente es impermanente en el sentido de agotamiento, sufrimiento en el sentido de peligro, y no-yo en el sentido de falta de esencia; as\xed, el entendimiento de delimitarla de manera resumida es conocimiento por comprensi\xf3n. La sensaci\xf3n\u2026 la conciencia\u2026 el ojo\u2026 [pe]\u2026 la vejez y la muerte\u2026 [pe]\u2026 es conocimiento por comprensi\xf3n\xbb."}},{id:"vism-20.5",pali:"So tasseva pa\xf1casu khandhesu aniccadukkh\u0101nattasammasanassa thirabh\u0101vatth\u0101ya, ya\u1e43 ta\u1e43 bhagavat\u0101 \u2018\u2018katamehi catt\u0101r\u012bs\u0101ya \u0101k\u0101rehi anulomika\u1e43 khanti\u1e43 pa\u1e6dilabhati, katamehi catt\u0101r\u012bs\u0101ya \u0101k\u0101rehi sammattaniy\u0101ma\u1e43 okkamat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti etassa vibha\u1e45ge \u2013",translations:{en:"For the sake of making firm the contemplation of the five aggregates as impermanent, suffering, and not-self, in the analysis of what was said by the Blessed One: 'By what forty aspects does one acquire conformity acceptance? By what forty aspects does one enter the fixed course of rightness?'\u2014",pt:"Para a consolida\xe7\xe3o dessa mesma investiga\xe7\xe3o sobre a imperman\xeancia, o sofrimento e o n\xe3o-eu nos cinco agregados, o Aben\xe7oado, na an\xe1lise da seguinte quest\xe3o: 'Atrav\xe9s de quais quarenta os aspectos obt\xe9m-se a aceita\xe7\xe3o em conformidade? Atrav\xe9s de quais quarenta os aspectos entra-se no caminho correto da certeza?' \u2014",es:"Con el fin de fortalecer ese mismo juicio de impermanencia, sufrimiento y no-yo en los cinco agregados para ese yogui, el Bendito explic\xf3 en el an\xe1lisis de la pregunta: \u2018\xbfA trav\xe9s de qu\xe9 cuarenta aspectos se obtiene la paciencia conforme? \xbfA trav\xe9s de qu\xe9 cuarenta aspectos se entra en el sendero de la rectitud?\u2019:"}},{id:"vism-20.6",pali:"So eva\u1e43 anicc\u0101nupassan\u0101dipa\u1e6dipakkh\u0101na\u1e43 niccasa\xf1\xf1\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 pah\u0101nena visuddha\xf1\u0101\u1e47o sammasana\xf1\u0101\u1e47assa p\u0101ra\u1e43 gantv\u0101, ya\u1e43 ta\u1e43 sammasana\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101nantara\u1e43 \u2018\u2018paccuppann\u0101na\u1e43 dhamm\u0101na\u1e43 vipari\u1e47\u0101m\u0101nupassane pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 udayabbay\u0101nupassane \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti (pa\u1e6di. ma. m\u0101tik\u0101 1.6) udayabbay\u0101nupassana\u1e43 vutta\u1e43, tassa adhigam\u0101ya yoga\u1e43 \u0101rabhati. \u0100rabham\u0101no ca sa\u1e45khepato t\u0101va \u0101rabhati. Tatr\u0101ya\u1e43 p\u0101\u1e37i \u2013",translations:{en:"Thus, with his knowledge purified by abandoning the perception of permanence and so on, the counterparts of the contemplation of impermanence and so on, and having gone beyond the knowledge of comprehension, he undertakes the practice to attain the contemplation of arising and passing away. This, which follows the knowledge of comprehension, is spoken of as 'wisdom in contemplating the alteration of present phenomena, knowledge in the contemplation of arising and passing away' (Pa\u1e6dis. M. 1:6). When undertaking this, he begins at first in brief. Here is the P\u0101li text:",pt:"Aquele iogue, tendo purificado seu conhecimento por meio do abandono da percep\xe7\xe3o de perman\xeancia, etc., que s\xe3o opostos \xe0 contempla\xe7\xe3o da imperman\xeancia, etc., e tendo alcan\xe7ado o limite do conhecimento de investiga\xe7\xe3o (sammasana\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), inicia o esfor\xe7o para alcan\xe7ar a contempla\xe7\xe3o do surgimento e desaparecimento, que \xe9 dita imediatamente ap\xf3s o conhecimento de investiga\xe7\xe3o: \u201cA sabedoria na contempla\xe7\xe3o da mudan\xe7a dos dhammas presentes \xe9 o conhecimento na contempla\xe7\xe3o do surgimento e desaparecimento\u201d (Pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101magga M\u0101tik\u0101 1.6). Ao iniciar, ele come\xe7a de forma resumida. Aqui est\xe1 o texto em Pali:",es:"Aquel yogui, cuyo conocimiento se ha purificado mediante el abandono de la percepci\xf3n de permanencia y dem\xe1s, que son opuestos a la contemplaci\xf3n de la impermanencia y dem\xe1s, habiendo llegado al final del conocimiento de la comprensi\xf3n, se esfuerza para alcanzar el conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n del surgimiento y la desaparici\xf3n, del cual se dice inmediatamente despu\xe9s del conocimiento de la comprensi\xf3n: \xabLa sabidur\xeda en la contemplaci\xf3n del cambio de los estados presentes es el conocimiento en la contemplaci\xf3n del surgimiento y la desaparici\xf3n\xbb. Al comenzar, se esfuerza primero de manera resumida. Al respecto, este es el texto del P\u0101li:"}},{id:"vism-20.7",pali:"Athassa im\u0101ya taru\u1e47avipassan\u0101ya \u0101raddhavipassakassa dasa vipassanupakkiles\u0101 uppajjanti. Vipassanupakkiles\u0101 hi pa\u1e6divedhappattassa ariyas\u0101vakassa ceva vippa\u1e6dipannakassa ca nikkhittakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nassa kus\u012btapuggalassa nuppajjanti. Samm\u0101pa\u1e6dipannakassa pana yuttapayuttassa \u0101raddhavipassakassa kulaputtassa uppajjantiyeva.",translations:{en:"Then, for this one who has commenced insight with this tender insight, ten corruptions of insight arise. For the corruptions of insight do not arise for a noble disciple who has attained penetration, nor for one who is practicing wrongly, nor for one who has laid aside his meditation subject, nor for a lazy person. But they do indeed arise for a son of good family who is practicing rightly, is properly engaged, and has commenced insight.",pt:"Ent\xe3o, para esse iogue que iniciou a pr\xe1tica de vipassana, por meio deste vipassana incipiente, surgem as dez imperfei\xe7\xf5es de vipassana (vipassan\u016bpakkilesa). Pois as imperfei\xe7\xf5es de vipassana n\xe3o surgem em um nobre disc\xedpulo que j\xe1 alcan\xe7ou a penetra\xe7\xe3o (dos caminhos e frutos), nem em quem pratica de forma err\xf4nea, nem em quem abandonou o tema de medita\xe7\xe3o, nem em uma pessoa pregui\xe7osa. Contudo, elas certamente surgem no filho de boa fam\xedlia que pratica corretamente, que se empenha continuamente e que iniciou a pr\xe1tica de vipassana.",es:"Entonces, para este meditador que ha iniciado la visi\xf3n cabal con esta visi\xf3n cabal incipiente, surgen las diez imperfecciones de la visi\xf3n cabal. Ciertamente, las imperfecciones de la visi\xf3n cabal no les surgen ni a los nobles disc\xedpulos (ariyas\u0101vaka) que han alcanzado la penetraci\xf3n, ni a quienes practican err\xf3neamente, ni a quienes han abandonado el tema de meditaci\xf3n, ni a las personas perezosas. Sin embargo, s\xed les surgen a los hijos de buena familia que practican correctamente, que son diligentes y que han iniciado la visi\xf3n cabal."}},{id:"vism-20.8",pali:"Katame pana te dasa upakkiles\u0101ti? Obh\u0101so, \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, p\u012bti, passaddhi, sukha\u1e43, adhimokkho, paggaho, upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, upekkh\u0101, nikant\u012bti. Vutta\xf1heta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"Now, what are these ten corruptions? Illumination, knowledge, rapture, tranquility, happiness, resolution, exertion, establishment, equanimity, and delight. For it has been said:",pt:"Quais s\xe3o essas dez imperfei\xe7\xf5es? A saber: a aura luminosa (obh\u0101sa), o conhecimento (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), o arrebatamento (p\u012bti), a tranquilidade (passaddhi), a felicidade (sukha), a forte convic\xe7\xe3o (adhimokkha), o esfor\xe7o (paggaha), o estabelecimento da aten\xe7\xe3o (upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na), a equanimidade (upekkh\u0101) e o apego sutil (nikanti). Pois assim foi dito:",es:"\xbfCu\xe1les son estas diez imperfecciones? El aura luminosa (obh\u0101sa), el conocimiento (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), el arrebato (p\u012bti), la tranquilidad (passaddhi), la felicidad (sukha), la resoluci\xf3n (adhimokkha), el esfuerzo (paggaha), el establecimiento de la atenci\xf3n (upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na), la ecuanimidad (upekkh\u0101) y el apego sutil (nikanti). As\xed se ha dicho:"}},{id:"vism-20.9",pali:"Tattha obh\u0101so ti vipassanobh\u0101so. Tasmi\u1e43 uppanne yog\u0101vacaro \u2018\u2018na vata me ito pubbe evar\u016bpo obh\u0101so uppannapubbo, addh\u0101 maggappattosmi phalapattosm\u012b\u2019\u2019ti amaggameva \u2018\u2018maggo\u2019\u2019ti, aphalameva ca \u2018\u2018phala\u2019\u2019nti ga\u1e47h\u0101ti. Tassa amagga\u1e43 \u2018\u2018maggo\u2019\u2019ti aphala\u1e43 \u2018\u2018phala\u2019\u2019nti ga\u1e47hato vipassan\u0101v\u012bthi ukkant\u0101 n\u0101ma hoti. So attano m\u016blakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 vissajjetv\u0101 obh\u0101sameva ass\u0101dento nis\u012bdati.",translations:{en:"Herein, illumination means the illumination of insight. When it arises, the meditator thinks: 'Indeed, never before has such an illumination arisen in me. Surely, I have attained the path, I have attained the fruit!' He grasps what is not the path as 'path' and what is not the fruit as 'fruit.' For him who thus grasps the non-path as path and the non-fruit as fruit, the course of insight is said to have gone astray. Abandoning his basic meditation subject, he sits down just enjoying the illumination.",pt:"Aqui, \u2018aura\u2019 (obh\u0101sa) refere-se \xe0 aura luminosa de vipassana. Quando ela surge, o meditador pensa: \u2018Certamente, tal aura luminosa nunca havia surgido em mim antes; sem d\xfavida, alcancei o caminho, alcancei o fruto\u2019. Assim, ele toma o que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho como \u2018o caminho\u2019, e o que n\xe3o \xe9 o fruto como \u2018o fruto\u2019. Para aquele que toma o n\xe3o-caminho como \u2018o caminho\u2019 e o n\xe3o-fruto como \u2018o fruto\u2019, diz-se que o curso de vipassana foi desviado de sua rota. Abandonando seu tema de medita\xe7\xe3o original, ele permanece sentado apenas desfrutando da aura luminosa.",es:"En ese contexto, \xabaura luminosa\xbb se refiere al aura de la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassanobh\u0101sa). Cuando esta surge, el meditador piensa: \xabCiertamente, nunca antes me hab\xeda surgido un aura de tal naturaleza; sin duda he alcanzado el Sendero, he alcanzado el Fruto\xbb. As\xed, toma lo que no es el Sendero como \xabel Sendero\xbb y lo que no es el Fruto como \xabel Fruto\xbb. Al tomar lo que no es el Sendero como \xabel Sendero\xbb y lo que no es el Fruto como \xabel Fruto\xbb, se dice que el curso de su visi\xf3n cabal se ha desviado. \xc9l, abandonando su tema de meditaci\xf3n original, permanece deleit\xe1ndose \xfanicamente en el aura luminosa."}},{id:"vism-20.10",pali:"\xd1\u0101\u1e47a nti vipassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43. Tassa kira r\u016bp\u0101r\u016bpadhamme tulayantassa t\u012brentassa vissa\u1e6d\u1e6dhaindavajiramiva avihatavega\u1e43 tikhi\u1e47a\u1e43 s\u016bra\u1e43 ativisada\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 uppajjati.",translations:{en:"Knowledge means insight knowledge. It is said that for one who is weighing and judging material and immaterial phenomena, there arises a knowledge that is sharp, brave, and exceedingly clear, with its speed unimpeded like the thunderbolt of Indra that has been released.",pt:"\u2018Conhecimento\u2019 (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) refere-se ao conhecimento de vipassana. Para aquele que est\xe1 avaliando e investigando os dhammas f\xedsicas e mentais, surge um conhecimento afiado, poderoso, extremamente claro e de velocidade inabal\xe1vel, como o raio de Sakka quando lan\xe7ado.",es:"El t\xe9rmino 'conocimiento' (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) se refiere al conocimiento de la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a). Para aquel meditador que analiza e investiga los fealidades f\xedsicos y mentales (r\u016bp\u0101r\u016bpadhamma), surge un conocimiento extremadamente claro, agudo, valiente y de una velocidad imparable, como el rayo de Indra lanzado."}},{id:"vism-20.11",pali:"P\u012bt\u012b ti vipassan\u0101p\u012bti. Tassa kira tasmi\u1e43 samaye khuddak\u0101p\u012bti, kha\u1e47ik\u0101p\u012bti, okkantik\u0101p\u012bti, ubbeg\u0101p\u012bti, phara\u1e47\u0101p\u012bt\u012bti aya\u1e43 pa\xf1cavidh\u0101 p\u012bti sakalasar\u012bra\u1e43 p\u016brayam\u0101n\u0101 uppajjati.",translations:{en:"Rapture means insight-rapture. It is said that at that time these five kinds of rapture arise, filling his entire body: minor rapture, momentary rapture, showering rapture, uplifting rapture, and pervading rapture.",pt:"\u2018Arrebatamento\u2019 (p\u012bti) refere-se ao arrebatamento de vipassana. Para ele, naquele momento, surge este arrebatamento de cinco tipos, preenchendo todo o seu corpo: o arrebatamento menor (khuddak\u0101 p\u012bti), o arrebatamento moment\xe2neo (kha\u1e47ik\u0101 p\u012bti), o arrebatamento inundante (okkantik\u0101 p\u012bti), o arrebatamento elevador (ubbeg\u0101 p\u012bti) e o arrebatamento pervasivo (phara\u1e47\u0101 p\u012bti).",es:"El t\xe9rmino 'gozo' (p\u012bti) se refiere al gozo de la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassan\u0101p\u012bti). En ese momento, surgen en el meditador los cinco tipos de gozo: el gozo menor (khuddak\u0101), el gozo moment\xe1neo (kha\u1e47ik\u0101), el gozo descendente (okkantik\u0101), el gozo transportador (ubbeg\u0101) y el gozo omnipresente (phara\u1e47\u0101), llenando todo su cuerpo."}},{id:"vism-20.12",pali:"Passaddh\u012b ti vipassan\u0101passaddhi. Tassa kira tasmi\u1e43 samaye ratti\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne v\u0101 div\u0101\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne v\u0101 nisinnassa k\u0101yacitt\u0101na\u1e43 neva daratho, na g\u0101rava\u1e43, na kakkha\u1e37at\u0101, na akamma\xf1\xf1at\u0101, na gela\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, na va\u1e45kat\u0101 hoti, atha kho panassa k\u0101yacitt\u0101ni passaddh\u0101ni lah\u016bni mud\u016bni kamma\xf1\xf1\u0101ni suvisad\u0101ni ujuk\u0101niyeva honti. So imehi passaddh\u0101d\u012bhi anuggahitak\u0101yacitto tasmi\u1e43 samaye am\u0101nusi\u1e43 n\u0101ma rati\u1e43 anubhavati. Ya\u1e43 sandh\u0101ya vutta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"Tranquility means insight-tranquility. It is said that at that time, for one sitting in his night quarters or day quarters, there is no distress, heaviness, rigidity, unwieldiness, sickness, or crookedness of body and mind. Instead, his body and mind are tranquil, light, malleable, wieldy, proficient, and straight. With his body and mind aided by these qualities beginning with tranquility, at that time he experiences a superhuman delight. In reference to this it has been said:",pt:"\u2018Tranquilidade\u2019 (passaddhi) refere-se \xe0 tranquilidade de vipassana. Para ele, naquele momento, quer esteja sentado em seu local de repouso noturno ou diurno, n\xe3o h\xe1 afli\xe7\xe3o, peso, rigidez, inaptid\xe3o, enfermidade ou tortuosidade no corpo e na mente; pelo contr\xe1rio, seu corpo e sua mente tornam-se tranquilos, leves, male\xe1veis, d\xf3ceis, extremamente claros e retos. Com o corpo e a mente amparados por essas qualidades de tranquilidade e outras, ele experimenta, naquele momento, um deleite sobre-humano. Em refer\xeancia a isso, foi dito:",es:"El t\xe9rmino 'tranquilidad' (passaddhi) se refiere a la tranquilidad de la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassan\u0101passaddhi). En ese momento, ya sea sentado en su retiro nocturno o diurno, el meditador no experimenta angustia, pesadez, dureza, ineptitud, malestar ni doblez en su cuerpo y mente. Por el contrario, su cuerpo y mente est\xe1n tranquilos, ligeros, suaves, aptos para el trabajo, extremadamente claros y rectos. Con su cuerpo y mente sostenidos por esta tranquilidad y otras cualidades, experimenta en ese momento un deleite sobrehumano. En referencia a esto, se dijo:"}},{id:"vism-20.13",pali:"Sukha nti vipassan\u0101sukha\u1e43. Tassa kira tasmi\u1e43 samaye sakalasar\u012bra\u1e43 abhisandayam\u0101na\u1e43 atipa\u1e47\u012bta\u1e43 sukha\u1e43 uppajjati.",translations:{en:"\"Sukha\" means the happiness of insight. For at that time, an extremely refined happiness arises in him, suffusing his entire body.",pt:"\u2018Felicidade\u2019 (sukha) refere-se \xe0 felicidade de vipassana. Para ele, naquele momento, surge uma felicidade extremamente sublime que inunda todo o seu corpo.",es:"El t\xe9rmino 'felicidad' (sukha) se refiere a la felicidad de la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassan\u0101sukha). En ese momento, surge una felicidad sumamente exquisita que inunda todo su cuerpo."}},{id:"vism-20.14",pali:"Adhimokkho ti saddh\u0101. Vipassan\u0101sampayutt\u0101yeva hissa cittacetasik\u0101na\u1e43 atisayapas\u0101dabh\u016bt\u0101 balavat\u012b saddh\u0101 uppajjati.",translations:{en:"\"Adhimokkha\" means faith. For a powerful faith associated only with insight arises in him, which is an exceptional clarity concerning the mind and mental factors.",pt:"\u2018Forte convic\xe7\xe3o\u2019 (adhimokkha) refere-se \xe0 f\xe9 (saddh\u0101). De fato, surge nele uma f\xe9 poderosa associada a vipassana, que constitui uma extrema purifica\xe7\xe3o e clareza da mente e dos fatores mentais.",es:"El t\xe9rmino 'resoluci\xf3n' (adhimokkha) se refiere a la fe (saddh\u0101). Surge en \xe9l una fe poderosa que produce una claridad extraordinaria en la mente y sus factores mentales asociados con la visi\xf3n cabal."}},{id:"vism-20.15",pali:"Paggaho ti v\u012briya\u1e43. Vipassan\u0101sampayuttameva hissa asithila\u1e43 anacc\u0101raddha\u1e43 supaggahita\u1e43 v\u012briya\u1e43 uppajjati.",translations:{en:"\"Paggaha\" means energy. For energy associated only with insight arises in him that is not lax, not over-exerted, and well-sustained.",pt:"\u2018Esfor\xe7o\u2019 (paggaha) refere-se \xe0 energia (v\u012briya). De fato, surge nele uma energia associada a vipassana, que n\xe3o \xe9 frouxa nem excessivamente tensa, mas sim bem equilibrada e sustentada.",es:"El t\xe9rmino 'esfuerzo' (paggaha) se refiere a la energ\xeda (v\u012briya). Surge en \xe9l un esfuerzo bien sostenido, asociado con la visi\xf3n cabal, que no es ni demasiado laxo ni demasiado tenso."}},{id:"vism-20.16",pali:"Upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na nti sati. Vipassan\u0101sampayutt\u0101yeva hissa supa\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101 supati\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101 nikh\u0101t\u0101 acal\u0101 pabbatar\u0101jasadis\u0101 sati uppajjati. So ya\u1e43 ya\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101vajjati samann\u0101harati manasikaroti paccavekkhati, ta\u1e43 ta\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101namassa okkhanditv\u0101 pakkhanditv\u0101 dibbacakkhuno paraloko viya satiy\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"\"Upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\" means mindfulness. For mindfulness associated only with insight arises in him that is well-established, firmly founded, dug in, unshakable, like a king of mountains. Whatever object he adverts to, considers, gives attention to, or reviews, that very object presents itself to his mindfulness, leaping and jumping upon it, like another world to the divine eye.",pt:"\u2018Estabelecimento da aten\xe7\xe3o\u2019 (upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na) refere-se \xe0 aten\xe7\xe3o plena (sati). De fato, surge nele uma aten\xe7\xe3o plena associada a vipassana, que \xe9 bem estabelecida, bem fundamentada, inabal\xe1vel como um pilar profundamente fincado e semelhante ao rei das montanhas. Qualquer estado sobre o qual ele reflita, atenda, considere ou revise, esse estado manifesta-se \xe0 sua aten\xe7\xe3o plena, penetrando e mergulhando nele, assim como o outro mundo se manifesta para quem possui o olho divino.",es:"El t\xe9rmino 'presencia' (upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na) se refiere a la atenci\xf3n plena (sati). Surge en \xe9l una atenci\xf3n plena asociada con la visi\xf3n cabal, bien establecida, firme, profunda e inamovible como el rey de las monta\xf1as. Cualquier objeto que \xe9l considere, traiga a la mente, atienda o reflexione, dicho objeto se presenta y penetra en su atenci\xf3n de forma tan clara como el otro mundo para alguien dotado del ojo divino."}},{id:"vism-20.17",pali:"Upekkh\u0101 ti vipassanupekkh\u0101 ceva \u0101vajjanupekkh\u0101 ca. Tasmi\u1e43 hissa samaye sabbasa\u1e45kh\u0101resu majjhattabh\u016bt\u0101 vipassanupekkh\u0101pi balavat\u012b uppajjati. Manodv\u0101re \u0101vajjanupekkh\u0101pi. S\u0101 hissa ta\u1e43 ta\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101vajjantassa vissa\u1e6d\u1e6dhaindavajiramiva pattapu\u1e6de pakkhitta tattan\u0101r\u0101co viya ca s\u016br\u0101 tikhi\u1e47\u0101 hutv\u0101 vahati.",translations:{en:"\"Upekkh\u0101\" means both the equanimity of insight and the equanimity of adverting. At that time, a powerful equanimity of insight, which is a state of neutrality towards all formations, arises in him, as does the equanimity of adverting at the mind-door. For him, as he adverts to this or that object, the latter proceeds valiantly and sharply, like a discharged thunderbolt of Inda or like a heated iron arrow placed in a leaf-cup.",pt:"\u2018Equanimidade\u2019 (upekkh\u0101) refere-se tanto \xe0 equanimidade de vipassana (vipassanupekkh\u0101) quanto \xe0 equanimidade de advert\xeancia (\u0101vajjanupekkh\u0101). Pois, naquele momento, surge nele uma poderosa equanimidade de vipassana, que se mant\xe9m neutra diante de todas as forma\xe7\xf5es condicionadas. Surge tamb\xe9m a equanimidade de advert\xeancia na porta da mente. Para ele, ao refletir sobre este ou aquele estado, ela atua de forma afiada e poderosa, como o raio de Sakka quando lan\xe7ado, ou como uma flecha de ferro incandescente disparada contra um cesto de folhas.",es:"El t\xe9rmino 'ecuanimidad' (upekkh\u0101) se refiere tanto a la ecuanimidad de la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassanupekkh\u0101) como a la ecuanimidad de la advertencia (\u0101vajjanupekkh\u0101). En ese momento, surge poderosamente la ecuanimidad de la visi\xf3n cabal, que se mantiene neutral ante todas las formaciones (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ras), y tambi\xe9n la ecuanimidad de la advertencia en la puerta de la mente. Esta \xfaltima fluye de manera valiente y aguda cuando \xe9l advierte cada objeto, como el rayo de Indra lanzado o como una flecha de hierro candente disparada contra una cesta de hojas."}},{id:"vism-20.18",pali:"Nikant\u012b ti vipassan\u0101nikanti. Eva\u1e43 obh\u0101s\u0101dipa\u1e6dima\u1e47\u1e0dit\u0101ya hissa vipassan\u0101ya \u0101laya\u1e43 kurum\u0101n\u0101 sukhum\u0101 sant\u0101k\u0101r\u0101 nikanti uppajjati. Y\u0101 nikanti kilesoti pariggahetumpi na sakk\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"\"Nikanti\" means delight in insight. For as he forms an attachment to the insight adorned with light and so on, a subtle delight of peaceful appearance arises in him. This delight is such that it cannot even be grasped as a defilement.",pt:"\u2018Apego sutil\u2019 (nikanti) refere-se ao apego a vipassana (vipassan\u0101nikanti). Assim, surge nele um apego sutil e de aspecto pac\xedfico que se apega \xe0 sua pr\xe1tica de vipassana, a qual est\xe1 adornada com a aura luminosa e outras qualidades. Esse apego \xe9 t\xe3o sutil que n\xe3o se consegue sequer reconhec\xea-lo como uma impureza mental.",es:"El t\xe9rmino 'apego' (nikanti) se refiere al apego sutil hacia la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassan\u0101nikanti). Surge en \xe9l una forma sutil y pac\xedfica de deleite que genera apego hacia esa visi\xf3n cabal adornada con el resplandor y otras cualidades. Este apego es de tal naturaleza que el meditador no es capaz de identificarlo siquiera como una impureza (kilesa)."}},{id:"vism-20.19",pali:"Ettha ca obh\u0101s\u0101dayo upakkilesavatthut\u0101ya upakkiles\u0101ti vutt\u0101, na akusalatt\u0101. Nikanti pana upakkileso ceva upakkilesavatthu ca. Vatthuvaseneva cete dasa. G\u0101havasena pana samati\u1e43sa honti. Katha\u1e43? \u2018\u2018Mama obh\u0101so uppanno\u2019\u2019ti ga\u1e47hato hi di\u1e6d\u1e6dhig\u0101ho hoti, \u2018\u2018man\u0101po vata obh\u0101so uppanno\u2019\u2019ti ga\u1e47hato m\u0101nag\u0101ho, obh\u0101sa\u1e43 ass\u0101dayato ta\u1e47h\u0101g\u0101ho, iti obh\u0101se di\u1e6d\u1e6dhim\u0101nata\u1e47h\u0101vasena tayo g\u0101h\u0101. Tath\u0101 sesesup\u012bti eva\u1e43 g\u0101havasena samati\u1e43sa upakkiles\u0101 honti. Tesa\u1e43 vasena akusalo abyatto yog\u0101vacaro obh\u0101s\u0101d\u012bsu kampati vikkhipati. Obh\u0101s\u0101d\u012bsu ekeka\u1e43 \u2018\u2018eta\u1e43 mama, esohamasmi, eso me att\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (ma. ni. 1.241) samanupassati. Ten\u0101hu por\u0101\u1e47\u0101 \u2013",translations:{en:"Herein, light and the others are called corruptions because they are the basis for corruption, not because they are unwholesome. Delight, however, is both a corruption and a basis for corruption. By way of their basis, they are ten. But by way of grasping, they become thirty. How so? For one who grasps thinking, \"Light has arisen for me,\" there is grasping by view. For one who grasps thinking, \"Ah, how pleasing is the light that has arisen,\" there is grasping by conceit. For one who savors the light, there is grasping by craving. Thus, in the case of light, there are three kinds of grasping: by view, conceit, and craving. The same applies to the rest. In this way, by way of grasping, there are thirty corruptions. Because of them, the unskilled, inexpert yogi trembles and is distracted by light and the others. He regards each of them, from light onwards, thus: \"This is mine, this I am, this is my self.\" Therefore the ancients said:",pt:"E aqui, a aura e os demais dhammas s\xe3o chamados de 'imperfei\xe7\xf5es' por serem a base das imperfei\xe7\xf5es, e n\xe3o por serem dhammas prejudiciais. O apego sutil, por\xe9m, \xe9 tanto uma imperfei\xe7\xe3o quanto a base para as imperfei\xe7\xf5es. Pelo aspecto das bases, eles s\xe3o dez. Mas pelo aspecto do apego, eles se tornam trinta. Como? Pois para aquele que se apega pensando: 'A aura surgiu para mim', ocorre o apego da vis\xe3o incorreta; para aquele que se apega pensando: 'Que aura maravilhosa surgiu!', ocorre o apego do orgulho; e para aquele que se deleita na aura, ocorre o apego do desejo. Assim, em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 aura, h\xe1 tr\xeas tipos de apego por meio da vis\xe3o incorreta, do orgulho e do desejo. O mesmo se aplica aos demais. Desse modo, pelo aspecto do apego, h\xe1 trinta imperfei\xe7\xf5es. Sob a influ\xeancia delas, o praticante inexperiente e ignorante vacila e se dispersa diante da aura e dos outros dhammas. Ele contempla cada um deles, como a aura, etc., pensando: 'Isto \xe9 meu, isto eu sou, isto \xe9 o meu eu'. Por isso os antigos disseram:",es:"En este contexto, el resplandor y los dem\xe1s factores se denominan 'imperfecciones' (upakkilesa) porque constituyen el objeto de las mismas, no porque sean en s\xed mismos estados perjudiciales (akusala). Sin embargo, el apego (nikanti) es tanto una imperfecci\xf3n como el objeto de una imperfecci\xf3n. Estos son diez seg\xfan su base (vatthu), pero llegan a ser treinta seg\xfan el modo de aferramiento (g\u0101ha). \xbfC\xf3mo? Pues, para quien se aferra pensando: 'Ha surgido un resplandor en m\xed', existe el aferramiento por visi\xf3n err\xf3nea (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhig\u0101ho); para quien piensa: '\xa1Qu\xe9 agradable resplandor ha surgido!', existe el aferramiento por orgullo (m\u0101nag\u0101ho); y para quien se deleita en el resplandor, existe el aferramiento por deseo (ta\u1e47h\u0101g\u0101ho). As\xed, respecto al resplandor, existen tres tipos de aferramiento seg\xfan la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea, el orgullo y el deseo. Del mismo modo sucede con los dem\xe1s factores; de esta manera, seg\xfan el modo de aferramiento, hay treinta imperfecciones. Debido a ellas, el meditador (yog\u0101vacaro) que no es h\xe1bil ni experto se conmociona y se distrae ante el resplandor y los dem\xe1s factores. Considera a cada uno de ellos, como el resplandor, de la siguiente manera: 'Esto es m\xedo, esto soy yo, esto es mi s\xed-mismo (att\u0101)'. Por eso dijeron los antiguos:"}},{id:"vism-20.20",pali:"So eva\u1e43 upaparikkhitv\u0101 obh\u0101sa\u1e43 \u2018\u2018neta\u1e43 mama, nesohamasmi, na meso att\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (ma. ni. 1.241) samanupassati. \xd1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43\u2026pe\u2026 nikanti\u1e43 \u2018\u2018neta\u1e43 mama, nesohamasmi, na meso att\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (ma. ni. 1.241) samanupassati. Eva\u1e43 samanupassanto obh\u0101s\u0101d\u012bsu na kampati na vedhati. Ten\u0101hu por\u0101\u1e47\u0101 \u2013",translations:{en:"Having investigated in this way, he regards light thus: \"This is not mine, this I am not, this is not my self.\" He regards knowledge... he regards delight thus: \"This is not mine, this I am not, this is not my self.\" Regarding them thus, he does not tremble or shake on account of light and the others. Therefore the ancients said:",pt:"Tendo examinado dessa forma, ele contempla a aura assim: 'Isto n\xe3o \xe9 meu, isto eu n\xe3o sou, isto n\xe3o \xe9 o meu eu'. Ele contempla o conhecimento... [e os demais]... e o apego sutil assim: 'Isto n\xe3o \xe9 meu, isto eu n\xe3o sou, isto n\xe3o \xe9 o meu eu'. Contemplando dessa maneira, ele n\xe3o vacila nem treme diante da aura e dos outros dhammas. Por isso os antigos disseram:",es:"\xc9l, habi\xe9ndolo examinado de esta manera, contempla el resplandor as\xed: 'Esto no es m\xedo, esto no soy yo, esto no es mi s\xed-mismo'. Contempla el conocimiento... (y as\xed sucesivamente hasta)... el apego: 'Esto no es m\xedo, esto no soy yo, esto no es mi s\xed-mismo'. Al contemplar as\xed, no se conmociona ni se agita ante el resplandor y los dem\xe1s factores. Por eso dijeron los antiguos:"}}]},438,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,s,n,i,t){n.exports=[{id:"vism-21.1",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dhanna\u1e43 pana \xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101na\u1e43 vasena sikh\u0101ppatt\u0101 vipassan\u0101, navama\xf1ca sacc\u0101nulomika\xf1\u0101\u1e47anti aya\u1e43 pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi n\u0101ma. A\u1e6d\u1e6dhanna nti cettha upakkilesavimutta\u1e43 v\u012bthipa\u1e6dipannavipassan\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 udayabbay\u0101nupassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, bha\u1e45g\u0101nupassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, bhayatupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, \u0101d\u012bnav\u0101nupassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, nibbid\u0101nupassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, mu\xf1citukamyat\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101nupassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47anti im\u0101ni a\u1e6d\u1e6dha \xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni veditabb\u0101ni. Navama\u1e43 sacc\u0101nulomika\xf1\u0101\u1e47a nti anulomasseta\u1e43 adhivacana\u1e43. Tasm\u0101 ta\u1e43 samp\u0101detuk\u0101mena upakkilesavimutta\u1e43 udayabbaya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101di\u1e43 katv\u0101 etesu \xf1\u0101\u1e47esu yogo kara\u1e47\u012byo.",translations:{en:"Insight that has reached its culmination by means of the eight knowledges, and the ninth, the knowledge in conformity with the truths\u2014this is called the purification by knowledge and vision of the way. Herein, the eight knowledges are to be understood as: the knowledge of contemplation of arising and passing away, which is free from corruptions and reckoned as insight that has entered the path; the knowledge of contemplation of dissolution; the knowledge of the appearance of terror; the knowledge of contemplation of danger; the knowledge of contemplation of disenchantment; the knowledge of desire for deliverance; the knowledge of contemplation of reflection; and the knowledge of equanimity towards formations. The ninth, the knowledge in conformity with the truths, is a designation for conformity knowledge. Therefore, one who wishes to accomplish this should make an effort in these knowledges, beginning with the knowledge of contemplation of arising and passing away, which is free from corruptions.",pt:"O insight que atinge o \xe1pice por meio de oito conhecimentos, juntamente com o nono, que \xe9 o conhecimento de conformidade com as verdades, \xe9 chamado de Purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo Conhecimento e Vis\xe3o do Caminho da Pr\xe1tica. Aqui, por 'oito', devem ser entendidos estes oito conhecimentos: (1) o conhecimento da contempla\xe7\xe3o do surgimento e desaparecimento, que est\xe1 livre das imperfei\xe7\xf5es e segue o curso correto do insight; (2) o conhecimento da contempla\xe7\xe3o da dissolu\xe7\xe3o; (3) o conhecimento do aparecimento como terror; (4) o conhecimento da contempla\xe7\xe3o do perigo; (5) o conhecimento da contempla\xe7\xe3o do desencanto; (6) o conhecimento do desejo de liberta\xe7\xe3o; (7) o conhecimento da contempla\xe7\xe3o reflexiva; e (8) o conhecimento da equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es. O 'nono, conhecimento de conformidade com as verdades' \xe9 um sin\xf4nimo para o conhecimento de conformidade. Portanto, aquele que deseja realizar essa purifica\xe7\xe3o deve aplicar-se a esses conhecimentos, come\xe7ando com o conhecimento do surgimento e desaparecimento livre de imperfei\xe7\xf5es.",es:"La purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n del camino (pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi) consiste en el conjunto de conocimientos de la visi\xf3n interna que alcanzan su punto culminante mediante ocho conocimientos, siendo el noveno el conocimiento de conformidad con las verdades (sacc\u0101nulomika\xf1\u0101\u1e47a). En este contexto, bajo los ocho conocimientos deben entenderse: 1. El conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n del surgimiento y la desaparici\xf3n (udayabbay\u0101nupassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), que es la visi\xf3n interna libre de imperfecciones y en el curso correcto; 2. El conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n de la disoluci\xf3n; 3. El conocimiento de la apariencia de terror; 4. El conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n del peligro; 5. El conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n del desencanto; 6. El conocimiento del deseo de liberaci\xf3n; 7. El conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n reflexiva; y 8. El conocimiento de la ecuanimidad respecto a las formaciones. El noveno, el conocimiento de conformidad con las verdades, es un sin\xf3nimo de 'conformidad' (anuloma). Por lo tanto, quien desee perfeccionar dicha purificaci\xf3n debe esforzarse en estos conocimientos, comenzando por el conocimiento del surgimiento y la desaparici\xf3n libre de imperfecciones."}},{id:"vism-21.2",pali:"Puna udayabbaya\xf1\u0101\u1e47e yogo kimatthiyoti ce? Lakkha\u1e47asallakkha\u1e47attho. Udayabbaya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 hi he\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101 dasahi upakkilesehi upakkili\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43 hutv\u0101 y\u0101th\u0101vasarasato tilakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 sallakkhetu\u1e43 n\u0101sakkhi. Upakkilesavimutta\u1e43 pana sakkoti. Tasm\u0101 lakkha\u1e47asallakkha\u1e47atthamettha puna yogo kara\u1e47\u012byo.",translations:{en:"And why make effort again in the knowledge of contemplation of arising and passing away? For the purpose of discerning the characteristics. For the knowledge of contemplation of arising and passing away, having been previously defiled by the ten corruptions, was unable to discern the three characteristics as they really are. But when freed from the corruptions, it is able to. Therefore, effort must be made here again for the purpose of discerning the characteristics.",pt:"Se for perguntado: 'Qual \xe9 o prop\xf3sito de se aplicar novamente ao conhecimento do surgimento e desaparecimento?', a resposta \xe9: 'Com o prop\xf3sito de discernir claramente as caracter\xedsticas'. Pois o conhecimento do surgimento e desaparecimento anteriormente, estando corrompido pelas dez imperfei\xe7\xf5es, n\xe3o era capaz de discernir claramente as tr\xeas caracter\xedsticas de acordo com a sua verdadeira natureza. Mas, livre das imperfei\xe7\xf5es, ele \xe9 capaz. Portanto, deve-se aplicar novamente a ele aqui com o prop\xf3sito de discernir claramente as caracter\xedsticas.",es:"\xbfCu\xe1l es el prop\xf3sito de esforzarse nuevamente en el conocimiento del surgimiento y la desaparici\xf3n? El prop\xf3sito es el discernimiento preciso de las caracter\xedsticas (lakkha\u1e47asallakkha\u1e47attho). Pues el conocimiento del surgimiento y la desaparici\xf3n, al haber estado previamente manchado por las diez imperfecciones, no fue capaz de discernir con exactitud las tres caracter\xedsticas seg\xfan su naturaleza real. Pero una vez libre de imperfecciones, s\xed es capaz. Por ello, debe aplicarse nuevamente el esfuerzo aqu\xed para discernir con precisi\xf3n las caracter\xedsticas."}},{id:"vism-21.3",pali:"Ettha ca anicca\u1e43, aniccalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, dukkha\u1e43, dukkhalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43, anatt\u0101, anattalakkha\u1e47anti aya\u1e43 vibh\u0101go veditabbo. Tattha anicca nti khandhapa\xf1caka\u1e43. Kasm\u0101? Upp\u0101davaya\xf1\xf1athattabh\u0101v\u0101, hutv\u0101 abh\u0101vato v\u0101. Upp\u0101davaya\xf1\xf1athatta\u1e43 aniccalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 hutv\u0101 abh\u0101vasa\u1e45kh\u0101to v\u0101 \u0101k\u0101ravik\u0101ro.",translations:{en:"Herein, this distinction is to be understood: the impermanent and the characteristic of impermanence; suffering and the characteristic of suffering; not-self and the characteristic of not-self. Therein, 'the impermanent' refers to the five aggregates. Why? Because of their arising, passing away, and altering, or because they cease to be after having been. Arising, passing away, and alteration is the characteristic of impermanence; or it is the change of mode reckoned as ceasing to be after having been.",pt:"E aqui, deve-se compreender esta distin\xe7\xe3o: o impermanente, a caracter\xedstica da imperman\xeancia; o sofrimento, a caracter\xedstica do sofrimento; o n\xe3o-eu, a caracter\xedstica do n\xe3o-eu. Entre estes, 'o impermanente' refere-se aos cinco agregados. Por qu\xea? Devido ao seu estado de surgimento, desaparecimento e altera\xe7\xe3o, ou porque deixam de existir ap\xf3s terem surgido. O surgimento, o desaparecimento e a altera\xe7\xe3o constituem a caracter\xedstica da imperman\xeancia, ou a altera\xe7\xe3o de modo que \xe9 descrita como deixar de existir ap\xf3s ter surgido.",es:"En este punto, debe entenderse la distinci\xf3n entre: lo impermanente y la caracter\xedstica de impermanencia; lo sufriente y la caracter\xedstica de sufrimiento; el no-yo y la caracter\xedstica de no-yo. De ellos, 'lo impermanente' se refiere a los cinco agregados. \xbfPor qu\xe9? Debido a su estado de surgimiento, desaparici\xf3n y alteraci\xf3n, o bien por su inexistencia tras haber existido. El surgimiento, la desaparici\xf3n y la alteraci\xf3n constituyen la 'caracter\xedstica de impermanencia'; o bien, es el cambio de estado definido como la inexistencia tras haber existido."}},{id:"vism-21.4",pali:"Tayida\u1e43 sabbampi aya\u1e43 yog\u0101vacaro upakkilesavimuttena v\u012bthipa\u1e6dipannavipassan\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101tena udayabbay\u0101nupassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena y\u0101th\u0101vasarasato sallakkheti.",translations:{en:"This meditator discerns all this as it really is with the knowledge of contemplation of arising and passing away, which is free from corruptions and reckoned as insight that has entered the path.",pt:"O praticante discerne claramente tudo isso de acordo com a sua verdadeira natureza por meio do conhecimento da contempla\xe7\xe3o do surgimento e desaparecimento, que \xe9 livre de imperfei\xe7\xf5es e constitui o curso correto do insight.",es:"El practicante nota adecuadamente seg\xfan su verdadera naturaleza todo esto mediante el conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n del surgimiento y la desaparici\xf3n, que es llamado 'vipassana que ha entrado en el camino' y est\xe1 libre de las imperfecciones."}},{id:"vism-21.5",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 sallakkhetv\u0101 punappuna\u1e43 \u2018\u2018anicca\u1e43 dukkhamanatt\u0101\u2019\u2019ti r\u016bp\u0101r\u016bpadhamme tulayato t\u012brayato ta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 tikkha\u1e43 hutv\u0101 vahati, sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 lahu\u1e43 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhahanti, \xf1\u0101\u1e47e tikkhe vahante sa\u1e45kh\u0101resu lahu\u1e43 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhahantesu upp\u0101da\u1e43 v\u0101 \u1e6dhiti\u1e43 v\u0101 pavatta\u1e43 v\u0101 nimitta\u1e43 v\u0101 na samp\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101ti. Khayavayabhedanirodheyeva sati santi\u1e6d\u1e6dhati. Tassa \u2018\u2018eva\u1e43 uppajjitv\u0101 eva\u1e43 n\u0101ma sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragata\u1e43 nirujjhat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti passato etasmi\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101ne bha\u1e45g\u0101nupassana\u1e43 n\u0101ma vipassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 uppajjati. Ya\u1e43 sandh\u0101ya vutta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"For one who has thus discerned, as he repeatedly weighs and judges material and immaterial states as 'impermanent, suffering, not-self,' that knowledge becomes sharp and proceeds swiftly, and formations appear readily. When his knowledge proceeds sharply and formations appear readily, his mind does not alight on their arising, or standing, or occurrence, or sign. His mindfulness is established only on their destruction, passing away, breaking up, and cessation. For him who sees, 'Having thus arisen, the aggregate of formations thus ceases,' at that point the insight knowledge called 'contemplation of dissolution' arises. In reference to this it was said:",pt:"Para aquele que discerne dessa forma e repetidamente avalia e investiga os dhammas materiais e imateriais como 'impermanentes, sofrimento, n\xe3o-eu', esse conhecimento torna-se afiado e flui rapidamente; as forma\xe7\xf5es manifestam-se velozmente. Quando o conhecimento flui de forma afiada e as forma\xe7\xf5es manifestam-se velozmente, ele n\xe3o alcan\xe7a mais o surgimento, a perman\xeancia, a continuidade ou o sinal das forma\xe7\xf5es. A aten\xe7\xe3o estabelece-se apenas na cessa\xe7\xe3o, que consiste no esgotamento, no decl\xednio e na dissolu\xe7\xe3o. Para aquele que v\xea: 'Tendo surgido dessa forma, as forma\xe7\xf5es cessam dessa maneira', surge nesse est\xe1gio o conhecimento de insight chamado contempla\xe7\xe3o da dissolu\xe7\xe3o. Em refer\xeancia a isso, foi dito:",es:"Habiendo notado esto de tal manera, para aquel que sopesa y examina repetidamente los fealidades f\xedsicos y mentales como 'impermanentes, sufrimiento y no-yo', ese conocimiento se vuelve agudo y fluye; las formaciones aparecen r\xe1pidamente. Al fluir el conocimiento con agudeza y aparecer las formaciones r\xe1pidamente, no se llega al surgimiento, a la duraci\xf3n, al proceso ni al signo; la atenci\xf3n se establece \xfanicamente en el cese, que es el agotamiento, el desvanecimiento y la ruptura. Para aquel que ve: 'Habiendo surgido as\xed, este conjunto de formaciones cesa de esta manera', surge en ese punto el conocimiento de visi\xf3n profunda llamado contemplaci\xf3n de la disoluci\xf3n. En referencia a esto se ha dicho:"}},{id:"vism-21.6",pali:"\u2018\u2018Katha\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47apa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101 bha\u1e45g\u0101nupassane pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 vipassane \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43? R\u016bp\u0101ramma\u1e47at\u0101 citta\u1e43 uppajjitv\u0101 bhijjati, ta\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101 tassa cittassa bha\u1e45ga\u1e43 anupassati. Anupassat\u012b ti katha\u1e43 anupassati? Aniccato anupassati no niccato, dukkhato anupassati no sukhato, anattato anupassati no attato, nibbindati no nandati, virajjati no rajjati, nirodheti no samudeti, pa\u1e6dinissajjati no \u0101diyati.",translations:{en:"\"How is wisdom in the contemplation of dissolution by reflecting on the object, which is knowledge in insight? A mind having form as its object arises and breaks up. Having reflected on that object, one contemplates the dissolution of that mind. How does one contemplate? One contemplates it as impermanent, not as permanent; as suffering, not as pleasant; as not-self, not as self. One becomes disenchanted, one does not delight; one becomes dispassionate, one is not impassioned; one brings it to cessation, one does not cause it to originate; one relinquishes, one does not grasp.",pt:"\u201cComo a sabedoria na contempla\xe7\xe3o da dissolu\xe7\xe3o, ap\xf3s refletir sobre o objeto, \xe9 o conhecimento de insight? A mente que tem a forma como objeto surge e se dissolve; tendo refletido sobre esse objeto, contempla-se a dissolu\xe7\xe3o daquela mente. Como se contempla? Contempla-se como impermanente, n\xe3o como permanente; contempla-se como sofrimento, n\xe3o como felicidade; contempla-se como n\xe3o-eu, n\xe3o como eu; desapega-se, n\xe3o se deleita; torna-se desapaixonado, n\xe3o se apaixona; faz-se cessar, n\xe3o se faz surgir; abandona-se, n\xe3o se apega.",es:"'\xbfC\xf3mo es que el conocimiento de visi\xf3n profunda es la sabidur\xeda de la contemplaci\xf3n de la disoluci\xf3n habiendo reflexionado sobre el objeto? El pensamiento con la forma como objeto surge y se disuelve; habiendo reflexionado sobre ese objeto, contempla la disoluci\xf3n de ese pensamiento. \xbfC\xf3mo contempla? Lo contempla como impermanente, no como permanente; como sufrimiento, no como felicidad; como no-yo, no como el yo; se desencanta, no se deleita; se vuelve desapasionado, no se apega; causa el cese, no causa el surgimiento; renuncia, no se aferra."}},{id:"vism-21.7",pali:"\u2018\u2018Aniccato anupassanto niccasa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 pajahati. Dukkhato anupassanto sukhasa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, anattato anupassanto attasa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, nibbindanto nandi\u1e43, virajjanto r\u0101ga\u1e43, nirodhento samudaya\u1e43 pa\u1e6dinissajjanto \u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 pajahati.",translations:{en:"\"Contemplating as impermanent, one abandons the perception of permanence. Contemplating as suffering, one abandons the perception of pleasure. Contemplating as not-self, one abandons the perception of self. Becoming disenchanted, one abandons delight. Becoming dispassionate, one abandons lust. Bringing to cessation, one abandons origination. Relinquishing, one abandons grasping.\"",pt:"\u201cContemplando como impermanente, abandona-se a percep\xe7\xe3o de perman\xeancia. Contemplando como sofrimento, abandona-se a percep\xe7\xe3o de felicidade; contemplando como n\xe3o-eu, abandona-se a percep\xe7\xe3o de eu; desapegando-se, abandona-se o deleite; tornando-se desapaixonado, abandona-se a cobi\xe7a; fazendo cessar, abandona-se a origem; abandonando, desiste-se do apego.",es:"Al contemplar como impermanente, abandona la percepci\xf3n de permanencia. Al contemplar como sufrimiento, abandona la percepci\xf3n de felicidad; al contemplar como no-yo, abandona la percepci\xf3n del yo; al desencantarse, abandona el deleite; al volverse desapasionado, abandona el deseo; al causar el cese, abandona el origen; al renunciar, abandona el aferramiento."}},{id:"vism-21.8",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 sabbasa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101na\u1e43 khayavayabhedanirodh\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 bha\u1e45g\u0101nupassana\u1e43 \u0101sevantassa bh\u0101ventassa bahul\u012bkarontassa sabbabhavayonigati\u1e6dhitisatt\u0101v\u0101sesu pabhedak\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 sukhena j\u012bvituk\u0101massa bh\u012brukapurisassa s\u012bhabyagghad\u012bpiacchataracchayakkharakkhasaca\u1e47\u1e0dago\u1e47aca\u1e47\u1e0dakukkurapabhinnamadaca\u1e47\u1e0dahatthighora\u0101s\u012bvisaasanivicakkasus\u0101nara\u1e47abh\u016bmijalitaa\u1e45g\u0101rak\u0101su\u0101dayo viya mah\u0101bhaya\u1e43 hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhahanti. Tassa \u2018\u2018at\u012bt\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 niruddh\u0101, paccuppann\u0101 nirujjhanti, an\u0101gate nibbattanakasa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101pi evameva nirujjhissant\u012b\u2019\u2019ti passato etasmi\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101ne bhayatupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u0101ma uppajjati.",translations:{en:"As he thus cultivates, develops, and makes much of this contemplation of dissolution\u2014which has as its object the destruction, passing away, breaking up, and cessation of all formations\u2014the formations that bring about distinction in all kinds of becoming, birth-places, destinies, stations, and abodes of beings appear to him as a great terror, just as lions, tigers, leopards, bears, hyenas, yakkhas, raksasas, fierce bulls, savage dogs, fierce elephants in rut, terrible venomous snakes, thunderbolts, charnel grounds, battlefields, and blazing pits of embers appear to a timid man who wishes to live in comfort. When he sees, \u201cPast formations have ceased, present ones are ceasing, and future formations that would be generated will also cease in just the same way,\u201d at this stage the knowledge called \u2018appearance as terror\u2019 arises in him.",pt:"Para aquele que assim cultiva, desenvolve e pratica repetidamente a contempla\xe7\xe3o da dissolu\xe7\xe3o, que tem como objeto o fim, o decl\xednio, a quebra e a cessa\xe7\xe3o de todas as forma\xe7\xf5es, as forma\xe7\xf5es que se dissolvem em todos os planos de exist\xeancia, modos de gera\xe7\xe3o, destinos, esta\xe7\xf5es da consci\xeancia e moradas dos seres aparecem como um grande perigo, assim como le\xf5es, tigres, leopardos, ursos, hienas, dem\xf4nios, esp\xedritos malignos, touros ferozes, c\xe3es bravos, elefantes selvagens no cio, cobras venenosas terr\xedveis, raios, cemit\xe9rios, campos de batalha ou fossas de brasas ardentes apareceriam para um homem temeroso que deseja viver em seguran\xe7a. Para aquele que contempla que 'as forma\xe7\xf5es passadas cessaram, as presentes est\xe3o cessando e as futuras que surgir\xe3o tamb\xe9m cessar\xe3o da mesma forma', surge, neste est\xe1gio, o conhecimento conhecido como o estabelecimento do medo (bhayatupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\xf1\u0101\u1e47a).",es:"Para aquel que de esta manera cultiva, desarrolla y practica frecuentemente la contemplaci\xf3n de la disoluci\xf3n, teniendo como objeto el agotamiento, la desaparici\xf3n, la ruptura y el cese de todas las formaciones, estas formaciones que se disuelven continuamente en todos los niveles de existencia, formas de nacimiento, destinos, estaciones de la conciencia y moradas de los seres, se le presentan como un gran terror, tal como le aparecer\xedan leones, tigres, leopardos, osos, hienas, esp\xedritus, demonios, toros salvajes, perros bravos, elefantes enfurecidos, serpientes venenosas, rayos, cementerios, campos de batalla o fosos de brasas ardientes a un hombre temeroso que desea vivir en paz. Al contemplar que \u2018las formaciones del pasado cesaron, las del presente est\xe1n cesando, y las formaciones que surgir\xe1n en el futuro igualmente cesar\xe1n\u2019, en ese punto surge en \xe9l lo que se llama el conocimiento de la aparici\xf3n como terror (bhayatupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na-\xf1\u0101\u1e47a)."}},{id:"vism-21.9",pali:"Tassa ta\u1e43 bhayatupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101sevantassa bh\u0101ventassa bahul\u012bkarontassa sabbabhavayonigati\u1e6dhitisatt\u0101v\u0101sesu neva t\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, na le\u1e47a\u1e43, na gati, nappa\u1e6disara\u1e47a\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101yati. Sabbabhavayonigati\u1e6dhitiniv\u0101sagatesu sa\u1e45kh\u0101resu ekasa\u1e45kh\u0101repi patthan\u0101 v\u0101 par\u0101m\u0101so v\u0101 na hoti. Tayo bhav\u0101 v\u012btaccika\u1e45g\u0101rapu\u1e47\u1e47aa\u1e45g\u0101rak\u0101suyo viya, catt\u0101ro mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101 ghoravisa\u0101s\u012bvis\u0101 viya, pa\xf1cakkhandh\u0101 ukkhitt\u0101sikavadhak\u0101 viya, cha ajjhattik\u0101yatan\u0101ni su\xf1\xf1ag\u0101mo viya, cha b\u0101hir\u0101yatan\u0101ni g\u0101magh\u0101takacor\u0101 viya, satta vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e6d\u1e6dhitiyo, nava ca satt\u0101v\u0101s\u0101 ek\u0101dasahi agg\u012bhi \u0101ditt\u0101 sampajjalit\u0101 sajotibh\u016bt\u0101 viya ca, sabbe sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 ga\u1e47\u1e0dabh\u016bt\u0101 rogabh\u016bt\u0101 sallabh\u016bt\u0101 aghabh\u016bt\u0101 \u0101b\u0101dhabh\u016bt\u0101 viya ca nirass\u0101d\u0101 niras\u0101 mah\u0101\u0101d\u012bnavar\u0101sibh\u016bt\u0101 hutv\u0101 upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhahanti.",translations:{en:"For one who resorts to, develops, and cultivates that knowledge of appearance as terror, no protection, shelter, refuge, or resort is discerned in any becoming, birth-place, destiny, station, or abode of beings. In regard to the formations found in any becoming, birth-place, destiny, station, or abode, there is not even in a single formation any longing or grasping. The three kinds of existence appear like a pit of glowing embers; the four great elements like terribly venomous serpents; the five aggregates like slayers with raised swords; the six internal sense bases like an empty village; the six external sense bases like village-plundering robbers; the seven stations of consciousness and the nine abodes of beings like what is ablaze, burning, and has become a mass of flames from the eleven fires; and all formations present themselves as being like a boil, a disease, a dart, a calamity, and an affliction, as being tasteless, sapless, a great mass of danger.",pt:"Para o iogue que cultiva, desenvolve e pratica repetidamente esse conhecimento da apari\xe7\xe3o como terror, em todas as exist\xeancias, modos de gera\xe7\xe3o, destinos, esta\xe7\xf5es da consci\xeancia e moradas dos seres, n\xe3o se manifesta nenhuma prote\xe7\xe3o, nenhum abrigo, nenhum ref\xfagio, nenhum ponto de apoio. Entre as forma\xe7\xf5es contidas em todas as exist\xeancias, modos de gera\xe7\xe3o, destinos, esta\xe7\xf5es e moradas, n\xe3o h\xe1 desejo nem apego err\xf4neo por sequer uma \xfanica forma\xe7\xe3o. Os tr\xeas reinos de exist\xeancia aparecem como fossas cheias de brasas sem chamas; os quatro grandes elementos, como serpentes venenosas terr\xedveis; os cinco agregados, como carrascos com espadas erguidas; as seis bases internas dos sentidos, como uma aldeia deserta; as seis bases externas dos sentidos, como bandidos que destroem uma aldeia; as sete esta\xe7\xf5es da consci\xeancia e as nove moradas dos seres aparecem como se estivessem acesas, em chamas e ardendo em um \xfanico inc\xeandio pelos onze fogos; e todas as forma\xe7\xf5es aparecem como tumores, como doen\xe7as, como flechas, como males, como afli\xe7\xf5es, desprovidas de satisfa\xe7\xe3o, sem ess\xeancia, apresentando-se como uma imensa massa de perigo.",es:"Para aquel que cultiva, desarrolla y practica frecuentemente ese conocimiento de la apariencia como terror, no percibe refugio, ni abrigo, ni destino, ni amparo en ning\xfan tipo de existencia, forma de nacimiento, destino, estaci\xf3n de la conciencia o morada de los seres. No surge ning\xfan deseo ni apego por ninguna formaci\xf3n, ni siquiera por una sola, entre las formaciones que pertenecen a todas las existencias, formas de nacimiento, destinos, estaciones y moradas. Los tres tipos de existencia aparecen como fosas de brasas llenas de carbones ardientes sin llamas; los cuatro grandes elementos, como serpientes venenosas y feroces; los cinco agregados, como verdugos con espadas desenvainadas; las seis esferas internas de los sentidos, como una aldea vac\xeda; las seis esferas externas de los sentidos, como bandidos que saquean la aldea; las siete estaciones de la conciencia y las nueve moradas de los seres aparecen como si estuvieran ardiendo, llameando y resplandeciendo por los once fuegos; y todas las formaciones aparecen como tumores, como enfermedades, como dardos, como calamidades, como dolencias, desprovistas de placer, sin esencia, como una gran masa de peligro."}},{id:"vism-21.10",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Sukhena j\u012bvituk\u0101massa bh\u012brukapurisassa rama\u1e47\u012by\u0101k\u0101rasa\u1e47\u1e6dhitampi sav\u0101\u1e37akamiva vanagahana\u1e43, sasadd\u016bl\u0101 viya guh\u0101, sag\u0101harakkhasa\u1e43 viya udaka\u1e43, samussitakhagg\u0101 viya paccatthik\u0101, savisa\u1e43 viya bhojana\u1e43, sacoro viya maggo, \u0101dittamiva ag\u0101ra\u1e43, uyyuttasen\u0101 viya ra\u1e47abh\u016bmi. Yath\u0101 hi so puriso et\u0101ni sav\u0101\u1e37akavanagahan\u0101d\u012bni \u0101gamma bh\u012bto sa\u1e43viggo lomaha\u1e6d\u1e6dhaj\u0101to samantato \u0101d\u012bnavameva passati, evamev\u0101ya\u1e43 yog\u0101vacaro bha\u1e45g\u0101nupassan\u0101vasena sabbasa\u1e45kh\u0101resu bhayato upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhitesu samantato nirasa\u1e43 nirass\u0101da\u1e43 \u0101d\u012bnavameva passati. Tasseva\u1e43 passato \u0101d\u012bnava\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u0101ma uppanna\u1e43 hoti. Ya\u1e43 sandh\u0101ya ida\u1e43 vutta\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"How so? For a timid person who desires to live in comfort, even a delightfully configured forest thicket is like one with beasts of prey; a cave is like one with tigers; a body of water is like one with a water-demon; enemies are like those with raised swords; food is like that mixed with poison; a road is like one with a robber; a house is like one on fire; a battlefield is like one with an army arrayed for battle. Just as that person, having come to that forest thicket with beasts of prey and so on, becomes frightened, agitated, with his hair standing on end, and sees only danger all around, just so this meditator, by means of contemplating dissolution, when all formations have appeared as terror, sees on all sides only what is sapless, tasteless, and dangerous. For one who sees thus, the knowledge of danger arises. It is with reference to this that it was said:",pt:"Como? Assim como para um homem temeroso que deseja viver em paz e felicidade, mesmo um lugar de apar\xeancia agrad\xe1vel parece uma floresta densa cheia de feras, uma caverna habitada por tigres, uma \xe1gua infestada de crocodilos e monstros aqu\xe1ticos, inimigos com espadas erguidas, comida envenenada, um caminho cheio de salteadores, uma casa em chamas ou um campo de batalha com um ex\xe9rcito pronto para o combate. Pois, assim como aquele homem, ao chegar a essa floresta cheia de feras e outros perigos, fica amedrontado, aterrorizado, com os cabelos arrepiados, e v\xea apenas perigo por todos os lados; da mesma forma, este praticante, por meio da contempla\xe7\xe3o da dissolu\xe7\xe3o (bha\u1e45g\u0101nupassan\u0101), quando todas as forma\xe7\xf5es se apresentam como terror, v\xea apenas o perigo por todos os lados, como algo sem ess\xeancia e sem satisfa\xe7\xe3o. Para ele, que assim v\xea, surge o chamado conhecimento do perigo (\u0101d\u012bnava\xf1\u0101\u1e47a). Referindo-se a isso, foi dito o seguinte no Pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101magga:",es:"\xbfDe qu\xe9 manera? As\xed como para un hombre temeroso que desea vivir felizmente, incluso un espeso bosque de apariencia encantadora le parece lleno de fieras, una cueva le parece tener tigres, el agua le parece tener cocodrilos y monstruos, los enemigos le parecen tener espadas levantadas, la comida le parece tener veneno, el camino le parece tener ladrones, la casa le parece estar en llamas y el campo de batalla le parece tener un ej\xe9rcito movilizado; y as\xed como ese hombre, al llegar a tales lugares, se siente asustado, aterrorizado y con los vellos de punta, viendo solo el peligro por todas partes; del mismo modo, este yogui, mediante la contemplaci\xf3n de la disoluci\xf3n, cuando todas las formaciones aparecen como terror\xedficas, ve por todas partes solo el peligro, falto de esencia y de placer. Para quien ve de esta manera, surge el llamado conocimiento del peligro. Refiri\xe9ndose a esto se ha dicho lo siguiente:"}},{id:"vism-21.11",pali:"So eva\u1e43 sabbasa\u1e45kh\u0101re \u0101d\u012bnavato passanto sabbabhavayonigativi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e6d\u1e6dhitisatt\u0101v\u0101sagate sabhedake sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragate nibbindati ukka\u1e47\u1e6dhati n\u0101bhiramati.",translations:{en:"Thus, seeing all formations as dangerous, he becomes disenchanted with, is wearied by, and does not delight in the entire conditioned realm, which is subject to breaking up\u2014in all kinds of existence, origins, destinies, stations of consciousness, and abodes of beings.",pt:"Ele, vendo assim todas as forma\xe7\xf5es como perigosas, torna-se desapegado, enfadado e n\xe3o encontra prazer em toda a massa de forma\xe7\xf5es sujeitas \xe0 dissolu\xe7\xe3o em todas as exist\xeancias, modos de gera\xe7\xe3o, destinos, esta\xe7\xf5es da consci\xeancia e moradas dos seres.",es:"Aquel yogi, al contemplar as\xed todas las formaciones como un peligro, se desencanta (nibbindati), se hast\xeda y no encuentra placer en toda la variedad de formaciones sujetas a la desintegraci\xf3n que se encuentran en las tres esferas de existencia, los cuatro tipos de nacimiento, los cinco destinos, las siete estaciones de la conciencia y las nueve moradas de los seres."}},{id:"vism-21.12",pali:"Imin\u0101 pana nibbid\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena imassa kulaputtassa nibbindantassa ukka\u1e47\u1e6dhantassa anabhiramantassa sabbabhavayonigativi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e6d\u1e6dhitisatt\u0101v\u0101sagatesu sabhedakesu sa\u1e45kh\u0101resu ekasa\u1e45kh\u0101repi citta\u1e43 na sajjati, na laggati, na bajjhati, sabbasm\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragat\u0101 muccituk\u0101ma\u1e43 nissarituk\u0101ma\u1e43 hoti. Yath\u0101 ki\u1e43? Yath\u0101 n\u0101ma j\u0101labbhantaragato maccho, sappamukhagato ma\u1e47\u1e0d\u016bko, pa\xf1jarapakkhitto vanakukku\u1e6do, da\u1e37hap\u0101savasagato migo, ahitu\u1e47\u1e0dikahatthagato sappo, mah\u0101pa\u1e45kapakkhando ku\xf1jaro, supa\u1e47\u1e47amukhagato n\u0101gar\u0101j\u0101, r\u0101humukhappavi\u1e6d\u1e6dho cando, sapattapariv\u0101rito purisoti evam\u0101dayo tato tato muccituk\u0101m\u0101 nissarituk\u0101m\u0101va honti, eva\u1e43 tassa yogino citta\u1e43 sabbasm\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragat\u0101 muccituk\u0101ma\u1e43 nissarituk\u0101ma\u1e43 hoti. Athassa eva\u1e43 sabbasa\u1e45kh\u0101resu vigat\u0101layassa sabbasm\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragat\u0101 muccituk\u0101massa uppajjati mu\xf1citukamyat\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47anti.",translations:{en:"Now, through this knowledge of disenchantment, the mind of this clansman\u2014who is becoming disenchanted, wearied, and finds no delight\u2014does not cling to, adhere to, or get bound by even a single formation among all the formations subject to breaking up, in all kinds of existence, origins, destinies, stations of consciousness, and abodes of beings. His mind desires to be delivered and to escape from the entire conditioned realm. How so? Just as a fish that has gotten into a net, a frog in a snake\u2019s mouth, a wild fowl put in a cage, a deer caught in a strong snare, a snake in a snake-charmer\u2019s hand, an elephant that has plunged into a great mire, a N\u0101ga king in a supa\u1e47\u1e47a\u2019s mouth, the moon that has entered R\u0101hu\u2019s mouth, or a man surrounded by his enemies\u2014just as these all desire to be delivered and to escape from their respective situations, so the yogi\u2019s mind desires to be delivered and to escape from the entire conditioned realm. Then, for one who is thus without attachment to all formations and who desires deliverance from the entire conditioned realm, there arises the knowledge of the wish for deliverance.",pt:"Atrav\xe9s deste conhecimento do desapego, a mente deste nobre praticante, que se sente desapegado, enfadado e sem prazer, n\xe3o se apega, n\xe3o se prende e n\xe3o se amarra a sequer uma \xfanica forma\xe7\xe3o entre as forma\xe7\xf5es sujeitas \xe0 dissolu\xe7\xe3o em todas as exist\xeancias, modos de gera\xe7\xe3o, destinos, esta\xe7\xf5es da consci\xeancia e moradas dos seres. Ele deseja libertar-se e escapar de toda a massa de forma\xe7\xf5es. Como o qu\xea? Assim como um peixe preso em uma rede, um sapo na boca de uma cobra, um galo selvagem em uma gaiola, um cervo preso em uma armadilha forte, uma cobra nas m\xe3os de um encantador de serpentes, um elefante atolado em um grande p\xe2ntano, um rei naga na boca de um garuda, a lua na boca de Rahu ou um homem cercado por inimigos \u2014 todos estes desejam libertar-se e escapar de suas respectivas amarras e perigos \u2014, da mesma forma, a mente daquele iogue deseja libertar-se e escapar de toda a massa de forma\xe7\xf5es. Ent\xe3o, para aquele iogue que est\xe1 livre de apego a todas as forma\xe7\xf5es e deseja libertar-se de toda a massa de forma\xe7\xf5es, surge o conhecimento do desejo de liberta\xe7\xe3o (mu\xf1citukamyat\u0101-\xf1\u0101\u1e47a).",es:"A trav\xe9s de este conocimiento del desencanto, la mente de este noble disc\xedpulo, que siente hast\xedo, aburrimiento y falta de placer, no se apega, no se adhiere ni se encadena a ninguna formaci\xf3n de entre todas las que existen en los tres tipos de existencia, las cuatro formas de nacimiento, los cinco destinos, las siete estaciones de la conciencia y las nueve moradas de los seres, las cuales est\xe1n sujetas a la desintegraci\xf3n; por el contrario, desea liberarse y escapar de todo tipo de formaciones. \xbfC\xf3mo qu\xe9? As\xed como un pez atrapado en una red, una rana en la boca de una serpiente, un gallo de bosque en una jaula, un ciervo en un lazo firme, una serpiente en las manos de un encantador, un elefante hundido en un gran pantano, el rey de los nagas en la boca de un garuda, la luna en la boca de Rahu o un hombre rodeado de enemigos desean ardientemente liberarse y escapar de sus respectivos peligros; de igual modo, la mente de ese yogui desea liberarse y escapar de todas las formaciones. Entonces, en ese yogui que ha perdido el apego por todas las formaciones y desea liberarse de ellas, surge el conocimiento del deseo de liberaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-21.13",pali:"So eva\u1e43 sabbabhavayonigati\u1e6d\u1e6dhitiniv\u0101sagatehi sabhedakehi sa\u1e45kh\u0101rehi muccituk\u0101mo sabbasm\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragat\u0101 muccitu\u1e43 puna te eva\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101re pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101nupassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena tilakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101ropetv\u0101 parigga\u1e47h\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Thus, wishing to be delivered from formations that are subject to breaking up\u2014in all kinds of existence, origins, destinies, stations, and abodes\u2014in order to be delivered from the entire conditioned realm, he again comprehends those same formations by means of the knowledge of contemplation by reflection, applying the three characteristics to them.",pt:"Ele, desejando assim libertar-se das forma\xe7\xf5es sujeitas \xe0 dissolu\xe7\xe3o em todas as exist\xeancias, modos de gera\xe7\xe3o, destinos, esta\xe7\xf5es e moradas, a fim de se libertar de toda a massa de forma\xe7\xf5es, examina novamente essas mesmas forma\xe7\xf5es aplicando as tr\xeas caracter\xedsticas por meio do conhecimento da contempla\xe7\xe3o da reobserva\xe7\xe3o (pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101nupassan\u0101-\xf1\u0101\u1e47a).",es:"Deseando liberarse de todas las formaciones presentes en los diversos estados de existencia, nacimientos y destinos, para poder escapar de ellas, vuelve a examinar esas mismas formaciones aplicando las tres caracter\xedsticas mediante el conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n de la reobservaci\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-21.14",pali:"So sabbasa\u1e45kh\u0101re anaccantikato, t\u0101vak\u0101likato, upp\u0101davayaparicchinnato, palokato, calato, pabha\u1e45guto, addhuvato, vipari\u1e47\u0101madhammato, ass\u0101rakato, vibhavato, sa\u1e45khatato, mara\u1e47adhammatoti\u0101d\u012bhi k\u0101ra\u1e47ehi anicc\u0101 ti passati.",translations:{en:"He sees all formations as impermanent for such reasons as: because they are not lasting, because they are temporary, because they are limited by arising and passing away, because they are perishable, because they are trembling, because they are breaking up, because they are unstable, because they are subject to change, because they are essenceless, because they are subject to destruction, because they are conditioned, and because they are subject to death.",pt:"Assim, o iogue v\xea todas as forma\xe7\xf5es como impermanentes por raz\xf5es tais como: por n\xe3o serem eternas, por serem tempor\xe1rias, por serem limitadas pelo surgimento e desaparecimento, por serem propensas \xe0 desintegra\xe7\xe3o, por serem inst\xe1veis, por serem perec\xedveis, por n\xe3o serem duradouras, por estarem sujeitas \xe0 mudan\xe7a, por serem desprovidas de ess\xeancia, por serem desprovidas de solidez, por serem condicionadas e por estarem sujeitas \xe0 morte.",es:"\xc9l ve todas las formaciones como impermanentes por las siguientes razones: porque no son eternas, son temporales, est\xe1n limitadas por el surgimiento y la desaparici\xf3n, son perecederas, inestables, quebradizas, no duraderas, est\xe1n sujetas al cambio, carecen de esencia, tienden a la desaparici\xf3n, son condicionadas y est\xe1n sujetas a la muerte."}},{id:"vism-21.15",pali:"So eva\u1e43 pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101nupassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena \u2018\u2018sabbe sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 su\xf1\xf1\u0101\u2019\u2019ti pariggahetv\u0101 puna \u2018\u2018su\xf1\xf1amida\u1e43 attena v\u0101 attaniyena v\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (ma. ni. 3.69) dviko\u1e6dika\u1e43 su\xf1\xf1ata\u1e43 parigga\u1e47h\u0101ti. So eva\u1e43 neva att\u0101na\u1e43, na para\u1e43 ki\xf1ci attano parikkh\u0101rabh\u0101ve \u1e6dhita\u1e43 disv\u0101 puna \u2018\u2018n\u0101ha\u1e43 kvacani, kassaci ki\xf1canatasmi\u1e43, na ca mama kvacani, kismi\xf1ci ki\xf1canatatth\u012b\u2019\u2019ti y\u0101 ettha catuko\u1e6dik\u0101 su\xf1\xf1at\u0101 kathit\u0101, ta\u1e43 parigga\u1e47h\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Having thus grasped with the knowledge of contemplation by reflection that 'all formations are empty,' he further grasps the twofold emptiness: 'This is empty of self or of what belongs to self.' Seeing that neither a self nor anything other exists as a possession of his, he then grasps the fourfold emptiness stated here: 'I am not anywhere, nor am I anyone's possession in any way; and there is nothing of mine anywhere, nor is there for me any possession in anything.'",pt:"Tendo assim compreendido, por meio do conhecimento da contempla\xe7\xe3o reflexiva, que 'todas as forma\xe7\xf5es s\xe3o vazias', ele compreende novamente a vacuidade em dois aspectos: 'Isto \xe9 vazio de um eu ou de qualquer coisa pertencente a um eu'. N\xe3o vendo assim nem a si mesmo como um eu, nem qualquer outra pessoa ou coisa como pertencente a si mesmo, ele compreende novamente a vacuidade em quatro aspectos, conforme ensinado aqui: 'Eu n\xe3o sou em lugar algum, de ningu\xe9m, em qualquer propriedade; nem h\xe1 em lugar algum, em qualquer coisa, qualquer propriedade minha'.",es:"Habiendo comprendido as\xed mediante el conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n reflexiva que \u2018todas las formaciones son vac\xedas\u2019, el yogui comprende de nuevo la vacuidad de dos aspectos: \u2018Esto est\xe1 vac\xedo de un yo o de algo perteneciente a un yo\u2019. Al no ver as\xed un yo ni nada perteneciente a otro que se sit\xfae como propiedad propia, comprende de nuevo la vacuidad de cuatro aspectos que se menciona aqu\xed: \u2018Yo no soy nada en ning\xfan lugar para nadie, ni nada m\xedo es algo en ning\xfan lugar para nadie\u2019."}},{id:"vism-21.16",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Aya\xf1hi n\u0101ha\u1e43 kvacan\u012b ti kvaci att\u0101na\u1e43 na passati. Kassaci ki\xf1canatasmi nti attano att\u0101na\u1e43 kassaci parassa ki\xf1canabh\u0101ve upanetabba\u1e43 na passati. Bh\u0101ti\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nev\u0101 bh\u0101tara\u1e43, sah\u0101ya\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne v\u0101 sah\u0101ya\u1e43, parikkh\u0101ra\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne v\u0101 parikkh\u0101ra\u1e43 ma\xf1\xf1itv\u0101 upanetabba\u1e43 na passat\u012bti attho. Na ca mama kvacan\u012b ti ettha mama-sadda\u1e43 t\u0101va \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 na ca kvacan\u012b ti parassa ca att\u0101na\u1e43 kvaci napassat\u012bti ayamattho. Id\u0101ni mama-sadda\u1e43 \u0101haritv\u0101 mama kismi\xf1ci ki\xf1canatatth\u012b ti so parassa att\u0101 mama kismi\xf1ci ki\xf1canabh\u0101ve atth\u012bti na passat\u012bti. Attano bh\u0101ti\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne v\u0101 bh\u0101tara\u1e43, sah\u0101ya\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne v\u0101 sah\u0101ya\u1e43 parikkh\u0101ra\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne v\u0101 parikkh\u0101ranti kismi\xf1ci \u1e6dh\u0101ne parassa att\u0101na\u1e43 imin\u0101 ki\xf1canabh\u0101vena upanetabba\u1e43 na passat\u012bti attho. Evamaya\u1e43 yasm\u0101 neva katthaci att\u0101na\u1e43 passati, na ta\u1e43 parassa ki\xf1canabh\u0101ve upanetabba\u1e43 passati, na parassa att\u0101na\u1e43 passati, na parassa att\u0101na\u1e43 attano ki\xf1canabh\u0101ve upanetabba\u1e43 passati. Tasm\u0101nena catuko\u1e6dik\u0101 su\xf1\xf1at\u0101 pariggahit\u0101 hot\u012bti.",translations:{en:"How? 'I am not anywhere' means he does not see a self anywhere. 'Nor am I anyone's possession in any way' means he does not see his own self as something to be brought into a state of possession for any other person. That is, he does not see it as something to be brought over, thinking of it as a brother in the place of a brother, a friend in the place of a friend, or a possession in the place of a possession. As for 'and there is nothing of mine anywhere, nor is there for me any possession in anything,' here, setting aside the word 'mine' for a moment, 'and not anywhere' means he does not see another\u2019s self anywhere. Now, bringing in the word 'mine,' 'nor is there for me any possession in anything' means he does not see that another's self exists for him in any state of possession. That is, he does not see another\u2019s self as something to be brought into a state of possession for himself, such as a brother in the place of a brother, a friend in the place of a friend, or a possession in the place of a possession. Thus, because he neither sees a self anywhere, nor sees that self as something to be brought into a state of possession for another, nor sees another\u2019s self, nor sees another\u2019s self as something to be brought into a state of possession for himself, therefore this fourfold emptiness is grasped by him.",pt:"Como? 'Eu n\xe3o sou em lugar algum' significa que ele n\xe3o v\xea um eu em lugar nenhum. 'De ningu\xe9m, em qualquer propriedade' significa que ele n\xe3o v\xea o seu pr\xf3prio eu como algo a ser associado \xe0 propriedade de outrem, ou seja, ele n\xe3o v\xea a si mesmo como um irm\xe3o na posi\xe7\xe3o de irm\xe3o, como um amigo na posi\xe7\xe3o de amigo, ou como um pertence na posi\xe7\xe3o de pertence. 'Nem h\xe1 em lugar algum' \u2014 aqui, deixando de lado a palavra 'minha' por um momento, 'nem h\xe1 em lugar algum' significa que ele n\xe3o v\xea o eu de outrem em lugar nenhum. Agora, trazendo de volta a palavra 'minha', 'qualquer propriedade minha' significa que ele n\xe3o v\xea o eu de outrem como existindo em qualquer propriedade sua, ou seja, ele n\xe3o v\xea o eu de outrem como algo a ser associado \xe0 sua pr\xf3pria propriedade na posi\xe7\xe3o de irm\xe3o, amigo ou pertence em lugar algum. Assim, como ele n\xe3o v\xea um eu em lugar nenhum, nem o v\xea como algo a ser associado \xe0 propriedade de outrem, nem v\xea o eu de outrem, nem v\xea o eu de outrem como algo a ser associado \xe0 sua pr\xf3pria propriedade, diz-se que ele compreendeu a vacuidade em quatro aspectos.",es:"\xbfC\xf3mo? \u2018Yo no soy nada en ning\xfan lugar\u2019 significa que no ve un yo en ning\xfan lugar. \u2018Para nadie\u2019 significa que no ve un yo propio que deba ser atribuido a la condici\xf3n de propiedad de otro; el significado es que no lo ve como alguien que deba ser considerado en el lugar de un hermano, pensando: \u2018es un hermano\u2019, o en el lugar de un amigo, o en el lugar de un objeto. \u2018Ni nada m\xedo es algo en ning\xfan lugar\u2019: aqu\xed, dejando de lado por un momento la palabra \u2018m\xedo\u2019, \u2018nada en ning\xfan lugar\u2019 significa que no ve el yo de otro en ning\xfan lugar. Ahora, trayendo la palabra \u2018m\xedo\u2019, \u2018nada m\xedo es algo\u2019 significa que no ve que ese yo de otro exista como alguna propiedad suya; el significado es que no ve que el yo de otro deba ser atribuido a esta condici\xf3n de propiedad propia en ning\xfan lugar, ya sea como hermano en el lugar de su propio hermano, o como amigo o como objeto. De este modo, dado que no ve un yo en ninguna parte, ni ve que este deba ser atribuido como propiedad de otro, ni ve el yo de otro, ni ve que el yo de otro deba ser atribuido como propiedad suya, se dice que ha comprendido la vacuidad de cuatro aspectos."}},{id:"vism-21.17",pali:"Tassa ta\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101sevantassa bh\u0101ventassa bahul\u012bkarontassa adhimokkhasaddh\u0101 balavatar\u0101 nibbattati, v\u012briya\u1e43 supaggahita\u1e43 hoti, sati s\u016bpa\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101, citta\u1e43 susam\u0101hita\u1e43, tikkhatar\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101 uppajjati. Tassa \u2018\u2018d\u0101ni maggo uppajjissat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101re anicc\u0101ti v\u0101 dukkh\u0101ti v\u0101 anatt\u0101ti v\u0101 sammasitv\u0101 bhava\u1e45ga\u1e43 otarati. Bhava\u1e45g\u0101nantara\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101ya katanayeneva sa\u1e45kh\u0101re anicc\u0101ti v\u0101 dukkh\u0101ti v\u0101 anatt\u0101ti v\u0101 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 kurum\u0101na\u1e43 uppajjati manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana\u1e43. Tato bhava\u1e45ga\u1e43 \u0101va\u1e6d\u1e6detv\u0101 uppannassa tassa kiriyacittass\u0101nantara\u1e43 av\u012bcika\u1e43 cittasantati\u1e43 anuppabandham\u0101na\u1e43 tatheva sa\u1e45kh\u0101re \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 uppajjati pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 javanacitta\u1e43, ya\u1e43 parikamma nti vuccati. Tadanantara\u1e43 tatheva sa\u1e45kh\u0101re \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 uppajjati dutiya\u1e43 javanacitta\u1e43, ya\u1e43 upac\u0101ra nti vuccati. Tadanantarampi tatheva sa\u1e45kh\u0101re \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 uppajjati tatiya\u1e43 javanacitta\u1e43, ya\u1e43 anuloma nti vuccati. Ida\u1e43 nesa\u1e43 p\u0101\u1e6diyekka\u1e43 n\u0101ma\u1e43.",translations:{en:"For one who frequents, develops, and cultivates that knowledge of equanimity towards formations, resolute faith becomes stronger, energy is well exerted, mindfulness is well established, the mind is well concentrated, and a sharper equanimity towards formations arises. For him, at the moment when it can be said, 'Now the path will arise,' equanimity towards formations, after contemplating formations as impermanent, or as suffering, or as not-self, descends into the life-continuum. Immediately after the life-continuum, mind-door adverting arises, taking as its object the formations as impermanent, or as suffering, or as not-self, in the very same way that equanimity towards formations did. Then, immediately after that functional consciousness which arose turning from the life-continuum, continuing the mental continuum without interruption, the first impulsion-consciousness arises, having taken formations as its object in the very same way; this is called 'preparation.' Immediately after that, the second impulsion-consciousness arises, having taken formations as its object in the very same way; this is called 'access.' Immediately after that, too, the third impulsion-consciousness arises, having taken formations as its object in the very same way; this is called 'conformity.' These are their respective names.",pt:"Para aquele que cultiva, desenvolve e pratica repetidamente esse conhecimento de equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es, surge uma f\xe9 de convic\xe7\xe3o (adhimokkhasaddh\u0101) ainda mais forte, a energia (v\u012briya) torna-se bem sustentada, a aten\xe7\xe3o plena (sati) fica bem estabelecida, a mente (citta) torna-se bem concentrada, e surge uma equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es (sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101) extremamente afiada. No momento em que se pode dizer 'agora o caminho surgir\xe1', essa equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es, tendo investigado as forma\xe7\xf5es como impermanentes, dolorosas ou como n\xe3o-eu, desce ao fluxo do shava\u1e45ga (bhava\u1e45ga). Imediatamente ap\xf3s o bhava\u1e45ga, surge o an\xfancio pela porta da mente (manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana), tomando como objeto as forma\xe7\xf5es como impermanentes, dolorosas ou como n\xe3o-eu, exatamente pelo mesmo m\xe9todo empregado pela equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es. Depois disso, imediatamente ap\xf3s esse momento de consci\xeancia funcional (kiriyacitta) que surge tendo interrompido o bhava\u1e45ga, dando continuidade a uma corrente mental ininterrupta, surge o primeiro momento de consci\xeancia impulsiva (javana), tomando as forma\xe7\xf5es como objeto da mesma maneira, o qual \xe9 chamado de 'preparat\xf3rio' (parikamma). Imediatamente ap\xf3s este, tomando as forma\xe7\xf5es como objeto da mesma maneira, surge o segundo momento de consci\xeancia impulsiva, o qual \xe9 chamado de 'acesso' (upac\u0101ra). E imediatamente ap\xf3s este tamb\xe9m, tomando as forma\xe7\xf5es como objeto da mesma maneira, surge o terceiro momento de consci\xeancia impulsiva, o qual \xe9 chamado de 'conformidade' (anuloma). Estes s\xe3o os seus nomes individuais.",es:"Para aquel que cultiva, desarrolla y practica frecuentemente ese conocimiento de ecuanimidad respecto a las formaciones, la fe basada en la convicci\xf3n (adhimokkha-saddh\u0101) se vuelve m\xe1s poderosa, la energ\xeda est\xe1 bien aplicada, la atenci\xf3n est\xe1 bien establecida, la mente est\xe1 bien concentrada y surge una ecuanimidad respecto a las formaciones m\xe1s aguda. En el momento en que piensa: 'Ahora surgir\xe1 el camino', habiendo examinado las formaciones como impermanentes, o como sufrimiento, o como no-yo, la ecuanimidad respecto a las formaciones desciende al flujo del ser (bhava\u1e45ga). Inmediatamente despu\xe9s del bhava\u1e45ga, surge el anuncio en la puerta de la mente (manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana), tomando como objeto las formaciones como impermanentes, o como sufrimiento, o como no-yo, precisamente mediante el mismo m\xe9todo empleado por la ecuanimidad respecto a las formaciones. Luego, tras haber interrumpido el bhava\u1e45ga, inmediatamente despu\xe9s de esa conciencia funcional, surge el primer momento de impulsi\xf3n (javana), continuando la serie mental sin interrupci\xf3n y tomando como objeto las formaciones de la misma manera; a este se le llama 'preparaci\xf3n' (parikamma). Inmediatamente despu\xe9s de este, surge el segundo momento de impulsi\xf3n, tomando como objeto las formaciones de la misma manera; a este se le llama 'acceso' (upac\u0101ra). E inmediatamente despu\xe9s de este, surge el tercer momento de impulsi\xf3n, tomando como objeto las formaciones de la misma manera; a este se le llama 'conformidad' (anuloma). Estos son sus nombres individuales."}},{id:"vism-21.18",pali:"Ida\xf1ca pana anuloma\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ya vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nag\u0101miniy\u0101 vipassan\u0101ya pariyos\u0101na\u1e43 hoti. Sabbena sabba\u1e43 pana gotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nag\u0101miniy\u0101 vipassan\u0101ya pariyos\u0101na\u1e43. Id\u0101ni tass\u0101yeva vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nag\u0101miniy\u0101 vipassan\u0101ya asammohattha\u1e43 aya\u1e43 suttasa\u1e43sandan\u0101 veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"Now, this conformity knowledge is the culmination of the insight leading to emergence that has formations as its object. But it is change-of-lineage knowledge that is in every way the culmination of the insight leading to emergence. Now, for the sake of non-bewilderment regarding this same insight leading to emergence, this correlation with the Suttas should be understood.",pt:"Este conhecimento de conformidade \xe9 o \xe1pice da vipassana que conduz \xe0 emerg\xeancia e que tem as forma\xe7\xf5es como objeto. No entanto, em termos absolutos, o conhecimento de mudan\xe7a de linhagem (gotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) \xe9 o \xe1pice final da vipassana que conduz \xe0 emerg\xeancia. Agora, para evitar confus\xe3o a respeito dessa mesma vipassana que conduz \xe0 emerg\xeancia, deve-se compreender esta concord\xe2ncia com os Suttas.",es:"Este conocimiento de conformidad es el final de la vipassan\u0101 que conduce al surgimiento y que tiene a las formaciones como objeto. Pero en t\xe9rminos absolutos, el conocimiento de cambio de linaje (gotrabh\u016b\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) es el final de la vipassan\u0101 que conduce al surgimiento. Ahora, para evitar la confusi\xf3n respecto a esa misma vipassan\u0101 que conduce al surgimiento, debe conocerse esta correlaci\xf3n con los Suttas."}},{id:"vism-21.19",pali:"Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne \u2018\u2018anuloma\u1e43 gotrabhussa, anuloma\u1e43 vod\u0101nass\u0101\u2019\u2019 ti (pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101. 1.1.417) eva\u1e43 t\u012bhi n\u0101mehi vutt\u0101.",translations:{en:"In the Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na, it is said: \u201cConformity is a condition for change-of-lineage; conformity is a condition for purification\u201d (Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh I 7). Thus it is spoken of by three names.",pt:"No Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na, ela \xe9 referida por tr\xeas nomes, onde se diz: 'A conformidade \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mudan\xe7a de linhagem, a conformidade \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a purifica\xe7\xe3o'.",es:"En el Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na se dice: 'La conformidad es para el cambio de linaje; la conformidad es para la purificaci\xf3n' (Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101. I, 1, 417). De este modo, se ense\xf1a bajo estos tres nombres."}},{id:"vism-21.20",pali:"Itinekehi n\u0101mehi, kittit\u0101 y\u0101 mahesin\u0101; Vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nag\u0101min\u012b sant\u0101, parisuddh\u0101 vipassan\u0101.",translations:{en:"Thus by many a name has been extolled by the Great Sage that insight leading to emergence which is peaceful and utterly pure.",pt:"Assim, por muitos nomes \xe9 louvada pelo Grande S\xe1bio esta vipassana pac\xedfica e pur\xedssima que conduz \xe0 emerg\xeancia.",es:"As\xed, con diversos nombres, ha sido elogiada por el Gran Sabio aquella visi\xf3n cabal (vipassan\u0101) pura y serena que conduce al surgimiento (vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nag\u0101min\u012b)."}}]},439,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,n,i,s,t){i.exports=[{id:"vism-22.1",pali:"Ito para\u1e43 gotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti, ta\u1e43 maggassa \u0101vajjana\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101niyatt\u0101 neva pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi\u1e43 na \xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi\u1e43 bhajati, antar\u0101 abboh\u0101rikameva hoti. Vipassan\u0101sote patitatt\u0101 pana vipassan\u0101ti sa\u1e45kha\u1e43 gacchati. Sot\u0101pattimaggo sakad\u0101g\u0101mimaggo an\u0101g\u0101mimaggo arahattamaggoti imesu pana cat\u016bsu maggesu \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"After this, change-of-lineage knowledge arises. Since it is in the position of adverting to the path, it partakes of neither the purification of knowledge and vision of the way of practice nor the purification by knowledge and vision; it is simply unclassifiable in between. But since it has fallen into the stream of insight, it is reckoned as insight. However, the knowledge in these four paths\u2014the path of stream-entry, the path of once-return, the path of non-return, and the path of arahantship\u2014is called the purification by knowledge and vision.",pt:"Depois disso, ocorre o conhecimento de mudan\xe7a de linhagem (gotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47a). Como ele ocupa a posi\xe7\xe3o de an\xfancio (\u0101vajjana) para o caminho, n\xe3o pertence nem \xe0 pureza do conhecimento e vis\xe3o do caminho, nem \xe0 pureza do conhecimento e vis\xe3o, permanecendo entre ambas sem uma designa\xe7\xe3o espec\xedfica. No entanto, por ter ca\xeddo no fluxo da vipassana, ele \xe9 classificado como vipassana. O conhecimento nos quatro caminhos \u2014 a saber, o caminho da entrada na corrente (sot\u0101pattimagga), o caminho do retorno \xfanico (sakad\u0101g\u0101mimagga), o caminho do n\xe3o-retorno (an\u0101g\u0101mimagga) e o caminho do arahantado (arahattamagga) \u2014 \xe9 chamado de pureza do conhecimento e vis\xe3o (\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi).",es:"Despu\xe9s de esto surge el conocimiento de cambio de linaje (gotrabh\u016b\xf1\u0101\u1e47a). Debido a que ocupa el lugar de la advertencia (\u0101vajjana) para el camino, no se clasifica dentro de la purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n de la v\xeda ni dentro de la purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n; permanece entre ambas como un conocimiento que no puede ser designado formalmente. Sin embargo, al haber ca\xeddo en la corriente de la visi\xf3n cabal, se cuenta como tal. Pero en los cuatro caminos, a saber: el camino de la entrada en la corriente, el camino del que retorna una sola vez, el camino del que no retorna y el camino de la santidad (arahantado), el conocimiento se denomina purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n."}},{id:"vism-22.2",pali:"Tattha pa\u1e6dhamamagga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 t\u0101va samp\u0101detuk\u0101mena a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 ki\xf1ci k\u0101tabba\u1e43 n\u0101ma natthi. Ya\xf1hi anena k\u0101tabba\u1e43 siy\u0101, ta\u1e43 anulom\u0101vas\u0101na\u1e43 vipassana\u1e43 upp\u0101dentena katameva. Eva\u1e43 uppannaanuloma\xf1\u0101\u1e47assa panassa tehi t\u012bhipi anuloma\xf1\u0101\u1e47ehi attano bal\u0101nur\u016bpena th\u016blath\u016ble saccapa\u1e6dicch\u0101dake tamamhi antaradh\u0101pite sabbasa\u1e45kh\u0101ragatesu citta\u1e43 na pakkhandati, na santi\u1e6d\u1e6dhati, n\u0101dhimuccati, na sajjati, na laggati, na bajjhati. Padumapal\u0101sato udaka\u1e43 viya patil\u012byati patiku\u1e6dati pativattati. Sabba\u1e43 nimitt\u0101ramma\u1e47ampi sabba\u1e43 pavatt\u0101ramma\u1e47ampi palibodhato upa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti. Athassa sabbasmi\u1e43 nimittapavatt\u0101ramma\u1e47e palibodhato upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhite anuloma\xf1\u0101\u1e47assa \u0101sevanante animitta\u1e43 appavatta\u1e43 visa\u1e45kh\u0101ra\u1e43 nirodha\u1e43 nibb\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 kurum\u0101na\u1e43 puthujjanagotta\u1e43 puthujjanasa\u1e45kha\u1e43 puthujjanabh\u016bmi\u1e43 atikkamam\u0101na\u1e43 ariyagotta\u1e43 ariyasa\u1e45kha\u1e43 ariyabh\u016bmi\u1e43 okkamam\u0101na\u1e43 nibb\u0101n\u0101ramma\u1e47e pa\u1e6dham\u0101va\u1e6d\u1e6danapa\u1e6dham\u0101bhogapa\u1e6dhamasamann\u0101h\u0101rabh\u016bta\u1e43 maggassa anantarasamanantar\u0101sevanaupanissayanatthivigatavasena chahi \u0101k\u0101rehi paccayabh\u0101va\u1e43 s\u0101dhayam\u0101na\u1e43 sikh\u0101ppatta\u1e43 vipassan\u0101ya muddhabh\u016bta\u1e43 apunar\u0101va\u1e6d\u1e6daka\u1e43 uppajjati gotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Herein, for one who wishes to accomplish the knowledge of the first path, there is nothing further to be done. For whatever needed to be done by him has been done by producing the insight that culminates in conformity. For one for whom conformity knowledge has thus arisen, when the grosser and grosser darkness that conceals the truths has been made to disappear by those three conformity knowledges according to their strength, his mind does not plunge into, settle upon, become resolved upon, cling to, adhere to, or become bound by any formations. Like water on a lotus leaf, it recoils, shrinks back, and turns away. All sign-objects and all objects of occurrence appear as an obstruction. Then, when all sign-objects and objects of occurrence appear to him as an obstruction, at the end of the repetition of conformity knowledge, there arises the change-of-lineage knowledge, which makes the signless, non-occurrence, the unconditioned, cessation, Nibb\u0101na, its object; which transcends the lineage, designation, and plane of the ordinary person, and enters the lineage, designation, and plane of the noble ones; which is the first turning, first adverting, first attending to the object of Nibb\u0101na; which establishes its conditionality for the path in six ways\u2014by way of contiguity, immediate contiguity, repetition, decisive support, absence, and disappearance; which has reached the summit, is the crown of insight, and is non-reverting.",pt:"Para aquele que deseja realizar o conhecimento do primeiro caminho, n\xe3o h\xe1 mais nada a ser feito. Pois tudo o que deveria ser feito por ele j\xe1 foi realizado ao fazer surgir a vipassana que culmina no conhecimento de conformidade. Quando o conhecimento de conformidade surge dessa maneira, e a escurid\xe3o grosseira que encobre as verdades \xe9 dissipada por esses tr\xeas momentos de conformidade de acordo com a sua pr\xf3pria for\xe7a, a mente n\xe3o se lan\xe7a em dire\xe7\xe3o a nenhuma das forma\xe7\xf5es, n\xe3o se estabelece nelas, n\xe3o se resolve nelas, n\xe3o se apega, n\xe3o se prende e n\xe3o se vincula a elas. Ela recua, retrai-se e desvia-se delas, assim como a \xe1gua em uma folha de l\xf3tus. Todo objeto que possui sinal (nimitta) e todo objeto que possui continuidade (pavatta) se apresentam como um obst\xe1culo (palibodha). Ent\xe3o, quando todo objeto com sinal e continuidade se apresenta a ele como um obst\xe1culo, ao final da repeti\xe7\xe3o do conhecimento de conformidade, surge o conhecimento de mudan\xe7a de linhagem (gotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47a). Este conhecimento toma como objeto o Nibb\u0101na \u2014 que \xe9 sem sinal (animitta), sem continuidade (appavatta), n\xe3o-formado (visa\u1e45kh\u0101ra) e que \xe9 a cessa\xe7\xe3o (nirodha) \u2014, transcendendo a linhagem de pessoa comum (puthujjanagotta), a designa\xe7\xe3o de pessoa comum e o plano de pessoa comum, e ingressando na linhagem dos nobres (ariyagotta), na designa\xe7\xe3o dos nobres e no plano dos nobres. Ele constitui a primeira volta, o primeiro an\xfancio e a primeira aten\xe7\xe3o voltada ao Nibb\u0101na como objeto, atuando como condi\xe7\xe3o para o caminho de seis maneiras \u2014 a saber, por meio das condi\xe7\xf5es de proximidade (anantara), contiguidade (samanantara), repeti\xe7\xe3o (\u0101sevana), forte apoio (upanissaya), aus\xeancia (natthi) e desaparecimento (vigata) \u2014, alcan\xe7ando o \xe1pice, sendo o topo da vipassana e n\xe3o retornando jamais.",es:"En este punto, para el meditador que desea alcanzar el conocimiento del primer camino, no queda ninguna otra tarea por realizar. Pues lo que deb\xeda hacerse ya ha sido cumplido al generar la visi\xf3n cabal que culmina en el conocimiento de conformidad. Habiendo surgido este conocimiento de conformidad, mediante estos tres tipos de conformidad, seg\xfan su propia fuerza, se disipa la densa oscuridad de las impurezas que ocultan las verdades. Entonces, su mente ya no se lanza hacia todas las formaciones, no se establece en ellas, no se decide por ellas, no se apega, no se vincula ni se encadena a ellas. Se retira, se encoge y retrocede, como el agua de una hoja de loto. Toda percepci\xf3n de signos y toda percepci\xf3n de la continuidad de las formaciones se le presenta como un obst\xe1culo. Entonces, cuando toda percepci\xf3n de signos y de continuidad se le presenta como un obst\xe1culo, al final de la pr\xe1ctica repetida del conocimiento de conformidad, surge el conocimiento de cambio de linaje (gotrabh\u016b\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), el cual toma como objeto el Nibb\u0101na, que es sin signos, sin continuidad, libre de formaciones y cesaci\xf3n. Este conocimiento trasciende el linaje, la designaci\xf3n y el plano de la persona com\xfan (puthujjana) y entra en el linaje, la designaci\xf3n y el plano de los nobles (ariya). Constituye la primera advertencia, la primera atenci\xf3n y el primer examen del Nibb\u0101na como objeto. Realiza la funci\xf3n de condici\xf3n para el camino noble en seis formas: por medio de la condici\xf3n de contig\xfcidad, contig\xfcidad inmediata, repetici\xf3n, apoyo decisivo, ausencia y desaparici\xf3n. Este conocimiento es la cima de la visi\xf3n cabal, su punto culminante, y es de tal naturaleza que no hay marcha atr\xe1s."}},{id:"vism-22.3",pali:"\u2018\u2018Katha\u1e43 bahiddh\u0101 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101naviva\u1e6d\u1e6dane pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 gotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43? Upp\u0101da\u1e43 abhibhuyyat\u012bti gotrabhu. Pavatta\u1e43\u2026pe\u2026 up\u0101y\u0101sa\u1e43 abhibhuyyat\u012bti gotrabhu. Bahiddh\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101ranimitta\u1e43 abhibhuyyat\u012bti gotrabhu. Anupp\u0101da\u1e43 pakkhandat\u012bti gotrabhu. Appavatta\u1e43\u2026pe\u2026 anup\u0101y\u0101sa\u1e43 nirodha\u1e43 nibb\u0101na\u1e43 pakkhandat\u012bti gotrabhu. Upp\u0101da\u1e43 abhibhuyyitv\u0101 anupp\u0101da\u1e43 pakkhandat\u012bti gotrabh\u016b\u2019\u2019ti (pa\u1e6di. ma. 1.59) sabba\u1e43 vitth\u0101retabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"\u201cHow is wisdom in the emergence and turning away from the external change-of-lineage knowledge? Because it overcomes arising, it is change-of-lineage. Because it overcomes occurrence\u2026 because it overcomes distress, it is change-of-lineage. Because it overcomes the external sign of formations, it is change-of-lineage. Because it enters into non-arising, it is change-of-lineage. Because it enters into non-occurrence\u2026 into non-distress, into cessation, Nibb\u0101na, it is change-of-lineage. Because, having overcome arising, it enters into non-arising, it is change-of-lineage\u201d (Ps I 60). All this should be elaborated.",pt:"'Como a sabedoria na emerg\xeancia e na virada para longe do que \xe9 externo \xe9 o conhecimento de mudan\xe7a de linhagem (gotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47a)? \xc9 chamada de mudan\xe7a de linhagem (gotrabhu) porque supera o surgimento (upp\u0101da). \xc9 chamada de mudan\xe7a de linhagem porque supera a continuidade (pavatta)... [pe]... supera o desespero (up\u0101y\u0101sa). \xc9 chamada de mudan\xe7a de linhagem porque supera o sinal externo das forma\xe7\xf5es (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ranimitta). \xc9 chamada de mudan\xe7a de linhagem porque se lan\xe7a no n\xe3o-surgimento (anupp\u0101da). \xc9 chamada de mudan\xe7a de linhagem porque se lan\xe7a na n\xe3o-continuidade... [pe]... no n\xe3o-desespero, na cessa\xe7\xe3o, no Nibb\u0101na. \xc9 chamada de mudan\xe7a de linhagem porque, tendo superado o surgimento, lan\xe7a-se no n\xe3o-surgimento.' Tudo isso deve ser detalhado.",es:"\u201c\xbfC\xf3mo es que la sabidur\xeda que surge al emerger de lo externo (las formaciones) es el conocimiento de cambio de linaje? Se llama cambio de linaje porque supera el surgimiento. Supera la continuidad... (pe)... supera la desesperaci\xf3n. Supera los signos externos de las formaciones. Se lanza hacia el no-surgimiento. Se lanza hacia la no-continuidad... (pe)... hacia la no-desesperaci\xf3n, hacia la cesaci\xf3n, hacia el Nibb\u0101na. Habiendo superado el surgimiento, se lanza hacia el no-surgimiento; por eso se llama cambio de linaje\u201d (Pa\u1e6di. I, 59). Todo esto debe entenderse en detalle."}},{id:"vism-22.4",pali:"Tatr\u0101ya\u1e43 ek\u0101vajjanena ekav\u012bthiya\u1e43 pavattam\u0101n\u0101nampi anulomagotrabh\u016bna\u1e43 n\u0101n\u0101ramma\u1e47e pavattan\u0101k\u0101rad\u012bpik\u0101 upam\u0101 \u2013 yath\u0101 hi mah\u0101m\u0101tika\u1e43 la\u1e45ghitv\u0101 parat\u012bre pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101tuk\u0101mo puriso vegena dh\u0101vitv\u0101 m\u0101tik\u0101ya orimat\u012bre rukkhas\u0101kh\u0101ya bandhitv\u0101 olambita\u1e43 rajju\u1e43 v\u0101 ya\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e43 v\u0101 gahetv\u0101 ulla\u1e45ghitv\u0101 parat\u012braninnapo\u1e47apabbh\u0101rak\u0101yo hutv\u0101 parat\u012brassa uparibh\u0101ga\u1e43 patto ta\u1e43 mu\xf1citv\u0101 vedham\u0101no parat\u012bre patitv\u0101 sa\u1e47ika\u1e43 pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti, evamev\u0101ya\u1e43 yog\u0101vacaropi bhavayonigati\u1e6d\u1e6dhitiniv\u0101s\u0101na\u1e43 parat\u012brabh\u016bte nibb\u0101ne pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101tuk\u0101mo udayabbay\u0101nupassan\u0101din\u0101 vegena dh\u0101vitv\u0101 attabh\u0101varukkhas\u0101kh\u0101ya bandhitv\u0101 olambita\u1e43 r\u016bparajju\u1e43 v\u0101 vedan\u0101d\u012bsu a\xf1\xf1atarada\u1e47\u1e0da\u1e43 v\u0101 aniccanti v\u0101 dukkhanti v\u0101 anatt\u0101ti v\u0101ti anulom\u0101vajjanena gahetv\u0101 ta\u1e43 amu\xf1cam\u0101nova pa\u1e6dhamena anulomacittena ulla\u1e45ghitv\u0101 dutiyena parat\u012braninnapo\u1e47apabbh\u0101rak\u0101yo viya nibb\u0101naninnapo\u1e47apabbh\u0101ram\u0101naso hutv\u0101 tatiyena parat\u012brassa uparibh\u0101ga\u1e43 patto viya id\u0101ni pattabbassa nibb\u0101nassa \u0101sanno hutv\u0101 tassa cittassa nirodhena ta\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 mu\xf1citv\u0101 gotrabhucittena visa\u1e45kh\u0101re parat\u012brabh\u016bte nibb\u0101ne patati. Ek\u0101ramma\u1e47e pana aladdh\u0101sevanat\u0101ya vedham\u0101no so puriso viya na t\u0101va suppati\u1e6d\u1e6dhito hoti, tato magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101t\u012bti.",translations:{en:"Herein, this is an illustration to clarify the mode of occurrence, with different objects, of conformity and change-of-lineage, even though they arise in a single cognitive series with a single adverting. Just as a man, wishing to establish himself on the far shore after leaping over a great channel, runs swiftly, grabs a rope or a stick tied to a tree branch on the near shore and hanging down, leaps over, and with his body inclined and sloping towards the far shore, reaches the upper part of the far shore, releases that, and, trembling, lands on the far shore and slowly establishes himself; so too, this meditator, wishing to establish himself in Nibb\u0101na, which is the far shore to existences, births, destinations, stations of consciousness, and abodes, runs swiftly by means of the contemplation of rise and fall and so on. With the adverting for conformity, he grasps the rope of material form or the staff of one of the other aggregates such as feeling\u2014which are like things tied to a branch of the tree of personal existence\u2014as \u2018impermanent,\u2019 or \u2018painful,\u2019 or \u2018not-self.\u2019 Without releasing it, he leaps with the first conformity consciousness. With the second, his mind becomes inclined and sloping towards Nibb\u0101na, like the man's body inclined towards the far shore. With the third, he becomes close to Nibb\u0101na, which is now to be attained, like the man who has reached the upper part of the far shore. With the cessation of that consciousness, he releases that object of formations and, with the change-of-lineage consciousness, lands upon the unconditioned, the far shore which is Nibb\u0101na. However, like that trembling man, he is not yet well established because the power of repetition with a single object has not been obtained. Then, he becomes established by means of path knowledge.",pt:"Nesse contexto, esta \xe9 a met\xe1fora que ilustra o modo de ocorr\xeancia em diferentes objetos mentais do conhecimento de conformidade (anuloma) e do conhecimento de mudan\xe7a de linhagem (gotrabh\u016b), embora ocorram em um \xfanico processo cognitivo (v\u012bthi) por meio de uma \xfanica advert\xeancia (\u0101vajjana): assim como um homem que deseja cruzar um grande canal de \xe1gua e se estabelecer na outra margem corre velozmente, segura uma corda ou um bast\xe3o amarrado e pendurado em um galho de \xe1rvore na margem pr\xf3xima do canal, salta e, com o corpo inclinado, pendido e direcionado para a outra margem, alcan\xe7a a parte superior da outra margem, solta a corda ou o bast\xe3o e, tremendo, cai na outra margem e gradualmente se estabiliza; da mesma forma, este praticante (yog\u0101vacara), desejando estabelecer-se no Nibb\u0101na, que \xe9 como a outra margem em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s exist\xeancias, matrizes, destinos, esta\xe7\xf5es da consci\xeancia e moradas dos seres, corre velozmente por meio da contempla\xe7\xe3o do surgimento e desaparecimento, etc., e, por meio da advert\xeancia de conformidade, segura a corda da mat\xe9ria ou o bast\xe3o de qualquer um dos outros agregados, como a sensa\xe7\xe3o, etc., que est\xe3o amarrados e pendurados no galho da \xe1rvore do pr\xf3prio corpo f\xedsico, contemplando-os como impermanentes, insatisfat\xf3rios ou impessoais. Sem soltar esse objeto mental, ele salta com o primeiro momento de consci\xeancia de conformidade; com o segundo, sua mente se inclina, pende e se direciona para o Nibb\u0101na, assim como o corpo do homem inclinado para a outra margem; com o terceiro, como se tivesse alcan\xe7ado a parte superior da outra margem, ele se aproxima do Nibb\u0101na que est\xe1 prestes a ser alcan\xe7ado e, com a cessa\xe7\xe3o desse momento de consci\xeancia, soltando aquele objeto condicionado, ele cai, por meio da consci\xeancia de mudan\xe7a de linhagem, no Nibb\u0101na incondicionado, que \xe9 como a outra margem. No entanto, por n\xe3o ter obtido a repeti\xe7\xe3o (\u0101sevana) naquele \xfanico objeto mental, ele ainda n\xe3o est\xe1 firmemente estabelecido, assemelhando-se \xe0quele homem que treme; depois disso, ele se estabelece firmemente por meio do conhecimento do caminho (magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a).",es:"Aqu\xed se presenta una analog\xeda que ilustra c\xf3mo los conocimientos de conformidad y de cambio de linaje, aunque ocurren en un mismo proceso cognitivo (v\u012bthi) bajo una sola advertencia, act\xfaan sobre diferentes objetos: Imaginen a un hombre que desea cruzar una gran zanja y establecerse en la otra orilla. Corre con velocidad, toma una soga o una p\xe9rtiga atada y colgada de la rama de un \xe1rbol en la orilla cercana, salta con el cuerpo inclinado y dirigido hacia la otra orilla, y al llegar sobre la otra orilla, suelta la soga o la p\xe9rtiga, cae temblando en la otra orilla y se estabiliza lentamente. De igual modo, este meditador, deseando establecerse en el Nibb\u0101na, que es la otra orilla m\xe1s all\xe1 de los tipos de existencia, matrices, destinos, estaciones de la conciencia y moradas de los seres, corre con la velocidad del conocimiento de la contemplaci\xf3n del surgimiento y la desaparici\xf3n, etc. Mediante la advertencia de conformidad, toma la soga de la materialidad o la p\xe9rtiga de uno de los agregados mentales como la sensaci\xf3n, etc., atada a la rama del \xe1rbol de su propio ser, percibi\xe9ndola como impermanente, sufrida o no-yo. Sin soltar ese objeto, salta con el primer momento de conciencia de conformidad; con el segundo momento de conformidad, su mente se inclina, se dirige y se orienta hacia el Nibb\u0101na, como el hombre inclinado hacia la otra orilla; con el tercer momento de conformidad, estando cerca del Nibb\u0101na que est\xe1 a punto de alcanzar, como el hombre que ha llegado sobre la otra orilla, al cesar ese momento de conciencia, suelta el objeto de las formaciones y, mediante la conciencia de cambio de linaje, cae en el Nibb\u0101na, que es la otra orilla libre de formaciones. Sin embargo, al no haber obtenido a\xfan la condici\xf3n de repetici\xf3n en ese \xfanico objeto, se parece al hombre que todav\xeda tiembla y no est\xe1 firmemente establecido; posteriormente, se establece firmemente mediante el conocimiento del camino."}},{id:"vism-22.5",pali:"Na kevala\xf1cesa maggo lobhakkhandh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 nibbijjhanameva karoti, apica kho anamataggasa\u1e43s\u0101rava\u1e6d\u1e6dadukkhasamudda\u1e43 soseti, sabbaap\u0101yadv\u0101r\u0101ni pidahati, sattanna\u1e43 ariyadhan\u0101na\u1e43 sammukh\u012bbh\u0101va\u1e43 karoti, a\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e45gika\u1e43 micch\u0101magga\u1e43 pajahati, sabbaverabhay\u0101ni v\u016bpasameti, samm\u0101sambuddhassa orasaputtabh\u0101va\u1e43 upaneti, a\xf1\xf1esa\xf1ca anekasat\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101na\u1e43 pa\u1e6dil\u0101bh\u0101ya sa\u1e43vattat\u012bti eva\u1e43 anek\u0101nisa\u1e43sad\u0101yakena sot\u0101pattimaggena sampayutta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 sot\u0101pattimagge \xf1\u0101\u1e47anti.",translations:{en:"Not only does this path accomplish the piercing of the masses of greed and so forth, but it also dries up the ocean of suffering in the beginningless round of rebirths, closes all doors to the planes of misery, brings the seven noble treasures to presence, abandons the eightfold wrong path, allays all enmities and fears, leads to the state of being a true-born son of the Perfectly Enlightened One, and conduces to the attainment of many hundreds of other benefits. Thus, the knowledge associated with the path of stream-entry, which bestows these many benefits, is called \u2018knowledge in the path of stream-entry.\u2019",pt:"Este caminho n\xe3o apenas perfura as massas de cobi\xe7a, etc., mas tamb\xe9m seca o oceano de sofrimento do ciclo de renascimentos (sa\u1e43s\u0101ra) cujo in\xedcio \xe9 inconceb\xedvel, fecha todas as portas dos reinos de sofrimento (ap\u0101ya), manifesta as sete riquezas nobres (ariya-dhana), abandona o caminho \xf3ctuplo incorreto (micch\u0101magga), pacifica todas as hostilidades e temores, conduz ao estado de verdadeiro filho do Buda perfeitamente iluminado e concorre para a obten\xe7\xe3o de centenas de outros benef\xedcios. Assim, o conhecimento associado ao caminho da entrada na corrente, que concede in\xfameros benef\xedcios, \xe9 chamado de 'conhecimento no caminho da entrada na corrente' (sot\u0101pattimagge \xf1\u0101\u1e47a).",es:"Este camino no solo realiza la penetraci\xf3n de las masas de codicia y dem\xe1s, sino que tambi\xe9n seca el oc\xe9ano de sufrimiento del ciclo de renacimientos sin fin, cierra todas las puertas a los estados de privaci\xf3n, hace presentes los siete tesoros de los nobles, abandona el camino \xf3ctuple err\xf3neo, apacigua todos los peligros y hostilidades, conduce al estado de hijo leg\xedtimo del Buda perfectamente iluminado, y conduce a la obtenci\xf3n de otros cientos de beneficios. Por lo tanto, el conocimiento asociado con el camino de entrada en la corriente que otorga tales m\xfaltiples beneficios se llama 'conocimiento del camino de entrada en la corriente'."}},{id:"vism-22.6",pali:"Imassa pana \xf1\u0101\u1e47assa anantara\u1e43 tasseva vip\u0101kabh\u016bt\u0101ni dve t\u012b\u1e47i v\u0101 phalacitt\u0101ni uppajjanti. Anantaravip\u0101katt\u0101yeva hi lokuttarakusal\u0101na\u1e43 \u2018\u2018sam\u0101dhim\u0101nantarika\xf1\xf1am\u0101h\u016b\u2019\u2019ti (khu. p\u0101. 6.5) ca \u2018\u2018dandha\u1e43 \u0101nantarika\u1e43 p\u0101pu\u1e47\u0101ti \u0101sav\u0101na\u1e43 khay\u0101y\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (a. ni. 4.162) ca \u0101di vutta\u1e43. Keci pana eka\u1e43 dve t\u012b\u1e47i catt\u0101ri v\u0101 phalacitt\u0101n\u012bti vadanti, ta\u1e43 na gahetabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Furthermore, immediately after this knowledge, two or three fruition-consciousnesses arise, which are its very fruit. Indeed, it is because supramundane wholesome states yield immediate results that it is said: 'They call concentration that which has an immediate result,' and 'Slowly one attains the immediate path for the destruction of the cankers,' and so on. Some, however, say that one, two, three, or four fruition-consciousnesses arise, but that should not be accepted.",pt:"Imediatamente ap\xf3s este conhecimento, surgem dois ou tr\xeas momentos de consci\xeancia de frui\xe7\xe3o (phalacitta), que s\xe3o os seus resultados (vip\u0101ka). Pois, devido ao fato de os dhammas salutares supramundanos darem frutos imediatamente, foi dito: 'Eles chamam essa concentra\xe7\xe3o de imediata' e 'Ele alcan\xe7a lentamente o estado imediato para a destrui\xe7\xe3o das impurezas', entre outras passagens. No entanto, alguns dizem que surgem um, dois, tr\xeas ou quatro momentos de consci\xeancia de frui\xe7\xe3o; essa afirma\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o deve ser aceita.",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s de este conocimiento, surgen dos o tres momentos de consciencia de fruto que son su resultado. Debido a que las acciones sanas supramundanas dan su fruto de inmediato, se ha dicho: 'Aquel cuya concentraci\xf3n es inmediata' y 'alcanza r\xe1pidamente lo inmediato para la destrucci\xf3n de las impurezas'. Sin embargo, algunos dicen que surgen una, dos, tres o cuatro consciencias de fruto, pero eso no debe ser aceptado."}},{id:"vism-22.7",pali:"Ett\u0101vat\u0101 ca panesa sot\u0101panno n\u0101ma dutiyo ariyapuggalo hoti. Bhusa\u1e43 pamattopi hutv\u0101 sattakkhattu\u1e43 devesu ca manussesu ca sandh\u0101vitv\u0101 sa\u1e43saritv\u0101 dukkhassantassa kara\u1e47asamattho hoti. Phalapariyos\u0101ne panassa citta\u1e43 bhava\u1e45ga\u1e43 otarati, tato bhava\u1e45ga\u1e43 upacchinditv\u0101 maggapaccavekkha\u1e47atth\u0101ya uppajjati manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana\u1e43, tasmi\u1e43 niruddhe pa\u1e6dip\u0101\u1e6diy\u0101 satta maggapaccavekkha\u1e47ajavan\u0101n\u012bti. Puna bhava\u1e45ga\u1e43 otaritv\u0101 teneva nayena phal\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 paccavekkha\u1e47atth\u0101ya \u0101vajjan\u0101d\u012bni uppajjanti. Yesa\u1e43 uppattiy\u0101 esa magga\u1e43 paccavekkhati, phala\u1e43 paccavekkhati, pah\u012bnakilese paccavekkhati, avasi\u1e6d\u1e6dhakilese paccavekkhati, nibb\u0101na\u1e43 paccavekkhati.",translations:{en:"And with this, one becomes the one called a stream-enterer, the second noble person. Even if one were to be extremely heedless, after running and wandering on among devas and humans for at most seven times, one is capable of making an end of suffering. At the conclusion of the fruition, one's consciousness descends into the life-continuum. Then, having interrupted the life-continuum, mind-door-adverting arises for the purpose of reviewing the path. When that has ceased, in sequence seven path-reviewing impulsion-consciousnesses arise. Again, having descended into the life-continuum, adverting and so on arise in the same way for the purpose of reviewing the fruition and the rest. By the arising of these, this one reviews the path, reviews the fruition, reviews the abandoned defilements, reviews the remaining defilements, and reviews Nibb\u0101na.",pt:"Por meio disso, ele se torna a segunda pessoa nobre, chamada de 'aquele que entrou na corrente' (sot\u0101panna). Mesmo que seja extremamente negligente, ele \xe9 capaz de p\xf4r fim ao sofrimento ap\xf3s transmigrar e vagar no m\xe1ximo sete vezes entre deuses e humanos. Ao final da frui\xe7\xe3o, sua mente submerge no fluxo shava\u1e45ga (bhava\u1e45ga); em seguida, interrompendo o bhava\u1e45ga, surge a advert\xeancia pela porta da mente (manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana) para a revis\xe3o do caminho; quando esta cessa, ocorrem sucessivamente sete momentos de impuls\xe3o mental de revis\xe3o do caminho (maggapaccavekkha\u1e47ajavana). Depois, submergindo novamente no bhava\u1e45ga, surgem, da mesma maneira, os momentos de advert\xeancia, etc., para a revis\xe3o da frui\xe7\xe3o, etc. Com o surgimento desses momentos, ele revisa o caminho, revisa a frui\xe7\xe3o, revisa as impurezas eliminadas, revisa as impurezas restantes e revisa o Nibb\u0101na.",es:"De esta manera, este se convierte en la segunda persona noble llamada 'el que entra en la corriente'. Incluso si llegara a ser muy negligente, es capaz de poner fin al sufrimiento tras haber transmutado y vagado siete veces entre dioses y humanos. Al final del fruto, su consciencia desciende al flujo vital; luego, interrumpiendo el flujo vital, surge la advertencia del sentido mental con el fin de reflexionar sobre el camino. Al cesar esta, ocurren sucesivamente siete impulsos de reflexi\xf3n sobre el camino. Tras descender de nuevo al flujo vital, de la misma manera surgen la advertencia y dem\xe1s para reflexionar sobre el fruto y los otros factores. Mediante su surgimiento, este reflexiona sobre el camino, reflexiona sobre el fruto, reflexiona sobre las impurezas abandonadas, reflexiona sobre las impurezas restantes y reflexiona sobre el Nibb\u0101na."}},{id:"vism-22.8",pali:"So hi \u2018\u2018imin\u0101 vat\u0101ha\u1e43 maggena \u0101gato\u2019\u2019ti magga\u1e43 paccavekkhati, tato \u2018\u2018aya\u1e43 me \u0101nisa\u1e43so laddho\u2019\u2019ti phala\u1e43 paccavekkhati. Tato \u2018\u2018ime n\u0101ma me kiles\u0101 pah\u012bn\u0101\u2019\u2019ti pah\u012bnakilese paccavekkhati. Tato \u2018\u2018ime n\u0101ma me kiles\u0101 avasi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101\u2019\u2019ti uparimaggattayavajjhe kilese paccavekkhati. Avas\u0101ne ca \u2018\u2018aya\u1e43 me dhammo \u0101ramma\u1e47ato pa\u1e6dividdho\u2019\u2019ti amata\u1e43 nibb\u0101na\u1e43 paccavekkhati. Iti sot\u0101pannassa ariyas\u0101vakassa pa\xf1ca paccavekkha\u1e47\u0101ni honti. Yath\u0101 ca sot\u0101pannassa, eva\u1e43 sakad\u0101g\u0101mian\u0101g\u0101m\u012bnampi. Arahato pana avasi\u1e6d\u1e6dhakilesapaccavekkha\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u0101ma natth\u012bti. Eva\u1e43 sabb\u0101nipi ek\u016bnav\u012bsati paccavekkha\u1e47\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"For one reviews the path thus: 'Indeed, by this path have I come.' Then one reviews the fruition thus: 'This benefit has been gained by me.' Then one reviews the abandoned defilements thus: 'These defilements have been abandoned by me.' Then one reviews the remaining defilements\u2014those to be abandoned by the three higher paths\u2014thus: 'These defilements remain for me.' And finally, one reviews the deathless Nibb\u0101na thus: 'This state has been penetrated by me as its object.' Thus, for the noble disciple who is a stream-enterer, there are five kinds of reviewing. And as for the stream-enterer, so too for the once-returner and the non-returner. For the Arahant, however, there is no reviewing of remaining defilements. Thus, all together, there are what are called the nineteen kinds of reviewing.",pt:"Pois ele revisa o caminho pensando: 'Certamente vim por este caminho'; depois, revisa a frui\xe7\xe3o pensando: 'Este \xe9 o benef\xedcio que obtive'; em seguida, revisa as impurezas eliminadas pensando: 'Estas impurezas foram eliminadas por mim'; depois, revisa as impurezas restantes pensando: 'Estas impurezas ainda me restam', referindo-se \xe0quelas que devem ser eliminadas pelos tr\xeas caminhos superiores; e, por fim, revisa o Nibb\u0101na imortal pensando: 'Este estado foi penetrado por mim como objeto mental'. Assim, o nobre disc\xedpulo que entrou na corrente tem os cinco tipos de revis\xe3o. O mesmo ocorre com aquele que retorna uma \xfanica vez (sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b) e com aquele que n\xe3o retorna (an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b). Para o Arahat, no entanto, n\xe3o existe a revis\xe3o das impurezas restantes. Dessa forma, h\xe1 ao todo dezenove revis\xf5es.",es:"\xc9l reflexiona sobre el camino diciendo: 'Por este camino, ciertamente, he venido'. Luego reflexiona sobre el fruto: 'Este beneficio he obtenido'. Despu\xe9s reflexiona sobre las impurezas abandonadas: 'Tales impurezas han sido abandonadas por m\xed'. Luego reflexiona sobre las impurezas restantes que deben ser eliminadas por los tres caminos superiores: 'Tales impurezas a\xfan me quedan'. Finalmente, reflexiona sobre el Nibb\u0101na inmortal: 'Este es el fealidade que he penetrado como objeto'. As\xed, el noble disc\xedpulo que entra en la corriente tiene cinco reflexiones. Lo mismo ocurre para los que han entrado una sola vez y los que no regresan. Para el Arahat, sin embargo, no existe la reflexi\xf3n sobre las impurezas restantes. As\xed, en total, hay diecinueve reflexiones."}},{id:"vism-22.9",pali:"Ukka\u1e6d\u1e6dhaparicchedoyeva ceso. Pah\u012bn\u0101vasi\u1e6d\u1e6dhakilesapaccavekkha\u1e47a\xf1hi sekkh\u0101nampi hoti v\u0101 na v\u0101. Tassa hi paccavekkha\u1e47assa abh\u0101veneva mah\u0101n\u0101mo bhagavanta\u1e43 pucchi \u2018\u2018kosu n\u0101ma me dhammo ajjhatta\u1e43 appah\u012bno, yena me ekad\u0101 lobhadhamm\u0101pi citta\u1e43 pariy\u0101d\u0101ya ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhant\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (ma. ni. 1.175) sabba\u1e43 vitth\u0101rato veditabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"This, however, is only the maximum reckoning. For even for trainees, the reviewing of abandoned and remaining defilements may or may not occur. Indeed, it was precisely because of the absence of such reviewing that Mah\u0101n\u0101ma asked the Blessed One: 'What state, venerable sir, has not been abandoned within me, on account of which states of greed at times invade my mind and remain?' The entire matter should be understood in detail.",pt:"Este \xe9 o limite m\xe1ximo de classifica\xe7\xe3o. Pois a revis\xe3o das impurezas eliminadas e restantes pode ou n\xe3o ocorrer para os disc\xedpulos em treinamento (sekha). De fato, foi precisamente devido \xe0 aus\xeancia dessa revis\xe3o que o rei Mah\u0101n\u0101ma perguntou ao Aben\xe7oado: 'Senhor, que estado mental ainda n\xe3o foi eliminado dentro de mim, de modo que, \xe0s vezes, dhammas de cobi\xe7a dominam minha mente e nela permanecem?'. Tudo isso deve ser compreendido detalhadamente a partir do sutta.",es:"Esta es solo la delimitaci\xf3n extrema. Pues el examen de las impurezas abandonadas y de las restantes puede ocurrir o no para los Sekhas (aprendices). Debido precisamente a la ausencia de tal examen, Mah\u0101n\u0101ma pregunt\xf3 al Bienaventurado: '\xbfQu\xe9 estado interno no he abandonado todav\xeda, por el cual a veces los estados de codicia se apoderan de mi mente y permanecen?', y todo esto debe entenderse detalladamente."}},{id:"vism-22.10",pali:"Eva\u1e43 paccavekkhitv\u0101 pana so sot\u0101panno ariyas\u0101vako tasmi\xf1\xf1eva v\u0101 \u0101sane nisinno, aparena v\u0101 samayena k\u0101mar\u0101gaby\u0101p\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 tanubh\u0101v\u0101ya dutiy\u0101ya bh\u016bmiy\u0101 pattiy\u0101 yoga\u1e43 karoti. So indriyabalabojjha\u1e45g\u0101ni samodh\u0101netv\u0101 tadeva r\u016bpavedan\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101ravi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47abheda\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragata\u1e43 anicca\u1e43 dukkhamanatt\u0101ti \xf1\u0101\u1e47ena parimaddati, parivatteti, vipassan\u0101v\u012bthi\u1e43 og\u0101hati. Tasseva\u1e43 pa\u1e6dipannassa vuttanayeneva sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101vas\u0101ne ek\u0101vajjanena anulomagotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47esu uppannesu gotrabhuanantara\u1e43 sakad\u0101g\u0101mimaggo uppajjati. Tena sampayutta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 sakad\u0101g\u0101mimagge \xf1\u0101\u1e47a nti.",translations:{en:"Having reviewed thus, that noble disciple, the stream-enterer, either while seated on that very seat or at a later time, applies himself to the attenuation of sensual desire and ill will, and to the attainment of the second stage. Having brought the faculties, powers, and enlightenment factors into harmony, one crushes and turns over with knowledge that same conditioned reality\u2014differentiated as form, feeling, perception, formations, and consciousness\u2014as impermanent, suffering, and not-self, and one enters upon the path of insight. For one so practicing, in the way already described, at the culmination of equanimity towards formations, with a single adverting, when the conformity and change-of-lineage knowledges have arisen, immediately after change-of-lineage the path of the once-returner arises. The knowledge associated with that is the knowledge in the once-returner's path.",pt:"Ap\xf3s realizar essa revis\xe3o, aquele nobre disc\xedpulo que entrou na corrente, sentado no mesmo assento ou em outra ocasi\xe3o, empenha-se na pr\xe1tica para alcan\xe7ar o segundo est\xe1gio, a fim de atenuar o desejo sensorial (k\u0101mar\u0101ga) e a m\xe1 vontade (by\u0101p\u0101da). Ele harmoniza as faculdades espirituais (indriya), as for\xe7as (bala) e os fatores de ilumina\xe7\xe3o (bojjha\u1e45ga) e, com o conhecimento, examina repetidamente e de v\xe1rios modos aquele mesmo conjunto de forma\xe7\xf5es condicionadas, dividido em mat\xe9ria, sensa\xe7\xe3o, percep\xe7\xe3o, forma\xe7\xf5es mentais e consci\xeancia, contemplando-o como impermanente, insatisfat\xf3rio e impessoal, adentrando o processo de vipassan\u0101. Para ele que assim pratica, da mesma maneira descrita anteriormente, ao final do conhecimento de equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es condicionadas (sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101), por meio de uma \xfanica advert\xeancia, quando surgem os conhecimentos de conformidade e de mudan\xe7a de linhagem, imediatamente ap\xf3s este \xfaltimo, surge o caminho daquele que retorna uma \xfanica vez (sakad\u0101g\u0101mimagga). O conhecimento associado a ele \xe9 chamado de 'conhecimento no caminho daquele que retorna uma \xfanica vez' (sakad\u0101g\u0101mimagge \xf1\u0101\u1e47a).",es:"Habiendo reflexionado as\xed, el noble disc\xedpulo que ha entrado en la corriente (sot\u0101panna), sentado en ese mismo asiento o en otro momento, se esfuerza para alcanzar el segundo nivel con el fin de atenuar el deseo sensorial y la mala voluntad. Reuniendo las facultades, los poderes y los factores de iluminaci\xf3n, tritura y revuelve mediante el conocimiento el conjunto de las formaciones \u2014dividido en forma, sensaci\xf3n, percepci\xf3n, formaciones y conciencia\u2014 como impermanente, sufrimiento y no-yo, y entra en el camino de la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassan\u0101). Para quien as\xed practica, del mismo modo ya descrito, al final de la ecuanimidad hacia las formaciones y tras surgir los conocimientos de conformidad y de cambio de linaje en un solo acto de advertencia, surge el sendero del que retorna una vez (sakad\u0101g\u0101mimagga) inmediatamente despu\xe9s del cambio de linaje. El conocimiento asociado a este se denomina conocimiento del sendero del que retorna una vez."}},{id:"vism-22.11",pali:"Imass\u0101pi \xf1\u0101\u1e47assa anantara\u1e43 vuttanayeneva phalacitt\u0101ni veditabb\u0101ni. Ett\u0101vat\u0101 cesa sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b n\u0101ma catuttho ariyapuggalo hoti saki\u1e43deva ima\u1e43 loka\u1e43 \u0101gantv\u0101 dukkhassantakara\u1e47asamattho. Tato para\u1e43 paccavekkha\u1e47a\u1e43 vuttanayameva.",translations:{en:"Immediately after this knowledge also, the fruition-consciousnesses are to be understood in the way already described. And with this, one becomes the one called a once-returner, the fourth noble person, who is capable of making an end of suffering after having come to this world only one more time. Thereafter, the reviewing is just as has been described.",pt:"Imediatamente ap\xf3s este conhecimento, os momentos de consci\xeancia de frui\xe7\xe3o devem ser compreendidos da mesma maneira descrita anteriormente. Por meio disso, ele se torna a quarta pessoa nobre, chamada de 'aquele que retorna uma \xfanica vez' (sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), sendo capaz de p\xf4r fim ao sofrimento ap\xf3s retornar a este mundo apenas mais uma vez. Depois disso, a revis\xe3o ocorre exatamente da mesma maneira descrita.",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s de este conocimiento, los momentos de conciencia del fruto deben entenderse seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ya descrito. Por esto, \xe9l se convierte en la cuarta persona noble llamada 'el que retorna una vez' (sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), capaz de poner fin al sufrimiento tras regresar a este mundo solo una vez m\xe1s. Despu\xe9s de eso, la reflexi\xf3n ocurre del mismo modo ya mencionado."}},{id:"vism-22.12",pali:"Eva\u1e43 paccavekkhitv\u0101 ca so sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b ariyas\u0101vako tasmi\xf1\xf1eva v\u0101 \u0101sane nisinno aparena v\u0101 samayena k\u0101mar\u0101gaby\u0101p\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 anavasesappah\u0101n\u0101ya tatiy\u0101ya bh\u016bmiy\u0101 pattiy\u0101 yoga\u1e43 karoti, so indriyabalabojjha\u1e45g\u0101ni samodh\u0101netv\u0101 tadeva sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragata\u1e43 anicca\u1e43 dukkhamanatt\u0101ti \xf1\u0101\u1e47ena parimaddati, parivatteti, vipassan\u0101v\u012bthi\u1e43 og\u0101hati. Tasseva\u1e43 pa\u1e6dipannassa vuttanayeneva sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101vas\u0101ne ek\u0101vajjanena anulomagotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47esu uppannesu gotrabhuanantara\u1e43 an\u0101g\u0101mimaggo uppajjati, tena sampayutta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 an\u0101g\u0101mimagge \xf1\u0101\u1e47a nti.",translations:{en:"And having reviewed thus, that noble disciple, the once-returner, either while seated on that very seat or at a later time, applies himself to the abandoning without remainder of sensual desire and ill will, and to the attainment of the third stage. Having brought the faculties, powers, and enlightenment factors into harmony, one crushes and turns over with knowledge that same conditioned reality as impermanent, suffering, and not-self, and one enters upon the path of insight. For one so practicing, in the way already described, at the culmination of equanimity towards formations, with a single adverting, when the conformity and change-of-lineage knowledges have arisen, immediately after change-of-lineage the path of the non-returner arises. The knowledge associated with that is the knowledge in the non-returner's path.",pt:"Ap\xf3s realizar essa revis\xe3o, aquele nobre disc\xedpulo que retorna uma \xfanica vez, sentado no mesmo assento ou em outra ocasi\xe3o, empenha-se na pr\xe1tica para alcan\xe7ar o terceiro est\xe1gio, a fim de eliminar completamente o desejo sensorial e a m\xe1 vontade. Ele harmoniza as faculdades espirituais, as for\xe7as e os fatores de ilumina\xe7\xe3o e, com o conhecimento, examina repetidamente aquele mesmo conjunto de forma\xe7\xf5es condicionadas, contemplando-o como impermanente, insatisfat\xf3rio e impessoal, adentrando o processo de vipassan\u0101. Para ele que assim pratica, da mesma maneira descrita anteriormente, ao final do conhecimento de equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es condicionadas, por meio de uma \xfanica advert\xeancia, quando surgem os conhecimentos de conformidade e de mudan\xe7a de linhagem, imediatamente ap\xf3s este \xfaltimo, surge o caminho daquele que n\xe3o retorna (an\u0101g\u0101mimagga). O conhecimento associado a ele \xe9 chamado de 'conhecimento no caminho daquele que n\xe3o retorna' (an\u0101g\u0101mimagge \xf1\u0101\u1e47a).",es:"Habiendo reflexionado as\xed, el noble disc\xedpulo que retorna una vez, sentado en ese mismo asiento o en otro momento, se esfuerza para alcanzar el tercer nivel con el fin de abandonar sin remanente el deseo sensorial y la mala voluntad. Reuniendo las facultades, los poderes y los factores de iluminaci\xf3n, tritura y revuelve mediante el conocimiento ese mismo conjunto de las formaciones como impermanente, sufrimiento y no-yo, y entra en el camino de la visi\xf3n cabal. Para quien as\xed practica, del mismo modo ya descrito, al final de la ecuanimidad hacia las formaciones y tras surgir los conocimientos de conformidad y de cambio de linaje en un solo acto de advertencia, surge el sendero del que no retorna (an\u0101g\u0101mimagga) inmediatamente despu\xe9s del cambio de linaje. El conocimiento asociado a este se denomina conocimiento del sendero del que no retorna."}},{id:"vism-22.13",pali:"Imassapi \xf1\u0101\u1e47assa anantara\u1e43 vuttanayeneva phalacitt\u0101ni veditabb\u0101ni. Ett\u0101vat\u0101 cesa an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b n\u0101ma cha\u1e6d\u1e6dho ariyapuggalo hoti opap\u0101tiko tatthaparinibb\u0101y\u012b an\u0101vattidhammo pa\u1e6disandhivasena ima\u1e43 loka\u1e43 puna an\u0101gant\u0101. Tato para\u1e43 paccavekkha\u1e47a\u1e43 vuttanayameva.",translations:{en:"Immediately after this knowledge, the fruition consciousnesses are to be understood in the manner stated earlier. And by this much, this person is called a non-returner, the sixth noble person, who is spontaneously born and attains final Nibb\u0101na there, whose nature is not to return, not coming again to this world by way of rebirth-linking. Thereafter, the reviewing is in the same manner as stated earlier.",pt:"Imediatamente ap\xf3s este conhecimento, os momentos de consci\xeancia de frui\xe7\xe3o devem ser compreendidos da mesma maneira descrita anteriormente. Por meio disso, ele se torna a sexta pessoa nobre, chamada de 'aquele que n\xe3o retorna' (an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), que renasce espontaneamente (opap\u0101tika), alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na ali mesmo e tem a natureza de n\xe3o mais retornar, n\xe3o vindo novamente a este mundo por meio do renascimento. Depois disso, a revis\xe3o ocorre exatamente da mesma maneira descrita.",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s de este conocimiento, los momentos de conciencia del fruto deben entenderse seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ya descrito. Por esto, \xe9l se convierte en la sexta persona noble llamada 'el que no retorna' (an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), de nacimiento espont\xe1neo, que alcanza all\xed el Nibb\u0101na final y tiene la naturaleza de no regresar, sin volver a este mundo mediante el renacimiento. Despu\xe9s de eso, la reflexi\xf3n ocurre del mismo modo ya mencionado."}},{id:"vism-22.14",pali:"Eva\u1e43 paccavekkhitv\u0101 ca so an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b ariyas\u0101vako tasmi\xf1\xf1eva v\u0101 \u0101sane nisinno, aparena v\u0101 samayena r\u016bp\u0101r\u016bpar\u0101gam\u0101nauddhaccaavijj\u0101na\u1e43 anavasesappah\u0101n\u0101ya catutth\u0101ya bh\u016bmiy\u0101 pattiy\u0101 yoga\u1e43 karoti, so indriyabalabojjha\u1e45g\u0101ni samodh\u0101netv\u0101 tadeva sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragata\u1e43 anicca\u1e43 dukkhamanatt\u0101ti \xf1\u0101\u1e47ena parimaddati, parivatteti, vipassan\u0101v\u012bthi\u1e43 og\u0101hati. Tasseva\u1e43 pa\u1e6dipannassa vuttanayeneva sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101vas\u0101ne ek\u0101vajjanena anulomagotrabhu\xf1\u0101\u1e47esu uppannesu gotrabhuanantara\u1e43 arahattamaggo uppajjati, tena sampayutta\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 arahattamagge \xf1\u0101\u1e47a nti.",translations:{en:"Having reviewed thus, that non-returner noble disciple, whether seated in that very seat or at another time, makes an effort for the attainment of the fourth stage, for the abandoning without remainder of lust for form, lust for the formless, conceit, restlessness, and ignorance. Having unified the faculties, powers, and factors of awakening, with wisdom he thoroughly scrutinizes and turns over that same conditioned phenomenon as impermanent, suffering, and non-self, and he enters the path of insight. For one practicing thus, in the manner stated earlier, at the culmination of equanimity towards formations, with a single advertence, upon the arising of the adaptation and change-of-lineage knowledges, immediately after the change-of-lineage, the path of Arahantship arises. The knowledge associated with it is called the knowledge in the path of Arahantship.",pt:"Tendo refletido assim, aquele nobre disc\xedpulo n\xe3o-retornante (an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), sentado naquele mesmo assento ou em outra ocasi\xe3o, empenha-se para alcan\xe7ar o quarto est\xe1gio para o abandono completo do apego \xe0 forma, do apego ao sem-forma, do orgulho, da agita\xe7\xe3o e da ignor\xe2ncia. Tendo unificado as faculdades, os poderes e os fatores do despertar, ele examina e esmi\xfa\xe7a repetidamente com sabedoria aquele mesmo conjunto de forma\xe7\xf5es como impermanente, doloroso e n\xe3o-self, e ingressa na via da vis\xe3o meditativa (vipassana). Para ele, praticando dessa maneira, conforme o m\xe9todo descrito, ao final da equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es, com uma \xfanica advert\xeancia mental, tendo surgido os conhecimentos de conformidade e de mudan\xe7a de linhagem, imediatamente ap\xf3s o conhecimento de mudan\xe7a de linhagem, surge o caminho do arahant. O conhecimento associado a ele \xe9 o conhecimento do caminho do arahant.",es:"Habiendo reflexionado as\xed, el noble disc\xedpulo que no retorna, sentado en ese mismo asiento o en otro momento, se esfuerza para alcanzar el cuarto nivel con el fin de abandonar sin remanente el deseo por lo material y lo inmaterial, el orgullo, la agitaci\xf3n y la ignorancia. Reuniendo las facultades, los poderes y los factores de iluminaci\xf3n, tritura y revuelve mediante el conocimiento ese mismo conjunto de las formaciones como impermanente, sufrimiento y no-yo, y entra en el camino de la visi\xf3n cabal. Para quien as\xed practica, del mismo modo ya descrito, tras surgir los conocimientos de conformidad y de cambio de linaje en un solo acto de advertencia, surge el sendero de la santidad (arahattamagga) inmediatamente despu\xe9s del cambio de linaje. El conocimiento asociado a este se denomina conocimiento del sendero de la santidad."}},{id:"vism-22.15",pali:"Imassapi \xf1\u0101\u1e47assa anantara\u1e43 vuttanayeneva phalacitt\u0101ni veditabb\u0101ni. Ett\u0101vat\u0101 cesa arah\u0101 n\u0101ma a\u1e6d\u1e6dhamo ariyapuggalo hoti mah\u0101kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101savo antimadehadh\u0101r\u012b ohitabh\u0101ro anuppattasadattho parikkh\u012b\u1e47abhavasa\u1e43yojano samm\u0101da\xf1\xf1\u0101 vimutto sadevakassa lokassa aggadakkhi\u1e47eyyoti.",translations:{en:"Immediately after this knowledge, the fruition consciousnesses are to be understood in the manner stated earlier. And by this much, this person is called an Arahant, the eighth noble individual, a great one whose taints are destroyed, bearing his final body, with the burden laid down, having attained his own true goal, with the fetters of existence completely destroyed, rightly liberated through final knowledge, the supreme recipient of offerings in the world with its deities.",pt:"Imediatamente ap\xf3s este conhecimento, da mesma maneira descrita, devem ser compreendidas as mentes de frui\xe7\xe3o. Por meio disso, esta pessoa \xe9 chamada de Arahant, o oitavo indiv\xedduo nobre, um grande destruidor das m\xe1culas, portador do \xfaltimo corpo f\xedsico, aquele que dep\xf4s o fardo, alcan\xe7ou o seu pr\xf3prio objetivo, destruiu completamente os grilh\xf5es da exist\xeancia, libertou-se atrav\xe9s do correto conhecimento e \xe9 o supremo merecedor de oferendas para o mundo com os seus devas.",es:"Inmediatamente despu\xe9s de este conocimiento, los momentos de conciencia del fruto deben entenderse seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ya descrito. Por esto, \xe9l se convierte en la octava persona noble llamada Arahant, el gran destructor de las impurezas, portador del \xfaltimo cuerpo, que ha dejado la carga, ha alcanzado su propia meta, ha destruido por completo los grilletes de la existencia, est\xe1 liberado por el conocimiento correcto y es digno de las ofrendas supremas del mundo con sus dioses."}},{id:"vism-22.16",pali:"Id\u0101ni imiss\u0101yeva catu\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ya \xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhiy\u0101 \u0101nubh\u0101vavij\u0101nanattha\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"Now, for the purpose of understanding the power of this very purification by knowledge and vision, which comprises four knowledges\u2014",pt:"Agora, a fim de compreender o poder desta mesma purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o, que consiste em quatro conhecimentos:",es:"Ahora, con el fin de comprender el poder de esta Purificaci\xf3n por el Conocimiento y la Visi\xf3n, que consiste en los cuatro conocimientos:"}},{id:"vism-22.17",pali:"Ye yena pah\u0101tabb\u0101 dhamm\u0101, tesa\u1e43 pah\u0101na\xf1c\u0101 ti imesu pana cat\u016bsu \xf1\u0101\u1e47esu ye dhamm\u0101 yena \xf1\u0101\u1e47ena pah\u0101tabb\u0101, tesa\u1e43 pah\u0101na\xf1ca j\u0101nitabba\u1e43. Et\u0101ni hi yath\u0101yoga\u1e43 sa\u1e43yojanakilesamicchattalokadhammamacchariyavipall\u0101saganthaagati\u0101savaoghayogan\u012bvara\u1e47apar\u0101m\u0101saup\u0101d\u0101naanusayamalaakusalakammapathacittupp\u0101dasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 dhamm\u0101na\u1e43 pah\u0101nakar\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"Regarding the states to be abandoned and their abandonment\u2014among these four knowledges, it should be understood which states are to be abandoned by which knowledge, and their abandonment. For these knowledges, as is appropriate, bring about the abandonment of the states enumerated as: fetters, defilements, wrongness, worldly conditions, stinginess, distortions, bonds, wrong courses, taints, floods, yokes, hindrances, misapprehension, clinging, underlying tendencies, stains, unwholesome courses of action, and unwholesome thought-arisings.",pt:"Quanto \xe0 frase \u2018Quais estados devem ser abandonados por qual [conhecimento], e o abandono deles\u2019, deve-se compreender, entre estes quatro conhecimentos, quais estados devem ser abandonados por qual conhecimento, bem como o abandono deles. Pois estes [quatro conhecimentos], de acordo com a aplica\xe7\xe3o apropriada, realizam o abandono dos estados conhecidos como grilh\xf5es, defilezas, fatores incorretos, condi\xe7\xf5es mundanas, avarezas, distor\xe7\xf5es, la\xe7os, caminhos errados, influxos, inunda\xe7\xf5es, v\xednculos, obst\xe1culos, apegos err\xf4neos, apegos, tend\xeancias latentes, impurezas, caminhos de a\xe7\xe3o prejudicial e surgimentos de mente prejudicial.",es:"\xabQu\xe9 estados deben ser abandonados por cu\xe1l conocimiento, y su abandono\xbb: entre estos cuatro conocimientos del sendero, debe entenderse qu\xe9 estados se abandonan por qu\xe9 conocimiento y el proceso de su abandono. Estos cuatro conocimientos del sendero, seg\xfan corresponda, efect\xfaan el abandono de los estados conocidos como grilletes (sa\u1e43yojana), impurezas (kilesa), erroniedades (micchatta), condiciones mundanas (lokadhamma), mezquindades (macchariya), distorsiones (vipall\u0101sa), nudos (gantha), caminos err\xf3neos (agati), efluvios (\u0101sava), inundaciones (ogha), yugos (yoga), obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47a), aferramientos (par\u0101m\u0101sa), apegos (up\u0101d\u0101na), tendencias latentes (anusaya), manchas (mala), senderos de acci\xf3n malsana (akusalakammapatha) y surgimientos de la mente malsana (akusalacittupp\u0101da)."}},{id:"vism-22.18",pali:"Kicc\u0101ni pari\xf1\xf1\u0101d\u012bni, y\u0101ni vutt\u0101ni abhisamayak\u0101le; T\u0101ni ca yath\u0101sabh\u0101vena, j\u0101nitabb\u0101ni sabb\u0101n\u012bti.",translations:{en:"The functions\u2014full understanding and so on\u2014 Which were stated at the time of direct comprehension, And all these should be known According to their intrinsic nature.",pt:"Todas as fun\xe7\xf5es de compreens\xe3o plena, etc., que s\xe3o mencionadas no momento da penetra\xe7\xe3o, devem ser compreendidas de acordo com a sua natureza real.",es:"Las funciones, como el pleno conocimiento y otras, que han sido declaradas para el momento de la realizaci\xf3n (abhisamaya); todas ellas deben conocerse de acuerdo con su verdadera naturaleza."}},{id:"vism-22.19",pali:"Tividh\u0101 hoti pari\xf1\xf1\u0101, tath\u0101 pah\u0101nampi sacchikiriy\u0101pi; Dve bh\u0101van\u0101 abhimat\u0101, vinicchayo tattha \xf1\u0101tabbo.",translations:{en:"Full understanding is threefold; likewise are abandonment and realization. Two kinds of development are accepted; the analysis thereof should be understood.",pt:"Tr\xeas s\xe3o os tipos de compreens\xe3o plena, e da mesma forma o abandono e a realiza\xe7\xe3o direta; dois tipos de desenvolvimento s\xe3o aceitos; a decis\xe3o sobre isso deve ser conhecida.",es:"\u201cEl conocimiento pleno es de tres tipos, e igualmente el abandono y la realizaci\xf3n; el desarrollo se considera de dos tipos; se debe comprender all\xed el an\xe1lisis\u201d."}},{id:"vism-22.20",pali:"Tividh\u0101 hoti pari\xf1\xf1\u0101 ti \xf1\u0101tapari\xf1\xf1\u0101 t\u012bra\u1e47apari\xf1\xf1\u0101 pah\u0101napari\xf1\xf1\u0101ti eva\u1e43 pari\xf1\xf1\u0101 tividh\u0101 hoti. Tattha \u2018\u2018abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 \xf1\u0101ta\u1e6d\u1e6dhena \xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti (pa\u1e6di. ma. m\u0101tik\u0101 1.20) eva\u1e43 uddisitv\u0101 \u2018\u2018ye ye dhamm\u0101 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101t\u0101 honti, te te dhamm\u0101 \xf1\u0101t\u0101 hont\u012b\u2019\u2019ti (pa\u1e6di. ma. 1.75) eva\u1e43 sa\u1e45khepato, \u2018\u2018sabba\u1e43, bhikkhave, abhi\xf1\xf1eyya\u1e43. Ki\xf1ca, bhikkhave, sabba\u1e43 abhi\xf1\xf1eyya\u1e43? Cakkhu\u1e43, bhikkhave, abhi\xf1\xf1eyya\u2019\u2019nti\u0101din\u0101 (pa\u1e6di. ma. 1.2) nayena vitth\u0101rato vutt\u0101 \xf1\u0101tapari\xf1\xf1\u0101 n\u0101ma. Tass\u0101 sappaccayan\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101bhij\u0101nan\u0101 \u0101ve\u1e47ik\u0101 bh\u016bmi.",translations:{en:"\u2018Full understanding is threefold\u2019 means: full understanding as knowing (\xf1\u0101tapari\xf1\xf1\u0101), full understanding as investigating (t\u012bra\u1e47apari\xf1\xf1\u0101), and full understanding as abandoning (pah\u0101napari\xf1\xf1\u0101). Thus, full understanding is threefold. Therein, having first set forth the text, \u2018Wisdom of direct knowledge is knowledge in the sense of what is known\u2019 (Pa\u1e6dis. M., M\u0101tik\u0101 1.20), there is what is called \u2018full understanding as knowing,\u2019 which is stated in brief as, \u2018Whatever things are directly known, those things are known\u2019 (Pa\u1e6dis. M. 1.75), and in detail by the method beginning, \u2018Bhikkhus, all is to be directly known. And what, bhikkhus, is all to be directly known? The eye, bhikkhus, is to be directly known,\u2019 and so on (Pa\u1e6dis. M. 1.2). Its specific domain is the direct knowledge of name-and-form together with its conditions.",pt:"\u201cTr\xeas s\xe3o os tipos de compreens\xe3o plena\u201d: a saber, a compreens\xe3o plena do conhecido, a compreens\xe3o plena por investiga\xe7\xe3o e a compreens\xe3o plena por abandono; assim, a compreens\xe3o plena \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos. Entre estes, tendo sido enunciado resumidamente: 'A sabedoria do conhecimento direto \xe9 conhecimento no sentido de ser conhecido', e 'Quaisquer dhammas que s\xe3o conhecidos diretamente, esses dhammas s\xe3o conhecidos', ela \xe9 ensinada detalhadamente da seguinte maneira: 'Monges, tudo deve ser conhecido diretamente. E o que, monges, \xe9 o tudo que deve ser conhecido diretamente? O olho, monges, deve ser conhecido diretamente', etc. Isso \xe9 chamado de compreens\xe3o plena do conhecido. O seu dom\xednio exclusivo \xe9 o conhecimento que discerne a mente e a mat\xe9ria junto com suas causas.",es:"\u2018El conocimiento pleno es de tres tipos\u2019 significa: conocimiento pleno de lo conocido, conocimiento pleno por investigaci\xf3n y conocimiento pleno por abandono. All\xed, tras indicar brevemente: \u2018El conocimiento por sabidur\xeda superior es conocimiento en el sentido de lo conocido\u2019, y de forma resumida: \u2018Cualesquiera que sean los fealidades conocidos por sabidur\xeda superior, esos fealidades son conocidos\u2019; y extensamente por el m\xe9todo que comienza: \u2018Monjes, todo debe ser conocido por sabidur\xeda superior. \xbfY qu\xe9 es todo? El ojo, monjes, debe ser conocido...\u2019, esto es lo que se llama conocimiento pleno de lo conocido. Su dominio exclusivo es el conocimiento de la mente y la materia junto con sus causas."}}]},440,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,i,n,s,t){n.exports=[{id:"vism-23.1",pali:"Ya\u1e43 pana vutta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018pa\xf1\xf1\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101ya ko \u0101nisa\u1e43so\u2019\u2019ti, tattha vad\u0101ma. Aya\xf1hi pa\xf1\xf1\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101 n\u0101ma anekasat\u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101. Tass\u0101 d\u012bghen\u0101pi addhun\u0101 na sukara\u1e43 vitth\u0101rato \u0101nisa\u1e43sa\u1e43 pak\u0101setu\u1e43. Sa\u1e45khepato panass\u0101 n\u0101n\u0101kilesaviddha\u1e43sana\u1e43, ariyaphalaras\u0101nubhavana\u1e43, nirodhasam\u0101pattisam\u0101pajjanasamatthat\u0101, \u0101huneyyabh\u0101v\u0101disiddh\u012bti ayam\u0101nisa\u1e43so veditabbo.",translations:{en:"Now, as to what was asked, 'What is the benefit of developing wisdom?', we shall speak on that. This development of wisdom has many hundreds of benefits. It is not easy to declare its benefits in detail even over a long period of time. In brief, however, its benefit should be understood as this: the destruction of manifold defilements, the experiencing of the taste of the noble fruit, the capability to enter the attainment of cessation, and the accomplishment of states such as being worthy of offerings.",pt:"Quanto ao que foi dito: \u201cQual \xe9 o benef\xedcio do desenvolvimento da sabedoria?\u201d, responderemos a isso. Pois este desenvolvimento da sabedoria possui centenas de benef\xedcios. Mesmo em um longo per\xedodo de tempo, n\xe3o \xe9 f\xe1cil expor detalhadamente os seus benef\xedcios. Em resumo, por\xe9m, deve-se compreender que os seus benef\xedcios s\xe3o: a destrui\xe7\xe3o de v\xe1rias impurezas mentais (kilesas), a experi\xeancia do sabor do fruto nobre (ariyaphala), a capacidade de alcan\xe7ar a realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o (nirodhasam\u0101patti) e a realiza\xe7\xe3o de qualidades como a de ser digno de oferendas (\u0101huneyyabh\u0101va), etc.",es:"Con respecto a lo que se dijo anteriormente: \xab\xbfCu\xe1l es el beneficio del desarrollo de la sabidur\xeda?\xbb, daremos la respuesta aqu\xed. Ciertamente, este desarrollo de la sabidur\xeda conlleva innumerables beneficios. Ser\xeda dif\xedcil exponer en detalle sus beneficios incluso en un largo per\xedodo de tiempo. En resumen, estos beneficios deben entenderse como: (1) la destrucci\xf3n de diversas impurezas (kilesas), (2) la experiencia del sabor del fruto noble (ariya-phala), (3) la capacidad de alcanzar la obtenci\xf3n de la cesaci\xf3n (nirodha-sam\u0101patti), y (4) el logro del estado de ser digno de ofrendas (\u0101huneyya) y otros m\xe9ritos similares."}},{id:"vism-23.2",pali:"Tattha ya\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bpaparicchedato pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya sakk\u0101yadi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 vasena n\u0101n\u0101kilesaviddha\u1e43sana\u1e43 vutta\u1e43, aya\u1e43 lokik\u0101ya pa\xf1\xf1\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101ya \u0101nisa\u1e43so. Ya\u1e43 ariyamaggakkha\u1e47e sa\u1e43yojan\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 vasena n\u0101n\u0101kilesaviddha\u1e43sana\u1e43 vutta\u1e43, aya\u1e43 lokuttar\u0101ya pa\xf1\xf1\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101ya \u0101nisa\u1e43soti veditabbo.",translations:{en:"Herein, the destruction of manifold defilements by way of abandoning identity view and so on, beginning from the defining of mentality-materiality, has been spoken of; this is the benefit of the mundane development of wisdom. The destruction of manifold defilements by way of abandoning the fetters and so on at the moment of the noble path has been spoken of; this should be understood as the benefit of the supramundane development of wisdom.",pt:"Ali, a destrui\xe7\xe3o de v\xe1rias impurezas mentais por meio da vis\xe3o da identidade (sakk\u0101yadi\u1e6d\u1e6dhi), etc., a partir da delimita\xe7\xe3o de mente-e-mat\xe9ria (n\u0101mar\u016bpapariccheda), deve ser compreendida como o benef\xedcio do desenvolvimento da sabedoria mundana. A destrui\xe7\xe3o de v\xe1rias impurezas mentais por meio dos grilh\xf5es (sa\u1e43yojanas), etc., no momento do caminho nobre, deve ser compreendida como o benef\xedcio do desenvolvimento da sabedoria supramundana.",es:"En esto, lo que se dijo acerca de la destrucci\xf3n de diversas impurezas mediante el discernimiento de la mente y la materia (n\u0101ma-r\u016bpa), comenzando con la visi\xf3n de la identidad (sakk\u0101ya-di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi) y dem\xe1s, es el beneficio del desarrollo de la sabidur\xeda mundana. Lo que se dijo acerca de la destrucci\xf3n de diversas impurezas en el momento del sendero noble (ariya-magga) mediante los grilletes (sa\u1e43yojana) y dem\xe1s, debe entenderse como el beneficio del desarrollo de la sabidur\xeda supramundana."}},{id:"vism-23.3",pali:"Bh\u012bmaveg\u0101nupatit\u0101, asan\u012bva siluccaye; V\u0101yuvegasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dhito, ara\xf1\xf1amiva p\u0101vako.",translations:{en:"Like a thunderbolt of dreadful velocity falling upon a mountain peak; like a forest fire stirred up by the force of the wind;",pt:"Como um raio caindo com terr\xedvel velocidade sobre uma montanha rochosa; como um inc\xeandio florestal provocado pela for\xe7a do vento em uma floresta;",es:"Como un rayo que cae con fuerza aterradora sobre un macizo de roca; como un incendio forestal que se levanta por la fuerza del viento a trav\xe9s de un bosque\u2014"}},{id:"vism-23.4",pali:"Andhak\u0101ra\u1e43 viya ravi, satejujjalama\u1e47\u1e0dalo; D\u012bgharatt\u0101nupatita\u1e43, sabb\u0101natthavidh\u0101yaka\u1e43.",translations:{en:"like the sun with its blazing, brilliant orb dispelling the darkness; that which has persisted for a long night, the cause of all misfortune\u2014",pt:"Como o sol com seu disco brilhante e poderoso dissipa a escurid\xe3o; [assim a sabedoria destr\xf3i] aquilo que se abateu por muito tempo e que causa todo tipo de dano,",es:"Como el sol con su c\xedrculo resplandeciente destruye la oscuridad; as\xed tambi\xe9n la sabidur\xeda destruye [la red de las impurezas] que ha persistido por largo tiempo y causa todo tipo de infortunios."}},{id:"vism-23.5",pali:"Kilesaj\u0101la\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 hi, viddha\u1e43sayati bh\u0101vit\u0101; Sandi\u1e6d\u1e6dhikamato ja\xf1\xf1\u0101, \u0101nisa\u1e43samima\u1e43 idha.",translations:{en:"the net of defilements\u2014is shattered by wisdom when it is developed. Therefore, one should know this as the benefit visible here.",pt:"a saber, a rede de impurezas mentais (kilesas). Pois a sabedoria desenvolvida a destr\xf3i. Portanto, que se conhe\xe7a aqui este benef\xedcio vis\xedvel por si mesmo.",es:"La sabidur\xeda desarrollada destruye la red de las impurezas; por lo tanto, se debe conocer este beneficio visible aqu\xed en este desarrollo de la sabidur\xeda."}},{id:"vism-23.6",pali:"Ariyaphalaras\u0101nubhavana nti na kevala\xf1ca kilesaviddha\u1e43sana\xf1\xf1eva, ariyaphalaras\u0101nubhavanampi pa\xf1\xf1\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101ya \u0101nisa\u1e43so. Ariyaphalanti hi sot\u0101pattiphal\u0101di s\u0101ma\xf1\xf1aphala\u1e43 vuccati. Tassa dv\u012bh\u0101k\u0101rehi ras\u0101nubhavana\u1e43 hoti. Maggav\u012bthiya\xf1ca phalasam\u0101pattivasena ca pavattiya\u1e43. Tatr\u0101ssa maggav\u012bthiya\u1e43 pavatti dassit\u0101yeva.",translations:{en:"And the experience of the taste of the noble fruits: it is not only the destruction of defilements, but the experience of the taste of the noble fruits is also a benefit of the development of wisdom. Indeed, the noble fruit refers to the fruit of recluseship, such as the fruit of stream-entry and so on. The experience of its taste occurs in two ways: in the path-process and by way of the attainment of fruition. Therein, its occurrence in the path-process has already been shown.",pt:"A \u201cexperi\xeancia do sabor do fruto nobre\u201d (ariyaphalaras\u0101nubhavana) significa que n\xe3o apenas a destrui\xe7\xe3o das impurezas \xe9 o benef\xedcio, mas tamb\xe9m a experi\xeancia do sabor do fruto nobre \xe9 um benef\xedcio do desenvolvimento da sabedoria. Pois \u201cfruto nobre\u201d refere-se ao fruto da vida asc\xe9tica, como o fruto da entrada na corrente (sot\u0101pattiphala), etc. A experi\xeancia de seu sabor ocorre de duas maneiras: no processo cognitivo do caminho (maggav\u012bthi) e na ocorr\xeancia sob a forma de realiza\xe7\xe3o do fruto (phalasam\u0101patti). Ali, a sua ocorr\xeancia no processo cognitivo do caminho j\xe1 foi mostrada.",es:"Experimentar el sabor del fruto noble no se refiere \xfanicamente a la destrucci\xf3n de las impurezas; experimentar el sabor del fruto noble es tambi\xe9n un beneficio del desarrollo de la sabidur\xeda. Por \xabfruto noble\xbb se entienden los frutos de la vida asc\xe9tica (s\u0101ma\xf1\xf1aphala), como el fruto de la entrada en la corriente y otros. La experiencia de su sabor ocurre de dos maneras: en el proceso del sendero (magga-v\u012bthi) y en el transcurso de la obtenci\xf3n del fruto (phala-sam\u0101patti). De estas, su ocurrencia en el proceso del sendero ya ha sido mostrada."}},{id:"vism-23.7",pali:"Tattha k\u0101 phalasam\u0101patt\u012b ti y\u0101 ariyaphalassa nirodhe appan\u0101.",translations:{en:"Herein, what is fruition attainment? It is the absorption of the noble fruit into cessation.",pt:"Ali, \u201cO que \xe9 a realiza\xe7\xe3o do fruto?\u201d \xc9 a absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101) do fruto nobre na cessa\xe7\xe3o [Nibb\u0101na].",es:"En esto, respecto a \xab\xbfQu\xe9 es la obtenci\xf3n del fruto?\xbb, es la absorci\xf3n (appan\u0101) del fruto noble en la cesaci\xf3n (Nibb\u0101na)."}},{id:"vism-23.8",pali:"Tasm\u0101 ariyaphalasseta\u1e43, ras\u0101nubhavana\u1e43 idha; Vipassan\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101ya, \u0101nisa\u1e43soti vuccati.",translations:{en:"Therefore, this experiencing of the taste of the noble fruit is, in this context, called a benefit of cultivating insight.",pt:"Portanto, esta experi\xeancia da ess\xeancia do fruto nobre \xe9 chamada aqui de o benef\xedcio do desenvolvimento da vis\xe3o interior (vipassan\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101).",es:"Por lo tanto, se dice aqu\xed que esta experiencia del sabor del fruto noble es el beneficio del desarrollo de la visi\xf3n cabal (vipassan\u0101-bh\u0101van\u0101)."}},{id:"vism-23.9",pali:"Nirodhasam\u0101pattisam\u0101pajjanasamatthat\u0101 ti na kevala\xf1ca ariyaphalaras\u0101nubhavana\u1e43yeva, aya\u1e43 pana nirodhasam\u0101pattiy\u0101 sam\u0101pajjanasamatthat\u0101pi imiss\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101ya \u0101nisa\u1e43soti veditabbo.",translations:{en:"Not only the experience of the taste of the noble fruit, but also this ability to enter the attainment of cessation should be understood as a benefit of this development of wisdom.",pt:"A 'capacidade de alcan\xe7ar a realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o': deve-se compreender que n\xe3o apenas a experi\xeancia da ess\xeancia do fruto nobre, mas tamb\xe9m esta capacidade de alcan\xe7ar a realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o \xe9 um benef\xedcio deste desenvolvimento da sabedoria.",es:"No debe entenderse que solo la experiencia del sabor del fruto noble es el beneficio; tambi\xe9n la capacidad de alcanzar este logro del cese debe reconocerse como un beneficio de este desarrollo de la sabidur\xeda."}},{id:"vism-23.10",pali:"Tatrida\u1e43 nirodhasam\u0101pattiy\u0101 vibh\u0101vanattha\u1e43 pa\xf1h\u0101kamma\u1e43 \u2013 k\u0101 nirodhasam\u0101patti, ke ta\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjanti, ke na sam\u0101pajjanti, kattha sam\u0101pajjanti, kasm\u0101 sam\u0101pajjanti, katha\xf1cass\u0101 sam\u0101pajjana\u1e43 hoti, katha\u1e43 \u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, katha\u1e43 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43, vu\u1e6d\u1e6dhitassa ki\u1e43ninna\u1e43 citta\u1e43 hoti, matassa ca sam\u0101pannassa ca ko viseso, nirodhasam\u0101patti ki\u1e43 sa\u1e45khat\u0101 asa\u1e45khat\u0101 lokiy\u0101 lokuttar\u0101 nipphann\u0101 anipphann\u0101ti?",translations:{en:"Herein is a set of questions for the clarification of the attainment of cessation: What is the attainment of cessation? Who enters it? Who does not enter it? Where does one enter it? Why does one enter it? How does its entry come about? How does it remain? How does emergence from it occur? Upon emerging, to what is the mind inclined? What is the difference between one who is dead and one who has entered this attainment? Is the attainment of cessation conditioned or unconditioned, worldly or supramundane, produced or unproduced?",pt:"Aqui, para esclarecer a realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o, apresenta-se este questionamento: O que \xe9 a realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o? Quem a alcan\xe7a? Quem n\xe3o a alcan\xe7a? Onde a alcan\xe7am? Por que a alcan\xe7am? Como ocorre a sua entrada? Como ocorre a sua perman\xeancia? Como ocorre a sua sa\xedda? Para o que se inclina a mente daquele que dela saiu? Qual \xe9 a diferen\xe7a entre uma pessoa morta e uma que entrou nesta realiza\xe7\xe3o? A realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o \xe9 condicionada (sa\u1e45khata) ou incondicionada (asa\u1e45khata), mundana (lokiya) ou supramundana (lokuttara), produzida (nipphanna) ou n\xe3o produzida (anipphanna)?",es:"Para esclarecer el logro del cese, se plantean las siguientes preguntas: \xbfQu\xe9 es el logro del cese? \xbfQui\xe9nes lo alcanzan? \xbfQui\xe9nes no lo alcanzan? \xbfD\xf3nde lo alcanzan? \xbfPor qu\xe9 lo alcanzan? \xbfC\xf3mo ocurre su entrada? \xbfC\xf3mo es su persistencia? \xbfC\xf3mo es su salida? \xbfHacia qu\xe9 se inclina la mente de quien ha salido? \xbfCu\xe1l es la diferencia entre un difunto y alguien que ha entrado en el cese? \xbfEs el logro del cese algo condicionado o incondicionado, mundano o supramundano, real o no real?"}},{id:"vism-23.11",pali:"\u0100huneyyabh\u0101v\u0101disiddh\u012b ti na kevala\xf1ca nirodhasam\u0101pattiy\u0101 sam\u0101pajjanasamatthat\u0101va, aya\u1e43 pana \u0101huneyyabh\u0101v\u0101disiddhipi imiss\u0101 lokuttarapa\xf1\xf1\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101ya \u0101nisa\u1e43soti veditabbo. Avisesena hi catubbidh\u0101yapi etiss\u0101 bh\u0101vitatt\u0101 bh\u0101vitapa\xf1\xf1o puggalo sadevakassa lokassa \u0101huneyyo hoti p\u0101huneyyo dakkhi\u1e47eyyo a\xf1jal\u012bkara\u1e47\u012byo anuttara\u1e43 pu\xf1\xf1akkhetta\u1e43 lokassa.",translations:{en:"The accomplishment of being worthy of offerings and so forth: not only is the ability to attain the attainment of cessation a benefit, but this accomplishment of being worthy of offerings and so forth should also be understood as a benefit of developing this supramundane wisdom. For, without distinction, a person who has developed this fourfold wisdom becomes worthy of offerings, worthy of hospitality, worthy of gifts, worthy of reverential salutation, an unsurpassed field of merit for the world with its gods.",pt:"Quanto a 'A realiza\xe7\xe3o de ser digno de oferendas, etc.': deve-se compreender que n\xe3o apenas a capacidade de entrar na realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o, mas tamb\xe9m esta realiza\xe7\xe3o de ser digno de oferendas, etc., \xe9 um benef\xedcio do desenvolvimento desta sabedoria supramundana. Pois, por ter desenvolvido esta sabedoria supramundana em suas quatro formas sem distin\xe7\xe3o, a pessoa de sabedoria desenvolvida torna-se digna de oferendas trazidas de longe (\u0101huneyyo), digna de hospitalidade (p\u0101huneyyo), digna de doa\xe7\xf5es (dakkhi\u1e47eyyo), digna de rever\xeancia com as m\xe3os unidas (a\xf1jal\u012bkara\u1e47\u012byo) e um campo supremo de m\xe9rito para o mundo com os seus devas.",es:"La consecuci\xf3n de ser digno de ofrendas y dem\xe1s: debe entenderse que no solo la capacidad de entrar en el logro de la cesaci\xf3n, sino tambi\xe9n esta consecuci\xf3n de ser digno de ofrendas y dem\xe1s es un beneficio del desarrollo de esta sabidur\xeda supramundana. Pues, por haber desarrollado esta sabidur\xeda de cuatro tipos sin distinci\xf3n, la persona de sabidur\xeda desarrollada es digna de ofrendas, digna de hospitalidad, digna de dones, digna de ser saludada con las manos juntas y es el campo de m\xe9rito insuperable para el mundo, incluyendo a los devas."}},{id:"vism-23.12",pali:"Visesato panettha pa\u1e6dhamamaggapa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 t\u0101va bh\u0101vetv\u0101 mand\u0101ya vipassan\u0101ya \u0101gato mudindriyopi sattakkhattuparamo n\u0101ma hoti, sattasugatibhave sa\u1e43saritv\u0101 dukkhassanta\u1e43 karoti. Majjhim\u0101ya vipassan\u0101ya \u0101gato majjhimindriyo kola\u1e43kolo n\u0101ma hoti, dve v\u0101 t\u012b\u1e47i v\u0101 kul\u0101ni sandh\u0101vitv\u0101 sa\u1e43saritv\u0101 dukkhassanta\u1e43 karoti. Tikkh\u0101ya vipassan\u0101ya \u0101gato tikkhindriyo ekab\u012bj\u012b n\u0101ma hoti, eka\xf1\xf1eva m\u0101nusaka\u1e43 bhava\u1e43 nibbattetv\u0101 dukkhassanta\u1e43 karoti.",translations:{en:"Specifically, in this regard, one who has developed the wisdom of the first path, having come by way of dull insight and possessing dull faculties, is called a 'seven-times-at-most' one; having wandered through seven happy existences, he makes an end of suffering. One who has come by way of middling insight and possessing middling faculties is called a 'family-to-family' one; having run on and wandered through two or three families, he makes an end of suffering. One who has come by way of sharp insight and possessing sharp faculties is called a 'one-seed' one; having brought about only one human existence, he makes an end of suffering.",pt:"Especificamente, entre estes, aquele que desenvolveu a sabedoria do primeiro caminho e chegou por meio de uma percep\xe7\xe3o (vipassan\u0101) fraca, mesmo tendo faculdades embotadas, \xe9 chamado de 'aquele que tem no m\xe1ximo sete renascimentos' (sattakkhattuparama); tendo transmigrado por sete exist\xeancias em mundos felizes, ele p\xf5e fim ao sofrimento. Aquele que chegou por meio de uma percep\xe7\xe3o m\xe9dia e tem faculdades m\xe9dias \xe9 chamado de 'aquele que vai de fam\xedlia em fam\xedlia' (kola\u1e45kola); tendo transmigrado por duas ou tr\xeas fam\xedlias, ele p\xf5e fim ao sofrimento. Aquele que chegou por meio de uma percep\xe7\xe3o afiada e tem faculdades afiadas \xe9 chamado de 'aquele de uma \xfanica semente' (ekab\u012bj\u012b); tendo gerado apenas uma \xfanica exist\xeancia humana, ele p\xf5e fim ao sofrimento.",es:"Espec\xedficamente, entre estos cuatro conocimientos del camino, aquel que habiendo desarrollado el conocimiento del primer camino llega con una visi\xf3n profunda d\xe9bil y facultades embotadas es llamado sattakkhattuparama (el que renace siete veces como m\xe1ximo); \xe9l transita por siete existencias en los mundos felices y luego pone fin al sufrimiento. Aquel que llega con una visi\xf3n profunda media y facultades medias es llamado kolankola; tras transitar por dos o tres familias en mundos felices, pone fin al sufrimiento. Aquel que llega con una visi\xf3n profunda aguda y facultades agudas es llamado ekabiji (de una sola semilla); tras renacer en una sola existencia humana, pone fin al sufrimiento."}},{id:"vism-23.13",pali:"Dutiyamaggapa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b n\u0101ma hoti, sakideva ima\u1e43 loka\u1e43 \u0101gantv\u0101 dukkhassanta\u1e43 karoti.",translations:{en:"Having developed the wisdom of the second path, he becomes one called a once-returner. Having come to this world only once more, he makes an end of suffering.",pt:"Tendo desenvolvido a sabedoria do segundo caminho, torna-se um uma-vez-retornante (sakad\u0101g\u0101min); retornando apenas uma vez a este mundo, ele p\xf5e fim ao sofrimento.",es:"Habiendo desarrollado el conocimiento del segundo camino, se convierte en un sakadagami (el que retorna una vez); regresando a este mundo humano solo una vez m\xe1s, pone fin al sufrimiento."}},{id:"vism-23.14",pali:"Tatiyamaggapa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b n\u0101ma hoti. So indriyavemattat\u0101vasena antar\u0101parinibb\u0101y\u012b, upahaccaparinibb\u0101y\u012b, asa\u1e45kh\u0101raparinibb\u0101y\u012b, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101raparinibb\u0101y\u012b, uddha\u1e43soto akani\u1e6d\u1e6dhag\u0101m\u012bti pa\xf1cadh\u0101. Idha vih\u0101yani\u1e6d\u1e6dho hoti. Tattha antar\u0101parinibb\u0101y\u012b ti yattha katthaci suddh\u0101v\u0101sabhave upapajjitv\u0101 \u0101yuvemajjha\u1e43 appatv\u0101va parinibb\u0101yati. Upahaccaparinibb\u0101y\u012b ti \u0101yuvemajjha\u1e43 atikkamitv\u0101 parinibb\u0101yati. Asa\u1e45kh\u0101raparinibb\u0101y\u012b ti asa\u1e45kh\u0101rena appayogena uparimagga\u1e43 nibbatteti. Sasa\u1e45kh\u0101raparinibb\u0101y\u012b ti sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rena sappayogena uparimagga\u1e43 nibbatteti. Uddha\u1e43soto akani\u1e6d\u1e6dhag\u0101m\u012b ti yatthupapanno, tato uddha\u1e43 y\u0101va akani\u1e6d\u1e6dhabhav\u0101 \u0101ruyha tattha parinibb\u0101yati.",translations:{en:"Having developed the wisdom of the third path, he becomes one called a non-returner. According to the diversity of faculties, he is of five kinds: one who attains final Nibb\u0101na in the interval (antar\u0101parinibb\u0101y\u012b), one who attains final Nibb\u0101na upon landing (upahaccaparinibb\u0101y\u012b), one who attains final Nibb\u0101na without prompting (asa\u1e45kh\u0101raparinibb\u0101y\u012b), one who attains final Nibb\u0101na with prompting (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101raparinibb\u0101y\u012b), and one who goes upstream to the Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha realm (uddha\u1e43soto akani\u1e6d\u1e6dhag\u0101m\u012b). He is one who makes an end by abandoning this world. Therein, the 'one who attains final Nibb\u0101na in the interval' is one who, having been reborn in some Pure Abode, attains final Nibb\u0101na without reaching the midpoint of the lifespan. The 'one who attains final Nibb\u0101na upon landing' is one who attains final Nibb\u0101na after passing the midpoint of the lifespan. The 'one who attains final Nibb\u0101na without prompting' is one who produces the higher path without prompting, without exertion. The 'one who attains final Nibb\u0101na with prompting' is one who produces the higher path with prompting, with exertion. The 'one who goes upstream to the Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha realm' is one who, from where he has been reborn, ascends up to the Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha existence and there attains final Nibb\u0101na.",pt:"Tendo desenvolvido a sabedoria do terceiro caminho, torna-se um n\xe3o-retornante (an\u0101g\u0101min). Devido \xe0 diferen\xe7a em suas faculdades, ele \xe9 de cinco tipos: aquele que alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na no intervalo (antar\u0101parinibb\u0101y\u012b), aquele que alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na ap\xf3s ultrapassar a metade da vida (upahaccaparinibb\u0101y\u012b), aquele que alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na sem esfor\xe7o (asa\u1e45kh\u0101raparinibb\u0101y\u012b), aquele que alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na com esfor\xe7o (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101raparinibb\u0101y\u012b) e aquele que sobe a correnteza at\xe9 o reino Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha (uddha\u1e43soto akani\u1e6d\u1e6dhag\u0101m\u012b). Ele p\xf5e fim \xe0 exist\xeancia abandonando este mundo sensorial. Entre eles, 'aquele que alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na no intervalo' \xe9 quem, tendo renascido em qualquer uma das Moradas Puras (suddh\u0101v\u0101sa), alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na antes de atingir a metade do tempo de vida. 'Aquele que alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na ap\xf3s ultrapassar' \xe9 quem alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na ap\xf3s passar da metade do tempo de vida. 'Aquele que alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na sem esfor\xe7o' \xe9 quem produz o caminho superior sem esfor\xe7o ou aplica\xe7\xe3o intensa. 'Aquele que alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na com esfor\xe7o' \xe9 quem produz o caminho superior com esfor\xe7o e aplica\xe7\xe3o intensa. 'Aquele que sobe a correnteza at\xe9 o reino Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha' \xe9 quem, de onde quer que tenha renascido, ascende dali at\xe9 o reino Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha e ali alcan\xe7a o parinibb\u0101na.",es:"Habiendo desarrollado el conocimiento del tercer camino, se convierte en un anagami (el que no retorna). Debido a la diferencia en sus facultades, se divide en cinco tipos: el que alcanza el parinibbana en el intervalo (antaraparinibbayi), el que alcanza el parinibbana tras el punto medio (upahaccaparinibbayi), el que alcanza el parinibbana sin esfuerzo (asankharaparinibbayi), el que alcanza el parinibbana con esfuerzo (sasankharaparinibbayi) y el que fluye hacia arriba llegando al mundo Akanittha (uddhamsoto akanitthogami). Aqu\xed termina su existencia en el mundo de los sentidos. Entre ellos, el antaraparinibbayi es aquel que, habiendo renacido en cualquier mundo de las Moradas Puras, alcanza el parinibbana antes de llegar a la mitad de su vida. El upahaccaparinibbayi es aquel que alcanza el parinibbana tras haber pasado la mitad de su vida. El asankharaparinibbayi es aquel que produce el camino superior sin gran esfuerzo. El sasankharaparinibbayi es aquel que produce el camino superior con gran esfuerzo. El uddhamsoto akanitthogami es aquel que, desde su lugar de renacimiento, asciende hacia arriba hasta el mundo Akanittha y all\xed alcanza el parinibbana."}},{id:"vism-23.15",pali:"Catutthamaggapa\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 koci saddh\u0101vimutto hoti, koci pa\xf1\xf1\u0101vimutto hoti, koci ubhatobh\u0101gavimutto hoti, koci tevijjo, koci cha\u1e37abhi\xf1\xf1o, koci pa\u1e6disambhidappabhedappatto mah\u0101kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101savo. Ya\u1e43 sandh\u0101ya vutta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018maggakkha\u1e47e panesa ta\u1e43 ja\u1e6da\u1e43 vija\u1e6deti n\u0101ma. Phalakkha\u1e47e vija\u1e6ditaja\u1e6do sadevakassa lokassa aggadakkhi\u1e47eyyo hot\u012b\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"Having developed the wisdom of the fourth path, someone becomes one liberated by faith, someone one liberated by wisdom, someone one liberated in both ways, someone a possessor of the three true knowledges, someone a possessor of the six direct knowledges, or someone a great one whose cankers are destroyed who has reached the diversity of the analytical knowledges. It is with reference to him that it was said: 'At the moment of the path, he is called one who disentangles this tangle. At the moment of fruition, he has disentangled the tangle and is the foremost one worthy of gifts in the world with its gods.'",pt:"Tendo desenvolvido a sabedoria do quarto caminho, um torna-se libertado pela f\xe9 (saddh\u0101vimutta), outro libertado pela sabedoria (pa\xf1\xf1\u0101vimutta), outro duplamente libertado (ubhatobh\u0101gavimutta), outro detentor do tr\xedplice conhecimento (tevijja), outro detentor dos seis conhecimentos diretos (cha\u1e37abhi\xf1\xf1a), ou um grande destruidor das impurezas (mah\u0101kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101savo) que alcan\xe7ou as distin\xe7\xf5es do conhecimento anal\xedtico (pa\u1e6disambhid\u0101). Referindo-se a isso, foi dito: 'No momento do caminho, ele de fato desata aquele emaranhado. No momento do fruto, tendo desatado o emaranhado, ele torna-se o supremo receptor de oferendas para o mundo com os seus devas'.",es:"Habiendo desarrollado el conocimiento del cuarto camino, algunos son liberados por la fe (saddhavimutta), algunos son liberados por la sabidur\xeda (pannavimutta), algunos son liberados por ambos lados (ubhatobhagavimutta), algunos poseen el triple conocimiento (tevijja), algunos poseen los seis conocimientos superiores (chalabhinna) y otros son grandes arahants que han alcanzado la distinci\xf3n de los conocimientos anal\xedticos (patisambhidappatta). Con referencia a tal arahant se dijo: 'En el momento del camino, \xe9l est\xe1 desenredando ese enredo. En el momento del fruto, habiendo desenredado el enredo, se convierte en el supremo receptor de ofrendas para el mundo con sus deidades'."}},{id:"vism-23.16",pali:"Eva\u1e43 anek\u0101nisa\u1e43s\u0101, ariyapa\xf1\xf1\u0101ya bh\u0101van\u0101; Yasm\u0101 tasm\u0101 kareyy\u0101tha, rati\u1e43 tattha vicakkha\u1e47o.",translations:{en:"Thus the development of noble wisdom has many benefits; therefore a discerning person should take delight in it.",pt:"Visto que o desenvolvimento da nobre sabedoria traz tantos benef\xedcios, por isso, o homem s\xe1bio deve encontrar nele o seu deleite.",es:"Puesto que el desarrollo de la sabidur\xeda noble tiene tan variados beneficios, el sabio debe deleitarse en ese desarrollo."}},{id:"vism-23.17",pali:"\u2018\u2018S\u012ble pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya naro sapa\xf1\xf1o, citta\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1a\xf1ca bh\u0101vaya\u1e43; \u0100t\u0101p\u012b nipako bhikkhu, so ima\u1e43 vija\u1e6daye ja\u1e6da\u2019\u2019nti. \u2013",translations:{en:"\u201cA wise man, established in virtue, developing mind and wisdom, an ardent, discerning bhikkhu, can disentangle this tangle.\u201d \u2013",pt:"'Estabelecido na virtude, o homem s\xe1bio, desenvolvendo a mente e a sabedoria, o bhikkhu ardente e prudente, ele desata este emaranhado.'",es:"'El hombre sabio, establecido en la virtud, desarrollando la mente y la sabidur\xeda, el monje ardiente y prudente, \xe9l desenreda este enredo.' \u2014"}},{id:"vism-23.18",pali:"\u2018\u2018Imiss\u0101 d\u0101ni g\u0101th\u0101ya, kathit\u0101ya mahesin\u0101; Va\u1e47\u1e47ayanto yath\u0101bh\u016bta\u1e43, attha\u1e43 s\u012bl\u0101dibhedana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"\u201cNow, explaining as it truly is the meaning of this verse spoken by the Great Seer, with its divisions of virtue and so on...",pt:"'Agora, explicando como realmente \xe9 o significado da virtude e dos demais aspectos desta estrofe proferida pelo Grande S\xe1bio...'",es:"'Ahora, describiendo seg\xfan la realidad el significado de esta estrofa pronunciada por el Gran Sabio, detallando la virtud y los dem\xe1s componentes;"}},{id:"vism-23.19",pali:"\u2018\u2018Visuddhimagga\u1e43 bh\u0101sissa\u1e43, ta\u1e43 me sakkacca bh\u0101sato; Visuddhik\u0101m\u0101 sabbepi, nis\u0101mayatha s\u0101dhavo\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"\u201cI shall speak the Path of Purification; so let all you good people who desire purity listen attentively to me as I speak.\u201d",pt:"'Falarei sobre o Caminho da Purifica\xe7\xe3o (Visuddhimagga). Que todas as pessoas de bem que desejam a purifica\xe7\xe3o escutem-me com aten\xe7\xe3o enquanto falo.'",es:"'expondr\xe9 el Sendero de la Purificaci\xf3n; todos ustedes, buenas personas que desean la pureza, escuchen atentamente lo que dir\xe9'."}},{id:"vism-23.20",pali:"T\u0101va ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhatu lokasmi\u1e43, lokanitthara\u1e47esina\u1e43; Dassento kulaputt\u0101na\u1e43, naya\u1e43 s\u012bl\u0101disuddhiy\u0101.",translations:{en:"May this treatise remain in the world for so long, showing the method for the purity of virtue and so forth to the sons of good family who seek liberation from the world.",pt:"Que ele permane\xe7a no mundo por tanto tempo, mostrando aos filhos de boas fam\xedlias que buscam a liberta\xe7\xe3o do mundo o m\xe9todo de purifica\xe7\xe3o atrav\xe9s da virtude e dos demais aspectos.",es:"Que esta obra permanezca en el mundo mientras tanto, mostrando a los hijos de buena familia que buscan la liberaci\xf3n el m\xe9todo para la purificaci\xf3n a trav\xe9s de la virtud y dem\xe1s pr\xe1cticas."}}]},441,[]);
